INSERT INTO `monuments` VALUES (1,'bhaktapur-durbar-square','Bhaktapur Durbar Square','भक्तपुर दरबार क्षेत्र','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.672194,85.428104,'square','Hindu',NULL,NULL,'14th–18th century (Malla royal palace complex until 1769)','Malla','Newar palace square of brick-and-timber palaces, courtyards and pagoda and shikhara temples',1,'Royal palace square of the Malla kings of Bhaktapur, once said to hold 99 courtyards.','You are standing in Khwopa Layaku, the royal palace square of the old kingdom of Bhaktapur. Malla kings ruled from here until the Gorkhali conquest of 1769, and the square was once considered the grandest of the valley\'s three Durbar Squares. Look around and notice how open it feels. That space is a scar: earthquakes in 1833 and 1934 brought down palaces and temples that once crowded this ground. Tradition says the palace had ninety-nine courtyards; only about fifteen survive, mostly those tied to the goddess Taleju. Find the gilded statue of King Bhupatindra Malla on his stone column, hands folded toward the palace. Look closely at his leg and you may spot a bullet mark said to date from the battle of 1769. Ahead of you are the Palace of Fifty-five Windows and the shimmering Golden Gate. Since 1979 this square has been part of the Kathmandu Valley World Heritage Site.',NULL,'[\"It housed the kings of Bhaktapur until the kingdom was conquered by the Gorkhalis in 1769.\", \"Tradition says the palace once had 99 courtyards; only about 15 survive today.\", \"The 1833 and 1934 earthquakes destroyed many buildings, which is why the square looks unusually open.\", \"The 25 April 2015 earthquake damaged 116 historic and cultural monuments here.\"]',NULL,NULL,1800,500,0,90,'The April 2015 earthquake damaged 116 historic monuments in the square and destroyed the Vatsala Durga Temple, which has since been rebuilt.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/View_of_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-View_of_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg','Bikram Pratap Singh · CC BY-SA 3.0','square,hindu,malla,bhaktapur,unesco,palace,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121/\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4900869\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1192827651\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/entry-fees-of-the-heritage-sites-in-nepal/\"]','भक्तपुरका मल्ल राजाहरूको राजदरबार क्षेत्र, जहाँ ९९ वटा चोक थिए भनिन्छ।','तपाईं ख्वप लायकु, अर्थात् पुरानो भक्तपुर राज्यको राजदरबार क्षेत्रमा हुनुहुन्छ। सन् १७६९ मा गोरखालीले जित्ने बेलासम्म मल्ल राजाहरूले यहीँबाट शासन गरे। उपत्यकाका तीन दरबार क्षेत्रमध्ये यो सबैभन्दा भव्य मानिन्थ्यो। वरिपरि हेर्नुहोस्, कत्ति खुला छ! त्यो खाली ठाउँ भूकम्पले छोडेको घाउ हो। सन् १८३३ र १९३४ का भूकम्पले यहाँ भीडभाड गरेर बसेका दरबार र मन्दिर ढाले। परम्परा अनुसार दरबारमा ९९ वटा चोक थिए, अहिले करिब १५ वटा मात्र बाँकी छन्, धेरैजसो तलेजु भवानीसँग जोडिएका। ढुङ्गाको स्तम्भमाथि दरबारतिर हात जोडेर बसेका राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लको सुनले मोहोरिएको मूर्ति खोज्नुहोस्। उनको खुट्टा ध्यान दिएर हेर्नुभयो भने सन् १७६९ को युद्धमा लागेको भनिएको गोलीको दाग भेट्न सक्नुहुन्छ। अगाडि पचपन्न झ्याले दरबार र झिलिमिली सुनढोका छन्। सन् १९७९ देखि यो क्षेत्र काठमाडौँ उपत्यका विश्व सम्पदा स्थलको भाग हो।',NULL,'[\"सन् १७६९ मा गोरखालीले राज्य जित्ने बेलासम्म यहाँ भक्तपुरका राजाहरू बस्थे।\", \"परम्परा अनुसार दरबारमा ९९ वटा चोक थिए, अहिले करिब १५ वटा मात्र बाँकी छन्।\", \"सन् १८३३ र १९३४ का भूकम्पले धेरै भवन ढाले, त्यसैले यो क्षेत्र अरूभन्दा बढी खुला देखिन्छ।\", \"सन् २०१५ अप्रिल २५ को भूकम्पले यहाँका ११६ ऐतिहासिक तथा सांस्कृतिक स्मारकमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो।\"]','सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पले यहाँका ११६ ऐतिहासिक स्मारकमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो र वत्सला दुर्गा मन्दिर ढल्यो। त्यो मन्दिर अहिले फेरि बनिसकेको छ।','[{\"name\": \"Bisket Jatra\", \"note\": \"Bhaktapur\'s New Year festival; Bhairav\'s chariot is pulled around Taumadhi\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"बिस्केट जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"भक्तपुरको नयाँ वर्षको पर्व। भैरवको रथ तौमढी वरिपरि तानिन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Gai Jatra\", \"note\": \"Families who lost someone that year parade through the squares in costume\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"गाईजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"त्यस वर्ष आफन्त गुमाएका परिवारले भेषभूषा लगाएर चोकहरूमा घुम्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_during_Gai_Jatra.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_during_Gai_Jatra.jpg\", \"author\": \"Manish2mdr\", \"caption\": \"Bhaktapur Durbar Square during Gai Jatra\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_during_Gai_Jatra.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_2014.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_2014.jpg\", \"author\": \"Avista\", \"caption\": \"Bhaktapur Durbar Square, 2014\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_2014.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Bhaktapur_Durbar_SQ_before_april_earthquake.JPG/1280px-Bhaktapur_Durbar_SQ_before_april_earthquake.JPG\", \"author\": \"Bhupengrg\", \"caption\": \"The square before the April 2015 earthquake\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_Durbar_SQ_before_april_earthquake.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/BDS_groundshot.jpg/1280px-BDS_groundshot.jpg\", \"author\": \"Kp217c\", \"caption\": \"Ground-level view across the square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BDS_groundshot.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_2018-09_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_2018-09_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Bhaktapur Durbar Square, 2018\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square_2018-09_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"square\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Wide open brick plaza: long palace with 55 carved windows and a Golden Gate, a king on a pillar, stone Vatsala temple\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#9c8a6e\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"golden-door\", \"carved-windows\", \"carved-struts\", \"stone-pillar\", \"bell\", \"lion-statues\", \"gilded-pinnacle\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [200, 80], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(2,'fifty-five-window-palace','Palace of Fifty-five Windows','पचपन्न झ्याले दरबार','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur','bhaktapur-durbar-square',27.672158,85.428557,'palace','Secular',NULL,1708,'Completed 1708 under Bhupatindra Malla, replacing a 15th-century palace','Malla','Brick-and-timber Newar palace with a long row of carved wooden windows',1,'Bhupatindra Malla\'s palace famed for its carved windows and rare Malla-era murals.','Raise your eyes to the long brick façade in front of you and try counting the carved wooden windows. This is the Palace of Fifty-five Windows, Nge Nyapa Jhya Layaku in Newar. King Bhupatindra Malla completed it in 1708 after an earthquake in 1681 ruined an older palace from the fifteenth century. Look just above the ground floor and you will see a band of 147 tiny carvings of musical ragas, a hint that this palace was built with music in mind. The 1934 earthquake destroyed the top floor, and for decades it was patched with European roof tiles until a 2006 renovation restored traditional tiles and the projecting top-floor windows. Inside, out of sight, survive some of the finest Malla murals in Nepal. One shows the king and his queen, Vishva Lakshmi, painted as a cosmic Shiva and Parvati. Of all the palaces in the square, this façade has changed the least.',NULL,'[\"Bhupatindra Malla completed the palace in 1708.\", \"A cornice carries 147 miniature carvings of musical ragas.\", \"The 1934 earthquake destroyed its top floor; a 2006 renovation restored traditional roof tiles.\", \"Its murals include Bhupatindra Malla and Queen Vishva Lakshmi depicted as a cosmic Shiva and consort.\"]',NULL,NULL,1800,500,0,20,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/55_Jhyale_Darbar_bkt.JPG/1280px-55_Jhyale_Darbar_bkt.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:55_Jhyale_Darbar_bkt.JPG','Shristibaral · CC BY-SA 3.0','palace,secular,malla,bhaktapur,unesco,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13182983\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Pachpanna_Jhyale_Darbar\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121/\"]','भूपतीन्द्र मल्लको दरबार, जो कुँदिएका झ्याल र मल्लकालीन दुर्लभ भित्तेचित्रका लागि प्रसिद्ध छ।','तपाईंको अगाडि भएको लामो इँटाको भित्तातिर हेर्नुहोस् र कुँदिएका काठका झ्याल गन्ने प्रयास गर्नुहोस्। यो पचपन्न झ्याले दरबार हो, नेवारीमा ‘ङे ङ्यापा झ्या लायकु’। सन् १६८१ को भूकम्पले पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीको पुरानो दरबार ढालेपछि राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले सन् १७०८ मा यो दरबार पूरा गरे। भुइँतलाको ठीक माथि हेर्नुहोस्, सङ्गीतका रागहरूका १४७ वटा साना कुँदाइको पट्टी देख्नुहुनेछ। यो दरबार सङ्गीतलाई मनमा राखेर बनाइएको सङ्केत हो। सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पले माथिल्लो तला भत्कायो। धेरै दशकसम्म त्यसमा युरोपेली छानाका टाइल टालिएका थिए। सन् २००६ को मर्मतले परम्परागत टाइल र माथिल्लो तलाका बाहिर निस्किएका झ्याल फर्कायो। भित्र, नदेखिने गरी, नेपालकै उत्कृष्ट मल्लकालीन भित्तेचित्रमध्ये केही बाँकी छन्। एउटामा राजा र उनकी रानी विश्वलक्ष्मीलाई ब्रह्माण्डका शिव र पार्वतीका रूपमा चित्रण गरिएको छ। चोकका सबै दरबारमध्ये यसको अगाडिको भाग सबैभन्दा कम बदलिएको छ।',NULL,'[\"भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले सन् १७०८ मा दरबार पूरा गरे।\", \"एउटा कर्निसमा सङ्गीतका रागहरूका १४७ वटा साना कुँदाइ छन्।\", \"सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पले माथिल्लो तला भत्कायो। सन् २००६ को मर्मतले परम्परागत छानाका टाइल फर्कायो।\", \"यसका भित्तेचित्रमा भूपतीन्द्र मल्ल र रानी विश्वलक्ष्मीलाई ब्रह्माण्डका शिव र पार्वतीका रूपमा चित्रण गरिएको छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/55_Windows_Palace_01.jpg/1280px-55_Windows_Palace_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Krish Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Palace of Fifty-five Windows\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:55_Windows_Palace_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/55_Windows_Palace_02.jpg/1280px-55_Windows_Palace_02.jpg\", \"author\": \"Krish Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Row of carved wooden windows\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:55_Windows_Palace_02.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/55_windows_Palace_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-55_windows_Palace_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"The palace on Bhaktapur Durbar Square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:55_windows_Palace_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/55_Window_Palace%2C_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-55_Window_Palace%2C_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Palace facade with the Golden Gate\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:55_Window_Palace,_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/55window_palace_ST_%282%29.JPG/1280px-55window_palace_ST_%282%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"सृजना\", \"caption\": \"Fifty-five Window Palace from the square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:55window_palace_ST_(2).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Long brick facade with a continuous row of dark carved wooden windows along the top floor; Golden Gate at one end\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#3e2a1c\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"carved-windows\", \"golden-door\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [60, 15], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(3,'golden-gate-bhaktapur','Golden Gate (Lun Dhwakha)','सुनढोका','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur','bhaktapur-durbar-square',27.672230,85.428500,'gate','Hindu','Taleju',1754,'Built 1751–1754 under Ranajit Malla (planned from 1646)','Malla','Gilt-copper repoussé gateway with a torana showing Taleju, set in a brick palace wall',1,'A gilded gateway to the Taleju shrine, hailed as a masterpiece of Nepalese metalwork.','Stand in front of the gleaming doorway set into the palace wall. This is Lun Dhwakha, the Golden Gate, and it guards the way to the inner courtyards and the shrine of Taleju, the guardian goddess of the Malla kings. Look up at the arched panel over the door: the central many-armed figure is Taleju herself. The idea is older than the gate. In 1646 King Jagajjyoti Malla brought two goldsmiths from Lalitpur to make it, but they died before work began, perhaps because there was not enough gold. More than a century later, King Ranajit Malla funded the project, and the smiths\' descendants finished it in 1754. Notice the two Newar inscriptions of Ranajit Malla on either side. The English art historian Percy Brown called it the loveliest piece of art in the kingdom. Beyond the gate lies the Taleju temple, where entry is restricted to Hindus.',NULL,'[\"The gate was made between 1751 and 1754 by the smiths Subhakara, Karunakara and Ratikara.\", \"King Jagajjyoti Malla first planned it in 1646, but the project stalled for over a century.\", \"The central figure on the tympanum is an image of the goddess Taleju.\", \"It leads to the Taleju shrine; guidebooks report entry beyond is restricted to Hindus and photography is barred.\"]',NULL,NULL,1800,500,0,15,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/The_Golden_Gate_bkt.JPG/1280px-The_Golden_Gate_bkt.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Golden_Gate_bkt.JPG','Shristibaral · CC BY-SA 3.0','gate,hindu,malla,bhaktapur,unesco,palace,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Golden_Gate,_Bhaktapur_Durbar\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/points-of-interest/golden-gate/1438149\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121/\"]','तलेजु मन्दिरतर्फ जाने सुनौलो प्रवेशद्वार, जसलाई नेपाली धातुकलाको उत्कृष्ट नमुना मानिन्छ।','दरबारको पर्खालमा बनेको चम्किलो ढोकाअगाडि उभिनुहोस्। यो सुनढोका (लुन ध्वाखा) हो। यसले भित्री चोक र मल्ल राजाहरूकी रक्षक देवी तलेजुको मन्दिरतिर जाने बाटो रक्षा गर्छ। ढोकामाथिको अर्धगोलाकार तोरणमा हेर्नुहोस्: बीचमा धेरै हात भएकी आकृति स्वयं तलेजु हुन्। यो योजना ढोकाभन्दा पुरानो हो। सन् १६४६ मा राजा जगज्योति मल्लले ललितपुरबाट दुईजना सुनार ल्याएका थिए, तर काम सुरु हुनुअघि नै उनीहरू बिते, सायद पर्याप्त सुन नभएर होला। सय वर्षभन्दा बढीपछि राजा रणजित मल्लले खर्च जुटाए र ती सुनारका सन्तानले सन् १७५४ मा यो पूरा गरे। दुवै छेउमा रणजित मल्लका दुईवटा नेवारी शिलालेख छन्, ती पनि हेर्नुहोस्। अङ्ग्रेज कला इतिहासकार पर्सी ब्राउनले यसलाई राज्यकै सबैभन्दा सुन्दर कलाकृति भनेका थिए। ढोकापारि तलेजु मन्दिर छ, जहाँ हिन्दूबाहेक अरू जान पाउँदैनन्।',NULL,'[\"यो ढोका सन् १७५१ देखि १७५४ बीच सुनार सुभाकर, करुणाकर र रतिकरले बनाएका थिए।\", \"राजा जगज्योति मल्लले सन् १६४६ मा पहिलो पटक यसको योजना बनाएका थिए, तर काम सय वर्षभन्दा बढी रोकियो।\", \"तोरणको बीचको आकृति देवी तलेजुको मूर्ति हो।\", \"यसले तलेजु मन्दिरतर्फ लैजान्छ। पुस्तिकाहरूका अनुसार भित्र हिन्दूले मात्र जान पाउँछन् र फोटो खिच्न मनाही छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Bhaktapur_Durbar_square_and_Golden_Gate.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_Durbar_square_and_Golden_Gate.jpg\", \"author\": \"सरोज कुमार ढकाल\", \"caption\": \"Golden Gate in the palace wall\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_Durbar_square_and_Golden_Gate.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Golden_Gate_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Golden_Gate_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Manoguru\", \"caption\": \"Golden Gate at Bhaktapur Durbar Square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Golden_Gate_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Tympanum_of_Golden_Gate_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Tympanum_of_Golden_Gate_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Tympanum (torana) of the Golden Gate\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tympanum_of_Golden_Gate_at_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Garuda_of_Golden_Door_in_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Garuda_of_Golden_Door_in_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prakat Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Garuda figure on the Golden Gate\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garuda_of_Golden_Door_in_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Detail_of_Golden_Gate_-_Durbar_Square_-_Bhaktapur_-_Nepal_%2813510264414%29.jpg/1280px-Detail_of_Golden_Gate_-_Durbar_Square_-_Bhaktapur_-_Nepal_%2813510264414%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Adam Jones from Kelowna, BC, Canada\", \"caption\": \"Detail of the gilt repousse work\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detail_of_Golden_Gate_-_Durbar_Square_-_Bhaktapur_-_Nepal_(13510264414).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"gate\", \"roof\": \"flat\", \"notes\": \"Gilt copper doorway set in a red brick wall, topped by a semicircular torana with Garuda and a many-armed goddess\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#c9a227\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#9c4a2a\"], \"features\": [\"golden-door\", \"toran\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [4, 1], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(4,'vatsala-durga-temple','Vatsala Durga Temple','वत्सला दुर्गा मन्दिर','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur','bhaktapur-durbar-square',27.672197,85.428771,'shikhara','Hindu','Vatsala (a form of Durga)',NULL,'17th–18th century (dated 1672–74 by local sources; present form linked to Bhupatindra Malla c. 1715); rebuilt after 2015','Malla','Stone shikhara temple with a pillared portico and guardian animals on the stairway',1,'Stone shikhara of the mother goddess Vatsala, fronted by the famous \"barking dog\" bell.','In front of you rises a pale stone shikhara, a tower-like temple quite different from the tiered pagodas around it. It is dedicated to Vatsala, the loving mother goddess, a form of Durga that people of Bhaktapur believed would shield the city from epidemics. Climb your eyes up from the stone elephants and lions on the steps to the carved portico and the slender spires. Sources disagree on its exact age: a local history credits Jagat Prakash Malla in 1672, while historians link its present form to King Bhupatindra Malla, around 1715. Now look for the large bell on the platform. Locals call it the barking dog bell, because dogs nearby are said to bark and whine when it rings. In April 2015 the earthquake brought this temple down completely. What you see now was rebuilt with traditional stone masonry methods by Bhaktapur\'s own craftsmen, with the reconstruction completed around 2020 to 2021.','Locals call the large bell on the temple platform the barking dog bell, because it is believed that whenever it rings, dogs in the neighbourhood begin to bark and whine. The bell is attributed to King Bhupatindra Malla. The goddess herself, Vatsala or Bacchala, is believed to shield Bhaktapur from epidemics, and some historians think the temple was remodelled around 1715 while a plague was spreading through the valley.','[\"Vatsala is a mother-goddess form of Durga believed to protect the city from epidemics.\", \"The bell before the temple is locally called the \\\"barking dog bell\\\".\", \"The temple collapsed in the April 2015 earthquake.\", \"It was rebuilt using traditional stone masonry methods, with work finishing around 2020–2021.\"]',NULL,NULL,1800,500,0,15,'The temple collapsed in the 25 April 2015 earthquake and was rebuilt by Bhaktapur Municipality using traditional methods (completion reported c. 2020–2021).','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Batsala_devi_temple_Bhaktapur.jpg/1280px-Batsala_devi_temple_Bhaktapur.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batsala_devi_temple_Bhaktapur.jpg','सरोज कुमार ढकाल · CC BY-SA 4.0','shikhara,hindu,malla,bhaktapur,unesco,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/discover/vatsala-durga-temple/\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/vatsala-durga-temple-taleju-bell-bhaktapur.html\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/211082585\"]','मातृदेवी वत्सलाको ढुङ्गाको शिखर मन्दिर, जसको अगाडि प्रसिद्ध ‘भुक्ने कुकुर’ घण्ट छ।','तपाईंको अगाडि फिक्का रङको ढुङ्गाको शिखर मन्दिर उभिएको छ। वरपरका तले पगोडाभन्दा यो निकै फरक, मीनारजस्तो देखिन्छ। यो मातृदेवी वत्सलाको मन्दिर हो। उनी दुर्गाको रूप हुन् र भक्तपुरका मानिस उनले सहरलाई महामारीबाट जोगाउँछिन् भन्ने विश्वास गर्थे। भर्‍याङका ढुङ्गाका हात्ती र सिंहदेखि सुरु गरेर कुँदिएको बरन्डा र सुन्दर चुचुरासम्म आँखा लगाउँदै जानुहोस्। यो कहिले बनेको हो भन्नेमा स्रोतहरू एकमत छैनन्। एउटा स्थानीय इतिहासले सन् १६७२ मा जगत प्रकाश मल्लले बनाएको भन्छ। इतिहासकारहरू भने अहिलेको रूप राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले करिब सन् १७१५ मा दिएको मान्छन्। अब चौतारीमा रहेको ठूलो घण्ट खोज्नुहोस्। स्थानीयले यसलाई ‘भुक्ने कुकुरको घण्ट’ भन्छन्, किनकि यो बज्दा नजिकका कुकुर भुक्छन् र कन्हाउँछन् भन्ने विश्वास छ। सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पले यो मन्दिर पूरै ढाल्यो। अहिले देखिने मन्दिर भक्तपुरकै शिल्पीहरूले परम्परागत ढुङ्गाको चिनाइ विधिले फेरि बनाएका हुन्। काम करिब सन् २०२० देखि २०२१ सम्ममा सकियो।','मन्दिरको चौतारीमा भएको ठूलो घण्टलाई स्थानीयले ‘भुक्ने कुकुरको घण्ट’ भन्छन्। यो बज्दा छिमेकका कुकुर भुक्न र कन्हाउन थाल्छन् भन्ने विश्वास छ। यो घण्ट राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले राखेको भनिन्छ। देवी वत्सला (बच्छला) ले भक्तपुरलाई महामारीबाट जोगाउँछिन् भन्ने विश्वास छ। केही इतिहासकार उपत्यकामा प्लेग फैलिइरहेको बेला करिब सन् १७१५ तिर मन्दिर नयाँ गरी बनाइएको मान्छन्।','[\"वत्सला दुर्गाको मातृदेवी रूप हुन्, जसले सहरलाई महामारीबाट जोगाउँछिन् भन्ने विश्वास छ।\", \"मन्दिरअगाडिको घण्टलाई स्थानीयले ‘भुक्ने कुकुरको घण्ट’ भन्छन्।\", \"सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पमा मन्दिर ढल्यो।\", \"यसलाई परम्परागत ढुङ्गाको चिनाइ विधिले फेरि बनाइयो। काम करिब सन् २०२०–२०२१ मा सकियो।\"]','सन् २०१५ अप्रिल २५ को भूकम्पमा मन्दिर ढल्यो। भक्तपुर नगरपालिकाले परम्परागत विधिले यसलाई फेरि बनायो (काम करिब सन् २०२०–२०२१ मा सकिएको बताइन्छ)।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Bhaktapur_Vatsala_Durga_Temple.JPG/1280px-Bhaktapur_Vatsala_Durga_Temple.JPG\", \"author\": \"Deepayan Sarkar\", \"caption\": \"Vatsala Durga Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_Vatsala_Durga_Temple.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Bhaktapur_Vatsala_Devi_Temple.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_Vatsala_Devi_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Swagat Raj Pyakurel\", \"caption\": \"Vatsala Devi Temple, Bhaktapur\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_Vatsala_Devi_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Bhaktapur-Vatsala_Mandir_am_Palastplatz-03-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Vatsala_Mandir_am_Palastplatz-03-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Vatsala Temple on the palace square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Vatsala_Mandir_am_Palastplatz-03-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Bhaktapur-Vatsala_Mandir_am_Palastplatz-01-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Vatsala_Mandir_am_Palastplatz-01-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Stone shikhara of Vatsala Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Vatsala_Mandir_am_Palastplatz-01-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Bhaktapur_Durbar_square_and_Big_bell.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_Durbar_square_and_Big_bell.jpg\", \"author\": \"सरोज कुमार ढकाल\", \"caption\": \"Vatsala Temple with the big bell in front\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_Durbar_square_and_Big_bell.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"stone-spire\", \"notes\": \"Pale stone shikhara with a pillared porch, animal guardians up the stairs and a big bell on two pillars in front\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#a8957a\", \"#c9a227\", \"#5a4a32\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"bell\", \"lion-statues\", \"guardian-pairs-on-stairs\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [8, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 3, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(5,'nyatapola-temple','Nyatapola Temple','न्यातपोल मन्दिर','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.671410,85.429373,'pagoda','Hindu','Siddhi Lakshmi',1702,'Built December 1701 – July 1702 under Bhupatindra Malla','Malla','Five-tiered Newar pagoda on a five-level stepped plinth lined with stone guardians',0,'Nepal\'s tallest temple: five roofs, five plinths and five pairs of stone guardians.','You are in Taumadhi Square, looking up at the tallest temple in Nepal. Nyatapola simply means five roofs, and it is one of the very few temples named for its shape rather than its deity. King Bhupatindra Malla raised it in just six months, from December 1701 to July 1702, with timber, bricks and stone donated from across the kingdom. Now climb the stairway with your eyes. Each landing has a pair of guardians, and each pair is said to be ten times stronger than the one below: two legendary wrestlers, then elephants, then lions, then griffins, and finally the goddesses Simhini and Vyaghrini. Inside sits the tantric goddess Siddhi Lakshmi, but her image is hidden from the public; only priests may enter. At about 33 metres, this temple has survived the great earthquakes of 1934 and 2015, a tribute to the engineering of Bhaktapur\'s craftsmen.','Legend says the fierce god Bhairava, whose temple stands beside this one, was causing havoc in the city. To restrain him the king appealed to the goddess, who took the form of Siddhi Lakshmi. A more powerful temple was raised for her right in front of Bhairava\'s shrine, and guardians were placed in pairs up its stairway, each pair ten times stronger than the one below. With the goddess towering over him, Bhairava was subdued and peace returned to Bhaktapur.','[\"It was built in about six months, from December 1701 to July 1702.\", \"At about 33 m it is the tallest temple in Nepal.\", \"The name means \'five roofs\'; it is one of only two five-tiered temples in the Kathmandu Valley.\", \"It survived the 1934 and 2015 earthquakes.\"]',NULL,NULL,1800,500,0,30,'The temple survived the April 2015 earthquake, as it had survived the 1934 earthquake.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Nyatapol_by_GP15.JPG/1280px-Nyatapol_by_GP15.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nyatapol_by_GP15.JPG','Ganesh Paudel · CC BY-SA 3.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,bhaktapur,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyatapola_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1513892\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/85470341\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/entry-fees-of-the-heritage-sites-in-nepal/\"]','नेपालको सबैभन्दा अग्लो मन्दिर: पाँच छाना, पाँच तला र पाँच जोडी ढुङ्गाका द्वारपाल।','तपाईं तौमढी चोकमा हुनुहुन्छ, नेपालकै सबैभन्दा अग्लो मन्दिरतिर हेर्दै। न्यातपोल भनेको नै ‘पाँच छाना’ हो। देवताको नामले होइन, आकारले नाम पाएका थोरै मन्दिरमध्ये यो एक हो। राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले राज्यभरिबाट दान आएका काठ, इँट र ढुङ्गाले यसलाई छ महिनामै बनाए, सन् १७०१ को डिसेम्बरदेखि १७०२ को जुलाईसम्म। अब आँखैले भर्‍याङ चढ्नुहोस्। हरेक तलामा एक जोडी द्वारपाल छन् र हरेक जोडी तल्लोभन्दा दश गुणा बलियो मानिन्छ। पहिले दुई पौराणिक पहलमान, त्यसपछि हात्ती, सिंह, ग्रिफिन र अन्त्यमा सिंहिनी र व्याघ्रिणी देवी। भित्र तान्त्रिक देवी सिद्धिलक्ष्मी छिन्, तर उनको मूर्ति सबैले देख्न पाउँदैनन्। पुजारीले मात्र भित्र जान पाउँछन्। करिब ३३ मिटर अग्लो यो मन्दिर सन् १९३४ र २०१५ का ठूला भूकम्पमा पनि टिक्यो। यो भक्तपुरका शिल्पीहरूको इन्जिनियरिङ सिपको प्रमाण हो।','किंवदन्ती अनुसार, यो मन्दिरको छेउमै मन्दिर भएका उग्र देवता भैरवले सहरमा उत्पात मच्चाएका थिए। उनलाई रोक्न राजाले देवीसँग प्रार्थना गरे र देवीले सिद्धिलक्ष्मीको रूप लिइन्। भैरवको मन्दिरकै अगाडि उनका लागि अझ शक्तिशाली मन्दिर बनाइयो र त्यसको भर्‍याङमा जोडी जोडी द्वारपाल राखिए, हरेक जोडी तल्लोभन्दा दश गुणा बलियो। देवी आफूमाथि उभिएपछि भैरव शान्त भए र भक्तपुरमा फेरि शान्ति आयो।','[\"यो करिब छ महिनामा बनेको थियो, सन् १७०१ को डिसेम्बरदेखि १७०२ को जुलाईसम्म।\", \"करिब ३३ मिटर अग्लो भएकाले यो नेपालको सबैभन्दा अग्लो मन्दिर हो।\", \"नामको अर्थ ‘पाँच छाना’ हो। काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाका दुईवटा मात्र पाँच तले मन्दिरमध्ये यो एक हो।\", \"यो सन् १९३४ र २०१५ का भूकम्पमा बाँचेको थियो।\"]','सन् १९३४ मा जस्तै सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पमा पनि यो मन्दिर बाँच्यो।','[{\"name\": \"Bisket Jatra\", \"note\": \"Bhaktapur\'s New Year festival; Bhairav\'s chariot is pulled around Taumadhi\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"बिस्केट जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"भक्तपुरको नयाँ वर्षको पर्व। भैरवको रथ तौमढी वरिपरि तानिन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Gai Jatra\", \"note\": \"Families who lost someone that year parade through the squares in costume\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"गाईजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"त्यस वर्ष आफन्त गुमाएका परिवारले भेषभूषा लगाएर चोकहरूमा घुम्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-01-1976-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-01-1976-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Nyatapola Temple in 1976\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-01-1976-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-22-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-22-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Nyatapola rising above Taumadhi Square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-22-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-13-Treppe-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-13-Treppe-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Stairway lined with guardian statues\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-13-Treppe-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-14-unten_Ringer_Jayamalla%2BPhatta-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-14-unten_Ringer_Jayamalla%2BPhatta-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Wrestlers Jayamalla and Phatta on the lowest step\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Nyatapola_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-14-unten_Ringer_Jayamalla%2BPhatta-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/A_lion_guarding_Nyatapola_Temple.jpg/1280px-A_lion_guarding_Nyatapola_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Dzeerve\", \"caption\": \"Stone lion guarding the stairs\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_lion_guarding_Nyatapola_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/5_storey_Temple_of_BKT_%40_gai_jatra.jpg/1280px-5_storey_Temple_of_BKT_%40_gai_jatra.jpg\", \"author\": \"Satya krishna prajapati\", \"caption\": \"Nyatapola during Gai Jatra\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5_storey_Temple_of_BKT_@_gai_jatra.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Tall five-roofed pagoda on five stepped brick platforms; one central stair with a guardian pair on each level\", \"tiers\": 5, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"guardian-pairs-on-stairs\", \"lion-statues\", \"elephant-statues\"], \"height_m\": 30, \"footprint_m\": [25, 25], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 5, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(6,'bhairavnath-temple','Bhairavnath Temple','भैरवनाथ मन्दिर','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.671094,85.429470,'pagoda','Hindu','Bhairava (Kasi Vishwanath / Aakash Bhairav)',NULL,'Single-storey temple from the 17th century or earlier; made multi-roofed by Bhupatindra Malla c. 1717–18; rebuilt after 1934','Malla','Three-roofed pagoda on a rectangular base in Taumadhi Square',0,'Rectangular three-roofed temple of fierce Bhairava, partner to Nyatapola in Taumadhi Square.','Turn to the broad, rectangular temple beside Nyatapola in Taumadhi Square. This is the home of Bhairava, the fearsome form of Shiva, known here as Kasi Vishwanath and Aakash Bhairav. Its shape is unusual: instead of a square tower it stretches wide, under three roofs. The temple grew over time. It began as a single-storey shrine, and King Bhupatindra Malla rebuilt it with more roofs around 1717 to 1718, the same king who raised Nyatapola next door. The 1934 earthquake brought it down and it was rebuilt in the same form; in 2015 it was damaged again and repaired. Every spring during Bisket Jatra, Bhaktapur\'s new-year festival, Bhairava\'s huge chariot is hauled through these streets. Now glance back at towering Nyatapola. Local legend says the goddess\'s temple was raised right in front of this one to keep Bhairava\'s temper in check.','Oral tradition says Bhairava of Varanasi once came to Bhaktapur in disguise to watch the Bisket Jatra festival. A tantric priest recognised him and bound him with a spell. As Bhairava sank into the earth to escape back to Varanasi, the priest seized his head and cut it off with a sword. That is why, people say, the head worshipped here does not match the body of Kasi Vishwanath, and it is kept hidden in a box inside the temple.','[\"The deity is Bhairava, a fierce form of Shiva, called Kasi Vishwanath and Aakash Bhairav.\", \"Bhupatindra Malla expanded it into a multi-roofed temple around 1717–1718.\", \"It collapsed in the 1934 earthquake and was rebuilt in the same form.\", \"Bhairava\'s chariot is pulled through the city during the Bisket Jatra festival.\"]',NULL,NULL,1800,500,0,15,'The April 2015 earthquake damaged the temple, which was later renovated.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Bhaktapur-Bhairava_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-02-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Bhairava_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-02-2007-gje.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Bhairava_Mandir_am_Taumadhi_Tole-02-2007-gje.jpg','Gerd Eichmann · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,bhaktapur,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://www.bhaktapur.com/discover/bhairavnath-temple/\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/bhaktapur/attractions/bhairabnath-temple/a/poi-sig/449939/357114\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q854699\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bisket_Jatra\"]','उग्र भैरवको आयताकार तीन तले मन्दिर, जो तौमढी चोकमा न्यातपोलको जोडी हो।','तौमढी चोकमा न्यातपोलको छेउमा रहेको फराकिलो आयताकार मन्दिरतिर फर्कनुहोस्। यो शिवको भयङ्कर रूप भैरवको घर हो। यहाँ उनलाई काशी विश्वनाथ र आकाश भैरव पनि भनिन्छ। यसको आकार अनौठो छ। वर्गाकार टावरको सट्टा यो तीन छानामुनि चौडा फैलिएको छ। मन्दिर समयसँगै बढेको हो। सुरुमा यो एक तले मन्दिर थियो। राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले सन् १७१७ देखि १७१८ तिर थप छाना जोडेर यसलाई फेरि बनाए। छेउको न्यातपोल पनि उनै राजाले बनाएका हुन्। सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पले यो ढल्यो र उही रूपमा फेरि बनाइयो। सन् २०१५ मा फेरि क्षति पुग्यो र मर्मत गरियो। हरेक वसन्तमा भक्तपुरको नयाँ वर्षको पर्व बिस्केट जात्रामा भैरवको विशाल रथ यिनै गल्लीमा तानिन्छ। अब अग्लो न्यातपोलतिर फर्केर हेर्नुहोस्। स्थानीय किंवदन्ती अनुसार भैरवको रिस शान्त राख्न देवीको मन्दिर ठीक यसको अगाडि बनाइएको हो।','मौखिक परम्परा अनुसार वाराणसीका भैरव एक पटक बिस्केट जात्रा हेर्न भेष बदलेर भक्तपुर आएका थिए। एक तान्त्रिक पुजारीले उनलाई चिने र मन्त्रले बाँधिदिए। वाराणसी फर्कन भैरव जमिनमा भासिँदै गर्दा पुजारीले उनको टाउको समातेर तरवारले काटिदिए। मानिसहरू भन्छन्, त्यसैले यहाँ पूजा गरिने टाउको काशी विश्वनाथको धडसँग मिल्दैन। त्यो टाउको मन्दिरभित्र बाकसमा लुकाएर राखिएको छ।','[\"देवता भैरव हुन्। उनी शिवको उग्र रूप हुन् र उनलाई काशी विश्वनाथ र आकाश भैरव भनिन्छ।\", \"भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले सन् १७१७–१७१८ तिर यसलाई धेरै छाना भएको मन्दिर बनाए।\", \"यो सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पमा ढल्यो र उही रूपमा फेरि बनाइयो।\", \"बिस्केट जात्रामा भैरवको रथ सहरभर तानिन्छ।\"]','सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पले मन्दिरमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो। पछि यसको मर्मत गरियो।','[{\"name\": \"Bisket Jatra\", \"note\": \"Bhaktapur\'s New Year festival; Bhairav\'s chariot is pulled around Taumadhi\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"बिस्केट जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"भक्तपुरको नयाँ वर्षको पर्व। भैरवको रथ तौमढी वरिपरि तानिन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Bhairab_Nath_Temple%2C_Bhaktapur.jpg/1280px-Bhairab_Nath_Temple%2C_Bhaktapur.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Bhairavnath Temple, Taumadhi Square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhairab_Nath_Temple,_Bhaktapur.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/1_Bhairavnath_Temple%2C_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square%2C_NEPAL_01.jpg/1280px-1_Bhairavnath_Temple%2C_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square%2C_NEPAL_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Bhairavnath Temple from the square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1_Bhairavnath_Temple,_Bhaktapur_Durbar_Square,_NEPAL_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Bhairav_Nath_Temple%2C_Bhaktapur_01.jpg/1280px-Bhairav_Nath_Temple%2C_Bhaktapur_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Facade of Bhairavnath Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhairav_Nath_Temple,_Bhaktapur_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Bhairabhnath_and_Bisket_Jatra.jpg/1280px-Bhairabhnath_and_Bisket_Jatra.jpg\", \"author\": \"Youbesh Dhaubhadel\", \"caption\": \"Bhairavnath Temple during Bisket Jatra\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhairabhnath_and_Bisket_Jatra.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Bhairava_Temple%2C_Bhatgaon_-_Oldfield_collection_%281852%29_-_BL_WD_3318.jpg/1280px-Bhairava_Temple%2C_Bhatgaon_-_Oldfield_collection_%281852%29_-_BL_WD_3318.jpg\", \"author\": \"Henry Ambrose Oldfield\", \"caption\": \"Bhairava Temple painted by H. A. Oldfield, 1852\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhairava_Temple,_Bhatgaon_-_Oldfield_collection_(1852)_-_BL_WD_3318.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Broad rectangular three-roofed pagoda with a gilded roof crest, beside Nyatapola on the same square\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"carved-windows\", \"lion-statues\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [14, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(7,'dattatreya-temple','Dattatreya Temple','दत्तात्रेय मन्दिर','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.673539,85.435359,'pagoda','Hindu','Dattatreya',NULL,'15th century under Yaksha Malla (1427 in popular sources; 1470 / NS 590 per a local history); storeys added 1495','Malla','Tiered Newar pagoda guarded by stone wrestlers, with a Garuda pillar in front',0,'A 15th-century pagoda to Dattatreya in Tachupal Square, guarded by two stone wrestlers.','Welcome to Tachupal Square in the eastern part of old Bhaktapur. The tall pagoda before you belongs to Dattatreya, a deity revered as a combined form of Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva. It is said to be the only temple dedicated to him in Nepal. King Yaksha Malla built it in the fifteenth century; popular guides give 1427, while a local history records 1470, with more storeys added by his son in 1495. Look at the entrance: two stone wrestlers stand guard, the same legendary pair you can see at Nyatapola. In front of the temple, a Garuda kneels on a tall pillar, hands joined toward the shrine. You may hear a famous tale that the whole temple was built from the wood of a single tree, just like Kathmandu\'s Kasthamandap. Historians say there is no proof, but it is a story every guide loves to tell. Around you, the old priests\' houses include the Pujari Math with its celebrated Peacock Window.','A popular story claims the entire Dattatreya Temple was built from the timber of a single enormous tree, the same tale told about Kasthamandap in Kathmandu. Local historians note there is no solid proof, but the legend endures as a way of expressing how grand the temple seemed to the people who first saw it rise above Tachupal Square in the fifteenth century.','[\"It is dedicated to Dattatreya, revered as a combined form of Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva.\", \"King Yaksha Malla built it in the 15th century; sources give 1427 or 1470.\", \"Stone statues of the wrestlers Jaimal and Patta guard the entrance, as at Nyatapola.\", \"A Garuda statue on a pillar faces the temple with hands joined in greeting.\"]',NULL,NULL,1800,500,0,20,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Datatreya_Temple_05.jpg/1280px-Datatreya_Temple_05.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Datatreya_Temple_05.jpg','Krish Dulal · CC BY-SA 3.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,bhaktapur,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://www.bhaktapur.com/discover/dattatraya-temple/\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/dattatreya-temple-bhaktapur-a-quiet-masterpiece-of-newar-craftsmanship\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/bhaktapur/guide-to-dattatreya-square.html\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/11365112169\"]','तचपाल चोकमा रहेको १५ औं शताब्दीको दत्तात्रेय मन्दिर, जसको प्रवेशद्वारमा दुई ढुङ्गाका पहलमान पहरा दिन्छन्।','पुरानो भक्तपुरको पूर्वी भागको तचपाल चोकमा तपाईंलाई स्वागत छ। अगाडि उभिएको अग्लो पगोडा दत्तात्रेयको मन्दिर हो। दत्तात्रेयलाई ब्रह्मा, विष्णु र शिवको संयुक्त रूप मानेर पूजा गरिन्छ। नेपालमा उनको मन्दिर यही एउटा मात्र हो भनिन्छ। राजा यक्ष मल्लले पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीमा यो बनाएका थिए। चर्चित पुस्तिकाहरूले सन् १४२७ भन्छन्, तर एउटा स्थानीय इतिहासमा सन् १४७० लेखिएको छ। उनका छोराले सन् १४९५ मा थप तला जोडेका थिए। प्रवेशद्वारमा हेर्नुहोस्। दुई ढुङ्गाका पहलमान पहरा दिइरहेका छन्, न्यातपोलमा देखिने त्यही पौराणिक जोडी। मन्दिरको अगाडि अग्लो स्तम्भमाथि गरुड हात जोडेर मन्दिरतिर घुँडा टेकेर बसेको छ। तपाईंले एउटा चर्चित कथा सुन्न सक्नुहुन्छ। काठमाडौँको कास्थमण्डपझैं यो सिङ्गो मन्दिर पनि एउटै रुखको काठले बनेको हो रे। इतिहासकारहरू यसको प्रमाण छैन भन्छन्, तर हरेक गाइडले सुनाउन मन पराउने कथा हो यो। वरिपरिका पुराना पुजारीका घरमध्ये प्रसिद्ध मयूर झ्याल भएको पुजारी मठ पनि छ।','एउटा चर्चित कथा अनुसार सिङ्गो दत्तात्रेय मन्दिर एउटै विशाल रुखको काठले बनेको हो। काठमाडौँको कास्थमण्डपबारे पनि यस्तै कथा सुनाइन्छ। स्थानीय इतिहासकारहरू यसको ठोस प्रमाण छैन भन्छन्। तैपनि पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीमा तचपाल चोकमाथि उठेको यो मन्दिर पहिलो पटक देख्नेहरूलाई कति भव्य लागेको थियो भन्ने बताउने कथाका रूपमा यो आजसम्म चलिआएको छ।','[\"यो दत्तात्रेयको मन्दिर हो। उनलाई ब्रह्मा, विष्णु र शिवको संयुक्त रूप मानेर पूजा गरिन्छ।\", \"राजा यक्ष मल्लले १५ औं शताब्दीमा यो बनाएका थिए। स्रोतहरूले सन् १४२७ वा १४७० भन्छन्।\", \"न्यातपोलमा जस्तै जयमल र पत्ता नामका पहलमानका ढुङ्गाका मूर्तिले प्रवेशद्वारको रक्षा गर्छन्।\", \"स्तम्भमाथिको गरुडको मूर्ति हात जोडेर अभिवादन गर्दै मन्दिरतिर फर्केको छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-01-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-01-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Dattatreya Temple on Tachupal Tole\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-01-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-04-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-04-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Dattatreya Temple, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-04-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-07-Garudasaeule-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-07-Garudasaeule-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Garuda pillar in front of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-07-Garudasaeule-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-12-Ringer_Jayamalla%2BPhatta-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-12-Ringer_Jayamalla%2BPhatta-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Stone wrestlers Jayamalla and Phatta\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-12-Ringer_Jayamalla%2BPhatta-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-09-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-09-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Dattatreya Temple and its square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Dattatreya_Mandir_am_Tacapala_Tole-09-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Three-roofed pagoda with a front porch, two stone wrestlers on the stairs and a Garuda on a pillar facing it\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"guardian-pairs-on-stairs\", \"garuda-pillar\", \"stone-pillar\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 3, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(8,'peacock-window','Peacock Window (Pujari Math)','मयूर झ्याल','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.673263,85.435578,'window','Hindu',NULL,NULL,'15th century (window); Pujari Math rebuilt 1763','Malla','Carved latticed wooden window (Mhaykha Jhya) centred on a fan-tailed peacock',0,'A 15th-century carved window with a fan-tailed peacock, the most famous window in Nepal.','Step into the narrow lane beside the Pujari Math, a former priests\' house off Tachupal Square, and look up at the wall. There it is: the Peacock Window, Mhaykha Jhya in Newar. At its centre a peacock spreads its fan-shaped tail, and around it the lattice is alive with smaller carved birds and ornament. This window is usually dated to the fifteenth century, which makes it one of the oldest and most celebrated examples of Newar woodcarving. The building it sits in was first built in the fifteenth century and rebuilt in 1763. German experts renovated it in 1979, and today it houses the National Woodworking Museum. In 2015 the earthquake damaged the building and the wall around the window had to be rebuilt, yet the peacock survived intact. Take a moment to imagine the carver, working the wood by hand more than five hundred years ago.',NULL,'[\"The Newar name is Mhaykha Jhya, meaning \\\"peacock window\\\".\", \"The window is generally dated to the 15th century.\", \"The Pujari Math was first built in the 15th century and rebuilt in 1763.\", \"The building now houses the National Woodworking Museum.\"]',NULL,NULL,1800,500,0,15,'The 2015 earthquake damaged the Pujari Math and the wall around the window was rebuilt, but the Peacock Window itself survived intact.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Peacock_Window%2C_Pujari_Math_%285241413125%29.jpg/1280px-Peacock_Window%2C_Pujari_Math_%285241413125%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peacock_Window,_Pujari_Math_(5241413125).jpg','Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa · CC BY-SA 2.0','window,hindu,malla,bhaktapur,palace,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newar_window\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pujarimath_Museum\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/points-of-interest/pujari-math/1432551\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q16917852\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Peacock_window,_Bhaktapur\"]','१५ औं शताब्दीको कुँदिएको झ्याल, जसमा पुच्छर फिजाएको मयूर छ। यो नेपालकै सबैभन्दा प्रसिद्ध झ्याल हो।','तचपाल चोकछेउको पुजारीहरूको पुरानो घर, पुजारी मठको छेउको साँघुरो गल्लीमा पस्नुहोस् र भित्तातिर हेर्नुहोस्। त्यही हो मयूर झ्याल, नेवारीमा ‘म्हय्खा झ्या’। बीचमा मयूरले पङ्खाजस्तो पुच्छर फिजाएको छ र वरपरको जालीमा कुँदिएका साना चरा र बुट्टा जीवन्त देखिन्छन्। यो झ्याल सामान्यतया पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीको मानिन्छ। त्यसैले यो नेवारी काष्ठकलाका सबैभन्दा पुराना र चर्चित नमुनामध्ये एक हो। यो भवन पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीमा पहिलो पटक बनेको थियो र सन् १७६३ मा फेरि बनाइयो। जर्मन विशेषज्ञहरूले सन् १९७९ मा यसको मर्मत गरे। अहिले यसमा राष्ट्रिय काष्ठकला संग्रहालय छ। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले भवनमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो र झ्यालवरिपरिको भित्ता फेरि बनाउनुपर्‍यो, तर मयूर भने सग्लै रह्यो। पाँच सय वर्षभन्दा पहिले हातैले काठ कुँद्ने कलाकारको कल्पना गर्दै केही बेर उभिनुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"नेवारी नाम ‘म्हय्खा झ्या’ हो, जसको अर्थ ‘मयूर झ्याल’ हो।\", \"झ्याल सामान्यतया १५ औं शताब्दीको मानिन्छ।\", \"पुजारी मठ १५ औं शताब्दीमा पहिलो पटक बनेको थियो र सन् १७६३ मा फेरि बनाइयो।\", \"अहिले यो भवनमा राष्ट्रिय काष्ठकला संग्रहालय छ।\"]','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले पुजारी मठमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो र झ्यालवरिपरिको भित्ता फेरि बनाइयो, तर मयूर झ्याल आफैँ सग्लै रह्यो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-04-Pfauenfenster-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-04-Pfauenfenster-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The carved peacock window, Pujari Math\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-04-Pfauenfenster-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-02-Pfauenfenster-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-02-Pfauenfenster-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Peacock window, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-02-Pfauenfenster-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Peacock_window_%E2%80%93_Bhaktapur_%E2%80%93_01.jpg/1280px-Peacock_window_%E2%80%93_Bhaktapur_%E2%80%93_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Maesi64\", \"caption\": \"Peacock window close-up\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peacock_window_%E2%80%93_Bhaktapur_%E2%80%93_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Puhari_Math%2C_Peacock_Window_and_Shop_%285242008704%29.jpg/1280px-Puhari_Math%2C_Peacock_Window_and_Shop_%285242008704%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa\", \"caption\": \"Pujari Math with the peacock window\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puhari_Math,_Peacock_Window_and_Shop_(5242008704).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-12-Pfauenfenster-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-12-Pfauenfenster-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Peacock window wall after the 2015 earthquake\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur-Pujari_Math-12-Pfauenfenster-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Small dark latticed window with a carved peacock spreading its tail, set in a red brick monastery wall on a lane\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#3e2a1c\", \"#9c4a2a\"], \"features\": [\"carved-windows\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [20, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"city-street\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(9,'siddha-pokhari','Siddha Pokhari','सिद्ध पोखरी','Bhaktapur','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.671933,85.420419,'pond','Secular',NULL,NULL,'Traditionally 15th century under Yaksha Malla; some local historians argue for older origins','Malla','Large rectangular man-made reservoir pond',0,'Bhaktapur\'s biggest man-made pond, Ta Pukhu, wrapped in a legend of a trapped serpent.','Pause at the edge of this long, still pond on the western side of old Bhaktapur. This is Siddha Pokhari, called Ta Pukhu in Newar, which simply means the big pond. About 171 metres long, 73 metres wide and around three metres deep, it is the largest man-made pond in the city. Tradition credits King Yaksha Malla with building it in the fifteenth century, though some local historians argue its origins are even older. For centuries ponds like this stored water for the city, supported farming and gave people a place to gather. Now look into the water and think of the tale every child here knows: a powerful serpent spirit once ruled these depths, and a sorcerer who dared to fight it never came back as a man. That is why, the story goes, people from Thimi traditionally kept away from this pond.','A powerful Naga, a serpent spirit, was said to guard this pond. A tantric practitioner turned himself into a serpent to fight it underwater, first asking a friend from Thimi to scatter enchanted rice afterwards to restore his human form. But the friend, terrified by the two serpents thrashing in the water, ran away. The tantric stayed a serpent forever, and people from Thimi long avoided the pond, fearing revenge.','[\"Its Newar name, Ta Pukhu, means \\\"big pond\\\".\", \"It measures about 171 m by 73 m and is about 3 m deep.\", \"It is the largest man-made pond in Bhaktapur.\", \"Tradition credits King Yaksha Malla (15th century) with building it.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,20,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sidhapokhari_of_Bhaktapur.jpg/1280px-Sidhapokhari_of_Bhaktapur.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sidhapokhari_of_Bhaktapur.jpg','Maneesa stha · CC BY-SA 4.0','pond,secular,malla,bhaktapur,legend,water,bagmati','[\"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/the-legend-of-siddha-pokhari-in-bhaktapur\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/forgotten-history-of-siddha-pokhari/\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19712957\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/38605233\"]','भक्तपुरको सबैभन्दा ठूलो मानव निर्मित पोखरी, ता पुखु, जसको वरिपरि सर्पमा फसेको मानिसको किंवदन्ती छ।','पुरानो भक्तपुरको पश्चिम भागको यो लामो, शान्त पोखरीको किनारमा केही बेर रोकिनुहोस्। यो सिद्ध पोखरी हो, नेवारीमा ‘ता पुखु’ भनिने, जसको अर्थ नै ठूलो पोखरी हो। यो करिब १७१ मिटर लामो, ७३ मिटर चौडा र झण्डै तीन मिटर गहिरो छ। यो सहरको सबैभन्दा ठूलो मानव निर्मित पोखरी हो। परम्परा अनुसार राजा यक्ष मल्लले पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीमा यो बनाएका हुन्। केही स्थानीय इतिहासकार भने यो अझ पुरानो हो भन्छन्। सयौँ वर्षसम्म यस्ता पोखरीले सहरका लागि पानी जम्मा गरे, खेतीपातीमा सघाए र मानिसलाई भेट्ने ठाउँ दिए। अब पानीमा हेर्नुहोस् र यहाँका हरेक बच्चाले जानेको कथा सम्झनुहोस्। एउटा शक्तिशाली नाग आत्माले यही गहिराइमा राज गर्थ्यो। त्यससँग लड्न आँट गर्ने एक तान्त्रिक फेरि मानिस भएर फर्किएनन्। त्यसैले कथा अनुसार ठिमीका मानिस परम्परादेखि यो पोखरीबाट टाढै बस्थे।','यो पोखरीको रक्षा एउटा शक्तिशाली नाग, अर्थात् सर्प आत्माले गर्थ्यो भनिन्छ। एक तान्त्रिकले पानीभित्र त्यससँग लड्न आफैँ सर्पको रूप लिए। सुरुमै उनले ठिमीका एक साथीलाई पछि मन्त्र पढेको चामल छर्न भनेका थिए, ताकि आफू फेरि मानिस बन्न सकून्। तर पानीमा छटपटाइरहेका दुई सर्प देखेर डराएका ती साथी भागे। तान्त्रिक सधैँका लागि सर्प नै रहे। बदलाको डरले ठिमीका मानिस लामो समयसम्म यो पोखरीबाट टाढा बसे।','[\"यसको नेवारी नाम ‘ता पुखु’ को अर्थ ‘ठूलो पोखरी’ हो।\", \"यो करिब १७१ मिटर लामो, ७३ मिटर चौडा र करिब ३ मिटर गहिरो छ।\", \"यो भक्तपुरको सबैभन्दा ठूलो मानव निर्मित पोखरी हो।\", \"परम्परा अनुसार राजा यक्ष मल्ल (पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दी) ले यो बनाएका थिए।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Bhaktapur_shiddapokhari.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_shiddapokhari.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rabinphaiju\", \"caption\": \"Siddha Pokhari, Bhaktapur\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_shiddapokhari.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Bhaktapur_20180919_155238.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_20180919_155238.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ricky Partel\", \"caption\": \"Water and banks of Siddha Pokhari\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_20180919_155238.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Bhaktapur_20180919_155943.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_20180919_155943.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ricky Partel\", \"caption\": \"Siddha Pokhari, 2018\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_20180919_155943.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Bhaktapur_20180919_160132.jpg/1280px-Bhaktapur_20180919_160132.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ricky Partel\", \"caption\": \"Walkway around Siddha Pokhari\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaktapur_20180919_160132.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/A_Historical_Tree_%28Peepal%29_2.jpg\", \"author\": \"Punya\", \"caption\": \"Historic peepal tree at Siddha Pokhari\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Historical_Tree_(Peepal)_2.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pond\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Long rectangular walled pond with a walkway around it and small shrines and trees along its edges\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#4a6b5a\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#6b8e3a\"], \"features\": [\"ghat-steps\", \"sacred-tree\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [171, 73], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"pond\", \"city-street\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(10,'changu-narayan-temple','Changu Narayan Temple','चाँगुनारायण मन्दिर','Changunarayan','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.716347,85.427897,'pagoda','Hindu','Vishnu (Garuda Narayan)',1702,'Founded c. 4th century (Licchavi); present temple rebuilt 1702 after a fire','Licchavi','Two-tiered Newar pagoda with gilded doors and struts carved with the ten avatars of Vishnu',1,'One of Nepal\'s oldest Hindu temples, a hilltop Vishnu shrine with a pillar inscription from 464 AD.','You have climbed to the hilltop of Changu, once called Dolagiri, above the Manohara River. This is Changu Narayan, one of the oldest Hindu temples in Nepal, honouring Lord Vishnu. Its origins go back to around the fourth century, and the two-roofed temple you see was rebuilt in 1702 after a fire. Walk to the pillar near the entrance. It carries an inscription of the Licchavi king Manadeva dated 464 AD, one of the oldest inscriptions in the country. Now look for the stone Vishnu riding on Garuda: this seventh-century sculpture is pictured on Nepal\'s ten-rupee banknote. Study the roof struts and you will find the ten incarnations of Vishnu carved in wood, while pairs of lions, griffins and elephants guard the four doorways. Only the priest may see the main image inside. Since 1979 the temple has been part of the Kathmandu Valley World Heritage Site, and it was badly damaged in 2015.','A Brahmin named Sudarshan noticed his sacred cow returning without milk. Hiding by a champak tree, he saw a man step out of the tree and drink the milk. Furious, he struck the stranger with his sword, only to see him reveal himself as Vishnu. Vishnu told the grieving Brahmin the beheading was fated by an ancient curse, and promised to dwell on that hill forever, asking to be worshipped there. So began Changu Narayan.','[\"It is considered one of the oldest Hindu temples in Nepal, dating back to about the 4th century.\", \"A pillar inscription of King Manadeva dated 464 AD stands in the courtyard.\", \"A 7th-century sculpture of Vishnu on Garuda here appears on Nepal\'s 10-rupee banknote.\", \"The temple is one of seven monument zones of the Kathmandu Valley World Heritage Site (1979).\"]',NULL,NULL,400,300,0,60,'The temple was badly damaged in the April 2015 earthquake and restored over several years with heritage specialists and local craftspeople.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-12-ost-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-12-ost-2013-gje.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-12-ost-2013-gje.jpg','Gerd Eichmann · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,licchavi,changunarayan,unesco,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changu_Narayan_Temple\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121/\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1062150\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/186264410\", \"https://english.ratopati.com/story/40184\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/nepal/inspired-by-nepal-uk-architect-rebuilds-ancient-changu-narayan/\"]','नेपालका सबैभन्दा पुराना हिन्दू मन्दिरमध्ये एक, ४६४ ई. को स्तम्भलेख भएको डाँडामाथिको विष्णु मन्दिर।','तपाईं मनोहरा नदीमाथिको चाँगु डाँडामा पुग्नुभएको छ। पहिले यसलाई डोलागिरि भनिन्थ्यो। यो चाँगुनारायण हो, भगवान् विष्णुको मन्दिर र नेपालका सबैभन्दा पुराना हिन्दू मन्दिरमध्ये एक। यसको सुरुवात करिब चौथो शताब्दीतिर भएको हो। अहिले देखिने दुई छाने मन्दिर आगलागीपछि सन् १७०२ मा फेरि बनाइएको हो। प्रवेशद्वारनजिकको स्तम्भमा जानुहोस्। त्यसमा लिच्छवि राजा मानदेवको ४६४ ई. को अभिलेख छ। यो देशकै सबैभन्दा पुराना अभिलेखमध्ये एक हो। अब गरुडमाथि बसेका विष्णुको ढुङ्गाको मूर्ति खोज्नुहोस्। सातौँ शताब्दीको यो मूर्ति नेपालको दस रुपैयाँको नोटमा छापिएको छ। छानाका टेकाहरू ध्यान दिएर हेर्नुभयो भने विष्णुका दश अवतार काठमा कुँदिएका देख्नुहुन्छ। चारै ढोकामा सिंह, ग्रिफिन र हात्तीका जोडीले पहरा दिन्छन्। भित्रको मुख्य मूर्ति पुजारीले मात्र देख्न पाउँछन्। सन् १९७९ देखि यो मन्दिर काठमाडौँ उपत्यका विश्व सम्पदा स्थलको भाग हो। सन् २०१५ मा यसमा ठूलो क्षति पुगेको थियो।','सुदर्शन नामका एक ब्राह्मणले आफ्नी पवित्र गाई दूध नदिईकन फर्कने गरेको देखे। चम्पाको रूखनजिक लुकेर बस्दा उनले रूखबाट एक जना मानिस निस्केर दूध पिएको देखे। रिसले उनले त्यो अपरिचितलाई तरवारले हाने, तर ती मानिसले आफू विष्णु हुँ भनेर देखाए। विष्णुले शोकमा डुबेका ब्राह्मणलाई भने, शिर काटिनु पुरानो श्रापको नियति थियो। उनले सधैँ त्यही डाँडामा बस्ने वचन दिए र त्यहीँ आफ्नो पूजा गर्न भने। यसरी चाँगुनारायणको सुरुवात भयो।','[\"यो नेपालका सबैभन्दा पुराना हिन्दू मन्दिरमध्ये एक मानिन्छ। यो करिब चौथो शताब्दीको हो।\", \"आँगनमा राजा मानदेवको ४६४ ई. को स्तम्भलेख छ।\", \"यहाँको गरुडमाथि विष्णुको सातौँ शताब्दीको मूर्ति नेपालको १० रुपैयाँको नोटमा छापिएको छ।\", \"यो मन्दिर काठमाडौँ उपत्यका विश्व सम्पदा स्थल (१९७९) का सात सम्पदा क्षेत्रमध्ये एक हो।\"]','सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पमा मन्दिरमा ठूलो क्षति पुगेको थियो। सम्पदा विशेषज्ञ र स्थानीय शिल्पीहरूको सहयोगमा धेरै वर्षमा यसलाई फेरि बनाइयो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-02-nordost-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-02-nordost-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Changu Narayan Temple from the northeast\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-02-nordost-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-18-ost-Dachstreben-2014-gje.jpg/1280px-Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-18-ost-Dachstreben-2014-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Carved roof struts on the east side\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-18-ost-Dachstreben-2014-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-52-sued-Portal-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-52-sued-Portal-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Gilded south portal\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-52-sued-Portal-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-56-sued-Elefanten-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-56-sued-Elefanten-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Stone elephants at the south entrance\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Changu_Narayan-Garuda_Narayana-56-sued-Elefanten-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Changu_Narayan-Manadeva-Saeule-06-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Changu_Narayan-Manadeva-Saeule-06-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Pillar of King Manadeva (464 AD)\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Changu_Narayan-Manadeva-Saeule-06-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Two-roofed pagoda with gilded doors and densely carved struts in a hilltop courtyard, Garuda kneeling in front\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"golden-door\", \"carved-struts\", \"garuda-pillar\", \"stone-pillar\", \"elephant-statues\", \"lion-statues\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"hilltop\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(11,'dakshinkali-temple','Dakshinkali Temple','दक्षिणकाली मन्दिर','Dakshinkali','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.605258,85.263489,'courtyard','Hindu','Dakshinkali (Kali)',NULL,'Traditionally 17th century, attributed to King Pratap Malla of Kathmandu','Malla','Shrine compound; the sanctum of the goddess sits under a gilded canopy',0,'The valley\'s most famous Kali shrine, near Pharping, known for sacrifices on Tuesdays and Saturdays.','You have travelled to the southern edge of the Kathmandu Valley, about a kilometre beyond Pharping village, to one of Nepal\'s most important shrines to the goddess Kali. Dakshin means south, and this is Kali of the south. Tradition says King Pratap Malla of Kathmandu built the shrine in the seventeenth century after the goddess appeared to him in a dream. Dakshin Kali is typically shown with her right foot on Shiva\'s chest, and her sanctum here sits beneath a gilded canopy. Come on a Tuesday or a Saturday and you will see long queues of devotees carrying offerings, including cockerels and uncastrated male goats for animal sacrifice, the main form of worship here. The crowds swell even more during the Dashain festival. If sacrifice is hard to watch, you can observe respectfully from a distance. The area is also a popular hiking destination.','Tradition holds that the goddess Kali appeared to King Pratap Malla of Kathmandu in a dream and told him to build a shrine for her in the forest at the southern edge of the valley. The king obeyed, and the shrine of Dakshinkali, the Kali of the south, has drawn worshippers ever since. Another explanation of the name links it to Yama, lord of death, who lives in the south and is said to tremble at Kali\'s name.','[\"The temple is dedicated to the goddess Kali in her Dakshinkali form.\", \"Animal sacrifices of cockerels and uncastrated male goats are the main form of worship.\", \"Tuesdays and Saturdays are the busiest days, along with the Dashain festival.\", \"It lies about 1 km south of Pharping, around 22 km from Kathmandu.\"]',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,60,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Dakshin_Kali_main_Temple.JPG/1280px-Dakshin_Kali_main_Temple.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dakshin_Kali_main_Temple.JPG','Ashim nep · CC BY-SA 4.0','courtyard,hindu,malla,dakshinkali,legend,palace,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakshinkali_Temple\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/360060921\", \"https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/dakshinkali-temple\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/travel/pilgrimage-sites/the-goddess-of-the-south-dakshin-kali\"]','उपत्यकाको सबैभन्दा प्रसिद्ध काली मन्दिर, फर्पिङनजिक। मङ्गलबार र शनिबार हुने बलिका लागि चर्चित।','तपाईं काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाको दक्षिणी छेउ, फर्पिङ गाउँभन्दा करिब एक किलोमिटर पर, देवी कालीको नेपालकै सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण मन्दिरमध्ये एउटामा आइपुग्नुभएको छ। दक्षिण भनेको दक्षिण दिशा हो, त्यसैले यी दक्षिणकी काली हुन्। परम्परा अनुसार काठमाडौँका राजा प्रताप मल्लले सत्रौँ शताब्दीमा देवी सपनामा देखा परेपछि यो मन्दिर बनाएका थिए। दक्षिणकालीलाई प्रायः दाहिने खुट्टा शिवको छातीमा राखेको रूपमा देखाइन्छ। यहाँको गर्भगृह सुनौलो छत्रमुनि छ। मङ्गलबार वा शनिबार आउनुभयो भने भाले कुखुरा र बोका जस्ता भेटी बोकेका भक्तजनको लामो लाइन देख्नुहुन्छ। पशुबलि नै यहाँको पूजाको मुख्य तरिका हो। दशैँमा भीड अझै बढ्छ। बलि हेर्न गाह्रो लाग्छ भने टाढाबाट आदरपूर्वक हेर्न सक्नुहुन्छ। यो क्षेत्र हाइकिङका लागि पनि लोकप्रिय छ।','परम्परा अनुसार देवी कालीले काठमाडौँका राजा प्रताप मल्लको सपनामा देखा परेर उपत्यकाको दक्षिणी छेउको जङ्गलमा आफ्नो मन्दिर बनाउन भनिन्। राजाले आज्ञा मानेर मन्दिर बनाए र त्यसपछि दक्षिणकाली, अर्थात् दक्षिणकी काली, को मन्दिरमा भक्तजन आइरहेकै छन्। नामको अर्को व्याख्याले यसलाई दक्षिणमा बस्ने मृत्युका देवता यमसँग जोड्छ। कालीको नाम सुन्दा यम पनि थरथर काम्छन् भनिन्छ।','[\"यो मन्दिर दक्षिणकाली रूपकी देवी कालीलाई समर्पित छ।\", \"भाले कुखुरा र बोकाको पशुबलि यहाँको पूजाको मुख्य तरिका हो।\", \"मङ्गलबार र शनिबार सबैभन्दा व्यस्त दिन हुन्। दशैँ पनि त्यस्तै व्यस्त हुन्छ।\", \"यो फर्पिङको करिब १ किमी दक्षिणमा र काठमाडौँबाट करिब २२ किमी टाढा छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Main Durga festival; Taleju shrines and Durga temples draw worship and offerings\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दुर्गाको मुख्य चाड। तलेजुका मन्दिर र दुर्गा मन्दिरमा पूजा र चढावा चढाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Dakshinkali-Opferschrein-00a-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Dakshinkali-Opferschrein-00a-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Dakshinkali shrine, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dakshinkali-Opferschrein-00a-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Dakshinkali-Opferschrein-02-gje.jpg/1280px-Dakshinkali-Opferschrein-02-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Sacrificial shrine of Dakshinkali\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dakshinkali-Opferschrein-02-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Dakshin_Kali_Temple_Panorama.jpg/1280px-Dakshin_Kali_Temple_Panorama.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ashim nep\", \"caption\": \"Panorama of the Dakshinkali temple area\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dakshin_Kali_Temple_Panorama.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2009-03_Dakshinkali_04.jpg/1280px-2009-03_Dakshinkali_04.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ralf Lotys (Sicherlich)\", \"caption\": \"Dakshinkali, 2009\", \"license\": \"CC BY 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2009-03_Dakshinkali_04.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Dakshinkali-Umgebung-02-Terrassen-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Dakshinkali-Umgebung-02-Terrassen-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Terraced hillsides around Dakshinkali\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dakshinkali-Umgebung-02-Terrassen-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Open shrine yard in a wooded gorge where two streams meet; the goddess sits under a small gilded canopy\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#c9a227\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#9c8a6e\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"bell\", \"flags-red\", \"prayer-flags\", \"idol-visible\", \"ghat-steps\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [15, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"forest\", \"river\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(12,'adinath-lokeshwar-chobhar','Adinath Lokeshwar Temple, Chobhar','आदिनाथ मन्दिर','Kirtipur','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.665779,85.291395,'pagoda','Both','Adinath Lokeshwar (Anandadi Lokeshwar)',1640,'Built 15th century; rebuilt 1640','Malla','Newar pagoda temple whose walls are hung with metal pots, pans and utensils',0,'The \"pots and pans\" temple of Chobhar, sacred to both Hindus and Buddhists.','You are on the hilltop of Chobhar, at the edge of Kirtipur, where the Bagmati River slips out of the Kathmandu Valley through a narrow gorge. The pagoda in front of you honours Adinath Lokeshwar, also called Anandadi Lokeshwar. Buddhists see him as one of the four principal Lokeshwar bodhisattvas of the valley; Hindus count him among the four Matsyendranaths. The temple was built in the fifteenth century and rebuilt in 1640. Now look closely at the walls. They are hung with metal pots, pans and household utensils, which is why visitors call it the pots and pans temple. Accounts differ on how the custom began, but all link it to the welfare of loved ones after death. This hill is also tied to the valley\'s creation story: Manjushri is said to have cut the hills here, draining the ancient lake that once filled the valley so people could settle.','Long ago the Kathmandu Valley was a lake. The bodhisattva Manjushri came and cut the rim of the hills near Chobhar, letting the water drain away. The deity of the hill protested at being cut, but Manjushri promised that a great civilisation would grow in the drained valley and that a Lokeshwar would one day make his home on this very hill. Ages later, an image of Adinath was rescued from a river and enshrined here as Anandadi Lokeshwar.','[\"The temple is sacred to both Hindus and Buddhists.\", \"It was built in the 15th century and rebuilt in 1640.\", \"Visitors call it the \\\"pots and pans\\\" temple because of the utensils fixed to its walls.\", \"Adinath is one of the four principal Lokeshwars of the valley, also counted as a Matsyendranath.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-04-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-04-2007-gje.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-04-2007-gje.jpg','Gerd Eichmann · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,both,malla,kirtipur,hindu,buddhist,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adinath_Lokeshwar\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1818580586\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q16058104\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Adinath_Lokeshwar_Temple\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chobhar\"]','चोभारको ‘भाँडाकुँडा’ मन्दिर, हिन्दू र बौद्ध दुवैका लागि पवित्र।','तपाईं कीर्तिपुरको छेउको चोभारको डाँडामा हुनुहुन्छ, जहाँ बागमती नदी साँघुरो खोँचबाट काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाबाट बाहिर निस्कन्छ। अगाडिको पगोडा आदिनाथ लोकेश्वरको हो, जसलाई आनन्दादि लोकेश्वर पनि भनिन्छ। बौद्धहरू उनलाई उपत्यकाका चार प्रमुख लोकेश्वर बोधिसत्वमध्ये एक मान्छन्। हिन्दूहरू उनलाई चार मत्स्येन्द्रनाथमध्ये एक गन्छन्। मन्दिर पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीमा बनेको थियो र सन् १६४० मा फेरि बनाइयो। अब भित्ताहरू नजिकबाट हेर्नुहोस्। तिनमा धातुका भाँडा, कराही र घरका सामान झुन्ड्याइएका छन्। त्यसैले आगन्तुकले यसलाई भाँडाकुँडा मन्दिर भन्छन्। यो चलन कसरी सुरु भयो भन्नेमा कथा फरक फरक छन्, तर सबैले यसलाई मरेपछि प्रियजनको भलाइसँग जोड्छन्। यो डाँडा उपत्यकाको सृष्टिको कथासँग पनि जोडिएको छ। मञ्जुश्रीले यहाँ डाँडा काटेर उपत्यका भरिएको पुरानो तालको पानी बगाइदिए, ताकि मानिस बस्न सकून् भनिन्छ।','धेरै पहिले काठमाडौँ उपत्यका ताल थियो। बोधिसत्व मञ्जुश्री आएर चोभारनजिकको डाँडाको किनारा काटिदिए र पानी बगेर गयो। डाँडाका देवताले आफू काटिएकोमा विरोध गरे। तर मञ्जुश्रीले वचन दिए, पानी बगेपछि उपत्यकामा ठूलो सभ्यता फक्रिन्छ र एक दिन एक लोकेश्वरले यही डाँडामा बास गर्नेछन्। धेरै युगपछि नदीबाट उद्धार गरिएको आदिनाथको मूर्ति यहाँ आनन्दादि लोकेश्वरका रूपमा स्थापना गरियो।','[\"मन्दिर हिन्दू र बौद्ध दुवैका लागि पवित्र छ।\", \"यो पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीमा बनेको थियो र सन् १६४० मा फेरि बनाइयो।\", \"भित्तामा टाँसिएका भाँडाकुँडाका कारण आगन्तुकले यसलाई ‘भाँडाकुँडा’ मन्दिर भन्छन्।\", \"आदिनाथ उपत्यकाका चार प्रमुख लोकेश्वरमध्ये एक हुन् र उनलाई मत्स्येन्द्रनाथका रूपमा पनि गनिन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Adinath_Temple_Chovar_Lalitpur.jpg/1280px-Adinath_Temple_Chovar_Lalitpur.jpg\", \"author\": \"Dinesh 2016\", \"caption\": \"Adinath Temple, Chobhar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adinath_Temple_Chovar_Lalitpur.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-06-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-06-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Adinath Lokeshwar Temple, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-06-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-08-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-08-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Temple courtyard at Chobhar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-08-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-14-Donnerkeil-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-14-Donnerkeil-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Vajra (thunderbolt) in front of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chobhar-Adinath_Lokeshwar-14-Donnerkeil-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Adinath_temple_of_Chobar.jpg/1280px-Adinath_temple_of_Chobar.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bipinpraja\", \"caption\": \"Adinath temple of Chobhar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adinath_temple_of_Chobar.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Three-roofed pagoda on Chobhar hill with a stone shikhara chaitya before it; walls hung with metal pots and pans, prayer wheels at the sides\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#b0a090\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"bell\", \"chaityas\", \"prayer-wheels\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [10, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"brick-courtyard\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(13,'gorkha-durbar','Gorkha Durbar','गोरखा दरबार','Gorkha','Gandaki','Gorkha',NULL,28.004400,84.628900,'palace','Hindu','Gorakhkali and Kalika (temples within the palace); Gorakhnath (cave shrine)',NULL,'Built by King Ram Shah of Gorkha; Wikipedia dates it to the 16th century while other sources place Ram Shah\'s reign in the 17th century. The Kalika temple inside is dated to the 17th century.','Shah (Kingdom of Gorkha)','Fortified hilltop palace in Newar style, built mainly of brick, stone and timber. Walls are about three feet thick, floors rest on projecting wooden beams, and the wings rise over several levels with carved windows and struts. The Kalika temple has wood carvings of birds, animals and deities.',0,'Hilltop fortress-palace of the Shah kings of Gorkha and birthplace of Prithvi Narayan Shah, unifier of Nepal.','Catch your breath: you have climbed to a ridge about a thousand metres high, and the fortified palace in front of you is where modern Nepal began. King Ram Shah of Gorkha built this durbar, and in 1723 Prithvi Narayan Shah was born here, in the part called Dhuni Pati. From these walls, some three feet thick, he set out on the campaigns that unified Nepal. Look at the carved windows and the timber beams that carry the floors; Newar craftsmen from the valley shaped them. Inside the compound stand the temples of Kalika and Gorakhkali, and nearby is the cave where the yogi Gorakhnath is said to have meditated, which draws a fair every Baisakh Purnima. To the south burns the eternal flame, kept alight since unification. Now turn north. On a clear day Manaslu, Himalchuli, Annapurna and Ganesh Himal line the horizon. The 2015 earthquake damaged the palace, and restoration work by the Department of Archaeology began in November 2017.','The cave below the palace is believed to be the place where the yogi Gorakhnath, a disciple of Matsyendranath, sheltered and meditated; the Gorkha kingdom and the Gorkhali people take their name from him.','[\"Prithvi Narayan Shah, who began the unification of Nepal, was born in the palace in 1723.\", \"The palace sits on a hilltop at about 1,000 m, roughly an hour\'s walk from Gorkha bazaar.\", \"Its walls are about three feet thick and its floors are carried on extended wooden beams.\", \"UNESCO has listed \'The medieval palace complex of Gorkha\' on Nepal\'s Tentative List since 1996.\", \"Reconstruction after the 2015 earthquake began on 15 November 2017 under the Department of Archaeology.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,120,'The April 2015 earthquake partially damaged the palace. Reconstruction by the Department of Archaeology started on 15 November 2017 and was still ongoing in 2022.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Gorkha_Palace_2026_08.jpg/1280px-Gorkha_Palace_2026_08.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorkha_Palace_2026_08.jpg','Sonika Aryal · CC BY-SA 4.0','palace,hindu,shah (kingdom of gorkha),gorkha,legend,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gorkha_Palace\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q66133854\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/tentativelists/842/\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Gorkha_Palace\"]','गोरखाका शाह राजाहरूको डाँडामाथिको किल्लाजस्तो दरबार, र नेपाल एकीकरण गर्ने पृथ्वीनारायण शाहको जन्मस्थान।','एकछिन सास फेर्नुहोस्। तपाईं करिब एक हजार मिटर अग्लो डाँडामा पुग्नुभएको छ, र अगाडिको यो किल्लाजस्तो दरबारबाटै आधुनिक नेपालको सुरुवात भएको हो। गोरखाका राजा राम शाहले यो दरबार बनाए। सन् 1723 मा यहीँ, धुनीपाटी भनिने भागमा पृथ्वीनारायण शाहको जन्म भयो। करिब तीन फिट बाक्लो यिनै पर्खालबाट उनी नेपाल एकीकरणको अभियानमा निस्किए। कुँदिएका झ्याल र भुइँ थाम्ने काठका धरन हेर्नुहोस्; ती उपत्यकाका नेवार शिल्पीले बनाएका हुन्। परिसरभित्र कालिका र गोरखकालीका मन्दिर छन्। नजिकै योगी गोरखनाथले ध्यान गरेको भनिने गुफा छ, जहाँ हरेक बैशाख पूर्णिमामा मेला लाग्छ। दक्षिणतिर एकीकरणदेखि नै निरन्तर बलिरहेको अखण्ड ज्योति छ। अब उत्तरतिर फर्कनुहोस्। खुला दिनमा मनास्लु, हिमालचुली, अन्नपूर्ण र गणेश हिमाल लहरै देखिन्छन्। सन् 2015 को भूकम्पले दरबारमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो, र पुरातत्त्व विभागले नोभेम्बर 2017 मा पुनर्निर्माण सुरु गर्‍यो।','दरबारमुनिको गुफामा मत्स्येन्द्रनाथका शिष्य योगी गोरखनाथले बसेर ध्यान गरेको विश्वास गरिन्छ। गोरखा राज्य र गोरखाली जातिले उनैबाट नाम पाएका हुन्।','[\"नेपाल एकीकरण सुरु गर्ने पृथ्वीनारायण शाहको जन्म सन् 1723 मा यही दरबारमा भएको थियो।\", \"दरबार करिब 1,000 मिटर उचाइको डाँडामा छ, गोरखा बजारबाट करिब एक घण्टा हिँड्नुपर्छ।\", \"यसका पर्खाल करिब तीन फिट बाक्लो छन् र भुइँहरू बाहिर निस्किएका काठका धरनमा अडिएका छन्।\", \"युनेस्कोले सन् 1996 देखि \'गोरखाको मध्यकालीन दरबार परिसर\' लाई नेपालको अस्थायी सूचीमा राखेको छ।\", \"सन् 2015 को भूकम्पपछिको पुनर्निर्माण पुरातत्त्व विभागको नेतृत्वमा 15 नोभेम्बर 2017 मा सुरु भएको थियो।\"]','सन् 2015 अप्रिलको भूकम्पले दरबारमा आंशिक क्षति पुर्‍यायो। पुरातत्त्व विभागले 15 नोभेम्बर 2017 मा पुनर्निर्माण सुरु गर्‍यो, र सन् 2022 मा पनि काम चलिरहेको थियो।','[{\"name\": \"Baisakh Purnima fair\", \"note\": \"Annual fair held on the full-moon day of Baisakh at the Gorakhnath cave near the palace.\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"बैशाख पूर्णिमा मेला\", \"note_np\": \"दरबार नजिकैको गोरखनाथ गुफामा हरेक बैशाख पूर्णिमाका दिन लाग्ने वार्षिक मेला।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Gorkha_Palace_NP-GK-01_01.jpg/1280px-Gorkha_Palace_NP-GK-01_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bibek Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Carved wooden window and door on the palace facade\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorkha_Palace_NP-GK-01_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Gorkha_Palace_2026_02.jpg/1280px-Gorkha_Palace_2026_02.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sonika Aryal\", \"caption\": \"Devotees gathered in the palace courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorkha_Palace_2026_02.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Gorkha_Palace_Premises_01.jpg/1280px-Gorkha_Palace_Premises_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sonika Aryal\", \"caption\": \"Stone ramparts and walls of the palace premises\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorkha_Palace_Premises_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Gorkha_Palace_2026_11.jpg/1280px-Gorkha_Palace_2026_11.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sonika Aryal\", \"caption\": \"The palace crowning its forested ridge\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorkha_Palace_2026_11.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Gorkha_Palace_NP-GK-01_07.jpg/1280px-Gorkha_Palace_NP-GK-01_07.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bibek Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Inner courtyard of the palace with visitors\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorkha_Palace_NP-GK-01_07.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Long red-brick palace with dark carved wooden windows and low tiled pagoda roofs on a narrow wooded ridge top, stone ramparts below, white peaks to the north.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#9b3a2e\", \"#5a4632\", \"#c9b79a\"], \"features\": [\"carved-windows\", \"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [60, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\", \"himalaya-backdrop\", \"snow-peaks\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:45'),(14,'manakamana-temple','Manakamana Temple','मनकामना मन्दिर','Manakamana (Gorkha)','Gandaki','Gorkha',NULL,27.904224,84.583992,'pagoda','Hindu','Goddess Bhagawati (Manakamana), regarded as an incarnation of Lakshmi',1678,'Founded in 1678 according to Wikipedia; tradition places its origin in the 17th century under the Gorkha kings Ram Shah or Prithvipati Shah. Rebuilt and gilded between June 2015 and September 2018.','Shah (Kingdom of Gorkha)','Two-storey Nepalese pagoda with an ambulatory around the sanctum, carved timber struts and windows. After the 2018 restoration, the roof, door, finial and windows were gold-plated with about 14 kg of gold; limestone, surkhi, brick and wood were used.',0,'Hilltop pagoda of the wish-fulfilling goddess above the Trishuli and Marsyangdi rivers, famous for its cable car.','Welcome to Kafakdada hill, 1,300 metres above the meeting of the Trishuli and Marsyangdi rivers. The name of this temple is its promise: mana means heart and kamana means wish, and pilgrims believe the goddess Bhagawati grants the wishes of the faithful. The story goes back to the 17th century and the Gorkha court. The queen, it is said, had divine powers known only to her Magar priest, Lakhan Thapa. After the king died and she followed him onto the funeral pyre, she promised to return. Months later a farmer\'s plough split a stone that ran with blood and milk, and Lakhan Thapa built a shrine on that spot. To this day the priest must be his descendant. Look up at the two-tiered roof: after the 2015 earthquake tilted the temple, restorers gilded its roof, door and windows with about fourteen kilograms of gold. Before 1998 pilgrims walked for three hours; now the cable car lifts you in about ten minutes.','A Gorkha queen with secret divine powers committed sati after her husband\'s death, promising her priest Lakhan Thapa Magar she would reappear. Six months later a farmer split a stone that poured blood and milk; Lakhan Thapa\'s rituals stopped the flow and he built the shrine there.','[\"The temple stands at about 1,300 m on Kafakdada hill in Shahid Lakhan Rural Municipality, Gorkha.\", \"By tradition the priest must be a Magar descendant of Lakhan Thapa.\", \"Prithvi Narayan Shah set up a trust in 1764-65 to worship Manakamana and feed the pigeons every day.\", \"The Manakamana cable car, opened on 24 November 1998, runs 2.8 km from Kurintar in about 10 minutes.\", \"After the 2015 earthquake the temple was rebuilt and gold-plated, work finishing in September 2018.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,'The April 2015 earthquake cracked the roof and tilted the temple 9-12 inches to the north-east. Reconstruction under the Department of Archaeology began in June 2015 and was finished in September 2018, costing about NPR 130-140 million.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Gorkha_Manakamana_Temple.jpg/1280px-Gorkha_Manakamana_Temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorkha_Manakamana_Temple.jpg','Bhupendra Shrestha · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,shah (kingdom of gorkha),manakamana (gorkha),legend,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manakamana_Temple\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1727432206\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2385286\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Manakamana_Temple,_Gorkha\"]','त्रिशूली र मर्स्याङ्दी नदीमाथि डाँडामा रहेको इच्छा पूरा गर्ने देवीको पगोडा मन्दिर, केबलकारका लागि प्रसिद्ध।','काफकदाँडामा स्वागत छ, त्रिशूली र मर्स्याङ्दी नदी भेटिने ठाउँभन्दा 1,300 मिटर माथि। यो मन्दिरको नामले नै वचन दिन्छ: मन भनेको हृदय, कामना भनेको इच्छा। भक्तजनले विश्वास गर्छन्, देवी भगवतीले श्रद्धालुका इच्छा पूरा गर्छिन्। कथा सत्रौँ शताब्दीको गोरखा दरबारसँग जोडिन्छ। भनिन्छ, रानीसँग दैवी शक्ति थियो, जुन उनका मगर पुजारी लखन थापाले मात्र थाहा पाएका थिए। राजाको मृत्युपछि रानी सती गइन्, र फर्कने वचन दिएर गइन्। केही महिनापछि एक किसानको हलोले ढुङ्गा फुट्यो र त्यसबाट रगत र दूध बग्यो। लखन थापाले त्यही ठाउँमा मन्दिर बनाए। आजसम्म पनि पुजारी उनकै सन्तान हुनुपर्छ। माथि दुई तले छानातिर हेर्नुहोस्: सन् 2015 को भूकम्पले मन्दिर ढल्काएपछि जीर्णोद्धार गर्नेहरूले छाना, ढोका र झ्यालमा करिब चौध केजी सुन चढाए। सन् 1998 अघि तीर्थयात्री तीन घण्टा हिँडेर आउँथे; अहिले केबलकारले करिब दश मिनेटमै पुर्‍याउँछ।','गोरखाकी एक रानीसँग गुप्त दैवी शक्ति थियो। राजाको मृत्युपछि उनी सती गइन् र आफ्ना पुजारी लखन थापा मगरलाई फेरि देखा पर्ने वचन दिइन्। छ महिनापछि एक किसानले हलोले ढुङ्गा फोड्दा त्यसबाट रगत र दूध बग्यो। लखन थापाले पूजा गरेपछि त्यो बग्न बन्द भयो, र उनले त्यही ठाउँमा मन्दिर बनाए।','[\"मन्दिर गोरखाको शहीद लखन गाउँपालिकामा पर्ने काफकदाँडामा करिब 1,300 मिटर उचाइमा छ।\", \"परम्पराअनुसार पुजारी लखन थापाका मगर सन्तान नै हुनुपर्छ।\", \"पृथ्वीनारायण शाहले सन् 1764-65 मा मनकामनाको पूजा गर्न र हरेक दिन परेवालाई दाना खुवाउन गुठी राखेका थिए।\", \"मनकामना केबलकार 24 नोभेम्बर 1998 मा सुरु भएको हो; यो कुरिनटारबाट 2.8 किमी दूरी करिब 10 मिनेटमा पुग्छ।\", \"सन् 2015 को भूकम्पपछि मन्दिर पुनर्निर्माण गरेर सुनले सजाइयो; काम सेप्टेम्बर 2018 मा सकियो।\"]','सन् 2015 अप्रिलको भूकम्पले मन्दिरको छाना चर्कायो र मन्दिरलाई 9-12 इन्च उत्तरपूर्वतिर ढल्काइदियो। पुरातत्त्व विभागको जिम्मामा जुन 2015 मा सुरु भएको पुनर्निर्माण सेप्टेम्बर 2018 मा सकियो, जसमा करिब 13-14 करोड रुपैयाँ खर्च भयो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Artistic_view_of_Manakamana_temple.JPG/1280px-Artistic_view_of_Manakamana_temple.JPG\", \"author\": \"Anish Bista\", \"caption\": \"Carved roof struts and gilded details of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artistic_view_of_Manakamana_temple.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Bell_in_the_manakamana_Temple%2C_Nepal.JPG/1280px-Bell_in_the_manakamana_Temple%2C_Nepal.JPG\", \"author\": \"Pranaya mulepati\", \"caption\": \"Historic bell hung in the temple compound\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bell_in_the_manakamana_Temple,_Nepal.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Diyos_and_lakhbattis_at_the_Manakamana_temple.JPG/1280px-Diyos_and_lakhbattis_at_the_Manakamana_temple.JPG\", \"author\": \"Anish Bista\", \"caption\": \"Oil lamps and wicks offered by devotees\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diyos_and_lakhbattis_at_the_Manakamana_temple.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Manakamana_Mai_Temple.jpg/1280px-Manakamana_Mai_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gaurav Dhwaj Khadka\", \"caption\": \"Pilgrims crowding the courtyard during renovation\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manakamana_Mai_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Manakamana_Temple_Mankamana_Gorkha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%2813%29.jpg/1280px-Manakamana_Temple_Mankamana_Gorkha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%2813%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The gilded two-tier pagoda after restoration\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manakamana_Temple_Mankamana_Gorkha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(13).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Compact two-tier pagoda with fully gilded roofs and dark carved timber, ringed by a railing and crowds, on a paved hilltop with a cable-car station nearby.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"timber\", \"colors\": [\"#d4a62a\", \"#3b2a20\", \"#a8322a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"bell\", \"lamps-diyo\", \"carved-windows\", \"golden-door\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [12, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"stone-paved-plaza\", \"village\", \"himalaya-backdrop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(15,'muktinath-temple','Muktinath Temple','मुक्तिनाथ मन्दिर','Ranipauwa (Muktinath)','Gandaki','Mustang',NULL,28.816667,83.870833,'pagoda','Both','Vishnu as Muktinarayan (Hindu); Avalokiteshvara (Buddhist)',1815,'Present shrine built in 1814 or 1815 and credited to Queen Subarna Prabha Devi of Nepal; tradition says it replaced an earlier clay temple built by the kings of Jumla. The site itself is mentioned in the Vishnu Purana\'s Gandaki Mahatmya.','Shah','Small Newar-style pagoda with a three-tiered roof crowned by a golden brass pinnacle, standing in a courtyard enclosed by 108 bull-headed water spouts (Mukti Dhara) of copper or brass, inside a sacred poplar grove.',0,'One of the world\'s highest temples, at 3,800 m, sacred to Hindus as Vishnu\'s abode and to Buddhists as Chumig Gyatsa.','You have reached 3,800 metres, at the foot of the Thorong La pass, and the air is thin and cold. This is Muktinath, the Lord of Liberation, and both Hindus and Buddhists have walked here for centuries. Hindus come to Vishnu, who is said to have revealed himself here; it is one of the 108 Divya Desams of the Sri Vaishnava tradition and one of Nepal\'s Char Dham. Buddhists know the place as Chumig Gyatsa, the Hundred Springs, linked with Avalokiteshvara and with Padmasambhava. The small pagoda in front of you, with its three-tiered roof and golden pinnacle, was built around 1815 and is credited to Queen Subarna Prabha Devi. Now walk around it. One hundred and eight bull-headed spouts pour icy water, and brave pilgrims run beneath every one. Nearby, at the Jwala Mai shrine, a small flame burns on natural gas from the earth, so fire and water meet in one holy place.','The poplar trees of the sacred grove are said to have grown from the staffs of the eighty-four siddhas who passed through on their way to Tibet. Buddhists hold that Padmasambhava left a statue of himself at the Mharme Lhakhang Gompa before departing for Tibet.','[\"At about 3,800 m, Muktinath is one of the world\'s highest temples.\", \"Its courtyard is enclosed by 108 water spouts shaped like bull heads, called the Mukti Dhara.\", \"It is counted among the 108 Divya Desam of Sri Vaishnavism and among the 51 Shakta pithas.\", \"Tibetan Buddhists call it Chumig Gyatsa, the \'Hundred Waters\'.\", \"The nearby Jwala Mai temple shelters a flame fed by natural gas from the ground.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Muktinath_Temple_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Muktinath_Temple_%281%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muktinath_Temple_(1).jpg','Faj2323 · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,both,shah,ranipauwa (muktinath),hindu,buddhist,legend,water,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muktinath\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1025465\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Muktinath_Temple\"]','संसारका सबैभन्दा अग्ला मन्दिरमध्ये एक, 3,800 मिटरमा; हिन्दूका लागि विष्णुको वास र बौद्धका लागि चुमिग ग्यात्सा।','तपाईं थोरङ ला भञ्ज्याङको फेदीमा 3,800 मिटर उचाइमा पुग्नुभएको छ, जहाँ हावा पातलो र चिसो छ। यो मुक्तिनाथ हो, मुक्तिका स्वामी, जहाँ हिन्दू र बौद्ध दुवै धर्मका मानिस सयौँ वर्षदेखि आउँछन्। हिन्दूहरू विष्णुकहाँ आउँछन्; भनिन्छ, विष्णु यहीँ प्रकट भएका थिए। यो श्रीवैष्णव परम्पराको 108 दिव्य देशमध्ये एक र नेपालका चारधाममध्ये एक हो। बौद्धहरू यस ठाउँलाई चुमिग ग्यात्सा, अर्थात् सय धारा भन्छन्, र यसलाई अवलोकितेश्वर र पद्मसम्भवसँग जोड्छन्। तपाईंको अगाडिको सानो पगोडा, तीन तले छाना र सुनौलो गजुरसहित, करिब 1815 मा बनेको हो र रानी सुवर्ण प्रभा देवीको श्रेय दिइन्छ। अब यसको वरिपरि घुम्नुहोस्। 108 वटा गाईको मुखजस्ता धाराबाट चिसो पानी झर्छ, र साहसी तीर्थयात्री हरेक धारामुनि दौडिएर नुहाउँछन्। नजिकैको ज्वाला माईको मन्दिरमा जमिनबाट निस्कने प्राकृतिक ग्यासले सानो आगो बलिरहन्छ, यसरी एकै पवित्र ठाउँमा आगो र पानी भेटिन्छन्।','पवित्र वनका पोखरीका रूखहरू तिब्बततर्फ जाँदै गर्दा यहाँबाट गुज्रेका चौरासी सिद्धहरूका लट्ठीबाट उम्रेका हुन् भनिन्छ। बौद्धहरू मान्छन्, तिब्बत जानुअघि पद्मसम्भवले म्हार्मे ल्हाखाङ गुम्बामा आफ्नो मूर्ति छाडेका थिए।','[\"करिब 3,800 मिटरमा रहेको मुक्तिनाथ संसारका सबैभन्दा अग्ला मन्दिरमध्ये एक हो।\", \"यसको आँगन गाईको मुखजस्ता 108 वटा धाराले घेरिएको छ, जसलाई मुक्तिधारा भनिन्छ।\", \"यो श्रीवैष्णव परम्पराका 108 दिव्य देशमा र 51 शक्तिपीठमा गनिन्छ।\", \"तिब्बती बौद्धहरू यसलाई चुमिग ग्यात्सा, अर्थात् \'सय धारा\' भन्छन्।\", \"नजिकैको ज्वाला माईको मन्दिरमा जमिनबाट निस्कने प्राकृतिक ग्यासले बलेको आगो छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/108_water_sources_-_Muktinath%2C_Nepal_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-108_water_sources_-_Muktinath%2C_Nepal_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sergey Ashmarin\", \"caption\": \"The 108 water spouts of the Mukti Dhara\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:108_water_sources_-_Muktinath,_Nepal_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Inside_Muktinath_Temple.jpg/1280px-Inside_Muktinath_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Raunak Maskay\", \"caption\": \"Inside the main shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inside_Muktinath_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Main_Muktinath_temple_and_ponds_c.2016.jpg/1280px-Main_Muktinath_temple_and_ponds_c.2016.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nima t100\", \"caption\": \"Main temple and holy ponds\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Main_Muktinath_temple_and_ponds_c.2016.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Burning_candles_at_Muktinath-Temple_%28Nepal%2C_Region_of_Mustang%29.JPG/1280px-Burning_candles_at_Muktinath-Temple_%28Nepal%2C_Region_of_Mustang%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"Polyflux\", \"caption\": \"Butter lamps burning at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burning_candles_at_Muktinath-Temple_(Nepal,_Region_of_Mustang).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Muktinath_Temple_Mustang.jpg/1280px-Muktinath_Temple_Mustang.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gaurav.aryal\", \"caption\": \"The three-tiered pagoda in its courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muktinath_Temple_Mustang.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Small dark three-roofed pagoda inside a stone-walled yard ringed by a line of 108 brass bull-head spouts and two ponds, poplar grove, bare brown mountains.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"timber\", \"colors\": [\"#4a3b2c\", \"#c9a23a\", \"#b8b0a0\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"water-spouts\", \"bell\", \"prayer-flags\", \"sacred-tree\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": 9, \"footprint_m\": [6, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"sacred-grove\", \"pond\", \"desert-cliffs\", \"snow-peaks\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(16,'tal-barahi-temple','Tal Barahi Temple','तालबाराही मन्दिर','Pokhara','Gandaki','Kaski',NULL,28.207452,83.953443,'lake-shrine','Hindu','Goddess Barahi (Varahi), a form of the mother goddess (Ajima)',NULL,'Local belief dates the shrine to 1669 BS, when King Kulmandan Shah of Kaski is said to have built a thatched hut over a sacred stone on the island. King Mahendra rebuilt it in its current form in 2017 BS; rebuilt again in 2023-2026 after earthquake damage.','Shah (Kaski kings); rebuilt under King Mahendra','Small two-storey pagoda on an island in Phewa Lake, with carved wooden struts, windows and doors and a gilded pinnacle. Wikipedia notes an original stone structure with a two-storey roof; the 2023-26 rebuild used wood and brick in the old form, with Bhaktapur and Lalitpur artisans.',0,'A small island pagoda of the goddess Barahi in Phewa Lake, Pokhara\'s most important religious monument, reached only by boat.','Sit still in the boat for a moment as the shore of Lakeside drifts away. Ahead, on a small wooded island in the middle of Phewa Lake, rises the pagoda of Tal Barahi, the most important religious monument in Pokhara. Tal means lake, and Barahi is the mother goddess who is worshipped here as a symbol of female power. Local belief says that a stone on this mound was worshipped as the goddess long before any building stood here, and that King Kulmandan Shah of Kaski first sheltered it under a simple thatched hut. King Mahendra rebuilt the temple in 2017 BS. After the 2015 earthquake left it leaning about three inches to the south, craftsmen from Bhaktapur and Lalitpur rebuilt it again, keeping its old form. Step ashore at the landing, hear the bells and the flapping pigeons, and look back: on a clear morning the Annapurna range floats above the water behind you.','According to local folklore, King Kulmandan Shah of Kaski founded the temple by building a thatched hut over a stone on a mound in the lake, which had been worshipped as the goddess.','[\"The temple stands on a small island in Phewa Lake and can be reached only by boat, about five minutes from Barahi Ghat.\", \"Devotees especially visit in the Nepali months of Baisakh and Kartik.\", \"The 2015 earthquake tilted the temple about three inches to the south.\", \"Reconstruction began in 2080 BS (2023) under the Department of Archaeology at a cost of about NPR 15 million, mostly from devotees\' donations.\", \"During reconstruction, worship continued at a silver idol at the nearby Havan Kund.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,'The 2015 earthquake tilted the temple about three inches to the south and left parts submerged. Reconstruction began in 2023 and was reported complete in 2026, with reopening set for Ghatasthapana.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Barahi_island_Temple.jpg/1280px-Barahi_island_Temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barahi_island_Temple.jpg','Bibek28 · CC BY-SA 4.0','lake-shrine,hindu,shah (kaski kings); rebuilt under king mahendra,pokhara,legend,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tal_Barahi_Temple\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/11812281742\", \"https://english.ratopati.com/story/82487/reconstruction-of-talbarahi-temple-completed-open-to-devotees-from-ghatasthapana\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Tal_Barahi_Temple\"]','फेवा तालको टापुमा रहेको बाराही देवीको सानो पगोडा मन्दिर, पोखराको सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण धार्मिक स्थल, डुङ्गाबाट मात्र पुगिन्छ।','डुङ्गामा एकछिन चुपचाप बस्नुहोस्; लेकसाइडको किनारा विस्तारै टाढा हुँदै छ। अगाडि, फेवा तालको बीचमा रूख भएको सानो टापुमा तालबाराहीको पगोडा देखिन्छ, जुन पोखराको सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण धार्मिक स्थल हो। ताल भनेको सरोवर, र बाराही भनेको मातृशक्ति देवी हुन्, जसलाई यहाँ नारीशक्तिको प्रतीक मानेर पुजिन्छ। स्थानीय विश्वासअनुसार यो थुम्कोमा कुनै भवन बन्नुअघिदेखि नै एउटा ढुङ्गालाई देवी मानेर पूजा गरिन्थ्यो, र कास्कीका राजा कुलमन्दन शाहले पहिलो पटक त्यसमाथि सानो छाप्रो बनाइदिए। राजा महेन्द्रले वि.सं. 2017 मा मन्दिर फेरि बनाए। सन् 2015 को भूकम्पले मन्दिर करिब तीन इन्च दक्षिणतिर ढल्काएपछि भक्तपुर र ललितपुरका शिल्पीले पुरानै रूपमा यसलाई फेरि बनाए। घाटमा उत्रनुहोस्, घण्टाको आवाज र परेवाको फड्फडाहट सुन्नुहोस्, अनि पछाडि फर्किएर हेर्नुहोस्: सफा बिहान अन्नपूर्ण हिमाल पानीमाथि तैरिएझैँ देखिन्छ।','स्थानीय लोककथाअनुसार कास्कीका राजा कुलमन्दन शाहले तालको थुम्कोमा देवी मानेर पुजिने ढुङ्गामाथि छाप्रो बनाएर यो मन्दिर स्थापना गरेका थिए।','[\"मन्दिर फेवा तालको सानो टापुमा छ र बाराही घाटबाट करिब पाँच मिनेट डुङ्गामा मात्र पुगिन्छ।\", \"भक्तजन विशेष गरी बैशाख र कात्तिक महिनामा दर्शन गर्न जान्छन्।\", \"सन् 2015 को भूकम्पले मन्दिरलाई करिब तीन इन्च दक्षिणतिर ढल्काइदियो।\", \"पुरातत्त्व विभागको जिम्मामा वि.सं. 2080 (सन् 2023) मा सुरु भएको पुनर्निर्माणमा करिब 1 करोड 50 लाख रुपैयाँ खर्च भयो, जसमध्ये धेरै जसो भक्तजनको दान थियो।\", \"पुनर्निर्माणको बेला नजिकैको हवन कुण्डमा चाँदीको मूर्तिमा पूजा जारी रह्यो।\"]','सन् 2015 को भूकम्पले मन्दिर करिब तीन इन्च दक्षिणतिर ढल्काइदियो र केही भाग पानीमा डुब्यो। पुनर्निर्माण 2023 मा सुरु भएर 2026 मा सकिएको खबर आयो, र घटस्थापनाका दिन मन्दिर खोल्ने तय भयो।','[{\"name\": \"Dashain (Ghatasthapana)\", \"note\": \"Regular puja was set to resume on Ghatasthapana when the goddess\'s power returned to the old stone after rebuilding.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैं (घटस्थापना)\", \"note_np\": \"पुनर्निर्माणपछि देवीको शक्ति पुरानो ढुङ्गामा फर्केपछि घटस्थापनाका दिनदेखि नियमित पूजा सुरु हुने भएको थियो।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Barahi_Temple_%289191444126%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Barahi_Temple_%289191444126%29_%28cropped%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"দেবর্ষি রায় from Brno, Czech Republic\", \"caption\": \"The island temple seen from Phewa Lake\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barahi_Temple_(9191444126)_(cropped).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Aves_en_Barahi_Temple_%288512791125%29.jpg/1280px-Aves_en_Barahi_Temple_%288512791125%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Carlos Adampol Galindo from DF, México\", \"caption\": \"Birds perched on the temple roof\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aves_en_Barahi_Temple_(8512791125).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Barahi_mandir_Pokhara.jpg/1280px-Barahi_mandir_Pokhara.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bibek Raj Pandeya\", \"caption\": \"Close view of the temple and its carvings\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barahi_mandir_Pokhara.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/NP_Pokhara_0905_%2820%29_%2817258352855%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Diego Tirira from Quito, Ecuador\", \"caption\": \"Boats moored at the island landing\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NP_Pokhara_0905_(20)_(17258352855).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Phewa_Lake_and_The_Accompaniments%21.jpg/1280px-Phewa_Lake_and_The_Accompaniments%21.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gauravpkr\", \"caption\": \"The island temple with the Himalayan range behind\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phewa_Lake_and_The_Accompaniments!.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Tiny two-roofed grey-roofed dark-timber pagoda with a gold pinnacle on a tree-covered island in a green lake, boats at a small landing, Annapurna peaks behind.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"timber\", \"colors\": [\"#6b6a66\", \"#3e2f25\", \"#c9a23a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"bell\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 9, \"footprint_m\": [6, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"lake\", \"forest\", \"himalaya-backdrop\", \"snow-peaks\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(17,'bindhyabasini-temple-pokhara','Bindhyabasini Temple','बिन्ध्यबासिनी मन्दिर','Pokhara','Gandaki','Kaski',NULL,28.237778,83.984167,'shikhara','Hindu','Goddess Bindhyabasini, a manifestation of Durga (Yogamaya)',NULL,'Established around the 1760s; the temple itself is recorded as built in 1842 BS on 47 ropani of land. In June 1815 King Girvan Yuddha Bikram Shah appointed its priest. The present building is a later shikhara rebuild.','Kaski kings (tradition); Shah','White shikhara-style temple on a hilltop platform, approached by stone stairways from the east, north and south-east. Two golden metal lions flank the gate, and the complex holds shrines to Saraswati, Shiva, Hanuman, Ganesh and Vishnu.',0,'One of Pokhara\'s oldest temples: a white shikhara of goddess Bindhyabasini on a hill in Miruwa, old Pokhara.','Climb the stone stairs to this small hill in old Pokhara and you arrive at one of the city\'s oldest temples. The white shikhara in front of you belongs to Bindhyabasini, a form of Durga. Her story begins in Mathura, where she was born as the baby who escaped the tyrant Kamsa and rose into the sky, later making her home in the Vindhya hills of India. Legend says a king of Kaski, Siddhi Narayan Shah, dreamed of bringing her presence to his kingdom. His envoys carried a statue home from Vindhyachal, but on this hilltop it became impossible to move, so the temple was founded right here. Notice the two golden lions at the gate and the sindoor-red Hanuman by the Ganesh shrine. Around you are shrines to Saraswati, Shiva and Vishnu, and a Sanskrit school. Sadly, Pokhara\'s great fire of 1949 is said to have started here during an offering.','King Siddhi Narayan Shah of Kaski (or, in other accounts, King Khadgaman Malla of Parbat) dreamed he should bring the goddess from Vindhyachal in India. The statue his envoys carried back could not be lifted again on this hilltop, which was taken as the goddess\'s chosen home.','[\"The temple is in Ward 2, Miruwa, of Pokhara and is dedicated to Bindhyabasini, a manifestation of Durga.\", \"The temple was established around the 1760s; in 1815 King Girvan Yuddha Bikram Shah appointed its priest.\", \"Most of Pokhara was destroyed in a 1949 fire that allegedly began at the temple during an offering.\", \"A 12-person lift for disabled and elderly pilgrims was inaugurated by the President of Nepal on 7 March 2019.\", \"The complex is managed by the Bindhyabasini Dharmik Chhetra Bikash Samiti.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Bindabashini_Temple_01.JPG/1280px-Bindabashini_Temple_01.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindabashini_Temple_01.JPG','Prabina Karki · CC BY-SA 3.0','shikhara,hindu,kaski kings (tradition); shah,pokhara,legend,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bindhyabasini_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q16254765\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Bindhayawasini_Temple\"]','पोखराका सबैभन्दा पुराना मन्दिरमध्ये एक: पुरानो पोखराको मिरुवा डाँडामा रहेको बिन्ध्यबासिनी देवीको सेतो शिखर मन्दिर।','पुरानो पोखराको यो सानो डाँडामा ढुङ्गाका भ्याङ चढेर आउनुभयो भने तपाईं सहरकै पुराना मन्दिरमध्ये एकमा पुग्नुहुन्छ। अगाडिको सेतो शिखर बिन्ध्यबासिनीको हो, जो दुर्गाको एक रूप हुन्। उनको कथा मथुराबाट सुरु हुन्छ, जहाँ उनी अत्याचारी कंसबाट उम्केर आकाशमा उडेकी बच्चीका रूपमा जन्मिएकी थिइन्, र पछि भारतको विन्ध्य पर्वतमा बसोबास गरिन्। लोककथाअनुसार कास्कीका राजा सिद्धि नारायण शाहले आफ्नो राज्यमा देवीको उपस्थिति ल्याउने सपना देखे। उनका दूतले विन्ध्याचलबाट मूर्ति बोकेर ल्याए, तर यो डाँडामा आइपुगेपछि मूर्ति हल्लाउनै नसकिने भयो, त्यसैले मन्दिर यहीँ स्थापना गरियो। गेटका दुई सुनौला सिंह हेर्नुहोस्, र गणेशको मन्दिर नजिकै सिन्दूर लगाएका हनुमान पनि। वरिपरि सरस्वती, शिव र विष्णुका मन्दिर र एउटा संस्कृत विद्यालय छन्। दुःखको कुरा, सन् 1949 मा पोखरामा लागेको ठूलो आगलागी यहीँ भेटी चढाउँदा सुरु भएको भनिन्छ।','कास्कीका राजा सिद्धि नारायण शाहले (अर्को कथाअनुसार पर्वतका राजा खड्गमान मल्लले) भारतको विन्ध्याचलबाट देवीलाई ल्याउनुपर्छ भन्ने सपना देखे। दूतले बोकेर ल्याएको मूर्ति यो डाँडामा आइपुगेपछि फेरि उठाउन सकिएन, र यही ठाउँ देवीले रोजेको वासस्थान हो भन्ने मानियो।','[\"मन्दिर पोखराको वडा नं. 2, मिरुवामा छ र दुर्गाको रूप बिन्ध्यबासिनीलाई समर्पित छ।\", \"मन्दिर सन् 1760 को दशकतिर स्थापना भएको हो; सन् 1815 मा राजा गीर्वाणयुद्ध विक्रम शाहले यसको पुजारी नियुक्त गरे।\", \"सन् 1949 को आगलागीमा पोखराको धेरैजसो भाग नष्ट भयो, जुन भेटी चढाउँदा मन्दिरबाट सुरु भएको भनिन्छ।\", \"अपाङ्गता भएका र वृद्ध भक्तजनका लागि 12 जना अट्ने लिफ्ट 7 मार्च 2019 मा राष्ट्रपतिले उद्घाटन गरे।\", \"मन्दिर परिसर बिन्ध्यबासिनी धार्मिक क्षेत्र विकास समितिले व्यवस्थापन गर्छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Bindabasini_mandir.jpg/1280px-Bindabasini_mandir.jpg\", \"author\": \"Herogurung\", \"caption\": \"Devotees queueing at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindabasini_mandir.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Bindhyabasini_Temple_%289048739188%29.jpg/1280px-Bindhyabasini_Temple_%289048739188%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"দেবর্ষি রায় from Brno, Czech Republic\", \"caption\": \"The temple in its hilltop setting\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindhyabasini_Temple_(9048739188).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Bindabasini_temple.jpg/1280px-Bindabasini_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Premkgurung\", \"caption\": \"The white shikhara and its entrance\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindabasini_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Bindhyabasini_Temple_Complex_and_Devotees_02.jpg/1280px-Bindhyabasini_Temple_Complex_and_Devotees_02.jpg\", \"author\": \"Goutam1962\", \"caption\": \"Temple complex with devotees\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindhyabasini_Temple_Complex_and_Devotees_02.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2f/Bindhyabasini_Temple_Complex_and_Devotees_115.jpg\", \"author\": \"Goutam1962\", \"caption\": \"Devotees worshipping in the complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindhyabasini_Temple_Complex_and_Devotees_115.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"white-dome\", \"notes\": \"Bulbous white plastered shikhara with a red band and gold finial, a small carved porch in front, two golden lions at the gate on a paved hilltop.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#f2f2ef\", \"#c0302a\", \"#c9a23a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"lion-statues\", \"bell\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": 12, \"footprint_m\": [7, 7], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"stone-paved-plaza\", \"city-street\", \"sacred-tree\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(18,'bhadrakali-temple-pokhara','Bhadrakali Temple','भद्रकाली मन्दिर','Pokhara','Gandaki','Kaski',NULL,28.212500,84.007083,'pagoda','Hindu','Goddess Bhadrakali (Kali/Durga)',NULL,'Wikipedia and Wikidata give its founding year as 1817 (the calendar era is not stated); the hill was earlier known as Mudule Thumko.','unknown','Small tiered pagoda-roofed shrine with a gilded pinnacle on a brick and stone platform atop a forested hillock, with a Ganesh shrine, a kuti and stone lion guardians in the grounds.',0,'A hilltop pagoda of the goddess Bhadrakali in Kundahar, east Pokhara, reached by nearly 300 stone steps through the trees.','Count the steps as you climb: from the east there are 292 of them, from the south 265, and both lead you up through green woods to the top of a small hill in Kundahar, on the eastern side of Pokhara. Up here, at about 2,930 feet, stands the temple of Bhadrakali, the goddess of power and strength, a form of Kali and Durga. Before the temple was founded in 1817, people called this hill Mudule Thumko. The story told by devotees is simple and striking: the goddess spoke to a priest and told him to dig into the hill, and there he found her image. Since then she has been worshipped here as Bhadrakali. The temple grounds spread over 135 ropani, with a small Ganesh shrine and a stone lion keeping watch. Come during Dashain and thousands of worshippers fill these quiet paths.','The goddess Bhadrakali told a priest to dig into the hill, where he found her statue; since then it has been worshipped here as Bhadrakali.','[\"The temple stands atop a small hill in Kundahar, east Pokhara, at about 2,930 ft (about 890 m).\", \"The eastern approach has 292 steps and the southern approach 265 steps.\", \"The temple area covers about 135 ropani.\", \"Before the temple was founded, the hill was known as \'Mudule Thumko\'.\", \"Dashain is its most important festival, drawing thousands of devotees.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Bhadrakali_Temple%2CPokhara.JPG/1280px-Bhadrakali_Temple%2CPokhara.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhadrakali_Temple,Pokhara.JPG','Bibek28 · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,pokhara,legend,art,festival,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhadrakali_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q97357162\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/343226046\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Bhadrakali_Temple,_Pokhara\"]','पूर्वी पोखराको कुन्डहरमा रहेको भद्रकाली देवीको डाँडामाथिको पगोडा मन्दिर, रूखबीचको करिब 300 ढुङ्गाका भ्याङ चढेर पुगिन्छ।','भ्याङ चढ्दै गिन्नुहोस्: पूर्वबाट 292 वटा र दक्षिणबाट 265 वटा भ्याङ छन्, र दुवै हरियो जङ्गलबीचबाट पूर्वी पोखराको कुन्डहरको सानो डाँडाको टुप्पोमा पुग्छन्। करिब 2,930 फिट उचाइको यहाँ शक्ति र बलकी देवी भद्रकालीको मन्दिर छ, जो काली र दुर्गाको रूप हुन्। सन् 1817 मा मन्दिर स्थापना हुनुअघि यो डाँडालाई मुदुले थुम्को भनिन्थ्यो। भक्तजनले सुनाउने कथा सरल तर अनौठो छ: देवीले पुजारीसँग बोलेर डाँडा खन्न भनिन्, र त्यहीँ उनको मूर्ति भेटियो। त्यसपछि यहाँ उनलाई भद्रकालीका रूपमा पुजिन थालियो। मन्दिरको क्षेत्र 135 रोपनीमा फैलिएको छ, जहाँ सानो गणेश मन्दिर र रक्षा गर्ने ढुङ्गाको सिंह छन्। दशैंमा आउनुभयो भने यी शान्त बाटा हजारौँ भक्तजनले भरिएका हुन्छन्।','देवी भद्रकालीले पुजारीलाई डाँडा खन्न भनिन्, र त्यहाँ उनको मूर्ति भेटियो। त्यसपछि यहाँ उनको भद्रकालीका रूपमा पूजा हुन थालेको हो।','[\"मन्दिर पूर्वी पोखराको कुन्डहरमा सानो डाँडाको टुप्पोमा, करिब 2,930 फिट (करिब 890 मिटर) उचाइमा छ।\", \"पूर्वी बाटोमा 292 वटा र दक्षिणी बाटोमा 265 वटा भ्याङ छन्।\", \"मन्दिर क्षेत्र करिब 135 रोपनी फैलिएको छ।\", \"मन्दिर बन्नुअघि यो डाँडालाई \'मुदुले थुम्को\' भनिन्थ्यो।\", \"दशैं यहाँको सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण चाड हो, जसमा हजारौँ भक्तजन आउँछन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"The temple\'s most important festival, when thousands of devotees come to worship the goddess.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैं\", \"note_np\": \"मन्दिरको सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण चाड, जसमा हजारौँ भक्तजन देवीको पूजा गर्न आउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Bhadrakali_Temple_Apr_2022.jpg/1280px-Bhadrakali_Temple_Apr_2022.jpg\", \"author\": \"Thapa.lakshman\", \"caption\": \"The temple in April 2022\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhadrakali_Temple_Apr_2022.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bhadrakali_mandhir_premises.jpg/1280px-Bhadrakali_mandhir_premises.jpg\", \"author\": \"Thapa.lakshman\", \"caption\": \"Temple premises with a flowering tree\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhadrakali_mandhir_premises.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Bhadrakali_Temple_Kaski.JPG/1280px-Bhadrakali_Temple_Kaski.JPG\", \"author\": \"Urzen23\", \"caption\": \"Close view of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhadrakali_Temple_Kaski.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Bhadrakalientrance.jpg/1280px-Bhadrakalientrance.jpg\", \"author\": \"Himalayanwalkers\", \"caption\": \"Stone stairway entrance to the hill\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhadrakalientrance.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/Lion_guard_at_Bhadrakali_Temple%2C_Kundahar%2C_Pokhara.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ramnam\", \"caption\": \"Stone lion guard in the temple grounds\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lion_guard_at_Bhadrakali_Temple,_Kundahar,_Pokhara.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Small two-roofed red-brick pagoda with gold finial on a raised stone platform at the top of a tree-covered hillock, long stone stairs climbing to it.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8c3a2b\", \"#3e2f25\", \"#c9a23a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"bell\", \"lion-statues\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 10, \"footprint_m\": [6, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\", \"stone-paved-plaza\", \"city-street\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(19,'bindebasini-temple-bandipur','Bindebasini Temple, Bandipur','बिन्ध्यबासिनी मन्दिर, बन्दिपुर','Bandipur','Gandaki','Tanahun',NULL,27.937806,84.407078,'pagoda','Hindu','Goddess Bindhyabasini, a form of Durga',NULL,'Construction date not documented in the sources found; Bandipur bazaar itself grew after Newar traders from Bhaktapur settled here following 1768. The temple was rebuilt after the 2072 BS (2015) earthquake.','unknown','Two-tiered Newar pagoda of brick and carved timber on a stepped base, standing in the stone-paved square at the northern end of Bandipur bazaar, framed by two- and three-storey Newar trading houses with shuttered windows.',0,'A Newar pagoda of goddess Bindhyabasini at the head of Bandipur\'s preserved hilltop trading bazaar in Tanahun.','Walk the length of Bandipur\'s main street, past tall Newar houses with shuttered windows and shops under their verandas, and at the northern end you reach a small square with a pagoda at its heart. This is the temple of Bindhyabasini, a form of Durga. Bandipur was a Magar village until Newar traders from Bhaktapur arrived after Prithvi Narayan Shah conquered the Kathmandu Valley in 1768. Safe from malaria on this saddle of the Mahabharat range, they turned it into a busy stop on the India-Tibet trade route and brought their temples and architecture with them. Look at the carved roof struts and the brickwork, which echo the old pagodas of the valley. The 2015 earthquake damaged the temple, and it has been rebuilt. Locals still come to worship every day, and at the New Year an image of the goddess is pulled through town on a chariot.',NULL,'[\"Bandipur sits at about 1,030 m on a saddle of the Mahabharat range, some 700 m above the Marsyangdi valley.\", \"Newar traders from Bhaktapur developed Bandipur after Prithvi Narayan Shah conquered the Kathmandu Valley in 1768.\", \"The temple stands in the square at the northern end of Bandipur bazaar.\", \"It was rebuilt after the 2072 BS (2015) earthquake.\", \"Since 1998 Bandipur has been linked by an 8 km road from Dumre on the Prithvi Highway.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,'Damaged in the 2015 (2072 BS) earthquake and rebuilt afterwards, according to the Commons photographer\'s description.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg/1280px-Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(3).jpg','Rajesh Dhungana · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,bandipur,art,festival,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bandipur_Rural_Municipality\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/341126519\", \"https://www.yakandyeti.com/bandipur\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\"]','तनहुँको बन्दिपुरको संरक्षित डाँडामाथिको व्यापारिक बजारको टुप्पोमा रहेको बिन्ध्यबासिनी देवीको नेवारी पगोडा।','बन्दिपुरको मुख्य सडकमा सुरुदेखि अन्तसम्म हिँड्नुहोस्। झ्यालमा ढोका लगाइएका अग्ला नेवारी घर र तिनका बरण्डामुनिका पसल पार गरेर उत्तरतिरको छेउमा पुग्दा सानो चोक आउँछ, जसको बीचमा एउटा पगोडा छ। यो दुर्गाको एक रूप बिन्ध्यबासिनीको मन्दिर हो। बन्दिपुर मगरहरूको गाउँ थियो। सन् 1768 मा पृथ्वीनारायण शाहले काठमाडौं उपत्यका जितेपछि भक्तपुरका नेवार व्यापारी यहाँ आए। महाभारत पर्वत शृङ्खलाको यो भञ्ज्याङमा औलोको डर थिएन, त्यसैले उनीहरूले यसलाई भारत-तिब्बत व्यापार मार्गको व्यस्त बास बनाए र आफ्ना मन्दिर र वास्तुकला पनि ल्याए। छानाका कुँदिएका टोडा र इँटाको काम हेर्नुहोस्; यी उपत्यकाका पुराना पगोडासँग मिल्छन्। सन् 2015 को भूकम्पले मन्दिरमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो र पछि यसलाई फेरि बनाइयो। स्थानीयहरू आज पनि हरेक दिन पूजा गर्न आउँछन्, र नयाँ वर्षमा देवीको मूर्तिलाई रथमा राखेर सहरभरि तानिन्छ।',NULL,'[\"बन्दिपुर महाभारत पर्वत शृङ्खलाको भञ्ज्याङमा करिब 1,030 मिटर उचाइमा, मर्स्याङ्दी उपत्यकाभन्दा करिब 700 मिटर माथि छ।\", \"सन् 1768 मा पृथ्वीनारायण शाहले काठमाडौं उपत्यका जितेपछि भक्तपुरका नेवार व्यापारीले बन्दिपुरको विकास गरे।\", \"मन्दिर बन्दिपुर बजारको उत्तरी छेउको चोकमा छ।\", \"वि.सं. 2072 (सन् 2015) को भूकम्पपछि यो फेरि बनाइयो।\", \"सन् 1998 देखि बन्दिपुर पृथ्वी राजमार्गको दुम्रेबाट 8 किमी सडकले जोडिएको छ।\"]','वि.सं. 2072 (सन् 2015) को भूकम्पमा मन्दिरमा क्षति पुग्यो र पछि यसलाई फेरि बनाइयो, जुन कमन्सका फोटोग्राफरको वर्णनअनुसार हो।','[{\"name\": \"New Year chariot procession\", \"note\": \"An image of the goddess is placed in a chariot and pulled during the New Year celebration (travel guide).\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"नयाँ वर्षको रथयात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"नयाँ वर्षको उत्सवमा देवीको मूर्तिलाई रथमा राखेर तानिन्छ (यात्रा गाइडअनुसार)।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The temple at the head of Bandipur bazaar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Bandipur_%E2%80%93_Bindhybashini-Temple_-_01.jpg/1280px-Bandipur_%E2%80%93_Bindhybashini-Temple_-_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Maesi64\", \"caption\": \"Front view of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandipur_%E2%80%93_Bindhybashini-Temple_-_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The temple with the bazaar houses\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(2).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%285%29.jpg/1280px-Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%285%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Pagoda roofs and carved struts\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindyabasini_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(5).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Bindyabasini_Temple_of_Bandipur.JPG/1280px-Bindyabasini_Temple_of_Bandipur.JPG\", \"author\": \"Raajiv Kilana Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"The temple in its square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bindyabasini_Temple_of_Bandipur.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Two-roofed brick and dark-timber pagoda on a stepped base in a small paved square at the end of a street of tall Newar shophouses.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8a3b2a\", \"#3b2c22\", \"#c9a23a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"carved-windows\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": 10, \"footprint_m\": [6, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\", \"market-houses\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(20,'khadga-devi-temple-bandipur','Khadga Devi Temple','खड्गदेवी मन्दिर','Bandipur','Gandaki','Tanahun',NULL,27.938683,84.407774,'pagoda','Hindu','Khadga Devi, goddess of the sacred sword',NULL,'Construction date not documented in the sources found. The sword kept here is believed to have belonged to the 16th-century king Mukunda Sen.','unknown','Two-storey red-brick shrine with a pitched tiled roof topped by a small lantern and pinnacle, entered up a short flight of stone steps; set in a wide open ground with rest houses (pati) and large pipal trees above Bandipur bazaar.',0,'Hilltop shrine above Bandipur bazaar that guards a sacred sword said to have belonged to King Mukunda Sen, paraded at Dashain.','Climb a little above Bandipur\'s old bazaar and the houses give way to a wide open ground, shaded by great pipal trees. The red-brick shrine in front of you is the home of Khadga Devi, the goddess of the sword. Khadga means sword, and the treasure kept here is a blade believed to have belonged to Mukunda Sen, a king of the 16th century; tradition says it was a gift from Lord Shiva himself. For most of the year the doors stay shut. They open on Fulpati, during Dashain, when the town holds its Khadga Jatra. Then members of the Magar and Bishwokarma communities carry the sacred sword in procession through the streets, and Hindu devotees come to worship it. The temple is especially important to Bandipur\'s Newar Shrestha families. Stand by the pati, the old rest house, look out over the ridge, and imagine the drums and the flash of steel on festival day.','The sword kept in the temple is believed to have belonged to King Mukunda Sen and to have been a gift from Lord Shiva.','[\"Khadga Jatra, held during Dashain, centres on a religious service at the Khadga Devi temple.\", \"Magar and Bishwokarma communities parade a sacred sword through Bandipur during the jatra.\", \"The sword is believed to have belonged to King Mukunda Sen.\", \"The temple opens only on Fulpati, one day of the Dashain festival.\", \"A statue of Khadgamai stands in the sanctum, with pati rest houses and big pipal trees nearby.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%287%29.jpg/1280px-Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%287%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(7).jpg','Rajesh Dhungana · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,bandipur,legend,art,festival,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khadga_Jatra\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/6026620786\", \"https://www.yakandyeti.com/bandipur\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\"]','बन्दिपुर बजारमाथिको डाँडाको मन्दिर, जहाँ राजा मुकुन्द सेनको भनिने पवित्र खड्ग राखिएको छ र दशैंमा यात्रा गरिन्छ।','बन्दिपुरको पुरानो बजारभन्दा अलि माथि चढ्नुहोस्, घरहरू सकिएर ठूला पिपलका रूखले छाया पारेको फराकिलो चौर आउँछ। अगाडिको रातो इँटाको मन्दिर खड्गदेवीको वासस्थान हो, खड्गकी देवी। खड्ग भनेको तरबार हो, र यहाँ राखिएको तरबार सोह्रौँ शताब्दीका राजा मुकुन्द सेनको थियो भनिन्छ; परम्पराअनुसार यो स्वयं शिवको उपहार थियो। वर्षको धेरैजसो समय मन्दिरको ढोका बन्द रहन्छ। दशैंको फूलपातीका दिन ढोका खुल्छ, जब सहरमा खड्ग जात्रा हुन्छ। त्यसबेला मगर र विश्वकर्मा समुदायका मानिसले पवित्र खड्ग बोकेर सडकमा जुलुस निकाल्छन्, र हिन्दू भक्तजन पूजा गर्न आउँछन्। यो मन्दिर बन्दिपुरका नेवार श्रेष्ठ परिवारका लागि विशेष महत्त्वको छ। पुरानो पाटीमा उभिएर डाँडाको थुम्कोतर्फ हेर्नुहोस्, अनि चाडको दिन बज्ने बाजा र चम्किने तरबारको कल्पना गर्नुहोस्।','मन्दिरमा राखिएको खड्ग राजा मुकुन्द सेनको थियो र शिवको उपहार थियो भन्ने विश्वास छ।','[\"दशैंमा हुने खड्ग जात्राको केन्द्र खड्गदेवी मन्दिरको धार्मिक पूजा हो।\", \"जात्रामा मगर र विश्वकर्मा समुदायले पवित्र खड्ग बोकेर बन्दिपुरभर जुलुस निकाल्छन्।\", \"यो खड्ग राजा मुकुन्द सेनको थियो भन्ने विश्वास गरिन्छ।\", \"मन्दिर दशैंको एक दिन, फूलपातीमा मात्र खुल्छ।\", \"गर्भगृहमा खड्गमाईको मूर्ति छ, र नजिकै पाटी र ठूला पिपलका रूख छन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Khadga Jatra\", \"note\": \"During Dashain a sacred sword is worshipped and paraded through Bandipur; the temple opens on Fulpati.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"खड्ग जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"दशैंमा पवित्र खड्गको पूजा गरिन्छ र बन्दिपुरभर जुलुस निकालिन्छ; मन्दिर फूलपातीका दिन खुल्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The shrine in its wide hilltop ground\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Side view of the red-brick temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(2).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%284%29.jpg/1280px-Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%284%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Temple building and entrance steps\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(4).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%285%29.jpg/1280px-Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%285%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Stone steps leading up to the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(5).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%289%29.jpg/1280px-Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%289%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The temple seen across the open ground\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khadga_Mai_Temple_Bandipur_Tanahu_Gandaki_Pradesh_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(9).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Boxy two-storey bright red-brick shrine with a single pitched tiled roof and small top lantern, steps up to a central door, in a wide paved ground with pipal trees.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#c0482e\", \"#7a3324\", \"#d9b44a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-windows\", \"bell\", \"sacred-tree\"], \"height_m\": 9, \"footprint_m\": [9, 7], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"stone-paved-plaza\", \"village\", \"sacred-grove\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(21,'lo-manthang-walled-city','Lo Manthang Walled City','लोमान्थाङ','Lo Manthang','Gandaki','Mustang',NULL,29.182730,83.956770,'fort','Buddhist','Shakyamuni Buddha (Thubchen), Maitreya (Jampa Lhakhang)',1380,'Founded in 1380 by Ame Pal, first king of Lo, who built the city wall; the four-storey royal palace is dated to 1440. Thubchen and Jampa Lhakhang monasteries date from the 15th century.','Kings of Lo (Bista line descended from Ame Pal)','Compact fortified town of whitewashed and ochre mud-brick houses inside a rammed-earth and stone wall entered by one gate. The nine-cornered royal palace is of mud, stone and wood; red-walled Thubchen (37.2 x 24 m, 12 m high, 35 wooden pillars) and Jampa Lhakhang hold 15th-century murals.',0,'The 14th-century walled capital of the Kingdom of Lo in Upper Mustang, with a royal palace and 15th-century painted monasteries.','Pass through the single gate in this earthen wall and you are inside the capital of a kingdom that lasted more than six hundred years. Ame Pal, the warrior who founded the Kingdom of Lo, built this walled city in 1380, and his descendants ruled from here until Nepal became a republic in 2008. Around you are whitewashed houses with firewood stacked on their flat roofs, narrow alleys, and above them the many-cornered royal palace. Now look for the great red walls of the monasteries. Thubchen Lhakhang, from the 15th century, is held up by thirty-five wooden pillars, and its murals glow with turquoise, malachite and gold. Jampa Lhakhang, the Maitreya temple, holds what is said to be the world\'s largest collection of painted mandalas. Outside the wall stretch green barley fields in a desert of eroded cliffs. Upper Mustang was closed to outsiders until 1992, and foreigners still need a special permit to come here.',NULL,'[\"Lo Manthang was founded in 1380 by Ame Pal, who oversaw construction of the city wall.\", \"The last raja of Mustang, Jigme Dorje Palbar Bista, lost his title when Nepal became a republic in 2008.\", \"Jampa Lhakhang contains what is described as the world\'s largest collection of mandalas painted on its walls.\", \"Upper Mustang was closed to outsiders until 1992; foreigners need a special permit costing US$500 for ten days.\", \"The royal palace, damaged in 2015, was restored with help from the Gerda Henkel Foundation by 2073 BS.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,240,'The April 2015 earthquake damaged the royal palace, later restored with the Gerda Henkel Foundation, and severely damaged the 500-year-old wall paintings of Jampa Lhakhang.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Lo_Manthang%2C_The_Historic_Walled_City_of_Upper_Mustang.jpg/1280px-Lo_Manthang%2C_The_Historic_Walled_City_of_Upper_Mustang.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lo_Manthang,_The_Historic_Walled_City_of_Upper_Mustang.jpg','Pratikshyabhatta · CC BY-SA 4.0','fort,buddhist,kings of lo (bista line descended from ame pal),lo manthang,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lo_Manthang\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lo_Manthang_Palace\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thubchen_Lhakang_Monastery\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jampa_Lhakang_Monastery\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upper_Mustang\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q105753160\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Lo_Manthang\"]','माथिल्लो मुस्ताङमा रहेको लो राज्यको चौधौँ शताब्दीको पर्खालले घेरिएको राजधानी, जहाँ शाही दरबार र पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीका चित्रित गुम्बा छन्।','यो माटोको पर्खालको एउटै ढोकाबाट भित्र पस्नुहोस्; तपाईं छ सय वर्षभन्दा बढी टिकेको एउटा राज्यको राजधानीभित्र हुनुहुन्छ। लो राज्य स्थापना गर्ने योद्धा अमे पालले सन् 1380 मा यो पर्खालले घेरिएको सहर बनाए, र उनका सन्तानले सन् 2008 मा नेपाल गणतन्त्र नबनुन्जेल यहीँबाट शासन गरे। वरिपरि सेता पोतिएका घर छन्, तिनका सपाट छानामा दाउरा थुपारिएको छ। साँघुरा गल्ली छन्, र तिनको माथि धेरै कुना भएको शाही दरबार छ। अब गुम्बाका ठूला रातो भित्ता खोज्नुहोस्। पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीको थुबचेन ल्हाखाङ पैँतीस वटा काठका खम्बामा अडिएको छ, र यसका भित्ते चित्र फिरोजा, मालाकाइट र सुनले चम्किन्छन्। जम्पा ल्हाखाङ, मैत्रेयको मन्दिर, मा संसारकै सबैभन्दा ठूलो चित्रित मण्डलको सङ्ग्रह छ भनिन्छ। पर्खालबाहिर खिइएका पहाडी भिरको मरुभूमिबीच हरिया जौका खेत फैलिएका छन्। माथिल्लो मुस्ताङ सन् 1992 सम्म बाहिरी मानिसका लागि बन्द थियो, र विदेशीलाई अझै यहाँ आउन विशेष अनुमतिपत्र चाहिन्छ।',NULL,'[\"लोमान्थाङ सन् 1380 मा अमे पालले स्थापना गरेका हुन्, जसले सहरको पर्खाल बनाउन लगाए।\", \"मुस्ताङका अन्तिम राजा जिग्मे दोर्जे पाल्बार बिस्टाले सन् 2008 मा नेपाल गणतन्त्र बनेपछि राजाको पदवी गुमाए।\", \"जम्पा ल्हाखाङमा भित्तामा चित्रित मण्डलको संसारकै सबैभन्दा ठूलो सङ्ग्रह रहेको भनिन्छ।\", \"माथिल्लो मुस्ताङ सन् 1992 सम्म बाहिरी मानिसका लागि बन्द थियो; विदेशीले दश दिनका लागि अमेरिकी डलर 500 पर्ने विशेष अनुमतिपत्र लिनुपर्छ।\", \"सन् 2015 मा क्षति भएको शाही दरबार गेर्डा हेन्केल फाउन्डेसनको सहयोगमा वि.सं. 2073 सम्ममा पुनर्स्थापना गरियो।\"]','सन् 2015 अप्रिलको भूकम्पले शाही दरबारमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो, जुन पछि गेर्डा हेन्केल फाउन्डेसनको सहयोगमा पुनर्स्थापना गरियो, र जम्पा ल्हाखाङका पाँच सय वर्ष पुराना भित्ते चित्रमा गम्भीर क्षति पुर्‍यायो।','[{\"name\": \"Tiji\", \"note\": \"Spring masked-dance festival in Lo Manthang (about May; dates follow the Tibetan lunar calendar).\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"टिजी\", \"note_np\": \"लोमान्थाङमा वसन्त ऋतुमा हुने मुखुन्डा नाचको चाड (करिब मे महिनामा; मिति तिब्बती चन्द्र पात्रोअनुसार)।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Lo_Manthang_Royal_Palace.JPG/1280px-Lo_Manthang_Royal_Palace.JPG\", \"author\": \"Wimbex\", \"caption\": \"The royal palace inside the walled city\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lo_Manthang_Royal_Palace.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Mustang-Lo_Manthang-17-Thubchen_Lhakhang-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Mustang-Lo_Manthang-17-Thubchen_Lhakhang-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Red walls of Thubchen Lhakhang\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mustang-Lo_Manthang-17-Thubchen_Lhakhang-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Mustang-Lo_Manthang-40-Jampa_Lhakhang-gje.jpg/1280px-Mustang-Lo_Manthang-40-Jampa_Lhakhang-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Jampa Lhakhang monastery building\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mustang-Lo_Manthang-40-Jampa_Lhakhang-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Mustang-Lo_Manthang-30-Choede_Lhakhang-Weltenhueter_Sued_Virudhaka_mit_Schwert_und_Vollbart-gje.jpg/1280px-Mustang-Lo_Manthang-30-Choede_Lhakhang-Weltenhueter_Sued_Virudhaka_mit_Schwert_und_Vollbart-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Mural of a guardian king in Choede Lhakhang\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mustang-Lo_Manthang-30-Choede_Lhakhang-Weltenhueter_Sued_Virudhaka_mit_Schwert_und_Vollbart-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Alley_in_Lo_Manthang.jpg/1280px-Alley_in_Lo_Manthang.jpg\", \"author\": \"Carsten.nebel\", \"caption\": \"Whitewashed houses along an alley\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alley_in_Lo_Manthang.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Mustang-Lo_Manthang-06-Dachausflug-gje.jpg/1280px-Mustang-Lo_Manthang-06-Dachausflug-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Rooftop view over the red monasteries\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mustang-Lo_Manthang-06-Dachausflug-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"fort\", \"roof\": \"flat\", \"notes\": \"Dense block of flat-roofed white and grey mud houses inside an earthen wall, with a tall many-cornered palace and big blood-red monastery halls, ringed by green fields in brown desert.\", \"tiers\": 4, \"walls\": \"whitewashed-stone\", \"colors\": [\"#e8e2d4\", \"#a8322a\", \"#9c8a6a\"], \"features\": [\"watchtower\", \"prayer-flags\", \"chaityas\", \"prayer-wheels\"], \"height_m\": 12, \"footprint_m\": [300, 200], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"desert-cliffs\", \"terraced-fields\", \"monks-houses\", \"snow-peaks\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(22,'kagbeni-kag-chode-monastery','Kagbeni and Kag Chode Monastery','कागबेनी गुम्बा','Kagbeni','Gandaki','Mustang',NULL,28.837647,83.783574,'monastery','Buddhist','Buddha (Sakya tradition monastery)',1429,'Kag Chode Thupten Samphel Ling monastery was founded in 1429 CE, credited to the monk Tenpai Gyaltsen; its old wing is described as about 500 years old. The ruined Kag Khar fort-palace is older by local tradition.','unknown','Red-painted Tibetan-style gompa of rammed earth and timber on a spur above the Kali Gandaki, with an old wing and a newer building. The village is a tight cluster of flat-roofed mud-brick houses, chortens, and the four-storey adobe ruin of Kag Khar.',0,'Medieval fortified village at the gate of Upper Mustang, crowned by the red 15th-century Sakya monastery of Kag Chode.','Welcome to Kagbeni, a village of mud-brick houses and narrow tunnels at the meeting of two rivers, where the Kali Gandaki valley opens towards the old Kingdom of Lo. Beni means confluence, and pilgrims bound for Muktinath stop on these stony banks; Hindu families perform shraddha rites here for their ancestors. Look up at the blood-red walls on the spur above the river. That is Kag Chode Thupten Samphel Ling, a Sakya monastery founded in 1429 and remembered as the work of the monk Tenpai Gyaltsen. Its rammed-earth walls were built to resist both earthquakes and attackers. Nearby stand the crumbling adobe towers of Kag Khar, the old palace of a local king. At the village gates, look for the kheni, carved male and female guardians called ghost eaters, who replaced human sentries long ago. North of here begins Upper Mustang, where foreign visitors need a special permit to continue.','The kheni, a pair of male and female carved figures at the village gates, are believed to guard Kagbeni against evil and supernatural forces, earning them the name \'ghost eaters\'.','[\"Kag Chode Thupten Samphel Ling, the \'Red Monastery\', was founded in 1429 and belongs to the Sakya tradition.\", \"Kagbeni lies in the Kali Gandaki valley, on the trail from Jomsom to Lo Manthang near the turn to Muktinath.\", \"Foreign visitors need a special Upper Mustang permit to travel north of Kagbeni.\", \"The 2011 census counted 555 people in the village.\", \"An August 2023 flood on the Kagbeni river damaged the area and threatened the monastery.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Kag_Chode_Gompa%2C_Kagbeni.jpg/1280px-Kag_Chode_Gompa%2C_Kagbeni.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kag_Chode_Gompa,_Kagbeni.jpg','Sgnpkd · CC BY-SA 3.0','monastery,buddhist,kagbeni,legend,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kagbeni\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/297420323\", \"https://www.insidehimalayas.com/secrets-and-history-of-kagbeni-mustang/\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/tatopani-to-marpha/hotels/eagle-nest-guest-house/a/poi-sle/1506805/1341927\", \"https://teahouse.buddhistdoor.net/floods-in-mustang-nepal-threaten-historic-monastery-of-kag-chode-thupten-samphel-ling/\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/a-beautiful-tibetan-village-kagbeni\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Kagbeni\"]','माथिल्लो मुस्ताङको प्रवेशद्वारमा रहेको मध्यकालीन किल्लाबन्दी गाउँ, जहाँ पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीको रातो साक्य गुम्बा काग छोडे छ।','कागबेनीमा स्वागत छ। माटो-इँटाका घर र साँघुरा सुरुङजस्ता गल्ली भएको यो गाउँ दुई नदी मिल्ने ठाउँमा छ, जहाँबाट कालीगण्डकी उपत्यका पुरानो लो राज्यतिर खुल्छ। बेनी भनेको सङ्गम हो; मुक्तिनाथ जाने तीर्थयात्री यी ढुङ्गैढुङ्गाका किनारमा रोकिन्छन्, र हिन्दू परिवारले यहाँ पितृको श्राद्ध गर्छन्। नदीमाथिको डाँडामा रगत रङका भित्ता हेर्नुहोस्। त्यो काग छोडे थुप्तेन साम्फेल लिङ हो, सन् 1429 मा स्थापना भएको साक्य गुम्बा, जुन भिक्षु तेन्पाई ग्याल्त्सेनले बनाएको भनेर सम्झिन्छन्। यसका माटो थिचेर बनाएका भित्ता भूकम्प र आक्रमण दुवै सहने गरी बनाइएका थिए। नजिकै स्थानीय राजाको पुरानो दरबार कागखारका भत्किँदै गरेका माटोका टावर छन्। गाउँको ढोकामा खेनी भनिने कुँदिएका पुरुष र स्त्री रक्षक हेर्नुहोस्, जसलाई भूत खाने भनिन्छ; धेरै पहिले मानिस पहरेदारको सट्टा यिनै राखिन्थे। यहाँबाट उत्तरतिर माथिल्लो मुस्ताङ सुरु हुन्छ, जहाँ अगाडि जान विदेशीलाई विशेष अनुमतिपत्र चाहिन्छ।','गाउँको ढोकामा रहेका कुँदिएका पुरुष र स्त्रीका जोडी खेनीले कागबेनीलाई खराब र अलौकिक शक्तिबाट जोगाउँछन् भन्ने विश्वास छ, त्यसैले तिनलाई \'भूत खाने\' भनिन्छ।','[\"काग छोडे थुप्तेन साम्फेल लिङ, \'रातो गुम्बा\', सन् 1429 मा स्थापना भएको हो र साक्य परम्पराको हो।\", \"कागबेनी कालीगण्डकी उपत्यकामा, जोमसोमदेखि लोमान्थाङ जाने बाटोमा मुक्तिनाथतिर मोडिने ठाउँ नजिकै पर्छ।\", \"कागबेनीभन्दा उत्तर जान विदेशी पर्यटकलाई माथिल्लो मुस्ताङको विशेष अनुमतिपत्र चाहिन्छ।\", \"सन् 2011 को जनगणनाले गाउँमा 555 जना बासिन्दा गन्यो।\", \"सन् 2023 अगस्टमा कागबेनीको खोलामा आएको बाढीले क्षेत्रमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो र गुम्बालाई खतरामा पार्‍यो।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/A_kheni_%28ghost_eater%29_in_Kagbeni_-_note_what_hes_wielding._%284523541547%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa\", \"caption\": \"A kheni (ghost eater) guardian figure in Kagbeni\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_kheni_(ghost_eater)_in_Kagbeni_-_note_what_hes_wielding._(4523541547).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/A_traditional_chorten_in_Kagbeni_Mustang-WLV-0781.jpg/1280px-A_traditional_chorten_in_Kagbeni_Mustang-WLV-0781.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay Chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"A traditional chorten in Kagbeni\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_traditional_chorten_in_Kagbeni_Mustang-WLV-0781.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Kagbeni_Monastery.jpg/1280px-Kagbeni_Monastery.jpg\", \"author\": \"Jmhullot\", \"caption\": \"The red monastery of Kagbeni\", \"license\": \"CC BY 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kagbeni_Monastery.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kagbeni_Mustang_%28144%29.jpg/1280px-Kagbeni_Mustang_%28144%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Kagbeni village in the Kali Gandaki valley\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kagbeni_Mustang_(144).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Kag_chode%2CBuddhist_Temple_at_Kagbeni%2C_Mustang%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Kag_chode%2CBuddhist_Temple_at_Kagbeni%2C_Mustang%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nyoupaneroshan\", \"caption\": \"Kag Chode monastery building\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kag_chode,Buddhist_Temple_at_Kagbeni,_Mustang,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"gumba\", \"roof\": \"flat\", \"notes\": \"Large flat-roofed blood-red monastery block on a spur above a grey braided river, over a huddle of mud houses and ruined adobe towers, bare brown cliffs behind.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"ochre-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#9e2b25\", \"#d8cfbd\", \"#7d6a52\"], \"features\": [\"prayer-flags\", \"prayer-wheels\", \"chaityas\"], \"height_m\": 10, \"footprint_m\": [30, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"village\", \"river\", \"desert-cliffs\", \"terraced-fields\", \"snow-peaks\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(23,'galeshwor-dham','Galeshwor Dham','गलेश्वर धाम','Beni (Myagdi)','Gandaki','Myagdi',NULL,28.372324,83.568233,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva as Galeshwor, a self-manifested jyotirlinga',NULL,'Worship at the site is described as ancient; the date of the present temple building is not documented in the sources found. A donor gilded its pinnacle (gajur) in Mangsir 2082 BS (2025).','unknown','Two-tiered pagoda-roofed Shiva temple standing on a single huge rock of about three ropani at the river\'s edge, with stone steps down to the water and a narrow rock pool beside it whose level is said to stay constant all year.',0,'Riverside Shiva shrine on a great rock where the Rahughat meets the Kali Gandaki, north of Beni: the \'gateway to Muktinath\'.','Listen to the rivers. Here, about three kilometres north of Beni, the Rahughat stream rushes into the grey Kali Gandaki, and on a single enormous rock at their meeting stands Galeshwor, a temple of Shiva. Inside is a jyotirlinga believed to be swayambhu, self-manifested. The name comes from a legend: as Shiva carried the body of his wife Sati towards the Himalaya, her neck, gala in Nepali, fell here and took the form of Shiva. That is why pilgrims call this place the gateway to Muktinath; many stop here before heading up the Kali Gandaki valley. Beside the temple, between the rocks, lies a long narrow pool. People say it never dries in winter and never overflows in the monsoon. On Maha Shivaratri, crowds start gathering at four in the morning, coming from Myagdi, Baglung, Mustang, Parbat and Kaski to light a great lamp and offer prayers. In late 2025 a donor gilded the temple\'s pinnacle.','While Shiva carried the body of Sati towards the Himalaya, her neck (gala) fell at this spot and took the form of Shiva; hence the name Galeshwor, \'Lord of the neck\'.','[\"Galeshwor lies about 3 km north of Beni, the headquarters of Myagdi district, in Beni Municipality ward 9.\", \"The temple stands where the Rahughat (Rahu) river joins the Kali Gandaki.\", \"It is known as the gateway to Muktinath and is visited by both Hindus and Buddhists.\", \"More than 50,000 devotees were expected on Maha Shivaratri 2081 BS, according to the local development fund.\", \"The pool beside the temple is said to keep the same water level all year round.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Galeshwor.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galeshwor.jpg','PawilStha · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,beni (myagdi),legend,water,art,festival,gandaki','[\"https://ekantipur.com/pradesh-4/2025/02/26/crowd-of-devotees-at-galeshwar-temple-49-15.html\", \"https://ekantipur.com/gandaki-pradesh/2025/11/20/en/galeshwar-temple-shines-with-golden-light-in-gajur-27-08.html\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/5300595245\", \"https://hopnepal.com/blog/myagdi-district-gandaki-province\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galeshwor.jpg\"]','बेनीको उत्तरमा राहुघाट र कालीगण्डकी भेटिने ठाउँको ठूलो चट्टानमाथिको शिव मन्दिर: \'मुक्तिनाथको प्रवेशद्वार\'।','नदीको आवाज सुन्नुहोस्। यहाँ, बेनीभन्दा करिब तीन किलोमिटर उत्तरमा, राहुघाट खोला खैरो कालीगण्डकीमा जोडिन्छ, र तिनको सङ्गममा एउटै विशाल चट्टानमाथि शिवको मन्दिर गलेश्वर उभिएको छ। भित्र स्वयम्भू, अर्थात् आफैँ प्रकट भएको ज्योतिर्लिङ्ग छ भन्ने विश्वास छ। नाम एउटा कथाबाट आएको हो: शिवले पत्नी सतीको शव बोकेर हिमालतिर जाँदा उनको गला, नेपालीमा गला, यहीँ खस्यो र शिवको रूप लियो। त्यसैले तीर्थयात्री यस ठाउँलाई मुक्तिनाथको प्रवेशद्वार भन्छन्; धेरै मानिस कालीगण्डकी उपत्यका उक्लनुअघि यहीँ रोकिन्छन्। मन्दिरको छेउमा चट्टानबीच एउटा लामो साँघुरो कुण्ड छ। मानिस भन्छन्, यो जाडोमा कहिल्यै सुक्दैन र बर्खामा कहिल्यै बाहिर पोखिँदैन। महाशिवरात्रिमा बिहान चार बजेदेखि म्याग्दी, बाग्लुङ, मुस्ताङ, पर्वत र कास्कीबाट भक्तजन भेला भएर ठूलो दीप बाल्न र पूजा गर्न आउँछन्। सन् 2025 को अन्त्यमा एक दाताले मन्दिरको गजुर सुनले मोहोरिदिए।','शिवले सतीको शव बोकेर हिमालतिर जाँदा उनको गला (गला) यही ठाउँमा खस्यो र शिवको रूप लियो; त्यसैले यसको नाम गलेश्वर, अर्थात् \'गलाका ईश्वर\' भयो।','[\"गलेश्वर म्याग्दी जिल्लाको सदरमुकाम बेनीभन्दा करिब 3 किमी उत्तरमा, बेनी नगरपालिका वडा नं. 9 मा छ।\", \"मन्दिर राहुघाट (राहु) खोला कालीगण्डकीमा मिल्ने ठाउँमा छ।\", \"यो मुक्तिनाथको प्रवेशद्वारका रूपमा चिनिन्छ र हिन्दू र बौद्ध दुवैले दर्शन गर्छन्।\", \"स्थानीय विकास कोषका अनुसार वि.सं. 2081 को महाशिवरात्रिमा 50,000 भन्दा बढी भक्तजन आउने अपेक्षा गरिएको थियो।\", \"मन्दिरछेउको कुण्डको पानीको सतह वर्षभरि उही रहन्छ भनिन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Largest fair of the year; devotees from five districts offer puja and light a great lamp (mahadeep).\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"वर्षको सबैभन्दा ठूलो मेला; पाँच जिल्लाका भक्तजन पूजा गर्छन् र ठूलो दीप (महादीप) बाल्छन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Shrawan Mondays\", \"note\": \"Fairs are held on the Mondays of Shrawan.\", \"month\": \"Shrawan\", \"name_np\": \"श्रावण सोमबार\", \"note_np\": \"श्रावण महिनाका सोमबार मेला लाग्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Bala Chaturdashi\", \"note\": \"A fair is held at the temple on Bala Chaturdashi.\", \"month\": \"Mangsir\", \"name_np\": \"बाला चतुर्दशी\", \"note_np\": \"बाला चतुर्दशीका दिन मन्दिरमा मेला लाग्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Beni_galeshwor.jpg/1280px-Beni_galeshwor.jpg\", \"author\": \"Amrit Poudel\", \"caption\": \"The temple seen from the Beni side\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beni_galeshwor.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Temple_galeshwor.jpg/1280px-Temple_galeshwor.jpg\", \"author\": \"Amrit Poudel\", \"caption\": \"The pagoda temple on its rock\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Temple_galeshwor.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/19/Steps_from_river_to_Galeshwor_temple_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Raj Joshi\", \"caption\": \"Steps leading down from the temple to the river\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steps_from_river_to_Galeshwor_temple_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cb/Viewing_north_from_Galeshwor_temple_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Raj Joshi\", \"caption\": \"Looking north up the valley from the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viewing_north_from_Galeshwor_temple_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/Swostika_at_Galeshwor_temple_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Raj Joshi\", \"caption\": \"Swastika mosaic at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swostika_at_Galeshwor_temple_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/Lord_Bishnu_in_Galeshwor_temple_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Raj Joshi\", \"caption\": \"Image of Vishnu at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lord_Bishnu_in_Galeshwor_temple_-_panoramio.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Two-roofed pagoda with red roofs, cream-yellow walls and a gold pinnacle perched on a huge riverside rock in a steep green gorge, stone steps down to a grey river.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"ochre-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#b8402e\", \"#e3c873\", \"#c9a23a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"bell\", \"trident\", \"ghat-steps\", \"rock-face\"], \"height_m\": 10, \"footprint_m\": [8, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"riverbank-ghats\", \"forest\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(24,'devghat-dham','Devghat Dham','देवघाट धाम','Devghat (near Narayangadh)','Gandaki','Tanahun',NULL,27.742939,84.423081,'ghat','Hindu','Shiva and Vishnu (Harihar); Vishnu worshipped as Shaligram',NULL,'An ancient pilgrimage site; the start of its Makar Sankranti bathing fair is unknown. Its many temples, ashrams and the suspension bridge are of various modern dates.','unknown','A riverside pilgrimage town of small Hindu temples, ashrams, caves and bathing ghats along the meeting of the Trishuli and Kali Gandaki, joined across the river by a long suspension bridge linking Tanahun and Chitwan.',0,'Sacred confluence of the Trishuli and Kali Gandaki near Narayangadh, famed for its Maghe Sankranti bathing fair.','Stand on the stone steps and watch two great rivers become one. From the north-west comes the Kali Gandaki, which began near Muktinath; from the north-east comes the Trishuli, fed by Gosaikunda. Here at Devghat they meet and flow on together as the Narayani. Hindus call this place Harihar Kshetra, holy to both Shiva and Vishnu, and they search the gravel for Shaligram stones, worshipped as Vishnu himself. The sage Vasistha is said to have made his ashram here, and you will find temples, quiet ashrams and even a cave linked to the goddess Sita. Many elderly Hindus come to spend their last years beside these waters. Cross the swaying suspension bridge and you step from Tanahun into Chitwan. If you come on Maghe Sankranti in January, join the crowd: hundreds of thousands of pilgrims bathe at the confluence in one of the largest melas in Nepal. Nobody knows when this festival began.','The sage Vasistha is believed to have established his ashram and performed his austerities at Devghat.','[\"Devghat lies at the confluence of the Trishuli and Kali (Krishna) Gandaki rivers, about 7 km from Narayangadh.\", \"Below the confluence the combined river is known as the Narayani.\", \"Its Makar (Maghe) Sankranti mela is one of the largest religious fairs in Nepal; one report estimated over three lakh visitors.\", \"A historic suspension bridge links the Tanahun and Chitwan sides of the town.\", \"Pilgrims bathe and seek Shaligram stones, which Hindus worship as Vishnu.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,120,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%98%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9F_%28Devghat%29.jpg/1280px-%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%98%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9F_%28Devghat%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%98%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9F_(Devghat).jpg','Prakash Gopali85 · CC BY-SA 4.0','ghat,hindu,devghat (near narayangadh),legend,art,festival,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devghat\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/9798944138\", \"https://ekantipur.com/bagmati-pradesh/2025/01/14/en/at-devghat-the-crowd-of-makarsanaan-from-early-morning-49-12.html\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/travel/pilgrimage-sites/devghat\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%98%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9F_(Devghat).jpg\"]','नारायणगढ नजिक त्रिशूली र कालीगण्डकीको पवित्र सङ्गम, माघे सङ्क्रान्तिको स्नान मेलाका लागि प्रसिद्ध।','ढुङ्गाका भ्याङमा उभिएर दुई ठूला नदीलाई एक हुँदै गरेको हेर्नुहोस्। उत्तरपश्चिमबाट कालीगण्डकी आउँछ, जसको उद्गम मुक्तिनाथ नजिक हो; उत्तरपूर्वबाट त्रिशूली आउँछ, जसलाई गोसाइँकुण्डले पानी दिन्छ। यहाँ देवघाटमा तिनी भेटिन्छन् र नारायणी भएर सँगै बग्छन्। हिन्दूहरू यस ठाउँलाई हरिहर क्षेत्र भन्छन्, शिव र विष्णु दुवैको पवित्र स्थान, र तिनीहरू बालुवा-गिट्टीमा शालिग्राम ढुङ्गा खोज्छन्, जसलाई विष्णु नै मानेर पुजिन्छ। ऋषि वशिष्ठले यहीँ आश्रम बनाएका थिए भनिन्छ, र यहाँ मन्दिर, शान्त आश्रम र सीतासँग जोडिने गुफासमेत भेटिन्छन्। धेरै वृद्ध हिन्दू आफ्नो अन्तिम समय यिनै नदीको छेउमा बिताउन आउँछन्। हल्लिने झोलुङ्गे पुल तरेर तपाईं तनहुँबाट चितवनमा पुग्नुहुन्छ। माघे सङ्क्रान्तिमा, जनवरीमा, आउनुभयो भने भीडमा सामेल हुनुहोस्: नेपालकै ठूला मेलामध्ये एकमा सङ्गममा नुहाउन लाखौँ तीर्थयात्री आउँछन्। यो चाड कहिलेदेखि सुरु भयो, कसैलाई थाहा छैन।','ऋषि वशिष्ठले देवघाटमा आश्रम बनाएर तपस्या गरेका थिए भन्ने विश्वास छ।','[\"देवघाट त्रिशूली र कालीगण्डकी (कृष्णगण्डकी) नदीको सङ्गममा, नारायणगढबाट करिब 7 किमी टाढा छ।\", \"सङ्गमपछि मिलेको नदीलाई नारायणी भनिन्छ।\", \"यसको मकर (माघे) सङ्क्रान्ति मेला नेपालका सबैभन्दा ठूला धार्मिक मेलामध्ये एक हो; एक रिपोर्टले तीन लाखभन्दा बढी आगन्तुकको अनुमान गरेको थियो।\", \"एउटा ऐतिहासिक झोलुङ्गे पुलले सहरको तनहुँ र चितवनतर्फलाई जोड्छ।\", \"तीर्थयात्री यहाँ नुहाउँछन् र शालिग्राम ढुङ्गा खोज्छन्, जसलाई हिन्दूहरू विष्णु मानेर पुज्छन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Maghe Sankranti (Makar Snan)\", \"note\": \"Two-day mela starting the day before Sankranti; pilgrims bathe at the confluence.\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"माघे सङ्क्रान्ति (मकर स्नान)\", \"note_np\": \"सङ्क्रान्तिअघिको दिनदेखि सुरु हुने दुई दिने मेला; तीर्थयात्री सङ्गममा नुहाउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Devghat_suspension_bridge.jpg/1280px-Devghat_suspension_bridge.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nepalpicturesque\", \"caption\": \"Suspension bridge across the river at Devghat\", \"license\": \"CC BY 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devghat_suspension_bridge.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Devghat_Dham4.jpg/1280px-Devghat_Dham4.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Bhatta\", \"caption\": \"Confluence of the rivers at Devghat\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devghat_Dham4.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Devghat_temple.jpg/1280px-Devghat_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pranish subedi\", \"caption\": \"A temple at Devghat\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devghat_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Bageshwori_Temple_Devghat_Chitwan_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Bageshwori_Temple_Devghat_Chitwan_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Bageshwori Temple in the Devghat forest\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bageshwori_Temple_Devghat_Chitwan_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AF%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%B0_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0.JPG/1280px-%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AF%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%B0_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0.JPG\", \"author\": \"चिरञ्जीविखतिवडाः\", \"caption\": \"Vidyeshwar temple at Mahesh Sanskrit Gurukul, Devghat\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AF%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%B0_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Pashupati_Temple_in_Devghat.jpg/1280px-Pashupati_Temple_in_Devghat.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nawrj\", \"caption\": \"Pashupati (Shiva) temple at Devghat Dham at night\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pashupati_Temple_in_Devghat.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Wide river junction with sandbanks; on the point a cluster of small temples and ashrams among trees, stone bathing steps, and a long suspension bridge across the water.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#5f8a7a\", \"#d9d2c0\", \"#b8402e\"], \"features\": [\"ghat-steps\", \"trident\", \"bell\", \"lamps-diyo\", \"shiva-lingam\"], \"height_m\": 8, \"footprint_m\": [120, 60], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"riverbank-ghats\", \"forest\", \"village\", \"plains-fields\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(25,'siddha-cave-bimalnagar','Siddha Cave','सिद्ध गुफा','Bimalnagar (Bandipur)','Gandaki','Tanahun',NULL,27.948380,84.418520,'cave','Hindu','Shiva (rock formations venerated as his symbols; small shrine inside)',NULL,'A natural limestone (karst) cave. Local lore says a woman collecting herbs found it in 1989; German speleologists explored and surveyed it in 1990 and 1991.','unknown','Natural karst cave in layered limestone, entered from a forested slope above the Prithvi Highway. Wikipedia gives it 437 m deep and 50 m high; showcaves.com records 758 m of passages and 105 m vertical range. Stalactites and stalagmites fill the chambers.',0,'Huge limestone cave above Bimalnagar on the trail to Bandipur, full of stalactites and venerated by Shiva pilgrims.','Switch on your headlamp and let your eyes adjust. You are inside Siddha Gufa, one of the largest caves in Nepal, which opens high on the hillside above Bimalnagar, on the old trail up to Bandipur. Local lore says a woman gathering herbs stumbled on the entrance in 1989, and German cave explorers mapped it in 1990 and 1991. Wikipedia gives its depth as 437 metres and its height as about 50 metres, enough room, it is said, for 2,500 people. Look at the walls: layers of brown and white limestone, and formations that guides compare to an elephant, snake heads, butterflies and turtles. For pilgrims, these shapes are signs of Shiva, and a small shrine stands inside, along with a shelter where meditators sometimes stay. Listen too; clusters of bats hang in the darkness above you. Watch your step on the slippery path and ladders, and come back out to daylight and the green Marsyangdi hills.','Pilgrims regard the cave\'s rock formations as natural symbols of Shiva, and the cave has long been used by meditators, as its name \'Siddha\' (an accomplished ascetic) suggests.','[\"Wikipedia gives the cave a depth of 437 m and a height of 50 m, with room for about 2,500 people.\", \"Local lore says it was found in 1989 by a woman collecting herbs; German speleologists surveyed it in 1990-91.\", \"Showcaves.com lists 758 m of passages and a vertical range of 105 m, calling it Nepal\'s deepest known cave.\", \"The entrance is about 30 minutes\' walk uphill from Bimal Bazaar on the Prithvi Highway.\", \"Bats roost inside, and there is a small Shiva shrine.\"]','10:00','17:00',100,100,100,90,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar%2C_Nepal-WLV-1986.jpg/1280px-Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar%2C_Nepal-WLV-1986.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar,_Nepal-WLV-1986.jpg','Bijay Chaurasia · CC BY-SA 4.0','cave,hindu,bimalnagar (bandipur),legend,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siddha_Cave\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q16920737\", \"https://showcaves.com/english/np/showcaves/Siddha.html\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/travel/2019/09/06/finding-faces-in-siddha-gufa\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Siddha_cave,_Bandipur\"]','बन्दिपुर जाने बाटोमा बिमलनगर माथि रहेको ठूलो चूनढुङ्गाको गुफा, स्टालाक्टाइटले भरिएको र शिवका भक्तजनले पुज्ने ठाउँ।','हेडल्याम्प बालेर आँखा अँध्यारोमा अभ्यस्त हुन दिनुहोस्। तपाईं सिद्ध गुफाभित्र हुनुहुन्छ, नेपालकै ठूला गुफामध्ये एक, जसको मुख बन्दिपुर जाने पुरानो बाटोमा बिमलनगर माथिको डाँडामा छ। स्थानीयले भन्छन्, सन् 1989 मा जडीबुटी टिप्दै गरेकी एक महिलाले अनायासै गुफाको मुख भेटेकी थिइन्, र जर्मन गुफा अन्वेषकले सन् 1990 र 1991 मा यसको नक्सा बनाए। विकिपिडियाले यसको गहिराइ 437 मिटर र उचाइ करिब 50 मिटर भनेको छ, जहाँ 2,500 जना अट्छन् भनिन्छ। भित्ताहरू हेर्नुहोस्: खैरो र सेतो चूनढुङ्गाका तह, र गाइडले हात्ती, सर्पको टाउको, पुतली र कछुवासँग तुलना गर्ने आकृति। तीर्थयात्रीका लागि यी आकृति शिवका चिह्न हुन्, र भित्र सानो मन्दिर र कहिलेकाहीँ ध्यान गर्नेहरू बस्ने बास पनि छ। कान थाप्नुहोस् पनि; माथिको अँध्यारोमा चमेराका झुन्ड झुन्डिएका हुन्छन्। चिप्लो बाटो र भ्याङमा होसियारसँग पाइला राख्नुहोस्, अनि बाहिर निस्केर दिउँसोको उज्यालो र मर्स्याङ्दीका हरिया डाँडा हेर्नुहोस्।','तीर्थयात्रीले गुफाका चट्टानका आकृतिलाई शिवका प्राकृतिक चिह्न मान्छन्, र \'सिद्ध\' (सिद्धि पाएका तपस्वी) नामले जनाएझैँ यो गुफा लामो समयदेखि ध्यान गर्नेहरूले प्रयोग गर्दै आएका छन्।','[\"विकिपिडियाले गुफाको गहिराइ 437 मिटर र उचाइ 50 मिटर भनेको छ, जहाँ करिब 2,500 जना अट्छन्।\", \"स्थानीय कथनअनुसार जडीबुटी टिप्ने एक महिलाले सन् 1989 मा यो भेटेकी थिइन्; जर्मन गुफा अन्वेषकले सन् 1990-91 मा सर्भे गरे।\", \"शोकेभ्स डटकमले 758 मिटर बाटो र 105 मिटर ठाडो फरक सूचीबद्ध गरेको छ, र यसलाई नेपालको सबैभन्दा गहिरो ज्ञात गुफा भनेको छ।\", \"गुफाको मुखसम्म पृथ्वी राजमार्गको बिमल बजारबाट करिब 30 मिनेट उकालो हिँड्नुपर्छ।\", \"भित्र चमेरा बस्छन्, र सानो शिव मन्दिर छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Siddha_Cave.jpg/1280px-Siddha_Cave.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Sign at the cave giving its length and height\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siddha_Cave.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar%2C_Nepal-WLV-1940.jpg/1280px-Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar%2C_Nepal-WLV-1940.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay Chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Visitors at the cave entrance\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar,_Nepal-WLV-1940.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Bandipur_Cave_9916.JPG/1280px-Bandipur_Cave_9916.JPG\", \"author\": \"Indra Rai\", \"caption\": \"Stalactite formations inside the cave\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandipur_Cave_9916.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bandipur_Cave_9928.JPG/1280px-Bandipur_Cave_9928.JPG\", \"author\": \"Indra Rai\", \"caption\": \"Flowstone formations on the cave walls\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandipur_Cave_9928.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar%2C_Nepal-WLV-1957.jpg/1280px-Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar%2C_Nepal-WLV-1957.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay Chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Shrine inside the cave\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar,_Nepal-WLV-1957.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar%2C_Nepal-WLV-1936.jpg/1280px-Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar%2C_Nepal-WLV-1936.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay Chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Steps on the trail up to the cave\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siddha_Gufa-Cave_Bimal_Nagar,_Nepal-WLV-1936.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"cave\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Dark mouth in a mossy limestone cliff reached by steep stairs, opening into a vast brown-and-cream chamber hung with stalactites.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#8a6a45\", \"#d8c7a3\", \"#2b2420\"], \"features\": [\"rock-face\", \"fence-railing\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": 50, \"footprint_m\": [60, 437], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"cave-mouth\", \"forest\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(26,'kalika-bhagawati-temple-baglung','Kalika Bhagawati Temple','कालिका भगवती मन्दिर, बागलुङ','Baglung','Gandaki','Baglung',NULL,28.255900,83.613578,'pagoda','Hindu','Goddess Kalika (Kali)',NULL,'Founded, according to local folklore, by King Pratap Narayan Singh Malla of Parbat after his marriage to a daughter of King Manimukunda Sen; no firm construction date is documented in the sources found.','Malla kings of Parbat (tradition)','Three-tiered red pagoda with a broad lower roof over an ambulatory, set in a paved courtyard with entrances on all four cardinal sides, surrounded by smaller shrines to Shiva, Radha Krishna and Lakshmi Narayan inside a protected guthi forest.',0,'Baglung\'s great Kali temple, a three-tiered pagoda in a sacred forest above the Kali Gandaki, famed for its Chaite Dashain fair.','Step into the shade of the forest on the edge of Baglung bazaar and you will find a courtyard with four gateways, one for each direction. At its centre rises the red three-tiered pagoda of Kalika Bhagawati, the fierce goddess Kali. The story of this place begins with a wedding. King Pratap Narayan Singh Malla of Parbat married the daughter of King Manimukunda Sen and received an image of Kalika as part of her dowry. On the way home the wedding party sheltered in this forest for the night. In the morning, no one could lift the idol, so the king built a temple on the spot. Around you are smaller shrines to Shiva, Radha Krishna and Lakshmi Narayan. Come in Chaitra for Chaite Dashain, when thousands light oil lamps and some couples even marry here for the goddess\'s blessing. Since April 2016 pigeons are no longer sacrificed; they are set free instead.','King Pratap Narayan Singh Malla of Parbat received the goddess\'s idol as dowry from King Manimukunda Sen. When his wedding party rested overnight in this forest, the idol could not be moved the next morning, so he built the temple there.','[\"The temple stands south-east of Baglung town, above the Kali Gandaki River.\", \"Its courtyard has four entrances, one in each cardinal direction.\", \"Chaite Dashain, on the eighth day of the bright fortnight of Chaitra, is its biggest festival.\", \"On 13 April 2016 pigeon sacrifice was stopped; pigeons are now released in the temple grounds.\", \"The temple is surrounded by the protected Kalika Bhagawati Guthi Forest.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_14.jpg/1280px-Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_14.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_14.jpg','Nabin K. Sapkota · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla kings of parbat (tradition),baglung,legend,festival,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalika_Bhagawati_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60761465\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/910969785\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Kalika_Bhagawati_Temple\"]','बागलुङको ठूलो काली मन्दिर, कालीगण्डकीमाथिको पवित्र जङ्गलमा रहेको तीन तले पगोडा, चैते दशैंको मेलाका लागि प्रसिद्ध।','बागलुङ बजारको छेउको जङ्गलको छायामा पस्नुभयो भने चार दिशामा चारवटा ढोका भएको चोक भेटिन्छ। त्यसको बीचमा कालिका भगवतीको रातो तीन तले पगोडा उठेको छ, उग्र देवी कालीको मन्दिर। यस ठाउँको कथा एउटा विवाहबाट सुरु हुन्छ। पर्वतका राजा प्रताप नारायण सिंह मल्लले राजा मणिमुकुन्द सेनकी छोरीसँग विवाह गरे, र दाइजोमा कालिकाको मूर्ति पाए। घर फर्कने बाटोमा जन्तीले यही जङ्गलमा रात बिताए। बिहान कसैले पनि मूर्ति उठाउन सकेनन्, त्यसैले राजाले त्यही ठाउँमा मन्दिर बनाए। वरिपरि शिव, राधाकृष्ण र लक्ष्मीनारायणका साना मन्दिर छन्। चैतमा चैते दशैंमा आउनुहोस्, जब हजारौँ मानिसले तेलका बत्ती बाल्छन्, र केही जोडीले देवीको आशीर्वाद लिन यहीँ विवाह समेत गर्छन्। सन् 2016 अप्रिलदेखि परेवाको बलि दिइँदैन; बरु तिनलाई उडाइदिइन्छ।','पर्वतका राजा प्रताप नारायण सिंह मल्लले राजा मणिमुकुन्द सेनबाट दाइजोमा देवीको मूर्ति पाए। उनको जन्ती यही जङ्गलमा एक रात बसेपछि भोलिपल्ट मूर्ति सार्न सकिएन, त्यसैले उनले त्यहीँ मन्दिर बनाए।','[\"मन्दिर बागलुङ सहरको दक्षिणपूर्वमा, कालीगण्डकी नदीमाथि छ।\", \"यसको चोकमा चार दिशामा एक-एकवटा गरी चारवटा प्रवेशद्वार छन्।\", \"चैत शुक्ल अष्टमीमा पर्ने चैते दशैं यसको सबैभन्दा ठूलो चाड हो।\", \"13 अप्रिल 2016 मा परेवाको बलि बन्द गरियो; अहिले परेवा मन्दिर परिसरमा उडाइन्छ।\", \"मन्दिर संरक्षित कालिका भगवती गुठी जङ्गलले घेरिएको छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Chaite Dashain\", \"note\": \"Main festival on Chaitra Shukla Ashtami; devotees light oil lamps, perform puja and some marry here.\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"चैते दशैं\", \"note_np\": \"चैत शुक्ल अष्टमीको मुख्य चाड; भक्तजन तेलका बत्ती बाल्छन्, पूजा गर्छन् र केही यहीँ विवाह गर्छन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Celebrated from the bright fortnight of Ashwin to the full moon.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैं\", \"note_np\": \"असोज शुक्ल पक्षदेखि पूर्णिमासम्म मनाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_01.jpg/1280px-Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Ornate gateway to the temple courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_08.jpg/1280px-Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_08.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Stone structure in the temple grounds\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_08.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_05.jpg/1280px-Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_05.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Offerings and prayer cloths in the sacred forest\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baglung_Kalika_Temple_2018_05.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Baglung_Kalika_Temple_Marketplace.jpg/1280px-Baglung_Kalika_Temple_Marketplace.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sajansharma\", \"caption\": \"Stalls selling flowers and coconuts for puja\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baglung_Kalika_Temple_Marketplace.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Baglung_kalika_temple.jpg/1280px-Baglung_kalika_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bishow11\", \"caption\": \"The temple lit up at night\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baglung_kalika_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Balgung_Kalika_Temple_02.jpg/1280px-Balgung_Kalika_Temple_02.jpg\", \"author\": \"Acharya Bipin\", \"caption\": \"The temple courtyard and forest\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balgung_Kalika_Temple_02.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Red three-roofed pagoda with a very wide lowest roof over a pillared walkway, in a big paved courtyard with small shrines and gateways, tall sal forest all round.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#a8322a\", \"#5b4636\", \"#c9a23a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"bell\", \"toran\", \"lamps-diyo\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [14, 14], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"forest\", \"sacred-grove\", \"city-street\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(27,'gupteshwor-mahadev-cave','Gupteshwor Mahadev Cave','गुप्तेश्वर महादेव गुफा','Pokhara','Gandaki','Kaski',NULL,28.189444,83.957778,'cave','Hindu','Shiva (Gupteshwor Mahadev, \'the hidden lord\'), worshipped as a lingam',NULL,'A natural karst cave, reported discovered in 1950; the staircase entrance was built in 1991. It was first surveyed by Tony Waltham\'s British Karst Research Expedition, and a second British expedition studied its animals in 1976.','unknown','Natural cave in Pokhara conglomerate entered down a spiral concrete stairway, with a shrine chamber holding a Shiva lingam behind metal bars; a lower passage descends about 20 m to the Pardi Khola behind Devi\'s Fall. Showcaves.com gives 2,950 m length and 48 m vertical range.',0,'A Shiva cave shrine in Chhorepatan, Pokhara, whose lower passage lets you see Devi\'s Fall plunging from behind.','Wind your way down the spiral stairway at Chhorepatan and the noise of the city fades into the echo of rushing water. You are entering Gupteshwor Mahadev, the cave of the hidden Lord Shiva. In the first chamber, protected behind metal bars, stands the lingam that pilgrims come to worship, perhaps shaped by nature itself as a stalagmite. People here say the cave was found in 1950, and the entrance stairs you just used were built in 1991. If the season allows, keep going down. A damp, narrow passage drops about twenty metres to the river, and suddenly you are standing behind Devi\'s Fall, the waterfall across the road, watching the water of Phewa Lake thunder past in the darkness. British cave researchers came here in the 1970s to map the passages and to count its residents, including great leaf-nosed bats and fruit bats. Hold the railing and enjoy the cool air.',NULL,'[\"The cave lies in Pokhara-17, Chhorepatan, opposite Devi\'s (Davis) Fall.\", \"Water from Devi\'s Fall, the outflow of Phewa Lake (Pardi Khola), passes through the cave.\", \"Showcaves.com reports it was discovered in 1950 and its entrance staircase was built in 1991.\", \"A 1976 British expedition recorded great Himalayan leaf-nosed bats and fruit bats living inside.\", \"Showcaves.com lists the cave as about 2,950 m long with a vertical range of 48 m.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Gupteshwar_Parishar.jpg/1280px-Gupteshwar_Parishar.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gupteshwar_Parishar.jpg','Shalgina.dangi · CC BY-SA 4.0','cave,hindu,pokhara,art,gandaki','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gupteshwor_Mahadev_Cave\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q31154559\", \"https://showcaves.com/english/np/showcaves/Gupteshwor.html\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/pokhara/gupteshwor-mahadev-cave.html\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Gupteshwor_Mahadev_Cave\"]','पोखराको छोरेपाटनमा रहेको शिवको गुफा मन्दिर, जसको तल्लो बाटोबाट देवीको झरना पछाडिबाट खसेको देखिन्छ।','छोरेपाटनमा घुम्ती भ्याङ झर्दै जानुहोस्, सहरको कोलाहल बिस्तारै बग्दो पानीको गुञ्जनमा बदलिन्छ। तपाईं गुप्तेश्वर महादेव, लुकेका भगवान शिवको गुफामा पस्दै हुनुहुन्छ। पहिलो कोठामा फलामको जालीभित्र शिवलिङ्ग छ, जसलाई भक्तजन पूजा गर्न आउँछन्; सायद यो प्रकृतिले नै स्टालाग्माइटका रूपमा बनाएको हो। यहाँका मानिस भन्छन्, गुफा सन् 1950 मा भेटिएको थियो, र अहिले तपाईंले प्रयोग गरेको प्रवेशको भ्याङ सन् 1991 मा बनेको हो। मौसमले दिए तल झर्दै जानुहोस्। चिसो साँघुरो बाटो करिब बीस मिटर तल नदीसम्म पुग्छ, र अचानक तपाईं सडकपारिको देवीको झरनाको पछाडि उभिनुहुन्छ, अँध्यारोमा फेवा तालको पानी गर्जँदै खसिरहेको हेर्दै। बेलायती गुफा अनुसन्धानकर्ताहरू सन् 1970 को दशकमा यहाँको बाटो नक्सा बनाउन र बासिन्दा गन्न आए, जसमा ठूला पात-नाके चमेरा र फलफूल खाने चमेरा थिए। रेलिङ समाउनुहोस् र चिसो हावाको मज्जा लिनुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"गुफा पोखरा-17, छोरेपाटनमा, देवीको (डेभिस) झरनाको सामुन्ने छ।\", \"फेवा तालको निकास, पर्दी खोलाबाट बग्ने देवीको झरनाको पानी गुफाभित्र हुँदै जान्छ।\", \"शोकेभ्स डटकमका अनुसार यो सन् 1950 मा भेटिएको थियो र प्रवेशको भ्याङ सन् 1991 मा बनेको हो।\", \"सन् 1976 को बेलायती अभियानले भित्र बस्ने ठूला हिमाली पात-नाके चमेरा र फलफूल खाने चमेरा भेटेको थियो।\", \"शोकेभ्स डटकमले गुफा करिब 2,950 मिटर लामो र 48 मिटर ठाडो फरक भएको भनेको छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Circular_ladder_like_structure_in_Gupteshwor_CAVE_POKHARA.jpg/1280px-Circular_ladder_like_structure_in_Gupteshwor_CAVE_POKHARA.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin845\", \"caption\": \"Spiral stairway down into the cave\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Circular_ladder_like_structure_in_Gupteshwor_CAVE_POKHARA.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Devis_falla_viewed_from_Gupteshwor_Cave.jpg/1280px-Devis_falla_viewed_from_Gupteshwor_Cave.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin845\", \"caption\": \"Devi\'s Fall seen from inside the cave\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devis_falla_viewed_from_Gupteshwor_Cave.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Gupteswar_gufa.jpg/1280px-Gupteswar_gufa.jpg\", \"author\": \"Anupg44\", \"caption\": \"Long exposure inside Gupteshwor Cave\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gupteswar_gufa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Monument_at_Gupteshwor_Cave.jpg/1280px-Monument_at_Gupteshwor_Cave.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin845\", \"caption\": \"Monument at the cave complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monument_at_Gupteshwor_Cave.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Gupteswor_cave_interior.jpg/1280px-Gupteswor_cave_interior.jpg\", \"author\": \"Paradox7vr\", \"caption\": \"A narrow passage in the cave interior\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gupteswor_cave_interior.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Stairs_at_the_entrance_of_Gupteshwor_cave.jpg/1280px-Stairs_at_the_entrance_of_Gupteshwor_cave.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin845\", \"caption\": \"Stairs at the cave entrance\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stairs_at_the_entrance_of_Gupteshwor_cave.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"cave\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"A round sunken pit with a white-railed spiral staircase and blue painted walls leading down into a dark rock cave; daylight shaft over a thundering waterfall below.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#3f7fb5\", \"#e8e2d8\", \"#7a6650\"], \"features\": [\"rock-face\", \"fence-railing\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": 20, \"footprint_m\": [30, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"cave-mouth\", \"city-street\", \"river\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(28,'kakrebihar','Kakrebihar','काँक्रे विहार','Birendranagar','Karnali','Surkhet',NULL,28.564529,81.621302,'shikhara','Both',NULL,NULL,'Often dated to the 12th century; archaeologists quoted by the Nepali Times say 13th-14th century, and a signboard credits Ashok Challa (c. 1268 CE). Later ruined; reassembled by the Department of Archaeology from 2016.','Khas Malla (Khasa kingdom)','Stone shikhara temple on a forested hillock, reassembled by the Department of Archaeology from excavated carved blocks; its walls, facades, spires and wells resemble Kumaoni temples of the same era. Surrounded by scattered carved stone fragments and ruins.',0,'A reassembled stone shikhara temple of the Khasa era in a pine and sal forest above Surkhet Valley, with Buddhist and Hindu images.','You have climbed through pine and sal forest to a quiet hillock above Surkhet Valley. The stone temple in front of you once lay in pieces. For centuries its carved blocks were scattered across this hill, and nobody is fully sure what brought it down: some blame the great earthquake of 1833, others an invading army in the fourteenth century. Archaeologists link the site to the Khasa kingdom, whose kings bore the names Challa and Malla and ruled from Sinja and Jumla. The signboard here credits a king called Ashok Challa, around 1268. Look at the scattered fragments around you. Excavators found Buddha images here, but also Ganesh, Saraswati and Shiva, so many people see it as a shrine shared by two faiths. From 2016, craftsmen from Bhaktapur fitted the surviving stones back together, shape by shape, into the shikhara you see today. Before you leave, walk to the edge and look down over the green valley.','A local Tharu tale says the hill was a palace of the Pandava brothers of the Mahabharata. Another tells of a brother-in-law and sister-in-law who raced another pair to finish a temple in one night; when they lost, they broke their own work and fled, leaving the stones scattered.','[\"Statues of the Buddha and of Hindu deities including Ganesh, Saraswati and Shiva were found at the site.\", \"The Department of Archaeology excavated the site in 2000 and later rebuilt the temple using its original stones.\", \"Eight craftsmen from Bhaktapur, led by Chandra Ranjitkar, worked on the restoration that began in 2016, with a budget of Rs 81.8 million.\", \"The rebuilt shikhara temple is about six meters tall.\", \"Its stone architecture resembles temples in Kumaon, to the west, rather than those of the Kathmandu Valley.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Kakre_Bihar_Temple.jpg/1280px-Kakre_Bihar_Temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kakre_Bihar_Temple.jpg','Gaurav Dhwaj Khadka · CC BY-SA 4.0','shikhara,both,khas malla (khasa kingdom),birendranagar,hindu,buddhist,legend,art,karnali','[\"https://nepalitimes.com/buddhist-relics-in-western-nepal\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/national/2016/03/16/kakre-bihar-temple-being-restored\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surkhet_District#Kakrebihar\", \"https://ne.wikipedia.org/wiki/काँक्रे_विहार\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13179941\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/11028003793\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Kakrebihar\"]','सुर्खेत उपत्यकामाथि सल्ला र सालको जङ्गलमा फेरि जोडिएको खस कालको ढुङ्गाको शिखर मन्दिर, जहाँ बौद्ध र हिन्दू दुवै मूर्ति छन्।','तपाईं सल्ला र सालको जङ्गल हुँदै सुर्खेत उपत्यकामाथिको शान्त थुम्कोमा उक्लनुभएको छ। तपाईंको अगाडिको ढुङ्गाको मन्दिर कुनै बेला टुक्राटुक्रा भएर थुप्रिएको थियो। सयौँ वर्षसम्म यसका कुँदिएका ढुङ्गाका टुक्रा यही डाँडाभरि छरिएका थिए। के ले ढाल्यो भन्ने कसैलाई पक्का थाहा छैन। कसैले सन् १८३३ को ठूलो भूकम्पलाई दोष दिन्छन्, कसैले चौधौँ शताब्दीको आक्रमणकारी सेनालाई। पुरातत्त्वविद्हरू यो ठाउँलाई खस राज्यसँग जोड्छन्। त्यसका राजाका नाम चल्ल र मल्ल थिए र उनीहरूले सिँजा र जुम्लाबाट शासन गर्थे। यहाँको सूचना पाटीमा करिब १२६८ मा अशोक चल्ल नामका राजाले बनाएको भनिएको छ। वरपर छरिएका टुक्रा हेर्नुहोस्। खनेर निकाल्दा यहाँ बुद्धका मूर्ति भेटिए, तर गणेश, सरस्वती र शिवका पनि भेटिए। त्यसैले धेरैले यसलाई दुई धर्मको साझा तीर्थ ठान्छन्। सन् २०१६ देखि भक्तपुरका शिल्पीले बाँकी ढुङ्गा आकार मिलाएर एक-एक गरी जोडे र आज तपाईंले देख्ने शिखर बनाए। जानुअघि डाँडाको छेउसम्म गएर हरियो उपत्यकातिर हेर्नुहोस्।','एउटा स्थानीय थारू कथाअनुसार यो डाँडा महाभारतका पाण्डव दाजुभाइको दरबार थियो। अर्को कथामा देवर-भाउजूको एक जोडीले अर्को जोडीसँग एकै रातमा मन्दिर बनाउने होड गरे। हारेपछि उनीहरूले आफ्नै काम भत्काएर भागे, र ढुङ्गा छरिएर रहे।','[\"यस स्थलमा बुद्धका मूर्ति र गणेश, सरस्वती र शिवलगायत हिन्दू देवदेवीका मूर्ति भेटिए।\", \"पुरातत्त्व विभागले सन् २००० मा यो स्थलको उत्खनन गर्‍यो र पछि मौलिक ढुङ्गा प्रयोग गरेर मन्दिर पुनर्निर्माण गर्‍यो।\", \"चन्द्र रञ्जितकारको नेतृत्वमा भक्तपुरका आठ शिल्पीले सन् २०१६ मा सुरु भएको पुनर्स्थापनामा काम गरे। बजेट रु ८ करोड १८ लाख थियो।\", \"पुनर्निर्माण गरिएको शिखर मन्दिर करिब छ मिटर अग्लो छ।\", \"यसको ढुङ्गाको वास्तुकला काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाका मन्दिरभन्दा पश्चिमको कुमाउँका मन्दिरसँग मिल्दोजुल्दो छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Kakrebihar_After_Renovation.jpg/1280px-Kakrebihar_After_Renovation.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gr8lujah\", \"caption\": \"Kakrebihar temple after its renovation\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kakrebihar_After_Renovation.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Kakrebihar_34.jpg/1280px-Kakrebihar_34.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Poudel\", \"caption\": \"Ruins of the old temple before reconstruction\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kakrebihar_34.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Kakrebihar_6.jpg/1280px-Kakrebihar_6.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Poudel\", \"caption\": \"Carved stone fragments found at the site\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kakrebihar_6.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Stone_Buddha_statute_of_Kankre_Vihar.jpg/1280px-Stone_Buddha_statute_of_Kankre_Vihar.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajivkilanashrestha\", \"caption\": \"Stone Buddha image at Kakrebihar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stone_Buddha_statute_of_Kankre_Vihar.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Entrance_gate%2C_Kakrebihar.jpg/1280px-Entrance_gate%2C_Kakrebihar.jpg\", \"author\": \"Geetakrawal\", \"caption\": \"Entrance gate to the Kakrebihar forest\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_gate,_Kakrebihar.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Surkhet_Valley_from_Kakrebihar.jpg/1280px-Surkhet_Valley_from_Kakrebihar.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Poudel\", \"caption\": \"Surkhet Valley seen from the Kakrebihar hill\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surkhet_Valley_from_Kakrebihar.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"stone-spire\", \"notes\": \"Tan sandstone shikhara with a ribbed curving spire and amalaka top on a stepped platform, carved blocks around it, in pine and sal forest on a hilltop.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#b39a78\", \"#8a7356\", \"#3f5a2e\"], \"features\": [\"idol-visible\", \"stone-pillar\"], \"height_m\": 6, \"footprint_m\": [6, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:46'),(29,'chandannath-temple','Chandannath Temple','चन्दननाथ मन्दिर','Khalanga, Jumla','Karnali','Jumla',NULL,29.274208,82.183514,'dome-temple','Hindu','Dattatreya (Chandannath), with Bhairav (Bhairavnath) in the neighboring shrine',NULL,'Tradition places its founding in the Kalyal (Kallala) dynasty period. A royal order of King Rajendra dated VS 1881 (c. 1824 CE) sent 22 workers to build the temple of Shri Chandannath at Jumla.','Kalyal (traditional founding); rebuilt under the Shah kings','Small whitewashed square shrine with a yellow cornice band, crowned by a metal-clad onion dome and finial. Beside it stand very tall red-painted timber poles (lingo) carrying huge triangular saffron flags, shared with the adjoining Bhairavnath temple.',0,'The guardian temple of Jumla bazaar, famous for the towering flag poles that are replaced every Dashain.','You are in Khalanga, the old bazaar of Jumla, high in the Karnali hills. Look up first: those towering red poles with their enormous saffron flags are called lingo, and each is more than fifty feet of timber. Every year, on Ghatasthapana, the first day of Dashain, the people of Jumla take the old lingo down and raise a new one. They believe misfortune will follow if a pole breaks during the change, so the whole town holds its breath. Now lower your eyes to the little whitewashed shrine with its shining dome. Inside is Dattatreya, honored here as Chandannath. Local belief says an ascetic named Chandannath came from Kashmir carrying this image, and that he also brought the red Marsi rice that grows in these fields. Next door stands Bhairavnath. In 2016 thieves stole twenty-eight idols from this temple, and the town protested until many were recovered.','One story says a cow that gave no milk at home let her milk flow freely whenever she stood on this spot, so villagers knew the ground was holy and built the temple there. Another credits Chandannath of Kashmir with bringing the image of Dattatreya and red Marsi rice to Jumla.','[\"The lingo poles are more than 52 feet long and are replaced every year on Ghatasthapana, the first day of Dashain.\", \"A royal order of King Rajendra dated VS 1881 sent 22 workers to build the temple of Shri Chandannath at Jumla.\", \"On a night in November 2016, 28 idols including the main deity Dattatreya were stolen; police later recovered 14 idols.\", \"Local tradition says Chandannath of Kashmir introduced Jumla\'s red Marsi rice.\", \"The temple is managed by the Chandannath-Bhairavnath Guthi Management Committee.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Chandan_nath%2CJumla.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandan_nath,Jumla.JPG','Sunil Dongol · CC BY-SA 3.0','dome-temple,hindu,kalyal (traditional founding); rebuilt under the shah kings,khalanga, jumla,legend,art,festival,karnali','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chandannath_Temple\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/national/2016/11/28/28-ancient-idols-stolen-from-chandannath\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/national/2017/01/04/14-chandannath-idols-recovered\", \"https://nepalica.hadw-bw.de/nepal/catitems/viewitem/9062/487\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5070967\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Chandannath_Temple\"]','जुम्ला बजारको रक्षक मन्दिर, हरेक दशैँमा फेरिने अग्ला लिङ्गोका लागि प्रसिद्ध।','तपाईं कर्णालीको अग्लो पहाडमा रहेको जुम्लाको पुरानो बजार खलङ्गामा हुनुहुन्छ। पहिला माथि हेर्नुहोस्। ती अग्ला रातो खम्बामा ठूला केसरी झन्डा फहरिएका छन्। यिनलाई लिङ्गो भनिन्छ र हरेक लिङ्गो पचास फिटभन्दा लामो काठको हुन्छ। हरेक वर्ष दशैँको पहिलो दिन, घटस्थापनामा, जुम्लाका मानिसले पुरानो लिङ्गो झारेर नयाँ ठड्याउँछन्। फेर्दा खम्बा भाँचियो भने अनिष्ट हुन्छ भन्ने विश्वास छ, त्यसैले सारा सहर सास रोकेर हेर्छ। अब आँखा तल ल्याउनुहोस्। चम्किलो गुम्बजसहितको सानो सेतो मन्दिर देख्नुहुन्छ। भित्र दत्तात्रेय छन्, जसलाई यहाँ चन्दननाथका रूपमा पूजा गरिन्छ। स्थानीय विश्वासअनुसार चन्दननाथ नामका एक तपस्वी कश्मीरबाट यो मूर्ति बोकेर आएका थिए। यहाँका खेतमा फल्ने रातो मार्सी चामल पनि उनैले ल्याएका हुन्। छेउमै भैरवनाथको मन्दिर छ। सन् २०१६ मा चोरहरूले यो मन्दिरबाट अठ्ठाइसवटा मूर्ति चोरे। धेरै मूर्ति बरामद नभएसम्म सहरले आन्दोलन गर्‍यो।','एउटा कथाअनुसार घरमा दूध नदिने एउटी गाई यही ठाउँमा आएपछि भरर दूध दिन्थी। त्यसैले गाउँलेले यो भूमि पवित्र रहेछ भन्ने थाहा पाए र यहीँ मन्दिर बनाए। अर्को कथामा भनिन्छ, कश्मीरका चन्दननाथले दत्तात्रेयको मूर्ति र रातो मार्सी चामल जुम्ला ल्याएका थिए।','[\"लिङ्गो खम्बा ५२ फिटभन्दा लामा हुन्छन् र हरेक वर्ष दशैँको पहिलो दिन, घटस्थापनामा, फेरिन्छन्।\", \"राजा राजेन्द्रको वि.सं. १८८१ को शाही आदेशले जुम्लामा श्री चन्दननाथको मन्दिर बनाउन २२ जना कामदार पठाएको थियो।\", \"२०१६ नोभेम्बरको एक रात मुख्य देवता दत्तात्रेयसहित २८ वटा मूर्ति चोरी भए। प्रहरीले पछि १४ वटा बरामद गर्‍यो।\", \"स्थानीय मान्यताअनुसार कश्मीरका चन्दननाथले जुम्लामा रातो मार्सी चामल ल्याएका थिए।\", \"मन्दिर चन्दननाथ-भैरवनाथ गुठी व्यवस्थापन समितिले चलाउँछ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain (Ghatasthapana lingo change)\", \"note\": \"The old lingo poles are taken down and new ones raised on the first day of Dashain.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ (घटस्थापनामा लिङ्गो फेर्ने)\", \"note_np\": \"दशैँको पहिलो दिन पुराना लिङ्गो झारिन्छन् र नयाँ ठड्याइन्छन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Krishna Janmashtami jatra\", \"note\": \"Large crowds gather in Jumla Bazaar on the last day of the jatra.\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"कृष्ण जन्माष्टमी जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"जात्राको अन्तिम दिन जुम्ला बजारमा ठूलो भीड लाग्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"One of the major festivals that bring crowds to the temple.\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"मन्दिरमा भीड लाग्ने ठूला चाडमध्ये एक।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Channdannath_and_Bhairabnath.jpg/1280px-Channdannath_and_Bhairabnath.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prashant Shahi\", \"caption\": \"The giant lingo flag poles of Chandannath and Bhairabnath\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Channdannath_and_Bhairabnath.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Snowy_Chandannath_and_Bhairabnath.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prashant Shahi\", \"caption\": \"Chandannath and Bhairabnath temples during snowfall\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snowy_Chandannath_and_Bhairabnath.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Chandannath_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prashant Shahi\", \"caption\": \"The temple\'s golden dome after heavy snowfall\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandannath_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/06/Hanuman_Temple_beside_Chandannath_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prashant Shahi\", \"caption\": \"Hanuman statue beside Chandannath Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hanuman_Temple_beside_Chandannath_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Jumla_Jatra.jpg/1280px-Jumla_Jatra.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prashant Shahi\", \"caption\": \"Crowd at the Janmashtami jatra in Jumla Bazaar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jumla_Jatra.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Chandannath_and_Bhairabnath_Temple.jpg/1280px-Chandannath_and_Bhairabnath_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prashant Shahi\", \"caption\": \"Khalanga Bazaar, home of the temples, seen from afar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandannath_and_Bhairabnath_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"dome-temple\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Small white cube shrine with a yellow band under a big metal onion dome; beside it two very tall red timber poles carrying giant saffron triangular flags.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#f2f0ea\", \"#b8a26a\", \"#e0b030\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"flags-red\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [5, 5], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"market-houses\", \"terraced-fields\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(30,'sinja-valley','Sinja Valley','सिँजा उपत्यका','Hat Sinja, Jumla','Karnali','Jumla',NULL,29.398000,81.996000,'archaeological-site','Both','Kanakasundari (local goddess temple); Masto shrines',NULL,'Capital of the Khasa Malla kingdom from about the 12th to the 14th century; shikhara temples at Tarpibada date from the 13th-15th century.','Khasa Malla','Open mountain valley with the ruins of a medieval fortress (identified as Yatse) near Hat Sinja, temples such as Kanakasundari, stone dewal shrines, carved stone and timber memorial pillars, Buddhist cave chaityas and cliff inscriptions above the Hima River.',0,'The high Jumla valley that was the capital of the Khasa Malla kings and is called the birthplace of the Nepali language.','You are standing in Sinja, a wide valley in Jumla where the Hima River runs between dry hills and terraced fields. It looks peaceful and remote, but from about the twelfth to the fourteenth century this was the capital of the Khasa Malla kings, whose power stretched across western Nepal. Near the village of Hat Sinja are the ruins of a fortress that scholars identify as Yatse, their summer seat. Look across the river at the cliffs: caves there hold old Buddhist chaityas, and the rock carries inscriptions. Some of the earliest written examples of the Nepali language were found on cliffs like these and in nearby Dullu, which is why people call Sinja the birthplace of Nepali. As you walk, watch for carved memorial pillars standing by paths and bridges. Shamans called Masto still perform ancient rites in the stone dewals. In 2008 Nepal placed this valley on its UNESCO tentative list.',NULL,'[\"Sinja was the capital of the Khasa kingdom, which ruled western Nepal from about the 12th to the 14th century.\", \"The valley is often called the birthplace of the Nepali language; 13th-century Devanagari inscriptions were found on its cliffs and in nearby Dullu.\", \"Nepal added the Sinja Valley to the UNESCO World Heritage Tentative List on 30 January 2008.\", \"After the 14th century the Khasa kingdom broke up into 22 small kingdoms, the Baise Rajya.\", \"The Sinja River flows through the valley and joins the Karnali in Kalikot district.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,180,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Sinja_Valley%2C_Karnali.jpg/1280px-Sinja_Valley%2C_Karnali.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinja_Valley,_Karnali.jpg','Punyapaudel · CC BY-SA 4.0','archaeological-site,both,khasa malla,hat sinja, jumla,hindu,buddhist,art,karnali','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinja_Valley\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/tentativelists/5263\", \"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/heritage-foucus-area-sinja-valley\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khasa_Kingdom\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7524492\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Sinja_Valley\"]','खस मल्ल राजाहरूको राजधानी रहेको जुम्लाको अग्लो उपत्यका, जसलाई नेपाली भाषाको जन्मथलो भनिन्छ।','तपाईं जुम्लाको फराकिलो उपत्यका सिँजामा उभिनुभएको छ। यहाँ हिमा नदी सुख्खा डाँडा र पाखा खेतको बीचबाट बग्छ। ठाउँ शान्त र टाढा देखिन्छ। तर करिब बाह्रौँदेखि चौधौँ शताब्दीसम्म यो खस मल्ल राजाहरूको राजधानी थियो। उनीहरूको शक्ति पश्चिम नेपालभर फैलिएको थियो। हाट सिँजा गाउँनजिक एउटा किल्लाको भग्नावशेष छ। विद्वान्हरू यसलाई उनीहरू गर्मीमा बस्ने दरबार यात्से ठान्छन्। नदीपारिका चट्टानतिर हेर्नुहोस्। त्यहाँका गुफामा पुराना बौद्ध चैत्य छन् र चट्टानमा अभिलेख कुँदिएका छन्। नेपाली भाषाका सबैभन्दा पुराना लिखित नमुनामध्ये केही यस्तै चट्टानमा र नजिकैको दुल्लुमा भेटिएका थिए। त्यसैले मानिसहरू सिँजालाई नेपाली भाषाको जन्मथलो भन्छन्। हिँड्दा बाटो र पुलछेउ उभिएका कुँदिएका स्मारक स्तम्भ हेर्नुहोस्। मस्टो भनिने धामीहरूले अहिले पनि ढुङ्गाका देवालमा प्राचीन अनुष्ठान गर्छन्। सन् २००८ मा नेपालले यो उपत्यकालाई युनेस्कोको सम्भावित सूचीमा राख्यो।',NULL,'[\"सिँजा खस राज्यको राजधानी थियो। यो राज्यले करिब १२औँदेखि १४औँ शताब्दीसम्म पश्चिम नेपालमा शासन गर्‍यो।\", \"उपत्यकालाई प्रायः नेपाली भाषाको जन्मथलो भनिन्छ। यहाँका चट्टान र नजिकैको दुल्लुमा १३औँ शताब्दीका देवनागरी अभिलेख भेटिएका थिए।\", \"नेपालले २००८ जनवरी ३० मा सिँजा उपत्यकालाई युनेस्को विश्व सम्पदाको सम्भावित सूचीमा राखेको हो।\", \"१४औँ शताब्दीपछि खस राज्य टुक्रिएर २२ वटा साना राज्य बन्यो, जसलाई बाइसे राज्य भनिन्छ।\", \"सिँजा खोला उपत्यका हुँदै बग्छ र कालीकोट जिल्लामा कर्णालीमा मिसिन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Hima_River%2C_Sinja_Valley%2C_karnali.jpg/1280px-Hima_River%2C_Sinja_Valley%2C_karnali.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sumoon Rewolf\", \"caption\": \"The Hima River flowing through Sinja Valley\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hima_River,_Sinja_Valley,_karnali.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Narakot_Sinja_Valley.JPG/1280px-Narakot_Sinja_Valley.JPG\", \"author\": \"Soraj Shahi\", \"caption\": \"Narakot and the open floor of Sinja Valley\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narakot_Sinja_Valley.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Sinja_Valley.JPG/1280px-Sinja_Valley.JPG\", \"author\": \"Priyankar Chand\", \"caption\": \"Terraced fields and villages of Sinja Valley\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinja_Valley.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Sinja_valley.JPG/1280px-Sinja_valley.JPG\", \"author\": \"Soraj Shahi\", \"caption\": \"Sinja Valley from the hillside\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinja_valley.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Sinja_Valley_in_Winter.jpg/1280px-Sinja_Valley_in_Winter.jpg\", \"author\": \"asoqpathak\", \"caption\": \"Snow-covered forest above Sinja Valley in winter\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinja_Valley_in_Winter.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"ruins\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Wide dry-hill valley floor with a river and terraces; carved wooden and stone memorial pillars topped with human figures stand by a stone footbridge.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#a88f6a\", \"#4f6b3a\", \"#2f6fb3\"], \"features\": [\"stone-pillar\", \"rock-face\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [400, 200], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"terraced-fields\", \"village\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(31,'shirasthan-dullu','Shirasthan (Jwala Mandir), Dullu','शिरस्थान','Dullu','Karnali','Dailekh',NULL,28.840998,81.676516,'courtyard','Hindu','Jwala Devi (Sati), worshipped as natural gas flames',NULL,'Age of the shrine unknown; scholar Marie Lecomte-Tilouine notes the ritual layout of Dullu\'s flame shrines already existed in the Khasa Malla period (12th-14th century).','unknown','A small hillside shrine complex: a whitewashed single-storey building with a low pitched roof, a beaten-earth courtyard with a sacrificial post, collections of old carved stone images, and natural gas flames burning from rock niches.',0,'A flame shrine in Dullu where natural gas burns from the rocks, honored as the place where the head of the goddess Sati fell.','Step quietly into the courtyard and look down at the rocks by the wall. A small flame is burning straight out of the stone, with no wick and no oil. This is Shirasthan, in Rawatkot of Dullu, one of the five sacred sites of the Panchakoshi pilgrimage of Dailekh. Gas seeping from the ground keeps these flames alight, and pilgrims call the whole area Jwala Tirtha, the place of fire. The name means the place of the head. Hindu tradition, told in the Swasthani, says that as Shiva wandered carrying the body of his wife Sati, her head fell here; her navel fell at Nabhisthan nearby. Notice the collections of old carved stone images around you and the post where sacrifices are made. Its priest is an ascetic of the Nath sect. People say that when the sacred flames at Chandannath in Jumla or at Badimalika go out, they are lit again with fire carried from this place.','According to the Swasthani, Shiva carried the body of Sati across the world after her death, and her head fell at Shirasthan, giving the shrine its name. Her navel fell at nearby Nabhisthan.','[\"Shirasthan is one of the Panchakoshi pilgrimage sites of Dailekh, with Nabhisthan, Dhuleshwar, Padukasthan and Dungeshwar.\", \"Its flames burn from natural gas, so the area is also called Jwala Tirtha or Agni Tirtha.\", \"Local tradition says flames at Chandannath (Jumla) and Badimalika are relit from the flame here when they go out.\", \"The shrine\'s priest has been an ascetic of the Nath sect, as documented by researcher Marie Lecomte-Tilouine in 2003.\", \"The site is listed as a cultural heritage monument of Nepal (NP-DK-18, Shirsthan (Jwaladevi) Math).\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Holy_Flame.jpg/1280px-Holy_Flame.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holy_Flame.jpg','Girisumit1990 · CC BY-SA 4.0','courtyard,hindu,dullu,legend,palace,art,karnali','[\"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/panchakoshi-in-dailekh-pilgrimage.html\", \"https://seechac.org/dullu-the-sacred-capital-of-the-khas-malla-emperors-western-nepal/?lang=en\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_monuments_in_Dailekh,_Nepal\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/11033774721\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holy_Flame.jpg\"]','दुल्लुको ज्वाला मन्दिर, जहाँ चट्टानबाट प्राकृतिक ग्यास बल्छ। यो ठाउँ देवी सतीको शिर खसेको ठाउँ मानिन्छ।','चुपचाप आँगनमा पस्नुहोस् र पर्खालछेउका चट्टानमा हेर्नुहोस्। ढुङ्गाबाटै सानो आगो बलिरहेको छ। न बत्ती छ, न तेल। यो दुल्लुको रावतकोटमा रहेको शिरस्थान हो, दैलेखको पञ्चकोशी तीर्थका पाँच पवित्र स्थानमध्ये एक। जमिनबाट निस्कने ग्यासले यी ज्वाला बलिरहेका छन्, त्यसैले तीर्थयात्रीहरू यो क्षेत्रलाई ज्वाला तीर्थ, अर्थात् आगोको ठाउँ, भन्छन्। नामको अर्थ शिरको स्थान हो। स्वस्थानीमा भनिएको हिन्दू मान्यताअनुसार शिवले पत्नी सतीको शव बोकेर हिँड्दा उनको शिर यहीँ खस्यो र नाभि नजिकैको नाभिस्थानमा खस्यो। वरपर पुराना कुँदिएका ढुङ्गाका मूर्तिका थुप्रा र बलि दिने खम्बा हेर्नुहोस्। यहाँका पुजारी नाथ सम्प्रदायका तपस्वी हुन्। मानिस भन्छन्, जुम्लाको चन्दननाथ वा बडिमालिकाका पवित्र आगो निभे यहीँबाट आगो लगेर फेरि बालिन्छ।','स्वस्थानीअनुसार सतीको मृत्युपछि शिवले उनको शव बोकेर संसारभर हिँडे र उनको शिर शिरस्थानमा खस्यो। त्यसैले यो मन्दिरको नाम शिरस्थान रह्यो। उनको नाभि नजिकैको नाभिस्थानमा खस्यो।','[\"शिरस्थान दैलेखको पञ्चकोशी तीर्थका स्थानमध्ये एक हो। अरू चारवटा नाभिस्थान, धुलेश्वर, पादुकास्थान र डुङ्गेश्वर हुन्।\", \"यहाँका ज्वाला प्राकृतिक ग्यासबाट बल्छन्, त्यसैले यो क्षेत्रलाई ज्वाला तीर्थ वा अग्नि तीर्थ पनि भनिन्छ।\", \"स्थानीय मान्यताअनुसार चन्दननाथ (जुम्ला) र बडीमालिकाका ज्वाला निभे यहाँको ज्वालाबाट फेरि बालिन्छन्।\", \"अनुसन्धानकर्ता मारी लेकोम्त-तिलुइनले सन् २००३ मा लेखेअनुसार मन्दिरका पुजारी नाथ सम्प्रदायका तपस्वी हुँदै आएका छन्।\", \"यो स्थल नेपालको सांस्कृतिक सम्पदा स्मारकका रूपमा सूचीकृत छ (NP-DK-18, शिरस्थान (ज्वालादेवी) मठ)।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Place_for_worship.jpg/1280px-Place_for_worship.jpg\", \"author\": \"Girisumit1990\", \"caption\": \"Courtyard of the Shirasthan shrine with its whitewashed building\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Place_for_worship.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Flame_outside_Temple.jpg/1280px-Flame_outside_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Girisumit1990\", \"caption\": \"Natural gas flame burning from a rock niche\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flame_outside_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Another_holy_flame.jpg/1280px-Another_holy_flame.jpg\", \"author\": \"Girisumit1990\", \"caption\": \"Another of the sacred flames at Shirasthan\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Another_holy_flame.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Collections_of_carved_statues.jpg/1280px-Collections_of_carved_statues.jpg\", \"author\": \"Girisumit1990\", \"caption\": \"Old carved stone images kept at the shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collections_of_carved_statues.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Collections_of_carved_stones.jpg/1280px-Collections_of_carved_stones.jpg\", \"author\": \"Girisumit1990\", \"caption\": \"Collection of carved stones at Shirasthan\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collections_of_carved_stones.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Place_for_animal_sacrifice.jpg/1280px-Place_for_animal_sacrifice.jpg\", \"author\": \"Girisumit1990\", \"caption\": \"Sacrificial post area of the shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Place_for_animal_sacrifice.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"slate\", \"notes\": \"Low whitewashed shrine house with a stone-slate roof over a red earth courtyard; small flames flicker from dark rock niches heaped with rice and flowers.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#f0eee8\", \"#b0603a\", \"#6e6a62\"], \"features\": [\"lamps-diyo\", \"trident\", \"idol-visible\", \"rock-face\"], \"height_m\": 4, \"footprint_m\": [15, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"village\", \"terraced-fields\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(32,'dullu-kirtistambha','Prithvi Malla\'s Kirtistambha, Dullu','पृथ्वी मल्लको कीर्तिस्तम्भ, दुल्लु','Dullu','Karnali','Dailekh',NULL,28.860043,81.604254,'pillar','Both',NULL,1354,'Mid-14th century: the pillar is associated with King Prithvi Malla and dated 1354 CE according to anthropologist Pat Caplan; a nearby stone water tank inscribed by one of his ministers is dated 1358.','Khasa Malla','A flat upright stone stele with a rounded top, carved near the top with a stepped Buddhist chaitya above a line of large letters, and covered below with rows of inscription. It stands inside a protective metal railing in Dullu bazaar.',0,'An inscribed 14th-century stone pillar in Dullu that records the family tree of the Khasa Malla kings.','You are standing in Dullu, once the winter seat of the Khasa Malla kings, whose capital lay up in the Sinja Valley of Jumla. In front of you, behind its railing, rises a flat gray stone with a rounded top. This is a kirtistambha, a pillar of fame. Look near the top and you will see a small stepped chaitya, the Buddhist shrine shape, carved above a line of large letters. Below it, row after row of writing fills the stone. The pillar is associated with King Prithvi Malla and dated to 1354, and its inscription sets out the genealogy of his dynasty, naming Nagaraja as the founder who set up the capital at Sinja. The Italian scholar Giuseppe Tucci recorded these Dullu stones in the 1950s. Nearby you can find more carved pillars, and a stone water tank whose inscription says one of Prithvi Malla\'s ministers built it in 1358.',NULL,'[\"The pillar is associated with King Prithvi Malla and dated 1354 CE.\", \"Its inscription gives the genealogy of the Khasa Malla dynasty and names Nagaraja as the founder of the capital at Sinja.\", \"Italian Tibetologist Giuseppe Tucci recorded the Dullu stelae in the 1950s; they were re-photographed in 1969.\", \"A nearby stone water tank with a chaitya on top was built in 1358 by one of Prithvi Malla\'s ministers.\", \"It is listed as a cultural heritage monument of Nepal (NP-DK-05, Prithivi Malla\'s Kirtistambha).\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/97/%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%83%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AE.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%83%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AE.jpg','Rameshti · CC BY-SA 3.0','pillar,both,khasa malla,dullu,hindu,buddhist,art,karnali','[\"https://www.gold.ac.uk/global-change/people/pat-caplan/nepal-photo-gallery/dullu/\", \"https://bridges.monash.edu/articles/figure/Dulla_inscriptions/3846762\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_monuments_in_Dailekh,_Nepal\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/11033774850\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Prithivi_Malla\'s_Kirtistambha_(Dullu)\"]','दुल्लुमा रहेको १४औँ शताब्दीको अभिलेख कुँदिएको ढुङ्गाको स्तम्भ, जसमा खस मल्ल राजाहरूको वंशावली छ।','तपाईं दुल्लुमा हुनुहुन्छ। कुनै बेला यो खस मल्ल राजाहरूको जाडो बिताउने ठाउँ थियो। उनीहरूको राजधानी माथि जुम्लाको सिँजा उपत्यकामा थियो। तपाईंको अगाडि बारभित्र टुप्पो गोलो भएको चेप्टो खैरो ढुङ्गा उभिएको छ। यो कीर्तिस्तम्भ हो, अर्थात् कीर्तिको खम्बा। माथितिर हेर्नुहोस्। ठूला अक्षरको लहरमाथि सानो तहतह भएको चैत्य, बौद्ध मन्दिरको आकार, कुँदिएको देख्नुहुन्छ। त्यसमुनि ढुङ्गाभरि लहरै लहर लेखिएको छ। यो खम्बा राजा पृथ्वी मल्लसँग जोडिएको छ र सन् १३५४ को मानिन्छ। यसको अभिलेखमा उनको वंशको वंशावली छ, जसमा सिँजामा राजधानी बसाल्ने संस्थापकका रूपमा नागराजको नाम आउँछ। इटालीका विद्वान् ज्युसेप्पे तुच्चीले सन् १९५० को दशकमा दुल्लुका यी ढुङ्गाका अभिलेख टिपेका थिए। नजिकै अरू कुँदिएका खम्बा पनि भेट्न सकिन्छ। त्यहाँ एउटा ढुङ्गाको पानी ट्याङ्की पनि छ। त्यसको अभिलेखअनुसार पृथ्वी मल्लका एक मन्त्रीले त्यो सन् १३५८ मा बनाएका थिए।',NULL,'[\"यो खम्बा राजा पृथ्वी मल्लसँग जोडिएको छ र सन् १३५४ को मानिन्छ।\", \"यसको अभिलेखमा खस मल्ल वंशको वंशावली छ र सिँजामा राजधानी बसाल्ने संस्थापकका रूपमा नागराजको नाम छ।\", \"इटालीका तिब्बतविद् ज्युसेप्पे तुच्चीले सन् १९५० को दशकमा दुल्लुका शिलालेख टिपेका थिए। सन् १९६९ मा ती फेरि फोटो खिचिए।\", \"माथि चैत्य भएको नजिकैको ढुङ्गाको पानी ट्याङ्की सन् १३५८ मा पृथ्वी मल्लका एक मन्त्रीले बनाएका थिए।\", \"यो नेपालको सांस्कृतिक सम्पदा स्मारकका रूपमा सूचीकृत छ (NP-DK-05, पृथ्वी मल्लको कीर्तिस्तम्भ)।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AC.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rameshti\", \"caption\": \"Carved chaitya and large lettering at the top of the pillar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AC.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/75/%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%83%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AC.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rameshti\", \"caption\": \"Inscribed face of the pillar behind its protective railing\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%83%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AC.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/38/%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%83%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AC.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rameshti\", \"caption\": \"Small carved stone pillars nearby in Dullu\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%83%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AC.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/00/%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AE.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rameshti\", \"caption\": \"Stacked carved stone fragment kept behind a railing\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AE.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/76/%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%83%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AE.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rameshti\", \"caption\": \"Small stone chaitya near the Kirtistambha\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%83%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AE.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pillar\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Tall flat gray stone slab with a rounded top and a carved chaitya at the top, caged in a silver metal railing beside village houses.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#6f7470\", \"#a9aaa4\", \"#c8ccd0\"], \"features\": [\"stone-pillar\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [0.8, 0.3], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"village\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(33,'badimalika-temple','Badimalika Temple','बडिमालिका मन्दिर','Martadi','Sudurpashchim','Bajura',NULL,29.346916,81.477488,'shikhara','Hindu','Bhagawati (Malika Devi)',2025,'Ancient pilgrimage site of uncertain date, linked in legend to King Dipraj Chhatyal and the Jumla kings. The old shrine was demolished and a new temple was built by the Nepali Army between April and July 2025.','unknown','High-altitude ridge-top shrine. Photos from 2018 show a small whitewashed square shrine with a pyramidal roof inside dry-stone walls, an open white pavilion, and stone frames hung with hundreds of bells and tridents. The 2025 rebuild used sal wood, stone and mud.',0,'A Shakti shrine at about 4,200 m in Bajura, where tens of thousands of pilgrims climb for the full-moon festival of Janai Purnima.','Catch your breath: you are at roughly four thousand two hundred meters on a grassy ridge in Bajura, and this is Badimalika, one of the great goddess shrines of the far west. Pilgrims climb for hours over open, often slippery pastures, past places such as Triveni and the 22 Patan meadows, to reach this spot. Hindu tradition says that when Shiva carried the body of Sati, her left shoulder fell on this mountain, once called Mallagiri. Look at the frames around the shrine: they are hung with bells and tridents left by grateful pilgrims. Local legend tells of King Dipraj Chhatyal, whose bow was stopped by an unseen force while he hunted here, and who then built a temple for the goddess with help from the king of Jumla. Two priests serve here, one from Kalikot and one from Bajura. In 2025 the Nepali Army rebuilt the shrine, carrying materials up by helicopter and on foot.','When Sati\'s body was carried by Shiva, her left shoulder fell on Mallagiri, which became Malika. A later tale says King Dipraj Chhatyal was stopped from hunting here by an unseen force, dreamed of the goddess, and built her temple together with the king of Jumla.','[\"The temple stands at about 4,200 meters; the Nepali Army gives 4,220 m.\", \"Its main puja is held on Shrawan Shukla Chaturdashi, the day before Janai Purnima.\", \"It is served by two priests, one representing Kalikot district and the other Bajura district.\", \"The Nepali Army rebuilt the temple from April to July 2025 at a cost of about Rs 20 million, under the Ancient Monument Preservation Act.\", \"More than 45,000 devotees visited in one year, according to the temple priest.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,120,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Badimalika_Temple%2C_Bajura%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Badimalika_Temple%2C_Bajura%2C_Nepal.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badimalika_Temple,_Bajura,_Nepal.jpg','sigdelsanjog · CC BY-SA 4.0','shikhara,hindu,martadi,legend,art,sudurpashchim','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badimalika_Temple\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/nepal/nepali-army-constructs-temple-at-badimalika-pilgrimage-site-in-bajura\", \"https://english.ratopati.com/story/74271/badimalika-fair-from-bhadra-1-preparations-begin\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/nepal/badimalikas-high-altitude-appeal-grows-beyond-the-annual-pilgrimage\", \"https://www.buddhaair.com/blog/complete-guide-to-badimalika-trek\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13183742\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Badimalika_Temple\"]','बाजुरामा करिब ४,२०० मिटरमा रहेको शक्ति मन्दिर, जहाँ जनै पूर्णिमाको पर्वमा दसौँ हजार तीर्थयात्री उक्लिन्छन्।','सास फेर्नुहोस्। तपाईं बाजुराको घाँसे डाँडामा करिब चार हजार दुई सय मिटरको उचाइमा हुनुहुन्छ। यो बडिमालिका हो, सुदूरपश्चिमका ठूला देवी मन्दिरमध्ये एक। तीर्थयात्रीहरू खुला र प्रायः चिप्ला चरन हुँदै, त्रिवेणी र २२ पाटनजस्ता ठाउँ पार गर्दै, घण्टौँ हिँडेर यहाँ पुग्छन्। हिन्दू मान्यताअनुसार शिवले सतीको शव बोकेर हिँड्दा उनको देब्रे काँध यही पर्वतमा खस्यो। त्यतिबेला यसलाई मल्लगिरि भनिन्थ्यो। मन्दिरवरिपरिका फ्रेम हेर्नुहोस्। ती श्रद्धालुले चढाएका घण्टी र त्रिशूलले भरिएका छन्। स्थानीय कथाअनुसार राजा दिपराज छत्याल यहाँ सिकार खेल्दै गर्दा उनको धनु अदृश्य शक्तिले रोकियो। त्यसपछि उनले जुम्लाका राजाको सहयोगमा देवीको मन्दिर बनाए। यहाँ दुई पुजारी सेवामा छन्, एक कालीकोटका र एक बाजुराका। सन् २०२५ मा नेपाली सेनाले सामग्री हेलिकप्टर र पैदल बोकेर ल्याई मन्दिर फेरि बनायो।','शिवले सतीको शव बोकेर हिँड्दा उनको देब्रे काँध मल्लगिरिमा खस्यो र त्यो ठाउँ मालिका भयो। पछिको कथाअनुसार राजा दिपराज छत्यालले यहाँ सिकार खेल्दा अदृश्य शक्तिले रोक्यो। उनले देवीलाई सपनामा देखे र जुम्लाका राजासँग मिलेर देवीको मन्दिर बनाए।','[\"मन्दिर करिब ४,२०० मिटरमा छ। नेपाली सेनाले ४,२२० मिटर भनेको छ।\", \"यहाँको मुख्य पूजा जनै पूर्णिमाको अघिल्लो दिन, श्रावण शुक्ल चतुर्दशीमा, हुन्छ।\", \"यहाँ दुई पुजारी छन्, एक कालीकोट जिल्लाको र अर्का बाजुरा जिल्लाको प्रतिनिधि।\", \"नेपाली सेनाले प्राचीन स्मारक संरक्षण ऐनअन्तर्गत सन् २०२५ को अप्रिलदेखि जुलाईसम्म करिब २ करोड रुपैयाँ लगाएर मन्दिर पुनर्निर्माण गर्‍यो।\", \"मन्दिरका पुजारीका अनुसार एक वर्षमा ४५,००० भन्दा बढी भक्तजनले दर्शन गरे।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Malika Chaturdashi (Janai Purnima fair)\", \"note\": \"Main puja on Shrawan Shukla Chaturdashi, the day before Janai Purnima; the date can fall in Bhadra.\", \"month\": \"Shrawan\", \"name_np\": \"मालिका चतुर्दशी (जनै पूर्णिमा मेला)\", \"note_np\": \"मुख्य पूजा श्रावण शुक्ल चतुर्दशीमा, जनै पूर्णिमाको अघिल्लो दिन हुन्छ। मिति कहिलेकाहीँ भदौमा पर्न सक्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Ganga Dashahara\", \"note\": \"A state-sponsored puja is held and many pilgrims visit.\", \"month\": \"Jestha\", \"name_np\": \"गङ्गा दशहरा\", \"note_np\": \"राज्यको तर्फबाट पूजा गरिन्छ र धेरै तीर्थयात्री आउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Badimalika_Temple_4186M%2C_Bajura%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Badimalika_Temple_4186M%2C_Bajura%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"sigdelsanjog\", \"caption\": \"The hilltop shrine and stone walls before the 2025 rebuilding\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badimalika_Temple_4186M,_Bajura,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beautiful_Collection_of_Bells_seen_at_Badimalika_Temple%2C_Bajura%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Beautiful_Collection_of_Bells_seen_at_Badimalika_Temple%2C_Bajura%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"sigdelsanjog\", \"caption\": \"Rows of bells offered by pilgrims\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beautiful_Collection_of_Bells_seen_at_Badimalika_Temple,_Bajura,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Trishulas%2C_Mahadev%27s_weapon_seen_on_top_of_Badimalika_Temple%2C_Bajura%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Trishulas%2C_Mahadev%27s_weapon_seen_on_top_of_Badimalika_Temple%2C_Bajura%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"sigdelsanjog\", \"caption\": \"Tridents offered on top of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trishulas,_Mahadev%27s_weapon_seen_on_top_of_Badimalika_Temple,_Bajura,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Prayers_raising_Nepal%27s_Flag_in_front_of_Badimalika_Temple%2C_Bajura.jpg/1280px-Prayers_raising_Nepal%27s_Flag_in_front_of_Badimalika_Temple%2C_Bajura.jpg\", \"author\": \"sigdelsanjog\", \"caption\": \"Pilgrims raising a flag in front of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prayers_raising_Nepal%27s_Flag_in_front_of_Badimalika_Temple,_Bajura.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9F%E0%A5%8B.JPG/1280px-%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9F%E0%A5%8B.JPG\", \"author\": \"Punya\", \"caption\": \"The high pastures on the trail to Badimalika\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9F%E0%A5%8B.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%82%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87.JPG\", \"author\": \"Punya\", \"caption\": \"Worship at Badimalika Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%82%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"stone-spire\", \"notes\": \"Small white shrine with a pyramid roof inside dry-stone walls on a bare grassy summit; stone frames crowded with bells and tridents. Based on pre-2025 photos.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"whitewashed-stone\", \"colors\": [\"#f2f2ee\", \"#6d6a63\", \"#2f6fd0\"], \"features\": [\"bell\", \"trident\", \"flags-red\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [5, 5], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"snow-peaks\", \"himalaya-backdrop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(34,'ugratara-temple-dadeldhura','Ugratara Temple, Dadeldhura','उग्रतारा मन्दिर, डडेलधुरा','Dadeldhura (Amargadhi)','Sudurpashchim','Dadeldhura',NULL,29.334619,80.603599,'pagoda','Hindu','Ugratara (a form of the goddess Parvati / Bhagawati)',NULL,'Founding date unknown. Tradition says a Saud family farmer found the idol while ploughing; Naga Malla of Doti later renovated it, and King Birendra helped a later renovation. Since rebuilt with cement and concrete.','Doti (Malla) kings, per local tradition','Hilltop temple compound in a modern concrete version of the pagoda style: a pink and turquoise painted sanctum on a stepped platform with guardian and lion figures along the stairs, long arcaded halls with carved bracket pillars, and small tiered pagoda roofs, all ringed by prayer flags.',0,'The hilltop goddess temple of Dadeldhura, counted among the nine Shakti Peeths of the far west and host of the great Dehijant fair.','Walk up the paved path through the grass, and you reach the hilltop temple that people call the heart of Dadeldhura. Forest closes in on three sides, and the bright pink and turquoise temple rises in front of you on its stepped platform, with guardian figures and lions lining the stairs. This is Ugratara, a fierce form of the goddess, counted among the nine Shakti Peeths of Nepal\'s far west. The local story begins in a field: a farmer of the Saud family was ploughing when his blade struck a stone, and from that discovery came the first temple. Later, Naga Malla, a king of Doti, renovated it. People here believe Ugratara brings fertility and wealth, protects villages from disaster, and even reunites friends who have lost touch. Come on the full moon of Kartik and you will find the hill packed for Dehijant, described as the biggest religious fair in Sudurpashchim.','A farmer of the Saud family is said to have struck the goddess\'s stone image with his plough while working his field; The stone was protected and a temple built over it.','[\"The temple is about 4 km west of Dadeldhura bazaar, in Amargadhi Municipality-7.\", \"It is counted among the nine Shakti Peeths and nine Bhagawati temples of the far west.\", \"Local accounts say Naga Malla, king of Doti, renovated the temple after it was founded by a Saud family farmer.\", \"Its Dehijant fair on the full moon of Kartik is described as the biggest religious fair in the province.\", \"Devotees believe the goddess reunites friends and relatives who have lost touch.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Ugratara_Temple%2C_Dadeldhura%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Ugratara_Temple%2C_Dadeldhura%2C_Nepal.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ugratara_Temple,_Dadeldhura,_Nepal.jpg','Gunjan Raj Giri · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,doti (malla) kings, per local tradition,dadeldhura (amargadhi),legend,art,sudurpashchim','[\"https://nepaltraveller.com/travel/pilgrimage-sites/ugratara-temple\", \"https://ekantipur.com/sudurpaschim-pradesh/2025/10/27/en/ugratara-temple-shaktipeeth-made-of-bleeding-stones-26-57.html\", \"https://dineshkhabar.com/article/104589\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/842712043\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Ugratara_Temple,_Dadeldhura,_Nepal\"]','डडेलधुराको डाँडामाथिको देवी मन्दिर, सुदूरपश्चिमका नौ शक्तिपीठमध्ये एक र ठूलो देहिजन्त मेला लाग्ने ठाउँ।','घाँसका बीचको पक्की बाटो उक्लनुहोस्। तपाईं डडेलधुराको मुटु भनिने डाँडाको मन्दिरमा पुग्नुहुन्छ। तीन तिरबाट जङ्गलले घेरेको छ। चटकदार गुलाबी र फिरोजी रङको मन्दिर तपाईंको अगाडि तहतह चौतारीमाथि उभिएको छ। भर्‍याङको छेउमा रक्षक मूर्ति र सिंहका मूर्ति पङ्क्तिमा छन्। यो उग्रतारा हो, देवीको एक उग्र रूप, जो नेपालको सुदूरपश्चिमका नौ शक्तिपीठमध्ये एक मानिन्छ। स्थानीय कथा एउटा खेतबाट सुरु हुन्छ। साउद परिवारका एक किसान हलो जोत्दै थिए, उनको फाली ढुङ्गामा ठोक्कियो, र त्यही भेटबाट पहिलो मन्दिर बन्यो। पछि डोटीका राजा नाग मल्लले मन्दिर मर्मत गरे। यहाँका मानिस विश्वास गर्छन्, उग्रताराले सन्तान र धन दिन्छिन्, गाउँलाई विपत्तिबाट जोगाउँछिन्, र सम्पर्क टुटेका साथीलाई पनि फेरि जोडिदिन्छिन्। कार्तिक पूर्णिमामा आउनुभयो भने देहिजन्तका लागि डाँडा भरिएको देख्नुहुन्छ। यसलाई सुदूरपश्चिमको सबैभन्दा ठूलो धार्मिक मेला भनिन्छ।','साउद परिवारका एक किसानले खेत जोत्दा हलोले देवीको ढुङ्गाको मूर्तिमा ठोक्किएको भनिन्छ। त्यो ढुङ्गा जोगाइयो र त्यसमाथि मन्दिर बनाइयो।','[\"मन्दिर डडेलधुरा बजारभन्दा करिब ४ किमी पश्चिममा, अमरगढी नगरपालिका-७ मा छ।\", \"यो सुदूरपश्चिमका नौ शक्तिपीठ र नौ भगवती मन्दिरमध्ये एक मानिन्छ।\", \"स्थानीय भनाइअनुसार साउद परिवारका किसानले स्थापना गरेपछि डोटीका राजा नाग मल्लले मन्दिर मर्मत गरे।\", \"कार्तिक पूर्णिमामा लाग्ने देहिजन्त मेलालाई प्रदेशकै सबैभन्दा ठूलो धार्मिक मेला भनिन्छ।\", \"भक्तजनको विश्वास छ, देवीले सम्पर्क टुटेका साथी र आफन्तलाई फेरि जोडिदिन्छिन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dehijant fair\", \"note\": \"Held on Kartik Shukla Purnima with night-time puja; described as the biggest fair in the province.\", \"month\": \"Kartik\", \"name_np\": \"देहिजन्त मेला\", \"note_np\": \"कार्तिक शुक्ल पूर्णिमामा रातभर पूजासहित लाग्ने मेला। यसलाई प्रदेशकै सबैभन्दा ठूलो मेला भनिन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Ugratara_Temple_Dadeldhura_20151230_120955.jpg/1280px-Ugratara_Temple_Dadeldhura_20151230_120955.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ricky Partel\", \"caption\": \"The hilltop temple compound with its paved approach\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ugratara_Temple_Dadeldhura_20151230_120955.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Ugratara_temple_Dadeldhura_Nepal.JPG/1280px-Ugratara_temple_Dadeldhura_Nepal.JPG\", \"author\": \"Sanjayapirk\", \"caption\": \"Pink-painted side hall with carved bracket pillars\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ugratara_temple_Dadeldhura_Nepal.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Ugratara_Bhagabati_Temple.jpg/1280px-Ugratara_Bhagabati_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Yadav Singh Dhami\", \"caption\": \"Devotees at the temple veranda\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ugratara_Bhagabati_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Ugratara_Temple_Dadeldhura_20151230_135100.jpg/1280px-Ugratara_Temple_Dadeldhura_20151230_135100.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ricky Partel\", \"caption\": \"Painted entrance gate with the goddess and lions\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ugratara_Temple_Dadeldhura_20151230_135100.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/29/Ugratara_temple_Dadeldhura_.jpg\", \"author\": \"रमेश सिंह बोहरा\", \"caption\": \"Ugratara Temple on its hilltop in Dadeldhura\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ugratara_temple_Dadeldhura_.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Pink and turquoise painted sanctum atop wide striped steps lined with guardian statues and lions, an ornate arch with lions above the door, prayer flags all around.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#e8a3b5\", \"#3bb3a8\", \"#d9d4c8\"], \"features\": [\"guardian-pairs-on-stairs\", \"lion-statues\", \"bell\", \"prayer-flags\", \"toran\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [10, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 6, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\", \"garden-lawn\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(35,'ajaymerukot','Ajaymerukot','अजयमेरुकोट','Dadeldhura','Sudurpashchim','Dadeldhura',NULL,29.304000,80.591000,'fort','Hindu',NULL,NULL,'Founded by the 13th-14th century as a capital of the Doti kingdom that followed the Katyuri dynasty; inscriptions of King Niraya Pal (Saka 1250) and King Nag Malla (Saka 1306) were found. Destroyed in an attack in the 16th century.','Doti (Katyuri successors: Pal and Malla kings)','Hilltop palace-fort ruins: dry-stone walls of a two-storey palace of about 14 rooms with a central corridor and stone stair, carved stone shikhara shrines, pillared stone mandapas with concentric carved ceilings, defensive towers, wells and a stable.',0,'Ridge-top ruins of a medieval Doti capital, with carved stone shrines and a palace excavated for the first time in 2025.','You are on a ridge in Dadeldhura, where a river curls around three sides and only one path leads up. This was Ajaymerukot, one of the capitals of the Doti kingdom that rose after the old Katyuri realm broke apart. The name is often explained as ajaya, invincible, and meru, mountain, and you can see why. Look at the carved stone shrines with their stacked shikhara towers, and the pavilion whose stone pillars still hold up a heavy lintel. Stand beneath one ceiling and look up at rings of carved stone circling a lotus. The carvings are believed to be the work of Jaad artists from India. In 2025 the Department of Archaeology excavated the palace for the first time. They found a two-storey building with about fourteen rooms and inscriptions in eight places, naming kings Niraya Pal and Nag Malla. Tradition says the fort was destroyed in a sixteenth-century attack, and the capital moved to Silgadhi in Doti.','Local tradition links the name to a King Ajay Pal, but no record of such a ruler has been found.','[\"Ajaymerukot was one of the capitals of the Doti kingdom that emerged after the fall of the Katyuri dynasty.\", \"The 2025 excavation found inscriptions in eight places, including records of King Niraya Pal (Saka 1250) and King Nag Malla (Saka 1306).\", \"The main palace was a two-storey building with about 14 rooms, a central corridor and a stone staircase.\", \"After its destruction in the 16th century the Doti capital moved to Silgadhi.\", \"The ridge is protected by a river on three sides, leaving only one approach.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ajayamerukot._Dadeldhura_Pal.jpg/1280px-Ajayamerukot._Dadeldhura_Pal.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajayamerukot._Dadeldhura_Pal.jpg','कत्यूरी राजाका वंशज · CC BY-SA 4.0','fort,hindu,doti (katyuri successors: pal and malla kings),dadeldhura,legend,art,sudurpashchim','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajaymerukot\", \"https://risingnepaldaily.com/news/57537\", \"https://ekantipur.com/en/news/2025/02/20/historical-ajaymerukot-is-being-excavated-41-05.html\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q65395572\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Ajaymerukot\"]','मध्यकालीन डोटीको राजधानीको डाँडामाथिका भग्नावशेष। यहाँ कुँदिएका ढुङ्गाका मन्दिर छन् र सन् २०२५ मा पहिलोपटक दरबारको उत्खनन गरिएको थियो।','तपाईं डडेलधुराको एउटा डाँडामा हुनुहुन्छ। यहाँ तीन तिरबाट नदी घुमेर बगेको छ र माथि आउने बाटो एउटै मात्र छ। यो अजयमेरुकोट हो। पुरानो कत्यूरी राज्य टुक्रिएपछि उदाएको डोटी राज्यका राजधानीमध्ये एक। नामको अर्थ प्रायः अजय, अर्थात् अजेय, र मेरु, अर्थात् पर्वत, भनेर लगाइन्छ। यहाँ आएपछि किन त्यसो भनिएको हो भन्ने बुझिन्छ। शिखर शैलीका तहतह भएका कुँदिएका ढुङ्गाका मन्दिर हेर्नुहोस्। ढुङ्गाका खम्बाले अहिलेसम्म भारी पाटा थामेको मण्डप पनि हेर्नुहोस्। एउटा छतमुनि उभिएर माथि हेर्दा कमलको वरिपरि गोलो घुमेका कुँदिएका ढुङ्गाका घेरा देखिन्छन्। यी कुँदाइ भारतका जाद कलाकारको काम हो भन्ने मानिन्छ। सन् २०२५ मा पुरातत्त्व विभागले पहिलोपटक दरबारको उत्खनन गर्‍यो। उनीहरूले करिब चौध कोठा भएको दुई तले भवन भेट्टाए। आठ ठाउँमा अभिलेख पनि भेटिए, जसमा राजा निरय पाल र नाग मल्लको नाम छ। परम्पराअनुसार सोह्रौँ शताब्दीको आक्रमणमा किल्ला ध्वस्त भयो र राजधानी डोटीको सिलगढीमा सारियो।','स्थानीय मान्यताले नामलाई राजा अजय पालसँग जोड्छ, तर त्यस्ता राजाको कुनै अभिलेख भेटिएको छैन।','[\"अजयमेरुकोट कत्यूरी वंशको पतनपछि उदाएको डोटी राज्यका राजधानीमध्ये एक थियो।\", \"सन् २०२५ को उत्खननमा आठ ठाउँमा अभिलेख भेटिए, जसमा राजा निरय पाल (शक १२५०) र राजा नाग मल्ल (शक १३०६) का अभिलेख पनि छन्।\", \"मुख्य दरबार करिब १४ कोठा, बीचमा करिडोर र ढुङ्गाको भर्‍याङ भएको दुई तले भवन थियो।\", \"सोह्रौँ शताब्दीमा ध्वस्त भएपछि डोटीको राजधानी सिलगढीमा सारियो।\", \"डाँडा तीन तिरबाट नदीले सुरक्षित छ, माथि पुग्ने बाटो एउटै मात्र छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/Ajayamerukot.jpg\", \"author\": \"रमेश सिंह बोहरा\", \"caption\": \"Ruined stone mandapa with carved pillars\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajayamerukot.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Dadeldhura_Ajayameharu_kot_Baithak.jpg/1280px-Dadeldhura_Ajayameharu_kot_Baithak.jpg\", \"author\": \"कत्यूरी राजाका वंशज\", \"caption\": \"Pillared stone pavilion known as the royal baithak\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dadeldhura_Ajayameharu_kot_Baithak.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/11/Ajamerukot-Dadeldhura-%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A7%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%A8_%E0%A4%A1%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%9F%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B7%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B_%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%81%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D_%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%82%E0%A4%B6%E0%A4%9C_%E0%A4%A8%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%AF_%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2_%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B_%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%9F_%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A5%E0%A4%B2_%E0%A4%85%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%81.jpg\", \"author\": \"Kartikeyapur dynasty\", \"caption\": \"Dry-stone palace walls and a carved pillar fragment\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajamerukot-Dadeldhura-%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A7%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%A8_%E0%A4%A1%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%9F%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B7%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B_%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%81%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8D_%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%82%E0%A4%B6%E0%A4%9C_%E0%A4%A8%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%AF_%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2_%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B_%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%9F_%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A5%E0%A4%B2_%E0%A4%85%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%81.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Ajayamerukot100.jpg\", \"author\": \"रमेश सिंह बोहरा\", \"caption\": \"Carved concentric stone ceiling inside a shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajayamerukot100.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Ajameru_Fort%2C_%E0%A4%85%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%81_%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%9F_%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A5%E0%A4%B2.jpg/1280px-Ajameru_Fort%2C_%E0%A4%85%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%81_%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%9F_%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A5%E0%A4%B2.jpg\", \"author\": \"कत्यूरी राजाका वंशज\", \"caption\": \"Visitors at the excavated palace site on its ridge\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajameru_Fort,_%E0%A4%85%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%81_%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%9F_%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A5%E0%A4%B2.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}]','{\"kind\": \"ruins\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Gray dry-stone palace walls on a dry ridge, beside two small stacked-stone shikhara shrines and a pillared stone pavilion with a heavy lintel.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#8d8b84\", \"#b39f80\", \"#7a6a4a\"], \"features\": [\"stone-pillar\", \"carved-windows\"], \"height_m\": 3, \"footprint_m\": [30, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"river\", \"forest\", \"terraced-fields\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(36,'amargadhi-fort','Amargadhi Fort','अमरगढी किल्ला','Dadeldhura (Khalanga)','Sudurpashchim','Dadeldhura',NULL,29.299523,80.585827,'fort','Other',NULL,1790,'Built in 1847 BS (about 1790 CE) during the Gorkhali unification campaign under King Rana Bahadur Shah, with construction supervised by Amar Singh Thapa and other commanders.','Shah','Hilltop fort on a cliff above Khalanga, built of stone and timber: high battered stone walls, a stone stairway and concealed doorway, and stone-walled rooms around an inner yard. A statue of Amar Singh Thapa stands at the entrance.',0,'The 18th-century Gorkhali fort above Dadeldhura bazaar, linked to commander Amar Singh Thapa.','Climb the red-and-white painted steps and put your hand on this sloping stone wall. You are at Amargadhi, the fort that gives this municipality its name, perched on a cliff above Khalanga at about six and a half thousand feet. It was built around 1790, in 1847 by the Nepali calendar, as Gorkhali armies of King Rana Bahadur Shah pushed west to bring Doti into the growing kingdom. Commander Amar Singh Thapa and his officers supervised the work, and afterwards he established Gorkhali rule over the region. At the entrance his statue carries his famous boast that he is a tiger\'s cub, not a scavenging dog. Walk the narrow stone stair, find the hidden door, and look into the stone rooms where soldiers once lived. An old resident remembers cannons here that were fired at the nearby parade ground on Fulpati during Dashain. Since 2009 the municipality has cared for the fort.',NULL,'[\"The fort was built in 1847 BS (about 1790 CE) during the unification campaign of King Rana Bahadur Shah.\", \"Amar Singh Thapa, Kaji Jagat Pandey and several captains and subbas supervised its construction.\", \"Its shape is said to resemble a lion\'s head, with its walls likened to a mane.\", \"A resident who served at the fort recalled five cannons, about 50 rifles and a dozen Bhimsen-nal guns, which are now missing.\", \"Amargadhi Municipality has managed the fort since December 2009.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Amar_Gadi.jpg/1280px-Amar_Gadi.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amar_Gadi.jpg','Rajivkilanashrestha · CC BY-SA 4.0','fort,other,shah,dadeldhura (khalanga),art,festival,sudurpashchim','[\"https://risingnepaldaily.com/news/42081\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amargadhi\", \"https://dineshkhabar.com/node/40208\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/842555328\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Amargadhi\"]','डडेलधुरा बजारमाथिको १८औँ शताब्दीको गोरखाली किल्ला, सेनापति अमर सिंह थापासँग जोडिएको।','रातो र सेतो रङ लगाइएका भर्‍याङ उक्लनुहोस् र ढल्केको ढुङ्गाको पर्खालमा हात राख्नुहोस्। तपाईं अमरगढीमा हुनुहुन्छ। यही किल्लाले यो नगरपालिकाको नाम दिएको हो। यो खलङ्गामाथिको भीरमा करिब साढे छ हजार फिटको उचाइमा छ। करिब सन् १७९० मा, नेपाली संवत्मा १८४७ मा, यो बनेको थियो। त्यतिबेला राजा रणबहादुर शाहका गोरखाली सेना डोटीलाई बढ्दो राज्यमा मिलाउन पश्चिम लागेका थिए। सेनापति अमर सिंह थापा र उनका अधिकारीले निर्माणको रेखदेख गरे। पछि उनले यो क्षेत्रमा गोरखाली शासन जमाए। प्रवेशद्वारमा उनको मूर्ति छ। मूर्तिमा उनको प्रसिद्ध घोषणा लेखिएको छ: म बाघको बच्चा हुँ, फोहोर खाने कुकुर होइन। साँघुरो ढुङ्गाको भर्‍याङ हिँड्नुहोस्, लुकेको ढोका खोज्नुहोस्, र सिपाही बस्ने ढुङ्गाका कोठाभित्र हेर्नुहोस्। एक वृद्ध स्थानीयले यहाँ तोप हुन्थे भनी सम्झन्छन्। दशैँको फूलपातीमा नजिकैको परेड मैदानमा ती पड्काइन्थे। सन् २००९ देखि नगरपालिकाले किल्लाको हेरचाह गर्दै आएको छ।',NULL,'[\"किल्ला राजा रणबहादुर शाहको एकीकरण अभियानका बेला वि.सं. १८४७ (करिब सन् १७९०) मा बनेको थियो।\", \"अमर सिंह थापा, काजी जगत पाण्डे र केही कप्तान र सुब्बाले यसको निर्माणको रेखदेख गरे।\", \"यसको आकार सिंहको टाउकोजस्तो छ र पर्खाललाई त्यसको केशरसँग तुलना गरिन्छ भनिन्छ।\", \"किल्लामा काम गरेका एक स्थानीयले पाँचवटा तोप, करिब ५० वटा राइफल र एक दर्जन भीमसेन-नाल बन्दुक सम्झन्छन्। अहिले ती हराएका छन्।\", \"अमरगढी नगरपालिकाले सन् २००९ को डिसेम्बरदेखि किल्लाको व्यवस्थापन गर्दै आएको छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Fulpati (Bada Dashain)\", \"note\": \"Cannons were traditionally fired from the nearby Tudikhel on Fulpati.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"फूलपाती (बडा दशैँ)\", \"note_np\": \"फूलपातीका दिन नजिकैको टुँडिखेलबाट तोप पड्काउने चलन थियो।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Wall_of_Amargadi.jpg/1280px-Wall_of_Amargadi.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajivkilanashrestha\", \"caption\": \"Thick stone wall of the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wall_of_Amargadi.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Hidden_Door_of_Amargadi.jpg/1280px-Hidden_Door_of_Amargadi.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajivkilanashrestha\", \"caption\": \"A concealed doorway in the fort walls\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hidden_Door_of_Amargadi.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Amargadhi_killA.jpg/1280px-Amargadhi_killA.jpg\", \"author\": \"Mensahme01\", \"caption\": \"Stone-walled barrack rooms inside the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amargadhi_killA.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Amargadhi_Killa.jpg/1280px-Amargadhi_Killa.jpg\", \"author\": \"रमेश सिंह बोहरा\", \"caption\": \"Narrow stone stairway leading into the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amargadhi_Killa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Amarsingh_Thapa.JPG/1280px-Amarsingh_Thapa.JPG\", \"author\": \"Rajiv Timalsina\", \"caption\": \"Statue of Amar Singh Thapa at the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amarsingh_Thapa.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"fort\", \"roof\": \"slate\", \"notes\": \"Tall battered brown stone wall on a cliff edge, climbed by steps painted in red and white stripes; a small slate-roofed guard house on top.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#a07a55\", \"#c0392b\", \"#f2f2f2\"], \"features\": [\"watchtower\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [60, 40], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\", \"market-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(37,'tripurasundari-temple-baitadi','Tripurasundari Temple, Baitadi','त्रिपुरासुन्दरी मन्दिर, बैतडी','Baitadi (Tripurasundari)','Sudurpashchim','Baitadi',NULL,29.557770,80.393260,'pagoda','Hindu','Tripura Sundari (Ransaini Bhagwati)',NULL,'Founding date unknown; it is believed to have been built long before the reign of the Doti king Nagi Malla. The present building is a modern multi-roofed pagoda.','unknown','Three-roofed pagoda-style temple on a low stone platform: a wide front porch of red-painted pillars and cusped arches under a gabled roof with carved trim, topped by two diminishing tiled roofs and a gilded finial. The grassy courtyard holds small shrines, bells and tall flag poles.',0,'A hilltop Bhagwati temple in Baitadi, one of the seven prominent Bhagwati shrines of Nepal, drawing pilgrims from both sides of the Mahakali.','You have reached the grassy courtyard of Tripurasundari, in the hills of Baitadi near Nepal\'s western border. In front of you rises a temple with three stacked roofs, its porch held up by red pillars and pointed arches. Locally the goddess is called Ransaini, and with the title Bhagwati she is counted among the seven prominent Bhagwati temples of Nepal. Her name, Tripura Sundari, means the beautiful one of the three worlds. Look around the courtyard: tall poles with flags, small shrines, and bells hanging from the branches of a tree, each one a pilgrim\'s offering. People say the temple is older than the reign of King Nagi Malla of Doti, though no one knows exactly when it was founded. Come during Ashadhi Jatra in midsummer and you will see the goddess carried on a chariot to the village of Kapadi and back, with devotees arriving from Nepal and from India across the Mahakali.',NULL,'[\"Locally the goddess is known as Ransaini Bhagwati.\", \"It is counted among the seven prominent Bhagwati temples of Nepal.\", \"The temple is believed to predate the reign of the Doti king Nagi Malla.\", \"During Ashadhi Jatra the goddess is carried by chariot to Kapadi village and returned to the temple.\", \"Nepal listed it among its top 100 tourist destinations for Visit Nepal 2020.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Front_view_of_Tripurasundari_temple%2C_Baitadi.jpg/1280px-Front_view_of_Tripurasundari_temple%2C_Baitadi.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_view_of_Tripurasundari_temple,_Baitadi.jpg','Nirajan pant · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,baitadi (tripurasundari),art,festival,sudurpashchim','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tripura_Sundari_Temple,_Nepal\", \"https://dineshkhabar.com/node/139011\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/tripura-sundari-temple-a-sacred-shakti-peeth-in-the-hills-of-nepal\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q134311703\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Tripurasundari_temple,_Baitadi\"]','बैतडीको डाँडामाथिको भगवती मन्दिर, नेपालका सात प्रमुख भगवती मन्दिरमध्ये एक, जहाँ महाकालीका दुवै किनाराबाट तीर्थयात्री आउँछन्।','तपाईं नेपालको पश्चिमी सीमा नजिक, बैतडीको पहाडमा रहेको त्रिपुरासुन्दरीको घाँसे आँगनमा पुग्नुभएको छ। तपाईंको अगाडि तीन तहको छाना भएको मन्दिर उभिएको छ। यसको पोर्च रातो खम्बा र टुप्पो भएका मेहराबले अडिएको छ। स्थानीय रूपमा देवीलाई रणसैनी भनिन्छ। भगवतीको उपाधिसहित उनी नेपालका सात प्रमुख भगवती मन्दिरमध्ये गनिन्छिन्। त्रिपुरासुन्दरी नामको अर्थ तीन लोककी सुन्दरी हो। आँगनवरिपरि हेर्नुहोस्। अग्ला झन्डाका खम्बा छन्, साना मन्दिर छन्, र रूखका हाँगामा घण्टी झुन्डिएका छन्। हरेक घण्टी कुनै तीर्थयात्रीको चढाएको भेटी हो। मानिस भन्छन्, यो मन्दिर डोटीका राजा नागी मल्लको शासनकालभन्दा पुरानो हो। तर कहिले बनेको भन्ने ठ्याक्कै कसैलाई थाहा छैन। आषाढी जात्राको बेला, गर्मीको बीचमा, आउनुभयो भने देवीलाई रथमा राखेर कपडी गाउँ लगिने र फर्काइने देख्नुहुन्छ। त्यतिबेला नेपाल र महाकालीपारिको भारतबाट भक्तजन आउँछन्।',NULL,'[\"स्थानीय रूपमा देवीलाई रणसैनी भगवती भनिन्छ।\", \"यो नेपालका सात प्रमुख भगवती मन्दिरमध्ये एक गनिन्छ।\", \"मन्दिर डोटीका राजा नागी मल्लको शासनकालभन्दा पुरानो हो भन्ने विश्वास छ।\", \"आषाढी जात्रामा देवीलाई रथमा राखेर कपडी गाउँ लगिन्छ र फेरि मन्दिरमा ल्याइन्छ।\", \"नेपालले भ्रमण वर्ष २०२० का लागि यसलाई आफ्ना शीर्ष १०० पर्यटकीय गन्तव्यमा राखेको थियो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Ashadhi Jatra\", \"note\": \"Night worship on Asar Shukla Ashtami; main jatra on Navami, with a chariot procession to Kapadi.\", \"month\": \"Ashadh\", \"name_np\": \"आषाढी जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"असार शुक्ल अष्टमीमा रातभर पूजा हुन्छ। नवमीमा मुख्य जात्रा लाग्छ, जसमा रथ यात्रा कपडीसम्म जान्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Bada Dashain\", \"note\": \"Special fair and worship of the goddess during Dashain.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"बडा दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दशैँमा देवीको विशेष मेला र पूजा हुन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Chaite Dashain\", \"note\": \"A fair is held at the temple.\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"चैते दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"मन्दिरमा मेला लाग्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Tripurasundari_temple%2C_Baitadi.jpg/1280px-Tripurasundari_temple%2C_Baitadi.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirajan pant\", \"caption\": \"The temple with flag poles and small shrines in its courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tripurasundari_temple,_Baitadi.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Backside_view_of_Tripurasundari_temple%2C_Baitadi.jpg/1280px-Backside_view_of_Tripurasundari_temple%2C_Baitadi.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirajan pant\", \"caption\": \"Rear view of the tiered temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Backside_view_of_Tripurasundari_temple,_Baitadi.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Ghanta_at_the_Tripurasundari_temple.jpg/1280px-Ghanta_at_the_Tripurasundari_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirajan pant\", \"caption\": \"Bells hung in a tree in the temple courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghanta_at_the_Tripurasundari_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Main_entrance_gate_of_Tripurasundari_temple.jpg/1280px-Main_entrance_gate_of_Tripurasundari_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirajan pant\", \"caption\": \"Main entrance gate of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Main_entrance_gate_of_Tripurasundari_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Tripurasundari_Temple%2C_Baitadi%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Tripurasundari_Temple%2C_Baitadi%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirajan pant\", \"caption\": \"The temple\'s tiered roofs seen up close\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tripurasundari_Temple,_Baitadi,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Tripurasundari.jpg/1280px-Tripurasundari.jpg\", \"author\": \"Thehimalayanhealer\", \"caption\": \"The temple hill at Devikot with Himalayan peaks beyond\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tripurasundari.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Wide porch of red pillars and white cusped arches under a carved gable, topped by two smaller tiled pagoda roofs and a finial; grassy yard with flag poles.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"timber\", \"colors\": [\"#c0392b\", \"#9a5b3c\", \"#e8e4dc\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"bell\", \"flags-red\", \"sacred-tree\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [14, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"garden-lawn\", \"himalaya-backdrop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(38,'shaileshwori-temple-doti','Shaileshwori Temple, Silgadhi','शैलेश्वरी मन्दिर, सिलगढी','Silgadhi (Dipayal Silgadhi)','Sudurpashchim','Doti',NULL,29.266829,80.980876,'pagoda','Hindu','Shaileshwori (a form of Parvati)',NULL,'Date unknown; the goddess is said to be mentioned in the Skanda Purana. Silgadhi became the Doti capital after Ajaymerukot fell in the 16th century.','unknown','A small temple compound shaded by old trees on a stone-paved courtyard: a whitewashed and painted shrine hall with a red-trimmed gable, carved timber front and a small tiered tower roof, entered through a painted gateway guarded by lion statues and a large trident.',0,'The goddess temple of Silgadhi, said to be named in the Skanda Purana, where Parvati is believed to have emerged from a rock.','You are in Silgadhi, the old hill town of Doti, standing on a stone courtyard shaded by great trees. Ahead is the temple of Shaileshwori, one of the most famous shrines of Nepal\'s far-western hills. The name comes from shaila or shila, meaning rock. One telling says Shiva and Parvati chose these hills as a retreat, and when Brahma, Vishnu and the other gods came searching for Shiva, Parvati, embarrassed, hid by turning into stone. When the gods prayed to her, she emerged again, and the rock came to be worshipped as Shiladevi, later Shaileshwori. Look at the painted gateway with its lions and its giant trident, then step through to the shrine where devotees come every day to ask the goddess to ease their troubles and grant their wishes. Nepal honored this temple on a postage stamp in 1985. During Dashain the courtyard fills with devotees for special pujas, and the annual Shaileshwori Mela brings music and celebration to the town.','Parvati is said to have hidden herself as a stone when the gods came looking for Shiva in these hills; when they prayed to her she emerged from the rock, and the stone was worshipped as Shiladevi, later known as Shaileshwori.','[\"The goddess Shaileshwori is said to be mentioned in the Skanda Purana.\", \"Nepal issued a postage stamp showing the temple on 15 December 1985 in its Visit Nepal series.\", \"Her name comes from shila (rock), from the legend that Parvati emerged from a stone.\", \"After Ajaymerukot was destroyed in the 16th century, the Doti capital moved to Silgadhi, the town around this temple.\", \"Special pujas are held during Dashain, and an annual Shaileshwori Mela takes place.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Shree_Shaileshwori_Temple.jpg/1280px-Shree_Shaileshwori_Temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shree_Shaileshwori_Temple.jpg','Gaurav Dhwaj Khadka · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,silgadhi (dipayal silgadhi),legend,art,festival,sudurpashchim','[\"https://istampgallery.com/visit-nepal-series-1985/\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/shaileshwori-temple-dotis-peaceful-hideaway\", \"https://risingnepaldaily.com/news/57537\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/10538870509\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shree_Shaileshwori_Temple.jpg\"]','सिलगढीको देवी मन्दिर, जसको नाम स्कन्द पुराणमा आएको भनिन्छ, र जहाँ पार्वती चट्टानबाट प्रकट भएकी थिइन् भन्ने विश्वास छ।','तपाईं डोटीको पुरानो पहाडी सहर सिलगढीमा हुनुहुन्छ। ठूला रूखको छायाँमा ढुङ्गा ओछ्याइएको आँगनमा उभिनुभएको छ। अगाडि शैलेश्वरीको मन्दिर छ। यो सुदूरपश्चिमका पहाडका सबैभन्दा प्रसिद्ध मन्दिरमध्ये एक हो। नाम शैल वा शिला बाट आएको हो, जसको अर्थ चट्टान हो। एउटा कथाअनुसार शिव र पार्वतीले यी पहाडलाई एकान्तमा बस्ने ठाउँ बनाए। ब्रह्मा, विष्णु र अरू देवता शिवलाई खोज्दै आउँदा पार्वती लज्जित भएर ढुङ्गा बनी लुकिन्। देवताले प्रार्थना गरेपछि उनी फेरि प्रकट भइन्। त्यही चट्टानको शिलादेवी, पछि शैलेश्वरीका रूपमा पूजा हुन थाल्यो। सिंह र ठूलो त्रिशूल भएको रङ्गीन ढोका हेर्नुहोस्। त्यसपछि मन्दिरभित्र जानुहोस्। भक्तजन दिनहुँ यहाँ आएर देवीसँग आफ्ना दुःख हल्का गर्न र इच्छा पूरा गर्न प्रार्थना गर्छन्। सन् १९८५ मा नेपालले यो मन्दिरको हुलाक टिकट निकालेर सम्मान गर्‍यो। दशैँमा विशेष पूजाका लागि आँगन भक्तजनले भरिन्छ, र वार्षिक शैलेश्वरी मेलाले सहरमा सङ्गीत र रमाइलो ल्याउँछ।','देवताहरू शिवलाई खोज्दै यी पहाडमा आउँदा पार्वतीले आफूलाई ढुङ्गा बनाएर लुकाइन् भनिन्छ। उनीहरूले प्रार्थना गरेपछि उनी चट्टानबाट प्रकट भइन्, र त्यो ढुङ्गाको शिलादेवी, पछि शैलेश्वरीका रूपमा पूजा गरियो।','[\"देवी शैलेश्वरीको नाम स्कन्द पुराणमा आएको भनिन्छ।\", \"नेपालले सन् १९८५ डिसेम्बर १५ मा भिजिट नेपाल शृङ्खलामा यो मन्दिरको हुलाक टिकट जारी गर्‍यो।\", \"पार्वती ढुङ्गाबाट प्रकट भएकी कथाबाट उनको नाम शिला (चट्टान) बाट आएको हो।\", \"सोह्रौँ शताब्दीमा अजयमेरुकोट ध्वस्त भएपछि डोटीको राजधानी यही मन्दिरवरिपरिको सहर सिलगढीमा सारियो।\", \"दशैँमा विशेष पूजा हुन्छ र वार्षिक शैलेश्वरी मेला लाग्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Special pujas are offered to the goddess during Dashain.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दशैँमा देवीलाई विशेष पूजा चढाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Saileshwori_Doti1.jpg/1280px-Saileshwori_Doti1.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sanjib Chaudhary\", \"caption\": \"Painted gateway with lions and a giant trident before the shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saileshwori_Doti1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e5/Shaileshwori_Temple.JPG\", \"author\": \"Subbik\", \"caption\": \"The temple\'s gabled shrine and small tiered tower in 2010\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shaileshwori_Temple.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Shree_Shaileshwori_Temple_1.jpg/1280px-Shree_Shaileshwori_Temple_1.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gaurav Dhwaj Khadka\", \"caption\": \"Shaileshwori Temple in Silgadhi\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shree_Shaileshwori_Temple_1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Saileshwori_Doti2.jpg/1280px-Saileshwori_Doti2.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sanjib Chaudhary\", \"caption\": \"The temple compound under old trees\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saileshwori_Doti2.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/02/Saileswori_Temple..jpg\", \"author\": \"Bsnt Balayar\", \"caption\": \"Stone-paved courtyard of the temple after rain\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saileswori_Temple..jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Pink and red painted shrine hall with a triangular gable and small tiered tower, behind a painted gate with two lions and a giant trident, under big trees.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#e9b8c0\", \"#c0392b\", \"#3a8fc2\"], \"features\": [\"lion-statues\", \"trident\", \"bell\", \"toran\", \"flags-red\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"sacred-grove\", \"market-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(39,'ghodaghodi-temple','Ghodaghodi Temple and Lake','घोडाघोडी मन्दिर र ताल','Sukhad (Ghodaghodi Municipality)','Sudurpashchim','Kailali',NULL,28.684167,80.945278,'lake-shrine','Hindu','Ghodaghodi deity (linked in legend to Shiva and Parvati in the form of horses)',NULL,'Date of the shrine unknown; the present building is modern. The surrounding lake complex was designated a Ramsar wetland on 13 August 2003.','unknown','A small yellow-painted, flat-roofed shrine raised on a broad flight of steps on the lake shore, its fences hung thick with red and white cloth offerings. Inside, a tiled altar holds clay figures of horses and elephants beside an image of the goddess.',0,'A lakeside shrine in Kailali where devotees leave clay horses and elephants, beside a Ramsar-listed lake of lotus and birds.','Climb the broad steps and pause at the top: the fences around you are tied with hundreds of strips of red and white cloth, each one a prayer. This is the Ghodaghodi temple, on the shore of a lake in the forests of Kailali. The name comes from ghoda, horse. Legend says Shiva and Parvati once took the form of horses and roamed around this lake. Now look at the altar inside. Among the bells and lamps stand little clay horses and elephants, sometimes tigers too, brought by devotees in return for wishes granted. Local Tharu people gather here for the Agan Panchami festival and bathe in the lake. Walk down to the water afterwards. Ghodaghodi is part of a network of about thirteen lakes and ponds, a Ramsar wetland since 2003, where lotus leaves cover the surface and mugger crocodiles, otters and many birds live in the shade of the forest.','Shiva and Parvati are said to have turned into horses and roamed the area around the lake, giving Ghodaghodi (from ghoda, horse) its name.','[\"Ghodaghodi Lake Area was designated a Ramsar wetland of international importance on 13 August 2003; it covers 2,563 hectares.\", \"The site includes about 13 lakes and ponds; it lies at about 205 m in the Siwalik foothills.\", \"Devotees offer clay figures of horses, elephants and tigers at the shrine.\", \"Tharu people hold the Agan Panchami festival here and bathe in the lake.\", \"A February 2021 survey recorded 26 mugger crocodiles across 18 lakes in the area.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(2).jpg','Rajesh Dhungana · CC BY-SA 4.0','lake-shrine,hindu,sukhad (ghodaghodi municipality),legend,festival,sudurpashchim','[\"https://rsis.ramsar.org/ris/1314\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghodaghodi_Tal\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/travel/cities/ghodaghodi-playground-of-the-gods\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5556813\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Ghodaghodi_Temple\"]','कैलालीको तालकिनारको मन्दिर, जहाँ भक्तजनले माटाका घोडा र हात्ती चढाउँछन्। यो कमल र चराले भरिएको रामसार सूचीको तालको छेउमा छ।','फराकिलो भर्‍याङ चढेर माथि पुगी रोकिनुहोस्। तपाईंको वरिपरिका बारमा सयौँ रातो र सेतो कपडाका पट्टी बाँधिएका छन्, हरेक पट्टी एउटा प्रार्थना। यो कैलालीको जङ्गलमा रहेको तालको किनारको घोडाघोडी मन्दिर हो। नाम घोडा शब्दबाट आएको हो। कथाअनुसार शिव र पार्वतीले एक समय घोडाको रूप लिएर यो तालको वरिपरि घुमेका थिए। अब भित्रको वेदी हेर्नुहोस्। घण्टी र दियोका बीचमा साना माटाका घोडा र हात्ती, कहिलेकाहीँ बाघ पनि, राखिएका छन्। इच्छा पूरा भएपछि भक्तजनले ती ल्याएका हुन्। स्थानीय थारू समुदाय अगन पञ्चमीको चाडमा यहाँ भेला हुन्छन् र तालमा नुहाउँछन्। त्यसपछि पानीसम्म हिँडेर जानुहोस्। घोडाघोडी करिब तेह्रवटा ताल र पोखरीको जालोको भाग हो। सन् २००३ देखि यो रामसार सिमसार हो। यहाँ कमलका पातले पानीको सतह ढाकेको हुन्छ, र जङ्गलको छायामा मगर गोही, ऊदबिरालो र थुप्रै चरा बस्छन्।','शिव र पार्वती घोडा बनेर तालको वरिपरि घुमेको भनिन्छ। त्यसैले यो ठाउँको नाम घोडाघोडी (घोडा शब्दबाट) रह्यो।','[\"घोडाघोडी ताल क्षेत्रलाई सन् २००३ अगस्ट १३ मा अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय महत्त्वको रामसार सिमसार घोषित गरिएको थियो। यो २,५६३ हेक्टरमा फैलिएको छ।\", \"यो क्षेत्रमा करिब १३ ताल र पोखरी छन्। यो सिवालिक फेदमा करिब २०५ मिटरको उचाइमा छ।\", \"भक्तजनले मन्दिरमा घोडा, हात्ती र बाघका माटाका मूर्ति चढाउँछन्।\", \"थारूले यहाँ अगन पञ्चमीको चाड मनाउँछन् र तालमा नुहाउँछन्।\", \"सन् २०२१ फेब्रुअरीको सर्वेक्षणले यस क्षेत्रका १८ तालमा २६ वटा मगर गोही फेला पारेको थियो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Agan Panchami\", \"note\": \"Tharu festival in December; devotees bathe in the lake and worship at the shrine.\", \"month\": \"Mangsir\", \"name_np\": \"अगन पञ्चमी\", \"note_np\": \"डिसेम्बरमा मनाइने थारू चाड। भक्तजनले तालमा नुहाउँछन् र मन्दिरमा पूजा गर्छन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Maghi\", \"note\": \"A special fair is held at the temple.\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"माघी\", \"note_np\": \"मन्दिरमा विशेष मेला लाग्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Shrine interior hung with red and white cloth offerings\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%286%29.jpg/1280px-Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%286%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Clay horses and elephants offered to the deity\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghodaghodi_Temple_Sikhada_Ghodaghodi_Ghodaghodi_Lake_Kailali_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(6).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Ghodaghodi_Lake.JPG/1280px-Ghodaghodi_Lake.JPG\", \"author\": \"Ganesh Paudel\", \"caption\": \"Ghodaghodi Lake, the Ramsar wetland beside the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghodaghodi_Lake.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Ghoda_Ghodi_Lake_surrounded_by_mist.jpg/1280px-Ghoda_Ghodi_Lake_surrounded_by_mist.jpg\", \"author\": \"सुयाेग सत्याल\", \"caption\": \"The lake surrounded by morning mist\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghoda_Ghodi_Lake_surrounded_by_mist.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Ghodaghodi_Taal.jpg/1280px-Ghodaghodi_Taal.jpg\", \"author\": \"MITESHSTHA\", \"caption\": \"Lotus-covered waters of Ghodaghodi Tal\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghodaghodi_Taal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"flat\", \"notes\": \"Small yellow flat-roofed shrine on top of a wide flight of steps, fences hung with red and white cloth strips, beside a lotus-covered lake in forest.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"ochre-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#e6c95a\", \"#c0392b\", \"#f2f2f2\"], \"features\": [\"flags-red\", \"bell\", \"idol-visible\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 4, \"footprint_m\": [10, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 8, \"surroundings\": [\"lake\", \"forest\", \"sacred-grove\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(40,'khaptad-baba-ashram','Khaptad Baba Ashram','खप्तड बाबा आश्रम','Khaptad National Park (nearest towns Silgadhi and Mangalsen)','Sudurpashchim','Doti',NULL,29.386189,81.137163,'monastery','Hindu',NULL,NULL,'Hermitage of Khaptad Baba (Swami Sachchidananda), who settled in the Khaptad valley in the 1940s and lived there for about fifty years; Khaptad National Park was established on his advice in 1984.','unknown','A simple single-storey hermitage on an open grassy plateau ringed by fir forest: whitewashed stone walls, a long red-painted timber veranda, and a low pitched roof of stone slates, with a small outbuilding and a stone-ringed clearing in front.',0,'The forest hermitage where the sage Khaptad Baba lived for some fifty years, inside the national park founded on his advice.','You have walked up through rhododendron and fir to the high meadows of Khaptad, and in front of you is a modest whitewashed house with a red wooden veranda. This was the home of Khaptad Baba, also called Swami Sachchidananda. Born Shivanath Dogra in Kashmir, he trained as a doctor in Calcutta and studied surgery in Britain before giving it all up to become a renunciate. He wandered the mountains of Nepal and, in the 1940s, settled on this plateau to meditate, staying for about fifty years. Inside, people still keep the things he used: a sitar, his simple bed, and statues of the Baba himself. It was on his advice that the government created Khaptad National Park in 1984, protecting these meadows for leopards, bears and pheasants. A short walk away is Triveni, a sacred confluence, and every year around Jestha pilgrims climb up for the Ganga Dashahara fair.',NULL,'[\"Khaptad Baba was born Shivanath Dogra in Kashmir in 1880 and trained as a doctor before taking sannyas.\", \"He settled in the Khaptad valley in the 1940s and lived there for more than fifty years.\", \"Khaptad National Park was established in 1984 on his advice; it covers 225 square kilometers across Bajhang, Bajura, Achham and Doti.\", \"The ashram keeps two statues of the Baba, one wooden and one bronze, and objects he used, including a sitar and his bed.\", \"The Ganga Dashahara fair draws pilgrims to Khaptad once a year in the Jestha-Ashadh season.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Baba_hermitage_-_Khaptad_National_Park.jpg/1280px-Baba_hermitage_-_Khaptad_National_Park.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baba_hermitage_-_Khaptad_National_Park.jpg','Plamichhane · CC BY-SA 4.0','monastery,hindu,khaptad national park (nearest towns silgadhi and mangalsen),art,sudurpashchim','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khaptad_Baba\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khaptad_National_Park\", \"https://www.buddhaair.com/blog/Spiritual-Khaptad\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/480999246\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khaptad_Baba_Ashram.jpg\"]','ऋषि खप्तड बाबाले करिब पचास वर्ष बिताएको जङ्गलको आश्रम, उनकै सल्लाहमा स्थापित राष्ट्रिय निकुञ्जभित्र।','तपाईं गुराँस र सल्लाको जङ्गल हुँदै खप्तडको अग्ला चौरमा आइपुग्नुभएको छ। तपाईंको अगाडि रातो काठको बरन्डा भएको सादा सेतो घर छ। यो खप्तड बाबाको घर थियो। उनलाई स्वामी सच्चिदानन्द पनि भनिन्छ। कश्मीरमा शिवनाथ डोगराका रूपमा जन्मेका उनले कलकत्तामा डाक्टरी पढे र बेलायतमा शल्यचिकित्सा पढे। त्यसपछि सबै छोडेर सन्न्यासी भए। उनी नेपालका पहाडमा घुमे। सन् १९४० को दशकमा ध्यान गर्न यही पठारमा बसोबास गरे र करिब पचास वर्ष बसे। भित्र मानिसहरूले अहिले पनि उनले चलाएका सामान राखेका छन्: एउटा सितार, उनको सादा ओछ्यान र बाबाकै मूर्ति। उनकै सल्लाहमा सरकारले सन् १९८४ मा खप्तड राष्ट्रिय निकुञ्ज बनायो। यसले यी चौरलाई चितुवा, भालु र डाँफेका लागि जोगाएको छ। केही पर हिँड्दा त्रिवेणी भन्ने पवित्र सङ्गम छ। हरेक वर्ष जेठतिर तीर्थयात्री गङ्गा दशहराको मेलाका लागि माथि उक्लन्छन्।',NULL,'[\"खप्तड बाबा सन् १८८० मा कश्मीरमा शिवनाथ डोगराका रूपमा जन्मे र सन्न्यास लिनुअघि डाक्टरी तालिम लिए।\", \"उनी सन् १९४० को दशकमा खप्तड उपत्यकामा बसे र त्यहाँ पचास वर्षभन्दा बढी बसे।\", \"खप्तड राष्ट्रिय निकुञ्ज सन् १९८४ मा उनकै सल्लाहमा स्थापना भयो। यो बझाङ, बाजुरा, अछाम र डोटीमा फैलिएको छ र क्षेत्रफल २२५ वर्ग किलोमिटर छ।\", \"आश्रममा बाबाका दुईवटा मूर्ति छन्, एउटा काठको र एउटा काँसाको। उनले चलाएका सामान पनि छन्, जस्तै सितार र उनको ओछ्यान।\", \"गङ्गा दशहराको मेलाले जेठ-असारको मौसममा वर्षको एकपटक खप्तडमा तीर्थयात्री तान्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Ganga Dashahara Mela\", \"note\": \"Annual pilgrim fair at Khaptad in the Jestha-Ashadh season.\", \"month\": \"Jestha\", \"name_np\": \"गङ्गा दशहरा मेला\", \"note_np\": \"खप्तडमा जेठ-असारको मौसममा लाग्ने वार्षिक तीर्थयात्री मेला।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Khaptad_Baba_Ashram.jpg/1280px-Khaptad_Baba_Ashram.jpg\", \"author\": \"Dipalmalla\", \"caption\": \"The ashram among fir trees on the Khaptad plateau\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khaptad_Baba_Ashram.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Khaptad_Baba_Ashram_2.jpg/1280px-Khaptad_Baba_Ashram_2.jpg\", \"author\": \"Redpandamoon\", \"caption\": \"Wooden veranda of the ashram where the hermit lived\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khaptad_Baba_Ashram_2.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/%E0%A4%B8%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0.jpg/1280px-%E0%A4%B8%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0.jpg\", \"author\": \"जनक राज भट्ट\", \"caption\": \"Khaptad Baba\'s sitar, kept in the ashram\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%B8%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%A1%28%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BE%29.jpg/1280px-%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%A1%28%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BE%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"जनक राज भट्ट\", \"caption\": \"Khaptad Baba\'s bed, preserved in the ashram\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%A1(%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BE).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Khaptad_National_Park12.jpg/1280px-Khaptad_National_Park12.jpg\", \"author\": \"Utsab Raj Giri\", \"caption\": \"Frost on the meadows of Khaptad National Park\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khaptad_National_Park12.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"slate\", \"notes\": \"Long low white stone house with a red timber veranda and slate roof, alone on a grassy meadow edged by dark fir trees; white stones mark a circle in front.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"whitewashed-stone\", \"colors\": [\"#efeee9\", \"#8e3b2e\", \"#4a5a3a\"], \"features\": [\"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 5, \"footprint_m\": [14, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"forest\", \"hilltop\", \"garden-lawn\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(41,'baidyanath-dham-achham','Baidyanath Dham, Achham','बैद्यनाथ धाम, अछाम','Sanfebagar','Sudurpashchim','Achham',NULL,29.234449,81.216046,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva (as Baidyanath, lord of physicians)',NULL,'Ancient pilgrimage site said to be named in the Skanda Purana (Manas Khanda); mentioned by Abhaya Malla, king of Achham, in 1440 BS (c. 1383 CE). Seventeenth-century inscriptions mention the Shah kings.','Achham Malla (earliest record)','A compact two-roofed pagoda-style shrine with a whitewashed stone ground storey, two dark metal-sheet roofs and a gilded finial, standing in a paved and lawned compound with a white Nandi bull, small shrines and pavilions, beside a Vedic school.',0,'A Shiva shrine at a river confluence near Sanfebagar, Achham, where Shiva is worshipped as the divine healer and Vedic students study.','You are near Sanfebagar in Achham, where the Budhi Ganga meets the Saraswati, and in front of you is the compact two-roofed shrine of Baidyanath Dham. Notice the white Nandi bull facing the door, always watching his lord Shiva. The name means lord of physicians, and the story behind it is told in the Skanda Purana. Ravana, unable to see Shiva after meditating at Mount Kailash, came here to meditate instead. Shiva appeared and granted his wish, attaching his nine heads at this place, acting as a healer, a baidya. Long afterwards, around 1383, King Abhaya Malla of Achham wrote that this place could cure all diseases. Look for students in red and saffron: the shrine runs a Vedic school, the Ved Vidyashram. Come at Shivaratri and you will find pilgrims from Nepal and from India. Local legend even says Gorkhali soldiers who came here during unification were blinded and had to retreat, leaving their weapons behind.','Ravana, failing to see Shiva at Kailash, meditated here; Shiva appeared as a healer and restored his nine heads, giving the place its name Baidyanath. A later legend says invading Gorkhali soldiers were struck blind here and retreated, leaving their weapons.','[\"Baidyanath Dham stands at the confluence of the Budhi Ganga and Saraswati rivers in Achham district.\", \"The place is said to be mentioned in the Manas Khanda of the Skanda Purana.\", \"King Abhaya Malla of Achham mentioned it in 1440 BS, saying it could cure all diseases.\", \"The shrine runs a Vedic school, the Ved Vidyashram, which received NPR 2 million from the government in 2020.\", \"Pilgrims from Nepal and India visit during Maha Shivaratri.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/BaidyanathDham_Achham1.jpg/1280px-BaidyanathDham_Achham1.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BaidyanathDham_Achham1.jpg','Sanjib Chaudhary · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,achham malla (earliest record),sanfebagar,legend,art,festival,sudurpashchim','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baidyanath_Dham_(Nepal)\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BaidyanathDham_Achham1.jpg\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baidhyanath_Dham.jpg\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/6985223989\"]','अछामको साँफेबगर नजिक दुई नदीको सङ्गममा रहेको शिव मन्दिर, जहाँ शिवलाई दिव्य वैद्यका रूपमा पूजा गरिन्छ र वैदिक विद्यार्थी पढ्छन्।','तपाईं अछामको साँफेबगरनजिक हुनुहुन्छ। यहाँ बुढी गङ्गा र सरस्वती भेट्छन्। तपाईंको अगाडि बैद्यनाथ धामको सानो दुई तहको मन्दिर छ। ढोकातिर फर्केर बसेको सेतो नन्दी साँढे हेर्नुहोस्। ऊ सधैँ आफ्ना स्वामी शिवलाई हेरिरहन्छ। नामको अर्थ वैद्यहरूका स्वामी हो। यसको कथा स्कन्द पुराणमा भनिएको छ। कैलास पर्वतमा ध्यान गर्दा पनि शिवलाई देख्न नसकेका रावण यहाँ ध्यान गर्न आए। शिव प्रकट भए र उनको इच्छा पूरा गरिदिए। वैद्य बनेर उनले यही ठाउँमा रावणका नौ टाउको जोडिदिए। धेरै पछि, करिब १३८३ मा, अछामका राजा अभय मल्लले यो ठाउँले सबै रोग निको पार्न सक्छ भनेर लेखे। रातो र भगवा लुगा लगाएका विद्यार्थी खोज्नुहोस्। मन्दिरले वेद विद्याश्रम नामको वैदिक विद्यालय चलाउँछ। शिवरात्रिमा आउनुभयो भने नेपाल र भारतबाट आएका तीर्थयात्री भेट्नुहुन्छ। स्थानीय कथाअनुसार एकीकरणका बेला यहाँ आएका गोरखाली सिपाही अन्धा भए र हतियार छाडेर फर्कनुपर्‍यो।','कैलासमा शिवलाई देख्न नसकेका रावणले यहाँ ध्यान गरे। शिव वैद्यका रूपमा प्रकट भएर उनका नौ टाउको फर्काइदिए, र यो ठाउँ बैद्यनाथ कहलियो। पछिको एउटा कथाअनुसार आक्रमण गर्न आएका गोरखाली सिपाही यहाँ अन्धा भए र हतियार छाडेर फर्किए।','[\"बैद्यनाथ धाम अछाम जिल्लामा बुढी गङ्गा र सरस्वती नदीको सङ्गममा छ।\", \"यो ठाउँको नाम स्कन्द पुराणको मानस खण्डमा आएको भनिन्छ।\", \"अछामका राजा अभय मल्लले वि.सं. १४४० मा यसको उल्लेख गर्दै यसले सबै रोग निको पार्न सक्छ भनेका थिए।\", \"मन्दिरले वेद विद्याश्रम नामको वैदिक विद्यालय चलाउँछ। सन् २०२० मा सरकारले यसलाई २० लाख रुपैयाँ दियो।\", \"महाशिवरात्रिमा नेपाल र भारतका तीर्थयात्री दर्शन गर्न आउँछन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Pilgrims from Nepal and India visit the shrine.\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"नेपाल र भारतका तीर्थयात्री मन्दिर दर्शन गर्न आउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/BaidyanathDham_Achham2.jpg/1280px-BaidyanathDham_Achham2.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sanjib Chaudhary\", \"caption\": \"Vedic school students in red gathered before the shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BaidyanathDham_Achham2.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/Baidhyanath_Dham.jpg\", \"author\": \"Manoj Nath Yogi\", \"caption\": \"The two-roofed stone shrine with its white Nandi bull\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baidhyanath_Dham.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Small square stone shrine painted white with two dark metal pagoda roofs and a gold finial; a white Nandi bull on a plinth faces the door across a lawn.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"whitewashed-stone\", \"colors\": [\"#e8e6e0\", \"#3d3b38\", \"#d4a640\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"nandi-bull\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [5, 5], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"garden-lawn\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(42,'parshuram-dham-dadeldhura','Parshuram Dham','परशुराम धाम','Jogbudha (Parshuram Municipality)','Sudurpashchim','Dadeldhura',NULL,29.150385,80.270578,'ghat','Hindu','Parshuram (sixth incarnation of Vishnu)',NULL,'Ancient pilgrimage site said to be named in the Manas Khanda of the Skanda Purana; dates of the present shrines and the large Parshuram statue are not published.','unknown','A riverside pilgrimage ground on the rocky banks of the Mahakali: small painted shrines (Ganesh, Hanuman, Shiva) among trees along paved paths, an arched gateway, a small white shrine above the bathing place, and a towering painted statue of Parshuram holding an axe and bow on a stepped plinth.',0,'A sacred bathing place on the Mahakali in Dadeldhura, linked to Parshuram\'s penance and famous for its Maghe Sankranti fair.','You have come down to the wide, stony banks of the Mahakali River, the western border of Nepal, to Parshuram Dham. Look up first at the giant painted statue: a bearded sage with an axe in one hand and a bow beside him. This is Parshuram, the sixth incarnation of Vishnu. Legend says that after slaying the warriors of the Haihaya clan he came here to perform a great sacrifice as penance, and that later Yudhishthira of the Mahabharata also held a ceremony here and built a Dharma Dwar, a gate of right conduct. The site is said to be named in the Skanda Purana. Walk along the paths past small shrines of Ganesh, Hanuman and Shiva, then down to the water. Every year on Maghe Sankranti, the first of Magh, a great fair fills these banks, and by tradition twenty-two deities from Dadeldhura and Doti are carried here for a holy dip in the river.','After killing the Haihaya Kshatriyas, Parshuram is said to have performed a yagya here in penance; Yudhishthira later held a similar ceremony and built a Dharma Dwar (gate of right conduct).','[\"Parshuram Dham lies on the banks of the Mahakali River in Parshuram Municipality-5, Dadeldhura.\", \"The site is said to be mentioned in the Manas Khanda of the Skanda Purana.\", \"On Maghe Sankranti, 22 deities from Dadeldhura and Doti are traditionally brought here for a holy dip.\", \"It is about 30 km, roughly a two-hour ride, from Daiji on the East-West Highway.\", \"Devotees also bathe here on full-moon, new-moon and eclipse days.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Farshanam.png/1280px-Farshanam.png','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Farshanam.png','Mukesh061 · CC BY 4.0','ghat,hindu,jogbudha (parshuram municipality),legend,sudurpashchim','[\"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/parashuram-dham.html\", \"https://ekantipur.com/sudurpaschim-pradesh/2026/01/14/en/preparations-for-the-parshuram-mela-are-complete-03-47.html\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parshuram,_Dadeldhura\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/7874069330\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Farshanam.png\"]','डडेलधुरामा महाकालीको किनारको पवित्र स्नान स्थल, परशुरामको तपस्यासँग जोडिएको र माघे सङ्क्रान्ति मेलाका लागि प्रसिद्ध।','तपाईं नेपालको पश्चिमी सीमा महाकाली नदीको फराकिलो, ढुङ्गैढुङ्गा भएको किनारमा परशुराम धाम आइपुग्नुभएको छ। पहिला माथि रङ्गीन विशाल मूर्तिलाई हेर्नुहोस्। दाह्री भएका एक ऋषिको एक हातमा बन्चरो छ र छेउमा धनु छ। यी विष्णुका छैटौँ अवतार परशुराम हुन्। कथाअनुसार हैहय वंशका योद्धा मारेपछि प्रायश्चित्तका रूपमा उनी यहाँ ठूलो यज्ञ गर्न आए। पछि महाभारतका युधिष्ठिरले पनि यहाँ अनुष्ठान गरे र धर्मद्वार, अर्थात् सही आचरणको ढोका, बनाए। यो ठाउँको नाम स्कन्द पुराणमा आएको भनिन्छ। गणेश, हनुमान र शिवका साना मन्दिर भएर जाने बाटो हुँदै पानीसम्म ओर्लनुहोस्। हरेक वर्ष माघ १ गते, माघे सङ्क्रान्तिमा, यी किनारमा ठूलो मेला लाग्छ। परम्पराअनुसार डडेलधुरा र डोटीका बाइस देवतालाई नदीमा पवित्र स्नान गराउन यहाँ ल्याइन्छ।','हैहय क्षत्रिय मारेपछि परशुरामले प्रायश्चित्तका रूपमा यहाँ यज्ञ गरेको भनिन्छ। पछि युधिष्ठिरले पनि यस्तै अनुष्ठान गरे र धर्मद्वार (सही आचरणको ढोका) बनाए।','[\"परशुराम धाम डडेलधुराको परशुराम नगरपालिका-५ मा महाकाली नदीको किनारमा छ।\", \"यो ठाउँको नाम स्कन्द पुराणको मानस खण्डमा आएको भनिन्छ।\", \"माघे सङ्क्रान्तिमा डडेलधुरा र डोटीका २२ देवतालाई परम्परागत रूपमा पवित्र स्नानका लागि यहाँ ल्याइन्छ।\", \"पूर्व-पश्चिम राजमार्गको दैजीबाट यो करिब ३० किमी टाढा छ, गाडीमा लगभग दुई घण्टाको बाटो।\", \"भक्तजनले पूर्णिमा, औँसी र ग्रहणका दिनमा पनि यहाँ स्नान गर्छन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Maghe Sankranti fair\", \"note\": \"Big annual fair on Magh 1; 22 deities from Dadeldhura and Doti are brought for a holy dip.\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"माघे सङ्क्रान्ति मेला\", \"note_np\": \"माघ १ गते लाग्ने ठूलो वार्षिक मेला। डडेलधुरा र डोटीका २२ देवतालाई पवित्र स्नानका लागि ल्याइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Dhamparashuram.png/1280px-Dhamparashuram.png\", \"author\": \"Mukesh061\", \"caption\": \"Shrines and paths among the trees of Parshuram Dham\", \"license\": \"CC BY 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhamparashuram.png\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/Parshuram_Dham_Dadeldhura-1.jpg\", \"author\": \"कत्यूरी राजाका वंशज\", \"caption\": \"Bathing place on the rocky bank of the Mahakali River\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parshuram_Dham_Dadeldhura-1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Hanumantemple.jpg/1280px-Hanumantemple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Mukesh061\", \"caption\": \"Gateway flanked by small Hanuman and Shiva shrines\", \"license\": \"CC BY 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hanumantemple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/14/Ganeshmandir.jpg\", \"author\": \"Mukesh061\", \"caption\": \"Ganesh temple at Parshuram Dham\", \"license\": \"CC BY 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ganeshmandir.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"statue\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Towering painted statue of a bearded sage with an axe and tall bow on a stepped plinth, near small pink and orange shrines under trees by a stony river bank.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#e88f6a\", \"#2e8b57\", \"#c8a46a\"], \"features\": [\"idol-visible\", \"ghat-steps\", \"flags-red\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [8, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 5, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"riverbank-ghats\", \"forest\", \"garden-lawn\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(43,'kathmandu-durbar-square','Kathmandu Durbar Square','काठमाडौं दरबार क्षेत्र','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.704075,85.307083,'square','Both',NULL,NULL,'Malla-era core, mostly 16th–18th century CE; later Shah and Rana additions','Malla','Royal palace square of Newar pagoda temples, palace courtyards and Rana-era neoclassical wings',1,'The old royal heart of Kathmandu, where Malla and Shah kings were crowned among pagoda temples.','You are standing in the old royal heart of Kathmandu. For centuries, the kings of this city ruled from the palace in front of you, and the temples around you were their gifts to the gods. Look at the carved wooden windows and roof struts: this is Newar craftsmanship, mostly from the Malla kings of the 16th to 18th centuries. Later, the Shah kings who unified Nepal kept this palace as their seat and added the tall nine-storey Basantapur tower to the south. In 1979, this square became one of the seven monument zones of the Kathmandu Valley World Heritage Site. Then, on 25 April 2015, a powerful earthquake brought down several of its temples, including the ancient Kasthamandap. Much of what you see today has been carefully rebuilt using traditional brick, timber and techniques. As you walk, notice how daily life carries on: pigeons, vendors, worshippers ringing bells, and children playing on temple steps. Take your time, and let the square tell you its story one shrine at a time.',NULL,'[\"It is one of three royal Durbar Squares in the Kathmandu Valley, all part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site inscribed in 1979.\", \"The square takes its Nepali name, Hanuman Dhoka, from a stone statue of Hanuman at the palace gate.\", \"The 25 April 2015 earthquake reduced several buildings here to rubble, including Kasthamandap.\", \"Prithvi Narayan Shah added four lookout towers to the palace in 1768, including the nine-storey Basantapur tower.\"]','09:00','19:00',1000,500,0,120,'The April 2015 earthquake severely damaged the square, toppling Kasthamandap, Maju Dega and other temples; most have since been rebuilt.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-12-Mini-Vishnu-Pratapamalla-Jagannath-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-12-Mini-Vishnu-Pratapamalla-Jagannath-2013-gje.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-12-Mini-Vishnu-Pratapamalla-Jagannath-2013-gje.jpg','Gerd Eichmann · CC BY-SA 4.0','square,both,malla,kathmandu,hindu,buddhist,unesco,palace,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu_Durbar_Square\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanuman_Dhoka\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6122177\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/entry-fees-of-the-heritage-sites-in-nepal/\", \"https://ghalegroup.com/nepal-attractions-fees-timings/\"]','काठमाडौंको पुरानो शाही केन्द्र, जहाँ पगोडा शैलीका मन्दिरहरूका बीचमा मल्ल र शाह राजाहरूको राज्याभिषेक हुन्थ्यो।','तपाईं काठमाडौंको पुरानो शाही केन्द्रमा उभिनुभएको छ। शताब्दीयौंसम्म यो सहरका राजाहरूले तपाईंको अगाडिको दरबारबाट राज चलाए, र वरिपरिका मन्दिरहरू उनीहरूले देवताहरूलाई चढाएका उपहार थिए। कुँदिएका काठका झ्याल र छानाका टेकोहरू हेर्नुहोस्। यो नेवार शिल्पकला हो, धेरैजसो १६ औं देखि १८ औं शताब्दीका मल्ल राजाहरूको पालाको। पछि नेपाल एकीकरण गर्ने शाह राजाहरूले पनि यही दरबार आफ्नो गद्दी बनाइराखे र दक्षिणतिर अग्लो नौ तले बसन्तपुर बुर्ज थपे। सन् १९७९ मा यो चोक काठमाडौं उपत्यका विश्व सम्पदा स्थलका सात स्मारक क्षेत्रमध्ये एक बन्यो। त्यसपछि २५ अप्रिल २०१५ मा आएको शक्तिशाली भूकम्पले पुरानो काष्ठमण्डप लगायत यहाँका धेरै मन्दिर ढाल्यो। आज तपाईंले देख्ने धेरैजसो भाग परम्परागत इँटा, काठ र शिल्प प्रयोग गरेर होसियारीसाथ फेरि बनाइएको हो। हिँड्दै गर्दा हेर्नुहोस्, यहाँको दैनिक जीवन कसरी चलिरहेको छ: परेवा, व्यापारी, घण्टी बजाएर पूजा गर्ने मानिस र मन्दिरका भर्‍याङमा खेल्ने केटाकेटी। फुर्सदले हिँड्नुहोस् र एक-एक मन्दिर गर्दै चोकको कथा सुन्नुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"यो काठमाडौं उपत्यकाका तीनवटा शाही दरबार क्षेत्रमध्ये एक हो। तीनवटै सन् १९७९ मा युनेस्को विश्व सम्पदा सूचीमा परेका हुन्।\", \"यो चोकको नेपाली नाम हनुमानढोका दरबारको ढोकामा रहेको हनुमानको ढुङ्गाको मूर्तिबाट आएको हो।\", \"२५ अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पले यहाँका काष्ठमण्डप लगायत धेरै भवन भत्काएर थुप्रो बनायो।\", \"सन् १७६८ मा पृथ्वीनारायण शाहले दरबारमा चारवटा अवलोकन बुर्ज थपे, जसमध्ये एउटा नौ तले बसन्तपुर बुर्ज हो।\"]','सन् २०१५ को अप्रिलको भूकम्पले यो चोकमा ठूलो क्षति पुर्‍यायो। काष्ठमण्डप, माजुदेगः र अरू मन्दिर ढले। धेरैजसो पछि फेरि बनाइएका छन्।','[{\"name\": \"Indra Jatra\", \"note\": \"Masked dances, the Kumari chariot and the raised Indra pole fill the old royal square\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"इन्द्रजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"मुखुन्डो नाच, कुमारीको रथ र उठाइएको इन्द्रध्वजले पुरानो शाही चोक भरिन्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Main Durga festival; the Phulpati procession reaches Hanuman Dhoka on the seventh day\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दुर्गाको मुख्य चाड; सातौं दिन फूलपातीको जुलुस हनुमानढोका पुग्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Gai Jatra\", \"note\": \"Families who lost someone that year parade cows and costumed children through the square\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"गाईजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"त्यस वर्ष परिवारका कुनै सदस्यको मृत्यु भएका घरपरिवारले गाई र भेषधारी केटाकेटीसहित चोकमा जुलुस निकाल्छन्\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-06-Mahavishnu-Kuh-Vishnu-Pratapamalla-Jagannath-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-06-Mahavishnu-Kuh-Vishnu-Pratapamalla-Jagannath-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Temples and Pratap Malla\'s pillar in the square, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-06-Mahavishnu-Kuh-Vishnu-Pratapamalla-Jagannath-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-25-Kageshwor-Taleju-Indrapur-Kala_Bhairav-Jagannath-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-25-Kageshwor-Taleju-Indrapur-Kala_Bhairav-Jagannath-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Taleju\'s roofs above the Kageshwor and Indrapur temples, 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-25-Kageshwor-Taleju-Indrapur-Kala_Bhairav-Jagannath-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Kathmandu-Basantapur_Chowk-46-Basantapur_Durbar-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Basantapur_Chowk-46-Basantapur_Durbar-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Basantapur tower of the old royal palace, 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Basantapur_Chowk-46-Basantapur_Durbar-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-30-Maju_Dega-Narayana-Shiva_Parvati_Mandir-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-30-Maju_Dega-Narayana-Shiva_Parvati_Mandir-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Maju Dega, Narayan and Shiva-Parvati temples, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-30-Maju_Dega-Narayana-Shiva_Parvati_Mandir-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-02-abends-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-02-abends-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The square in the evening, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-02-abends-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-32-Maju_Dega-Shiva_Parvati-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-32-Maju_Dega-Shiva_Parvati-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Earthquake damage around Maju Dega, 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-32-Maju_Dega-Shiva_Parvati-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"square\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Brick palace with a white nine-storey Basantapur tower; tall Maju Dega on nine steps and gilded three-roofed Taleju\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"carved-struts\", \"carved-windows\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"garuda-pillar\", \"stone-pillar\", \"bell\", \"lion-statues\", \"watchtower\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [250, 150], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\", \"market-houses\", \"city-street\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(44,'kasthamandap','Kasthamandap','काष्ठमण्डप','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu','kathmandu-durbar-square',27.703957,85.305762,'pagoda','Hindu','Gorakhnath',NULL,'c. 7th century CE (radiocarbon/OSL dating after 2015)','Licchavi','Three-storey timber public shelter (mandapa) in Newar pagoda style; rebuilt 2018–2021',1,'The \'wooden shelter\' said to have given Kathmandu its name, rebuilt after the 2015 earthquake.','You are looking at Kasthamandap, whose name means \'wood-covered shelter\'. Many people believe the city of Kathmandu takes its name from this very building. For centuries it was a public rest house where travellers and traders gathered, and later a shrine to the yogi Gorakhnath was added inside. On 25 April 2015 the old three-storey timber hall collapsed completely. That tragedy led to a discovery: archaeologists from Nepal\'s Department of Archaeology, working with Durham and Stirling universities, dated soil from the foundations and found the building went back to the 7th century, the Licchavi era. They also recovered copper-plate inscriptions mentioning the 14th-century king Jayasthiti Malla. Local residents insisted on rebuilding it themselves, and work began in November 2018. Look closely at the fresh timber: it was raised by the community using traditional joinery, and the temple was formally inaugurated in April 2022.','A popular legend says Gorakhnath once came to watch the Machhindranath chariot festival in disguise. A tantric recognised him and would not let him go until he granted a boon. A great tree then sprang up on this spot, and the entire shelter was built from the wood of that single tree. Some tellings say the tree was the wish-granting Kalpavriksha itself.','[\"Its name means \'wood-covered shelter\' in Sanskrit.\", \"Post-2015 radiocarbon and OSL dating suggest it was built in the 7th century CE.\", \"Copper-plate inscriptions naming the 14th-century king Jayasthiti Malla were found in one of its pillars.\", \"Reconstruction began on 8 November 2018 and the rebuilt temple was inaugurated in April 2022.\"]','09:00','19:00',1000,500,0,20,'The building collapsed completely on 25 April 2015; it was rebuilt by the local community from 2018 and inaugurated in 2022.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Kasthamandap_Kathmandu_%282023%29.jpg/1280px-Kasthamandap_Kathmandu_%282023%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kasthamandap_Kathmandu_(2023).jpg','Chainwit. · CC BY 4.0','pagoda,hindu,licchavi,kathmandu,unesco,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kasthamandap\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6374805\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/183558418\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/nepal/president-bhandari-inaugurates-reconstructed-kashthamandap-temple\", \"https://www.sharesansar.com/newsdetail/rebuilding-of-kasthamandap-nears-final-phase-to-be-inaugurated-within-a-few-days-2021-11-23\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/kathmandu/kasthamandap.html\"]','\'काठको आश्रय\' भनिने यो भवनबाट काठमाडौंले नाम पाएको मानिन्छ। २०१५ को भूकम्पपछि यसलाई फेरि बनाइयो।','तपाईं काष्ठमण्डप हेर्दै हुनुहुन्छ, जसको अर्थ \'काठले बनेको आश्रय\' हो। धेरैले काठमाडौं सहरले नाम यही भवनबाट पाएको मान्छन्। शताब्दीयौंसम्म यो बटुवा र व्यापारीहरू जम्मा हुने सार्वजनिक सत्तल थियो, पछि भित्र योगी गोरखनाथको मन्दिर थपियो। २५ अप्रिल २०१५ मा तीन तले यो पुरानो काठको भवन पूरै ढल्यो। त्यही दुःखद घटनापछि एउटा खोज भयो। नेपालको पुरातत्त्व विभागले डरहम र स्टर्लिङ विश्वविद्यालयसँग मिलेर जगको माटो जाँच गर्दा भवन सातौं शताब्दीको, लिच्छविकालको रहेछ भन्ने पत्ता लाग्यो। चौधौं शताब्दीका राजा जयस्थिति मल्लको नाम उल्लेख भएका ताम्रपत्र पनि भेटिए। स्थानीय बासिन्दाले आफैं फेरि बनाउनुपर्छ भन्ने जिद्दी गरे, र सन् २०१८ को नोभेम्बरमा काम सुरु भयो। नयाँ काठलाई ध्यान दिएर हेर्नुहोस्: समुदायले परम्परागत जोड्ने शिल्प प्रयोग गरेर यसलाई उठाएको हो, र सन् २०२२ को अप्रिलमा मन्दिरको औपचारिक उद्घाटन भयो।','एउटा प्रचलित किंवदन्ती छ: गोरखनाथ भेष बदलेर मछिन्द्रनाथको रथयात्रा हेर्न आएका थिए। एक तान्त्रिकले उनलाई चिनेर वरदान नदिएसम्म जान दिएनन्। त्यसपछि यही ठाउँमा एउटा ठूलो रूख उम्रियो, र सबै सत्तल त्यही एउटै रूखको काठले बनाइयो। कतिपयले त्यो रूख इच्छा पूरा गर्ने कल्पवृक्ष नै थियो भन्छन्।','[\"संस्कृतमा यसको नामको अर्थ \'काठले बनेको आश्रय\' हो।\", \"सन् २०१५ पछिको रेडियोकार्बन र ओएसएल परीक्षणले यो सातौं शताब्दीमा बनेको हुन सक्ने देखाउँछ।\", \"यसको एउटा खम्बाभित्र चौधौं शताब्दीका राजा जयस्थिति मल्लको नाम भएका ताम्रपत्र भेटिएका थिए।\", \"पुनर्निर्माण सन् २०१८ नोभेम्बर ८ मा सुरु भयो र फेरि बनेको मन्दिर सन् २०२२ को अप्रिलमा उद्घाटन भयो।\"]','भवन सन् २०१५ अप्रिल २५ मा पूरै ढल्यो; स्थानीय समुदायले सन् २०१८ देखि फेरि बनायो र सन् २०२२ मा उद्घाटन भयो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Kasthamandap.jpg/1280px-Kasthamandap.jpg\", \"author\": \"Wonker\", \"caption\": \"The original timber pavilion at Maru Tole, before 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kasthamandap.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Kasthamandap_%28l%29_%26_Maju_Deval_%28r%29%2C_with_Swayambhunath_in_the_Distance_%285198441288%29.jpg/1280px-Kasthamandap_%28l%29_%26_Maju_Deval_%28r%29%2C_with_Swayambhunath_in_the_Distance_%285198441288%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa\", \"caption\": \"Kasthamandap and Maju Dega, with Swayambhu hill beyond\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kasthamandap_(l)_&_Maju_Deval_(r),_with_Swayambhunath_in_the_Distance_(5198441288).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Kasthamandap_2023.jpg/1280px-Kasthamandap_2023.jpg\", \"author\": \"MiraclePotato\", \"caption\": \"The rebuilt Kasthamandap in 2023\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kasthamandap_2023.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Kasthamandap%2C_Kathmandu-89.jpg/1280px-Kasthamandap%2C_Kathmandu-89.jpg\", \"author\": \"Immanuelle\", \"caption\": \"Kasthamandap at Maru Tole\", \"license\": \"CC BY 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kasthamandap,_Kathmandu-89.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Kasthamandap_%2851838%29.jpg/1280px-Kasthamandap_%2851838%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prakashphuyal30\", \"caption\": \"Wide view of Kasthamandap\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kasthamandap_(51838).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Broad, squat three-roof timber pavilion with an open pillared ground floor and a Gorakhnath shrine in the middle\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"timber\", \"colors\": [\"#4a3020\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [20, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"market-houses\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(45,'taleju-temple','Taleju Temple','तलेजु मन्दिर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu','kathmandu-durbar-square',27.704951,85.307922,'pagoda','Hindu','Taleju Bhawani',1564,'16th century CE (1564)','Malla','Multi-roofed Newar pagoda on a high stepped plinth with a golden torana',1,'Temple of the Malla kings\' royal goddess, opened to the public only once a year at Dashain.','Look up at the high gilded roofs in the north-east of the square. This is the Taleju Temple, built in 1564 by King Mahendra Malla for Taleju Bhawani, the royal patron goddess of the Malla dynasty. Taleju was the kings\' own protector, so her temple was raised high above the city on a stepped plinth, and its gilded roofs once announced royal power to everyone below. Unlike most temples here, its doors stay shut. The Taleju Temple opens to the public only once a year, during the great festival of Dashain. Inside are shrines to the goddess and to her human embodiment, the Kumari, the living goddess who lives just across the square. In 2015, when nearby temples collapsed, Taleju survived the earthquake. As you stand here, imagine the Malla kings climbing these steps in private worship, believing that the goddess on this platform kept their kingdom safe.','Legend says Taleju used to visit King Jaya Prakash Malla each night to play a dice game, on condition that he told no one. When the king\'s daughter secretly followed him, the angry goddess vanished. She later appeared in a dream, telling the king she would return in a young Shakya girl. This, tradition says, is how the custom of the royal Kumari began in Kathmandu.','[\"It was built in 1564 by King Mahendra Malla.\", \"Taleju Bhawani was the royal patron goddess of the Malla dynasty.\", \"The temple is opened to the public only once a year, during Dashain.\", \"A 17th-century necklace once kept here is now in the Art Institute of Chicago, and campaigners in Nepal seek its return.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,500,0,10,'The temple survived the 2015 earthquake while nearby structures collapsed.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Kathmandu-Taleju-12-Palast-2014-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Taleju-12-Palast-2014-gje.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Taleju-12-Palast-2014-gje.jpg','Gerd Eichmann · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,kathmandu,unesco,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taleju_Temple,_Kathmandu\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanuman_Dhoka\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kumari_(goddess)\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q83776242\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1414600808\", \"https://thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/temples-buildings-destroyed-nepal-earthquake-2015.html\"]','मल्ल राजाहरूकी कुलदेवीको मन्दिर, जुन वर्षमा एक पटक मात्र दशैँमा सर्वसाधारणका लागि खुल्छ।','चोकको उत्तर-पूर्वतिर उभिएका सुनौला अग्ला छाना हेर्नुहोस्। यो तलेजु मन्दिर हो, जसलाई सन् १५६४ मा राजा महेन्द्र मल्लले मल्ल वंशकी कुलदेवी तलेजु भवानीका लागि बनाएका थिए। तलेजु राजाहरूकी आफ्नै रक्षक देवी थिइन्, त्यसैले उनको मन्दिर भर्‍याङसहितको अग्लो आधारमा सहरभन्दा माथि बनाइयो। यसका सुनौला छानाले तल बस्ने सबैलाई राजाको शक्ति सम्झाउँथे। यहाँका धेरैजसो मन्दिरभन्दा फरक, यसका ढोका बन्द नै रहन्छन्। तलेजु मन्दिर वर्षमा एक पटक मात्र, दशैँको ठूलो चाडमा सर्वसाधारणका लागि खुल्छ। भित्र देवीको र उनको मानव रूप मानिने कुमारीको पूजास्थल छन्। कुमारी चोकको ठीक उताको घरमा बस्ने जीवित देवी हुन्। सन् २०१५ मा वरिपरिका मन्दिर ढल्दा तलेजु भने भूकम्पबाट जोगियो। यहाँ उभिएर कल्पना गर्नुहोस्: मल्ल राजाहरू यी भर्‍याङ चढेर एक्लै पूजा गर्थे र यही चौरमा बस्ने देवीले आफ्नो राज्यको रक्षा गर्छिन् भन्ने विश्वास गर्थे।','किंवदन्ती अनुसार तलेजु हरेक रात राजा जयप्रकाश मल्लसँग पासा खेल्न आउँथिन्, तर राजाले कसैलाई नभन्ने शर्तमा। राजाकी छोरीले लुकेर पछ्याएपछि रिसाएकी देवी अलप भइन्। पछि उनले राजालाई सपनामा भनिन्, \'म एउटी शाक्य कन्यामा फर्कनेछु।\' परम्परा अनुसार काठमाडौंमा राजकीय कुमारी प्रथा यसरी सुरु भयो।','[\"यो सन् १५६४ मा राजा महेन्द्र मल्लले बनाएका थिए।\", \"तलेजु भवानी मल्ल वंशकी कुलदेवी थिइन्।\", \"यो मन्दिर वर्षमा एक पटक मात्र, दशैँमा सर्वसाधारणका लागि खुल्छ।\", \"यहाँ कुनै बेला राखिएको सत्रौं शताब्दीको एउटा हार अहिले सिकागोको आर्ट इन्स्टिच्युटमा छ, र नेपालमा त्यसलाई फिर्ता ल्याउन अभियानकर्ताहरू माग गरिरहेका छन्।\"]','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा वरिपरिका संरचना ढल्दा यो मन्दिर जोगियो।','[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"The only time each year the temple is opened to the public, on Navami\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"वर्षमा एक पटक मात्र, नवमीका दिन मन्दिर सर्वसाधारणका लागि खुल्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Kathmandu-Taleju-06-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Taleju-06-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Taleju Temple\'s gilded roofs, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Taleju-06-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Kathmandu-Taleju-10-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Taleju-10-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Taleju Temple on its stepped plinth, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Taleju-10-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Kathmandu-Taleju-16-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Taleju-16-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Taleju Temple in 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Taleju-16-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Kathmandu-Taleju-20-Portal-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Taleju-20-Portal-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Gateway to the Taleju enclosure\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Taleju-20-Portal-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-02-vom_Basantapur_Bhavan-Taleju-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-02-vom_Basantapur_Bhavan-Taleju-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Taleju seen from the Basantapur palace wing\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-02-vom_Basantapur_Bhavan-Taleju-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Three gilded roofs on a 12-stage brick plinth; a wall on the 8th stage with 12 miniature temples; about 35 m tall\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#c9a227\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"toran\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": 35, \"footprint_m\": [30, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 12, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(46,'kumari-ghar','Kumari Ghar','कुमारी घर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu','kathmandu-durbar-square',27.703770,85.306524,'courtyard','Both','Kumari (Taleju)',1757,'18th century CE (1757)','Malla','Three-storey Newar bahal-style residence around a carved courtyard',1,'Home of Kathmandu\'s Royal Kumari, a young girl revered as a living goddess.','Step through the lion-guarded doorway into a quiet courtyard. This is Kumari Ghar, the home of the Royal Kumari of Kathmandu, a young girl from the Newar Shakya community who is worshipped as a living embodiment of the goddess Taleju. The three-storey building was built in 1757 under King Jaya Prakash Malla. Look up at the richly carved wooden windows around you. Sometimes the Kumari appears briefly at one of them, and devotees wait patiently for a glimpse. Please do not photograph her; it is not permitted. The Kumari rarely leaves this house. Her biggest public appearance comes during the Indra Jatra festival, when she is carried through the city in a chariot. In the days of the monarchy, the king would bow before her each year to receive a tika; today the president of Nepal performs a similar role. When the 2015 earthquake shattered temples around the square, this house stood unharmed.','One night, King Jaya Prakash Malla\'s secret game of dice with the goddess Taleju ended when his daughter followed him. Taleju vanished in anger, then returned in a dream: from now on, she said, she would live within a young girl of the Shakya community. To honour her, a girl was chosen and enthroned, and the tradition of the Kumari began.','[\"The house was built in 1757 under King Jaya Prakash Malla.\", \"The Royal Kumari is chosen from the Newar Shakya community.\", \"During Indra Jatra the Kumari is pulled through Kathmandu on a chariot.\", \"The house stood undamaged in the 2015 earthquake.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,500,0,15,'Kumari Ghar stood unharmed in 2015 amid the rubble of surrounding temples.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Entrance_of_Kumari_House-_Basantpur_Durbar_Square%2C_Kathmandu_Nepal-0366.jpg/1280px-Entrance_of_Kumari_House-_Basantpur_Durbar_Square%2C_Kathmandu_Nepal-0366.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_of_Kumari_House-_Basantpur_Durbar_Square,_Kathmandu_Nepal-0366.jpg','Bijay chaurasia · CC BY-SA 4.0','courtyard,both,malla,kathmandu,hindu,buddhist,unesco,legend,palace,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kumari_(goddess)\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu_Durbar_Square\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2659104413\", \"https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/kumari-ghar\", \"https://www.hinduismtoday.com/hpi/2015/05/13/nepal-s-living-goddess-devotees-were-unscathed-by-earthquake/\"]','काठमाडौंकी राजकीय कुमारीको घर; जीवित देवीका रूपमा पूजा गरिने सानी बालिका यहाँ बस्छिन्।','सिंहले पहरा दिएको ढोकाबाट एउटा शान्त चोकमा पस्नुहोस्। यो कुमारी घर हो, काठमाडौंकी राजकीय कुमारीको घर। उनी नेवार शाक्य समुदायकी सानी बालिका हुन् र देवी तलेजुको जीवित रूप मानेर पूजा गरिन्छ। तीन तले यो भवन सन् १७५७ मा राजा जयप्रकाश मल्लको पालामा बनेको हो। वरिपरिका कुँदिएका काठका झ्यालतिर हेर्नुहोस्। कहिलेकाहीँ कुमारी छोटो समयका लागि कुनै झ्यालमा देखा पर्छिन्, र भक्तजनहरू धैर्यसाथ एक झलकको प्रतीक्षा गर्छन्। कृपया उनको फोटो नखिच्नुहोस्; अनुमति छैन। कुमारी विरलै घरबाहिर निस्कन्छिन्। उनको सबैभन्दा ठूलो सार्वजनिक उपस्थिति इन्द्रजात्रामा हुन्छ, जब उनलाई रथमा राखेर सहरमा घुमाइन्छ। राजाको पालामा राजा हरेक वर्ष उनको अगाडि झुकेर टीका लगाउँथे; अहिले नेपालका राष्ट्रपतिले त्यस्तै भूमिका निभाउँछन्। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले चोकवरिपरिका मन्दिर ढाल्दा यो घर भने सुरक्षित रह्यो।','एक रात राजा जयप्रकाश मल्लले देवी तलेजुसँग लुकेर खेलेको पासा खेल उनकी छोरीले पछ्याएपछि टुंगियो। तलेजु रिसाएर अलप भइन्, अनि सपनामा आएर भनिन्, अब उनी शाक्य समुदायकी एउटी सानी बालिकामा बस्नेछिन्। उनको सम्मानमा एउटी बालिका छानेर सिंहासनमा राखियो, र कुमारी प्रथा सुरु भयो।','[\"यो घर राजा जयप्रकाश मल्लको पालामा सन् १७५७ मा बनेको हो।\", \"राजकीय कुमारी नेवार शाक्य समुदायबाट छानिन्छिन्।\", \"इन्द्रजात्रामा कुमारीलाई रथमा राखेर काठमाडौंमा तानिन्छ।\", \"सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा यो घरमा कुनै क्षति भएन।\"]','सन् २०१५ मा वरिपरिका मन्दिर भत्किए पनि कुमारी घर सुरक्षित रह्यो।','[{\"name\": \"Indra Jatra\", \"note\": \"The Kumari leaves her house and is pulled through old Kathmandu on a chariot\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"इन्द्रजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"कुमारी आफ्नो घरबाट निस्किन्छिन् र पुरानो काठमाडौंमा रथमा तानिन्छिन्\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-20-Innenhof-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-20-Innenhof-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Inner courtyard of the Kumari house, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-20-Innenhof-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-22-Fenster-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-22-Fenster-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Carved windows overlooking the courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-22-Fenster-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-24-Schnitzerei-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-24-Schnitzerei-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Wood carving detail\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Kumarihaus-24-Schnitzerei-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Kumari_Ghar%2C_Kathmandu_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Kumari_Ghar%2C_Kathmandu_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Faj2323\", \"caption\": \"Kumari Ghar facing Durbar Square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kumari_Ghar,_Kathmandu_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Dharma_dhatu_mandal.jpg/1280px-Dharma_dhatu_mandal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Manish dangol\", \"caption\": \"Dharmadhatu mandala inside the courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dharma_dhatu_mandal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Three-storey brick house with deeply carved latticed windows round a small inner courtyard; white lions guard the door\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#f2efe6\"], \"features\": [\"carved-windows\", \"lion-statues\", \"toran\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [25, 25], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(47,'kal-bhairav','Kal Bhairav','काल भैरव','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu','kathmandu-durbar-square',27.704719,85.307097,'statue','Hindu','Bhairav (fierce form of Shiva)',NULL,'Installed in the square in the 17th century (reign of Pratap Malla, 1641–1674)','Malla','Large open-air stone relief, painted, said to be carved from a single stone',1,'A fearsome six-armed Bhairav; lying before him was once believed to bring instant death.','Face the huge, dark figure with wild eyes and a crown of skulls. This is Kal Bhairav, the terrifying form of Shiva who destroys evil. He has six arms and tramples a demon under his feet. According to tradition, the image was found in a paddy field and brought to the square by King Pratap Malla in the 17th century, and it is said to be carved from a single stone. For a long time, people believed that anyone who told a lie in front of Kal Bhairav would die on the spot. Royal courtiers swore oaths of loyalty here, and witnesses were brought before him to testify. Notice the offerings of flowers, rice and red powder at his feet, and the lamps lit by worshippers. Even today, many people find it hard to look him in the eye while saying something untrue. During Dashain, animal sacrifices are still offered here.','People said that no one could lie in front of Kal Bhairav and live. Anyone who spoke a falsehood before him would vomit blood and die on the spot. So, in the days of the kings, courtiers swore their loyalty before him and witnesses in criminal cases were made to testify in his presence. Fear of his gaze, it is said, was often enough to make the guilty confess.','[\"Kal Bhairav is a fierce form of Shiva.\", \"Tradition says King Pratap Malla placed the image in the square after it was found in a paddy field.\", \"The figure is believed to be carved from a single stone.\", \"The six-armed god stands on a demon and wears a garland of skulls.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,500,0,10,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Bhairab_statue_at_Hanumandhoka%2C_Basantapur.jpg/1280px-Bhairab_statue_at_Hanumandhoka%2C_Basantapur.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhairab_statue_at_Hanumandhoka,_Basantapur.jpg','Ronishash · CC BY-SA 4.0','statue,hindu,malla,kathmandu,unesco,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaal_Bhairav,_Kathmandu\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q106208411\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/196261745\", \"https://nepalitimes.com/the-mystery-of-the-black-bhairab\"]','छ हात भएको डरलाग्दो भैरव; उनको अगाडि झुटो बोल्नेको तुरुन्तै मृत्यु हुन्छ भन्ने विश्वास थियो।','जङ्गली आँखा र खप्परको मुकुट भएको त्यो विशाल कालो मूर्तिको सामना गर्नुहोस्। यो कालभैरव हो, खराबीको नाश गर्ने शिवको भयानक रूप। उनका छ हात छन् र पाउमुनि एउटा दानव कुल्चेका छन्। परम्परा अनुसार यो मूर्ति धानखेतमा भेटिएको थियो र सत्रौं शताब्दीमा राजा प्रताप मल्लले यो चोकमा ल्याएका थिए। यो एउटै ढुङ्गाबाट कुँदिएको भनिन्छ। लामो समयसम्म मानिसहरू कालभैरवको अगाडि झुटो बोल्ने जो कोही त्यहीँ मर्छ भन्ने विश्वास गर्थे। दरबारका मानिसहरूले यहीँ वफादारीको शपथ खान्थे र साक्षीहरूलाई पनि उनकै अगाडि बयान दिन ल्याइन्थ्यो। उनको पाउमा चढाइएका फूल, चामल र सिन्दूर र भक्तजनले बालेका बत्ती हेर्नुहोस्। आजभोलि पनि धेरैलाई झुटो कुरा भन्दै उनको आँखामा हेर्न गाह्रो लाग्छ। दशैँमा यहाँ अहिले पनि पशुबलि चढाइन्छ।','कालभैरवको अगाडि झुटो बोल्ने कोही पनि बाँच्दैन भनिन्थ्यो। उनको सामु झुटो बोल्नेले रगत बान्ता गरेर त्यहीँ मर्थ्यो रे। त्यसैले राजाको पालामा दरबारका मानिसहरूले उनकै अगाडि वफादारीको शपथ खान्थे र फौजदारी मुद्दाका साक्षीलाई उनको उपस्थितिमा बयान दिन लगाइन्थ्यो। उनको नजरको डरले नै दोषीलाई अपराध स्वीकार गर्न बाध्य बनाउँथ्यो भनिन्छ।','[\"कालभैरव शिवको भयानक रूप हुन्।\", \"परम्परा अनुसार धानखेतमा भेटिएपछि राजा प्रताप मल्लले यो मूर्ति चोकमा राखेका हुन्।\", \"यो मूर्ति एउटै ढुङ्गाबाट कुँदिएको मानिन्छ।\", \"छ हात भएका यी देवता दानवमाथि उभिएका छन् र खप्परको माला लगाएका छन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Animal sacrifices are still offered before the image during Dashain\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दशैँमा यो मूर्तिको अगाडि अहिले पनि पशुबलि चढाइन्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Indra Jatra\", \"note\": \"Masked dances, the Kumari chariot and the raised Indra pole fill the old royal square\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"इन्द्रजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"मुखुन्डो नाच, कुमारीको रथ र उठाइएको इन्द्रध्वजले पुरानो शाही चोक भरिन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-02-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-02-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The six-armed Kal Bhairav image, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-02-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-24-Opfergaben-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-24-Opfergaben-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Offerings at Kal Bhairav\'s feet, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-24-Opfergaben-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-16-abends-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-16-abends-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Kal Bhairav in the evening\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-16-abends-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-06-Vishnu-Indrapur-Degutale-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-06-Vishnu-Indrapur-Degutale-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Kal Bhairav with Vishnu, Indrapur and Degutale temples behind\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-06-Vishnu-Indrapur-Degutale-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-22-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-22-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Kal Bhairav, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Kal_Bhairav-22-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"statue\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Huge black six-armed stone Bhairav with gold crown and skull garland, trampling a demon, behind a low railing\", \"tiers\": 0, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#1f1f1f\", \"#c9a227\", \"#a02020\"], \"features\": [\"idol-visible\", \"fence-railing\", \"lamps-diyo\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [4, 2], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(48,'jagannath-temple','Jagannath Temple','जगन्नाथ मन्दिर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu','kathmandu-durbar-square',27.704631,85.307232,'pagoda','Hindu','Jagannath (Vishnu/Krishna)',1563,'16th century CE (c. 1563; attribution debated)','Malla','Two-roofed Newar pagoda on a three-tiered plinth with carved erotic roof struts',1,'A 16th-century pagoda famous for the erotic carvings on its roof struts.','Walk around this two-roofed pagoda near the palace gate and look up at the slanting wooden struts that hold up the roof. You will notice small carved scenes, some of them openly erotic. This is the Jagannath Temple, one of the oldest structures in the square, dedicated to Jagannath, a form of Vishnu. It is usually dated to around 1563, in the reign of King Mahendra Malla, although King Pratap Malla later claimed to have built it, and historians still debate the date. Why the erotic carvings? Nobody knows for sure. Some people say they celebrate life and fertility; a popular folk belief says they protect the temple from lightning. The upper roof was damaged in the great earthquake of 1934 and the temple was rebuilt in 1936 using original materials. In 2015, when other temples fell around it, Jagannath survived.',NULL,'[\"The temple is commonly dated to about 1563, during Mahendra Malla\'s reign; Pratap Malla later claimed it.\", \"Its roof struts carry well-known erotic carvings.\", \"It was damaged in the 1934 earthquake and rebuilt in 1936 with original materials.\", \"It survived the 2015 earthquake.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,500,0,10,'The temple survived the 2015 earthquake.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Jagannath_Temple_at_Hanumandhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Jagannath_Temple_at_Hanumandhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jagannath_Temple_at_Hanumandhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg','Suraj Belbase · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,kathmandu,unesco,art,bagmati','[\"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/169429518\", \"https://www.kvptnepal.org/project/jagannath-temple\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/jagannath-temple-a-fusion-of-art-and-spirituality\", \"https://thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/temples-buildings-destroyed-nepal-earthquake-2015.html\"]','सोह्रौं शताब्दीको पगोडा, जसका छानाका टेकोमा कुँदिएका कामुक नक्काशीका लागि प्रख्यात छ।','दरबारको ढोकाछेउको यो दुई छाने पगोडाको वरिपरि घुम्नुहोस् र छाना थाम्ने ढल्केका काठका टेकोतिर हेर्नुहोस्। तपाईंले साना नक्काशी गरिएका दृश्य देख्नुहुनेछ, कतिपय खुलमखुल्ला कामुक। यो जगन्नाथ मन्दिर हो, चोकका सबैभन्दा पुराना संरचनामध्ये एक, विष्णुको रूप जगन्नाथलाई समर्पित। यसलाई सामान्यतया सन् १५६३ तिरको, राजा महेन्द्र मल्लको पालाको मानिन्छ। पछि राजा प्रताप मल्लले आफैंले बनाएको दाबी गरे, र इतिहासकारहरू अझै मितिबारे बहस गर्छन्। कामुक नक्काशी किन? पक्का कसैलाई थाहा छैन। कोही भन्छन् यसले जीवन र उर्वरताको उत्सव मनाउँछ; एउटा लोकप्रिय लोकविश्वास छ, यसले मन्दिरलाई चट्याङबाट जोगाउँछ। सन् १९३४ को ठूलो भूकम्पमा माथिल्लो छाना क्षतिग्रस्त भयो र सन् १९३६ मा पुरानै सामग्री प्रयोग गरेर मन्दिर फेरि बनाइयो। सन् २०१५ मा वरिपरिका अरू मन्दिर ढल्दा जगन्नाथ भने जोगियो।',NULL,'[\"यो मन्दिर सामान्यतया सन् १५६३ तिरको, राजा महेन्द्र मल्लको पालाको मानिन्छ; पछि प्रताप मल्लले आफूले बनाएको दाबी गरे।\", \"यसका छानाका टेकोमा प्रख्यात कामुक नक्काशी छन्।\", \"सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पमा क्षति भएपछि सन् १९३६ मा पुरानै सामग्री प्रयोग गरेर यो फेरि बनाइयो।\", \"यो सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा जोगियो।\"]','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा यो मन्दिर जोगियो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Kathmandu-Jagannath-04-hinter_Pratapamalla-vor_Taleju-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Jagannath-04-hinter_Pratapamalla-vor_Taleju-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Jagannath Temple behind Pratap Malla\'s pillar, Taleju beyond\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Jagannath-04-hinter_Pratapamalla-vor_Taleju-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Kathmandu-Jagannath-20-vierkoepfige_Gottheit-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Jagannath-20-vierkoepfige_Gottheit-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Four-headed deity carved on a roof strut\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Jagannath-20-vierkoepfige_Gottheit-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Kathmandu-Jagannath-16-Gevoegel-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Jagannath-16-Gevoegel-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Pigeons on the temple roofs, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Jagannath-16-Gevoegel-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Jagannath_Temple%2C_Kathmandu_17_May_2019.jpg/1280px-Jagannath_Temple%2C_Kathmandu_17_May_2019.jpg\", \"author\": \"Alexey Komarov\", \"caption\": \"Jagannath Temple in May 2019\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jagannath_Temple,_Kathmandu_17_May_2019.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Carvings_in_the_ceiling_beams_of_The_Jagannath_temple.jpg/1280px-Carvings_in_the_ceiling_beams_of_The_Jagannath_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"sat.yamln3.14\", \"caption\": \"Carved timber beams of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carvings_in_the_ceiling_beams_of_The_Jagannath_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Two-roofed brick pagoda on a three-stepped plinth, its roof struts carved with small erotic scenes, beside the palace gate\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 3, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"market-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(49,'hanuman-dhoka-palace','Hanuman Dhoka Palace','हनुमान ढोका दरबार','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu','kathmandu-durbar-square',27.704099,85.307449,'palace','Secular',NULL,NULL,'Mid-16th century CE, expanded in the 17th–19th centuries','Malla','Malla palace of multiple courtyards (chowks) with Shah towers and Rana-era wings',1,'The royal palace of Malla and Shah kings, entered through a gate guarded by Hanuman.','Before you is the gate that gives this whole square its name. A stone statue of Hanuman, the monkey god, dated to 1672, guards the entrance, wrapped in red cloth and shaded by an umbrella, his face smeared with red paste. Beside him, a 1673 sculpture shows Narasimha, half-man and half-lion, tearing apart a demon. Beyond the gate lies the royal palace of the Malla kings, and later the Shah kings, built around courtyards called chowks. The oldest eastern wing dates to the mid-16th century, and King Pratap Malla expanded it in the 17th. In Nasal Chowk, King Birendra was crowned in 1975. The royal family lived here until 1886, when they moved to Narayanhiti Palace. Today, parts of the palace are a museum. It was badly damaged in the 2015 earthquake and has been restored in phases.','Outside the palace stands Pratap Malla\'s stone inscription written in fifteen languages. It is a jaladroni, a drinking fountain stone. It was set up by Pratap Malla, a king proud of his learning who styled himself Kavindra, king of poets. Legend says that if anyone ever reads and understands all fifteen languages, milk instead of water will flow from its spout.','[\"The Hanuman statue at the gate is dated to 1672.\", \"King Birendra was crowned in Nasal Chowk in 1975.\", \"The royal family lived here until 1886, then moved to Narayanhiti Palace.\", \"A nearby stone inscription is written in fifteen languages.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,500,0,60,'The palace buildings were severely damaged in the 2015 earthquake and have been restored in phases since.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Hanuman_Dhoka_Durbar_Square_Kathmandu_%282023%29_01.jpg/1280px-Hanuman_Dhoka_Durbar_Square_Kathmandu_%282023%29_01.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hanuman_Dhoka_Durbar_Square_Kathmandu_(2023)_01.jpg','Chainwit. · CC BY 4.0','palace,secular,malla,kathmandu,unesco,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanuman_Dhoka\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q12947124\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/11365076769\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121\"]','मल्ल र शाह राजाहरूको शाही दरबार, जसको ढोकामा हनुमानले पहरा दिएका छन्।','तपाईंको अगाडि यो सम्पूर्ण चोकलाई नाम दिने ढोका छ। सन् १६७२ को मानिने बाँदर देवता हनुमानको ढुङ्गाको मूर्तिले ढोकामा पहरा दिएको छ, रातो कपडाले बेरिएको, छाताले छाया पारिएको र अनुहारमा रातो अबिर दलिएको। उनको छेउमै सन् १६७३ को नरसिंहको मूर्ति छ, आधा मानिस र आधा सिंह, जसले दानवलाई चिरिरहेको छ। ढोकाभित्र मल्ल राजाहरूको, पछि शाह राजाहरूको शाही दरबार छ, जुन चोक भनिने आँगनवरिपरि बनेको छ। सबैभन्दा पुरानो पूर्वी भाग सोह्रौं शताब्दीको मध्यतिरको हो र सत्रौं शताब्दीमा राजा प्रताप मल्लले यसलाई फराकिलो बनाए। नासल चोकमा सन् १९७५ मा राजा वीरेन्द्रको राज्याभिषेक भएको थियो। शाही परिवार सन् १८८६ सम्म यहीँ बस्यो र त्यसपछि नारायणहिटी दरबार सर्‍यो। आज दरबारका केही भाग सङ्ग्रहालय छन्। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा यो नराम्ररी क्षतिग्रस्त भयो र चरणबद्ध रूपमा पुनर्स्थापना गरिँदै आएको छ।','दरबारको बाहिर प्रताप मल्लले राखेको पन्ध्र भाषामा लेखिएको ढुङ्गाको अभिलेख छ। यो जलद्रोणी हो, अर्थात् पानी खाने धारो ढुङ्गा। आफ्नो विद्वत्तामा गर्व गर्ने र आफूलाई \'कविन्द्र\' अर्थात् कविहरूका राजा भन्ने राजा प्रताप मल्लले यसलाई राखेका थिए। किंवदन्ती छ, यदि कसैले यी पन्ध्रवटै भाषा पढेर बुझ्यो भने यसको धाराबाट पानीको सट्टा दूध बग्नेछ।','[\"ढोकामा रहेको हनुमानको मूर्ति सन् १६७२ को मानिन्छ।\", \"राजा वीरेन्द्रको राज्याभिषेक सन् १९७५ मा नासल चोकमा भएको थियो।\", \"शाही परिवार सन् १८८६ सम्म यहीँ बस्यो, त्यसपछि नारायणहिटी दरबार सर्‍यो।\", \"नजिकैको एउटा ढुङ्गाको अभिलेख पन्ध्र भाषामा लेखिएको छ।\"]','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा दरबारका भवनहरू गम्भीर क्षतिग्रस्त भए र त्यसयता चरणबद्ध रूपमा पुनर्स्थापना गरिँदै छन्।','[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Main Durga festival; the Phulpati procession reaches Hanuman Dhoka on the seventh day\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दुर्गाको मुख्य चाड; सातौं दिन फूलपातीको जुलुस हनुमानढोका पुग्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Indra Jatra\", \"note\": \"The tall Indra pole (lingo) is raised in front of the palace to open the festival\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"इन्द्रजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"इन्द्रजात्रा सुरु हुँदा दरबारको अगाडि अग्लो इन्द्रध्वज (लिङ्गो) उठाइन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Eingang-04-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Eingang-04-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Palace entrance by the Hanuman statue, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Eingang-04-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Nasal_Chowk-02-Pancamukhi_Hanuman_Mandir-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Nasal_Chowk-02-Pancamukhi_Hanuman_Mandir-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Nasal Chowk and the five-roofed Panchamukhi Hanuman temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Nasal_Chowk-02-Pancamukhi_Hanuman_Mandir-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Lohan_Chowk-02-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Lohan_Chowk-02-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Lohan Chowk courtyard, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Lohan_Chowk-02-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Nasal_Chowk-42-Fenster-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Nasal_Chowk-42-Fenster-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Carved window in Nasal Chowk\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Nasal_Chowk-42-Fenster-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-aussen-02-Inschrift_Pratapamallas-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-aussen-02-Inschrift_Pratapamallas-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Pratap Malla\'s stone inscription outside the palace\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-aussen-02-Inschrift_Pratapamallas-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Erdbebenschaden-02-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Erdbebenschaden-02-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Earthquake damage to the palace, 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Hanuman_Dhoka-Erdbebenschaden-02-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Red-cloaked Hanuman under an umbrella beside the painted gate; brick wings with carved windows and the nine-storey tower\", \"tiers\": 9, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c0392b\"], \"features\": [\"carved-windows\", \"carved-struts\", \"watchtower\", \"lion-statues\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [150, 100], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(50,'maju-dega','Maju Dega','माजु देग','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu','kathmandu-durbar-square',27.704277,85.306202,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva',1692,'Late 17th century CE (1692)','Malla','Three-roofed Newar pagoda on a nine-tiered brick plinth',1,'A towering Shiva temple on nine tall steps, destroyed in 2015 and rebuilt.','Climb the tall stepped plinth in front of you, if it is open, and you will understand why Maju Dega has long been a favourite seat for watching life in the square. This Shiva temple was built in 1692 by Riddhi Lakshmi, the queen mother of King Bhupatindra Malla. It stands on a nine-tiered brick plinth and rises in three roofs, making it one of the most visible temples in Durbar Square. Inside is a Shiva linga. For decades, travellers rested on its steps; it even appears in the 1971 Indian film Hare Rama Hare Krishna, filmed partly here. On 25 April 2015 the temple collapsed completely in the earthquake. Reconstruction began in October 2018, and today the temple stands again on its old plinth, rebuilt with brick and carved timber. Look out across the square from here and you can see why the Malla court valued this view.',NULL,'[\"It was built in 1692 by Queen Mother Riddhi Lakshmi.\", \"The temple stands on a nine-tiered brick plinth.\", \"The 1971 film Hare Rama Hare Krishna was filmed on its premises.\", \"It was completely destroyed in 2015; reconstruction began in October 2018.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,500,0,15,'The temple collapsed completely in the 2015 earthquake; reconstruction began in October 2018 and it has since been rebuilt.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Maju_Dega_Temple%2C_Hanuman_Dhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Maju_Dega_Temple%2C_Hanuman_Dhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maju_Dega_Temple,_Hanuman_Dhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg','Safalphotos · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,kathmandu,unesco,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maju_Dega\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/183562980\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/kathmandu/reconstruction-of-quake-damaged-maju-dega-temple-begins\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maju_Dega_Temple,_Hanuman_Dhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg\"]','नौ तह भएको उच्च आधारमा उभिएको शिवको अग्लो मन्दिर, २०१५ मा ढलेर फेरि बनाइएको।','तपाईंको अगाडिको अग्लो भर्‍याङदार आधारमा चढ्नुहोस् (खुला भए), अनि बुझ्नुहुनेछ किन माजुदेगः लामो समयदेखि चोकको जीवन हेर्ने प्रिय ठाउँ हो। यो शिव मन्दिर सन् १६९२ मा राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लकी आमा रानी रिद्धि लक्ष्मीले बनाएकी थिइन्। यो नौ तह भएको इँटाको आधारमाथि उभिएको छ र तीन छानामा उठेको छ, जसले गर्दा यो दरबार क्षेत्रका सबैभन्दा सजिलै देखिने मन्दिरमध्ये एक हो। भित्र शिवलिङ्ग छ। दशकौंसम्म बटुवाहरू यसका भर्‍याङमा सुस्ताउँथे; सन् १९७१ को भारतीय फिल्म \'हरे राम हरे कृष्ण\' पनि यहीँ केही भाग खिचिएको थियो। २५ अप्रिल २०१५ मा भूकम्पले मन्दिर पूरै ढाल्यो। सन् २०१८ को अक्टोबरमा पुनर्निर्माण सुरु भयो, र आज मन्दिर इँटा र कुँदिएको काठले बनाइएर आफ्नै पुरानो आधारमा फेरि उभिएको छ। यहाँबाट चोकभरि हेर्नुहोस्; मल्ल दरबारले यो दृश्यलाई किन महत्त्व दिन्थ्यो भन्ने बुझ्नुहुनेछ।',NULL,'[\"यो सन् १६९२ मा राजमाता रिद्धि लक्ष्मीले बनाएकी थिइन्।\", \"मन्दिर नौ तह भएको इँटाको आधारमाथि उभिएको छ।\", \"सन् १९७१ को फिल्म \'हरे राम हरे कृष्ण\' यसको परिसरमा खिचिएको थियो।\", \"सन् २०१५ मा यो पूरै ध्वस्त भयो; पुनर्निर्माण सन् २०१८ को अक्टोबरमा सुरु भयो।\"]','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा मन्दिर पूरै ढल्यो; पुनर्निर्माण सन् २०१८ को अक्टोबरमा सुरु भयो र अहिले यो फेरि बनिसकेको छ।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-02-Kamadev-Narayana-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-02-Kamadev-Narayana-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Maju Dega with the Kamadev and Narayan temples, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-02-Kamadev-Narayana-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-06-Kamadev-Narayana-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-06-Kamadev-Narayana-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Maju Dega\'s stepped plinth, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-06-Kamadev-Narayana-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-12-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-12-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Ruins of Maju Dega after the 2015 earthquake\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-12-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Giant_Lingam_at_Maju_Dega%2C_Kathmandu-1.jpg/1280px-Giant_Lingam_at_Maju_Dega%2C_Kathmandu-1.jpg\", \"author\": \"Immanuelle\", \"caption\": \"The large Shiva linga inside Maju Dega\", \"license\": \"CC BY 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giant_Lingam_at_Maju_Dega,_Kathmandu-1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-14-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-14-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Collapsed temple site, 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Maju_Dega-14-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Three-roofed Shiva temple raised on a very tall nine-stepped brick plinth where people sit to watch the square\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"shiva-lingam\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [24, 24], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 9, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"market-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(51,'ashok-binayak','Ashok Binayak','अशोक विनायक','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu','kathmandu-durbar-square',27.704190,85.305970,'pagoda','Hindu','Ganesh',NULL,'Date unknown','unknown','Small single-roofed shrine plated in gold, with no gajur (pinnacle)',1,'A tiny golden Ganesh shrine, one of the valley\'s four most important, with no pinnacle on its roof.','It is easy to walk past this small golden shrine beside Kasthamandap, but locals never do. This is Ashok Binayak, also called Maru Ganesh, and it is one of the four most important Ganesh shrines in the Kathmandu Valley. The other three are Chandra Binayak, Surya Binayak and Jal Binayak. Ganesh, the elephant-headed god, removes obstacles, so many people stop here before a journey, an exam or a new business. Tuesday is Ganesh\'s day, and that is when the crowds are biggest. Look at the roof: unlike most temples, it has no gajur, the pointed pinnacle on top. Local people say this missing pinnacle gave the neighbourhood its name, Maru, which in Newari means \'does not have\'. The whole exterior is plated in gold. Across the narrow lane, look for a small statue of a mouse, Ganesh\'s loyal vehicle.',NULL,'[\"It is one of the four principal Ganesh shrines of the Kathmandu Valley.\", \"Its roof has no gajur (pinnacle); \'Maru\' is said to mean \'does not have\' in Newari.\", \"Tuesday, Ganesh\'s day, draws the most worshippers.\", \"A statue of a mouse, Ganesh\'s vehicle, faces the shrine across the lane.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,500,0,10,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Ashok_Vinayak_at_Hanuman-Dhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Ashok_Vinayak_at_Hanuman-Dhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashok_Vinayak_at_Hanuman-Dhoka_Durbar_Square.jpg','Suraj Belbase · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,kathmandu,unesco,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashok_Binayak_Temple\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2084347901\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/kathmandu/ashok-binayak-maru-ganesh.html\"]','गणेशको सानो सुनौलो मन्दिर, उपत्यकाका चार प्रमुख गणेश मन्दिरमध्ये एक, जसको छानामा गजुर छैन।','काष्ठमण्डपको छेउको यो सानो सुनौलो मन्दिरलाई बेवास्ता गरेर हिँड्न सजिलो छ, तर स्थानीयहरू कहिल्यै त्यसो गर्दैनन्। यो अशोक विनायक हो, जसलाई मरु गणेश पनि भनिन्छ, र यो काठमाडौं उपत्यकाका चार सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण गणेश मन्दिरमध्ये एक हो। अरू तीनवटा चन्द्र विनायक, सूर्य विनायक र जल विनायक हुन्। हात्तीको टाउको भएका गणेश विघ्न हर्ने देवता हुन्, त्यसैले धेरै मानिस यात्रा, परीक्षा वा नयाँ व्यापार सुरु गर्नुअघि यहाँ रोकिन्छन्। मंगलबार गणेशको दिन हो, र त्यतिबेला भीड सबैभन्दा बढी हुन्छ। छानातिर हेर्नुहोस्: धेरैजसो मन्दिरमा जस्तो यसमा माथि टुप्पो हुने गजुर छैन। स्थानीयहरू भन्छन्, यही गजुर नहुनाले टोलले \'मरु\' नाम पायो, जसको नेवारीमा अर्थ \'नभएको\' हो। पूरै बाहिरी भाग सुनले मोडिएको छ। साँघुरो गल्लीको उताबाट गणेशको वाहन मुसाको सानो मूर्ति खोज्नुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"यो काठमाडौं उपत्यकाका चार प्रमुख गणेश मन्दिरमध्ये एक हो।\", \"यसको छानामा गजुर (टुप्पो) छैन; नेवारीमा \'मरु\' को अर्थ \'नभएको\' हो भनिन्छ।\", \"गणेशको दिन मंगलबार सबैभन्दा धेरै भक्तजन आउँछन्।\", \"गल्लीको उता गणेशको वाहन मुसाको मूर्ति मन्दिरतिर फर्केर छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"The Ganesh image is dressed in a silver or metal cover for the festival\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दशैँमा गणेशको मूर्तिलाई चाँदी वा धातुको कवच ओढाइन्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Indra Jatra\", \"note\": \"The image is again decorated with its metal cover\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"इन्द्रजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"इन्द्रजात्रामा मूर्तिलाई फेरि धातुको कवचले सजाइन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Ashok_vinyak_also_called_Maru_Ganesh.jpg/1280px-Ashok_vinyak_also_called_Maru_Ganesh.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"The gold-plated shrine of Maru Ganesh\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashok_vinyak_also_called_Maru_Ganesh.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Maru_Ganesh_%2822685%29.jpg/1280px-Maru_Ganesh_%2822685%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prakashphuyal30\", \"caption\": \"Ashok Binayak shrine\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maru_Ganesh_(22685).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-58-Schrein_mit_Glocken-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-58-Schrein_mit_Glocken-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The shrine with its bells, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Durbar_Square-58-Schrein_mit_Glocken-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Ashok_Binayak_Temple_Maru_Ganesh_Temple_Maru_Tole_Hanumandhoka_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Ashok_Binayak_Temple_Maru_Ganesh_Temple_Maru_Tole_Hanumandhoka_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Ashok Binayak in Maru Tole\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashok_Binayak_Temple_Maru_Ganesh_Temple_Maru_Tole_Hanumandhoka_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Ashok_Binayak_Temple_%282026%29.jpg/1280px-Ashok_Binayak_Temple_%282026%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"SristiAwasthi21\", \"caption\": \"Ashok Binayak in 2026\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashok_Binayak_Temple_(2026).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Tiny single-roof shrine plated in gold with no pinnacle on top, hung with bells, on a lane corner by Kasthamandap\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#c9a227\", \"#a02020\", \"#8b3a2b\"], \"features\": [\"idol-visible\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [3, 3], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"city-street\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(52,'swayambhunath','Swayambhunath','स्वयम्भूनाथ','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.714939,85.290391,'stupa','Both','Adi-Buddha (Swayambhu)',NULL,'Ancient; Licchavi-era works recorded c. 5th century CE','Licchavi','Hilltop hemispherical stupa with gilded harmika painted with the Buddha\'s eyes and a 13-ring spire',1,'The \'self-arisen\' hilltop stupa watching over the valley, beloved by Buddhists, Hindus and monkeys.','You have reached the top of the hill, and the great white dome of Swayambhunath rises in front of you. Swayambhu means \'self-arisen\'. Look up at the golden tower: on each side, the eyes of the Buddha gaze out over the valley in all four directions. Above them, thirteen gilded rings represent the thirteen stages on the path to enlightenment. This is one of the oldest and most sacred Buddhist sites in Nepal, yet Hindus worship here too, and you will find shrines of both faiths side by side. Licchavi kings carried out works here, and in the 17th century King Pratap Malla built the long eastern stairway that many visitors climb. Watch your belongings: troops of monkeys live on the hill, which is why travellers call it the Monkey Temple. Walk clockwise around the stupa, spin the prayer wheels, and enjoy one of the best views of Kathmandu.','Long ago, the Kathmandu Valley was a great lake. A Buddha sowed a lotus seed in it, and a thousand-petalled lotus bloomed, glowing with a self-born light, Swayambhu. The bodhisattva Manjushri wanted pilgrims to reach it, so he cut a gorge through the hills with his sword. The water drained away, the valley became fertile land, and the lotus became the hill.','[\"Swayambhu means \'self-arisen\' or \'self-sprung\'.\", \"It was inscribed as part of the Kathmandu Valley World Heritage Site in 1979.\", \"King Pratap Malla built the long eastern stairway in the 17th century.\", \"The 13 gilded rings of the spire represent 13 stages towards enlightenment.\"]',NULL,NULL,200,50,0,90,'The complex was damaged in 2015; the cracked Pratappur shikhara was demolished in 2017 and it and the Anantapur shikhara were rebuilt.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Swayambhunath_2018.jpg/1280px-Swayambhunath_2018.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swayambhunath_2018.jpg','Nabin K. Sapkota · CC BY-SA 4.0','stupa,both,licchavi,kathmandu,hindu,buddhist,unesco,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swayambhunath\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q12946982\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/201223707\", \"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/reconstruction-of-pratappur-anantapur-temples-over.html\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/miscellaneous/2017/01/18/pratappur-temple-demolished\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/kathmandu/all-can-enter-swayambhunath-stupa-for-free-on-buddha-jayanti/\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/entry-fees-of-the-heritage-sites-in-nepal/\"]','\'स्वयम्भू\' अर्थात् आफैं प्रकट भएको भनिने डाँडाको स्तूप, जसलाई बौद्ध, हिन्दू र बाँदर सबैले माया गर्छन्।','तपाईं डाँडाको टुप्पोमा पुग्नुभयो, र स्वयम्भूनाथको विशाल सेतो गुम्बज तपाईंको अगाडि उठेको छ। स्वयम्भू भनेको \'आफैं प्रकट भएको\' हो। सुनको टावरतिर हेर्नुहोस्: चारै दिशातर्फ उपत्यकामाथि बुद्धका आँखाले हेरिरहेका छन्। त्यसमाथि तेह्रवटा सुनौला घेरा छन्, जसले ज्ञान प्राप्तिको बाटोका तेह्र चरण जनाउँछन्। यो नेपालका सबैभन्दा पुराना र पवित्र बौद्ध स्थलमध्ये एक हो, तर यहाँ हिन्दूहरू पनि पूजा गर्छन्, र दुवै धर्मका मन्दिर छेउछाउ भेटिन्छन्। लिच्छवि राजाहरूले यहाँ काम गराएका थिए, र सत्रौं शताब्दीमा राजा प्रताप मल्लले धेरै पर्यटकले चढ्ने लामो पूर्वी भर्‍याङ बनाए। आफ्ना सामानको ख्याल राख्नुहोस्: डाँडामा बाँदरका बथान बस्छन्, त्यसैले यात्रुहरू यसलाई बाँदर मन्दिर भन्छन्। स्तूपलाई घडीको दिशामा घुम्नुहोस्, मानी घुमाउनुहोस्, र काठमाडौंको सबैभन्दा राम्रो दृश्यमध्ये एकको आनन्द लिनुहोस्।','धेरै पहिले काठमाडौं उपत्यका ठूलो ताल थियो। एक बुद्धले त्यसमा कमलको बीज रोपे, र हजार पत्ती भएको कमल फक्र्यो, जसबाट आफैं जन्मेको ज्योति, स्वयम्भू, झलमल्ल चम्किन्थ्यो। बोधिसत्व मञ्जुश्रीले तीर्थयात्रीहरू त्यहाँ पुगून् भन्ने चाहे, र आफ्नो तरबारले डाँडाहरू काटेर एउटा खोँच बनाए। पानी बग्यो, उपत्यका उर्वर भूमि बन्यो, र कमल डाँडो बन्यो।','[\"स्वयम्भूको अर्थ \'आफैं प्रकट भएको\' वा \'स्वयं उत्पन्न\' हो।\", \"यो सन् १९७९ मा काठमाडौं उपत्यका विश्व सम्पदा स्थलको अंशका रूपमा सूचीकृत भयो।\", \"राजा प्रताप मल्लले सत्रौं शताब्दीमा लामो पूर्वी भर्‍याङ बनाए।\", \"शिखरका तेह्रवटा सुनौला घेराले ज्ञान प्राप्तिका तेह्र चरण जनाउँछन्।\"]','सन् २०१५ मा परिसरमा क्षति पुग्यो; चर्किएको प्रतापपुर शिखर सन् २०१७ मा भत्काइयो, र त्यो तथा अनन्तपुर शिखर फेरि बनाइयो।','[{\"name\": \"Buddha Jayanti\", \"note\": \"Buddha’s birthday; pilgrims climb the hill and circle the stupa\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"बुद्ध जयन्ती\", \"note_np\": \"बुद्धको जन्मदिन; तीर्थयात्रीहरू डाँडा चढेर स्तूपको परिक्रमा गर्छन्\"}, {\"name\": \"Gunla\", \"note\": \"Newar Buddhist holy month; devotees walk up to the stupa each morning with music\", \"month\": \"Shrawan\", \"name_np\": \"गुँला\", \"note_np\": \"नेवार बौद्धहरूको पवित्र महिना; भक्तजनहरू हरेक बिहान बाजा बजाउँदै स्तूपसम्म हिँड्छन्\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Swayambhunath-Hauptstupa-02-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Swayambhunath-Hauptstupa-02-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The main stupa, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swayambhunath-Hauptstupa-02-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Swayambhunath-Hauptstupa-18-Buddha-Gesicht-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Swayambhunath-Hauptstupa-18-Buddha-Gesicht-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Buddha\'s eyes painted on the harmika\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swayambhunath-Hauptstupa-18-Buddha-Gesicht-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Swayambhunath-02-vom_Palastplatz-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Swayambhunath-02-vom_Palastplatz-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Swayambhu hill seen from Durbar Square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swayambhunath-02-vom_Palastplatz-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Swayambhunath-Gebetsfahnen-02-Pratapur_Shikara-Anantapur_Shikara-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Swayambhunath-Gebetsfahnen-02-Pratapur_Shikara-Anantapur_Shikara-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Prayer flags and the Pratappur and Anantapur shikharas\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swayambhunath-Gebetsfahnen-02-Pratapur_Shikara-Anantapur_Shikara-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Swayambhunath-Affe-06-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Swayambhunath-Affe-06-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"A monkey on the hill, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swayambhunath-Affe-06-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Swayambhunath-Ausblick_auf_Kathmandu-12-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Swayambhunath-Ausblick_auf_Kathmandu-12-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"View over Kathmandu from the hilltop\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swayambhunath-Ausblick_auf_Kathmandu-12-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"stupa\", \"roof\": \"white-dome\", \"notes\": \"White dome on a wooded hilltop; gilded harmika with painted eyes and a 13-ring spire; two white shikharas and a big vajra\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#f4f1ea\", \"#c9a227\", \"#2b4c8c\"], \"features\": [\"dome-white\", \"harmika\", \"buddha-eyes\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"prayer-flags\", \"prayer-wheels\", \"chaityas\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [30, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\", \"monks-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(53,'boudhanath','Boudhanath Stupa','बौद्धनाथ','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.721427,85.362008,'stupa','Buddhist',NULL,NULL,'Present structure likely 14th century CE; tradition dates a stupa here to the 5th–6th century','Licchavi','Massive mandala-plan spherical stupa on three terraces, with harmika eyes and a 13-step spire',1,'One of the world\'s largest stupas, the heart of Kathmandu\'s Tibetan Buddhist community.','Join the stream of pilgrims walking clockwise around this enormous white dome. Boudhanath is the largest spherical stupa in Nepal and one of the largest in the world. Seen from above, it forms a giant mandala. It stood on the ancient trade route between Tibet and India, and Tibetan merchants rested and prayed here for centuries. After 1959, many Tibetan refugees settled around it and built more than fifty monasteries, so today you will hear Tibetan prayers, smell butter lamps and see monks in maroon robes. Newar chronicles link the first stupa here to Licchavi kings, although the present structure probably dates from the 14th century. In 2015 the earthquake badly damaged its upper section. It was taken down, reinforced and rebuilt, and the stupa reopened in November 2016. Look up at the eyes on the gilded tower, then spin the prayer wheels as you complete your circle.','A Tibetan legend tells of Samvari, a poultry woman who saved her earnings to build a great stupa. She asked the king for land, and he said \'Jarung!\' – \'Let it be done!\' When jealous nobles saw how huge it would be, the king could not take back his word; it had \'slipped from his tongue\' (khashor). So the stupa became Jarung Khashor.','[\"It is the largest spherical stupa in Nepal.\", \"It was inscribed as part of the Kathmandu Valley World Heritage Site in 1979.\", \"After 1959, Tibetan refugees built more than 50 monasteries around the stupa.\", \"After 2015 damage, the upper part was rebuilt and the stupa reopened in November 2016.\"]','00:00','23:59',400,100,0,75,'The 2015 earthquake damaged the upper part of the stupa, which was dismantled and rebuilt; it reopened in November 2016.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Boudha_Stupa_2018_04.jpg/1280px-Boudha_Stupa_2018_04.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boudha_Stupa_2018_04.jpg','Nabin K. Sapkota · CC BY-SA 4.0','stupa,buddhist,licchavi,kathmandu,unesco,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudha_Stupa\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q889902\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/56688296\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/valley/2016/10/31/boudhanath-rebuilding-nears-completion\", \"https://radionepalonline.com/2022/09/08/323963.html\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/entry-fees-of-the-heritage-sites-in-nepal/\"]','विश्वकै सबैभन्दा ठूला स्तूपमध्ये एक, काठमाडौंको तिब्बती बौद्ध समुदायको केन्द्र।','यो विशाल सेतो गुम्बजलाई घडीको दिशामा घुम्दै गरेका तीर्थयात्रीको लहरमा सामेल हुनुहोस्। बौद्धनाथ नेपालको सबैभन्दा ठूलो गोलाकार स्तूप हो र विश्वकै ठूलामध्ये एक हो। माथिबाट हेर्दा यो एउटा विशाल मण्डलजस्तो देखिन्छ। यो तिब्बत र भारतबीचको पुरानो व्यापारिक बाटोमा पर्थ्यो, र तिब्बती व्यापारीहरू शताब्दीयौंसम्म यहाँ आराम र प्रार्थना गर्थे। सन् १९५९ पछि धेरै तिब्बती शरणार्थी यसको वरिपरि बसोबास गरे र पचासभन्दा बढी गुम्बा बनाए, त्यसैले आज यहाँ तिब्बती प्रार्थना सुनिन्छ, घिउबत्तीको बास्ना आउँछ र रातो-खैरो चीवर लगाएका भिक्षु देखिन्छन्। नेवार इतिहासले यहाँको पहिलो स्तूपलाई लिच्छवि राजाहरूसँग जोड्छन्, तर अहिलेको संरचना सम्भवतः चौधौं शताब्दीको हो। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले यसको माथिल्लो भागमा ठूलो क्षति पुर्‍यायो। त्यसलाई भत्काएर बलियो बनाइयो र फेरि बनाइयो, अनि स्तूप सन् २०१६ को नोभेम्बरमा फेरि खुल्यो। सुनौलो टावरका आँखातिर हेर्नुहोस्, अनि परिक्रमा पूरा गर्दै मानी घुमाउनुहोस्।','एउटा तिब्बती किंवदन्तीमा कुखुरा पाल्ने महिला सम्वरीको कथा छ, जसले कमाइ जोगाएर ठूलो स्तूप बनाउने सपना देखिन्। उनले राजासँग जग्गा मागिन्, र राजाले \'जरुङ!\' भने, अर्थात् \'गर्नू!\'। स्तूप कति विशाल हुने रहेछ भनेर देखेर ईर्ष्यालु दरबारीहरू रिसाए, तर राजाले आफ्नो वचन फिर्ता लिन सकेनन्; त्यो उनको मुखबाट \'चुहिइसकेको\' (खाशोर) थियो। यसरी स्तूप जरुङ खाशोर भयो।','[\"यो नेपालको सबैभन्दा ठूलो गोलाकार स्तूप हो।\", \"यो सन् १९७९ मा काठमाडौं उपत्यका विश्व सम्पदा स्थलको अंशका रूपमा सूचीकृत भयो।\", \"सन् १९५९ पछि तिब्बती शरणार्थीहरूले स्तूपवरिपरि पचासभन्दा बढी गुम्बा बनाए।\", \"सन् २०१५ मा क्षति पुगेपछि माथिल्लो भाग फेरि बनाइयो र स्तूप सन् २०१६ को नोभेम्बरमा फेरि खुल्यो।\"]','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले स्तूपको माथिल्लो भागमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो; त्यसलाई भत्काएर फेरि बनाइयो र स्तूप सन् २०१६ को नोभेम्बरमा फेरि खुल्यो।','[{\"name\": \"Losar\", \"note\": \"Tibetan New Year; crowds circle the stupa and new prayer flags are hung\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"ल्होसार\", \"note_np\": \"तिब्बतीहरूको नयाँ वर्ष; भीडले स्तूपको परिक्रमा गर्छ र नयाँ प्रार्थना झन्डा झुन्ड्याइन्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Buddha Jayanti\", \"note\": \"Buddha’s birthday; butter lamps are lit and the stupa is circled all day\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"बुद्ध जयन्ती\", \"note_np\": \"बुद्धको जन्मदिन; घिउबत्ती बालिन्छ र दिनभरि स्तूपको परिक्रमा गरिन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Bodnath-Stupa-04-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Bodnath-Stupa-04-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The great stupa, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodnath-Stupa-04-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Bodnath-Stupa-10-Augen-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Bodnath-Stupa-10-Augen-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Buddha\'s eyes on the harmika\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodnath-Stupa-10-Augen-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Bodnath-Terrassen-02-Gebetsfahnen-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Bodnath-Terrassen-02-Gebetsfahnen-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Prayer flags over the terraces\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodnath-Terrassen-02-Gebetsfahnen-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bodnath-Butterlampen-04-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Bodnath-Butterlampen-04-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Butter lamps lit by pilgrims\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodnath-Butterlampen-04-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Bodnath-Umgang-08-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Bodnath-Umgang-08-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The circuit around the stupa, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodnath-Umgang-08-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Bodnath-Stupa-32-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Bodnath-Stupa-32-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Damaged spire after the 2015 earthquake\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodnath-Stupa-32-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"stupa\", \"roof\": \"white-dome\", \"notes\": \"Huge white dome on a three-level stepped mandala plinth; gilded harmika with eyes and 13 steps; flags radiate to a ring of houses\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#f4f1ea\", \"#c9a227\", \"#b5332e\"], \"features\": [\"dome-white\", \"harmika\", \"buddha-eyes\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"prayer-flags\", \"prayer-wheels\", \"lamps-diyo\"], \"height_m\": 36, \"footprint_m\": [100, 100], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 3, \"surroundings\": [\"monks-houses\", \"market-houses\", \"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(54,'pashupatinath','Pashupatinath Temple','पशुपतिनाथ मन्दिर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.710495,85.348645,'pagoda','Hindu','Pashupati (Shiva)',NULL,'Recorded by c. 400 CE; present form renovated in 1692','Licchavi','Two-roofed gilded Newar pagoda with four silver-plated doors, in a large riverside temple precinct',1,'Nepal\'s holiest Shiva temple, on the sacred Bagmati River with its cremation ghats.','You are on the banks of the sacred Bagmati River at Pashupatinath, the holiest Shiva temple in Nepal and one of the most important in South Asia. Its existence is recorded as early as 400 CE. The main pagoda has two gilded copper roofs, a golden pinnacle and four doors covered in silver. Inside is a four-faced stone linga of Shiva as Pashupati, Lord of all living beings. Only Hindus may enter the main temple, but you can watch from across the river. The precinct covers about 246 hectares and holds hundreds of smaller shrines. Along the river you will see the ghats where Hindus are cremated, a moving reminder that, for believers, this is a sacred place to end life\'s journey. Each evening, priests perform the aarti with lamps and chanting. The festival of Maha Shivaratri draws huge crowds. In 2015, the main temple came through the earthquake largely unharmed.','In the Mahabharata legend, the Pandava brothers sought Shiva\'s forgiveness after their war. Shiva hid from them as a bull and sank into the earth, reappearing in parts across the Himalaya: the hump appeared at Kedarnath, and his head, it is said, emerged here at Pashupatinath. The other parts are said to have appeared at Rudranath, Tungnath and Madhyamaheshwar, which is why pilgrims link this temple with those shrines.','[\"The temple precinct covers about 246 hectares and includes 518 smaller temples and shrines.\", \"The main pagoda is 23.7 metres tall with four silver-covered doors.\", \"Only four priests may touch the linga; the Bhatta priests perform daily worship.\", \"Its existence is recorded as early as 400 CE, and the present form dates to a 1692 renovation.\"]','04:00','21:00',1000,1000,0,90,'The main temple was largely unaffected in 2015, though dozens of structures in the wider Pashupati area were damaged and later restored.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Pashupatinath_Temple-2020.jpg/1280px-Pashupatinath_Temple-2020.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pashupatinath_Temple-2020.jpg','Bijay Chaurasia · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,licchavi,kathmandu,unesco,legend,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pashupatinath_Temple\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q380384\", \"https://ghalegroup.com/nepal-attractions-fees-timings/\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/entry-fees-of-the-heritage-sites-in-nepal/\", \"https://eastmojo.com/neighbourhood-watch/nepal/2023/06/15/71-heritage-sites-damaged-in-2015-nepal-quake-restored-report/\"]','नेपालको सबैभन्दा पवित्र शिव मन्दिर, पवित्र बागमती नदीको किनारमा, दाहसंस्कार घाटसहित।','तपाईं पवित्र बागमती नदीको किनारमा पशुपतिनाथमा हुनुहुन्छ, नेपालको सबैभन्दा पवित्र शिव मन्दिर र दक्षिण एसियाकै सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण मन्दिरमध्ये एक। यसको अस्तित्वबारे सन् ४०० जति पुरानो उल्लेख पाइन्छ। मुख्य पगोडामा तामामा सुन लगाइएका दुईवटा छाना, सुनको गजुर र चाँदीले मोडिएका चारवटा ढोका छन्। भित्र पशुपति, अर्थात् सबै प्राणीका स्वामी शिवको चारमुखे ढुङ्गाको लिङ्ग छ। मुख्य मन्दिरभित्र हिन्दूहरूलाई मात्र प्रवेश छ, तर तपाईं नदीको पारिबाट हेर्न सक्नुहुन्छ। परिसर करिब २४६ हेक्टरमा फैलिएको छ र सयौं साना मन्दिर छन्। नदीको किनारमा हिन्दूहरूको दाहसंस्कार हुने घाट देख्नुहुन्छ, जुन विश्वासीहरूका लागि जीवनको यात्रा सकिने पवित्र ठाउँ हो भन्ने मार्मिक सम्झना हो। हरेक साँझ पुजारीहरूले बत्ती बाल्दै मन्त्र जप्दै आरती गर्छन्। महाशिवरात्रिको चाडमा ठूलो भीड लाग्छ। सन् २०१५ मा मुख्य मन्दिर भूकम्पबाट प्रायः जोगियो।','महाभारतको कथा अनुसार पाण्डव दाजुभाइले युद्धपछि शिवसँग क्षमा माग्न खोजे। शिव गोरुको रूपमा लुकेर धर्तीमा पसे र हिमालयभरि टुक्राटुक्रामा देखा परे: कुम केदारनाथमा देखियो, र उनको टाउको यहाँ पशुपतिनाथमा देखियो भनिन्छ। अरू भाग रुद्रनाथ, तुङ्गनाथ र मध्यमहेश्वरमा देखा परेको भनिन्छ, त्यसैले तीर्थयात्रीहरू यो मन्दिरलाई ती मन्दिरसँग जोड्छन्।','[\"मन्दिर परिसर करिब २४६ हेक्टरमा फैलिएको छ र ५१८ साना मन्दिर र देवालय छन्।\", \"मुख्य पगोडा २३.७ मिटर अग्लो छ र चाँदीले मोडिएका चारवटा ढोका छन्।\", \"लिङ्ग छुन पाउने चार जना पुजारी मात्र हुन्; भट्ट पुजारीहरूले दैनिक पूजा गर्छन्।\", \"यसको अस्तित्व सन् ४०० जति पहिलेदेखि उल्लेख छ, र अहिलेको रूप सन् १६९२ को जीर्णोद्धारबाट बनेको हो।\"]','सन् २०१५ मा मुख्य मन्दिर प्रायः प्रभावित भएन, यद्यपि फराकिलो पशुपति क्षेत्रका दर्जनौं संरचनामा क्षति पुग्यो र पछि पुनर्स्थापना गरियो।','[{\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Shiva’s great night; huge crowds and sadhus from Nepal and India\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"शिवको महारात्रि; नेपाल र भारतबाट ठूलो भीड र साधुहरू आउँछन्\"}, {\"name\": \"Teej\", \"note\": \"Women in red fast and queue to worship Shiva for their families\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"तीज\", \"note_np\": \"रातो लुगा लगाएका महिलाहरू आफ्नो परिवारका लागि व्रत बसेर शिवको पूजा गर्न लाइन लाग्छन्\"}, {\"name\": \"Bala Chaturdashi\", \"note\": \"Seeds are scattered for departed relatives and lamps lit through the night\", \"month\": \"Mangsir\", \"name_np\": \"बाला चतुर्दशी\", \"note_np\": \"मृत आफन्तका लागि बीउ छरिन्छ र रातभर बत्ती बालिन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Kathmandu-Pashupatinath-Tempel-02-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Pashupatinath-Tempel-02-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Gilded roofs of the main temple, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Pashupatinath-Tempel-02-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Kathmandu-Pashupatinath-Tempel-10-Aussichtsplattform-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Pashupatinath-Tempel-10-Aussichtsplattform-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The temple seen from the terrace across the Bagmati\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Pashupatinath-Tempel-10-Aussichtsplattform-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pashupatinath-Bagmatibruecke-14-Surya_Ghats-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Pashupatinath-Bagmatibruecke-14-Surya_Ghats-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Ghats on the Bagmati river\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pashupatinath-Bagmatibruecke-14-Surya_Ghats-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Pashupatinath-Bagmatibruecke-10-Votivstupas-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Pashupatinath-Bagmatibruecke-10-Votivstupas-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Rows of small Shiva shrines by the river\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pashupatinath-Bagmatibruecke-10-Votivstupas-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Pashupatinath-Menschen-04-Saddhu-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Pashupatinath-Menschen-04-Saddhu-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"A sadhu at Pashupatinath\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pashupatinath-Menschen-04-Saddhu-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Aarati_Pashupatinath_temple%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Aarati_Pashupatinath_temple%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Girisumit1990\", \"caption\": \"Evening aarti on the riverbank\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aarati_Pashupatinath_temple,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Two-tier gilded pagoda on a square plinth with four silver doors; a huge gilded Nandi bull faces the west door\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#c9a227\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#c0c0c0\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"nandi-bull\", \"trident\", \"bell\", \"shiva-lingam\"], \"height_m\": 23.7, \"footprint_m\": [22, 22], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"riverbank-ghats\", \"river\", \"sacred-grove\", \"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(55,'budhanilkantha','Budhanilkantha Temple','बूढानीलकण्ठ मन्दिर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.778126,85.362341,'statue','Hindu','Vishnu (Jalashayana Narayan)',NULL,'Statue believed to be over 1,400 years old (c. 7th century CE)','Licchavi','Open-air temple: a 5 m reclining Vishnu carved from a single stone in a 13 m sunken pool',0,'A giant sleeping Vishnu floats in a sacred pool beneath Shivapuri hill.','At the foot of Shivapuri hill, at the northern edge of the valley, lies one of Nepal\'s most astonishing sculptures. In a long sunken pool, the god Vishnu reclines on the coils of a cosmic serpent, as if asleep on the waters. The statue is about five metres long, carved from a single block of black stone, and is considered the largest stone carving in Nepal. It is believed to be more than 1,400 years old. In his four hands Vishnu holds a discus, a club, a conch shell and a gem. Strangely, the name Budhanilkantha means \'Old Blue Throat\', a title of Shiva, because the spring feeding the pool is said to be linked with the sacred lake of Gosaikunda. Each year, on Haribodhini Ekadashi in October or November, thousands of pilgrims come to celebrate Vishnu waking from his four-month sleep. For centuries, Nepal\'s kings never came here, fearing a prophecy.','King Pratap Malla is said to have had a vision: if he ever visited Budhanilkantha, he would die early. From then on, it was believed that any king of Nepal who looked upon the sleeping Vishnu would meet the same fate. Royal family members after him never visited the temple, out of fear of the prophecy, even though Budhanilkantha is one of the valley\'s best-loved shrines of Vishnu.','[\"The reclining Vishnu is about 5 metres long and carved from a single stone.\", \"It lies in a recessed pool about 13 metres long.\", \"The name means \'Old Blue Throat\', a title of Shiva.\", \"Thousands gather here for Haribodhini Ekadashi in Kartik (Oct–Nov).\"]',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Budhanilkantha_Narayan_Murti_%282023%29_-_IMG_03.jpg/1280px-Budhanilkantha_Narayan_Murti_%282023%29_-_IMG_03.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budhanilkantha_Narayan_Murti_(2023)_-_IMG_03.jpg','Chainwit. · CC BY-SA 4.0','statue,hindu,licchavi,kathmandu,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budhanilkantha_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1001415\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/85552443\"]','सुतिरहेका विष्णुको विशाल मूर्ति शिवपुरी डाँडामुनिको पवित्र कुण्डमा तैरिरहेको छ।','उपत्यकाको उत्तरी छेउमा शिवपुरी डाँडाको फेदमा नेपालका सबैभन्दा अचम्मका मूर्तिमध्ये एक छ। एउटा लामो गहिरो कुण्डमा विष्णु भगवान् ब्रह्माण्डीय सर्पको कुण्डलीमाथि पानीमा निदाएझैँ पल्टिएका छन्। मूर्ति करिब पाँच मिटर लामो छ, एउटै कालो ढुङ्गाको टुक्राबाट कुँदिएको र नेपालको सबैभन्दा ठूलो ढुङ्गाको कुँदाइ मानिन्छ। यो १,४०० वर्षभन्दा पुरानो भएको विश्वास गरिन्छ। चारवटा हातमा विष्णुले चक्र, गदा, शङ्ख र मणि बोकेका छन्। अचम्मको कुरा, बूढानीलकण्ठ नामको अर्थ \'बूढो नीलो कण्ठ\' हो, जुन शिवको उपाधि हो, किनभने कुण्डलाई पानी दिने मूल गोसाइँकुण्डसँग जोडिएको भनिन्छ। हरेक वर्ष अक्टोबर वा नोभेम्बरको हरिबोधिनी एकादशीमा विष्णु चार महिनाको निद्राबाट ब्युँझने दिन मनाउन हजारौं तीर्थयात्री आउँछन्। शताब्दीयौंसम्म नेपालका राजाहरू एउटा भविष्यवाणीको डरले यहाँ कहिल्यै आएनन्।','राजा प्रताप मल्लले एउटा दर्शन देखेका थिए भनिन्छ: यदि उनी कहिल्यै बूढानीलकण्ठ गए भने चाँडै मर्नेछन्। त्यसपछि सुतिरहेका विष्णुलाई हेर्ने नेपालका जुनसुकै राजाको त्यही गति हुन्छ भन्ने विश्वास बस्यो। उनीपछिका शाही परिवारका सदस्यहरू त्यो भविष्यवाणीको डरले मन्दिर कहिल्यै गएनन्, यद्यपि बूढानीलकण्ठ उपत्यकाका सबैभन्दा प्रिय विष्णु मन्दिरमध्ये एक हो।','[\"सुतिरहेका विष्णुको मूर्ति करिब पाँच मिटर लामो छ र एउटै ढुङ्गाबाट कुँदिएको छ।\", \"यो करिब १३ मिटर लामो गहिरो कुण्डमा पल्टिएको छ।\", \"यो नामको अर्थ \'बूढो नीलो कण्ठ\' हो, जुन शिवको उपाधि हो।\", \"कार्तिक (अक्टोबर-नोभेम्बर) को हरिबोधिनी एकादशीमा यहाँ हजारौं भक्तजन जम्मा हुन्छन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Haribodhini Ekadashi\", \"note\": \"Thousands come for the day Vishnu is believed to wake from his four-month sleep\", \"month\": \"Kartik\", \"name_np\": \"हरिबोधिनी एकादशी\", \"note_np\": \"विष्णु चार महिनाको निद्राबाट ब्युँझने दिन मानिएको दिनमा हजारौं आउँछन्\"}, {\"name\": \"Harishayani Ekadashi\", \"note\": \"A fair marks the day Vishnu is believed to begin his four-month sleep\", \"month\": \"Ashadh\", \"name_np\": \"हरिशयनी एकादशी\", \"note_np\": \"विष्णु चार महिनाको निद्रा सुरु गर्ने दिन मानिएको दिनमा मेला लाग्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-22-gje.jpg/1280px-Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-22-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The reclining Vishnu in his pool\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-22-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-09-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-09-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Budhanilkantha Vishnu, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-09-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-01-1976-gje.jpg/1280px-Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-01-1976-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The image photographed in 1976\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-01-1976-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-23-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-23-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Budhanilkantha Vishnu, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-23-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-15-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-15-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Detail of the stone Vishnu\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budhanilkantha-Vishnu-15-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"statue\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"A 5 m black stone Vishnu reclining on a coiled many-headed serpent, lying in a 13 m rectangular sunken pool\", \"tiers\": 0, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#3a3a3a\", \"#4a6a6a\", \"#d9822b\"], \"features\": [\"idol-visible\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [13, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"pond\", \"forest\", \"garden-lawn\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(56,'bagh-bhairab-kirtipur','Bagh Bhairab Temple, Kirtipur','बाघभैरव मन्दिर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.679443,85.276464,'pagoda','Hindu','Bagh Bhairab (Bhairav as a tiger)',NULL,'16th century CE','Malla','Newar pagoda-style temple in Kirtipur\'s old town',0,'Kirtipur\'s tiger god, guarding a hilltop town that held out against the Gorkha army.','You have climbed into the old hilltop town of Kirtipur, and here stands its guardian, Bagh Bhairab, the god Bhairav in the form of a tiger. Locals call him Ajudeu, the grandfather god, and believe he protects the town. The temple dates back to the 16th century. Look at its walls: hanging here are swords said to have been used by Prithvi Narayan Shah\'s army in the Battle of Kirtipur, when the Gorkha king fought to take this town on his way to unifying Nepal. Inside, the god\'s image is made of clay, and it is renewed every twenty to thirty years, a task performed by a Bajracharya Buddhist priest. Every year, on the first day of Bhadra in mid-August, the town celebrates the Bagh Bhairab Jatra with music and a Lakhey dance. Devotees say that walking around the temple 108 times brings success and good health.','Shepherd boys grazing their sheep once modelled a tiger from clay. One boy went to find a leaf to make its tongue. When he returned, a sheep was missing and the tongueless tiger\'s mouth was open. The townsfolk believed Bhairav had entered the clay tiger, and they built a temple around it. The image of the god, it is said, still has no tongue.','[\"Bagh Bhairab is Bhairav, a form of Shiva, in the shape of a tiger.\", \"Swords said to be from the 18th-century Battle of Kirtipur are displayed on the temple.\", \"The clay image is renewed every 20–30 years by a Bajracharya priest.\", \"The Bagh Bhairab Jatra is held on the first day of Bhadra (mid-August).\"]',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Bagh_Bhairab_Temple%2C_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%98_%E0%A4%AD%E0%A5%88%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%B5_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%2C_Kirtipur%2C_Kathmandu.jpg/1280px-Bagh_Bhairab_Temple%2C_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%98_%E0%A4%AD%E0%A5%88%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%B5_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%2C_Kirtipur%2C_Kathmandu.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagh_Bhairab_Temple,_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%98_%E0%A4%AD%E0%A5%88%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%B5_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0,_Kirtipur,_Kathmandu.jpg','Shadow Ayush · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,kathmandu,legend,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagh_Bhairab_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19680989\", \"https://nepalitimes.com/the-city-of-good-deeds\", \"https://honeyguideapps.com/blog/bagh-bhairav-temple-kirtipur-nepal\"]','किर्तिपुरका बाघरूपी देवता, गोरखाली सेनाको अगाडि टिकेको डाँडाको सहरका रक्षक।','तपाईं किर्तिपुरको डाँडामाथिको पुरानो सहरमा चढ्नुभएको छ, र यहाँ यसका रक्षक बाघभैरव, बाघको रूपमा भैरव देवता, उभिएका छन्। स्थानीयहरू उनलाई अजुदेउ, अर्थात् हजुरबुबा देवता भन्छन् र सहरको रक्षा गर्छन् भन्ने विश्वास गर्छन्। मन्दिर सोह्रौं शताब्दीदेखिको हो। भित्ताहरू हेर्नुहोस्: यहाँ पृथ्वीनारायण शाहको सेनाले किर्तिपुरको युद्धमा प्रयोग गरेका भनिएका तरबार झुन्ड्याइएका छन्, जतिबेला गोरखाका राजा नेपाल एकीकरणको बाटोमा यो सहर लिन लडेका थिए। भित्र देवताको मूर्ति माटोको हो, र हरेक बीस-तीस वर्षमा यसलाई नयाँ बनाइन्छ, जुन काम वज्राचार्य बौद्ध पुजारीले गर्छन्। हरेक वर्ष भदौ पहिलो गते, अगस्टको बीचतिर, सहरले बाजा र लाखे नाचसहित बाघभैरव जात्रा मनाउँछ। भक्तजनहरू भन्छन्, मन्दिरलाई १०८ पटक परिक्रमा गर्दा सफलता र स्वास्थ्य मिल्छ।','भेडा चराइरहेका गोठालाहरूले एकपटक माटोको बाघ बनाए। एउटा केटो जिब्रो बनाउन पात खोज्न गयो। फर्किंदा एउटा भेडा हराएको थियो र जिब्रो नभएको बाघको मुख खुलेको थियो। सहरका मानिसले भैरव माटोको बाघमा पसे भन्ने विश्वास गरे र त्यसको वरिपरि मन्दिर बनाए। भनिन्छ, देवताको मूर्तिमा अझै जिब्रो छैन।','[\"बाघभैरव भनेको बाघको रूपमा शिवका रूप भैरव हुन्।\", \"अठारौं शताब्दीको किर्तिपुर युद्धका भनिएका तरबार मन्दिरमा प्रदर्शन गरिएका छन्।\", \"माटोको मूर्ति हरेक २०-३० वर्षमा वज्राचार्य पुजारीले नयाँ बनाउँछन्।\", \"बाघभैरव जात्रा भदौ पहिलो गते (अगस्टको बीच) मा हुन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Bagh Bhairab Jatra\", \"note\": \"On 1 Bhadra a new image is made and carried round town with music and a Lakhey dance\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"बाघभैरव जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"भदौ १ गते नयाँ मूर्ति बनाइन्छ र बाजा तथा लाखे नाचसहित सहरभर घुमाइन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Bagh_Bhairab_temple_in_early_morning.jpg/1280px-Bagh_Bhairab_temple_in_early_morning.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pratik Mani Gyawali\", \"caption\": \"South-east view with morning worshippers\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagh_Bhairab_temple_in_early_morning.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Bagh_Bhairab_temple_and_the_ancient_weapons.jpg/1280px-Bagh_Bhairab_temple_and_the_ancient_weapons.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pratik Mani Gyawali\", \"caption\": \"Old swords hung on the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagh_Bhairab_temple_and_the_ancient_weapons.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Bagh_Bhairab_Temple_from_back.jpg/1280px-Bagh_Bhairab_Temple_from_back.jpg\", \"author\": \"Maneesa stha\", \"caption\": \"The temple seen from behind\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagh_Bhairab_Temple_from_back.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Bagh_Bhairab_temple_at_Kirtipur_hill.jpg/1280px-Bagh_Bhairab_temple_at_Kirtipur_hill.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pratik Mani Gyawali\", \"caption\": \"Bagh Bhairab Temple on Kirtipur hill\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagh_Bhairab_temple_at_Kirtipur_hill.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Bagh_Bhairab_Temple%2C_Kirtipur_01.jpg/1280px-Bagh_Bhairab_Temple%2C_Kirtipur_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Bagh Bhairab Temple, Kirtipur\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagh_Bhairab_Temple,_Kirtipur_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Three-roofed brick pagoda whose upper walls are hung with old swords and shields, in a brick square on Kirtipur hill\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"toran\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [15, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"newar-houses\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:47'),(57,'seto-machindranath','Seto Machindranath Temple (Jana Bahal)','सेतो मछिन्द्रनाथ मन्दिर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.706686,85.310210,'pagoda','Both','Seto Machindranath (Avalokiteshvara / Karunamaya)',NULL,'Believed established c. 10th century CE; present temple Malla era','Malla','Multi-roofed Newar pagoda standing in the middle of a Buddhist bahal courtyard',0,'A hidden courtyard temple of the white Karunamaya, revered by Buddhists and Hindus alike.','Slip off busy Kel Tol, between Asan and Indra Chowk, through a gateway into a calm courtyard. In the middle stands the temple of Seto Machindranath, the White Machindranath, known to Newars as Janabaha Dyo or Karunamaya, the compassionate one. Buddhists see him as Avalokiteshvara, the bodhisattva of compassion; Hindus worship him too. The temple is believed to go back to around the 10th century. Notice the many small shrines, metal statues and prayer lamps around the courtyard, and worshippers counting beads as they pray. The deity\'s white face is repainted every year. In the bathing ceremony in winter, the image is washed with water, milk, ghee and honey, and the living goddess Kumari attends. Each spring, during Chaitra, the deity rides a towering chariot through old Kathmandu for five days, pulled by crowds through Asan, Hanuman Dhoka and Lagan. Daily rituals here start around four in the morning.','In the days of King Yaksha Malla, Yama, the god of death, came to worship at Swayambhu and was captured by the king and his tantric guru, who demanded immortality. Yama prayed to Avalokiteshvara for help. The white god rose from the water and told the king to build him a temple and pull him in a chariot each year, blessing people with happiness and long life.','[\"The deity is worshipped as Avalokiteshvara by Buddhists and revered by Hindus.\", \"His chariot procession runs for five days in the month of Chaitra.\", \"The Kumari attends the deity\'s annual bathing ritual.\", \"The courtyard was originally called Kanak Chaitya Mahavihar, after a chaitya of Kanakmuni Buddha.\"]',NULL,NULL,0,0,0,20,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Kathmandu-Janbahal-20-Seto_Machindranath-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Janbahal-20-Seto_Machindranath-2015-gje.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Janbahal-20-Seto_Machindranath-2015-gje.jpg','Gerd Eichmann · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,both,malla,kathmandu,hindu,buddhist,legend,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seto_Machindranath\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jana_bahal\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q17060445\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q23833903\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/111984917\"]','सेतो करुणामयको लुकेको चोकभित्रको मन्दिर, बौद्ध र हिन्दू दुवैले मान्ने।','भीडभाड भएको केलटोल, असन र इन्द्रचोकको बीचबाट एउटा ढोकाभित्र पसेर शान्त चोकमा पुग्नुहोस्। बीचमा सेतो मछिन्द्रनाथको मन्दिर छ, जसलाई नेवारहरू जनबहाः द्यः वा करुणामय, अर्थात् दयालु देवता भन्छन्। बौद्धहरू उनलाई करुणाका बोधिसत्व अवलोकितेश्वर मान्छन्; हिन्दूहरूले पनि पूजा गर्छन्। मन्दिर दशौं शताब्दीतिरको हो भन्ने विश्वास छ। चोकवरिपरि धेरै साना मन्दिर, धातुका मूर्ति र प्रार्थनाका बत्ती हेर्नुहोस्, अनि माला फर्काउँदै प्रार्थना गर्ने भक्तजनलाई। देवताको सेतो अनुहार हरेक वर्ष फेरि रङ्गाइन्छ। जाडोमा हुने नुहाउने अनुष्ठानमा मूर्तिलाई पानी, दूध, घिउ र मह चढाएर नुहाइन्छ, र जीवित देवी कुमारी उपस्थित हुन्छिन्। हरेक वसन्तमा, चैतमा, देवता असन, हनुमानढोका र लगनबाट पाँच दिन अग्लो रथमा चढेर पुरानो काठमाडौं घुम्छन्, भीडले तान्दै। यहाँको दैनिक पूजा बिहान चार बजेतिर सुरु हुन्छ।','राजा यक्ष मल्लको पालामा मृत्युका देवता यमराज स्वयम्भूमा पूजा गर्न आएका थिए र राजा र उनका तान्त्रिक गुरुले उनलाई बन्दी बनाएर अमरताको माग गरे। यमले अवलोकितेश्वरसँग मद्दत मागे। सेतो देवता पानीबाट उठे र राजालाई आफ्नो मन्दिर बनाउन र हरेक वर्ष रथमा तान्न भने, र मानिसलाई सुख र दीर्घायुको आशीर्वाद दिने बताए।','[\"बौद्धहरू यी देवतालाई अवलोकितेश्वरका रूपमा पूजा गर्छन्, र हिन्दूहरू पनि सम्मान गर्छन्।\", \"उनको रथयात्रा चैत महिनामा पाँच दिन चल्छ।\", \"देवताको वार्षिक स्नान अनुष्ठानमा कुमारी उपस्थित हुन्छिन्।\", \"चोकको मूल नाम कनकमुनि बुद्धको चैत्यका नाममा कनक चैत्य महाविहार थियो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Seto Machindranath Jatra\", \"note\": \"Jana Baha Dyah Jatra: a tall chariot is pulled through old Kathmandu for five days\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"सेतो मछिन्द्रनाथ जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"जनबहाः द्यःयात्रा: अग्लो रथ पाँच दिनसम्म पुरानो काठमाडौंमा तानिन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Kathmandu-Janbahal-12-Seto_Machindranath-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Janbahal-12-Seto_Machindranath-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The temple in the Jana Bahal courtyard, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Janbahal-12-Seto_Machindranath-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Kathmandu-Janbahal-06-Seto_Machindranath_innen-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Janbahal-06-Seto_Machindranath_innen-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Inside the temple courtyard, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Janbahal-06-Seto_Machindranath_innen-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Kathmandu-Janbahal-02-Seto_Machindranath-Waechterfigur-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Janbahal-02-Seto_Machindranath-Waechterfigur-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Guardian figure at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Janbahal-02-Seto_Machindranath-Waechterfigur-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Kathmandu-Janbahal-14-Seto_Machindranath-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Janbahal-14-Seto_Machindranath-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Seto Machindranath temple, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Janbahal-14-Seto_Machindranath-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Kathmandu-Janbahal-26-Seto_Machindranath-Venus-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Janbahal-26-Seto_Machindranath-Venus-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"European-style statue in the courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Janbahal-26-Seto_Machindranath-Venus-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Two gilded roofs over a brass-plated front with toranas, standing in a small courtyard crowded with chaityas and pillars\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#c9a227\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#b08d57\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"toran\", \"golden-door\", \"lion-statues\", \"chaityas\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [10, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"newar-houses\", \"market-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(58,'rani-pokhari','Rani Pokhari','रानी पोखरी','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.707847,85.315447,'pond','Hindu','Shiva (central temple)',1670,'17th century CE (1670)','Malla','Large square artificial tank with a central shikhara-style Shiva temple reached by a causeway',0,'A king\'s pond of grief, built in 1670 to console a queen who had lost her son.','In the busy heart of modern Kathmandu lies a quiet square of water: Rani Pokhari, the Queen\'s Pond. It was built in 1670 by King Pratap Malla to console his queen, who was overcome with grief after their son was trampled to death by an elephant. To make the pond holy, the king had water brought from sacred places in Nepal and India, including Gosaikunda, Muktinath, Badrinath and Kedarnath. The pond measures about 180 by 140 metres. In the middle, reached by a causeway, stands a Shiva temple, rebuilt in shikhara style. On the southern bank, look for a stone elephant carrying images of Pratap Malla and his two sons. The 2015 earthquake damaged the site, and its restoration became controversial when concrete was proposed. After protests, it was rebuilt in the traditional style, finished in 2020, and opened to the public in 2025. The central temple opens only once a year, on Bhai Tika during Tihar.',NULL,'[\"King Pratap Malla built it in 1670 for his grieving queen.\", \"Water from holy sites such as Gosaikunda and Muktinath was poured in to sanctify it.\", \"A stone elephant on the south bank carries images of Pratap Malla and his two sons.\", \"The central temple opens to the public only on Bhai Tika during Tihar.\"]','05:00','16:00',0,0,0,30,'The pond and its central temple were damaged in 2015; after a disputed restoration, traditional reconstruction finished in October 2020.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rani_Pokhari_2020-IMG_0226.jpg/1280px-Rani_Pokhari_2020-IMG_0226.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rani_Pokhari_2020-IMG_0226.jpg','Bijay Chaurasia · CC BY-SA 4.0','pond,hindu,malla,kathmandu,water,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rani_Pokhari\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5300315\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/visual-stories/2025/03/24/ranipokhari\", \"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/ranipokhari-open-to-the-public.html\"]','सन् १६७० मा छोरा गुमाएकी रानीलाई सान्त्वना दिन राजाले बनाएको शोकको पोखरी।','आधुनिक काठमाडौंको चहलपहलको बीचमा पानीको एउटा शान्त वर्गाकार ठाउँ छ: रानी पोखरी, अर्थात् रानीको पोखरी। यो सन् १६७० मा राजा प्रताप मल्लले आफ्नी रानीलाई सान्त्वना दिन बनाएका थिए, जो हात्तीले कुल्चिएर छोराको मृत्यु भएपछि शोकले विह्वल थिइन्। पोखरीलाई पवित्र बनाउन राजाले गोसाइँकुण्ड, मुक्तिनाथ, बद्रीनाथ र केदारनाथ लगायत नेपाल र भारतका पवित्र स्थानबाट पानी मगाएका थिए। पोखरी करिब १८० मिटर लामो र १४० मिटर चौडा छ। बीचमा, पुलबाट पुगिने ठाउँमा, शिखर शैलीमा फेरि बनाइएको शिव मन्दिर छ। दक्षिणी किनारमा प्रताप मल्ल र उनका दुई छोराको मूर्ति बोकेको ढुङ्गाको हात्ती खोज्नुहोस्। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले यो ठाउँमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो, र कंक्रिट प्रयोग गर्ने प्रस्ताव आएपछि यसको पुनर्स्थापना विवादित बन्यो। विरोधपछि यसलाई परम्परागत शैलीमा फेरि बनाइयो, सन् २०२० मा सकियो, र सन् २०२५ मा सर्वसाधारणका लागि खुल्यो। बीचको मन्दिर तिहारमा भाइटीकाका दिन वर्षमा एक पटक मात्र खुल्छ।',NULL,'[\"राजा प्रताप मल्लले शोकमा डुबेकी आफ्नी रानीका लागि सन् १६७० मा यो बनाएका थिए।\", \"यसलाई पवित्र बनाउन गोसाइँकुण्ड र मुक्तिनाथ जस्ता तीर्थस्थानको पानी हालिएको थियो।\", \"दक्षिणी किनारको ढुङ्गाको हात्तीमा प्रताप मल्ल र उनका दुई छोराको मूर्ति छ।\", \"बीचको मन्दिर तिहारमा भाइटीकाका दिन मात्र सर्वसाधारणका लागि खुल्छ।\"]','सन् २०१५ मा पोखरी र यसको बीचको मन्दिरमा क्षति पुग्यो; विवादित पुनर्स्थापनापछि परम्परागत पुनर्निर्माण सन् २०२० को अक्टोबरमा सकियो।','[{\"name\": \"Bhai Tika\", \"note\": \"Last day of Tihar, the only day the central temple is opened to the public\", \"month\": \"Kartik\", \"name_np\": \"भाइटीका\", \"note_np\": \"तिहारको अन्तिम दिन, बीचको मन्दिर सर्वसाधारणका लागि खुल्ने एकमात्र दिन\"}, {\"name\": \"Chhath\", \"note\": \"Devotees offer prayers to the setting and rising sun from the water’s edge\", \"month\": \"Kartik\", \"name_np\": \"छठ\", \"note_np\": \"भक्तजनहरू पानीको किनारबाट अस्ताउँदो र उदाउँदो सूर्यलाई प्रार्थना चढाउँछन्\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6b/Rani_pokhari_ca_1950.jpg\", \"author\": \"Karrattul\", \"caption\": \"Bird\'s-eye view of Rani Pokhari, around 1950\", \"license\": \"Public domain\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rani_pokhari_ca_1950.jpg\", \"license_url\": null}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/Elephant_statue_and_rest_house.jpg\", \"author\": \"Karrattul\", \"caption\": \"17th-century stone elephant and round rest house\", \"license\": \"Public domain\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elephant_statue_and_rest_house.jpg\", \"license_url\": null}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Kathmandu-Rani_Pokhari-04-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Kathmandu-Rani_Pokhari-04-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"The pond and central temple, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathmandu-Rani_Pokhari-04-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Rani_Pokhari_2020_Sept.%28Wide_view%29.jpg/1280px-Rani_Pokhari_2020_Sept.%28Wide_view%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Bhatta\", \"caption\": \"The rebuilt pond, September 2020\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rani_Pokhari_2020_Sept.(Wide_view).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Ghantaghar_and_Ranipokhari.jpg/1280px-Ghantaghar_and_Ranipokhari.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gaurav Dhwaj Khadka\", \"caption\": \"Rani Pokhari with the Ghantaghar clock tower\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghantaghar_and_Ranipokhari.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/Ranipokhari_clock_tower_1930s.jpg\", \"author\": \"Zulufive\", \"caption\": \"The pond and clock tower before the 1934 earthquake\", \"license\": \"Public domain\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ranipokhari_clock_tower_1930s.jpg\", \"license_url\": null}]','{\"kind\": \"pond\", \"roof\": \"stone-spire\", \"notes\": \"Big rectangular tank with a small white temple in the middle joined to the bank by a causeway; stone elephant on the south bank\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#4f7b6b\", \"#ecebe4\", \"#8b3a2b\"], \"features\": [\"elephant-statues\", \"fence-railing\", \"ghat-steps\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [180, 140], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"city-street\", \"garden-lawn\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(59,'dharahara','Dharahara','धरहरा','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.700545,85.312169,'tower','Secular',NULL,1832,'Original 1832; rebuilt after 1934; new tower opened 2021–2024','Shah','Minaret-style tower in Mughal and European style; rebuilt in 2018–2024 as an earthquake-resistant tower with a bronze mast',0,'Bhimsen Thapa\'s watchtower, fallen twice in earthquakes and rebuilt as a symbol of resilience.','Look up at the white minaret-like tower rising above Sundhara. This is Dharahara, first built in 1832 by Bhimsen Thapa, Nepal\'s powerful Mukhtiyar, under the commission of Queen Lalit Tripurasundari. Its style borrows from Mughal and European architecture. It served as a military watchtower: when something important happened, bugles were blown from the top to call soldiers together. The great earthquake of 1934 left only two of its nine storeys standing, and Rana prime minister Juddha Shumsher had it restored. Then, at lunchtime on 25 April 2015, the tower collapsed, leaving only its base; 180 bodies were recovered from the rubble. Nepal chose to rebuild. Construction began in 2018, the new earthquake-resistant tower was inaugurated on 24 April 2021, and it fully opened to the public on Constitution Day, 19 September 2024. Near its foot, a glass enclosure protects the remains of the old tower.',NULL,'[\"Bhimsen Thapa built the original tower in 1832 for Queen Lalit Tripurasundari.\", \"Bugles were blown from the top to summon soldiers when events of national importance occurred.\", \"The 2015 earthquake toppled the tower; 180 bodies were retrieved from its debris.\", \"The rebuilt tower fully opened to the public on 19 September 2024, Constitution Day.\"]','10:30','17:00',1000,500,200,60,'The tower collapsed on 25 April 2015 leaving only its base; a new earthquake-resistant tower was built from 2018 and fully opened in September 2024.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Dharahara_with_Mountain_Range.jpg/1280px-Dharahara_with_Mountain_Range.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dharahara_with_Mountain_Range.jpg','Safalphotos · CC BY-SA 4.0','tower,secular,shah,kathmandu,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dharahara\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5269090\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/11622074774\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/kathmandu/2024/11/24/dharahara-begins-charging-entry-fees\", \"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/dharahara-entry-fee-introduced-from-today-charges-apply-for-photography-as-well.html\", \"https://myrepublica.nagariknetwork.com/news/dharahara-generates-revenue-of-nearly-rs-50-million-11-39.html\"]','भीमसेन थापाले बनाएको निगरानी स्तम्भ, दुईपटक भूकम्पमा ढलेको, र अहिले दृढताको प्रतीकका रूपमा फेरि बनाइएको।','सुन्धाराको माथि उठेको मिनारजस्तो सेतो स्तम्भतिर हेर्नुहोस्। यो धरहरा हो, जसलाई सन् १८३२ मा नेपालका शक्तिशाली मुख्तियार भीमसेन थापाले रानी ललित त्रिपुरासुन्दरीको आदेशमा पहिलो पटक बनाएका थिए। यसको शैली मुगल र युरोपेली वास्तुकलाबाट प्रभावित छ। यो सैनिकको निगरानी स्तम्भ थियो: केही महत्त्वपूर्ण घटना हुँदा सिपाहीहरूलाई बोलाउन माथिबाट बिगुल बजाइन्थ्यो। सन् १९३४ को ठूलो भूकम्पले नौ तलामध्ये दुई तला मात्र बाँकी राख्यो, र राणा प्रधानमन्त्री जुद्ध शमशेरले त्यसलाई मर्मत गराए। त्यसपछि २५ अप्रिल २०१५ को दिउँसो खाजा खाने बेला स्तम्भ ढल्यो, आधार मात्र बाँकी रह्यो; भग्नावशेषबाट १८० शव निकालिए। नेपालले फेरि बनाउने निर्णय गर्‍यो। सन् २०१८ मा निर्माण सुरु भयो, भूकम्प-प्रतिरोधी नयाँ स्तम्भ २४ अप्रिल २०२१ मा उद्घाटन भयो, र संविधान दिवस, १९ सेप्टेम्बर २०२४ मा यो सर्वसाधारणका लागि पूर्ण रूपमा खुल्यो। यसको फेदमा पुरानो स्तम्भका अवशेष सिसाको घेराभित्र जोगाइएका छन्।',NULL,'[\"भीमसेन थापाले सन् १८३२ मा रानी ललित त्रिपुरासुन्दरीका लागि मूल स्तम्भ बनाएका थिए।\", \"राष्ट्रिय महत्त्वका घटना हुँदा सिपाहीहरूलाई बोलाउन माथिबाट बिगुल बजाइन्थ्यो।\", \"सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले स्तम्भ ढाल्यो; भग्नावशेषबाट १८० शव निकालिए।\", \"फेरि बनाइएको स्तम्भ संविधान दिवस, १९ सेप्टेम्बर २०२४ मा सर्वसाधारणका लागि पूर्ण रूपमा खुल्यो।\"]','स्तम्भ सन् २०१५ अप्रिल २५ मा ढल्यो र आधार मात्र बाँकी रह्यो; सन् २०१८ देखि भूकम्प-प्रतिरोधी नयाँ स्तम्भ बनाइयो र सेप्टेम्बर २०२४ मा पूर्ण रूपमा खुल्यो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Dharahara_2011.jpg/1280px-Dharahara_2011.jpg\", \"author\": \"Swagat Raj Pyakurel\", \"caption\": \"The old Dharahara tower in 2011\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dharahara_2011.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Bhimsen_Tower.png/1280px-Bhimsen_Tower.png\", \"author\": \"Madan Puraskar Pustakalaya\", \"caption\": \"Historic photograph of Bhimsen Tower\", \"license\": \"Public domain\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimsen_Tower.png\", \"license_url\": null}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Dharahara_after_renovation.jpeg/1280px-Dharahara_after_renovation.jpeg\", \"author\": \"Nirjal stha\", \"caption\": \"The new Dharahara after reconstruction\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dharahara_after_renovation.jpeg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Dharahara_%28Bhimsen_Stambha%29_is_a_72-metre-tall_%28236_ft%29_Tower_at_the_Centre_of_Sundhara%2CKathmandu%2CNepal_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Dharahara_%28Bhimsen_Stambha%29_is_a_72-metre-tall_%28236_ft%29_Tower_at_the_Centre_of_Sundhara%2CKathmandu%2CNepal_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Saddam Hussain Ansari\", \"caption\": \"The rebuilt 72-metre tower at Sundhara\", \"license\": \"CC BY 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dharahara_(Bhimsen_Stambha)_is_a_72-metre-tall_(236_ft)_Tower_at_the_Centre_of_Sundhara,Kathmandu,Nepal_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Dharahara_at_Night.jpg/1280px-Dharahara_at_Night.jpg\", \"author\": \"Biman Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Dharahara lit up at night\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dharahara_at_Night.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pillar\", \"roof\": \"white-dome\", \"notes\": \"Tall white minaret-style tower with a balcony near the top and a bronze mast on the roof, rebuilt next to the old stump\", \"tiers\": 22, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#f2f0ea\", \"#b08d57\", \"#9a9a9a\"], \"features\": [\"minaret-turrets\", \"arched-windows\", \"watchtower\"], \"height_m\": 72, \"footprint_m\": [20, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"city-street\", \"garden-lawn\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(60,'nuwakot-durbar','Nuwakot Durbar (Saat Tale Durbar)','नुवाकोट दरबार','Bidur','Bagmati','Nuwakot',NULL,27.913761,85.164754,'palace','Hindu',NULL,NULL,'18th century; the present palace was built after Prithvi Narayan Shah conquered Nuwakot in 1801 BS (1744-45). Wikidata gives inception c. 1750.','Shah','Seven-storey brick fort-palace with 6-foot-thick walls on an 84 x 36 ft plinth, carved Newar windows (aankhi jhyal) and a glazed-tile roof, built by craftsmen from Lalitpur in Kathmandu style. Annexes include Ranga Mahal and the Garad Ghar.',0,'Seven-storey hilltop palace that Prithvi Narayan Shah used as his base for the unification of Nepal.','You are standing on the ridge of Nuwakot, looking up at the Saat Tale Durbar, the seven-storey palace. After Prithvi Narayan Shah captured Nuwakot in 1744, he moved his capital here from Gorkha, because this ridge sits on the old trade route between the Kathmandu Valley and Tibet. Each floor had a job. Courtiers and guards waited on the ground floor, the king held meetings on the first, the royal couple slept on the second, soldiers kept watch higher up, and the fifth and sixth floors served as a prison for captured kings. Notice how thick the walls are, about six feet, more fort than home. Craftsmen from Lalitpur carved the windows you see. Look south-east to the Ranga Mahal, the old theatre hall, and east to the guard house. The 2015 earthquake badly damaged the complex, and restoration has been under way since.',NULL,'[\"Prithvi Narayan Shah moved his capital from Gorkha to Nuwakot after conquering it in 1801 BS (1744-45).\", \"The main palace has seven storeys, which is why locals call it Saat Tale (seven-storey) Durbar.\", \"Its plinth measures 84 by 36 feet and its walls are about 6 feet thick.\", \"The fifth and sixth floors were used as a prison; the King of Tanahun was held here.\", \"The palace has been on Nepal\'s UNESCO Tentative List since 2008.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,'The April 2015 earthquake devastated the palace complex; it has been under restoration since, with work slowed by the pandemic.','https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Nuwakot_Darbar_01.JPG/1280px-Nuwakot_Darbar_01.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuwakot_Darbar_01.JPG','Krish Dulal · CC BY-SA 3.0','palace,hindu,shah,bidur,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuwakot_Palace\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q24960303\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/tentativelists/5260/\", \"https://en.setopati.com/social/162959\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Nuwakot_Palace\"]','पृथ्वीनारायण शाहले नेपाल एकीकरणको आधार बनाएको डाँडाको सात तले दरबार।','तपाईं नुवाकोटको डाँडामा उभिनुभएको छ र अगाडि सात तले दरबार देख्दै हुनुहुन्छ। सन् १७४४ मा पृथ्वीनारायण शाहले नुवाकोट जितेपछि राजधानी गोरखाबाट यहीँ सारे, किनकि यो डाँडा काठमाडौँ उपत्यका र तिब्बत जोड्ने पुरानो व्यापारिक बाटोमा पर्छ। हरेक तल्लाको आफ्नै काम थियो। भुइँतल्लामा दरबारिया र पहरेदार बस्थे, पहिलो तल्लामा राजाले बैठक गर्थे, दोस्रो तल्लामा राजा-रानी सुत्थे, माथिल्ला तल्लामा सिपाहीले पहरा दिन्थे, र पाँचौँ र छैटौँ तल्ला बन्दी बनाइएका राजाहरूको कारागार थियो। भित्ता कति बाक्लो छ हेर्नुहोस्, करिब छ फिट, घरभन्दा किल्ला जस्तै। तपाईंले देखेका झ्याल ललितपुरका सिपालुले कुँदेका हुन्। दक्षिण-पूर्वमा पुरानो नाचघर रङ्गमहल र पूर्वमा पहरा घर हेर्नुहोस्। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले यो परिसरमा ठूलो क्षति पुर्‍यायो, र त्यसयता पुनर्स्थापनाको काम चलिरहेको छ।',NULL,'[\"वि.सं. १८०१ (सन् १७४४-४५) मा नुवाकोट जितेपछि पृथ्वीनारायण शाहले राजधानी गोरखाबाट यहीँ सारे।\", \"मुख्य दरबारमा सात तल्ला छन्, त्यसैले स्थानीयले यसलाई सात तले दरबार भन्छन्।\", \"जगको नाप ८४ फिट गुणा ३६ फिट छ, र भित्ता करिब ६ फिट बाक्लो छन्।\", \"पाँचौँ र छैटौँ तल्ला कारागार थिए; तनहुँका राजालाई यहीँ राखिएको थियो।\", \"सन् २००८ देखि यो दरबार नेपालको युनेस्को अस्थायी सूचीमा छ।\"]','सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पले दरबार परिसर ध्वस्त पारेको थियो। त्यसयता पुनर्स्थापना भइरहेको छ, तर महामारीले काम ढिलो भएको छ।','[{\"name\": \"Sindure Jatra\", \"note\": \"Vermilion-smeared procession from the nearby Bhairabi Temple to the Taleju temple beside the palace.\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"सिन्दूर जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"नजिकैको भैरवी मन्दिरबाट दरबार छेउको तलेजु मन्दिरसम्म सिन्दूर दलेर निकालिने जात्रा।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Saat_Talle_Durbar_view.jpg/1280px-Saat_Talle_Durbar_view.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajivkilanashrestha\", \"caption\": \"The seven-storey palace seen from the courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saat_Talle_Durbar_view.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Nuwakot_Durbar_Area.jpg/1280px-Nuwakot_Durbar_Area.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sueracepant\", \"caption\": \"Ranga Mahal and Garad Ghar in front of the palace\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuwakot_Durbar_Area.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/A_big_window_at_Sat_Talle_Durbar_-_Flickr_-_askmeaks.jpg\", \"author\": \"Abhishek Singh from Pune, India\", \"caption\": \"Large carved window of the Saat Tale Durbar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_big_window_at_Sat_Talle_Durbar_-_Flickr_-_askmeaks.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Temple_of_Taleju.jpg/1280px-Temple_of_Taleju.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajivkilanashrestha\", \"caption\": \"Taleju temple beside the palace complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Temple_of_Taleju.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Ancient_Nuwakot_bazar.jpg/1280px-Ancient_Nuwakot_bazar.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sueracepant\", \"caption\": \"Old Nuwakot bazaar with the palace rising above it\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Nuwakot_bazar.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Nuwakot_Durbar_after_Earthquake.jpg/1280px-Nuwakot_Durbar_after_Earthquake.jpg\", \"author\": \"SusantBasnet14\", \"caption\": \"The palace after the 2015 earthquake\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuwakot_Durbar_after_Earthquake.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Tall narrow seven-storey brick tower with rows of dark carved windows and a small tiled lookout room on top; small pagoda temple at its side.\", \"tiers\": 7, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#B5653F\", \"#3B2A22\", \"#8C8C8C\"], \"features\": [\"carved-windows\", \"watchtower\"], \"height_m\": 25, \"footprint_m\": [25.6, 11], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"brick-courtyard\", \"village\", \"himalaya-backdrop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(61,'bhairabi-temple-nuwakot','Bhairabi Temple, Nuwakot','भैरवी मन्दिर (नुवाकोट)','Bidur','Bagmati','Nuwakot',NULL,27.912583,85.163750,'pagoda','Hindu','Bhairavi',NULL,'18th century; sources differ, some credit Jagat Jaya Malla and others the reign of Prithvi Narayan Shah. Bahadur Shah added the copper roof in 1793.','Malla / Shah (disputed)','West-facing pagoda temple of traditional brick and carved timber with a copper roof installed in 1793. Pairs of metal and stone lions guard the main door; two female figures holding vermilion flank the main stair. Ashtamatrika sculptures are kept inside.',0,'Pagoda temple of the goddess Bhairavi just south of Nuwakot\'s seven-storey palace, home of the Sindure Jatra.','Walk about two hundred metres south of the seven-storey palace and you reach the temple of the goddess Bhairavi, consort of Bhairav. People here also call her Gandaki Bhairavi, after the Trishuli Gandaki river flowing far below. Face the main door: it opens to the west. Two pairs of lions guard it, one cast in metal and one carved in stone, and on either side of the stair stand two women with their hands full of sindur, red vermilion. That is a clue to the temple\'s great festival, the Sindure Jatra, when the crowd smears one another red. Look up at the copper roof. Bahadur Shah fixed it in 1793 and, in the same year, placed a copper plate here announcing Nepal\'s victory over Tibet and China, storing captured weapons on the upper floor. The 2015 earthquake devastated this temple, and you are seeing it after restoration finished in August 2020.','The temple\'s priest, called the Dhami, was traditionally forbidden to cross the Trishuli and Tadi rivers without the king\'s permission; when he dies, his eldest son takes his place.','[\"The temple lies about 200 m south of the seven-storey Nuwakot Palace.\", \"In 1793 Bahadur Shah installed a copper plate here declaring Nepal\'s victory in the Sino-Nepalese War, and stored captured weapons on the second storey.\", \"The current copper roof was installed by Bahadur Shah in 1793.\", \"The main door faces west and is guarded by a metal pair and a stone pair of lions.\", \"Devastated by the April 2015 earthquake, the temple was restored in August 2020.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,'The April 2015 earthquake devastated the temple; restoration was completed in August 2020.','https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Pray_Nuwakot.jpg/1280px-Pray_Nuwakot.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pray_Nuwakot.jpg','Sueracepant · CC BY-SA 3.0','pagoda,hindu,malla / shah (disputed),bidur,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhairabi_Temple,_Nuwakot\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q106506210\", \"https://en.setopati.com/social/162959\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/nuwakot/attractions/bhairabi-temple/a/poi-sig/1505871/1317534\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Bhairabi_Temple,_Nuwakot\"]','नुवाकोटको सात तले दरबारको ठीक दक्षिणमा रहेको भैरवी देवीको पगोडा मन्दिर, सिन्दुरे जात्राको थलो।','सात तले दरबारबाट करिब दुई सय मिटर दक्षिणतिर हिँड्नुभयो भने भैरवकी शक्ति भैरवी देवीको मन्दिरमा पुग्नुहुन्छ। धेरै तल बग्ने त्रिशूली गण्डकी नदीका नाममा यहाँका मानिसले उनलाई गण्डकी भैरवी पनि भन्छन्। मुख्य ढोकातिर हेर्नुहोस्, त्यो पश्चिमतिर खुल्छ। ढोकाको रक्षा दुई जोडी सिंहले गर्छन्, एक जोडी धातुको र अर्को जोडी ढुङ्गाको। सिँढीको दुवैतिर सिन्दूर बोकेका दुई महिलाको मूर्ति छन्। यो मन्दिरको ठूलो पर्व सिन्दुरे जात्राको सङ्केत हो, जब भीडले एकअर्कालाई रातो सिन्दूरले रङ्ग्याउँछ। माथि तामाको छानातिर हेर्नुहोस्। बहादुर शाहले सन् १७९३ मा यो छाना हालेका थिए। त्यही वर्ष उनले तिब्बत र चीनमाथि नेपालको विजय घोषणा गर्ने तामाको पाता यहाँ राखे, र कब्जा गरेका हतियार माथिल्लो तल्लामा भण्डारण गरे। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले यो मन्दिर ध्वस्त पार्‍यो। तपाईंले अहिले हेरिरहेको मन्दिर सन् २०२० अगस्टमा पुनर्स्थापना सकिएपछिको हो।','यस मन्दिरका पुजारीलाई धामी भनिन्छ। परम्परा अनुसार राजाको अनुमति नलिई उनले त्रिशूली र ताडी नदी तर्न पाउँदैनथे। उनको मृत्यु भएपछि जेठो छोराले उनको ठाउँ लिन्छ।','[\"मन्दिर सात तले नुवाकोट दरबारबाट करिब २०० मिटर दक्षिणमा छ।\", \"सन् १७९३ मा बहादुर शाहले यहाँ नेपाल-चीन युद्धमा नेपालको विजय घोषणा गर्ने तामाको पाता राखे, र कब्जा गरेका हतियार दोस्रो तल्लामा भण्डारण गरे।\", \"अहिलेको तामाको छाना बहादुर शाहले सन् १७९३ मा राखेका हुन्।\", \"मुख्य ढोका पश्चिमतिर फर्केको छ र धातुको एक जोडी तथा ढुङ्गाको एक जोडी सिंहले त्यसको रक्षा गर्छन्।\", \"सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पले ध्वस्त भएको मन्दिर सन् २०२० अगस्टमा पुनर्स्थापना गरियो।\"]','सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पले मन्दिर ध्वस्त पार्‍यो। पुनर्स्थापना सन् २०२० अगस्टमा सकियो।','[{\"name\": \"Sindure Jatra (Bhairavi Jatra)\", \"note\": \"Procession to the Taleju temple in which participants smear each other with vermilion; animal sacrifices are offered.\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"सिन्दुरे जात्रा (भैरवी जात्रा)\", \"note_np\": \"तलेजु मन्दिरसम्म जुलुस निस्कन्छ, जसमा सहभागीले एकअर्कालाई सिन्दूर दल्छन्। पशुबलि पनि चढाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/The_Barahi_temple_-_Flickr_-_askmeaks.jpg\", \"author\": \"Abhishek Singh from Pune, India\", \"caption\": \"The Bhairabi (Barahi) temple and its roof struts\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Barahi_temple_-_Flickr_-_askmeaks.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Vairab_mandira%2Cnuwakot.JPG\", \"author\": \"Sunil Dongol\", \"caption\": \"Bhairabi Temple on the east side of the palace area\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vairab_mandira,nuwakot.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Nuwakot_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Nuwakot_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Arksarkar\", \"caption\": \"Nuwakot Durbar Square around the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuwakot_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4d/Way_to_Barahi_Temple_-_Flickr_-_askmeaks.jpg\", \"author\": \"Abhishek Singh from Pune, India\", \"caption\": \"Lane leading up to the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Way_to_Barahi_Temple_-_Flickr_-_askmeaks.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Squat two-roof pagoda with wide dark eaves edged in red, gilded finial, and lion pairs on a low walled courtyard.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#7A4A32\", \"#B23A2A\", \"#C9A227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"lion-statues\", \"guardian-pairs-on-stairs\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": 12, \"footprint_m\": [10, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"brick-courtyard\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(62,'gosaikunda','Gosaikunda','गोसाइँकुण्ड','Dhunche','Bagmati','Rasuwa',NULL,28.082750,85.413611,'lake-shrine','Hindu','Shiva',NULL,'Natural alpine lake revered since ancient times; the Gosaikunda lake complex was designated a Ramsar wetland on 29 September 2007.','unknown','Glacial lake of 13.8 ha at 4,380 m in Langtang National Park, one of a group of lakes covering 1,030 ha. Small stone shrines and cairns stand on its shore; it is frozen for about six months a year.',0,'Sacred high-altitude lake at 4,380 m, said to have been made by Shiva\'s trident, where thousands bathe at Janai Purnima.','Catch your breath. You are at 4,380 metres, beside the sacred lake of Gosaikunda in Langtang National Park. Hindus say that when the gods churned the ocean, Shiva swallowed a deadly poison to save the world. His throat burned, so he thrust his trident into this mountainside, and cold water gushed out to form the lake in front of you. Look at the stillness of the water and the bare rock around it. For roughly six months each winter the surface freezes solid. In August, on the full moon of Janai Purnima, the shore fills with thousands of pilgrims who walk two or three days up from Dhunche to bathe here and carry the water home. Down in Patan, people believe the pond at Kumbheshwar is fed by this same lake. Since 2007 the lakes around you have been protected as a Ramsar wetland of international importance.','During the churning of the ocean (Samudra Manthan) Shiva swallowed poison; to cool his burning throat he struck the mountain with his trident, and the water that sprang out formed Gosaikunda.','[\"The lake lies at 4,380 m and has a surface area of 13.8 ha.\", \"The Gosaikunda lake complex, 1,030 ha in size, was designated a Ramsar site on 29 September 2007.\", \"The lake stays frozen for about six months in winter.\", \"Legend says the spring feeding the Kumbheshwar pond in Patan is connected to Gosaikunda.\", \"Among Newars the lake is called Silu, the subject of a well-known song and film.\"]',NULL,NULL,3000,1500,0,120,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Gosaikund-lake.JPG/1280px-Gosaikund-lake.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gosaikund-lake.JPG','Nischitbaral · CC BY-SA 4.0','lake-shrine,hindu,dhunche,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gosaikunda\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2565308\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/nepal/10000-visit-gosainkunda-this-year-on-janai-purnima-festival\", \"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/seeking-holy-water-in-nepals-himalayas.html\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/permit-entry-fees-national-parks.html\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Gosainkunda_Lake\"]','४,३८० मिटरको उचाइमा रहेको पवित्र हिमाली ताल, शिवको त्रिशूलले बनाएको भनिने, जहाँ जनै पूर्णिमामा हजारौँ मानिस नुहाउँछन्।','एकछिन सास फेर्नुहोस्। तपाईं लाङटाङ राष्ट्रिय निकुञ्जभित्र ४,३८० मिटरको उचाइमा पवित्र ताल गोसाइँकुण्डको छेउमा हुनुहुन्छ। हिन्दूहरू भन्छन्, देवताहरूले समुद्र मन्थन गर्दा शिवले संसार बचाउन भयानक विष पिए। उनको घाँटी पोल्यो, त्यसैले उनले यही पहाडमा त्रिशूल रोपे, र चिसो पानी फुत्किएर तपाईंको अगाडिको ताल बन्यो। पानी कति शान्त छ र वरिपरि कस्तो नाङ्गो चट्टान छ, हेर्नुहोस्। हरेक जाडोमा करिब छ महिना यसको सतह पूरै जम्छ। अगस्टमा, जनै पूर्णिमाको दिन धुन्चेबाट दुई-तीन दिन हिँडेर आएका हजारौँ तीर्थयात्रीले यसको किनार भरिन्छ। उनीहरू यहाँ नुहाउँछन् र पानी घर लैजान्छन्। तल पाटनमा कुम्भेश्वरको पोखरीमा पानी यही तालबाट आउँछ भन्ने विश्वास छ। सन् २००७ देखि तपाईंवरिपरिका तालहरू अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय महत्त्वको रामसार सिमसारका रूपमा संरक्षित छन्।','समुद्र मन्थनका बेला शिवले विष पिए। पोलिरहेको घाँटी चिसो पार्न उनले त्रिशूलले पहाडमा प्रहार गरे, र त्यहाँबाट निस्केको पानीले गोसाइँकुण्ड बन्यो।','[\"ताल ४,३८० मिटरको उचाइमा छ र यसको सतह १३.८ हेक्टर क्षेत्रफलमा फैलिएको छ।\", \"१,०३० हेक्टरको गोसाइँकुण्ड ताल क्षेत्र सन् २००७ सेप्टेम्बर २९ मा रामसार स्थल घोषित भयो।\", \"जाडोमा ताल करिब छ महिना जमेको हुन्छ।\", \"पाटनको कुम्भेश्वर पोखरीमा पानी दिने मुहान गोसाइँकुण्डसँग जोडिएको छ भन्ने किंवदन्ती छ।\", \"नेवारहरूले यस ताललाई सिलु भन्छन्, जुन एउटा चर्चित गीत र चलचित्रको विषय हो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Janai Purnima\", \"note\": \"Around 10,000 pilgrims bathe in the lake on the Shrawan full moon and take its water home.\", \"month\": \"Shrawan\", \"name_np\": \"जनै पूर्णिमा\", \"note_np\": \"श्रावणको पूर्णिमामा करिब १०,००० तीर्थयात्री तालमा नुहाउँछन् र त्यसको पानी घर लैजान्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Clouds_over_the_sacred_lake_Gosaikunda.jpg/1280px-Clouds_over_the_sacred_lake_Gosaikunda.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ravi Mulmi\", \"caption\": \"Clouds drifting over the sacred lake\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clouds_over_the_sacred_lake_Gosaikunda.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Frozen_Gosaikund.jpg/1280px-Frozen_Gosaikund.jpg\", \"author\": \"AjayKumarShrestha\", \"caption\": \"Gosaikunda frozen in winter\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frozen_Gosaikund.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Water_cairns%2C_Gosaikunda_%284934408014%29.jpg/1280px-Water_cairns%2C_Gosaikunda_%284934408014%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Felix Dance\", \"caption\": \"Stone cairns standing in the water\", \"license\": \"CC BY 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Water_cairns,_Gosaikunda_(4934408014).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Gosai_Kunda.jpg/1280px-Gosai_Kunda.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sunderkri\", \"caption\": \"The lake and surrounding slopes\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gosai_Kunda.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/BhairavKunda.jpg/1280px-BhairavKunda.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nishan Pandit\", \"caption\": \"Bhairav Kunda, one of the neighbouring lakes\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BhairavKunda.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Gosaikunda_001.jpg/1280px-Gosaikunda_001.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Wide view of the lake basin\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gosaikunda_001.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pond\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Dark still lake in a bowl of bare grey rock and snow, with small stone cairns and a tiny shrine on the shore.\", \"tiers\": 0, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#3E5566\", \"#E8ECEF\", \"#6B6B6B\"], \"features\": [\"rock-face\"], \"height_m\": 0, \"footprint_m\": [500, 300], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"lake\", \"snow-peaks\", \"himalaya-backdrop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(63,'dolakha-bhimsen-temple','Dolakha Bhimsen Temple','दोलखा भीमसेन मन्दिर','Dolakha (Bhimeshwor Municipality)','Bagmati','Dolakha',NULL,27.649000,86.089200,'courtyard','Hindu','Bhimsen (Bhimeshwor / Bhindyo)',NULL,'Founding date unknown; an inscription dated 1611 AD records a renovation of the temple.','unknown','Roofless shrine: the triangular black stone idol sits open to the sky inside a walled brick-and-stone enclosure entered through a metal grille gate flanked by stone guardian figures, with a tall pillar topped by a statue rising behind the gate.',0,'Roofless Newar shrine in old Dolakha bazaar whose triangular stone idol of Bhimsen is said to sweat before national disasters.','Step through the grille gate in old Dolakha bazaar and look up: there is no roof. The idol of Bhimsen, called Bhindyo by the Newars of this town, sits open to the sky, a triangular block of black stone. Traders pray to him for good business, and around five thousand people come every week. Devotees say the stone shows three faces in a day: Bhimeshwor in the morning, Mahadev through the day and Narayan in the evening. Local legend says twelve porters once built a cooking fire against this stone; their rice would not cook, and when one hit the stone with his ladle, it bled milk mixed with blood. The idol is famous for sweating. Drops reportedly appeared before the 1934 earthquake and before the 2001 royal massacre, and the priest would soak the sweat in cotton and send it to the palace, which replied with offerings to turn away misfortune.','Twelve porters used the triangular stone as part of their cooking stove. Their rice stayed raw where it touched the stone; one porter struck it with his ladle, the stone cracked and bled blood-coated milk, and they realised it was Bhimsen.','[\"The temple is roofless; the triangular stone idol stands open to the sky.\", \"An inscription dated 1611 AD records a renovation of the temple; its founding date is unknown.\", \"The idol is believed to appear as Bhimeshwor in the morning, Mahadev by day and Narayan in the evening.\", \"Sweating of the idol is read as a bad omen; it was reported in 1934, before the 2001 royal massacre and on 20 February 2020.\", \"The temple draws around 5,000 worshippers every week.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Dolakha_Bhimsen.jpg/1280px-Dolakha_Bhimsen.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dolakha_Bhimsen.jpg','Shadow Ayush · CC BY-SA 4.0','courtyard,hindu,dolakha (bhimeshwor municipality),legend,palace,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolakha_Bhimsen_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19679215\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/kathmandu/atonement-worship-bhimeshwor-temple-prasad-sent-prez\", \"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/the-legendary-khadga-jatra-of-dolakha.html\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Bhimeshwar_Temple\"]','पुरानो दोलखा बजारको छाना नभएको नेवारी मन्दिर, जहाँको त्रिकोणाकार ढुङ्गाको भीमसेनले राष्ट्रिय विपत्तिअघि पसिना आउँछ भनिन्छ।','पुरानो दोलखा बजारको जालीदार ढोकाबाट भित्र पस्नुहोस् र माथि हेर्नुहोस्। छाना छैन। यहाँका नेवारले भिन्द्यो भन्ने भीमसेनको मूर्ति कालो ढुङ्गाको त्रिकोणाकार डल्लो हो, र त्यो खुला आकाशमुनि बसेको छ। व्यापारीहरू राम्रो व्यापारको प्रार्थना गर्छन्, र हरेक हप्ता करिब पाँच हजार मानिस आउँछन्। भक्तजन भन्छन्, यो ढुङ्गाले एकै दिनमा तीन रूप देखाउँछ: बिहान भीमेश्वर, दिनभर महादेव र साँझ नारायण। स्थानीय कथा अनुसार एकपटक बाह्र जना भरियाले यही ढुङ्गाको सहारा लिएर खाना पकाउन आगो बालेका थिए। उनीहरूको भात पाकेन। एकजनाले डाडुले ढुङ्गामा हिर्काउँदा त्यसबाट रगत मिसिएको दूध बग्यो। यो मूर्ति पसिना आउने भनेर प्रसिद्ध छ। सन् १९३४ को भूकम्प र सन् २००१ को शाही हत्याकाण्डअघि थोपा देखिएको भनिन्छ। पुजारीले पसिना कपासमा सोसेर दरबारमा पठाउँथे, र दरबारले दुर्भाग्य टार्न भेटीसहित जवाफ पठाउँथ्यो।','बाह्र जना भरियाले त्रिकोणाकार ढुङ्गालाई चुलोको एक भाग बनाए। ढुङ्गा छोएको ठाउँमा उनीहरूको भात काँचै रह्यो। एकजना भरियाले डाडुले हिर्काउँदा ढुङ्गा चर्कियो र रगतले मिसिएको दूध बग्यो। तब उनीहरूले बुझे, त्यो त भीमसेन रहेछ।','[\"मन्दिरमा छाना छैन, त्रिकोणाकार ढुङ्गाको मूर्ति खुला आकाशमुनि छ।\", \"सन् १६११ को एउटा शिलालेखमा मन्दिर मर्मत गरेको उल्लेख छ। मन्दिर कहिले बनेको हो, थाहा छैन।\", \"मूर्ति बिहान भीमेश्वर, दिनमा महादेव र साँझ नारायणको रूपमा देखिन्छ भन्ने विश्वास छ।\", \"मूर्तिले पसिना आउनु अशुभ मानिन्छ। सन् १९३४ मा, सन् २००१ को शाही हत्याकाण्डअघि र २०२० फेब्रुअरी २० मा पसिना आएको बताइएको थियो।\", \"मन्दिरमा हरेक हप्ता करिब ५,००० भक्तजन आउँछन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain (Khadga Jatra)\", \"note\": \"Dolakha\'s Dashain begins with puja at the Bhimeshwor temple, followed by the town\'s sword (Khadga) procession.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ (खड्गजात्रा)\", \"note_np\": \"दोलखाको दशैँ भीमेश्वर मन्दिरमा पूजाबाट सुरु हुन्छ, त्यसपछि सहरमा खड्गजात्रा निस्कन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Dolakha_bhimsen_Temple.jpg/1280px-Dolakha_bhimsen_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Krish Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Entrance gate with stone guardians and bells\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dolakha_bhimsen_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Bhimeshwor_Dolakha1.JPG/1280px-Bhimeshwor_Dolakha1.JPG\", \"author\": \"Ganesh Paudel\", \"caption\": \"The temple enclosure walls seen from below\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimeshwor_Dolakha1.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Bhimeshwor_1.JPG/1280px-Bhimeshwor_1.JPG\", \"author\": \"Nawaraj Ghimire\", \"caption\": \"The idol of Bhimeshwor\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimeshwor_1.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Bhimeswar_temple_periphery.JPG/1280px-Bhimeswar_temple_periphery.JPG\", \"author\": \"Suresh Uprety\", \"caption\": \"Devotees in the temple periphery\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimeswar_temple_periphery.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Bhimeshwor_Dolakha2.JPG/1280px-Bhimeshwor_Dolakha2.JPG\", \"author\": \"Ganesh Paudel\", \"caption\": \"Stone steps and lane in old Dolakha bazaar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimeshwor_Dolakha2.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Open-roofed walled brick enclosure with a grille gate guarded by two stone figures and a tall pillar with a statue on top.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#A0472F\", \"#3A2E28\", \"#C9A227\"], \"features\": [\"stone-pillar\", \"bell\", \"guardian-pairs-on-stairs\", \"idol-visible\", \"prayer-flags\"], \"height_m\": 6, \"footprint_m\": [15, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"newar-houses\", \"market-houses\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(64,'kalinchowk-bhagawati','Kalinchowk Bhagawati Temple','कालिञ्चोक भगवती','Kuri (Kalinchowk Rural Municipality)','Bagmati','Dolakha',NULL,27.757778,86.041389,'sculpture','Hindu','Bhagawati (Kalinchowk Bhagawati)',NULL,'Founding date not documented in the sources consulted; a cable car from Kuri village was added in 2018.','unknown','Open-air summit shrine at 3,842 m: a small low enclosure crowded with iron tridents, bells and layers of prayer flags and cloth offerings, with a holy pond inside the temple area. Reached by stone steps from Kuri village or by cable car.',0,'Hilltop shrine of the goddess Bhagawati at 3,842 m in Dolakha, crowded with tridents, bells and prayer flags.','You are standing at 3,842 metres, on the summit of Kalinchowk in Dolakha, and the shrine of the goddess Bhagawati is right in front of you. There is no grand building here. Instead, look at the forest of black iron tridents, the bells, and the thick layers of red, yellow and blue flags that devotees have tied around the goddess. This hilltop lies in the Gaurishankar Conservation Area, near the sources of the Sun Koshi and Tamakoshi rivers. For generations pilgrims climbed up from Kuri village on foot, an hour and a half of stone steps. Since 2018 a cable car does the climb in minutes, and in winter the slopes turn white and people come to play in the snow. On a clear day, turn around: the snow peaks of Gaurishankar and the Jugal and Ganesh ranges line the horizon. At Dashain and Janai Purnima the summit is packed with worshippers.',NULL,'[\"The shrine stands at 3,842 m in ward 1 of Kalinchowk Rural Municipality, Dolakha.\", \"It lies in the Gaurishankar Conservation Area, near where the Sun Koshi and Tamakoshi rivers are sourced.\", \"A cable car from Kuri village opened in 2018; walking up takes about an hour and a half.\", \"In winter the area is popular for snow, skiing and views of Gaurishankar, Jugal and Ganesh Himal.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kalinchowk_Bhagawati_temple.jpg/1280px-Kalinchowk_Bhagawati_temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalinchowk_Bhagawati_temple.jpg','Janak Bhatta · CC BY-SA 4.0','sculpture,hindu,kuri (kalinchowk rural municipality),water,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalinchowk_Bhagwati_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13357831\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/kalinchowk-dolakha-a-himalayan-escape-of-snow-spirituality-and-scenic-beauty\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Kalinchowk_Bhagwati_Shrine\"]','दोलखाको ३,८४२ मिटरको उचाइमा रहेको भगवती देवीको डाँडाको मन्दिर, त्रिशूल, घण्ट र प्रार्थना ध्वजाले भरिएको।','तपाईं दोलखाको कालिञ्चोकको शिखरमा ३,८४२ मिटरको उचाइमा हुनुहुन्छ, र भगवती देवीको मन्दिर ठीक तपाईंको अगाडि छ। यहाँ कुनै भव्य भवन छैन। बरु कालो फलामका त्रिशूलको जङ्गल, घण्ट, र भक्तजनले देवीको वरिपरि बाँधेका रातो, पहेँलो र निलो झन्डाका बाक्ला तह हेर्नुहोस्। यो डाँडा गौरीशङ्कर संरक्षण क्षेत्रमा पर्छ, सुनकोशी र तामाकोशी नदीको मुहान नजिकै। पुस्तौँदेखि तीर्थयात्री कुरी गाउँबाट ढुङ्गाका भर्‍याङ चढ्दै पैदल आउँथे, जसमा डेढ घण्टा लाग्थ्यो। सन् २०१८ देखि केबल कारले त्यो बाटो केही मिनेटमै पुर्‍याउँछ। जाडोमा भिरालो सेतो हुन्छ र मानिस हिउँमा खेल्न आउँछन्। मौसम खुला छ भने पछाडि फर्केर हेर्नुहोस्: गौरीशङ्कर, जुगल र गणेश हिमालका हिउँले ढाकिएका चुचुरा क्षितिजमा लहरै देखिन्छन्। दशैँ र जनै पूर्णिमामा शिखर भक्तजनले भरिन्छ।',NULL,'[\"मन्दिर दोलखाको कालिञ्चोक गाउँपालिका वडा १ मा ३,८४२ मिटरको उचाइमा छ।\", \"यो गौरीशङ्कर संरक्षण क्षेत्रमा पर्छ, जहाँ सुनकोशी र तामाकोशी नदीको मुहान नजिकै छ।\", \"कुरी गाउँबाट केबल कार सन् २०१८ मा सुरु भयो। हिँडेर चढ्दा करिब डेढ घण्टा लाग्छ।\", \"जाडोमा यो ठाउँ हिउँ, स्कीइङ र गौरीशङ्कर, जुगल र गणेश हिमालको दृश्यका लागि लोकप्रिय छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"The summit is especially crowded with pilgrims during Dashain.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दशैँमा शिखरमा तीर्थयात्रीको विशेष भीड हुन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Janai Purnima\", \"note\": \"Pilgrims from across Nepal climb to the shrine at Janai Purnima.\", \"month\": \"Shrawan\", \"name_np\": \"जनै पूर्णिमा\", \"note_np\": \"जनै पूर्णिमामा देशभरिका तीर्थयात्री मन्दिर चढ्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Kalinchowk_Bhagawati_temple2.jpg/1280px-Kalinchowk_Bhagawati_temple2.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Bhatta\", \"caption\": \"Holy bell at the shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalinchowk_Bhagawati_temple2.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Holy_Pond_inside_the_Kalinchwok_Temple.jpg/1280px-Holy_Pond_inside_the_Kalinchwok_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Saroj Pandey\", \"caption\": \"Holy pond inside the temple area\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holy_Pond_inside_the_Kalinchwok_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Kalinchok_climbing_steps2.JPG/1280px-Kalinchok_climbing_steps2.JPG\", \"author\": \"Ganesh Paudel\", \"caption\": \"Stone steps climbing from Kuri Bazaar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalinchok_climbing_steps2.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Kalinchok2.JPG/1280px-Kalinchok2.JPG\", \"author\": \"Ganesh Paudel\", \"caption\": \"Himalayan range seen from Kalinchowk\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalinchok2.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Kalinchowk_Bhagwati_Shrine.JPG/1280px-Kalinchowk_Bhagwati_Shrine.JPG\", \"author\": \"Nikesh balami\", \"caption\": \"The summit shrine area\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalinchowk_Bhagwati_Shrine.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"statue\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Tiny open shrine buried under layered red, yellow and blue cloth with tall black iron tridents sticking up, on a bare rocky summit.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#C0392B\", \"#F1C40F\", \"#2E86C1\"], \"features\": [\"trident\", \"bell\", \"prayer-flags\", \"flags-red\", \"rock-face\"], \"height_m\": 4, \"footprint_m\": [6, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"snow-peaks\", \"himalaya-backdrop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(65,'namobuddha','Namo Buddha Stupa','नमोबुद्ध स्तूप','Namobuddha','Bagmati','Kavrepalanchok',NULL,27.573236,85.582567,'stupa','Buddhist','Shakyamuni Buddha (as Prince Mahasattva)',NULL,'Date of construction not documented in the sources consulted; the stupa is said to hold the bone relics of Prince Mahasattva, an earlier incarnation of the Buddha.','unknown','Whitewashed dome stupa on a square stepped base with a gilded spire and Buddha eyes, surrounded by smaller white chaityas and strings of prayer flags. A stairway leads up to the Thrangu Tashi Yangtse (Namo Buddha) Monastery on the hilltop.',0,'Stupa marking where a prince, an earlier life of the Buddha, gave his body to feed a starving tigress and her cubs.','You are at Namo Buddha, 52 kilometres south-east of Kathmandu, and this white stupa holds one of the most moving stories in Buddhism. Long ago, a prince named Mahasattva, an earlier life of the Buddha, walked these hills with his brothers. They came upon a tigress so weak from hunger that she could not feed her cubs. Out of compassion, the prince offered his own body so they could live. The stupa in front of you is said to hold his bone relics, and the name means homage to the Buddha. Walk clockwise around it under the prayer flags, past the smaller white chaityas. Then climb the stairway into the woods. Up there, beside the large Thrangu Tashi Yangtse monastery, is the spot where the prince is said to have been eaten, with a carving of the tigress and her cubs. Pilgrims of every Tibetan Buddhist tradition still come here.','Prince Mahasattva, an earlier incarnation of Shakyamuni Buddha, found a starving tigress unable to feed her cubs and gave his own body to save them; the stupa is said to enshrine his bone relics.','[\"Namo Buddha lies about 52 km south-east of Kathmandu in Kavrepalanchok District.\", \"The stupa is said to house the bone relics of Prince Mahasattva.\", \"It is considered one of the three most important stupas and pilgrimage sites around the Kathmandu Valley.\", \"The Karma Kagyu Thrangu Tashi Yangtse Monastery stands on the hill above the stupa.\", \"In Tibetan the site is called Takmo Lujin, meaning \'tigress body-gift\'.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/NamobuddhaStupa.jpg/1280px-NamobuddhaStupa.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NamobuddhaStupa.jpg','Prasanna Bajracharya · CC BY-SA 4.0','stupa,buddhist,namobuddha,legend,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Namo_Buddha\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thrangu_Tashi_Yangtse_Monastery,_Nepal\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/553340076\", \"https://www.voatibetan.com/a/2145831.html\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NamobuddhaStupa.jpg\"]','भोकले कमजोर बाघिनी र उनका बच्चालाई आफ्नो शरीर दिने राजकुमारको सम्झनामा बनेको स्तूप। ती राजकुमार बुद्धका पूर्वजन्म थिए।','तपाईं काठमाडौँबाट ५२ किलोमिटर दक्षिण-पूर्वमा रहेको नमोबुद्धमा हुनुहुन्छ। यो सेतो स्तूपले बौद्ध धर्मको सबैभन्दा मार्मिक कथाहरूमध्ये एउटा बोकेको छ। धेरै पहिले महासत्त्व नाम गरेका एक राजकुमार, जो बुद्धका पूर्वजन्म थिए, आफ्ना दाजुभाइसँग यी डाँडामा घुम्दै थिए। उनीहरूले एउटी बाघिनी भेटे। ऊ भोकले यति कमजोर थिई कि आफ्ना बच्चालाई दूध खुवाउन सक्दैनथी। दयाले गर्दा राजकुमारले आफ्नो शरीर अर्पण गरे, ताकि तिनीहरू बाँच्न सकून्। तपाईंको अगाडिको स्तूपमा उनका अस्थि अवशेष छन् भनिन्छ, र नामको अर्थ बुद्धलाई नमन हो। प्रार्थना ध्वजामुनि साना सेता चैत्य नाघ्दै स्तूपलाई घडीको दिशामा घुम्नुहोस्। त्यसपछि सिँढी चढेर जङ्गलतिर जानुहोस्। माथि ठूलो थ्राङ्गु ताशी याङ्त्से गुम्बाको छेउमा राजकुमारलाई बाघिनीले खाएको ठाउँ भनिन्छ, जहाँ बाघिनी र उनका बच्चाको कुँदाइ छ। तिब्बती बौद्ध धर्मका सबै परम्पराका तीर्थयात्री अहिले पनि यहाँ आउँछन्।','शाक्यमुनि बुद्धको पूर्वजन्मका राजकुमार महासत्त्वले बच्चालाई खुवाउन नसक्ने भोकी बाघिनी भेटे, र तिनीहरूलाई बचाउन आफ्नो शरीर दिए। स्तूपमा उनका अस्थि अवशेष राखिएको भनिन्छ।','[\"नमोबुद्ध काठमाडौँबाट करिब ५२ किलोमिटर दक्षिण-पूर्व, काभ्रेपलाञ्चोक जिल्लामा छ।\", \"स्तूपमा राजकुमार महासत्त्वका अस्थि अवशेष छन् भनिन्छ।\", \"यो काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाआसपासका तीन सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण स्तूप र तीर्थस्थलमध्ये एक मानिन्छ।\", \"कर्मा कग्यु परम्पराको थ्राङ्गु ताशी याङ्त्से गुम्बा स्तूपमाथिको डाँडामा छ।\", \"तिब्बती भाषामा यो ठाउँलाई टक्मो लुजिन भनिन्छ, जसको अर्थ \'बाघिनीलाई शरीर दान\' हो।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Namura_stupa.jpg/1280px-Namura_stupa.jpg\", \"author\": \"Kamal Ratna Tuladhar\", \"caption\": \"Main stupa of Namura with smaller stupas around it\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namura_stupa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Namo_Buddha-IMG_6397.jpg/1280px-Namo_Buddha-IMG_6397.jpg\", \"author\": \"Wang Lama Humla\", \"caption\": \"Stupas and prayer flags on the hill\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namo_Buddha-IMG_6397.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Namobuddha_feeding_tigers.jpg/1280px-Namobuddha_feeding_tigers.jpg\", \"author\": \"Lusifor ,manoj shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Carving of the prince feeding the tigress and cubs\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namobuddha_feeding_tigers.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Namobuddha_main_hall.jpg/1280px-Namobuddha_main_hall.jpg\", \"author\": \"Lusifor ,manoj shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Main prayer hall of the monastery\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namobuddha_main_hall.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Namobuddha_Stupa%2C_Namobuddha.jpg/1280px-Namobuddha_Stupa%2C_Namobuddha.jpg\", \"author\": \"Creepanta\", \"caption\": \"The stupa and its surroundings\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namobuddha_Stupa,_Namobuddha.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"stupa\", \"roof\": \"white-dome\", \"notes\": \"White dome on a square railed base with a gilded spire, prayer flags strung radially from the top, and a row of small white chaityas beside it.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#F4F4F2\", \"#C9A227\", \"#B03A2E\"], \"features\": [\"dome-white\", \"harmika\", \"buddha-eyes\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"prayer-flags\", \"chaityas\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 12, \"footprint_m\": [14, 14], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\", \"monks-houses\", \"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(66,'indreshwar-mahadev-panauti','Indreshwar Mahadev Temple','इन्द्रेश्वर महादेव मन्दिर','Panauti','Bagmati','Kavrepalanchok',NULL,27.585253,85.517566,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva (Indreshwar Mahadev)',1294,'First built over a lingam in 1294, often called the oldest surviving temple in Nepal; Lonely Planet notes the present shrine dates mainly from the 15th century.','unknown','Three-tiered Newar pagoda of brick and carved timber on a stepped stone plinth, one of the largest and tallest pagoda temples in Nepal. The roof struts of the two lower storeys carry fine woodcarving, and the upper section is hung with pots and pans offered by newly-wed couples.',0,'Three-roofed Shiva pagoda in Panauti, first built in 1294 and often called Nepal\'s oldest surviving temple.','Welcome to Panauti, an old trading town on the salt route between Tibet and India, and to its great temple of Indreshwar Mahadev. You are looking at one of the largest and tallest pagoda temples in Nepal, three roofs high. A temple was first raised on this spot over a Shiva lingam in 1294, which is why many call it the oldest surviving temple in the country. Walk slowly around it and study the roof struts on the lower two storeys; their carving is among the finest Newar woodwork anywhere. Now look higher. See the pots and pans hanging from the upper roof? They were offered by young married couples hoping for a happy, prosperous home. Facing the door, a stone bull, Nandi, waits for his master. This temple came through the 2015 earthquake in good condition. Every twelve years in Magh, the town\'s Makar Mela fills the river confluence nearby with pilgrims.','Local tradition holds that Shiva created the lingam here himself; the hidden \'third river\' of Panauti is said to begin at this temple and flow to the confluence below.','[\"The temple was first built over a lingam in 1294.\", \"It is one of the largest and tallest pagoda temples in Nepal, with three roofs.\", \"Pots and pans hung on the upper storey are offerings from young married couples.\", \"Panauti\'s medieval complex was placed on Nepal\'s UNESCO Tentative List in 1996.\", \"The temple survived the 2015 earthquake in good condition.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,'Wikipedia reports the temple survived the 2015 earthquake in good condition, though Lonely Planet notes some visible damage.','https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Indreshwar_Mahadev_Temple_in_Panauti.jpg/1280px-Indreshwar_Mahadev_Temple_in_Panauti.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indreshwar_Mahadev_Temple_in_Panauti.jpg','Prakat Shrestha · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,panauti,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panauti\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q108544599\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/points-of-interest/indreshwar-mahadev-temple/1432726\", \"https://www.windhorsetours.com/sights/panauti\", \"https://nepalitimes.com/creation-to-destruction-then-revival\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Indreshwar_Temple,_Panauti\"]','पनौतीको तीन छाने शिव पगोडा, सन् १२९४ मा पहिलो पटक बनेको र प्रायः नेपालकै सबैभन्दा पुरानो बाँचेको मन्दिर भनिने।','तिब्बत र भारतबीचको नुन बाटोमा पर्ने पुरानो व्यापारिक सहर पनौतीमा र यहाँको ठूलो इन्द्रेश्वर महादेव मन्दिरमा तपाईंलाई स्वागत छ। तपाईं नेपालका सबैभन्दा ठूला र अग्ला पगोडा मन्दिरमध्ये एउटा हेर्दै हुनुहुन्छ, जसमा तीन छाना छन्। यही ठाउँमा सन् १२९४ मा शिवलिङ्गमाथि पहिलो पटक मन्दिर बनाइएको थियो, त्यसैले धेरैले यसलाई देशको सबैभन्दा पुरानो बाँचेको मन्दिर भन्छन्। वरिपरि बिस्तारै हिँड्नुहोस् र तलका दुई तल्लाका छानाका टेकाहरू ध्यान दिएर हेर्नुहोस्। तिनका कुँदाइ सबैभन्दा राम्रा नेवारी काष्ठकलामध्ये पर्छन्। अब माथि हेर्नुहोस्। माथिल्लो छानामा भाँडाकुँडा झुन्डिएका देख्नुभयो? ती नवविवाहित जोडीले सुखी र सम्पन्न घरको आशामा चढाएका हुन्। ढोकाको सामुन्ने ढुङ्गाको साँढे, नन्दी, आफ्ना स्वामीको पर्खाइमा छ। यो मन्दिर सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा राम्रो अवस्थामै बाँच्यो। हरेक बाह्र वर्षमा माघमा लाग्ने पनौतीको मकर मेलाले नजिकैको नदीको सङ्गम तीर्थयात्रीले भरिन्छ।','स्थानीय मान्यता अनुसार शिवले आफैँ यहाँ लिङ्ग बनाएका हुन्। पनौतीको लुकेको \'तेस्रो नदी\' यही मन्दिरबाट सुरु भएर तलको सङ्गमसम्म बग्छ भनिन्छ।','[\"मन्दिर पहिलो पटक सन् १२९४ मा लिङ्गमाथि बनाइएको थियो।\", \"यो तीन छाना भएको नेपालका सबैभन्दा ठूला र अग्ला पगोडा मन्दिरमध्ये एउटा हो।\", \"माथिल्लो तल्लामा झुन्ड्याइएका भाँडाकुँडा नवविवाहित जोडीले चढाएका भेटी हुन्।\", \"पनौतीको मध्यकालीन परिसर सन् १९९६ मा नेपालको युनेस्को अस्थायी सूचीमा राखियो।\", \"मन्दिर सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा राम्रो अवस्थामै बाँच्यो।\"]','विकिपिडियाका अनुसार मन्दिर सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा राम्रो अवस्थामै बाँच्यो, तर लोनली प्लानेटले केही देखिने क्षति भएको उल्लेख गरेको छ।','[{\"name\": \"Makar Mela\", \"note\": \"Held every 12 years in Magh at the river confluence below the temple.\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"मकर मेला\", \"note_np\": \"हरेक १२ वर्षमा माघमा मन्दिरमुनिको नदीको सङ्गममा लाग्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Indreshower_Temple%2C_Panauti.JPG/1280px-Indreshower_Temple%2C_Panauti.JPG\", \"author\": \"Ram kumar kc\", \"caption\": \"The three-roofed temple from the courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indreshower_Temple,_Panauti.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Statue_of_bull_in_front_of_Mahadev_temple.jpg/1280px-Statue_of_bull_in_front_of_Mahadev_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Roman Raghu Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Stone bull (Nandi) facing the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_bull_in_front_of_Mahadev_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Door_of_Indreshwor_mahadev.jpg/1280px-Door_of_Indreshwor_mahadev.jpg\", \"author\": \"Roman Raghu Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Carved door of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Door_of_Indreshwor_mahadev.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Wooden_carved_sculpture_20180918_113835.jpg/1280px-Wooden_carved_sculpture_20180918_113835.jpg\", \"author\": \"Roman Raghu Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Wooden carved strut figure\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wooden_carved_sculpture_20180918_113835.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Indreshowor_mahadev_bell.jpg/1280px-Indreshowor_mahadev_bell.jpg\", \"author\": \"Lusifor ,manoj shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Temple bell said to date from the 18th century\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indreshowor_mahadev_bell.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Tall three-roofed brick pagoda with deep tiled eaves and carved struts, on a stepped stone plinth in an open paved courtyard.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#9C5B3B\", \"#4A3426\", \"#C9A227\"], \"features\": [\"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"nandi-bull\", \"lion-statues\", \"bell\", \"carved-windows\"], \"height_m\": 20, \"footprint_m\": [14, 14], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"newar-houses\", \"river\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(67,'chandeshwori-temple-banepa','Chandeshwori Temple','चण्डेश्वरी मन्दिर','Banepa','Bagmati','Kavrepalanchok',NULL,27.635833,85.532222,'pagoda','Hindu','Chandeshwori (form of Parvati, slayer of the demon Chanda)',NULL,'Believed to have been built in the 17th century; the story of the goddess is told in the Nepal Mahatmya of the Skanda Purana.','unknown','Three-roofed pagoda with gilded metal roofs and carved struts, set in a stone-paved courtyard with stone pillars, small shikhara shrines and a lingam shrine in front. A mural shows the goddess slaying Chanda, and a wall painting of Bhairav is said to be the largest in Nepal Mandala.',0,'Three-roofed golden pagoda above Banepa where the goddess is said to have killed the demon Chanda.','Follow the lane about a kilometre north-east of Banepa town, along the Punyamata river, and the golden roofs of Chandeshwori rise from the forest edge. This temple, believed to date from the 17th century, honours the mother goddess who defeated the demon Chanda. Shiva had given Chanda a boon that only a woman could kill him, and he terrorised the world. The gods hid in this forest as birds, and the goddess slipped into a tree. When Chanda cut the tree down, she burst out on a great lion and slew him. From the belly of the demon, a devotee of Shiva, a lingam grew; you can see it in the small shrine just in front of the main temple. Now find the huge painting of Bhairav on one of the walls, said to be the largest in the old Nepal Mandala. Locals say the rocks by the river still bear marks of the battle.','The demon Chanda could be killed only by a woman. Hiding in the Banepa forest, the mother goddess emerged from a tree he cut down, rode out on a lion and killed him; a Shiva lingam grew from his belly, now in the shrine before the temple.','[\"The temple lies about 1 km north-east of Banepa along the Punyamata river.\", \"It is believed to have been built in the 17th century.\", \"A mural shows Chandeshwori slaying the demon Chanda.\", \"A painting of Bhairav on one wall is said to be the largest in the Nepal Mandala.\", \"The lingam in the small shrine in front is said to have grown from the demon\'s belly.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Chandeshwari_Temple.JPG/1280px-Chandeshwari_Temple.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandeshwari_Temple.JPG','Brian Dell · Public domain','pagoda,hindu,banepa,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chandeshwori_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5071024\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/chandeshwori-jatra-banepas-enduring-festival-of-devotion-and-divine-victory\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/art-culture/2025/05/03/a-town-in-step-with-its-ancestors\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Chandeshwori_temple,_Banepa\"]','बनेपामाथि रहेको तीन छाने सुनौलो पगोडा, जहाँ देवीले चण्ड दानवलाई मारेकी भनिन्छ।','बनेपा सहरबाट करिब एक किलोमिटर उत्तर-पूर्वतिर पुण्यमाता खोलाछेउको बाटो हिँड्नुहोस्। जङ्गलको किनारमा चण्डेश्वरीका सुनौला छाना देखिन्छन्। १७ औं शताब्दीको मानिने यो मन्दिर चण्ड दानवलाई हराउने मातृदेवीको हो। शिवले चण्डलाई कुनै नारीले मात्र मार्न सक्ने वरदान दिएका थिए, र उसले संसारलाई आतङ्कित पारेको थियो। देवताहरू चरा बनेर यही जङ्गलमा लुके, र देवी एउटा रुखभित्र पसिन्। चण्डले रुख काटेपछि उनी ठूलो सिंहमाथि चढेर बाहिर निस्किन् र उसलाई मारिन्। शिवका भक्त ती दानवको पेटबाट शिवलिङ्ग उम्रियो। त्यो तपाईं मुख्य मन्दिरको ठीक अगाडिको सानो मन्दिरमा देख्न सक्नुहुन्छ। अब भित्तामा भैरवको ठूलो चित्र खोज्नुहोस्। त्यो पुरानो नेपाल मण्डलमै सबैभन्दा ठूलो चित्र भनिन्छ। स्थानीय भन्छन्, नदीका चट्टानमा अहिले पनि युद्धका चिन्ह छन्।','चण्ड दानवलाई कुनै नारीले मात्र मार्न सक्थ्यो। बनेपाको जङ्गलमा लुकेकी मातृदेवी उसले काटेको रुखबाट निस्किन्। उनी सिंहमा चढेर बाहिर आइन् र उसलाई मारिन्। उसको पेटबाट शिवलिङ्ग उम्रियो, जो अहिले मन्दिरअगाडिको सानो मन्दिरमा छ।','[\"मन्दिर बनेपाबाट करिब १ किमी उत्तर-पूर्वमा पुण्यमाता खोलाछेउ छ।\", \"यो १७ औं शताब्दीमा बनेको मानिन्छ।\", \"एउटा भित्तेचित्रमा चण्डेश्वरीले चण्ड दानवलाई मारेको देखाइएको छ।\", \"एउटा भित्तामा रहेको भैरवको चित्र नेपाल मण्डलमै सबैभन्दा ठूलो भनिन्छ।\", \"अगाडिको सानो मन्दिरमा रहेको शिवलिङ्ग दानवको पेटबाट उम्रिएको भनिन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Chandeshwori Jatra\", \"note\": \"Banepa\'s chariot festival around Baisakh Purnima, opening with the pre-dawn Mata Puja (Chirag Yatra).\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"चण्डेश्वरी जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"वैशाख पूर्णिमाको वरिपरि बनेपामा निस्कने रथयात्रा, जुन बिहानैको माता पूजा (चिराग यात्रा) बाट सुरु हुन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Chandeshwori_Temple%2C_Banepa%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Chandeshwori_Temple%2C_Banepa%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Algosig\", \"caption\": \"Entrance gate of the temple complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandeshwori_Temple,_Banepa,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Chandeswori_temple_with_chandeswori_forest.JPG/1280px-Chandeswori_temple_with_chandeswori_forest.JPG\", \"author\": \"Rajesh2044\", \"caption\": \"The temple against Chandeshwori forest\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandeswori_temple_with_chandeswori_forest.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Door_Aculpture_at_Chandeshwori_Temple_Banepa.jpg/1280px-Door_Aculpture_at_Chandeshwori_Temple_Banepa.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rupendra Neupane\", \"caption\": \"Carved sculpture on the temple door\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Door_Aculpture_at_Chandeshwori_Temple_Banepa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Banepa_jatra2.JPG/1280px-Banepa_jatra2.JPG\", \"author\": \"MaharjanAshok58\", \"caption\": \"Banepa Jatra procession\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banepa_jatra2.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Chandeswori_temple_surrounding.JPG/1280px-Chandeswori_temple_surrounding.JPG\", \"author\": \"Rajesh2044\", \"caption\": \"Shrines surrounding the main temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandeswori_temple_surrounding.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Three gilded roofs stacked on a brick pagoda, with a long hanging pennant from the pinnacle, stone pillars topped with figures and white shikhara shrines in front.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#C9A227\", \"#7A3B2E\", \"#9E9E9E\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"stone-pillar\", \"bell\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"toran\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [10, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"forest\", \"sacred-grove\", \"river\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(68,'palanchok-bhagawati','Palanchok Bhagawati Temple','पलाञ्चोक भगवती मन्दिर','Panchkhal','Bagmati','Kavrepalanchok',NULL,27.628611,85.673889,'pagoda','Hindu','Bhagawati (eighteen-armed Durga)',NULL,'Believed (by tradition) to date from the reign of the Licchavi king Manadeva (464-505 AD); not firmly documented.','Licchavi (traditional attribution)','Pagoda-style temple with two tiled roofs edged in red cloth frills and a tall gilded pinnacle, on a hilltop courtyard. Inside is a three-foot black stone image of the goddess with 18 arms.',0,'Hilltop pagoda of the 18-armed goddess Bhagawati, revered as the elder sister of all Bhagawatis in Nepal.','You have climbed to the summit of Palanchok hill, 1,563 metres up, seven kilometres north of Panchkhal on the Araniko Highway. In front of you is the temple of Palanchok Bhagawati, whom devotees call the elder sister of all the Bhagawati goddesses of Nepal. Tradition says the shrine goes back to the Licchavi king Manadeva, who ruled about fifteen hundred years ago. Peer into the sanctum. The goddess is carved from black stone, only about three feet tall, yet she has eighteen arms, each ready to protect her devotees from danger and misfortune. Tuesdays and Saturdays are her special days, and at Dashain and Chaite Dashain thousands of pilgrims queue here with offerings. Now turn around. From this hilltop you can see the Himalaya stretching across the northern sky. The 2015 earthquake left the temple leaning slightly, and it spent the following years under scaffolding while repairs were carried out.',NULL,'[\"The temple stands at 1,563 m on Palanchok hill, about 7 km north of Panchkhal.\", \"Its black stone idol of the goddess is about three feet tall and has 18 arms.\", \"Tradition dates the temple to King Manadeva (464-505 AD).\", \"Palanchok Bhagawati is regarded as the elder sister of the other Bhagawati shrines of Nepal.\", \"The Kshama ritual is held on the full moons of Baisakh and Jestha.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,'The April 2015 earthquake left the main temple slightly tilted; it was under scaffolding for repairs in 2018. The nearby Kalika Bhagawati temple was razed.','https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Palanchowk_Bhagawati_Temple.jpg/1280px-Palanchowk_Bhagawati_Temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palanchowk_Bhagawati_Temple.jpg','Gaurav_Dhwaj_Khadka · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,licchavi (traditional attribution),panchkhal,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palanchok_Bhagawati_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7126679\", \"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/steeped-in-history-and-legend-palanchok-bhagwati.html\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Palanchok_Bhagawati_Temple\"]','अठार हात भएकी देवी भगवतीको डाँडाको पगोडा, नेपालका सबै भगवतीकी जेठी दिदीका रूपमा पूजिने।','तपाईं अरनिको राजमार्गमा पाँचखालबाट सात किलोमिटर उत्तरमा रहेको पलाञ्चोक डाँडाको १,५६३ मिटर उचाइको टुप्पोमा पुग्नुभएको छ। तपाईंको अगाडि पलाञ्चोक भगवतीको मन्दिर छ। भक्तजन उनलाई नेपालका सबै भगवती देवीकी जेठी दिदी भन्छन्। परम्परा अनुसार यो मन्दिर करिब पन्ध्र सय वर्षअघि शासन गरेका लिच्छवि राजा मानदेवको पालासम्म पुग्छ। गर्भगृहभित्र हेर्नुहोस्। देवी कालो ढुङ्गाबाट कुँदिएकी छिन्, करिब तीन फिट मात्र अग्ली, तर उनका अठारवटा हात छन्। हरेक हातले भक्तजनलाई खतरा र दुर्भाग्यबाट जोगाउन तयार छ। मङ्गलबार र शनिबार उनका विशेष दिन हुन्, र दशैँ र चैते दशैँमा हजारौँ तीर्थयात्री भेटी लिएर यहाँ लाइन लाग्छन्। अब पछाडि फर्केर हेर्नुहोस्। यो डाँडाबाट उत्तरको आकाशभरि फैलिएको हिमाल देखिन्छ। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले मन्दिरलाई अलिकति ढल्काएको थियो, र त्यसपछिका वर्षहरूमा मर्मत हुँदा मन्दिर टेको र बाँसका भरीले घेरिएको थियो।',NULL,'[\"मन्दिर पाँचखालबाट करिब ७ किमी उत्तर, पलाञ्चोक डाँडामा १,५६३ मिटरको उचाइमा छ।\", \"देवीको कालो ढुङ्गाको मूर्ति करिब तीन फिट अग्लो छ र यसका १८ हात छन्।\", \"परम्परा अनुसार मन्दिर राजा मानदेव (सन् ४६४-५०५) को पालाको हो।\", \"पलाञ्चोक भगवतीलाई नेपालका अरू भगवती मन्दिरकी जेठी दिदी मानिन्छ।\", \"क्षमा पूजा वैशाख र जेठको पूर्णिमामा गरिन्छ।\"]','सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पले मुख्य मन्दिर अलिकति ढल्कियो। सन् २०१८ मा मर्मतका लागि त्यसलाई टेकोले घेरिएको थियो। नजिकैको कालिका भगवती मन्दिर भत्किएर सखाप भयो।','[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Thousands of devotees come to offer prayers and sacrifices.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"हजारौँ भक्तजन पूजा गर्न र बलि चढाउन आउँछन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Chaite Dashain\", \"note\": \"Second major pilgrimage season of the year at the temple.\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"चैते दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"मन्दिरमा वर्षको दोस्रो ठूलो तीर्थयात्राको समय।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Palanchok_Bhagawati.jpg/1280px-Palanchok_Bhagawati.jpg\", \"author\": \"Krish Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Devotees in the temple courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palanchok_Bhagawati.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Palanchowk-bhagawati_%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%AD%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%87_%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2.jpg\", \"author\": \"Akt1860\", \"caption\": \"Palanchok Bhagawati temple, Kavre\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palanchowk-bhagawati_%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%AD%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%87_%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B2.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c2/%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9E%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%9A%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%95_%E0%A4%AD%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0.jpg\", \"author\": \"Punya\", \"caption\": \"The temple and its pinnacle\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9E%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%9A%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%95_%E0%A4%AD%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Palanchok.jpg/1280px-Palanchok.jpg\", \"author\": \"Krish Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Hilltop setting of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palanchok.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9E%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%9A%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%95_%E0%A4%AD%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80.JPG\", \"author\": \"Punya\", \"caption\": \"Palanchok Bhagawati shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%9E%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%9A%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%95_%E0%A4%AD%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%80.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Two-roof pagoda with grey tile roofs trimmed by red cloth frills and a tall slender gilded spire, in a hilltop courtyard.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#6E6A64\", \"#B22222\", \"#C9A227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"trident\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": 12, \"footprint_m\": [9, 9], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"brick-courtyard\", \"himalaya-backdrop\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(69,'halesi-mahadev','Halesi Mahadev (Halesi-Maratika Caves)','हलेसी महादेव','Mahadevasthan (Halesi Tuwachung)','Koshi','Khotang',NULL,27.190061,86.622392,'cave','Both','Shiva (Mahadev); Padmasambhava and Mandarava for Buddhists; ancestral deity of the Kirati Rai',NULL,'Natural cave; referred to in Himalayan literature as early as the 12th century, in the Kathang Zanglingma biography of Padmasambhava.','unknown','Natural limestone cave with an east-facing half-moon entrance, about 67 ft below the surface, round in plan with a 193 ft diameter and a second cave beneath. Shrines and railings fill the cave mouth; a Buddhist monastery stands on the hill nearby.',0,'Sacred cave in Khotang revered by Hindus as Shiva\'s hiding place and by Buddhists as the cave of long life.','Go down the steps and stand at the mouth of the cave. Its entrance is shaped like a half moon and faces east, toward the morning sun. You are at Halesi, in the hills of Khotang, between the Dudh Koshi and Sun Koshi rivers, and three faiths share this cave. Hindus call it Halesi Mahadev, the Pashupatinath of the east. They say Shiva hid inside for six thousand years to escape the demon Bhasmasur, who could burn anything he touched to ash. Look for the natural stone lingam in the darkness. Buddhists know the place as Maratika, where Guru Padmasambhava and his consort Mandarava are said to have gained the power of long life, so you will see monks and a monastery on the hill above. For the Kirati Rai people it is an ancestral home, where their forefather once lived. On Shivaratri and Bala Chaturdashi the cave fills with pilgrims.','Shiva hid in this cave for 6,000 years to escape the demon Bhasmasur. For Buddhists, Padmasambhava and Mandarava attained the vidyadhara of longevity here.','[\"The cave entrance is half-moon shaped and faces east.\", \"The cave is about 67 ft below the surface and has a diameter of about 193 ft, with another cave beneath it.\", \"It lies between the Dudh Koshi and Sun Koshi rivers, about 185 km south-west of Mount Everest.\", \"It is mentioned in Himalayan literature as far back as the 12th century.\", \"The Kirati Rai regard Halesi as an ancestral place of their forefather Raechhakule.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Halesi_~_Maratika_cave_entrance.jpg/1280px-Halesi_~_Maratika_cave_entrance.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Halesi_~_Maratika_cave_entrance.jpg','Christopher J. Fynn · CC BY-SA 4.0','cave,both,mahadevasthan (halesi tuwachung),hindu,buddhist,legend,art,festival,koshi','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halesi-Maratika_Caves\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6755052\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Halesi_~_Maratika_caves\"]','खोटाङको पवित्र गुफा, हिन्दूले शिव लुकेको ठाउँ मानेर र बौद्धले दीर्घायुको गुफा मानेर पुज्ने।','सिँढी ओर्लेर गुफाको मुखमा उभिनुहोस्। यसको प्रवेशद्वार अर्धचन्द्रको आकारको छ र बिहानको घामतिर, पूर्वतिर फर्केको छ। तपाईं दूधकोशी र सुनकोशी नदीको बीचमा रहेको खोटाङको डाँडामा, हलेसीमा हुनुहुन्छ। यो गुफा तीन धर्मले साझा रूपमा मान्छन्। हिन्दूले यसलाई हलेसी महादेव, अर्थात् पूर्वको पशुपतिनाथ भन्छन्। उनीहरू भन्छन्, भस्मासुर नाम गरेको दानवले जे छोए पनि खरानी बनाउँथ्यो। उसबाट बच्न शिव छ हजार वर्ष यही गुफाभित्र लुकेका थिए। अँध्यारोमा प्राकृतिक ढुङ्गाको शिवलिङ्ग खोज्नुहोस्। बौद्धले यो ठाउँलाई मारातिका भन्छन्। गुरु पद्मसम्भव र उनकी सहचरी मन्दारवाले यहीँ दीर्घायुको शक्ति पाएका भनिन्छ, त्यसैले माथिको डाँडामा भिक्षु र गुम्बा देख्नुहुन्छ। किराती राईका लागि यो पुर्खाको थलो हो, जहाँ उनीहरूका पुर्खा बसेका थिए। शिवरात्रि र बाला चतुर्दशीमा गुफा तीर्थयात्रीले भरिन्छ।','शिव भस्मासुर दानवबाट बच्न यो गुफामा ६,००० वर्ष लुकेका थिए। बौद्धका लागि यहाँ पद्मसम्भव र मन्दारवाले दीर्घायुको विद्याधर सिद्धि पाएका थिए।','[\"गुफाको प्रवेशद्वार अर्धचन्द्राकार छ र पूर्वतिर फर्केको छ।\", \"गुफा सतहभन्दा करिब ६७ फिट तल छ र यसको व्यास करिब १९३ फिट छ। यसमुनि अर्को गुफा पनि छ।\", \"यो दूधकोशी र सुनकोशी नदीको बीचमा, सगरमाथाबाट करिब १८५ किमी दक्षिण-पश्चिममा छ।\", \"हिमाली साहित्यमा यो बाह्रौँ शताब्दीदेखि नै उल्लेख भएको पाइन्छ।\", \"किराती राईले हलेसीलाई आफ्ना पुर्खा रैछकुलेको थलो मान्छन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"One of the best-attended fairs at the cave.\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"गुफामा सबैभन्दा धेरै मानिस जुट्ने मेलाहरूमध्ये एउटा।\"}, {\"name\": \"Bala Chaturdashi\", \"note\": \"Large religious fair held at Halesi.\", \"month\": \"Mangsir\", \"name_np\": \"बाला चतुर्दशी\", \"note_np\": \"हलेसीमा लाग्ने ठूलो धार्मिक मेला।\"}, {\"name\": \"Ram Navami\", \"note\": \"Devotees throng the cave on Ram Navami.\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"रामनवमी\", \"note_np\": \"रामनवमीका दिन भक्तजन गुफामा भीड लगाउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/View_of_Maratika_~_Halesi.jpg/1280px-View_of_Maratika_~_Halesi.jpg\", \"author\": \"Christopher J. Fynn\", \"caption\": \"Halesi village and hillside around the caves\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Maratika_~_Halesi.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5.JPG/1280px-%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5.JPG\", \"author\": \"Punya\", \"caption\": \"Natural lingam of Mahadev inside the cave\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Maratika_Chimey_Takten_Choling_Monastery.jpg/1280px-Maratika_Chimey_Takten_Choling_Monastery.jpg\", \"author\": \"Christopher J. Fynn\", \"caption\": \"Maratika Chimey Takten Choling Monastery\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maratika_Chimey_Takten_Choling_Monastery.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Cave_Haleshi_Mahadev_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Cave_Haleshi_Mahadev_%282%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pratap Baniya\", \"caption\": \"Cave opening towards the sky\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cave_Haleshi_Mahadev_(2).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B8%E0%A4%B0.jpg/1280px-%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B8%E0%A4%B0.jpg\", \"author\": \"Punya\", \"caption\": \"Outer premises of Halesi Mahadev\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%B5_%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%80_%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B8%E0%A4%B0.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"cave\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Huge dark overhanging grey rock mouth with white-railed stone steps descending into it and small shrines inside.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#6F6A5E\", \"#2B2620\", \"#FFFFFF\"], \"features\": [\"rock-face\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"fence-railing\", \"prayer-flags\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": 20, \"footprint_m\": [59, 59], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"cave-mouth\", \"hilltop\", \"village\", \"forest\", \"monks-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(70,'pathibhara-devi','Pathibhara Devi Temple','पाथीभरा देवी मन्दिर','Phungling (Taplejung)','Koshi','Taplejung',NULL,27.429444,87.767722,'sculpture','Hindu','Pathibhara Devi (Durga); revered by Limbu people as Yuma Sammang on Mukkumlung hill',NULL,'Ancient hilltop sacred rock revered by Limbu and Hindu devotees; the Pathibhara Area Development Committee formed in 1995, and in 2001 the rock was replaced by a statue of Durga.','unknown','Open-air hilltop shrine at 3,794 m: a richly dressed statue of the goddess under a canopy, surrounded by tridents, huge bells and lines of prayer flags, with small shelter buildings on the stony summit.',0,'Shaktipeeth on a 3,794 m summit in Taplejung, sacred to Hindus as Durga and to Limbus as Mukkumlung.','You have reached the summit of Pathibhara, 3,794 metres up in Taplejung, a long climb north-east of Phungling bazaar. Ring one of the great bells and listen to it echo across the ridges. Long before any statue stood here, the Limbu people revered a great rock on this hilltop, and they saw the whole Mukkumlung hill as a form of their goddess Yuma Sammang. Hindus saw the same rock as Durga, and today Pathibhara is counted among the Shakti Peethas. Local legend tells of shepherds who lost hundreds of sheep on this very spot. In a dream the goddess asked them for a sacrifice and a shrine; when they obeyed, the lost flock came back. Since 2001 a statue of Durga has stood in place of the rock. Look east on a clear morning: the white wall of Kanchenjunga fills the sky. Pilgrims from across Nepal and India climb here believing she grants their wishes.','Shepherds lost hundreds of sheep while grazing here. The goddess appeared in their dream and asked for a sacrifice and a shrine; when they offered it, the lost herd returned, and the custom of sacrifice at the temple began.','[\"The temple stands at 3,794 m, about 19.4 km north-east of Phungling.\", \"Limbus revere the hill as Mukkumlung, a natural form of the goddess Yuma Sammang.\", \"In 2001 the sacred rock on the summit was replaced with a statue of Durga.\", \"It is one of the Shakti Peethas and a side route of the Kanchenjunga trek.\", \"Kanchenjunga and Kumbhakarna can be seen from the temple.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Pathibhara_2014.JPG/1280px-Pathibhara_2014.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pathibhara_2014.JPG','Avista7 · CC BY-SA 4.0','sculpture,hindu,phungling (taplejung),legend,koshi','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pathibhara_Devi_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7144777\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Pathibhara_Temple\"]','ताप्लेजुङको ३,७९४ मिटरको टुप्पोमा रहेको शक्तिपीठ, हिन्दूका लागि दुर्गा र लिम्बूका लागि मुक्कुम्लुङका रूपमा पवित्र।','तपाईं ताप्लेजुङमा ३,७९४ मिटर माथि पाथीभराको टुप्पोमा पुग्नुभएको छ। फुङलिङ बजारबाट उत्तर-पूर्वतिर लामो उकालो पार गर्नुपर्छ। ठूला घण्टमध्ये एउटा बजाउनुहोस् र त्यसको आवाज डाँडाभरि गुञ्जिएको सुन्नुहोस्। यहाँ कुनै मूर्ति राखिनुभन्दा धेरै पहिले लिम्बू जातिले डाँडाको ठूलो चट्टानलाई पुज्थे, र उनीहरू पूरै मुक्कुम्लुङ डाँडालाई आफ्नी देवी युमा साम्माङको रूप मान्थे। हिन्दूले त्यही चट्टानलाई दुर्गा देखे, र आज पाथीभरा शक्तिपीठमध्ये गनिन्छ। स्थानीय कथा अनुसार यही ठाउँमा गोठालाले सयौँ भेडा गुमाएका थिए। सपनामा देवीले उनीहरूसँग बलि र मन्दिर मागिन्। उनीहरूले त्यसै गरेपछि हराएको बथान फर्कियो। सन् २००१ देखि चट्टानको ठाउँमा दुर्गाको मूर्ति छ। मौसम खुला भएको बिहान पूर्वतिर हेर्नुहोस्। कञ्चनजङ्घाको सेतो पर्खालले आकाश भरिन्छ। नेपाल र भारतभरिका तीर्थयात्री देवीले इच्छा पूरा गर्छिन् भन्ने विश्वासमा यहाँ उक्लन्छन्।','यहाँ चराउँदा गोठालाले सयौँ भेडा गुमाए। देवी उनीहरूको सपनामा आइन् र बलि र मन्दिर मागिन्। उनीहरूले चढाएपछि हराएको बथान फर्कियो, र त्यसपछि मन्दिरमा बलि दिने चलन सुरु भयो।','[\"मन्दिर ३,७९४ मिटरको उचाइमा, फुङलिङबाट करिब १९.४ किमी उत्तर-पूर्वमा छ।\", \"लिम्बूले यो डाँडालाई मुक्कुम्लुङ, अर्थात् देवी युमा साम्माङको प्राकृतिक रूप मानेर पुज्छन्।\", \"सन् २००१ मा टुप्पोको पवित्र चट्टानको ठाउँमा दुर्गाको मूर्ति राखियो।\", \"यो शक्तिपीठमध्ये एउटा हो र कञ्चनजङ्घा ट्रेकको एउटा सहायक बाटो हो।\", \"मन्दिरबाट कञ्चनजङ्घा र कुम्भकर्ण हिमाल देखिन्छन्।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Mt._Kanchanjunga_n_Mt._Kumbhakarna_as_seen_from_Pathivara_temple%2C_Taplejung.jpg/1280px-Mt._Kanchanjunga_n_Mt._Kumbhakarna_as_seen_from_Pathivara_temple%2C_Taplejung.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shrestha Aajib\", \"caption\": \"Kanchenjunga and Kumbhakarna seen from the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mt._Kanchanjunga_n_Mt._Kumbhakarna_as_seen_from_Pathivara_temple,_Taplejung.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Buddhist_Prayer_Flags_at_Pathibhara_Devi_Temple.jpg/1280px-Buddhist_Prayer_Flags_at_Pathibhara_Devi_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Salman Gurung\", \"caption\": \"Buddhist prayer flags at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buddhist_Prayer_Flags_at_Pathibhara_Devi_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Huge_bell_at_Pathibhara_Devi_temple.jpg/1280px-Huge_bell_at_Pathibhara_Devi_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Salman Gurung\", \"caption\": \"Huge bell at Pathibhara Devi temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huge_bell_at_Pathibhara_Devi_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Mountain_on_which_Pathibhara_Temple_is_located.jpg/1280px-Mountain_on_which_Pathibhara_Temple_is_located.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nepalsom\", \"caption\": \"The mountain on which the temple stands\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountain_on_which_Pathibhara_Temple_is_located.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Pathibhara_Temple_Area_2018_1.jpg/1280px-Pathibhara_Temple_Area_2018_1.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pratap Baniya\", \"caption\": \"Building in the temple area on a misty day\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pathibhara_Temple_Area_2018_1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"statue\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Golden-faced goddess dressed in red cloth under a red canopy, ringed by tridents, big bells and prayer flags on a misty stone summit.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#C0392B\", \"#D4AC0D\", \"#F5F5F5\"], \"features\": [\"idol-visible\", \"trident\", \"bell\", \"prayer-flags\", \"flags-red\"], \"height_m\": 3, \"footprint_m\": [5, 5], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"snow-peaks\", \"himalaya-backdrop\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(71,'barahachhetra','Barahachhetra','बराहक्षेत्र','Barahakshetra (near Dharan)','Koshi','Sunsari',NULL,26.876614,87.165846,'dome-temple','Hindu','Varaha (boar incarnation of Vishnu) with Lakshmi',NULL,'Ancient tirtha mentioned in the Brahma, Varaha and Skanda Puranas and the Mahabharata; the present main temple was rebuilt by Juddha Shumsher in 1991 BS (c. 1934-35) after the 1990 BS (1934) earthquake.','Rana (present building)','Group of whitewashed dome-roofed temples on terraces above the Saptakoshi river, including the main Varaha temple and shrines of Lakshmi, Panchayan, Guruvaraha, Suryavaraha, Kokavaraha and Nageshwar, with pilgrim rest houses. Statues over 1,500 years old have been found here.',0,'One of Nepal\'s Char Dham: white-domed temples of Vishnu\'s boar incarnation where the Koka meets the Koshi.','Listen: below you, the mighty Saptakoshi thunders out of the hills where the Koka river joins it. You are at Barahachhetra, one of the four great pilgrimage dhams of Nepal, praised in the Puranas and even in the Mahabharata. The story says that when a demon dragged the earth down toward the underworld, Lord Vishnu took the form of Varaha, a mighty boar, and lifted her back up on his tusk. Then he rested here beside the Koshi with his wife Lakshmi. Find the large image of Varaha holding the earth. The white domed temple you see is fairly new; the 1934 earthquake brought the old one down, and Juddha Shumsher had it rebuilt. Yet statues more than fifteen hundred years old have been found around you. Limbu people call this place Mouksik Sawalung, the winter home of the god Dungdung Sammang. At Kartik Purnima and Makar Sankranti, crowds come to bathe in the river.','When the earth was being dragged into Patala, Vishnu took the form of the boar Varaha and lifted her out on his tusk, then sat with Lakshmi on the bank of the Koshi; the place is named after that incarnation.','[\"Barahachhetra is one of the Char Dham (four great pilgrimage sites) of Nepal.\", \"It lies at the confluence of the Koka and Koshi rivers in Sunsari District.\", \"The present temple was rebuilt by Juddha Shumsher in 1991 BS after the 1990 BS (1934) earthquake.\", \"There are nine temples in the complex, and statues over 1,500 years old have been found here.\", \"Limbus call it Mouksik:Sawalung, the winter residence of the god Dungdung Sammang.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Barahachhetra_temple_of_Sunsari.jpg/1280px-Barahachhetra_temple_of_Sunsari.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barahachhetra_temple_of_Sunsari.jpg','Qrystal45 · CC BY-SA 4.0','dome-temple,hindu,rana (present building),barahakshetra (near dharan),legend,art,koshi','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baraha_Kshetra\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4858196\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/3116761691\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barahachhetra_temple_of_Sunsari.jpg\"]','नेपालका चार धाममध्ये एउटा। कोका र कोशीको सङ्गममा विष्णुको वराह अवतारका सेता गुम्बज भएका मन्दिर छन्।','सुन्नुहोस्, तपाईंको तल कोका खोला मिसिने ठाउँमा शक्तिशाली सप्तकोशी पहाडबाट गर्जिँदै निस्किन्छ। तपाईं बराहक्षेत्रमा हुनुहुन्छ, नेपालका चार ठूला तीर्थधाममध्ये एउटा, जसको महिमा पुराण र महाभारतमा समेत लेखिएको छ। कथा अनुसार एउटा दानवले पृथ्वीलाई पाताल तानेपछि भगवान् विष्णुले वराह, अर्थात् ठूलो बँगुरको रूप लिए, र पृथ्वीलाई आफ्नो दाह्रामा उठाएर माथि ल्याए। त्यसपछि उनी पत्नी लक्ष्मीसँग यहाँ कोशीको किनारमा विश्राम गरे। पृथ्वी बोकेका वराहको ठूलो मूर्ति खोज्नुहोस्। तपाईंले देखेको सेतो गुम्बज भएको मन्दिर अलि नयाँ हो। सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पले पुरानो मन्दिर ढाल्यो, र जुद्ध शमशेरले त्यसलाई फेरि बनाइदिए। तैपनि तपाईंको वरिपरि पन्ध्र सय वर्षभन्दा पुराना मूर्ति भेटिएका छन्। लिम्बूले यो ठाउँलाई मौक्सिक सावालुङ भन्छन्, देवता डुङ्डुङ साम्माङको जाडोको बासस्थान। कार्तिक पूर्णिमा र माघे सङ्क्रान्तिमा नदीमा नुहाउन भीड लाग्छ।','पृथ्वीलाई पाताल तानिँदै गर्दा विष्णुले वराह बँगुरको रूप लिएर उनलाई दाह्रामा उठाएर बाहिर ल्याए। त्यसपछि उनी लक्ष्मीसँग कोशीको किनारमा बसे। यो ठाउँको नाम त्यही अवतारबाट राखिएको हो।','[\"बराहक्षेत्र नेपालका चार धाम (चार ठूला तीर्थस्थल) मध्ये एउटा हो।\", \"यो सुनसरी जिल्लामा कोका र कोशी नदीको सङ्गममा छ।\", \"हालको मन्दिर जुद्ध शमशेरले वि.सं. १९९० (सन् १९३४) को भूकम्पपछि वि.सं. १९९१ मा बनाएका थिए।\", \"परिसरमा नौवटा मन्दिर छन्, र यहाँ १,५०० वर्षभन्दा पुराना मूर्ति भेटिएका छन्।\", \"लिम्बूले यसलाई मौक्सिक सावालुङ भन्छन्, देवता डुङ्डुङ साम्माङको जाडोको बासस्थान।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Kartik Purnima\", \"note\": \"Special fair; pilgrims from India especially come at this full moon.\", \"month\": \"Kartik\", \"name_np\": \"कार्तिक पूर्णिमा\", \"note_np\": \"विशेष मेला लाग्छ। यो पूर्णिमामा खासगरी भारतबाट तीर्थयात्री आउँछन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Makar Sankranti\", \"note\": \"Pilgrims from the hills of Nepal bathe at the confluence.\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"मकर सङ्क्रान्ति\", \"note_np\": \"नेपालका पहाडी भेगका तीर्थयात्री सङ्गममा नुहाउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Statue_of_Baraha.jpg/1280px-Statue_of_Baraha.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pushpendra khadka\", \"caption\": \"Statue of Varaha\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Baraha.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Baraha_with_Earth.jpg/1280px-Baraha_with_Earth.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pushpendra khadka\", \"caption\": \"Varaha lifting the Earth\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baraha_with_Earth.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Barahakshetra_Temple_Main_Gate.jpg/1280px-Barahakshetra_Temple_Main_Gate.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pushpendra khadka\", \"caption\": \"Main gate of the Barahakshetra temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barahakshetra_Temple_Main_Gate.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Barahachhetra_sapta_koshi.JPG/1280px-Barahachhetra_sapta_koshi.JPG\", \"author\": \"Manoj.ktr\", \"caption\": \"The Saptakoshi river at Barahachhetra\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barahachhetra_sapta_koshi.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Barahakshetra_Baraha_Dharan_Sunsari_Koshi_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Barahakshetra_Baraha_Dharan_Sunsari_Koshi_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Temple complex above the river\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barahakshetra_Baraha_Dharan_Sunsari_Koshi_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"dome-temple\", \"roof\": \"white-dome\", \"notes\": \"Cluster of white domed temples with small spires on terraces, a brown-roofed pavilion in front, and a wide grey river under forested hills.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#F2F2F0\", \"#9C6B3E\", \"#5D7A3A\"], \"features\": [\"dome-white\", \"domes-multiple\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"fence-railing\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [12, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"forest\", \"riverbank-ghats\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(72,'tengboche-monastery','Tengboche Monastery','टेङबोचे गुम्बा','Tengboche (Khumbu Pasang Lhamu Rural Municipality)','Koshi','Solukhumbu',NULL,27.836000,86.763944,'monastery','Buddhist','Shakyamuni Buddha (with Manjushri and Maitreya)',1916,'Founded in 1916 by Lama Gulu; destroyed by the 1934 earthquake and rebuilt, burnt in a fire on 19 January 1989, rebuilt with international help and reconsecrated in 1993.','unknown','Stone-masonry Tibetan Buddhist gompa with a large courtyard; the Dokhang prayer hall holds a two-storey statue of Shakyamuni flanked by Manjushri and Maitreya. A rebuilt painted entrance gate, mani stones and chortens surround it. Largest gompa in the Khumbu.',0,'The largest gompa in the Khumbu, at 3,867 m on the Everest trail, with Everest and Ama Dablam behind it.','Take a slow breath; you are at 3,867 metres, on a knoll above the meeting of the Dudh Koshi and Imja rivers. In front of you is Tengboche Monastery, the largest gompa in the Khumbu and home to Sherpa monks of the Nyingma tradition. Lama Gulu founded it in 1916, with blessings from the Rongbuk monastery on the Tibetan side of Everest. Its life has been dramatic. The 1934 earthquake flattened it, and in January 1989 an electrical fire destroyed its old scriptures, statues and murals. Monks, Sherpas and friends from around the world rebuilt it, and it was consecrated again in 1993. Walk through the painted gate and into the prayer hall, where a Buddha rises through two floors. Expeditions stop here to light candles and ask for a safe climb. Now step outside and look up the valley: Everest, Lhotse and the sharp peak of Ama Dablam stand right behind the roof.','Lama Sangwa Dorje, founder of the Pangboche monastery, is said to have foreseen a monastery at Tengboche and left his footprint on a rock while meditating here; the stone fractured in the 1989 fire.','[\"Tengboche stands at 3,867 m and is the largest gompa in the Khumbu region.\", \"It was founded in 1916 by Lama Gulu, linked to the Rongbuk Monastery in Tibet.\", \"It was destroyed by the 1934 earthquake and again by fire on 19 January 1989.\", \"The rebuilt monastery was consecrated in 1993.\", \"The Mani Rimdu festival is held here each autumn.\"]',NULL,NULL,3000,1500,NULL,60,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Tengboche_Monastery_with_Views_of_Mount_Everest%2C_Lhotse_and_Ama_Dablam.jpg/1280px-Tengboche_Monastery_with_Views_of_Mount_Everest%2C_Lhotse_and_Ama_Dablam.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tengboche_Monastery_with_Views_of_Mount_Everest,_Lhotse_and_Ama_Dablam.jpg','Rohit Sharma · CC BY-SA 4.0','monastery,buddhist,tengboche (khumbu pasang lhamu rural municipality),legend,art,festival,koshi','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tengboche_Monastery\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7699760\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/13050800\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/permit-entry-fees-national-parks.html\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/nepal/local-govt-imposes-rs-2000-entry-fee-foreigners-visiting-mt-everest-region\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Tengboche_Monastery\"]','एभरेस्ट मार्गमा ३,८६७ मिटरको उचाइमा रहेको खुम्बुको सबैभन्दा ठूलो गुम्बा, जसको पछाडि एभरेस्ट र अमा दब्लम देखिन्छन्।','बिस्तारै सास लिनुहोस्। तपाईं ३,८६७ मिटरको उचाइमा, दूधकोशी र इम्जा नदी मिल्ने ठाउँमाथिको टिलामा हुनुहुन्छ। तपाईंको अगाडि टेङबोचे गुम्बा छ, खुम्बुको सबैभन्दा ठूलो गुम्बा र निङमा परम्पराका शेर्पा भिक्षुहरूको थलो। लामा गुलुले सन् १९१६ मा यसको स्थापना गरे, एभरेस्टको तिब्बततिरको रोङबुक गुम्बाको आशीर्वादसहित। यसको इतिहास निकै उतारचढावको छ। सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पले यो ढल्यो, र सन् १९८९ को जनवरीमा बिजुलीको आगलागीले यसका पुराना धर्मग्रन्थ, मूर्ति र भित्तेचित्र नष्ट गर्‍यो। भिक्षु, शेर्पा र संसारभरिका साथीभाइले यसलाई फेरि बनाए, र सन् १९९३ मा यो फेरि प्रतिष्ठित गरियो। रङ्गीन ढोकाबाट प्रार्थना कक्षमा पस्नुहोस्, जहाँ बुद्धको मूर्ति दुई तल्लाजति अग्लो छ। आरोहीहरू यहाँ बत्ती बालेर सुरक्षित आरोहणको कामना गर्न रोकिन्छन्। अब बाहिर निस्केर उपत्यकातिर हेर्नुहोस्: एभरेस्ट, ल्होत्से र अमा दब्लमको तीखो चुचुरो छानाको ठीक पछाडि उभिएका छन्।','पाङबोचे गुम्बाका संस्थापक लामा सङ्वा दोर्जेले टेङबोचेमा गुम्बा बन्छ भनेर पहिल्यै देखेका थिए, र यहीँ ध्यान गर्दा चट्टानमा आफ्नो पाइलाको छाप छाडेका थिए भनिन्छ। सन् १९८९ को आगलागीमा त्यो ढुङ्गा चर्कियो।','[\"टेङबोचे ३,८६७ मिटरको उचाइमा छ र खुम्बु क्षेत्रको सबैभन्दा ठूलो गुम्बा हो।\", \"यो सन् १९१६ मा लामा गुलुले स्थापना गरेका हुन्, र यसको सम्बन्ध तिब्बतको रोङबुक गुम्बासँग छ।\", \"यो सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पले र फेरि १९ जनवरी १९८९ को आगलागीले नष्ट भयो।\", \"फेरि बनाइएको गुम्बा सन् १९९३ मा प्रतिष्ठित गरियो।\", \"मानी रिम्दु पर्व यहाँ हरेक शरद ऋतुमा मनाइन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Mani Rimdu\", \"note\": \"The Sherpas\' most important festival, held in the tenth Tibetan month (October-November) with masked dances.\", \"month\": \"Kartik\", \"name_np\": \"मानी रिम्दु\", \"note_np\": \"शेर्पाहरूको सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण चाड, तिब्बती पात्रोको दसौँ महिना (अक्टोबर-नोभेम्बर) मा मुकुन्डो नाचसहित मनाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Tengboche_Gompa-1.JPG/1280px-Tengboche_Gompa-1.JPG\", \"author\": \"Moralist\", \"caption\": \"Exterior of Tengboche Gompa\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tengboche_Gompa-1.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Tengboche_Gompa-2.JPG/1280px-Tengboche_Gompa-2.JPG\", \"author\": \"Moralist\", \"caption\": \"The gompa seen from the inner courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tengboche_Gompa-2.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Tengboche_Monastery_Gate.jpg/1280px-Tengboche_Monastery_Gate.jpg\", \"author\": \"Niklassletteland\", \"caption\": \"Painted entrance gate of the monastery\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tengboche_Monastery_Gate.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Tengboche_Monastery1.jpg/1280px-Tengboche_Monastery1.jpg\", \"author\": \"Steve Hicks\", \"caption\": \"Murals and paintings inside the monastery\", \"license\": \"CC BY 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tengboche_Monastery1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Stupa_and_mani_stones_at_Tengboche_Monastery.jpg/1280px-Stupa_and_mani_stones_at_Tengboche_Monastery.jpg\", \"author\": \"Faj2323\", \"caption\": \"Stupa and mani stones at Tengboche\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stupa_and_mani_stones_at_Tengboche_Monastery.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"gumba\", \"roof\": \"flat\", \"notes\": \"Three-storey whitewashed stone gompa with rows of dark maroon-framed windows, gilded roof finial, white chorten and an ornate painted gate with snow lions; Ama Dablam behind.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"whitewashed-stone\", \"colors\": [\"#F2F2F0\", \"#6E2C2C\", \"#C9A227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"prayer-flags\", \"toran\", \"chaityas\", \"carved-windows\", \"lion-statues\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [25, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"snow-peaks\", \"himalaya-backdrop\", \"monks-houses\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(73,'dantakali-temple-dharan','Dantakali Temple','दन्तकाली मन्दिर','Dharan','Koshi','Sunsari',NULL,26.818600,87.290900,'pagoda','Hindu','Dantakali (form of Sati / Kali)',NULL,'Founder unknown; scriptures say a king of Bengal repaired it. A pagoda until the 1934 earthquake, rebuilt with a dome, damaged again in the 1988 earthquake and restored to pagoda form.','unknown','Small two-roofed pagoda with grey roofs, red-orange walls and a gilded pinnacle inside a whitewashed walled compound entered through an arched red gateway on Bijayapur hill. The pagoda form was restored after the 1988 earthquake toppled an earlier dome (gumbaj) roof.',0,'Shakti Peeth on Bijayapur hill in Dharan, said to mark where the tooth of the goddess Sati fell.','Climb the steps of Bijayapur hill above Dharan and pass under the arched red gate. You have come to Dantakali, one of the Shakti Peethas, the places where pieces of the goddess Sati fell to earth. When Sati gave up her life, grieving Shiva wandered the world carrying her body, and parts of it dropped across the land. Here, devotees believe, fell her tooth: danta means tooth, so this is the temple of the tooth of Kali. The Swasthani Bratakatha, a scripture many Nepali families read each winter, mentions this place. The building has had a hard century. It was a pagoda until the earthquake of 1934 knocked it down. It came back with a dome roof, which the 1988 earthquake toppled in turn, and then it was rebuilt as the pagoda you see. Budhasubba and Pindeshwor are both a short walk away. At Dashain the queue of worshippers stretches down the hill.','As Shiva carried the dead body of Sati across the world, her tooth (danta) fell at this spot, making it a Shakti Peeth.','[\"The temple\'s name comes from danta (tooth) and Kali; it marks where Sati\'s tooth is believed to have fallen.\", \"It is mentioned in the Swasthani Bratakatha.\", \"It was a pagoda until the 1934 earthquake, then had a dome roof that fell in the 1988 earthquake.\", \"It lies about 1 km from Pindeshwor and 1.5 km from Budhasubba on Bijayapur hill.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Front_View_Of_Dantakali_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg/1280px-Front_View_Of_Dantakali_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_View_Of_Dantakali_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg','Shalgina.dangi · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,dharan,legend,art,festival,koshi','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dantakali_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60786069\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/travel/2019/11/08/are-you-planning-a-trip-to-dharan-here-are-seven-places-around-the-city-you-would-want-to-visit\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/dantakali-temple\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Dantakali_Temple\"]','धरानको बिजयपुर डाँडामा रहेको शक्तिपीठ, जहाँ सती देवीको दाँत खसेको भनिन्छ।','धरानमाथिको बिजयपुर डाँडाका सिँढी चढ्नुहोस् र मेहराब आकारको रातो ढोकामुनि हिँड्नुहोस्। तपाईं दन्तकालीमा आइपुग्नुभएको छ। यो शक्तिपीठमध्ये एउटा हो, जहाँ सती देवीका अङ्ग पृथ्वीमा खसेका थिए। सतीले प्राण त्यागेपछि शोकमा डुबेका शिव उनको शव बोकेर संसारभर घुमे, र उनका अङ्ग देशभर खसे। भक्तजनको विश्वास अनुसार यहाँ उनको दाँत खस्यो। दन्त भनेको दाँत हो, त्यसैले यो कालीको दाँतको मन्दिर हो। धेरै नेपाली परिवारले हरेक जाडोमा पढ्ने स्वस्थानी व्रतकथामा यो ठाउँको नाम आउँछ। यो मन्दिरले एक कठिन शताब्दी बितायो। सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पले ढाल्नुअघि यो पगोडा थियो। त्यसपछि यो गुम्बजको छानासहित बन्यो, जुन सन् १९८८ को भूकम्पले फेरि ढाल्यो, र अहिले तपाईंले देखेको पगोडाको रूपमा फेरि बनाइयो। बुढासुब्बा र पिण्डेश्वर दुवै थोरै हिँडाइमै छन्। दशैँमा भक्तजनको लाइन डाँडाभर तलसम्म पुग्छ।','शिवले सतीको मृत शरीर बोकेर संसारभर घुम्दा उनको दाँत (दन्त) यही ठाउँमा खस्यो, र यो शक्तिपीठ बन्यो।','[\"मन्दिरको नाम दन्त (दाँत) र कालीबाट आएको हो। सतीको दाँत खसेको मानिने ठाउँ यही हो।\", \"यो स्वस्थानी व्रतकथामा उल्लेख छ।\", \"सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पसम्म यो पगोडा थियो, त्यसपछि गुम्बजको छाना बन्यो, जुन सन् १९८८ को भूकम्पमा ढल्यो।\", \"यो बिजयपुर डाँडामा पिण्डेश्वरबाट करिब १ किमी र बुढासुब्बाबाट १.५ किमी टाढा छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Biggest crowds of the year; a fair is held on the eve of Dashain and animal sacrifices are offered.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"वर्षकै सबैभन्दा ठूलो भीड हुन्छ। दशैँको अघिल्लो साँझ मेला लाग्छ र पशुबलि चढाइन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Teej\", \"note\": \"Many women devotees visit during Teej.\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"तीज\", \"note_np\": \"तीजमा धेरै महिला भक्तजन दर्शन गर्न आउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Dantakali_Temple_As_Seen_Through_The_Main_Gate.jpg/1280px-Dantakali_Temple_As_Seen_Through_The_Main_Gate.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shalgina.dangi\", \"caption\": \"The temple seen through the main gate\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dantakali_Temple_As_Seen_Through_The_Main_Gate.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Side_View_Of_Dantakali_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg/1280px-Side_View_Of_Dantakali_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shalgina.dangi\", \"caption\": \"Side view of Dantakali Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Side_View_Of_Dantakali_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Dantakali_dharan.jpg/1280px-Dantakali_dharan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gunjan Raj Giri\", \"caption\": \"Dantakali temple in Dharan\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dantakali_dharan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Dantakali_Shaktipeeth_in_Dharan.jpg/1280px-Dantakali_Shaktipeeth_in_Dharan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Tdo1993\", \"caption\": \"Dantakali Shaktipeeth\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dantakali_Shaktipeeth_in_Dharan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Dantakali_Temple_02.jpg/1280px-Dantakali_Temple_02.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay Shah\", \"caption\": \"The temple on the slopes of Bijayapur\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dantakali_Temple_02.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"slate\", \"notes\": \"Small two-roof pagoda with grey roofs, red-orange walls and gold pinnacle, seen through a red arched gate with a yellow nameboard in a whitewashed wall.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"ochre-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#C8553D\", \"#B8B8B0\", \"#E2B33C\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"toran\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": 10, \"footprint_m\": [8, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"city-street\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(74,'budha-subba-temple','Budha Subba Temple','बुढासुब्बा मन्दिर','Dharan','Koshi','Sunsari',NULL,26.823268,87.293656,'sculpture','Other','Budha Subba (spirit of the Limbu king Buddhi Karna Raya Khebang); also linked with Shiva and Parvati as Theba Sammang an',NULL,'Said to be the tomb of Buddhi Karna Raya Khebang, last Limbu king of Bijaypur, killed in 1773; date of the shrine itself not documented.','unknown','Small Kirat shrine on Bijayapur hill: an open pavilion with a low hipped roof and red pillars beside a yellow arched shrine, set in a grove of tuftless bamboo hung with sacred threads and bells.',0,'Kirat shrine in a bamboo grove in Dharan, said to be the tomb of the last Limbu king of Bijaypur.','Step into the bamboo grove on Bijayapur hill in Dharan and listen to the stems creak in the wind. This is Budha Subba, a shrine of the Kirat people, and its story is a sad one. Bijaypur was once a capital of the Limbuwan kingdom. In 1773 its last Limbu king, Buddhi Karna Raya Khebang, was lured here for talks and killed by assassins sent by the Gorkhali king. People say his spirit stayed near his tomb, friendly and helpful, and local Limbus began to worship him as the old king, the Budha Subba, who brings good luck. Now look closely at the bamboo. Some say Shiva and Parvati, disguised as a Limbu king and queen, once planted their hunting bows here, and these bamboos grew from them without tufts at the top. Young couples used to carve their names on the stems; today they tie colourful threads instead and hope their love lasts.','Shiva and Parvati, in the guise of the Yakthung king and queen Theba Sammang and Yuma Sammang, stuck their bows into the ground here while hunting; tuftless bamboo sprouted from the bows.','[\"The shrine is said to be the tomb of Buddhi Karna Raya Khebang, the last Limbu king of Bijaypur, killed in 1773.\", \"Bijaypur was a capital of the Limbuwan kingdom according to historian Iman Singh Chemjong.\", \"The bamboo here grows without a tuft at the top, which legend links to Shiva and Parvati\'s bows.\", \"Couples once wrote their names on the bamboo; the temple committee stopped this, and threads are tied instead.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Budha_Subba_Temple_Front_View.jpg/1280px-Budha_Subba_Temple_Front_View.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budha_Subba_Temple_Front_View.jpg','Pushpendra khadka · CC BY-SA 4.0','sculpture,other,dharan,legend,koshi','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budha_Subba_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4985069\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/9796128091\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budha_Subba_Temple_Front_View.jpg\"]','धरानको बाँसघारीभित्रको किराँत मन्दिर, विजयपुरका अन्तिम लिम्बू राजाको समाधि भनिने।','धरानको विजयपुर डाँडाको बाँसघारीभित्र पस्नुहोस् र हावामा बाँसका ठाँटहरू चर्केको सुन्नुहोस्। यो बुढासुब्बा हो, किराँत जातिको मन्दिर, र यसको कथा दुःखद छ। विजयपुर कुनै बेला लिम्बूवान राज्यको राजधानी थियो। सन् १७७३ मा यसका अन्तिम लिम्बू राजा बुद्धिकर्ण राय खेबाङलाई वार्ताका लागि यहाँ बोलाइयो, र गोर्खाली राजाले पठाएका हत्याराले उनलाई मारे। मानिस भन्छन्, उनको आत्मा उनको समाधिनजिकै रह्यो, मिलनसार र सहयोगी भएर। स्थानीय लिम्बूले उनलाई शुभ गराउने पुरानो राजा, बुढा सुब्बा मानेर पुज्न थाले। अब बाँसलाई नजिकबाट हेर्नुहोस्। कसैले भन्छन्, लिम्बू राजा र रानीको भेषमा शिव र पार्वतीले यहीँ सिकारका बेला आफ्ना धनुष रोपे, र ती धनुषबाट टुप्पोमा झुप्पा नभएका यी बाँस उम्रिए। पहिले जवान जोडीले बाँसका ठाँटमा आफ्नो नाम कुँदेर लेख्थे। आजकल उनीहरू रङ्गीन धागो बाँध्छन् र आफ्नो माया टिकिरहोस् भनी कामना गर्छन्।','याक्थुङ राजा र रानी थेबा साम्माङ र युमा साम्माङको भेषमा शिव र पार्वतीले सिकार खेल्दा यहाँ भुइँमा आफ्ना धनुष रोपे। ती धनुषबाट झुप्पा नभएको बाँस उम्रियो।','[\"यो मन्दिर विजयपुरका अन्तिम लिम्बू राजा बुद्धिकर्ण राय खेबाङको समाधि भनिन्छ। उनलाई सन् १७७३ मा मारिएको थियो।\", \"इतिहासकार इमानसिंह चेम्जोङका अनुसार विजयपुर लिम्बूवान राज्यको एउटा राजधानी थियो।\", \"यहाँको बाँस टुप्पोमा झुप्पा नभई उम्रन्छ, जसलाई किंवदन्तीले शिव र पार्वतीका धनुषसँग जोड्छ।\", \"जोडीले पहिले बाँसमा आफ्नो नाम लेख्थे। मन्दिर समितिले त्यो रोक्यो, र अहिले धागो बाँधिन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/96/Colorful_Threads_%283965274345%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prashant Shrestha from Kathmandu, Nepal\", \"caption\": \"Colourful threads tied by visitors\", \"license\": \"CC BY 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colorful_Threads_(3965274345).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Bells_at_a_Temple.jpg/1280px-Bells_at_a_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Lordsamp\", \"caption\": \"Temple bells at Budhasubba\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bells_at_a_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Side_View_Of_Budhasubba_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg/1280px-Side_View_Of_Budhasubba_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shalgina.dangi\", \"caption\": \"Side view of the shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Side_View_Of_Budhasubba_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Budhasubba_Dharan.jpg/1280px-Budhasubba_Dharan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Bhatta\", \"caption\": \"Tuftless bamboo grove at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budhasubba_Dharan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Budha_Subba_Temple_North_View.jpg/1280px-Budha_Subba_Temple_North_View.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pushpendra khadka\", \"caption\": \"North view of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budha_Subba_Temple_North_View.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"statue\", \"roof\": \"flat\", \"notes\": \"Low open pavilion with a pale green hipped roof and red posts beside a bright yellow arched shrine, inside a bamboo grove hung with threads.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"timber\", \"colors\": [\"#E3C832\", \"#B22222\", \"#6B8E23\"], \"features\": [\"bell\", \"sacred-tree\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": 5, \"footprint_m\": [10, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"sacred-grove\", \"forest\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(75,'pindeshwor-babadham','Pindeshwor Babadham','पिण्डेश्वर बाबाधाम','Dharan','Koshi','Sunsari',NULL,26.813300,87.294600,'shikhara','Hindu','Shiva (Pindeshwor)',NULL,'Founding date not documented in the sources consulted; local scholar Prem Prasad Parajuli says the temple is mentioned in 18 chapters of the Skanda Purana.','unknown','Orange-painted shikhara-style Shiva temple with a tall spire and trident, joined to a long arcaded hall of arched openings, in a walled compound in Dharan-14. Oil lamps are kept burning continuously inside.',0,'Shiva temple in Dharan where Shrawan pilgrims walk barefoot from Barahachhetra carrying Koshi water to pour on the lingam.','You are at Pindeshwor Babadham in Dharan, a temple of Lord Shiva that comes alive in the monsoon month of Shrawan. Every Monday of that month, thousands of devotees arrive on foot, many barefoot, chanting Bol Bam. They have walked more than twenty kilometres from Barahachhetra, carrying pots of holy water from the Saptakoshi river, to pour over Shiva here. Devotees say wishes come true if you offer Koshi and Koka water at Barahachhetra, then water from the Kaushiki bank here at Pindeshwor. Look up at the orange spire and its trident, then at the long row of arches beside it. Inside, oil lamps are never allowed to go out. A local scholar says this place appears in eighteen chapters of the Skanda Purana, and people also link it to the origin of rudraksha beads. Dantakali and Budhasubba are just up the hill, so many pilgrims visit all three together.','Local belief links the site to the origin of rudraksha beads and says it appears in 18 chapters of the Skanda Purana.','[\"On every Monday of Shrawan, devotees carry Saptakoshi water from Barahachhetra, many walking barefoot over 20 km.\", \"Oil lamps are kept burning continuously in the temple.\", \"Maha Shivaratri and Bala Chaturdashi are also major festivals here.\", \"A Pindeshwor Rath Yatra chariot festival around Dharan Bazaar was held for the second time in March 2026.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_15.jpg/1280px-Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_15.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_15.jpg','Bijay Shah · CC BY-SA 4.0','shikhara,hindu,dharan,legend,festival,koshi','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pindeshwor_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60751045\", \"https://en.himalpress.com/devotees-throng-pindeshwar-temple-in-pictures/\", \"https://ekantipur.com/koshi-pradesh/2026/03/19/en/pindeshwor-rath-yatra-in-dharan-23-49.html\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Pindeshwor_Temple\"]','धरानको शिव मन्दिर, जहाँ श्रावणमा तीर्थयात्री बराहक्षेत्रबाट खाली खुट्टा कोशीको पानी बोकेर शिवलिङ्गमा चढाउन हिँड्छन्।','तपाईं धरानको पिण्डेश्वर बाबाधाममा हुनुहुन्छ। यो भगवान् शिवको मन्दिर हो, जो वर्षा महिना श्रावणमा रौनकमय हुन्छ। त्यस महिनाको हरेक सोमबार हजारौँ भक्तजन \'बोल बम\' भन्दै हिँडेर आइपुग्छन्, धेरैजना खाली खुट्टा। उनीहरू बराहक्षेत्रबाट बीस किलोमिटरभन्दा बढी हिँडेर, सप्तकोशी नदीको पवित्र जलको घडा बोकेर यहाँ शिवलाई चढाउन आउँछन्। भक्तजन भन्छन्, बराहक्षेत्रमा कोशी र कोकाको पानी चढाएर त्यसपछि यहाँ पिण्डेश्वरमा कौशिकीको किनारको पानी चढाए मनोकामना पूरा हुन्छ। सुन्तला रङको शिखर र त्रिशूल हेर्नुहोस्, अनि छेउको मेहराबको लामो लहर। भित्र तेलका दियो कहिल्यै निभ्न दिइँदैन। एक जना स्थानीय विद्वान भन्छन्, यो ठाउँको नाम स्कन्द पुराणका अठारह अध्यायमा आउँछ, र मानिस यसलाई रुद्राक्षको उत्पत्तिसँग पनि जोड्छन्। दन्तकाली र बुढासुब्बा डाँडामाथि नै छन्, त्यसैले धेरै तीर्थयात्री तीनै ठाउँ सँगै दर्शन गर्छन्।','स्थानीय विश्वासले यो ठाउँलाई रुद्राक्षको उत्पत्तिसँग जोड्छ, र स्कन्द पुराणका १८ अध्यायमा यसको नाम आउँछ भन्छ।','[\"श्रावणको हरेक सोमबार भक्तजन बराहक्षेत्रबाट सप्तकोशीको पानी बोकेर २० किमीभन्दा बढी हिँड्छन्, धेरैजना खाली खुट्टा।\", \"मन्दिरमा तेलका दियो निरन्तर बलिरहन्छन्।\", \"महाशिवरात्रि र बाला चतुर्दशी पनि यहाँका प्रमुख चाड हुन्।\", \"धरान बजारवरिपरि पिण्डेश्वर रथयात्रा, अर्थात् रथको चाड, दोस्रो पटक सन् २०२६ को मार्चमा मनाइएको थियो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Shrawan Mondays (Bol Bam)\", \"note\": \"Devotees walk from Barahachhetra with Saptakoshi water to pour on Shiva every Monday.\", \"month\": \"Shrawan\", \"name_np\": \"श्रावण सोमबार (बोल बम)\", \"note_np\": \"भक्तजन हरेक सोमबार बराहक्षेत्रबाट सप्तकोशीको जल बोकेर पैदल हिँडेर शिवलिङ्गमा चढाउँछन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Major night of Shiva worship at the temple.\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"मन्दिरमा शिवपूजाको सबैभन्दा ठूलो रात।\"}, {\"name\": \"Bala Chaturdashi\", \"note\": \"Annual festival observed at the temple.\", \"month\": \"Mangsir\", \"name_np\": \"बाला चतुर्दशी\", \"note_np\": \"मन्दिरमा मनाइने वार्षिक चाड।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Panorama_View_Of_Pindeswari_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg/1280px-Panorama_View_Of_Pindeswari_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shalgina.dangi\", \"caption\": \"Panorama of the Pindeshwor temple complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_View_Of_Pindeswari_Temple_Of_Dharan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Pindeshwar_Mahadev.jpg/1280px-Pindeshwar_Mahadev.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rishavkhatri\", \"caption\": \"Pindeshwar Mahadev\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindeshwar_Mahadev.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Pindeshwar_Temple_01.jpg/1280px-Pindeshwar_Temple_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prabina Karki\", \"caption\": \"Pindeshwar Temple, Dharan\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindeshwar_Temple_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_16.jpg/1280px-Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_16.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay Shah\", \"caption\": \"Pindeshwor temple courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_16.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_17.jpg/1280px-Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_17.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay Shah\", \"caption\": \"Another view of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindeshwor_Temple-Dharan_17.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"stone-spire\", \"notes\": \"Orange pointed shikhara spire with a trident, attached to a long low orange hall with a row of arched openings.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"ochre-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#E07B39\", \"#B5452E\", \"#F2D16B\"], \"features\": [\"trident\", \"arched-windows\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"lamps-diyo\", \"flags-red\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [30, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"city-street\", \"garden-lawn\", \"hilltop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(76,'makwanpur-gadhi','Makwanpur Gadhi','मकवानपुरगढी','Hetauda (Makwanpurgadhi Rural Municipality)','Bagmati','Makwanpur',NULL,27.411027,85.147508,'fort','Other',NULL,NULL,'Stronghold of the Sen kings of Makwanpur; Wikipedia credits Tula Sen, while Ekantipur says Luhang built it in VS 1622 (c. 1565). Captured by Gorkha in VS 1819 (1762-63).','Sen','Hilltop stone fort at about 1,017 m, surrounded by a wall about 25 ft high and 7 ft wide and a 10-ft-deep defensive ditch, enclosing the ruined walls of the Sen palace. Old cannons such as the \'Kali Top\' are displayed in the grounds.',0,'Hilltop stone fort of the Sen kings near Hetauda, fought over by Gorkha in 1762-63 and by the British in 1816.','You are standing inside Makwanpur Gadhi, about 1,000 metres up on a ridge east of Hetauda. Before Nepal was unified, this stone fort was the stronghold of the Sen kings of Makwanpur. Run your hand along the wall: it once rose about 25 feet and was 7 feet thick, with a ditch 10 feet deep outside to stop attackers. The Sens and the Shahs were family. King Hemkarna Sen\'s daughter, Indra Kumari, married Prithvi Narayan Shah of Gorkha. Yet family ties did not keep the peace. Prithvi Narayan Shah\'s forces attacked and took this fort in 1762, and fought here again the next year against the army of Mir Kasim, the Nawab of Bengal. In 1816 it saw battle once more, in the war with the British East India Company. Look for the old iron cannon called Kali Top. In 2015 Nepal Post put this fort on a postage stamp.','Ekantipur reports a story that Hemkarna Sen promised a white elephant as dowry to his son-in-law Prithvi Narayan Shah, but his son Digbandhan Sen refused to hand it over, souring relations before the conquest.','[\"The fort was the main stronghold of the Sen dynasty of Makwanpur before Nepal\'s unification.\", \"Battles of Makwanpur were fought here in 1762, 1763 and 1816.\", \"Its wall is described as about 25 ft high and 7 ft wide, with a 10-ft-deep defensive ditch.\", \"It sits at about 1,017 m, roughly 16-17 km from Hetauda.\", \"The Government of Nepal issued a postage stamp featuring the fort in 2015.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Ruin_Makwanpur_Gadi_Palace.JPG/1280px-Ruin_Makwanpur_Gadi_Palace.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruin_Makwanpur_Gadi_Palace.JPG','Rajivkilanashrestha · CC BY-SA 4.0','fort,other,sen,hetauda (makwanpurgadhi rural municipality),legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makwanpur_Gadhi\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makwanpurgadhi\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q109905451\", \"https://english.ratopati.com/story/82642/arent-you-going-to-visit-hetauda-during-dashain-and-tihar-holidays\", \"https://ekantipur.com/bagmati-pradesh/2026/01/24/en/victory-festival-celebrated-at-makwanpur-fort-20-35.html\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/exploring-makwanpur\"]','हेटौँडा नजिकको सेन राजाहरूको डाँडाको ढुङ्गाको किल्ला, जसका लागि सन् १७६२-६३ मा गोर्खाले र सन् १८१६ मा अङ्ग्रेजले लडाइँ गरे।','तपाईं हेटौँडाको पूर्वतिरको डाँडामा करिब १,००० मिटर माथि मकवानपुरगढीभित्र उभिनुभएको छ। नेपाल एकीकरण हुनुअघि यो ढुङ्गाको किल्ला मकवानपुरका सेन राजाहरूको गढ थियो। पर्खालमा हात फेर्नुहोस्। यो कुनै बेला करिब २५ फिट अग्लो र ७ फिट बाक्लो थियो, र आक्रमणकारी रोक्न बाहिर १० फिट गहिरो खाल्डो थियो। सेन र शाह नातेदार थिए। राजा हेमकर्ण सेनकी छोरी इन्द्र कुमारीको विवाह गोरखाका पृथ्वीनारायण शाहसँग भएको थियो। तैपनि नातेदारीले शान्ति टिकाउन सकेन। पृथ्वीनारायण शाहको सेनाले सन् १७६२ मा यो किल्लामा आक्रमण गरी कब्जा गर्‍यो, र अर्को वर्ष बङ्गालका नवाब मीर कासिमको सेनाविरुद्ध यहीँ फेरि लड्यो। सन् १८१६ मा ब्रिटिश ईस्ट इन्डिया कम्पनीसँगको युद्धमा यहाँ फेरि लडाइँ भयो। काली तोप भनिने पुरानो फलामको तोप खोज्नुहोस्। सन् २०१५ मा नेपाल हुलाकले यो किल्लाको चित्र भएको हुलाक टिकट निकाल्यो।','एकान्तिपुरका अनुसार हेमकर्ण सेनले ज्वाइँ पृथ्वीनारायण शाहलाई दाइजोमा सेतो हात्ती दिने वचन दिएका थिए, तर उनका छोरा दिग्बन्धन सेनले दिन मानेनन्, र विजयअघि नै सम्बन्ध बिग्रियो भन्ने कथा छ।','[\"किल्ला नेपाल एकीकरणअघि मकवानपुरका सेन वंशको मुख्य गढ थियो।\", \"मकवानपुरका युद्ध यहाँ सन् १७६२, १७६३ र १८१६ मा लडिए।\", \"यसको पर्खाल करिब २५ फिट अग्लो र ७ फिट चौडा, र बाहिर १० फिट गहिरो सुरक्षा खाल्डो भएको बताइन्छ।\", \"यो करिब १,०१७ मिटरको उचाइमा, हेटौँडाबाट करिब १६-१७ किमी टाढा छ।\", \"नेपाल सरकारले सन् २०१५ मा यो किल्लाको चित्र भएको हुलाक टिकट निकाल्यो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Victory festival\", \"note\": \"Celebrated at the fort on Magh 10, the date given for the Gorkhali attack of VS 1819.\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"विजय उत्सव\", \"note_np\": \"वि.सं. १८१९ को गोरखाली आक्रमणको मिति मानिने माघ १० गते गढीमा मनाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Makwanpur_Gadhi.JPG/1280px-Makwanpur_Gadhi.JPG\", \"author\": \"Krish Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Stone walls of the fort above the fields\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Makwanpur_Gadhi.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Kali_Top.JPG/1280px-Kali_Top.JPG\", \"author\": \"Krish Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Kali Top, the historic cannon of the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kali_Top.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Makwanpurgadhi_staircase.jpg/1280px-Makwanpurgadhi_staircase.jpg\", \"author\": \"Subodhpaudel123\", \"caption\": \"Staircase leading up to the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Makwanpurgadhi_staircase.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Cannon_makwanpur.JPG/1280px-Cannon_makwanpur.JPG\", \"author\": \"Krish Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Another cannon displayed at the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cannon_makwanpur.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"fort\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Roofless ruined rectangle of thick dark rubble-stone walls with a grassy interior and a narrow ditch, on a green ridge above terraced fields.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#5E5A50\", \"#7A8B4A\", \"#3F3B35\"], \"features\": [], \"height_m\": 7.6, \"footprint_m\": [40, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"terraced-fields\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(77,'upardang-gadhi','Upardang Gadhi','उपरदाङगढी','Ichchhakamana Rural Municipality (near Bharatpur)','Bagmati','Chitwan',NULL,27.761667,84.582778,'fort','Other',NULL,NULL,'Sources differ: Nepal Traveller credits Shatrubhanjan Shah, grandson of Prithvi Narayan Shah, during the war with the British; Ekantipur links it to the Sen era. It was Chitwan\'s headquarters until the early 1960s.','Shah (disputed; some sources say Sen)','Hilltop fort at about 1,275 m enclosed by a carved stone wall, with a weapon house (Kot Ghar), a well, a two-room house, a gate, a wooden bridge and a temple inside; the Department of Archaeology notes its walls, defensive ditch and entry tunnel.',0,'Stone hill fort above the Chitwan valley, once the valley\'s capital and Chitwan\'s district headquarters until the 1960s.','You have climbed to Upardang Gadhi, 1,275 metres up in the hills of northern Chitwan, about an hour\'s ride from Bharatpur. Look down: the whole Chitwan valley spreads out below, and this is why the fort was built here. Before Nepal\'s unification, this valley was its own small kingdom, and its historic capital was right here at Upardang. Walk along the low stone walls. Historians do not fully agree on who built them. One account credits Shatrubhanjan Shah, grandson of Prithvi Narayan Shah, who strengthened the fort during the war with the British; another links it to the earlier Sen kings. Inside, find the old weapon house, the well and the small temple. Until the early 1960s this was Chitwan\'s district headquarters, and land revenue was collected here long after. Cannons and shells have been recovered from the site, and restoration began in 2023 with the Department of Archaeology.',NULL,'[\"Before Nepal\'s unification, Upardanggadhi was the historic capital of the Chitwan valley kingdom.\", \"The fort sits at about 1,275 m above sea level.\", \"It was Chitwan\'s district headquarters until the early 1960s, before the move to Bharatpur.\", \"Cannons, shells and old weapons have been recovered from the fort.\", \"Renovation in coordination with the Department of Archaeology began in 2023.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,NULL,'https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_095440.jpg/1280px-Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_095440.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_095440.jpg','Bharatadhikarimb · CC BY-SA 4.0','fort,other,shah (disputed; some sources say sen),ichchhakamana rural municipality (near bharatpur),art,bagmati','[\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q109658342\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chitwan_Valley\", \"https://www.nepaltraveller.com/news/renovation-of-upardanggarhi-chitwans-historical-fort\", \"https://ekantipur.com/news/2026/01/08/en/chandi-cannon-rises-above-danggarhi-photos-08-57.html\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Upardanggadhi\"]','चितवन उपत्यकामाथिको ढुङ्गाको डाँडे किल्ला, एक समय उपत्यकाको राजधानी र सन् १९६० को दशकसम्म चितवनको जिल्ला सदरमुकाम।','तपाईं उत्तरी चितवनका डाँडामा १,२७५ मिटरको उचाइमा रहेको उपरदाङगढीमा पुग्नुभएको छ। भरतपुरबाट यहाँ पुग्न करिब एक घण्टा लाग्छ। तल हेर्नुहोस्। सारा चितवन उपत्यका तल फैलिएको छ, र यही कारणले यहाँ किल्ला बनाइएको थियो। नेपाल एकीकरणअघि यो उपत्यका आफ्नै सानो राज्य थियो, र यसको ऐतिहासिक राजधानी यहीँ उपरदाङमा थियो। होचा ढुङ्गाका पर्खालछेउछेउ हिँड्नुहोस्। यो कसले बनाए भन्नेमा इतिहासकार पूरै एकमत छैनन्। एउटा विवरणले पृथ्वीनारायण शाहका नाति शत्रुभञ्जन शाहलाई श्रेय दिन्छ, जसले अङ्ग्रेजसँगको युद्धमा किल्ला बलियो बनाएका थिए। अर्कोले यसलाई पहिलेका सेन राजासँग जोड्छ। भित्र पुरानो हतियार घर, इनार र सानो मन्दिर खोज्नुहोस्। सन् १९६० को दशकको सुरुसम्म यो चितवनको जिल्ला सदरमुकाम थियो, र त्यसपछि पनि लामो समय यहीँ मालपोत उठाइन्थ्यो। यो ठाउँबाट तोप र गोला भेटिएका छन्, र सन् २०२३ मा पुरातत्त्व विभागसँग मिलेर पुनर्स्थापना सुरु भयो।',NULL,'[\"नेपाल एकीकरणअघि उपरदाङगढी चितवन उपत्यका राज्यको ऐतिहासिक राजधानी थियो।\", \"किल्ला समुद्र सतहभन्दा करिब १,२७५ मिटरको उचाइमा छ।\", \"भरतपुरमा सदरमुकाम सर्नुअघि, सन् १९६० को दशकको सुरुसम्म, यो चितवनको जिल्ला सदरमुकाम थियो।\", \"किल्लाबाट तोप, गोला र पुराना हतियार भेटिएका छन्।\", \"पुरातत्त्व विभागसँगको समन्वयमा नवीकरण सन् २०२३ मा सुरु भयो।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Upardanggadhi.jpg/1280px-Upardanggadhi.jpg\", \"author\": \"Dhrubaadhikary\", \"caption\": \"Upardanggadhi fort, Chitwan\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Upardanggadhi.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_092501.jpg/1280px-Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_092501.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bharatadhikarimb\", \"caption\": \"Remains inside the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_092501.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_103959.jpg/1280px-Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_103959.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bharatadhikarimb\", \"caption\": \"Stone walls of the fort\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_103959.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_104006.jpg/1280px-Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_104006.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bharatadhikarimb\", \"caption\": \"Fort grounds on the hilltop\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_104006.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_104630.jpg/1280px-Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_104630.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bharatadhikarimb\", \"caption\": \"View around Upardanggadhi\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Upardanggadhi_Chitwan_20180303_104630.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"fort\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Low dark stone walls outlining rectangular rooms and a compound on a dry grassy hilltop, with hazy forested ridges behind.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#4A4540\", \"#B49A62\", \"#6E7C5A\"], \"features\": [], \"height_m\": 2, \"footprint_m\": [60, 40], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(78,'maya-devi-temple-lumbini','Maya Devi Temple','मायादेवी मन्दिर','Lumbini','Lumbini','Rupandehi',NULL,27.469609,83.275831,'archaeological-site','Buddhist','Maya Devi (mother of the Buddha); nativity of Siddhartha Gautama',2003,'Sacred space first marked in the 6th century BCE (timber shrine found 2013); brick temple of Ashoka\'s time c. 249 BCE; rebuilt 1939 under Kaiser Shumsher; present protective temple built 2003 by the Lumbini Development Trust','Maurya (original brick shrine)','Plain white rectangular protective building raised over the excavated brick foundations of earlier shrines. Inside, a raised walkway circles the ruins down to the marker stone of the Buddha\'s birth and the worn stone nativity sculpture.',1,'The temple over the marker stone that Buddhists venerate as the exact spot where Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha, was born.','Take off your shoes and step inside quietly. Under this plain white roof lies one of the most sacred spots on earth for Buddhists. Tradition says Queen Maya Devi was travelling to her parents\' home in Devdaha when she stopped in the Lumbini garden, held the branch of a sal tree, and gave birth to Prince Siddhartha, who became the Buddha. Walk the raised path and look down at the old brick foundations. Emperor Ashoka\'s builders laid bricks here around 249 BCE, and in 2013 archaeologists working under this floor found traces of a timber shrine from the sixth century BCE, among the earliest Buddhist shrines known in South Asia. Follow the line of pilgrims to a small stone under glass: the marker stone of the birth. Nearby is the worn nativity sculpture, showing Maya holding the branch with her sister Prajapati at her side. Outside, the Puskarini pond is where Maya is said to have bathed before the birth.','Before the birth, Queen Maya dreamed that a white elephant carrying a lotus entered her right side, a sign interpreted as the coming of a great ruler or a Buddha. She gave birth standing, holding a sal branch in the Lumbini garden, and died seven days later.','[\"The temple houses the marker stone and the nativity sculpture linked to the Buddha\'s birth.\", \"Excavations by UNESCO, Durham University, Nepal\'s Department of Archaeology and the Lumbini Development Trust began in 2010.\", \"In 2013 the team reported a timber shrine dated to the 6th century BCE beneath the brick temple.\", \"The present temple building was completed in 2003 by the Lumbini Development Trust.\", \"Lumbini was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1997.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,700,20,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/1_Lumbini%2C_Maya_Devi_Temple.jpg/1280px-1_Lumbini%2C_Maya_Devi_Temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1_Lumbini,_Maya_Devi_Temple.jpg','Ricky Partel · CC BY-SA 4.0','archaeological-site,buddhist,maurya (original brick shrine),lumbini,unesco,legend,art','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maya_Devi_Temple,_Lumbini\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumbini\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q15238480\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/343151593\", \"https://lumbinidevtrust.gov.np/page/2_669b8de37d303\", \"https://ekantipur.com/lumbini-pradesh/2026/05/17/en/arbitrary-increase-in-mayadevi-temple-entry-fee-locals-protest-against-high-entry-fee-42-00.html\", \"https://www.historyhit.com/locations/maya-devi-temple/\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Maya_Devi_Temple,_Lumbini\"]','बौद्धहरूले सिद्धार्थ गौतम, अर्थात् बुद्ध जन्मेको ठ्याक्कै ठाउँ मान्ने चिह्न ढुङ्गामाथि बनेको मन्दिर।','जुत्ता खोलेर चुपचाप भित्र पस्नुहोस्। यो सादा सेतो छानामुनि बौद्धहरूका लागि संसारकै सबैभन्दा पवित्र ठाउँ मध्ये एउटा छ। परम्परा अनुसार रानी मायादेवी देवदहमा रहेको माइत जाँदै गर्दा लुम्बिनीको बगैँचामा रोकिइन्, सालको हाँगा समातिन् र राजकुमार सिद्धार्थलाई जन्म दिइन्, जो पछि बुद्ध भए। माथिको बाटोमा हिँडेर तल पुराना इँटाका जग हेर्नुहोस्। सम्राट अशोकका कारिगरले यहाँ करिब 249 ई.पू. मा इँटा बिछ्याएका थिए। सन् 2013 मा यही भुइँमुनि काम गर्दै गरेका पुरातत्त्वविद्हरूले ई.पू. छैटौँ शताब्दीको काठको मन्दिरका चिह्न भेटे, जुन दक्षिण एसियाका सबैभन्दा पुराना बौद्ध मन्दिरमध्ये मानिन्छ। तीर्थयात्रीको लाइन पछ्याएर सिसामुनिको सानो ढुङ्गासम्म पुग्नुहोस्। त्यो नै जन्मको चिह्न ढुङ्गा हो। नजिकै घिसिएको जन्मको मूर्ति छ, जसमा माया सालको हाँगा समातेर उभिएकी र छेउमा उनकी बहिनी प्रजापति छिन्। बाहिर पुष्करिणी पोखरी छ, जहाँ जन्म दिनुअघि माया नुहाएकी थिइन् भनिन्छ।','जन्म हुनुअघि रानी मायाले सपना देखिन्, कमलको फूल बोकेको एउटा सेतो हात्ती उनको दायाँ कोखमा पस्यो। यसलाई महान् शासक वा बुद्ध जन्मने सङ्केत मानियो। उनले लुम्बिनीको बगैँचामा सालको हाँगा समातेर उभिँदै बच्चा जन्माइन् र सात दिनपछि बितिन्।','[\"मन्दिरभित्र बुद्धको जन्मसँग जोडिएको चिह्न ढुङ्गा र जन्मको मूर्ति राखिएका छन्।\", \"युनेस्को, डरहम विश्वविद्यालय, नेपालको पुरातत्त्व विभाग र लुम्बिनी विकास कोषले सन् 2010 मा उत्खनन सुरु गरे।\", \"सन् 2013 मा टोलीले इँटाको मन्दिरमुनि ई.पू. छैटौँ शताब्दीको काठको मन्दिर भेटिएको जानकारी दियो।\", \"अहिलेको मन्दिर भवन सन् 2003 मा लुम्बिनी विकास कोषले बनाइसकेको हो।\", \"लुम्बिनी सन् 1997 मा युनेस्कोको विश्व सम्पदा सूचीमा परेको हो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Buddha Jayanti\", \"note\": \"Full-moon day of Baisakh marking the Buddha\'s birth; pilgrims gather in the Sacred Garden around the temple.\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"बुद्ध जयन्ती\", \"note_np\": \"बुद्धको जन्मको सम्झनामा बैशाख पूर्णिमाका दिन मनाइन्छ। मन्दिर वरिपरिको पवित्र उद्यानमा तीर्थयात्री भेला हुन्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Evening_view_of_Maya_Devi_Temple%2C_Lumbini.jpg/1280px-Evening_view_of_Maya_Devi_Temple%2C_Lumbini.jpg\", \"author\": \"Arjun Bhadra Khanal\", \"caption\": \"The white temple in evening light\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evening_view_of_Maya_Devi_Temple,_Lumbini.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/67/Marker_stone_of_exact_birth_place_of_Buddha.jpg\", \"author\": \"Jonas Maria E. at en.wikipedia\", \"caption\": \"The marker stone of the Buddha\'s birth inside the temple\", \"license\": \"Public domain\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marker_stone_of_exact_birth_place_of_Buddha.jpg\", \"license_url\": null}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Exact_Birth_Place_of_the_Buddha_lumbini_IMG_20160201_151524.jpg/1280px-Exact_Birth_Place_of_the_Buddha_lumbini_IMG_20160201_151524.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ricky Partel\", \"caption\": \"Pilgrims at the birth spot inside the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Exact_Birth_Place_of_the_Buddha_lumbini_IMG_20160201_151524.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Ancient_Wall_outside_Maya_Devi_Temple.jpg/1280px-Ancient_Wall_outside_Maya_Devi_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Santosh Khatiwada\", \"caption\": \"Ancient brick foundations outside the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Wall_outside_Maya_Devi_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Maya_Devi_Temple_and_Ashoka_Pillar%2C_Lumbini%2C_Rupandehi%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Maya_Devi_Temple_and_Ashoka_Pillar%2C_Lumbini%2C_Rupandehi%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"The temple with the Ashoka pillar in the Sacred Garden\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maya_Devi_Temple_and_Ashoka_Pillar,_Lumbini,_Rupandehi,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"flat\", \"notes\": \"Low, boxy white building with a small raised upper block and pinnacle; red-brick ruins, the Ashoka pillar and a pond with a prayer-flag-hung bodhi tree beside it. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#F2F0EA\", \"#B5643C\", \"#4F7A3A\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"prayer-flags\", \"sacred-tree\", \"stone-pillar\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 12, \"footprint_m\": [40, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"garden-lawn\", \"pond\", \"sacred-grove\", \"plains-fields\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(79,'ashoka-pillar-lumbini','Ashoka Pillar, Lumbini','लुम्बिनीको अशोक स्तम्भ','Lumbini','Lumbini','Rupandehi',NULL,27.469681,83.275668,'pillar','Buddhist',NULL,-249,'3rd century BCE (traditionally c. 249 BCE), set up by the Mauryan emperor Ashoka on his visit to the Buddha\'s birthplace; inscription found in December 1896','Maurya','Polished sandstone monolith standing inside a low railing beside the Maya Devi Temple. The lower part, buried for centuries, carries a five-line Brahmi inscription in Prakrit; a later inscription of King Ripu Malla is cut higher up. The horse capital described by Xuanzang is lost.',1,'Emperor Ashoka\'s stone pillar whose Brahmi inscription declares that the Buddha Shakyamuni was born here.','Stand by the railing and look at this smooth grey column. Around 249 BCE the Mauryan emperor Ashoka came here on pilgrimage, twenty years after his coronation, and had this pillar raised. For centuries it lay half buried and forgotten, until December 1896, when a Nepali team led by General Khadga Shumsher Rana dug around its base, with the archaeologist Alois Führer close by. Low down they found five lines of Brahmi script that say, in short: the king came himself and worshipped, because here the Buddha Shakyamuni was born. He also made the village of Lumbini free of taxes, paying only an eighth share. Those words turned a forgotten mound into the recognised birthplace of the Buddha. Look higher and you may spot a later line, Om mani padme hum, carved for King Ripu Malla in the fourteenth century. The Chinese pilgrim Xuanzang saw a horse on top; today the crown is gone.',NULL,'[\"The Brahmi inscription was uncovered in December 1896 by General Khadga Shumsher Rana\'s team, with Alois Anton Führer.\", \"It records that Ashoka visited twenty years after his anointing because the Buddha Shakyamuni was born here.\", \"The inscription says Ashoka made Lumbini village tax-free, paying only an eighth share of produce.\", \"A later inscription on the pillar reads \'Om mani padme hum\' with the name of King Ripu Malla, dated Saka 1234.\", \"Ashoka scholar Harry Falk calls the inscription\'s authenticity \'beyond dispute\'.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,700,20,20,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/BRP_Lumbini_Ashoka_pillar.jpg/1280px-BRP_Lumbini_Ashoka_pillar.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BRP_Lumbini_Ashoka_pillar.jpg','Bibek Raj Pandeya · CC BY-SA 4.0','pillar,buddhist,maurya,lumbini,unesco,art','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumbini_pillar_inscription\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumbini\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pillars_of_Ashoka\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q85782651\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/4285950089\", \"https://lumbinidevtrust.gov.np/page/2_669b8de37d303\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Ashoka_pillar_(Lumbini)\"]','सम्राट अशोकको ढुङ्गाको स्तम्भ, जसको ब्राह्मी शिलालेखले शाक्यमुनि बुद्ध यहीँ जन्मेका थिए भनेर बताउँछ।','रेलिङको छेउमा उभिएर यो चिल्लो खैरो स्तम्भ हेर्नुहोस्। करिब २४९ ई.पू. मा मौर्य सम्राट अशोक राज्याभिषेकको बीस वर्षपछि तीर्थयात्रामा यहाँ आएर यो स्तम्भ खडा गराए। सयौँ वर्षसम्म यो आधा गाडिएर बिर्सिएको अवस्थामा रह्यो। सन् १८९६ को डिसेम्बरमा जनरल खड्ग शमशेर राणाको नेतृत्वमा नेपाली टोलीले यसको फेद वरिपरि खन्यो, नजिकै पुरातत्त्वविद् आलोइस फ्युरर पनि थिए। तल्तिर उनीहरूले ब्राह्मी लिपिका पाँच लाइन भेटे। त्यसमा छोटकरीमा लेखिएको छ: राजा आफैँ आएर पूजा गरे, किनभने यहाँ शाक्यमुनि बुद्ध जन्मेका थिए। उनले लुम्बिनी गाउँलाई करमुक्त पनि बनाए, उब्जनीको आठौँ भाग मात्र तिर्नुपर्ने गरी। ती शब्दले बिर्सिएको थुम्कोलाई बुद्धको जन्मस्थलका रूपमा चिनायो। अलि माथि हेर्नुभयो भने पछि कुँदिएको ॐ मणि पद्मे हुम् पनि देख्न सक्नुहुन्छ, जुन चौधौँ शताब्दीमा राजा रिपु मल्लका लागि कुँदिएको थियो। चिनियाँ तीर्थयात्री ह्वेनसाङले टुप्पोमा घोडा देखेका थिए, तर आज त्यो टुप्पो हराइसकेको छ।',NULL,'[\"ब्राह्मी शिलालेख सन् १८९६ को डिसेम्बरमा जनरल खड्ग शमशेर राणाको टोलीले आलोइस एन्टोन फ्युररसँग मिलेर फेला पारेको हो।\", \"त्यसमा लेखिएको छ, अशोक राज्याभिषेकको बीस वर्षपछि यहाँ आए, किनभने यहाँ शाक्यमुनि बुद्ध जन्मेका थिए।\", \"शिलालेख अनुसार अशोकले लुम्बिनी गाउँलाई करमुक्त बनाए र उब्जनीको आठौँ भाग मात्र तिर्नुपर्ने गरे।\", \"स्तम्भमा पछि कुँदिएको शिलालेखमा राजा रिपु मल्लको नामसहित ॐ मणि पद्मे हुम् लेखिएको छ, जसको मिति शक १२३४ हो।\", \"अशोकसम्बन्धी विद्वान ह्यारी फाल्कले यो शिलालेख साँचो हुनमा कुनै विवाद छैन भनेका छन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Buddha Jayanti\", \"note\": \"Baisakh full-moon celebration of the Buddha\'s birth in the Sacred Garden around the pillar.\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"बुद्ध जयन्ती\", \"note_np\": \"स्तम्भ वरिपरिको पवित्र उद्यानमा बैशाख पूर्णिमाका दिन बुद्धको जन्मको उत्सव मनाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Lumbini_-_Pillar_Edict_in_Brahmi_Script%2C_Lumbini_%289241396121%29.jpg/1280px-Lumbini_-_Pillar_Edict_in_Brahmi_Script%2C_Lumbini_%289241396121%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Photo Dharma from Penang, Malaysia\", \"caption\": \"The Brahmi inscription of Ashoka on the pillar\", \"license\": \"CC BY 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lumbini_-_Pillar_Edict_in_Brahmi_Script,_Lumbini_(9241396121).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Lumbini_pillar_Medieval_inscription.jpg/1280px-Lumbini_pillar_Medieval_inscription.jpg\", \"author\": \"David Lowry\", \"caption\": \"King Ripu Malla\'s later inscription higher on the shaft\", \"license\": \"CC BY 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lumbini_pillar_Medieval_inscription.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Ashoka_Pillar%2C_Mayadevi_Temple%2C_Lumbini.jpg/1280px-Ashoka_Pillar%2C_Mayadevi_Temple%2C_Lumbini.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rangan Datta Wiki\", \"caption\": \"The pillar inside its railing beside the Maya Devi Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashoka_Pillar,_Mayadevi_Temple,_Lumbini.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lumbini_pillar_excavation_1896.jpg/1280px-Lumbini_pillar_excavation_1896.jpg\", \"author\": \"Alois Anton Führer (26 November 1853, Limburg an der Lahn, G\", \"caption\": \"The pillar during the 1896 excavation\", \"license\": \"Public domain\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lumbini_pillar_excavation_1896.jpg\", \"license_url\": null}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/76/Ashoka_Pillar_Lumbini_Nepal_1956.jpg\", \"author\": \"Unknown authorUnknown author\", \"caption\": \"The pillar photographed in 1956\", \"license\": \"Public domain\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashoka_Pillar_Lumbini_Nepal_1956.jpg\", \"license_url\": null}]','{\"kind\": \"pillar\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Plain round grey stone shaft with no capital, inside a small square railing, often hung with prayer scarves; the white Maya Devi Temple right behind. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#8C8478\", \"#B5643C\", \"#F2F0EA\"], \"features\": [\"stone-pillar\", \"fence-railing\", \"prayer-flags\"], \"height_m\": 6, \"footprint_m\": [6, 6], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"garden-lawn\", \"brick-courtyard\", \"sacred-grove\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(80,'tilaurakot','Tilaurakot','तिलौराकोट','Taulihawa','Lumbini','Kapilvastu',NULL,27.575915,83.054724,'archaeological-site','Buddhist',NULL,NULL,'Settled from about 1000 BCE; first urban phase radiocarbon-dated to about 570 BCE and earthen wall to about 450 BCE; occupied into the Kushan period (to about the 3rd century CE)','Shakya','Fortified city mound of about 500 x 400 m on the Banganga river, laid out on a grid. Excavated brick walls, an inner walled complex over 100 x 100 m with monumental gateways on the north and west, a tower on the south wall, a moat, ponds and stupa mounds survive among sal forest.',0,'Brick ruins of a walled ancient city widely identified with Kapilavastu, where Prince Siddhartha grew up.','Walk through the gap in these old brick walls and imagine a busy town around you. Many scholars believe this was Kapilavastu, capital of the Shakya clan, where Prince Siddhartha lived for his first twenty-nine years before he left to seek enlightenment. Archaeologists have found that a planned town stood here by about 570 BCE, with streets running north to south and east to west, and an earlier wooden fence built against the floods of the Banganga river beside you. Find the east gate, its brick jambs still standing in the grass. Inside the walls was a second walled complex over a hundred metres across, perhaps the palace that the Chinese pilgrims Faxian and Xuanzang described. South of the citadel, digging in 2012 turned up nine tonnes of iron slag from ancient workshops. Listen to the birds in the sal trees and remember that a prince once walked these lanes.',NULL,'[\"It lies on the bank of the Banganga river, about 27 km west of Lumbini.\", \"P. C. Mukherji of the Archaeological Survey of India first excavated it in 1899.\", \"The fortified citadel measures about 500 by 400 metres and follows a grid plan.\", \"Excavations in 2012 uncovered 9 tonnes of iron slag dated to around 400 BCE.\", \"Nepal placed it on the UNESCO World Heritage Tentative List in 1996.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Suddhodana_Palace-east_gate.JPG/1280px-Suddhodana_Palace-east_gate.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suddhodana_Palace-east_gate.JPG','DiverDave · CC BY-SA 4.0','archaeological-site,buddhist,shakya,taulihawa,water,art,lumbini','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tilaurakot\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapilavastu_(ancient_city)\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3417973\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/19990298\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/travel/2019/09/21/seven-historical-sites-in-kapilvastu-that-you-probably-didn-t-know-about\", \"https://dur.ac.uk/departments/academic/archaeology/research/archaeology-research-projects/tilaurakot/\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Tilaurakot\"]','पर्खाल भएको प्राचीन सहरका इँटाका भग्नावशेष, जसलाई राजकुमार सिद्धार्थ हुर्केको कपिलवस्तु भनेर धेरैले चिन्छन्।','यी पुराना इँटाका पर्खालको खाली ठाउँबाट भित्र पस्नुहोस् र वरिपरि व्यस्त सहर छ भनेर सोच्नुहोस्। धेरै विद्वानको विश्वास छ, यही शाक्य वंशको राजधानी कपिलवस्तु थियो। यहीँ राजकुमार सिद्धार्थले ज्ञानको खोजीमा निस्कनुअघि आफ्ना पहिलो उनन्तीस वर्ष बिताएका थिए। पुरातत्त्वविद्हरूले पत्ता लगाएका छन्, करिब ५७० ई.पू. सम्ममा यहाँ योजना बनाएर बसाइएको सहर थियो, जहाँ उत्तर-दक्षिण र पूर्व-पश्चिम सडक थिए, र छेउको बाणगङ्गा नदीको बाढीबाट जोगिन पहिले काठको बार लगाइएको थियो। पूर्वी ढोका खोज्नुहोस्, घाँसमा अझै उभिएका यसका इँटाका चौखट भेट्टाउनुहुनेछ। पर्खालभित्र सय मिटरभन्दा बढी फराकिलो अर्को पर्खाल लगाइएको परिसर थियो, सायद चिनियाँ तीर्थयात्री फाहियान र ह्वेनसाङले वर्णन गरेको दरबार यही हो। गढीको दक्षिणतिर सन् २०१२ मा खन्दा पुराना कार्यशालाबाट नौ टन फलामको धातुमल भेटियो। सालका रुखमा चराको चिरबिर सुन्नुहोस् र सम्झनुहोस्, कुनै बेला एक राजकुमार यिनै गल्लीमा हिँडेका थिए।',NULL,'[\"यो लुम्बिनीबाट करिब २७ किमी पश्चिममा, बाणगङ्गा नदीको किनारमा छ।\", \"भारतीय पुरातत्त्व सर्वेक्षणका पी. सी. मुखर्जीले सन् १८९९ मा पहिलो पटक यहाँ उत्खनन गरेका थिए।\", \"किल्ला जस्तो गढीको नाप करिब ५०० गुणा ४०० मिटर छ, र यो जाली जस्तो योजनामा बनेको छ।\", \"सन् २०१२ को उत्खननमा करिब ४०० ई.पू. को ९ टन फलामको धातुमल भेटियो।\", \"नेपालले यसलाई सन् १९९६ मा युनेस्कोको विश्व सम्पदा अस्थायी सूचीमा राखेको थियो।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Tilaurakot%2C_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Western_Nepal_1%2C_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg/1280px-Tilaurakot%2C_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Western_Nepal_1%2C_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Excavated brick walls of the ancient city\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tilaurakot,_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Western_Nepal_1,_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Tilaurakot%2C_Kapilvastu_Ancient_Shakya_Capital_01.jpg/1280px-Tilaurakot%2C_Kapilvastu_Ancient_Shakya_Capital_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sabina Bajracharya\", \"caption\": \"Ruins inside the citadel\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tilaurakot,_Kapilvastu_Ancient_Shakya_Capital_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Tilaurakot%2C_Kapilvastu_Ancient_Shakya_Capital_05.jpg/1280px-Tilaurakot%2C_Kapilvastu_Ancient_Shakya_Capital_05.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sabina Bajracharya\", \"caption\": \"Brick foundations among the trees\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tilaurakot,_Kapilvastu_Ancient_Shakya_Capital_05.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Shiva_Linga_Tilaurakot_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg/1280px-Shiva_Linga_Tilaurakot_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"A Shiva linga venerated at the site\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shiva_Linga_Tilaurakot_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(3).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Samai_Mai_Temple_Anandabag_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Samai_Mai_Temple_Anandabag_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Samai Mai temple on a mound south of the citadel\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samai_Mai_Temple_Anandabag_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"ruins\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Low red-brick wall stubs and a gateway gap in a rectangular walled enclosure under tall sal trees, with a moat and river at one side. Wall height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#A0522D\", \"#5E7D3A\", \"#C9B48A\"], \"features\": [\"sacred-tree\", \"shiva-lingam\"], \"height_m\": 3, \"footprint_m\": [500, 400], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"forest\", \"river\", \"plains-fields\", \"pond\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(81,'kudan-nigrodharama','Kudan (Nigrodharama)','कुदान (न्यग्रोधाराम)','Taulihawa','Lumbini','Kapilvastu',NULL,27.527994,83.040560,'archaeological-site','Buddhist',NULL,NULL,'Buddhist monastic site traditionally dated to the Buddha\'s lifetime; excavation reported a wooden post-hole dated to the 8th century BCE; visible brick stupas are later','Shakya (tradition)','Excavated brick stupa mounds and monastery foundations in open grassland, with a well and the remains of a large pond. A small Hindu shrine with a Shiva linga sits on top of the main stupa mound, reached by a stair hung with prayer flags.',0,'Ruined stupas at Kudan, identified with Nigrodharama, where the Buddha is said to have met his father after enlightenment.','You are standing at Kudan, a short ride south of Taulihawa, in grassland dotted with old brick mounds. Buddhist tradition identifies this place with Nigrodharama, the banyan grove monastery near Kapilavastu. It is said that King Suddhodana built a great vihara here so he could meet his son again, for the first time since the prince had become the Buddha. Here, the story goes, the Buddha taught his family, among them his wife Yashodhara and his young son Rahula. Climb the stair, decorated with fluttering prayer flags, to the top of the main stupa mound. Notice the small Shiva shrine perched there: Hindu and Buddhist devotion have long shared this ground. In 2016 a team from Durham University, UNESCO and Nepal\'s archaeology department reported a wooden post-hole here, which some link to the Buddha\'s first sermon on his visit home. Look across the fields toward Tilaurakot, the old city he once left behind.','King Suddhodana built a large vihara in the banyan grove to receive his son, now the Buddha, who preached here to the Shakyas, including Yashodhara and Rahula.','[\"The Lumbini Development Trust places Kudan about 3 km south of Taulihawa and identifies it with Nigrodharama.\", \"Tradition says the Buddha met his father, King Suddhodana, here for the first time after his enlightenment.\", \"In 2016 excavators reported a post-hole that some believe marks the Buddha\'s first sermon on his visit home.\", \"Surviving remains include three stupas, a well and the ruins of a large pond.\", \"A small Shiva shrine stands on top of the main stupa mound.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,40,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Kudan_%28Ancient_Nigrodharama%29%2C_Kapilvastu%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Kudan_%28Ancient_Nigrodharama%29%2C_Kapilvastu%2C_Nepal.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kudan_(Ancient_Nigrodharama),_Kapilvastu,_Nepal.jpg','Afzal Khan Visuals · CC BY-SA 4.0','archaeological-site,buddhist,shakya (tradition),taulihawa,legend,water,lumbini','[\"https://lumbinidevtrust.gov.np/page/2_667f8489290b3\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/travel/2019/09/21/seven-historical-sites-in-kapilvastu-that-you-probably-didn-t-know-about\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/national/2016/01/31/buddha-post-hole-found-in-nigrodharam-area\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/kudan-archeological-site\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/19980399\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Nigrodharama\"]','कुदानका भत्किएका स्तूप, न्यग्रोधाराम भनेर चिनिने ठाउँ, जहाँ बुद्धले ज्ञान पाएपछि आफ्ना पितासँग भेट गरेका थिए भनिन्छ।','तपाईं तौलिहवाबाट अलि दक्षिण कुदानमा हुनुहुन्छ, जहाँ घाँसे मैदानमा पुराना इँटाका थुम्का छरिएका छन्। बौद्ध परम्परा अनुसार यो ठाउँ कपिलवस्तु नजिकको बरको बगैँचामा रहेको विहार, न्यग्रोधाराम हो। भनिन्छ, राजकुमार बुद्ध भएपछि छोरालाई पहिलो पटक भेट्न राजा शुद्धोदनले यहाँ ठूलो विहार बनाए। कथा अनुसार यहीँ बुद्धले आफ्नो परिवारलाई उपदेश दिए, जसमा उनकी पत्नी यशोधरा र सानो छोरा राहुल पनि थिए। प्रार्थना झण्डा फहराएको सिँढी चढेर मुख्य स्तूपको थुम्कामाथि पुग्नुहोस्। त्यहाँ एउटा सानो शिव मन्दिर छ, हेर्नुहोस्। हिन्दू र बौद्धको आस्था लामो समयदेखि यही ठाउँमा सँगै बसेको छ। सन् 2016 मा डरहम विश्वविद्यालय, युनेस्को र नेपालको पुरातत्त्व विभागको टोलीले यहाँ काठको खम्बा गाडिएको प्वाल भेटेको जनायो। कतिपयले यसलाई घर फर्कँदा बुद्धले दिएको पहिलो प्रवचनसँग जोड्छन्। खेतपारि तिलौराकोटतिर हेर्नुहोस्, उनले कुनै बेला छाडेर गएको पुरानो सहर।','राजा शुद्धोदनले बरको बगैँचामा आफ्ना छोरा, अब बुद्ध भएकालाई स्वागत गर्न ठूलो विहार बनाए। बुद्धले यहीँ शाक्यहरूलाई उपदेश दिए, जसमा यशोधरा र राहुल पनि थिए।','[\"लुम्बिनी विकास कोषका अनुसार कुदान तौलिहवाबाट करिब 3 किलोमिटर दक्षिणमा छ र यसलाई न्यग्रोधाराम भनेर चिनिन्छ।\", \"परम्परा अनुसार बुद्धले ज्ञान पाएपछि पहिलो पटक आफ्ना पिता राजा शुद्धोदनलाई यहीँ भेटेका थिए।\", \"सन् 2016 मा उत्खननकर्ताहरूले एउटा खम्बा गाडिएको प्वाल भेटेको जनाए, जसलाई कतिपयले घर फर्कँदा बुद्धले दिएको पहिलो प्रवचनको चिह्न मान्छन्।\", \"बाँकी अवशेषमा तीनवटा स्तूप, एउटा इनार र ठूलो पोखरीको भग्नावशेष छन्।\", \"मुख्य स्तूपको थुम्कामाथि सानो शिव मन्दिर छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Nigrodharama.jpg/1280px-Nigrodharama.jpg\", \"author\": \"User:BPG\", \"caption\": \"Brick foundations of the Nigrodharama monastery\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.5\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nigrodharama.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Nigrodharama1.jpg/1280px-Nigrodharama1.jpg\", \"author\": \"User:BPG\", \"caption\": \"Panorama of the excavated mounds\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.5\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nigrodharama1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Shiva_Temple_Kudan_Ancient_Place_Buddha_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg/1280px-Shiva_Temple_Kudan_Ancient_Place_Buddha_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The Shiva shrine on top of the main stupa\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shiva_Temple_Kudan_Ancient_Place_Buddha_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Shiva_Linga_Kudan_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Shiva_Linga_Kudan_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The Shiva linga worshipped on the mound\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shiva_Linga_Kudan_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Nigrodharam_Kudan_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg/1280px-Nigrodharam_Kudan_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Excavated brickwork at Kudan\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nigrodharam_Kudan_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(3).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"ruins\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Stepped red-brick stupa mound with a railed stair strung with prayer flags to a tiny shrine on top; a second low brick block beside it; big trees behind. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#9C5B3B\", \"#7A8F3E\", \"#2F6FB0\"], \"features\": [\"prayer-flags\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"sacred-tree\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 6, \"footprint_m\": [40, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 3, \"surroundings\": [\"plains-fields\", \"forest\", \"pond\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(82,'gotihawa','Gotihawa','गोटिहवा','Taulihawa','Lumbini','Kapilvastu',NULL,27.528399,83.014972,'pillar','Buddhist','Krakuchhanda (Kakusandha) Buddha',NULL,'Ashoka\'s pillar of the 3rd century BCE beside a brick stupa; excavation in 1993-94 found remains going back to about 900 BCE','Maurya (pillar)','The broken lower stump of a polished Ashokan sandstone pillar, without inscription, stands in a fenced enclosure beside the excavated brick base of a stupa associated with Krakuchhanda Buddha.',0,'Village with Ashoka\'s broken pillar and a brick stupa, revered as the birthplace of Krakuchhanda Buddha.','Look at the stump of polished stone in front of you. It is all that stands here of a pillar raised by Emperor Ashoka in the third century BCE, and unlike the one at Lumbini it carries no inscription. Buddhist tradition says this village, once called Khemavati, was the birthplace of Krakuchhanda Buddha, known in Pali as Kakusandha, one of the Buddhas said to have come before Siddhartha Gautama. Ashoka is believed to have stopped here on his pilgrimage to Lumbini. Turn to the brick mound beside the pillar: it is the base of a stupa, generally linked with the nirvana of Krakuchhanda. Scholars have suggested that the broken pillar pieces now lying at Nigali Sagar, a few kilometres away, may originally have stood on this very base. Excavations in 1993 and 1994 found pottery and brickwork going back to around 900 BCE. Pause in the quiet fields and picture pilgrims on the same road two thousand years ago.','Theravada tradition says Krakuchhanda Buddha was born in the Khemavati park here, son of the chaplain Aggidatta of King Khemankara.','[\"Ancient Khemavati is identified with modern Gotihawa.\", \"The Ashoka pillar here has no surviving inscription.\", \"Scholars have suggested its base was the original base of the Nigali Sagar pillar fragments.\", \"A 1993-94 excavation found relics dating back to about 900 BCE.\", \"Krakuchhanda is counted as the 25th of the 29 Buddhas in the Buddhavamsa.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Gotihawa_Ashok_Pillar_Buddha_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Gotihawa_Ashok_Pillar_Buddha_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gotihawa_Ashok_Pillar_Buddha_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg','Rajesh Dhungana · CC BY-SA 4.0','pillar,buddhist,maurya (pillar),taulihawa,legend,art,lumbini','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotihawa\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakusandha_Buddha\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nigali_Sagar\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3425576\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/5237478021\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/travel/2019/09/21/seven-historical-sites-in-kapilvastu-that-you-probably-didn-t-know-about\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Ashoka_Pillar,_Gotihawa\"]','अशोकको भाँचिएको स्तम्भ र इँटाको स्तूप भएको गाउँ, क्रकुच्छन्द बुद्धको जन्मस्थलका रूपमा मानिने।','तपाईंको अगाडिको पालिस गरिएको ढुङ्गाको मुढो हेर्नुहोस्। ई.पू. तेस्रो शताब्दीमा सम्राट अशोकले खडा गराएको स्तम्भको यहाँ यति मात्र बाँकी छ। लुम्बिनीको स्तम्भ जस्तो यसमा कुनै शिलालेख छैन। बौद्ध परम्परा अनुसार यो गाउँ, जसलाई पहिले खेमवती भनिन्थ्यो, क्रकुच्छन्द बुद्धको जन्मस्थल हो। पालीमा उनलाई कक्कुसन्ध भनिन्छ, जो सिद्धार्थ गौतम भन्दा पहिले आएका भनिने बुद्धमध्ये एक हुन्। अशोक लुम्बिनीको तीर्थयात्रामा जाँदा यहाँ रोकिएका थिए भन्ने मानिन्छ। स्तम्भको छेउको इँटाको थुप्रोतिर फर्कनुहोस्। त्यो स्तूपको आधार हो, जसलाई सामान्यतया क्रकुच्छन्दको निर्वाणसँग जोडिन्छ। केही किमी टाढा निग्लीसागरमा अहिले रहेका भाँचिएको स्तम्भका टुक्रा सुरुमा यही आधारमा उभिएका हुन सक्छन् भनी विद्वान्हरूले भनेका छन्। सन् 1993 र 1994 को उत्खननमा करिब ई.पू. 900 सम्मका माटाका भाँडा र इँटाको काम भेटिए। शान्त खेतमा केही बेर रोकिनुहोस् र दुई हजार वर्षअघि यही बाटोमा हिँडेका तीर्थयात्रीको कल्पना गर्नुहोस्।','थेरवाद परम्परा अनुसार क्रकुच्छन्द बुद्ध यहाँको खेमवती उद्यानमा जन्मिए। उनी राजा खेमङ्करका पुरोहित अग्गिदत्तका छोरा थिए।','[\"प्राचीन खेमवतीलाई अहिलेको गोटिहवा मानिन्छ।\", \"यहाँको अशोक स्तम्भमा कुनै शिलालेख बाँकी छैन।\", \"विद्वान्हरूले यसको आधार निग्लीसागरमा रहेका स्तम्भका टुक्राको सुरुको आधार हुन सक्छ भनेका छन्।\", \"सन् 1993-94 को उत्खननमा करिब ई.पू. 900 सम्मका अवशेष भेटिए।\", \"बुद्धवंशमा क्रकुच्छन्दलाई 29 बुद्धमध्ये 25 औँ गनिएको छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The pillar stump and stupa base in the fields\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg/1280px-Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Close view of the polished pillar stump\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(3).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%2818%29.jpg/1280px-Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%2818%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The pillar site and its surroundings\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gotihawa_Achok_Pillar_Taulihawa_Kapilbastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(18).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Gotihawa_Ashok_Pillar_Buddha_Kapilvastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%284%29.jpg/1280px-Gotihawa_Ashok_Pillar_Buddha_Kapilvastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%284%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The fenced pillar enclosure\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gotihawa_Ashok_Pillar_Buddha_Kapilvastu_Lumbini_Zone_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(4).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Nigli_Sagar_Historical_Pond_Gotihawa_Kapilbastu_Buddha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg/1280px-Nigli_Sagar_Historical_Pond_Gotihawa_Kapilbastu_Buddha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"A historic pond in the Gotihawa area\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nigli_Sagar_Historical_Pond_Gotihawa_Kapilbastu_Buddha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pillar\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Short broken stone pillar stump in a railing, next to a low round red-brick stupa base, in flat farmland. Heights estimated.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#7D7468\", \"#9C5B3B\", \"#7A8F3E\"], \"features\": [\"stone-pillar\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 3, \"footprint_m\": [20, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"plains-fields\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(83,'ramagrama-stupa','Ramagrama Stupa','रामग्राम स्तूप','Ramgram (Parasi)','Lumbini','Nawalparasi (West)',NULL,27.497778,83.681111,'stupa','Buddhist','Relics of Gautama Buddha',NULL,'Original relic stupa traditionally raised by the Koliyas after the Buddha\'s death; Nepal\'s Department of Archaeology dates the present structure between the Mauryan and Gupta periods','Koliya (tradition)','Unexcavated brick stupa buried under a grassy earthen mound about 10 m high and 23.5 m across. Geophysical survey shows a square Kushan-era monastery buried beside it. A large bodhi tree hung with prayer flags grows at the foot of the mound.',0,'A grassy mound hiding a brick stupa believed to be the only original Buddha relic stupa never opened.','What looks like a gentle green hill in front of you is in fact a stupa. Buddhist texts say that when the Buddha died, his ashes were divided among eight kingdoms, and the Koliyas of Ramagrama, his mother\'s people, built a stupa over their share. About three centuries later Emperor Ashoka set out to open the eight stupas and spread the relics among thousands of new ones. The Mahavamsa says that when he reached Ramagrama, a naga, a serpent guardian, stopped him. That is why this is believed to be the only one of the eight never opened. Nepal\'s archaeologists think the brick core under the grass is still intact. A survey also found a square monastery buried nearby; its bricks kept crops from growing, so the spot became known as the unlucky field. Walk slowly around the mound, under the prayer flags on the bodhi tree, and remember that relics may lie a few metres beneath your feet.','When Ashoka came to take the relics, a powerful naga guarding the stupa prevented him, so the Ramagrama stupa alone kept its original relics.','[\"It is one of eight stupas built over the Buddha\'s divided ashes, according to Buddhist texts.\", \"Nepali archaeologists consider it the only intact original stupa enshrining the Buddha\'s relics.\", \"The stupa complex is about 10 m high and 23.5 m in diameter.\", \"A geophysical survey revealed a buried square Kushan-era monastery beside the mound.\", \"It was added to UNESCO\'s World Heritage Tentative List on 23 May 1996.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,40,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Ramgram_Stupa_2.jpg/1280px-Ramgram_Stupa_2.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramgram_Stupa_2.jpg','Sukrat Gaud · CC BY-SA 4.0','stupa,buddhist,koliya (tradition),ramgram (parasi),legend,art,lumbini','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramagrama_stupa\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7288751\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/5303966021\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Ramagrama_stupa\"]','घाँसले ढाकिएको थुम्कोभित्र लुकेको इँटाको स्तूप, बुद्धको अस्थि राखिएका मौलिक स्तूपमध्ये कहिल्यै नखोलिएको एउटै मानिने।','तपाईंको अगाडि सानो हरियो डाँडा जस्तो देखिने चिज वास्तवमा स्तूप हो। बौद्ध ग्रन्थ अनुसार बुद्धको निधनपछि उनको अस्थि आठ राज्यमा बाँडिएको थियो। बुद्धकी आमाका आफन्त रामग्रामका कोलियहरूले आफ्नो भागमाथि स्तूप बनाए। करिब तीन सय वर्षपछि सम्राट अशोकले आठै स्तूप खोलेर अस्थि हजारौँ नयाँ स्तूपमा बाँड्न थाले। महावंश अनुसार उनी रामग्राम पुग्दा एउटा नाग, अर्थात् सर्प रक्षकले उनलाई रोक्यो। त्यसैले यो आठमध्ये कहिल्यै नखोलिएको एउटै स्तूप हो भनिन्छ। नेपालका पुरातत्त्वविद्हरूको विचारमा घाँसमुनिको इँटाको भित्री भाग अझै नबिग्रिएको छ। सर्वेक्षणमा नजिकै गाडिएको चौकोर विहार पनि भेटियो। त्यसका इँटाले बाली उम्रन दिँदैनथे, त्यसैले त्यो ठाउँ अशुभ खेत भनेर चिनियो। बोधिवृक्षमा झुन्ड्याइएका प्रार्थना झण्डामुनि थुम्कोको वरिपरि बिस्तारै हिँड्नुहोस्, र सम्झनुहोस्, तपाईंको खुट्टामुनि केही मिटर तल अस्थि हुन सक्छ।','अशोक अस्थि लिन आउँदा स्तूपको रक्षा गर्ने शक्तिशाली नागले उनलाई रोक्यो। त्यसैले रामग्राम स्तूपले मात्र आफ्ना मौलिक अस्थि जोगाएर राख्यो।','[\"बौद्ध ग्रन्थ अनुसार यो बुद्धको बाँडिएको अस्थिमाथि बनेका आठ स्तूपमध्ये एउटा हो।\", \"नेपालका पुरातत्त्वविद्हरूले यसलाई बुद्धको अस्थि राखिएको नबिग्रिएको एउटै मौलिक स्तूप मान्छन्।\", \"स्तूप परिसर करिब १० मिटर अग्लो र २३.५ मिटर व्यासको छ।\", \"माटोमुनि जाँच गर्ने सर्वेक्षणले थुम्कोको छेउमा गाडिएको कुषाण कालको चौकोर विहार देखायो।\", \"यो २३ मे १९९६ मा युनेस्कोको विश्व सम्पदा सम्भावित सूचीमा थपिएको थियो।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Ramagrama_Stupa.jpg/1280px-Ramagrama_Stupa.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sukrat Gaud\", \"caption\": \"The grass-covered relic stupa mound\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramagrama_Stupa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Ramgram_Stupa_Entry_View.jpg/1280px-Ramgram_Stupa_Entry_View.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sukrat Gaud\", \"caption\": \"The approach to the stupa from the entrance\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramgram_Stupa_Entry_View.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Ramgram_Stupa_Gate_Statue.jpg/1280px-Ramgram_Stupa_Gate_Statue.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sukrat Gaud\", \"caption\": \"Gate and statue near the stupa\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramgram_Stupa_Gate_Statue.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ec/Ramagrama_stupa_in_Nawalparasi.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ravijung\", \"caption\": \"The mound and the bodhi tree with prayer flags\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramagrama_stupa_in_Nawalparasi.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Ramgram_Stupa_5.jpg/1280px-Ramgram_Stupa_5.jpg\", \"author\": \"Sukrat Gaud\", \"caption\": \"Another view of the Ramagrama mound\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramgram_Stupa_5.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"stupa\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"A smooth round grass-covered mound, no visible brick, with a large bodhi tree hung with prayer flags at its foot. Model as a green earthen dome.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#3E8E2F\", \"#2C4F1E\", \"#D9473B\"], \"features\": [\"prayer-flags\", \"sacred-tree\", \"fence-railing\"], \"height_m\": 10, \"footprint_m\": [23.5, 23.5], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"garden-lawn\", \"plains-fields\", \"sacred-grove\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:48'),(84,'rishikesh-temple-ridi','Rishikesh Temple, Ridi','ऋषिकेश मन्दिर, रिडी','Ridi','Lumbini','Palpa',NULL,27.934339,83.437586,'pagoda','Hindu','Rishikesh (Hrishikesha), a form of Vishnu',NULL,'16th century tradition: founded by Mukunda Sen, first king of Palpa (reigned c. 1518-1553), who is said to have found the image in the Kali Gandaki; the complex mixes medieval and Sen-period styles','Sen (Palpa)','Temple complex of brick buildings with carved timber windows and struts, rows of hanging bells, ochre and red painted shrines and a paved courtyard above the ghats of the Kali Gandaki. The black stone image of Rishikesh stands in a tiled sanctum.',0,'Riverside Vishnu temple at Ridi, where the Ridi Khola meets the Kali Gandaki, famed for the Maghe Sankranti fair.','Listen to the two rivers below you. Here at Ridi the Ridi Khola joins the Kali Gandaki, at the meeting point of Palpa, Gulmi and Syangja, and Hindu tradition counts this place, Ruru Kshetra, among the four holy dhams of Nepal. Climb the stone steps into the courtyard and ring one of the brass bells. Inside the small tiled sanctum stands a black stone image of Rishikesh, a form of Lord Vishnu, dressed in yellow and heavy with garlands. Legend says Mukunda Sen, the first king of Palpa, found this very image while taking a holy dip in the Kali Gandaki, and built the temple to house it. Look at the river stones: shaligrams, the fossil stones honoured as symbols of Vishnu, are found along this bank. Each Maghe Sankranti the town fills for the Ridi Mela, when pilgrims bathe for three days, called Jethi, Maili and Kanchhi Sankranti, hoping for moksha. The ghats are also an old cremation site.','King Mukunda Sen of Palpa is said to have found the image of Rishikesh in the Kali Gandaki while bathing and founded the temple for it.','[\"Ruru Kshetra lies at the confluence of the Ridi Khola and the Kali Gandaki, where Gulmi, Palpa and Syangja meet.\", \"It is counted as one of the Char Dham of Nepal.\", \"The Rishikesh Complex of Ruru Kshetra was added to UNESCO\'s Tentative List on 30 January 2008.\", \"The Ridi Mela at Maghe Sankranti has three bathing days: Jethi, Maili and Kanchhi Sankranti.\", \"UNESCO\'s entry notes the tradition of Bhaktini Amas, female mendicants, at the site.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Rishikesh_Mandir%2C_Palpa%2C_Nepal_03.jpg/1280px-Rishikesh_Mandir%2C_Palpa%2C_Nepal_03.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rishikesh_Mandir,_Palpa,_Nepal_03.jpg','Acharya Bipin · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,sen (palpa),ridi,legend,art,lumbini','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruru_Kshetra\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rishikesh_Complex_of_Ruru_Kshetra\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mukunda_Sen\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/tentativelists/5259\", \"https://ekantipur.com/lumbini-pradesh/2026/01/15/en/crowds-gather-at-ridi-ruru-area-the-confluence-of-palpa-gulmi-and-syangja-to-celebrate-sankranti-bathing-and-fair-21-59.html\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/3464974411\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Rishikesh_Temple,_Palpa\"]','रिडी खोला र कालीगण्डकीको सङ्गममा रहेको नदी किनारको विष्णु मन्दिर, माघे सङ्क्रान्तिको मेलाका लागि प्रसिद्ध।','तल बग्ने दुई नदीको आवाज सुन्नुहोस्। यहाँ रिडीमा रिडी खोला कालीगण्डकीमा मिसिन्छ, जहाँ पाल्पा, गुल्मी र स्याङ्जा भेट्छन्। हिन्दू परम्परामा यो ठाउँ, रुरु क्षेत्र, नेपालका चार पवित्र धाममध्ये एक मानिन्छ। ढुङ्गाका भर्‍याङ उक्लेर आँगनमा पुग्नुहोस् र पित्तलका घण्टमध्ये एउटा बजाउनुहोस्। टायल बिछ्याएको सानो गर्भगृहभित्र भगवान् विष्णुको रूप ऋषिकेशको कालो ढुङ्गाको मूर्ति छ, पहेँलो वस्त्र लगाएको र माला भारी भएको। कथा अनुसार पाल्पाका पहिलो राजा मुकुन्द सेनले कालीगण्डकीमा पवित्र स्नान गर्दा यही मूर्ति भेटे, र त्यसलाई राख्न मन्दिर बनाए। नदीका ढुङ्गा हेर्नुहोस्। विष्णुको प्रतीक मानिने शालिग्राम, अर्थात् जीवाश्म ढुङ्गा, यही किनारमा पाइन्छन्। हरेक माघे सङ्क्रान्तिमा रिडी मेलाका लागि यहाँ भीड लाग्छ। मोक्षको आशामा तीर्थयात्रीहरू जेठी, माइली र कान्छी सङ्क्रान्ति भनिने तीन दिन स्नान गर्छन्। घाटहरू पुरानो दाहसंस्कार गर्ने ठाउँ पनि हुन्।','पाल्पाका राजा मुकुन्द सेनले कालीगण्डकीमा नुहाउँदा ऋषिकेशको मूर्ति भेटे र त्यसका लागि मन्दिर बनाए भनिन्छ।','[\"रुरु क्षेत्र रिडी खोला र कालीगण्डकीको सङ्गममा छ, जहाँ गुल्मी, पाल्पा र स्याङ्जा जोडिन्छन्।\", \"यसलाई नेपालका चार धाममध्ये एक मानिन्छ।\", \"रुरु क्षेत्रको ऋषिकेश परिसर ३० जनवरी २००८ मा युनेस्कोको सम्भावित सूचीमा थपियो।\", \"माघे सङ्क्रान्तिको रिडी मेलामा तीन स्नान दिन हुन्छन्: जेठी, माइली र कान्छी सङ्क्रान्ति।\", \"युनेस्कोको विवरणमा यहाँ भक्तिनी आमा, अर्थात् महिला साधुहरूको परम्परा रहेको उल्लेख छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Ridi Mela (Maghe Sankranti)\", \"note\": \"Three-day bathing fair in the Kali Gandaki with worship at the Rishikesh temple.\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"रिडी मेला (माघे सङ्क्रान्ति)\", \"note_np\": \"कालीगण्डकीमा स्नान र ऋषिकेश मन्दिरमा पूजा गरिने तीन दिने स्नान मेला।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Rishikeshdham_Temple.jpg/1280px-Rishikeshdham_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Siddhant2057\", \"caption\": \"The black stone image of Rishikesh in its sanctum\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rishikeshdham_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Rishikesh_Mandir%2C_Palpa%2C_Nepal_04.jpg/1280px-Rishikesh_Mandir%2C_Palpa%2C_Nepal_04.jpg\", \"author\": \"Acharya Bipin\", \"caption\": \"Brick shrines and rows of temple bells\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rishikesh_Mandir,_Palpa,_Nepal_04.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Rishikesh_Mandir%2C_Palpa%2C_Nepal_01.jpg/1280px-Rishikesh_Mandir%2C_Palpa%2C_Nepal_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Acharya Bipin\", \"caption\": \"Steps leading up into the temple complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rishikesh_Mandir,_Palpa,_Nepal_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Rishikesh_Mandir%2C_Palpa%2C_Nepal_02.jpg/1280px-Rishikesh_Mandir%2C_Palpa%2C_Nepal_02.jpg\", \"author\": \"Acharya Bipin\", \"caption\": \"Old brick and timber buildings of Ridi\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rishikesh_Mandir,_Palpa,_Nepal_02.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Rishikeshav_inside_Rishikeshav_Temple%2C_Palpa.jpg/1280px-Rishikeshav_inside_Rishikeshav_Temple%2C_Palpa.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prakat Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"The deity Rishikeshav inside the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rishikeshav_inside_Rishikeshav_Temple,_Palpa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Brick temple buildings with carved windows, frames of hanging bells and ochre domed shrines on a paved courtyard above river ghats in a steep green valley. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#B5653F\", \"#E8B730\", \"#A52A2A\"], \"features\": [\"bell\", \"carved-windows\", \"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"ghat-steps\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": 9, \"footprint_m\": [30, 25], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"riverbank-ghats\", \"stone-paved-plaza\", \"village\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(85,'rani-mahal-palpa','Rani Mahal','रानीमहल','Tansen','Lumbini','Palpa',NULL,27.926708,83.527799,'palace','Other',NULL,1893,'Late 19th century: built from 1893 by General Khadga Shumsher Rana in memory of his wife Tej Kumari Devi; abandoned in 1902; restored by the Government of Nepal from 2017','Rana','European-style Rana palace on a rocky bank of the Kali Gandaki: a two-storey main block with arched windows, columns and a pitched red roof, above terraces of white balustraded buildings and stairways that step down to the river.',0,'A white Rana palace on the Kali Gandaki, built by Khadga Shumsher for his late wife and called the Taj Mahal of Nepal.','You have come down a long valley road to a palace that seems to grow out of the riverbank. In 1892 Tej Kumari Devi, youngest wife of General Khadga Shumsher Rana, died here in Palpa. Khadga Shumsher had been banished from Kathmandu after a failed plot against Prime Minister Bir Shumsher, and he turned his grief into this building. The design is said to be by a British architect, with workers brought from India, soldiers and local villagers, some of them forced to labour. It took about four years. He named the forest Rani Ban and the riverbank Rani Ghat. Look at the grand white terraces stepping down to the grey-green Kali Gandaki. That is why people call it the Taj Mahal of Nepal: both were built for a lost love beside a river. In 1902 Khadga Shumsher fled to India, and the palace slowly fell to ruin until the government restored it from 2017 and opened a museum inside.',NULL,'[\"General Khadga Shumsher Rana began the palace in 1893 in memory of his wife Tej Kumari Devi.\", \"It took around four years to build, reportedly to a British architect\'s design.\", \"Khadga Shumsher fled to India with his family in 1902, abandoning the palace.\", \"The Government of Nepal restored it from 2017 and set up a museum inside.\", \"It is about half an hour by road from Tansen.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,50,60,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Palpa%2C_Ranighat_Palace%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Palpa%2C_Ranighat_Palace%2C_Nepal.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palpa,_Ranighat_Palace,_Nepal.jpg','Vyacheslav Argenberg · CC BY 4.0','palace,other,rana,tansen,art,lumbini','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranighat_Palace\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13185406\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/3359338503\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/news/rani-mahal-is-the-choice-on-valentines-day\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Rani_Mahal,_Palpa_District\"]','कालीगण्डकी किनारको सेतो राणा दरबार, खड्ग शमशेरले आफ्नी दिवङ्गत पत्नीका लागि बनाएको र नेपालको ताजमहल भनिने।','लामो उपत्यकाको बाटो हुँदै तपाईं नदी किनारबाट उम्रिएजस्तो देखिने दरबारमा आइपुग्नुभएको छ। सन् 1892 मा जनरल खड्ग शमशेर राणाकी कान्छी पत्नी तेज कुमारी देवीको यहीँ पाल्पामा निधन भयो। प्रधानमन्त्री वीर शमशेरविरुद्धको असफल षड्यन्त्रपछि खड्ग शमशेरलाई काठमाडौँबाट निकालिएको थियो। उनले आफ्नो शोक यही भवनमा उतारे। नक्सा कुनै बेलायती वास्तुकारले बनाएको भनिन्छ। कामदार भारतबाट ल्याइएका थिए, साथै सिपाही र स्थानीय गाउँलेहरू पनि थिए, जसमध्ये कतिपयलाई जबरजस्ती काममा लगाइएको थियो। यसमा करिब चार वर्ष लाग्यो। उनले जङ्गलको नाम रानी वन र नदी किनारको नाम रानीघाट राखे। खैरो-हरियो कालीगण्डकीतिर तल झर्दै गएका भव्य सेता तल्ला हेर्नुहोस्। त्यसैले मानिसहरू यसलाई नेपालको ताजमहल भन्छन्, किनभने दुवै नदी किनारमा गुमाएको मायाका लागि बनाइएका हुन्। सन् 1902 मा खड्ग शमशेर भारत भागे र दरबार बिस्तारै भत्किँदै गयो। सरकारले सन् 2017 देखि यसलाई मर्मत गर्‍यो र भित्र सङ्ग्रहालय खोल्यो।',NULL,'[\"जनरल खड्ग शमशेर राणाले आफ्नी पत्नी तेज कुमारी देवीको सम्झनामा सन् 1893 मा दरबार बनाउन सुरु गरे।\", \"यो बनाउन करिब चार वर्ष लाग्यो, र बेलायती वास्तुकारको नक्सा अनुसार बनेको भनिन्छ।\", \"खड्ग शमशेर सन् 1902 मा परिवारसहित भारत भागे र दरबार छाडे।\", \"नेपाल सरकारले सन् 2017 देखि यसलाई मर्मत गर्‍यो र भित्र सङ्ग्रहालय बनायो।\", \"यो तानसेनबाट सडकमार्गबाट करिब आधा घण्टाको दूरीमा छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Rani_Mahal%2C_Kaligandaki%2C_Palpa.jpg/1280px-Rani_Mahal%2C_Kaligandaki%2C_Palpa.jpg\", \"author\": \"Arjun Bhadra Khanal\", \"caption\": \"The palace above the Kali Gandaki river\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rani_Mahal,_Kaligandaki,_Palpa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Rani_Mahal_of_Palpa.JPG/1280px-Rani_Mahal_of_Palpa.JPG\", \"author\": \"Gaurab\", \"caption\": \"Rani Mahal on the riverbank\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rani_Mahal_of_Palpa.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Ranimahal_front_view.jpg/1280px-Ranimahal_front_view.jpg\", \"author\": \"Mynameisrabin\", \"caption\": \"Front view of the main palace block\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ranimahal_front_view.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/RANI_MAHAL_PALPA.jpg/1280px-RANI_MAHAL_PALPA.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rebellion12345\", \"caption\": \"A close view of the palace buildings\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RANI_MAHAL_PALPA.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Rani_Mahal.JPG/1280px-Rani_Mahal.JPG\", \"author\": \"Sailesh.baidya\", \"caption\": \"Panorama of the palace and the river gorge\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rani_Mahal.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Two-storey colonnaded main block (blue trim, red pitched roof) on top of stepped white terraces with balustrades dropping to a wide brown river. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#F4F4F0\", \"#2E8FD0\", \"#C0504D\"], \"features\": [\"arched-windows\", \"fence-railing\", \"ghat-steps\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [80, 50], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 4, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"forest\", \"riverbank-ghats\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(86,'tansen-durbar','Tansen Durbar','तानसेन दरबार','Tansen','Lumbini','Palpa',NULL,27.867361,83.545139,'palace','Other',NULL,1927,'Early 20th century: Wikipedia and Wikidata give 1927 under Pratap Shumsher Rana (a museum report gives 1903); destroyed in a Maoist attack in the mid-2000s, rebuilt, and opened as a museum (formally inaugurated 29 May 2019)','Rana','Large three-storey Rana palace in neoclassical style around a courtyard, with deep red walls, white pilasters and window hoods, green latticed windows and a central balcony porch over the entrance, with corner towers.',0,'Red-and-white Rana governors\' palace in the heart of Tansen, rebuilt after its destruction and now the Palpa Museum.','Stand in the open square and look at the long red facade in front of you, picked out with white columns and green latticed windows. This is Tansen Durbar, built for the Rana governors who ran western Nepal from Palpa. Wikipedia credits Pratap Shumsher Rana and the year 1927. For decades this was the seat of Rana power in the western hills. Then, during the Maoist conflict in the mid-2000s, the palace was destroyed in an attack on Tansen. What you see now is a rebuilding that follows the old design. Since 2019 it has been formally open as the Palpa Durbar Museum, run under Tansen Municipality, so you can walk the corridors that governors once paced. Step back and notice the central balcony over the entrance; it is the focal point of the whole facade. Then wander downhill into Tansen\'s lanes of old Newar houses.',NULL,'[\"It was the seat of the Rana governors of Palpa during the Rana period.\", \"Wikipedia dates it to 1927 under Pratap Shumsher Jang Bahadur Rana.\", \"The palace was destroyed by Maoists during the civil war and later rebuilt.\", \"The Palpa Durbar Museum was formally inaugurated on 29 May 2019.\", \"The museum is closed on Tuesdays.\"]','10:00','16:30',100,50,15,60,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_01.jpg/1280px-Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_01.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_01.jpg','Acharya Bipin · CC BY-SA 4.0','palace,other,rana,tansen,art,lumbini','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tansen_Durbar\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19678683\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/news/120\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Tansen_Durbar\"]','तानसेनको मुटुमा रहेको रातो र सेतो राणा गभर्नरहरूको दरबार, ध्वस्त भएपछि पुनर्निर्माण गरिएको र अहिले पाल्पा दरबार सङ्ग्रहालय।','खुला चोकमा उभिएर तपाईंको अगाडि सेता खम्बा र हरिया जालीदार झ्यालले सजिएको लामो रातो अगाडिको भाग हेर्नुहोस्। यो तानसेन दरबार हो, जुन पाल्पाबाट पश्चिम नेपाल चलाउने राणा गभर्नरहरूका लागि बनाइएको थियो। विकिपिडियाले यसको श्रेय प्रताप शमशेर राणा र सन् 1927 लाई दिन्छ। दशकौँसम्म यो पश्चिमी पहाडमा राणा शक्तिको केन्द्र थियो। त्यसपछि सन् 2000 को मध्यतिरको माओवादी द्वन्द्वका बेला तानसेनमाथिको आक्रमणमा दरबार ध्वस्त भयो। अहिले देखिने भवन पुरानै डिजाइन पछ्याएर बनाइएको हो। सन् 2019 देखि यो तानसेन नगरपालिकाले चलाएको पाल्पा दरबार सङ्ग्रहालयका रूपमा औपचारिक रूपमा खुला छ, त्यसैले गभर्नरहरू कुनै बेला टहलिने बार्दलीमा तपाईं हिँड्न सक्नुहुन्छ। अलि पछाडि सरेर प्रवेशद्वारमाथिको बीचको बार्दली हेर्नुहोस्। यही पूरै अगाडिको भागको केन्द्र हो। त्यसपछि तानसेनका पुराना नेवार घरका गल्लीतिर ओरालो हिँड्नुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"राणा कालमा यो पाल्पाका राणा गभर्नरहरूको कार्यालय थियो।\", \"विकिपिडिया अनुसार यो प्रताप शमशेर जङ्गबहादुर राणाको पालामा सन् 1927 मा बनेको हो।\", \"गृहयुद्धका बेला माओवादीहरूले दरबार ध्वस्त पारे र पछि फेरि बनाइयो।\", \"पाल्पा दरबार सङ्ग्रहालयको औपचारिक उद्घाटन सन् 2019 मे 29 मा भयो।\", \"सङ्ग्रहालय मङ्गलबार बन्द रहन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Palpa10.JPG/1280px-Palpa10.JPG\", \"author\": \"जनक राज भट्ट\", \"caption\": \"Palpa Darbar seen from the square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palpa10.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_13.jpg/1280px-Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_13.jpg\", \"author\": \"Acharya Bipin\", \"caption\": \"Wide view of the rebuilt palace\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_13.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_06.jpg/1280px-Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_06.jpg\", \"author\": \"Acharya Bipin\", \"caption\": \"Detail of the red facade and windows\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_06.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Palpa_Durbar_%2CTansen_Palpa_01.jpg/1280px-Palpa_Durbar_%2CTansen_Palpa_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Acharya Bipin\", \"caption\": \"The palace in the centre of Tansen\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palpa_Durbar_,Tansen_Palpa_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_12.jpg/1280px-Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_12.jpg\", \"author\": \"Acharya Bipin\", \"caption\": \"The museum courtyard side of the palace\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palpa_Durbar_%26_Museum_12.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"slate\", \"notes\": \"Long curved three-storey facade painted deep red with white pilasters and window hoods, green lattice windows, a pillared porch with balcony at centre and taller corner blocks. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#A8322D\", \"#F2F0EA\", \"#2E6B4A\"], \"features\": [\"arched-windows\", \"carved-windows\"], \"height_m\": 14, \"footprint_m\": [60, 40], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"city-street\", \"newar-houses\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(87,'swargadwari','Swargadwari','स्वर्गद्वारी','Bhingri','Lumbini','Pyuthan',NULL,28.121034,82.674323,'pagoda','Hindu','Swargadwari Mahaprabhu (Swami Hamsananda); Vishnu and Shiva shrines; sacred fire (yajna)',1895,'Late 19th century: established as a pilgrimage centre by Swami Hamsananda (Narayan Gautam), who is said to have lit the continuous sacrificial fire on Baisakh full moon 1952 BS (1895 CE)','unknown','Hilltop ashram of white and pink plastered temples with stepped slate roofs and small gilded pinnacles, set behind dry-stone walls and railings among palms and pines at about 2,100 m.',0,'Hilltop ashram in Pyuthan where a sacred fire is said to have burned since 1895, honouring cows and Swami Hamsananda.','Catch your breath: you have climbed to about 2,100 metres, and the hills of Pyuthan roll away below you. Swargadwari means gateway to heaven. Local belief says the five Pandava brothers worshipped Shiva here for the last time before climbing to heaven. The ashram you see was founded by a guru called Swami Hamsananda, born Narayan Gautam, who spent much of his life in these hills herding and milking thousands of cows. That is why cows are honoured here so specially. Accounts say that on the full moon of Baisakh in 1952 BS, around 1895, he started an unbroken fire sacrifice for world peace, and devotees say the flame has been kept burning ever since. Walk past the stone walls to the white temple with its slate roof and gold pinnacle, and look in at the main image. If you come on Baisakh or Kartik full moon, you will share the hill with crowds of pilgrims.','The Pandavas are believed to have worshipped Mahadev here for the last time before ascending to heaven in the Dwapara Yuga.','[\"Wikipedia gives its altitude as about 2,100 m; other sources say 2,121 m or 2,300 m.\", \"It is said to have been founded by Swami Hamsananda (Narayan Gautam), who herded thousands of cows here.\", \"Devotees hold that a sacrificial fire lit in 1895 has burned continuously since.\", \"It is listed in Nepal\'s national inventory of cultural and historic heritage sites.\", \"After the civil war, donations of fodder fell so low that the resident cattle were at risk of starving.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,120,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Swargadwari_temple.jpg/1280px-Swargadwari_temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swargadwari_temple.jpg','Niraj Subedi · CC BY-SA 3.0','pagoda,hindu,bhingri,legend,art,lumbini','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swargadwari\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/travel/2020/01/18/gateway-to-heaven-and-beyond\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/swargadwari-pyuthanthe-gateway-that-keeps-its-promises\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/804148107\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Swargadwari\"]','प्यूठानको डाँडामाथिको आश्रम, जहाँ सन् १८९५ देखि पवित्र धुनी बलिरहेको भनिन्छ। यहाँ स्वामी हंसानन्द र गाईको विशेष सम्मान गरिन्छ।','अलि सास फेर्नुहोस्। तपाईं करिब २,१०० मिटर माथि चढ्नुभएको छ, र प्यूठानका डाँडा तपाईंको तल फैलिएका छन्। स्वर्गद्वारी भनेको स्वर्गको ढोका हो। स्थानीय विश्वास अनुसार पाँच पाण्डव दाजुभाइले स्वर्ग जानुअघि अन्तिम पटक यहीँ शिवको पूजा गरेका थिए। तपाईंले देखेको आश्रम स्वामी हंसानन्द नामका गुरुले स्थापना गरेका हुन्। उनको जन्मनाम नारायण गौतम थियो। उनले आफ्नो धेरै जीवन यी डाँडामा हजारौँ गाई चराउँदै र दुहुँदै बिताए। त्यसैले यहाँ गाईको विशेष सम्मान गरिन्छ। विवरण अनुसार सन् १८९५ तिर, वि.सं. १९५२ को वैशाख पूर्णिमामा, उनले विश्व शान्तिका लागि नभुसिने यज्ञ सुरु गरे। भक्तजन भन्छन्, त्यो आगो तब देखि आजसम्म बलिरहेको छ। ढुङ्गाका पर्खाल कटेर स्लेटको छाना र सुनौलो टुप्पो भएको सेतो मन्दिरसम्म पुग्नुहोस्, र मुख्य मूर्ति हेर्नुहोस्। वैशाख वा कात्तिक पूर्णिमामा आउनुभयो भने तीर्थयात्रीको भीडसँग डाँडा बाँड्नुपर्नेछ।','द्वापर युगमा स्वर्ग जानुअघि पाण्डवहरूले अन्तिम पटक यहीँ महादेवको पूजा गरेका थिए भन्ने मानिन्छ।','[\"विकिपिडियाले यसको उचाइ करिब २,१०० मिटर भनेको छ। अरू स्रोतले २,१२१ मिटर वा २,३०० मिटर भनेका छन्।\", \"यो स्वामी हंसानन्द (नारायण गौतम) ले स्थापना गरेको भनिन्छ, जसले यहाँ हजारौँ गाई चराए।\", \"भक्तजनको विश्वास छ, सन् १८९५ मा बालिएको यज्ञको आगो तब देखि निरन्तर बलिरहेको छ।\", \"यो नेपालको सांस्कृतिक तथा ऐतिहासिक सम्पदा स्थलहरूको राष्ट्रिय सूचीमा परेको छ।\", \"गृहयुद्धपछि घाँस दानाको चन्दा यति घट्यो कि यहाँका गाईवस्तु भोकै मर्ने खतरामा परे।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Baisakh Purnima\", \"note\": \"Full-moon fair marking the day the sacred fire is said to have been lit in 1895.\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"वैशाख पूर्णिमा\", \"note_np\": \"सन् १८९५ मा पवित्र धुनी बालिएको भनिने दिनको सम्झनामा लाग्ने पूर्णिमाको मेला।\"}, {\"name\": \"Kartik Purnima\", \"note\": \"Kartik full-moon pilgrimage fair at the ashram.\", \"month\": \"Kartik\", \"name_np\": \"कात्तिक पूर्णिमा\", \"note_np\": \"आश्रममा लाग्ने कात्तिक पूर्णिमाको तीर्थयात्रा मेला।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Swargdwari.jpg/1280px-Swargdwari.jpg\", \"author\": \"Niraj Subedi\", \"caption\": \"The main image of the Swargadwari temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swargdwari.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/View_of_Swargadwari_Temple_Phythan.jpg/1280px-View_of_Swargadwari_Temple_Phythan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bishal Budhathoki\", \"caption\": \"The temple complex on its hilltop\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Swargadwari_Temple_Phythan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Sunrise_view_from_swargadwari.JPG/1280px-Sunrise_view_from_swargadwari.JPG\", \"author\": \"Araz cafle\", \"caption\": \"Sunrise from Swargadwari\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunrise_view_from_swargadwari.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/View_of_mountain_range_from_swargadwari.JPG/1280px-View_of_mountain_range_from_swargadwari.JPG\", \"author\": \"Araz cafle\", \"caption\": \"Mountain view from the ashram\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_mountain_range_from_swargadwari.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Swargadwari.jpg/1280px-Swargadwari.jpg\", \"author\": \"Niraj Subedi\", \"caption\": \"Another view of Swargadwari\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swargadwari.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"slate\", \"notes\": \"White two-tier temple with grey slate roofs and a gold finial, pink side shrines, dry-stone walls and tall palm trees on a hilltop. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#F2F0EA\", \"#E3A5B0\", \"#6E6A63\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"fence-railing\", \"flags-red\", \"trident\"], \"height_m\": 10, \"footprint_m\": [60, 40], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(88,'bageshwori-temple-nepalgunj','Bageshwori Temple','बागेश्वरी मन्दिर','Nepalgunj','Lumbini','Banke',NULL,28.061796,81.623814,'pagoda','Hindu','Bageshwori (Bhagawati, Shakti Peetha of Sati\'s tongue)',NULL,'Shrine identified after Banke and the \'Naya Muluk\' districts were returned to Nepal (1860); rebuilt several times, notably after 2025 BS and 2033 BS (1968 and 1976 CE)','unknown','Modern three-tier pagoda-style temple with copper-sheathed roofs edged in red, gilded pillars and rows of bells around the sanctum, set in a paved courtyard. Beside it lies the Siddha Pokhari pond with a Mahadev shrine in the middle.',0,'Busy Shakti Peetha in central Nepalgunj where Sati\'s tongue is believed to have fallen, beside the Siddha Pokhari pond.','Step off the busy streets of Nepalgunj into this bright courtyard and listen to the bells. Devotees believe this is the spot where the tongue of the goddess Sati fell to earth, making it one of her Shakti Peethas. In Nepali, tongue is jibro, and local tradition says the goddess\'s name changed from Bakyeshwari, lady of speech, to Bageshwari. The story goes that a holy man and his disciple, on their way to Pashupati, spent a night here, and the goddess told the guru in a dream that her seat was in a hollow in the ground. Pilgrims still look into that hollow. The chief priests trace their line back to that disciple. Walk round to the Siddha Pokhari pond. In its middle stands a Mahadev temple whose image of Shiva has a moustache, which locals say is the only one of its kind. Come at Dashain, when soldiers and police carry in the Fulpati on Saptami.','A wandering holy man bound for Pashupati dreamed that the goddess\'s seat lay in a hollow here; the temple was founded on that spot, and Sati\'s tongue is believed to have fallen there.','[\"It stands in Gharbari Tol, ward 2 of Nepalgunj, Banke District.\", \"Devotees count it among the Shakti Peethas, where Sati\'s tongue is believed to have fallen.\", \"The chief priests are said to descend from the disciple who came with the founding holy man.\", \"During Dashain the army and police bring in the Fulpati on Saptami.\", \"The Mahadev temple in the Siddha Pokhari has an image of Shiva with a moustache.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,40,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Bageshwari_Temple.jpg/1280px-Bageshwari_Temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bageshwari_Temple.jpg','Ricky Partel · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,nepalgunj,legend,water,festival,lumbini','[\"https://ne.wikipedia.org/wiki/बागेश्वरी_मन्दिर,_नेपालगन्ज\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13183892\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1323518139\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bageshwari_Temple.jpg\"]','नेपालगञ्जको बीचमा रहेको व्यस्त शक्तिपीठ, जहाँ सतीको जिब्रो खसेको विश्वास गरिन्छ। छेउमा सिद्ध पोखरी छ।','नेपालगञ्जका व्यस्त सडकबाट यो उज्यालो आँगनमा पस्नुहोस् र घण्टको आवाज सुन्नुहोस्। भक्तजनले यही ठाउँमा देवी सतीको जिब्रो खसेको विश्वास गर्छन्, त्यसैले यो उनका शक्तिपीठमध्ये एक हो। नेपालीमा जिब्रोलाई जिब्रो नै भनिन्छ। स्थानीय परम्परा अनुसार देवीको नाम वाक्येश्वरी, अर्थात् वाणीकी देवीबाट बागेश्वरी भयो। कथा यस्तो छ, एक साधु र उनका चेला पशुपति जाँदै गर्दा यहाँ रात बिताए। देवीले गुरुलाई सपनामा भनिन्, उनको आसन भुइँको एउटा खाल्डोमा छ। तीर्थयात्री अझै त्यो खाल्डोमा हेर्छन्। मुख्य पुजारीहरू आफ्नो वंश त्यही चेलासम्म जोड्छन्। सिद्ध पोखरीतिर पनि जानुहोस्। त्यसको बीचमा महादेवको मन्दिर छ, जहाँको शिवको मूर्तिमा जुँगा छ। यस्तो मूर्ति यही एउटा मात्र हो भनेर स्थानीय भन्छन्। दशैँमा आउनुहोस्, जब सैनिक र प्रहरीले सप्तमीका दिन फूलपाती ल्याउँछन्।','पशुपति जाँदै गरेका एक घुमन्ते साधुले सपनामा देखे, देवीको आसन यहाँको खाल्डोमा छ। त्यही ठाउँमा मन्दिर बनाइयो, र सतीको जिब्रो त्यहीँ खसेको विश्वास गरिन्छ।','[\"यो बाँके जिल्लाको नेपालगञ्ज वडा २ को घरबारी टोलमा छ।\", \"भक्तजन यसलाई शक्तिपीठमध्ये एक गन्छन्, जहाँ सतीको जिब्रो खसेको विश्वास गरिन्छ।\", \"मुख्य पुजारीहरू मन्दिर स्थापना गर्ने साधुसँग आएका चेलाका सन्तान हुन् भनिन्छ।\", \"दशैँमा सेना र प्रहरीले सप्तमीका दिन फूलपाती ल्याउँछन्।\", \"सिद्ध पोखरीको महादेव मन्दिरमा जुँगा भएको शिवको मूर्ति छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Huge crowds on Saptami, Ashtami and Navami; the Fulpati arrives on Saptami and sacrifices are offered on Ashtami.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"सप्तमी, अष्टमी र नवमीमा ठूलो भीड हुन्छ। फूलपाती सप्तमीमा आइपुग्छ र अष्टमीमा बलि चढाइन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Crowds worship at the Mahadev temple in the Siddha Pokhari.\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"सिद्ध पोखरीको महादेव मन्दिरमा भक्तजनको भीड लाग्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Teej\", \"note\": \"Women gather at the temple during Teej.\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"तीज\", \"note_np\": \"तीजमा महिलाहरू मन्दिरमा भेला हुन्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Bageshwari_Temple%2C_Nepalgunj%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Bageshwari_Temple%2C_Nepalgunj%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Mohan K. Duwal\", \"caption\": \"The temple in the heart of Nepalgunj\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bageshwari_Temple,_Nepalgunj,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Jungeshwor_Mahadev%28Bageshwari_Temple%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Aradhya Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"The Mahadev shrine in the pond beside the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jungeshwor_Mahadev(Bageshwari_Temple).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Bageshwori_Temple_Nepalgunj_Banke_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Bageshwori_Temple_Nepalgunj_Banke_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The pagoda roofs of Bageshwori temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bageshwori_Temple_Nepalgunj_Banke_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Bageshwori_Temple_%281%29.JPG/1280px-Bageshwori_Temple_%281%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Devotees in the temple courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bageshwori_Temple_(1).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Bageshwori_Mandir.JPG/1280px-Bageshwori_Mandir.JPG\", \"author\": \"Raajiv Kilana Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Another view of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bageshwori_Mandir.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Three stacked pale metal roofs trimmed in red with a gold pinnacle and red flag; orange-red pillared ground floor hung with bells; lion statues at the steps. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"ochre-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#E8721C\", \"#C8102E\", \"#E7E3D6\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"bell\", \"lion-statues\", \"trident\", \"flags-red\"], \"height_m\": 15, \"footprint_m\": [20, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"pond\", \"city-street\", \"market-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(89,'janaki-mandir','Janaki Mandir','जानकी मन्दिर','Janakpur','Madhesh','Dhanusha',NULL,26.730411,85.925660,'palace','Hindu','Sita (Janaki), with Rama',1910,'Completed in 1910 CE by Queen Vrisha Bhanu of Orchha (Tikamgarh); on the spot where a golden image of Sita was reportedly found in 1657 by the saint Shurkishordas','unknown','Three-storey palace-like temple built entirely of stone and marble, fully white, over about 1,480 square metres. Its facade rises in domes, turrets and latticed windows; 60 rooms are decorated with coloured glass, engravings and paintings, and walls carry Madhubani paintings.',0,'Gleaming white marble temple of Sita in Janakpur, called the Nau Lakha Mandir after its nine-lakh building cost.','Shade your eyes: the white marble glows in the Terai sun. This is the Janaki Mandir, the temple of Sita, called Janaki because she was the daughter of King Janak of Mithila. People also call it the Nau Lakha Mandir, the nine-lakh temple, because its building is said to have cost about nine lakh coins. It was completed in 1910 by Queen Vrisha Bhanu of Orchha in central India. Tradition says that in 1657 the saint Shurkishordas found a golden image of Sita on this very spot, and that King Janak once worshipped Shiva\'s bow here. Look up at the domes and turrets, then step inside, where the temple holds some 60 rooms decorated with coloured glass, engravings and paintings, and Madhubani art on the walls. Next door is the wedding pavilion where, Hindus believe, Sita chose Rama as her husband. Come at Vivaha Panchami to see that wedding re-enacted.','The Sita Swayamvara, in which Sita chose Rama after he broke Shiva\'s bow, is believed to have taken place here; King Janak is said to have worshipped the bow on this site.','[\"Queen Vrisha Bhanu of Orchha (Tikamgarh) built the temple in 1910.\", \"It is called Nau Lakha Mandir because building it cost about nine lakh coins.\", \"The three-storey temple covers about 1,480 square metres and is built of stone and marble.\", \"It was placed on UNESCO\'s World Heritage Tentative List in 2008.\", \"Nepal has declared the temple area a protected monument zone under the Ancient Monuments Preservation Act, 1956.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,60,'Reports on 26 April 2015 said the temple had partly collapsed in the April 2015 earthquake.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Janaki_Temple_Janakpurdham_%2CNepal.jpg/1280px-Janaki_Temple_Janakpurdham_%2CNepal.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janaki_Temple_Janakpurdham_,Nepal.jpg','Rashikafle · CC BY-SA 4.0','palace,hindu,janakpur,legend,art,madhesh','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janaki_Mandir\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3161830\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/3595105449\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Janaki_Mandir\"]','जनकपुरमा सीताको चम्किलो सेतो सङ्गमरमरको मन्दिर, नौ लाख सिक्का खर्च भएकाले नौलखा मन्दिर भनिने।','आँखामाथि हात राख्नुहोस्। तराईको घाममा सेतो सङ्गमरमर चम्कन्छ। यो जानकी मन्दिर हो, सीताको मन्दिर। मिथिलाका राजा जनककी छोरी भएकाले उनलाई जानकी भनिन्छ। मानिसहरू यसलाई नौलखा मन्दिर, अर्थात् नौ लाखको मन्दिर पनि भन्छन्, किनभने यो बनाउन करिब नौ लाख सिक्का खर्च भएको भनिन्छ। मध्य भारतको ओरछाकी रानी वृषभानु कुँवरीले सन् 1910 मा यसलाई पूरा गराइन्। परम्परा अनुसार सन् 1657 मा सन्त शुरकिशोरदासले यही ठाउँमा सीताको सुनको मूर्ति भेटे, र राजा जनकले यहीँ शिवको धनुषको पूजा गर्थे। माथि गुम्बज र बुर्जा हेर्नुहोस्, अनि भित्र पस्नुहोस्। मन्दिरमा रङ्गीन सिसा, कुँदाइ र चित्रले सजिएका करिब 60 कोठा छन्, र भित्तामा मधुबनी कला छ। छेउमै विवाह मण्डप छ। हिन्दूहरूको विश्वास अनुसार सीताले यहीँ रामलाई आफ्नो पति रोजेकी थिइन्। विवाह पञ्चमीमा आउनुभयो भने त्यो विवाहको पुनःप्रदर्शन देख्न पाउनुहुन्छ।','यहीँ सीता स्वयंवर भएको मानिन्छ, जहाँ रामले शिवको धनुष भाँचेपछि सीताले उनलाई रोजिन्। राजा जनकले यही ठाउँमा धनुषको पूजा गर्थे भनिन्छ।','[\"ओरछा (टिकमगढ)की रानी वृषभानु कुँवरीले सन् 1910 मा मन्दिर बनाइन्।\", \"यो बनाउन करिब नौ लाख सिक्का खर्च भएकाले यसलाई नौलखा मन्दिर भनिन्छ।\", \"तीन तले यो मन्दिर करिब 1,480 वर्गमिटरमा फैलिएको छ र ढुङ्गा तथा सङ्गमरमरले बनेको छ।\", \"सन् 2008 मा यसलाई युनेस्कोको विश्व सम्पदा सम्भावित सूचीमा राखिएको थियो।\", \"नेपालले प्राचीन स्मारक संरक्षण ऐन, 1956 अन्तर्गत मन्दिर क्षेत्रलाई संरक्षित स्मारक क्षेत्र घोषणा गरेको छ।\"]','सन् 2015 अप्रिल 26 का प्रतिवेदनमा अप्रिल 2015 को भूकम्पले मन्दिर आंशिक रूपमा भत्किएको बताइएको थियो।','[{\"name\": \"Vivaha Panchami\", \"note\": \"Celebrates the wedding of Rama and Sita; the marriage is re-enacted in Janakpur.\", \"month\": \"Mangsir\", \"name_np\": \"विवाह पञ्चमी\", \"note_np\": \"राम र सीताको विवाह मनाइन्छ। जनकपुरमा विवाहको पुनःप्रदर्शन गरिन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Ram Navami\", \"note\": \"Rama\'s birthday draws thousands of pilgrims to the temple.\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"रामनवमी\", \"note_np\": \"रामको जन्मदिनमा मन्दिरमा हजारौँ तीर्थयात्री आउँछन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Major festival when the temple is crowded with worshippers.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"ठूलो चाड, जब मन्दिर भक्तजनले भरिन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Janaki_temple_janakpurdham_nepal.jpg/1280px-Janaki_temple_janakpurdham_nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Crish mandal\", \"caption\": \"The temple illuminated at night\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janaki_temple_janakpurdham_nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/2009-03_Janakpur_05.jpg/1280px-2009-03_Janakpur_05.jpg\", \"author\": \"Ralf Lotys (Sicherlich)\", \"caption\": \"The white facade of Janaki Mandir\", \"license\": \"CC BY 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2009-03_Janakpur_05.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Inside_view_of_the_Janki_Mandir_of_Janakpur%2C_Nepal..JPG/1280px-Inside_view_of_the_Janki_Mandir_of_Janakpur%2C_Nepal..JPG\", \"author\": \"User:Adutta.np\", \"caption\": \"Inside the temple of Ram and Sita\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inside_view_of_the_Janki_Mandir_of_Janakpur,_Nepal..JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Interior_View_of_Janaki_Temple%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7460-Pano.jpg/1280px-Interior_View_of_Janaki_Temple%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7460-Pano.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Panorama of the inner courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Interior_View_of_Janaki_Temple,_Janakpur-September_22,_2016-IMG_7460-Pano.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Janaki_Mandir_of_Janakpurdham%2C_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Janaki_Mandir_of_Janakpurdham%2C_Nepal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Aditya Pal\", \"caption\": \"Wide view of the temple front\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janaki_Mandir_of_Janakpurdham,_Nepal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"dome-temple\", \"roof\": \"white-dome\", \"notes\": \"Symmetrical white marble facade with a big central dome, many small domed turrets (chhatris) and arched latticed windows, orange flags on top. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#F7F5EF\", \"#E07B2A\", \"#C9302C\"], \"features\": [\"domes-multiple\", \"minaret-turrets\", \"arched-windows\", \"carved-windows\", \"flags-red\"], \"height_m\": 25, \"footprint_m\": [50, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"garden-lawn\", \"city-street\", \"pond\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(90,'ram-mandir-janakpur','Ram Mandir, Janakpur','राम मन्दिर, जनकपुर','Janakpur','Madhesh','Dhanusha',NULL,26.728370,85.926860,'pagoda','Hindu','Rama',1782,'First built in the 17th century by Chaturbhuj Giri; rebuilt in 1782 by the Gorkhali general Amar Singh Thapa','Shah (Gorkhali rebuilding)','Two-tiered Nepali pagoda temple of exposed red brick with carved timber struts, rows of small bells under the eaves and a gilded pinnacle, standing in a paved courtyard with stone columns. The Rajdevi Shakti temple shares the complex.',0,'One of Janakpur\'s oldest temples, a red-brick pagoda to Rama rebuilt in 1782 by General Amar Singh Thapa.','Here, in the plains of Mithila, you are looking at something unusual: a hill-style Nepali pagoda. This is the Ram Mandir, one of the oldest temples in Janakpur. Its first shrine is credited to a holy man named Chaturbhuj Giri in the seventeenth century. In 1782 the Gorkhali general Amar Singh Thapa rebuilt it in the pagoda style you see today, with two brick storeys, carved timber struts and a gilded pinnacle. Count the little bells hanging under the roof edges; they ring when the wind blows. The temple stands directly in front of the sacred Dhanush Sagar, one of Janakpur\'s many holy ponds, so take a moment to look across the water. Inside the same complex is the Rajdevi Mandir, a Shakti shrine. Janakpur believes Sita was born and married here, so a temple to her husband Rama feels very much at home a short walk from the Janaki Mandir.',NULL,'[\"It is one of the oldest Hindu temples in Janakpur.\", \"Chaturbhuj Giri is credited with building the first temple in the 17th century.\", \"The Gorkhali general Amar Singh Thapa rebuilt it in 1782.\", \"It is built in traditional Nepali pagoda style, unlike most Terai temples.\", \"It stands in front of the Dhanush Sagar pond and includes the Rajdevi Shakti temple.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Main_Mandir_of_Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7622.jpg/1280px-Main_Mandir_of_Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7622.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Main_Mandir_of_Ram_Mandir,_Janakpur-September_22,_2016-IMG_7622.jpg','Bijay chaurasia · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,shah (gorkhali rebuilding),janakpur,art,madhesh','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ram_Mandir,_Janakpur\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janaki_Mandir\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q127425128\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Ram_Mandir,_Janakpur\"]','जनकपुरका सबैभन्दा पुराना मन्दिरमध्ये एक, सन् 1782 मा सेनापति अमरसिंह थापाले पुनर्निर्माण गरेको रामको रातो इँटाको पगोडा।','यहाँ, मिथिलाको समथर भूमिमा, तपाईं एउटा अनौठो चिज हेर्दै हुनुहुन्छ, पहाडी शैलीको नेपाली पगोडा। यो राम मन्दिर हो, जनकपुरका सबैभन्दा पुराना मन्दिरमध्ये एक। सत्रौँ शताब्दीमा चतुर्भुज गिरि नामका सन्तले यहाँ पहिलो मन्दिर बनाएको मानिन्छ। सन् 1782 मा गोर्खाली सेनापति अमरसिंह थापाले यसलाई अहिलेको पगोडा शैलीमा फेरि बनाए, दुई तले इँटाको भवन, कुँदिएका काठका टेकासहित र माथि सुनौलो टुप्पो। छानाको किनारमुनि झुन्डिएका साना घण्टी गन्नुहोस्। हावा चल्दा ती बज्छन्। मन्दिर जनकपुरका धेरै पवित्र पोखरीमध्ये एक, पवित्र धनुषसागरको ठीक अगाडि छ, त्यसैले पानीपारि हेर्न केही बेर रोकिनुहोस्। यही परिसरभित्र राजदेवी मन्दिर पनि छ, जुन शक्तिको मन्दिर हो। जनकपुरवासीको विश्वास छ, सीताको जन्म र विवाह यहीँ भएको थियो। त्यसैले उनका पति रामको मन्दिर जानकी मन्दिरबाट छोटो पैदल दूरीमा हुनु एकदमै स्वाभाविक लाग्छ।',NULL,'[\"यो जनकपुरका सबैभन्दा पुराना हिन्दू मन्दिरमध्ये एक हो।\", \"चतुर्भुज गिरिले 17 औँ शताब्दीमा पहिलो मन्दिर बनाएको मानिन्छ।\", \"गोर्खाली सेनापति अमरसिंह थापाले सन् 1782 मा यसलाई फेरि बनाए।\", \"धेरैजसो तराईका मन्दिर भन्दा फरक, यो परम्परागत नेपाली पगोडा शैलीमा बनेको छ।\", \"यो धनुषसागर पोखरीको अगाडि छ र यसमा राजदेवी शक्ति मन्दिर पनि पर्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Ram Navami\", \"note\": \"Rama\'s birthday, celebrated across Janakpur\'s temples.\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"रामनवमी\", \"note_np\": \"रामको जन्मदिन, जनकपुरका मन्दिरमा मनाइन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Vivaha Panchami\", \"note\": \"Janakpur celebrates the wedding of Rama and Sita.\", \"month\": \"Mangsir\", \"name_np\": \"विवाह पञ्चमी\", \"note_np\": \"जनकपुरमा राम र सीताको विवाह उत्सव मनाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Gajur_of_Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7623.jpg/1280px-Gajur_of_Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7623.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"The gilded pinnacle (gajur) of the Ram Mandir\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gajur_of_Ram_Mandir,_Janakpur-September_22,_2016-IMG_7623.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Eastern_entrance_of_Rajdevi_Temple%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7608.jpg/1280px-Eastern_entrance_of_Rajdevi_Temple%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7608.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Eastern entrance of the Rajdevi temple in the complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_entrance_of_Rajdevi_Temple,_Janakpur-September_22,_2016-IMG_7608.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7610.jpg/1280px-Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7610.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Inside the Ram Mandir complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram_Mandir,_Janakpur-September_22,_2016-IMG_7610.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7615.jpg/1280px-Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7615.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Shrines in the temple courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram_Mandir,_Janakpur-September_22,_2016-IMG_7615.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7638.jpg/1280px-Ram_Mandir%2C_Janakpur-September_22%2C_2016-IMG_7638.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Another view of the Ram Mandir complex\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram_Mandir,_Janakpur-September_22,_2016-IMG_7638.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Compact two-tier brick pagoda with dark timber struts, fringe of small bells and a tall gilded spire, beside squat red stone columns on a pale paved court. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#A9512F\", \"#5B4636\", \"#C9A54A\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"bell\", \"carved-windows\"], \"height_m\": 12, \"footprint_m\": [12, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"pond\", \"city-street\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(91,'dhanusha-dham','Dhanusha Dham (Dhanush Mandir)','धनुषाधाम (धनुष मन्दिर)','Dhanushadham','Madhesh','Dhanusha',NULL,26.830660,86.057003,'shikhara','Hindu','Fragment of Shiva\'s bow (Dhanush), with Rama and Sita',NULL,'','unknown','Small modern Terai temple: a low painted enclosure wall in yellow, red and blue with an entrance shrine topped by a small domed shikhara and gilded finial, under a large spreading tree. A fossilised piece said to be part of the bow is venerated inside.',0,'Village shrine where a piece of Shiva\'s bow, broken by Rama to win Sita, is believed to have fallen and turned to stone.','You have travelled out from Janakpur into the villages of Dhanusha, the district that takes its name from the object honoured here. In the Ramayana, King Janak promised his daughter Sita to whoever could string the mighty bow of Shiva. Prince Rama lifted it, bent it, and snapped it in two. Hindus believe that one piece of that broken bow fell at this spot, and inside the Dhanush Mandir devotees honour a fossilised fragment said to be part of it. Walk through the bright gate painted with the words Sita Ram and pause under the great tree that shades the shrine. Even the district\'s name, Dhanusha, comes from the bow. Visit in Magh, when the Makar Mela is held on Sundays and, according to Janakpur\'s heritage catalogue, hundreds of thousands of devotees crowd Dhanushadham. It is a quiet, rural stop on the Ramayana trail around Janakpur.','When Rama broke Shiva\'s bow at Sita\'s swayamvara in Janakpur, a piece of it is believed to have fallen here, where it lies as a fossil.','[\"It is believed to be where a piece of Shiva\'s bow fell after Rama broke it at Sita\'s swayamvara.\", \"Devotees venerate a fossilised fragment said to come from the bow.\", \"The Makar Mela, held on Sundays in Magh, draws huge crowds.\", \"It lies in Dhanushadham Municipality, north-east of Janakpur in Dhanusha District.\", \"Dhanusha District takes its name from the dhanush, or bow.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Dhanush_Mandir%2C_Dhanushadham_Janakpur.jpg/1280px-Dhanush_Mandir%2C_Dhanushadham_Janakpur.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhanush_Mandir,_Dhanushadham_Janakpur.jpg','Aditya Pal · CC BY-SA 4.0','shikhara,hindu,dhanushadham,legend,art,madhesh','[\"https://janakpurmun.gov.np/sites/janakpurmun.gov.np/files/documents/Janakpur-Heritage-Catalogue-design-hz8wr4.pdf\", \"https://sacredsites.com/asia/nepal/janakpur.html\", \"https://embed.wionews.com/photos/janakpur-to-dhanusha-dham-top-hindu-pilgrimage-sites-in-nepal-linked-to-the-ramayana-1757595619323\", \"https://ne.wikipedia.org/wiki/धनुषाधाम\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/4422055489\"]','गाउँको मन्दिर, जहाँ सीतालाई जित्न रामले भाँचेको शिवको धनुषको एक टुक्रा खसेर ढुङ्गा बनेको विश्वास गरिन्छ।','तपाईं जनकपुरबाट धनुषाका गाउँतिर आउनुभएको छ। यहाँ पूजिने वस्तुबाटै यो जिल्लाले आफ्नो नाम पाएको हो। रामायणमा राजा जनकले शिवको शक्तिशाली धनुषमा प्रत्यञ्चा चढाउन सक्नेलाई आफ्नी छोरी सीता दिने वचन दिएका थिए। राजकुमार रामले त्यसलाई उठाए, झुकाए र दुई टुक्रा पारे। हिन्दूको विश्वास छ, त्यो भाँचिएको धनुषको एक टुक्रा यही ठाउँमा खस्यो। धनुष मन्दिरभित्र भक्तजनले त्यसैको अंश मानिने जीवाश्म बनेको टुक्राको पूजा गर्छन्। सीता राम लेखिएको रङ्गीन ढोकाबाट भित्र जानुहोस् र मन्दिरमा छहारी दिने ठूलो रुखमुनि केही बेर रोकिनुहोस्। जिल्लाको नाम धनुषा पनि धनुषबाटै आएको हो। माघमा आउनुहोस्, जब आइतबारहरूमा मकर मेला लाग्छ। जनकपुरको सम्पदा सूची अनुसार त्यतिबेला लाखौँ भक्तजन धनुषाधाममा भीड लगाउँछन्। जनकपुरवरपरको रामायण यात्रामा यो शान्त, गाउँले विश्राम स्थल हो।','जनकपुरमा सीताको स्वयंवरमा रामले शिवको धनुष भाँच्दा त्यसको एक टुक्रा यहीँ खसेको र जीवाश्मका रूपमा रहेको विश्वास गरिन्छ।','[\"रामले सीताको स्वयंवरमा शिवको धनुष भाँचेपछि त्यसको एक टुक्रा खसेको ठाउँ यही हो भन्ने विश्वास गरिन्छ।\", \"भक्तजनले धनुषबाट आएको भनिने जीवाश्म बनेको टुक्राको पूजा गर्छन्।\", \"माघका आइतबार लाग्ने मकर मेलामा ठूलो भीड हुन्छ।\", \"यो धनुषा जिल्लामा, जनकपुरको उत्तर-पूर्वमा रहेको धनुषाधाम नगरपालिकामा पर्छ।\", \"धनुषा जिल्लाले आफ्नो नाम धनुष, अर्थात् धनुबाट पाएको हो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Makar Mela\", \"note\": \"Fair held on Sundays of Magh; hundreds of thousands of devotees visit Dhanushadham.\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"मकर मेला\", \"note_np\": \"माघका आइतबार लाग्ने मेला। लाखौँ भक्तजन धनुषाधाम आउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Dhanush%28bow%29_of_lord_Ram_at_Dhanush_Mandir%2C_Dhanushadham_Janakpur.jpg/1280px-Dhanush%28bow%29_of_lord_Ram_at_Dhanush_Mandir%2C_Dhanushadham_Janakpur.jpg\", \"author\": \"Aditya Pal\", \"caption\": \"The stone \'bow\' fragment venerated in the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhanush(bow)_of_lord_Ram_at_Dhanush_Mandir,_Dhanushadham_Janakpur.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The Dhanushadham temple area\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Shrines at Dhanushadham\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(2).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg/1280px-Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%283%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Another view of Dhanushadham\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(3).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%289%29.jpg/1280px-Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%289%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Surroundings of the Dhanush temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhanushadham_Govindapur_Janakpur_Dhanusha_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(9).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"flat\", \"notes\": \"Long low yellow wall with red base and blue trim, a central gateway shrine with a small yellow dome and gold finial, all under one huge shady tree. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"ochre-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#F2C230\", \"#C0392B\", \"#2D6FB5\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"bell\", \"sacred-tree\"], \"height_m\": 7, \"footprint_m\": [40, 25], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"village\", \"plains-fields\", \"sacred-grove\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(92,'gadhimai-temple','Gadhimai Temple','गढीमाई मन्दिर','Bariyarpur (Mahagadhimai)','Madhesh','Bara',NULL,26.993022,85.046952,'pagoda','Hindu','Gadhimai, an aspect of Kali',NULL,'The Gadhimai festival is said to have begun around 1759; the temple building is modern','unknown','Small cream-painted shrine with arched openings decorated with relief tigers, a balustraded roof terrace and a stepped two-tier tiled roof in red and gold, set under large trees in an open fairground.',0,'Shrine of the goddess Gadhimai in Bara, home of a five-yearly festival known for mass animal sacrifice.','You are in Bariyarpur, about seven kilometres east of Kalaiya and close to the Indian border. The modest shrine in front of you belongs to Gadhimai, honoured as an aspect of Kali, the goddess of power. Look for the painted tigers marching across its walls. Every five years this quiet place is overwhelmed by the Gadhimai festival, which is said to have begun around 1759, when a local landlord named Bhagwan Chaudhary dreamed in jail that a blood offering to the goddess would set him free. Pilgrims from Nepal and India bring coconuts, sweets and red cloth, and many also bring animals. The festival has been called the largest animal sacrifice event in the world, and it has drawn strong protests from animal rights groups and many Nepali Hindus. In 2019 Nepal\'s Supreme Court ordered an end to live sacrifices, but reports say the order has been widely ignored. The most recent festival began on 2 December 2024.','The festival is said to have begun when Bhagwan Chaudhary, imprisoned, dreamed that Gadhimai would free him if he offered her a blood sacrifice.','[\"The temple is in Mahagadhimai Municipality, about 7 km east of Kalaiya in Bara District.\", \"The Gadhimai festival is held every five years and is said to date from around 1759.\", \"An estimated 250,000 or more animals were sacrificed during the 2009 festival.\", \"Nepal\'s Supreme Court ordered an end to live animal sacrifice in 2019, but the order is widely ignored.\", \"The 2024 festival started on 2 December.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Gadhimai_Temple_%282%29.JPG/1280px-Gadhimai_Temple_%282%29.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gadhimai_Temple_(2).JPG','बिप्लब आनन्द · CC BY-SA 3.0','pagoda,hindu,bariyarpur (mahagadhimai),legend,art,festival,madhesh','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gadhimai_Temple\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gadhimai_festival\", \"https://newsonair.gov.in/gadhimai-mahotsav-continues-to-be-the-worlds-biggest-animal-slaughter-event\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5516371\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/315262567\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Gadhimai_Temple\"]','बाराकी देवी गढीमाईको मन्दिर, पाँच वर्षमा लाग्ने र पशुबलिका लागि चर्चित मेलाको थलो।','तपाईं कलैयाबाट करिब सात किलोमिटर पूर्व, भारतीय सीमा नजिकको बरियारपुरमा हुनुहुन्छ। तपाईंको अगाडिको सादा मन्दिर गढीमाईको हो, जसलाई शक्तिकी देवी कालीको रूप मानिन्छ। भित्तामा लस्करै चित्र बनाइएका बाघ हेर्नुहोस्। हरेक पाँच वर्षमा यो शान्त ठाउँ गढीमाई मेलाले भरिन्छ। यो मेला करिब सन् १७५९ मा सुरु भएको भनिन्छ, जब भगवान् चौधरी नाम गरेका एक स्थानीय जमिनदारले जेलमा सपना देखे, देवीलाई रगतको भेटी चढाए उनी छुट्नेछन्। नेपाल र भारतबाट तीर्थयात्री नरिवल, मिठाई र रातो कपडा ल्याउँछन्, र धेरैले पशु पनि ल्याउँछन्। यो मेलालाई संसारकै सबैभन्दा ठूलो पशुबलि हुने कार्यक्रम भनिएको छ। पशु अधिकारका समूह र धेरै नेपाली हिन्दूले यसको कडा विरोध गरेका छन्। सन् २०१९ मा नेपालको सर्वोच्च अदालतले जीवित पशुबलि बन्द गर्न आदेश दियो, तर प्रतिवेदन अनुसार त्यो आदेश धेरैले मानेका छैनन्। पछिल्लो मेला सन् २०२४ डिसेम्बर २ मा सुरु भयो।','जेलमा रहेका भगवान् चौधरीले सपना देखे, रगतको बलि चढाए गढीमाईले उनलाई मुक्त गर्नेछिन्। त्यसपछि मेला सुरु भएको भनिन्छ।','[\"मन्दिर बारा जिल्लाको कलैयाबाट करिब ७ किमी पूर्वको महागढीमाई नगरपालिकामा छ।\", \"गढीमाई मेला हरेक पाँच वर्षमा हुन्छ र करिब सन् १७५९ देखि सुरु भएको भनिन्छ।\", \"सन् २००९ को मेलामा अनुमानित २,५०,००० वा त्योभन्दा बढी पशुको बलि दिइएको थियो।\", \"नेपालको सर्वोच्च अदालतले सन् २०१९ मा जीवित पशुबलि बन्द गर्न आदेश दियो, तर त्यो आदेश धेरैले मानेका छैनन्।\", \"सन् २०२४ को मेला डिसेम्बर २ मा सुरु भयो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Gadhimai Mela\", \"note\": \"Held every five years (most recently from 2 Dec 2024); notorious for mass animal sacrifice.\", \"month\": \"Mangsir\", \"name_np\": \"गढीमाई मेला\", \"note_np\": \"हरेक पाँच वर्षमा लाग्ने मेला (पछिल्लो पटक २०२४ डिसेम्बर २ देखि)। सामूहिक पशुबलिका लागि बदनाम।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Gadhimai_Temple_%281%29.JPG/1280px-Gadhimai_Temple_%281%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"बिप्लब आनन्द\", \"caption\": \"Devotees at the Gadhimai shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gadhimai_Temple_(1).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Gadhimai_Temple_%283%29.JPG/1280px-Gadhimai_Temple_%283%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"बिप्लब आनन्द\", \"caption\": \"The shrine and its tiled roof\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gadhimai_Temple_(3).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Gadhimai_Temple_%285%29.JPG/1280px-Gadhimai_Temple_%285%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"बिप्लब आनन्द\", \"caption\": \"The temple grounds at Bariyarpur\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gadhimai_Temple_(5).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Gadhimai_Temple_%286%29.JPG/1280px-Gadhimai_Temple_%286%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"बिप्लब आनन्द\", \"caption\": \"Pilgrims around the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gadhimai_Temple_(6).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/Arena_for_Gadhimai_buffalo_sacrifice_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Wolf Gordon Clifton / Animal People, Inc.\", \"caption\": \"The walled arena used during the Gadhimai festival\", \"license\": \"CC BY 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arena_for_Gadhimai_buffalo_sacrifice_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Cream shrine with ogee arches and big relief tigers on the walls, a white balustrade terrace and a small two-tier red-and-gold tiled roof, under tall trees. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#EFE6D2\", \"#B7472A\", \"#E1B12C\"], \"features\": [\"flags-red\", \"fence-railing\", \"sacred-tree\", \"lamps-diyo\"], \"height_m\": 9, \"footprint_m\": [10, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"sacred-grove\", \"plains-fields\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(93,'chhinnamasta-bhagawati','Chhinnamasta Bhagawati Temple','छिन्नमस्ता भगवती मन्दिर','Rajbiraj','Madhesh','Saptari',NULL,26.451079,86.731189,'pagoda','Hindu','Chhinnamasta Bhagawati (headless form of the goddess)',NULL,'Founded in the late 13th century by King Shaktisimhadeva (Shakrasimhadeva) of the Karnat dynasty after his overthrow in 1295; damaged by Tughlaq armies in 1324; the present building is modern','Karnat (Simraungadh)','Three-tier pagoda-style temple with red sheet roofs edged in white, bands of red and yellow under the eaves and a lotus finial, inside a railed queueing yard with a hanging bell and covered pavilions.',0,'Saptari\'s oldest and most revered shrine, founded by a dethroned Karnat king, where the goddess\'s image has lost its head.','You are about ten kilometres from Rajbiraj, close to the Indian border, at the most revered shrine in Saptari. Its old name is Sakhada Bhagawati. The story begins in Simraungadh, capital of the Karnat kings of Mithila. In 1295 King Shaktisimhadeva, also called Shakrasimhadeva, was overthrown by his own minister. He came here to spend his last years in forest retreat, cleared the jungle, and set up his goddess, named after him as Sakhreswari. His fort stood nearby, at a place still called Gadhi Gaachhi. In 1324 the armies of Sultan Ghiyasuddin Tughlaq crossed this land on their way to Simraungadh and damaged the temple and its image. Because the goddess\'s image is headless, people call her Chhinnamasta, she whose head is severed. Step under the red tiered roofs and ring the great bell. At Bada Dashain, thousands of devotees from Nepal and India come here.',NULL,'[\"It was founded in the 13th century by Shaktisimhadeva, fifth ruler of the Karnat dynasty.\", \"Shaktisimhadeva was overthrown in a coup by his minister Chadeshwar Thakur in 1295.\", \"Tughlaq armies damaged the temple and its idol in 1324.\", \"The name Chhinnamasta refers to the goddess\'s missing head.\", \"It is about 10 km from Rajbiraj, in Chhinnamasta Rural Municipality.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,40,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple_NP_SAP_01.jpg/1280px-Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple_NP_SAP_01.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple_NP_SAP_01.jpg','Bijay chaurasia · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,karnat (simraungadh),rajbiraj,festival,madhesh','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simraungadh\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13181099\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/5037212575\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple,_Saptari\"]','सप्तरीको सबैभन्दा पुरानो र श्रद्धेय मन्दिर, पदच्युत कर्नाट राजाले स्थापना गरेको, जहाँ देवीको मूर्तिको शिर छैन।','तपाईं राजविराजबाट करिब दस किलोमिटर टाढा, भारतीय सीमा नजिकै, सप्तरीको सबैभन्दा श्रद्धेय मन्दिरमा हुनुहुन्छ। यसको पुरानो नाम सखडा भगवती हो। कथा मिथिलाका कर्नाट राजाको राजधानी सिमरौनगढबाट सुरु हुन्छ। सन् 1295 मा राजा शक्तिसिंहदेव, जसलाई शक्रसिंहदेव पनि भनिन्छ, आफ्नै मन्त्रीबाट गद्दीबाट हटाइए। उनी जीवनका अन्तिम वर्ष वनमा एकान्तवासमा बिताउन यहाँ आए, जङ्गल सफा गरे र आफ्नी देवीलाई स्थापना गरे, जसलाई उनकै नामबाट सखरेश्वरी भनियो। उनको किल्ला नजिकै गढी गाछी भनिने ठाउँमा थियो, जुन नाम आजसम्म चलिरहेको छ। सन् 1324 मा सुल्तान गियासुद्दीन तुगलकका सेना सिमरौनगढ जाने बाटोमा यो भूमि हुँदै गए, र मन्दिर तथा मूर्तिमा क्षति पुर्‍याए। देवीको मूर्तिमा शिर छैन, त्यसैले मानिसहरू उनलाई छिन्नमस्ता, अर्थात् शिर काटिएकी देवी भन्छन्। तह-तहका रातो छानामुनि पसेर ठूलो घण्टा बजाउनुहोस्। बडा दशैँमा नेपाल र भारतबाट हजारौँ भक्तजन यहाँ आउँछन्।',NULL,'[\"यो तेह्रौँ शताब्दीमा कर्नाट वंशका पाँचौँ शासक शक्तिसिंहदेवले स्थापना गरेका थिए।\", \"सन् 1295 मा शक्तिसिंहदेवलाई उनका मन्त्री चडेश्वर ठाकुरले विद्रोह गरेर गद्दीबाट हटाए।\", \"तुगलकका सेनाले सन् 1324 मा मन्दिर र यसको मूर्तिमा क्षति पुर्‍याए।\", \"छिन्नमस्ता नामले देवीको शिर नभएकोलाई जनाउँछ।\", \"यो राजविराजबाट करिब 10 किलोमिटर टाढा, छिन्नमस्ता गाउँपालिकामा छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Bada Dashain\", \"note\": \"Thousands of devotees from Nepal and India come to worship Bhagawati.\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"बडा दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"नेपाल र भारतबाट हजारौँ भक्तजन भगवतीको पूजा गर्न आउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple%2C_Saptari.jpg/1280px-Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple%2C_Saptari.jpg\", \"author\": \"बिप्लब आनन्द\", \"caption\": \"The temple of Chhinnamasta Bhagawati\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple,_Saptari.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Chhinamasta.JPG/1280px-Chhinamasta.JPG\", \"author\": \"बिप्लब आनन्द\", \"caption\": \"Another view of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chhinamasta.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple_NP_SAP_02.jpg/1280px-Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple_NP_SAP_02.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"The tiered roofs and lotus finial\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinnamasta_Bhagawati_Temple_NP_SAP_02.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Chhinnamasta_Temple%2C_Saptari-WLV-0807.jpg/1280px-Chhinnamasta_Temple%2C_Saptari-WLV-0807.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay Chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"The temple compound in Saptari\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chhinnamasta_Temple,_Saptari-WLV-0807.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Chinnamasta_Bhagwati_Temple_Rajbiraj_%284%29.JPG/1280px-Chinnamasta_Bhagwati_Temple_Rajbiraj_%284%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Devotees at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinnamasta_Bhagwati_Temple_Rajbiraj_(4).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Three stacked red roofs with white edges and yellow bands, a pink-and-green lotus finial with trident on top; railings and a blue tin-roofed pavilion in front. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#C8402E\", \"#F2F0EA\", \"#E8B730\"], \"features\": [\"bell\", \"fence-railing\", \"flags-red\"], \"height_m\": 14, \"footprint_m\": [14, 14], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"village\", \"plains-fields\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(94,'simraungadh-ranivas','Simraungadh and Ranivas Temple','सिम्रौनगढ र रानीवास मन्दिर','Simraungadh','Madhesh','Bara',NULL,26.889392,85.114597,'shikhara','Hindu','Rama and Sita (Ranivas temple); Kankali Mai nearby',1878,'Capital of the Karnat kings of Mithila from 1097 CE to the early 14th century; the present Ranivas Ram Janaki temple was built in 1878 by Jagat Jung Rana on ruins believed to be the old palace','Karnat (capital); Rana (Ranivas temple)','White shikhara temple with red and green bands, an arcaded colonnade around the sanctum, small corner spires and a gilded trident finial, raised on a stepped plinth among crumbling brick palace walls and arches of the Ranivas complex.',0,'Medieval capital of the Karnat kings of Mithila, where a Rana-era Ram Janaki temple rises from ancient palace ruins.','Stand among these broken brick arches and imagine a royal city. From 1097 this was Simraungadh, capital of the Karnat kings, founded by Nanyadeva, whose realm covered Tirhut or Mithila on both sides of today\'s border. The city sat inside earthen ramparts and ditches roughly seven and a half kilometres long, and the Tibetan monk Dharmasvamin passed through in the thirteenth century. In front of you is the white Ranivas temple, also called the Ram Janaki Mandir. Its story is tragic. In 1877 Prime Minister Jung Bahadur Rana died at Patharghat in Rautahat after a hunt near here. His queen Hiranya Garbha Devi, before committing sati, wished for a temple, and their son Jagat Jung Rana built this one in 1878. People believe it stands on the old palace of the Karnat kings. Look inside at the bronze images of Rama and Sita, then visit the Kankali temple and the great Jharokhar pond nearby.',NULL,'[\"Nanyadeva established the Karnat dynasty at Simraungadh in 1097 CE.\", \"The fortified city\'s main enclosure is about 7.5 km north-south and 4.5 km east-west.\", \"Jagat Jung Rana built the Ranivas Ram Janaki temple in 1878 at the wish of his mother Hiranya Garbha Devi.\", \"The Ranivas complex is said to cover 600 bighas.\", \"The nearby Jharokhar pond, about 800 years old, once covered 52 bighas.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Raniwas_Temple.jpg/1280px-Raniwas_Temple.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raniwas_Temple.jpg','Gaurav Dhwaj Khadka · CC BY-SA 4.0','shikhara,hindu,karnat (capital); rana (ranivas temple),simraungadh,madhesh','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simraungadh\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q21013701\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/659614567\", \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Simraungadh\"]','मिथिलाका कर्नाट राजाको मध्यकालीन राजधानी, जहाँ पुराना दरबारका भग्नावशेषमाथि राणाकालीन राम जानकी मन्दिर उभिएको छ।','यी भत्किएका इँटाका मेहराबबीच उभिएर शाही सहरको कल्पना गर्नुहोस्। सन् 1097 देखि यो सिमरौनगढ थियो, कर्नाट राजाहरूको राजधानी। यसको स्थापना नान्यदेवले गरेका थिए, र उनको राज्य आजको सीमाका दुवै छेउमा तिरहुत, अर्थात् मिथिलाभर फैलिएको थियो। सहर माटाका गह्रा र खाडलले घेरिएको थियो, जो करिब साढे सात किलोमिटर लामा थिए। तेह्रौँ शताब्दीमा तिब्बती भिक्षु धर्मस्वामी यहाँबाट गए। तपाईंको अगाडि सेतो रानीवास मन्दिर छ, जसलाई राम जानकी मन्दिर पनि भनिन्छ। यसको कथा दुःखद छ। सन् 1877 मा प्रधानमन्त्री जङ्गबहादुर राणा यहाँ नजिकै सिकार खेलेपछि रौतहटको पथरघाटमा बितेका थिए। उनकी रानी हिरण्य गर्भा देवीले सती जानुअघि एउटा मन्दिर चाहेकी थिइन्। उनका छोरा जगतजङ्ग राणाले सन् 1878 मा यो मन्दिर बनाए। मानिसहरूको विश्वास छ, यो कर्नाट राजाहरूको पुरानो दरबारमाथि उभिएको छ। भित्र राम र सीताका काँसाका मूर्ति हेर्नुहोस्, अनि नजिकैको कङ्काली मन्दिर र ठूलो झरोखर पोखरी पनि घुम्नुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"नान्यदेवले सन् 1097 मा सिमरौनगढमा कर्नाट वंश स्थापना गरे।\", \"किल्लाबन्दी गरिएको सहरको मुख्य घेरा उत्तर-दक्षिण करिब 7.5 किमी र पूर्व-पश्चिम 4.5 किमी छ।\", \"जगतजङ्ग राणाले आमा हिरण्य गर्भा देवीको इच्छा अनुसार सन् 1878 मा रानीवास राम जानकी मन्दिर बनाए।\", \"रानीवास परिसर 600 बिघामा फैलिएको भनिन्छ।\", \"नजिकैको झरोखर पोखरी, करिब 800 वर्ष पुरानो, पहिले 52 बिघामा फैलिएको थियो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Ram Navami\", \"note\": \"Thousands of worshippers from Nepal and India gather at Simraungadh\'s Kankali temple.\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"रामनवमी\", \"note_np\": \"नेपाल र भारतबाट हजारौँ भक्तजन सिमरौनगढको कङ्काली मन्दिरमा भेला हुन्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Ram_Janaki_Temple_at_Ranibas.jpg/1280px-Ram_Janaki_Temple_at_Ranibas.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gaurav Dhwaj Khadka\", \"caption\": \"Images of Rama, Sita and Lakshmana in the Ranivas temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram_Janaki_Temple_at_Ranibas.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Ranivas_Dwarpal.jpg/960px-Ranivas_Dwarpal.jpg\", \"author\": \"Scyfie\", \"caption\": \"A door-guardian statue at Ranivas\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ranivas_Dwarpal.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Jharokhar_Pokhari_Simroungarh.jpg/1280px-Jharokhar_Pokhari_Simroungarh.jpg\", \"author\": \"Scyfie\", \"caption\": \"Jharokhar Pokhari, the great medieval pond\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jharokhar_Pokhari_Simroungarh.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f5/12th_century_Stone_Inscription_from_Simroungarh_in_Tirhuta_script.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bharat Shah\", \"caption\": \"A 12th-century inscription in Tirhuta script from Simraungadh\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:12th_century_Stone_Inscription_from_Simroungarh_in_Tirhuta_script.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Pillar_at_Simroungarh.jpg/1280px-Pillar_at_Simroungarh.jpg\", \"author\": \"Scyfie\", \"caption\": \"An old stone pillar at Simraungadh\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pillar_at_Simroungarh.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"stone-spire\", \"notes\": \"White curved shikhara spire striped red and green with small corner spires, over an arcaded white colonnade on a stepped plinth; ruined brick palace arches around it. Height estimated.\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#F2F0EA\", \"#B03A2E\", \"#6FAF8A\"], \"features\": [\"trident\", \"arched-windows\", \"gilded-pinnacle\"], \"height_m\": 18, \"footprint_m\": [16, 16], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 3, \"surroundings\": [\"village\", \"plains-fields\", \"brick-courtyard\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(95,'patan-durbar-square','Patan Durbar Square','पाटन दरबार क्षेत्र','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur',NULL,27.673399,85.325056,'square','Both',NULL,NULL,'Ancient crossroads; most present buildings date from the 17th century under Siddhi Narasimha Malla and Srinivasa Malla','Malla','Newar brick-and-timber palace complex with pagoda and shikhara temples facing the royal palace',1,'The red-brick royal square of the Malla kings of Lalitpur, packed with temples, courtyards and carvings.','You are standing in the heart of old Lalitpur, the city the Newars call Yala. This brick-paved square grew from an ancient crossroads into the royal seat of the Malla kings, and most of what surrounds you was built in the 1600s under King Siddhi Narasimha Malla and his son Srinivasa. Look east and you will see the long palace, divided into courtyards such as Mul Chowk, Sundari Chowk and Keshav Narayan Chowk, today home to the Patan Museum. Facing it, a line of temples turns its doorways toward the palace, so the gods and the kings looked at each other across the square. Hindu and Buddhist traditions share this space easily; Patan is said to hold 136 bahals and 55 major temples. In April 2015 a powerful earthquake brought down temples here, including Char Narayan and Hari Shankar, and much has since been rebuilt with salvaged original parts. Take your time, look up at the carved roof struts, and listen for the great bell.',NULL,'[\"Patan Durbar Square is one of seven Monument Zones of the Kathmandu Valley UNESCO World Heritage Site, inscribed in 1979.\", \"Most of the present architecture dates from the 17th century, under Siddhi Narasimha Malla and Srinivasa Malla.\", \"The main temples stand opposite the western face of the palace, with their entrances facing east toward it.\", \"The square was heavily damaged in the April 2015 earthquake and reopened to visitors in June 2015.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,250,0,120,'The April 2015 earthquake heavily damaged the square; Char Narayan and Hari Shankar temples collapsed and were later rebuilt using salvaged original elements.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Patan_Durbar_Square-2644.jpg/1280px-Patan_Durbar_Square-2644.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan_Durbar_Square-2644.jpg','Bijay Chaurasia · CC BY-SA 4.0','square,both,malla,lalitpur,hindu,buddhist,unesco,palace,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/121/\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2230569085\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/miscellaneous/2015/06/11/patan-durbar-square-opens-to-public-from-today\", \"https://wmf.org/node/17515\", \"https://www.thirdrockadventures.com/blog/heritage-sites-in-nepal-and-entrance-fees-to-visit\"]','ललितपुरका मल्ल राजाहरूको रातो इँटाको शाही चोक, जहाँ मन्दिर, आँगन र कुँदिएका कलाकृति भरिएका छन्।','तपाईं पुरानो ललितपुरको मुटुमा उभिनुभएको छ, जसलाई नेवारहरू यल भन्छन्। इँटा छापिएको यो चोक पुरानो चौबाटोबाट बढ्दै मल्ल राजाहरूको दरबार बन्यो। वरिपरि देखिने धेरैजसो कुरा राजा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्ल र उनका छोरा श्रीनिवासको पालामा १६०० को दशकमा बनेका हुन्। पूर्वतिर हेर्नुहोस्, लामो दरबार देखिन्छ। त्यसमा मूल चोक, सुन्दरी चोक र केशव नारायण चोक जस्ता आँगन छन्, र आज त्यहाँ पाटन संग्रहालय छ। त्यसको सामुन्ने मन्दिरहरूको लाम छ, जसका ढोका दरबारतिर फर्केका छन्। त्यसैले देवता र राजाले चोकको आरपार एकअर्कालाई हेर्थे। हिन्दू र बौद्ध परम्परा यहाँ सँगसँगै सजिलै बाँचेका छन्; पाटनमा १३६ बहाल र ५५ वटा मुख्य मन्दिर छन् भनिन्छ। अप्रिल २०१५ को ठूलो भूकम्पले चार नारायण र हरि शङ्कर लगायत धेरै मन्दिर ढाल्यो। अहिले धेरै मन्दिर बचेका पुराना भाग प्रयोग गरेर फेरि बनाइएका छन्। आफ्नै गतिमा घुम्नुहोस्, कुँदिएका छानाका टेकोहरू माथि हेर्नुहोस्, र ठूलो घण्टाको आवाज सुन्नुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"पाटन दरबार क्षेत्र काठमाडौं उपत्यकाको युनेस्को विश्व सम्पदा स्थलका सात सम्पदा क्षेत्रमध्ये एक हो, जुन सन् १९७९ मा सूचीमा परेको हो।\", \"अहिलेका धेरैजसो भवन १७ औं शताब्दीमा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्ल र श्रीनिवास मल्लको पालामा बनेका हुन्।\", \"मुख्य मन्दिरहरू दरबारको पश्चिमी भागको सामुन्ने छन्, र तिनका ढोका पूर्वतिर, दरबारतिर फर्केका छन्।\", \"अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पले चोकमा ठूलो क्षति पुर्‍यायो, र जुन २०१५ मा यो फेरि पर्यटकका लागि खुल्यो।\"]','अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पले चोकमा ठूलो क्षति पुर्‍यायो। चार नारायण र हरि शङ्कर मन्दिर ढले, र पछि बचेका पुराना भाग प्रयोग गरेर फेरि बनाइए।','[{\"name\": \"Krishna Janmashtami\", \"note\": \"Krishna\'s birthday; devotees queue and sing hymns through the night at Krishna Mandir\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"कृष्ण जन्माष्टमी\", \"note_np\": \"कृष्णको जन्मदिन; भक्तजन कृष्ण मन्दिरमा लाइन लाग्छन् र रातभरि भजन गाउँछन्\"}, {\"name\": \"Rato Machhindranath Jatra\", \"note\": \"The god\'s tall chariot is pulled through Patan over several weeks\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"रातो मच्छिन्द्रनाथ जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"देवताको अग्लो रथ धेरै हप्तासम्म पाटनका गल्लीमा तानिन्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Main Durga festival; Taleju shrines and Durga temples draw worship and offerings\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दुर्गाको मुख्य चाड; तलेजुका मन्दिर र दुर्गा मन्दिरमा पूजा र चढावा चढाइन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Patan-Palastplatz-02-von_oben-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Palastplatz-02-von_oben-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Patan Durbar Square seen from above, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Palastplatz-02-von_oben-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Patan-Palastplatz-08-Harishankar-zwei_Tempel-Narayana-Krishna-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Palastplatz-08-Harishankar-zwei_Tempel-Narayana-Krishna-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Hari Shankar and neighbouring temples on the square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Palastplatz-08-Harishankar-zwei_Tempel-Narayana-Krishna-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Patan-Palastplatz-34-Krishna-Vishwanath-Bhimsen-Palast-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Palastplatz-34-Krishna-Vishwanath-Bhimsen-Palast-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Krishna Mandir, Vishwanath and Bhimsen temples beside the palace\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Palastplatz-34-Krishna-Vishwanath-Bhimsen-Palast-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Patan-Palastplatz-24-Degutale-Talejuglocke-Cyasilim-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Palastplatz-24-Degutale-Talejuglocke-Cyasilim-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Degutale temple, Taleju Bell and Chyasin Dega on the square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Palastplatz-24-Degutale-Talejuglocke-Cyasilim-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Patan-Palastplatz-10-Yoganarendramallasaeule-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Palastplatz-10-Yoganarendramallasaeule-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Pillar of King Yoganarendra Malla facing the palace\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Palastplatz-10-Yoganarendramallasaeule-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"square\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Long brick palace on the east side; a row of pagodas and the stone Krishna Mandir face it, with a king on a tall pillar\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#5a3a28\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"carved-struts\", \"carved-windows\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"garuda-pillar\", \"stone-pillar\", \"bell\", \"lion-statues\", \"water-spouts\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [160, 70], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\", \"market-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(96,'krishna-mandir','Krishna Mandir','कृष्ण मन्दिर','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur','patan-durbar-square',27.673623,85.324964,'shikhara','Hindu','Krishna',1637,'17th century (1637, King Siddhi Narasimha Malla)','Malla','Three-storey stone shikhara in the Granthakuta style with 21 golden pinnacles',1,'A 17th-century stone shikhara with 21 golden pinnacles and carved scenes from the Mahabharata and Ramayana.','In front of you rises a temple made almost entirely of stone, unusual in a valley of brick and timber pagodas. This is Krishna Mandir, built in 1637 by King Siddhi Narasimha Malla in a local shikhara style called Granthakuta. Count the pinnacles if you can: there are 21, all gilded. The temple has three storeys. On the first floor sits the main shrine of Krishna, with Radha and Rukmini on either side. The second floor is dedicated to Shiva and the third to Lokeshwor, the compassionate Avalokiteshvara, a quiet sign of how Hindu and Buddhist worship meet in Patan. Now step closer to the beams above the pillars. The first-floor carvings tell stories from the Mahabharata, and the second-floor carvings illustrate the Ramayana. On Krishnashtami, Krishna\'s birthday, thousands of devotees crowd this square. The temple was damaged in the 2015 earthquake and restored in 2018. Look across to the column topped by Garuda, kneeling toward his lord.','It is said that one night King Siddhi Narasimha Malla saw Lord Krishna and his consort Radha standing in front of the royal palace. Moved by the vision, he ordered a temple to be built on the very spot where they had appeared, and Krishna Mandir rose there, facing the palace across the square. Even today, the main entrance of the temple looks toward the royal palace, as if Krishna were still keeping watch over the king.','[\"Built in 1637 by King Siddhi Narasimha Malla (some sources give 1667, but the king had abdicated by 1661).\", \"It has 21 golden pinnacles above three storeys.\", \"First-floor beam carvings show the Mahabharata; second-floor carvings show the Ramayana.\", \"The upper floors are dedicated to Shiva and to Lokeshwor (Avalokiteshvara).\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,250,0,20,'Damaged in the April 2015 earthquake and restored in 2018.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Patan-Krishna_Mandir-08-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Krishna_Mandir-08-2013-gje.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Krishna_Mandir-08-2013-gje.jpg','Gerd Eichmann · CC BY-SA 4.0','shikhara,hindu,malla,lalitpur,unesco,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krishna_Mandir,_Patan\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/120443307\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/krishna-mandir-a-marble-of-stone-carving\"]','१७ औं शताब्दीको ढुङ्गाको शिखर मन्दिर, जसमा २१ वटा सुनौला गजुर छन् र महाभारत र रामायणका दृश्य कुँदिएका छन्।','तपाईंको अगाडि लगभग पूरै ढुङ्गाले बनेको मन्दिर उभिएको छ। इँटा र काठका पगोडा भएको यो उपत्यकामा यस्तो मन्दिर विरलै पाइन्छ। यो कृष्ण मन्दिर हो, जसलाई सन् १६३७ मा राजा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्लले ग्रन्थकूट भनिने स्थानीय शिखर शैलीमा बनाएका थिए। सक्नुहुन्छ भने गजुर गन्नुहोस्: जम्मा २१ वटा छन्, सबै सुनौला। मन्दिर तीन तलाको छ। पहिलो तलामा कृष्णको मुख्य मन्दिर छ, दुवैतिर राधा र रुक्मिणी छन्। दोस्रो तला शिवलाई र तेस्रो तला करुणामय अवलोकितेश्वर अर्थात् लोकेश्वरलाई समर्पित छ। यसले पाटनमा हिन्दू र बौद्ध पूजा कसरी मिल्छ भन्ने चुपचाप देखाउँछ। अब खम्बामाथिका धरन नजिकबाट हेर्नुहोस्। पहिलो तलाका कुँदाइमा महाभारतका कथा छन्, र दोस्रो तलाका कुँदाइमा रामायणका दृश्य छन्। कृष्णको जन्मदिन कृष्णाष्टमीमा हजारौँ भक्तजन यो चोकमा भेला हुन्छन्। २०१५ को भूकम्पले मन्दिरमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो, र सन् २०१८ मा यसलाई मर्मत गरियो। अब सामुन्नेको गरुड चढेको खम्बातिर हेर्नुहोस्, जसले आफ्ना स्वामीतिर घुँडा टेकेर बसेको छ।','भनिन्छ, एक रात राजा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्लले भगवान् कृष्ण र उनकी सँगिनी राधालाई शाही दरबारको अगाडि उभिएको देखे। त्यो दर्शनले राजा भावुक भए र ती जहाँ देखिएका थिए, ठीक त्यही ठाउँमा मन्दिर बनाउन आदेश दिए। त्यसरी कृष्ण मन्दिर चोकको पारि दरबारतिर फर्केर उठ्यो। आज पनि मन्दिरको मुख्य ढोका शाही दरबारतिरै फर्केको छ, मानौँ कृष्ण अझै राजाको रक्षा गरिरहेका छन्।','[\"सन् १६३७ मा राजा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्लले बनाएका हुन् (केही स्रोतले १६६७ भन्छन्, तर राजाले १६६१ सम्ममा गद्दी छाडिसकेका थिए)।\", \"तीन तलामाथि २१ वटा सुनौला गजुर छन्।\", \"पहिलो तलाका धरनका कुँदाइमा महाभारत छ; दोस्रो तलाका कुँदाइमा रामायण छ।\", \"माथिल्ला तला शिव र लोकेश्वर (अवलोकितेश्वर) लाई समर्पित छन्।\"]','अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पमा क्षति भएको थियो, र सन् २०१८ मा मर्मत गरियो।','[{\"name\": \"Krishna Janmashtami\", \"note\": \"Krishna\'s birthday; devotees queue and sing hymns through the night at Krishna Mandir\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"कृष्ण जन्माष्टमी\", \"note_np\": \"कृष्णको जन्मदिन; भक्तजन लाइन लागेर कृष्ण मन्दिरमा रातभर भजन गाउँछन्\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Patan-KrishnaMandir-GoldenPinnacle.jpg/1280px-Patan-KrishnaMandir-GoldenPinnacle.jpg\", \"author\": \"sailesh.baidya (Sailesh Raj Baidya)\", \"caption\": \"Gilded pinnacles atop Krishna Mandir\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-KrishnaMandir-GoldenPinnacle.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Patan-Krishna_Mandir-14-Szene_aus_dem_Ramayana-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Krishna_Mandir-14-Szene_aus_dem_Ramayana-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Stone frieze with a scene from the Ramayana\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Krishna_Mandir-14-Szene_aus_dem_Ramayana-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Krisnna_Temple_and_Garuda_at_Patan.jpg/1280px-Krisnna_Temple_and_Garuda_at_Patan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Krishna Mandir with the Garuda statue on its pillar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krisnna_Temple_and_Garuda_at_Patan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Steps_to_Krishna_Mandir.jpg/1280px-Steps_to_Krishna_Mandir.jpg\", \"author\": \"Kumud.parajuli\", \"caption\": \"Stone steps leading up to Krishna Mandir\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steps_to_Krishna_Mandir.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6b/Krishna_mandir_at_Night_%283917510265%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prashant Shrestha from Kathmandu, Nepal\", \"caption\": \"Krishna Mandir lit up at night\", \"license\": \"CC BY 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krishna_mandir_at_Night_(3917510265).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"stone-spire\", \"notes\": \"Grey stone tower ringed by open pillared pavilions with 21 small spires; Garuda kneels on a pillar in front\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#a8957a\", \"#c9a227\", \"#6b5a45\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"garuda-pillar\", \"stone-pillar\", \"lion-statues\", \"guardian-pairs-on-stairs\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 3, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(97,'patan-museum','Patan Museum (Keshav Narayan Chowk)','पाटन संग्रहालय','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur','patan-durbar-square',27.673444,85.325335,'museum','Both',NULL,1734,'Palace courtyard in its present form from 1734 (Malla period); museum opened in 1997','Malla','Restored Malla palace quadrangle (Keshav Narayan Chowk) with a gilded doorway, adapted as a museum',1,'A Malla royal courtyard turned into a museum of Hindu and Buddhist sacred art.','Walk through the golden doorway and you enter Keshav Narayan Chowk, the northern courtyard of the old Malla palace. The palace was built on the site of a Buddhist monastery, renovated many times, and its present appearance dates from 1734. After the 1934 earthquake destroyed the east wing it was rebuilt, and for a while the building even housed a public school. Restoration began in 1982, led by the Austrian architect Götz Hagmüller, and in 1997 King Birendra opened the Patan Museum here. The collection, curated by the scholar Mary Shepherd Slusser, explains the sacred art and iconography of Hinduism and Buddhism. Most objects are cast bronzes and gilt copper repoussé, crafts for which Patan\'s metalworkers are famous. As you move between galleries, notice how the old timber windows frame the courtyard. In 2017 the restored Sundari Chowk, with the royal Tusha Hiti bath, was added to the museum. When you need a pause, the museum café is a pleasant spot.',NULL,'[\"The museum was inaugurated in 1997 by King Birendra Bir Bikram Shah.\", \"It occupies Keshav Narayan Chowk, a courtyard of the Malla royal palace whose present appearance dates from 1734.\", \"The restoration, begun in 1982, was led by Austrian architect Götz Hagmüller; the collection was curated by Mary Shepherd Slusser.\", \"Most exhibits are cast bronzes and gilt copper repoussé work, crafts Patan is famous for.\"]','10:30','17:30',1000,250,NULL,90,'Keshav Narayan Chowk was listed among the palace structures with minor damage after the April 2015 earthquake.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Keshav_Narayan_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Keshav_Narayan_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keshav_Narayan_Chowk,_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg','Shadow Ayush · CC BY-SA 4.0','museum,both,malla,lalitpur,hindu,buddhist,unesco,palace,courtyard,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Museum\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\", \"https://patanmuseum.gov.np/\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1904110313\", \"https://thehimalayantimes.com/ampArticle/111543\"]','मल्ल राजाको दरबारको आँगन, जुन अहिले हिन्दू र बौद्ध पवित्र कलाको संग्रहालय बनेको छ।','सुनौलो ढोकाबाट भित्र पस्नुहोस्, तपाईं पुरानो मल्ल दरबारको उत्तरी आँगन केशव नारायण चोकमा पुग्नुहुन्छ। दरबार बौद्ध विहार भएको ठाउँमा बनेको थियो, धेरै पटक मर्मत भयो, र अहिलेको रूप सन् १७३४ को हो। १९३४ को भूकम्पले पूर्वी भाग ढालेपछि त्यसलाई फेरि बनाइयो, र केही समय त्यहाँ सार्वजनिक विद्यालय पनि चलेको थियो। सन् १९८२ मा अस्ट्रियाली वास्तुकार गोट्ज ह्यागमुलरको नेतृत्वमा मर्मत सुरु भयो, र १९९७ मा राजा वीरेन्द्रले यहाँ पाटन संग्रहालय उद्घाटन गरे। विद्वान मेरी शेफर्ड स्लसरले सजाएको यो सङ्ग्रहले हिन्दू र बौद्ध धर्मका पवित्र कला र मूर्तिकलाको अर्थ बुझाउँछ। धेरैजसो वस्तु ढलौटका काँसा र सुनको पानी चढाएका तामाका ठोकेर बनाइएका कलाकृति हुन्, जुन शिल्पका लागि पाटनका धातुकर्मी प्रसिद्ध छन्। कोठा-कोठा घुम्दा पुराना काठका झ्यालले आँगनलाई कसरी फ्रेम बनाएका छन्, हेर्नुहोस्। सन् २०१७ मा तुषा हिटी भएको शाही नुहाउने ठाउँसहित मर्मत गरिएको सुन्दरी चोक संग्रहालयमा थपियो। थकाइ लागे संग्रहालयको क्याफे बसेर आराम गर्न राम्रो ठाउँ हो।',NULL,'[\"संग्रहालय सन् १९९७ मा राजा वीरेन्द्र वीर विक्रम शाहले उद्घाटन गरेका हुन्।\", \"यो मल्ल राजदरबारको केशव नारायण चोकमा छ, जसको अहिलेको रूप सन् १७३४ को हो।\", \"सन् १९८२ मा सुरु भएको मर्मत अस्ट्रियाली वास्तुकार गोट्ज ह्यागमुलरको नेतृत्वमा भयो; सङ्ग्रह मेरी शेफर्ड स्लसरले सजाएकी हुन्।\", \"धेरैजसो प्रदर्शित वस्तु ढलौटका काँसा र सुनको पानी चढाएका तामाका ठोकेर बनाइएका कलाकृति हुन्, जुन शिल्पका लागि पाटन प्रसिद्ध छ।\"]','अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पपछि केशव नारायण चोक सामान्य क्षति भएका दरबारका संरचनाहरूमा गनिएको थियो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Patan_Museum%2C_The_Museum_behind_the_Golden_Door_1.jpg/1280px-Patan_Museum%2C_The_Museum_behind_the_Golden_Door_1.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Golden door at the entrance of the Patan Museum\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan_Museum,_The_Museum_behind_the_Golden_Door_1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/2023_-_Patan_Museum_-_Keshav_Narayan_Chowk_%26_Bidya_Mandira_-_img_0.jpg/1280px-2023_-_Patan_Museum_-_Keshav_Narayan_Chowk_%26_Bidya_Mandira_-_img_0.jpg\", \"author\": \"Chainwit.\", \"caption\": \"Keshav Narayan Chowk courtyard, 2023\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2023_-_Patan_Museum_-_Keshav_Narayan_Chowk_%26_Bidya_Mandira_-_img_0.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Wooden_Window_inside_Patan_Museum-IMG_3651.jpg/1280px-Wooden_Window_inside_Patan_Museum-IMG_3651.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijay chaurasia\", \"caption\": \"Carved wooden window inside the museum\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wooden_Window_inside_Patan_Museum-IMG_3651.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Mangal_Hiti_viewed_from_Patan_Museum.jpg/1280px-Mangal_Hiti_viewed_from_Patan_Museum.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bidhan Rajkarnikar\", \"caption\": \"Mangal Hiti seen from the Patan Museum\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mangal_Hiti_viewed_from_Patan_Museum.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"palace\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Brick palace wing on the square with a gilded copper door and gilded window above it; square inner courtyard\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"golden-door\", \"carved-windows\", \"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [40, 40], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(98,'bhimsen-temple','Bhimsen Temple','भीमसेन मन्दिर','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur','patan-durbar-square',27.673873,85.325182,'pagoda','Hindu','Bhimsen',1680,'17th century (1680, King Srinivasa Malla)','Malla','Newar pagoda known for three interconnected golden windows on its upper facade',1,'A Malla-era pagoda to Bhimsen, the Pandava hero worshipped by Newar traders as a god of business.','At the northern end of the square stands the temple of Bhimsen, built by King Srinivasa Malla in 1680. Bhimsen is Bhima, the second of the five Pandava brothers in the Mahabharata, famous for his strength and courage. Here in Patan, though, he has another role: Newar merchants and traders worship him as a god of business and trade, so you may see shopkeepers stopping to pray. Look up at the facade and find its pride, three interconnected golden windows gleaming above the square. The temple is a working shrine, so visitors are not allowed inside and photography inside is not permitted; enjoy it from the square instead. Notice how it sits in line with Vishwanath Temple and Krishna Mandir, all facing the palace across the bricks. The 2015 earthquake left the temple partially damaged, and it has been repaired since. Before you move on, stand back far enough to see the whole building and imagine the merchants who have prayed here for over three centuries.',NULL,'[\"Built by King Srinivasa Malla in 1680.\", \"Renowned for its three interconnected golden windows.\", \"Newars worship Bhimsen, the Pandava hero, as a god of business and trade.\", \"Tourists are not allowed inside, and photography inside is not permitted.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,250,0,15,'Partially damaged in the April 2015 earthquake and later repaired.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Patan_Bhimsen_Temple_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Patan_Bhimsen_Temple_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan_Bhimsen_Temple_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg','Rajesh Dhungana · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,lalitpur,unesco,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/326472980\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/miscellaneous/2015/06/11/patan-durbar-square-opens-to-public-from-today\"]','भीमसेनको मल्लकालीन पगोडा; पाण्डव वीर भीमसेनलाई नेवार व्यापारीले व्यापारका देवता मानेर पूजा गर्छन्।','चोकको उत्तरी छेउमा राजा श्रीनिवास मल्लले सन् १६८० मा बनाएको भीमसेनको मन्दिर छ। भीमसेन महाभारतका पाँच पाण्डव दाजुभाइमध्ये दोस्रा भीम हुन्, जो आफ्नो बल र साहसका लागि चर्चित छन्। तर पाटनमा उनको अर्कै भूमिका छ। नेवार व्यापारीहरू उनलाई व्यवसाय र व्यापारका देवता मानेर पूजा गर्छन्, त्यसैले पसलेहरू रोकिएर प्रार्थना गरिरहेका तपाईंले देख्न सक्नुहुन्छ। अगाडिको भाग हेर्नुहोस् र यसको शान आँखा लाग्ने गरी जोडिएका तीनवटा सुनौला झ्याल खोज्नुहोस्, जो चोकमाथि चम्किरहेका छन्। यो पूजा भइरहेको मन्दिर भएकाले भित्र जान दिइँदैन र भित्र फोटो खिच्न पनि पाइँदैन; चोकबाटै हेरेर मज्जा लिनुहोस्। यो विश्वनाथ मन्दिर र कृष्ण मन्दिरसँग एउटै लाइनमा छ, र सबै इँटा छापिएको चोकको पारि दरबारतिर फर्केका छन्। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले मन्दिरमा आंशिक क्षति पुर्‍यायो, र त्यसपछि मर्मत गरियो। अघि बढ्नुअघि अलि पर उभिएर पूरै भवन हेर्नुहोस्, र तीन सय वर्षभन्दा बढी यहाँ प्रार्थना गर्ने व्यापारीहरूको कल्पना गर्नुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"राजा श्रीनिवास मल्लले सन् १६८० मा बनाएका हुन्।\", \"जोडिएका तीनवटा सुनौला झ्यालका लागि प्रसिद्ध छ।\", \"नेवारहरू पाण्डव वीर भीमसेनलाई व्यवसाय र व्यापारका देवता मानेर पूजा गर्छन्।\", \"पर्यटकलाई भित्र जान दिइँदैन, र भित्र फोटो खिच्न पनि पाइँदैन।\"]','अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पमा आंशिक क्षति भएको थियो, र पछि मर्मत गरियो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Bhimsen_Temple%2C_with_Vishwanath_Temple_in_back_%288094976148%29.jpg/1280px-Bhimsen_Temple%2C_with_Vishwanath_Temple_in_back_%288094976148%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa\", \"caption\": \"Bhimsen Temple with Vishwanath Temple behind\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimsen_Temple,_with_Vishwanath_Temple_in_back_(8094976148).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Bhimsen_temple_and_water_taps_at_Patan_Durbar_Square_1.jpg/1280px-Bhimsen_temple_and_water_taps_at_Patan_Durbar_Square_1.jpg\", \"author\": \"Manoguru\", \"caption\": \"Bhimsen Temple and the stone water taps nearby\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimsen_temple_and_water_taps_at_Patan_Durbar_Square_1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Bhimsen_Temple_%E2%80%93_Patan_-_01.jpg/1280px-Bhimsen_Temple_%E2%80%93_Patan_-_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Maesi64\", \"caption\": \"Bhimsen Temple, Patan Durbar Square\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimsen_Temple_%E2%80%93_Patan_-_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Bhimsen_temple_patan_GP_%282%29.JPG/1280px-Bhimsen_temple_patan_GP_%282%29.JPG\", \"author\": \"Ganesh Paudel\", \"caption\": \"Bhimsen Temple, upper facade\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhimsen_temple_patan_GP_(2).JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Patan-Bhimsen-10-Baustelle-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Bhimsen-10-Baustelle-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Bhimsen Temple under reconstruction\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Bhimsen-10-Baustelle-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Rectangular brick pagoda whose first floor carries a projecting balcony of three joined gilded windows\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"carved-windows\", \"lion-statues\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [10, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(99,'vishwanath-temple','Vishwanath Temple','विश्वनाथ मन्दिर','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur','patan-durbar-square',27.673700,85.325177,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva',1627,'17th century (1627, reign of Siddhi Narasimha Malla)','Malla','Newar pagoda with carved roof struts, guarded by two stone elephants',1,'A Shiva pagoda guarded by stone elephants, with Nandi the bull waiting on the other side.','Between Krishna Mandir and Bhimsen Temple stands Vishwanath, a temple to Lord Shiva built in 1627 during the reign of Siddhi Narasimha Malla. Start at the front steps, where two stone elephants stand guard at the entrance. Then walk around to the other side: there sits a sculpture of Nandi the bull, Shiva\'s faithful vehicle. Inside, out of sight, a stone linga is enshrined, the abstract form in which Shiva is worshipped. Now tilt your head back and study the carved wooden roof struts. Among the many figures you may spot erotic scenes, imagery widespread on Shiva temples in India and common in the Kathmandu Valley, often read as symbols of creation and fertility. The temple was partially damaged in the April 2015 earthquake and has since been repaired. It is one of the oldest temples on this row, built a decade before Krishna Mandir, so you are looking at nearly four centuries of devotion. Pause here, and watch how locals touch the steps as they pass.',NULL,'[\"Built in 1627 during the reign of Siddhi Narasimha Malla.\", \"Two stone elephants guard the front entrance.\", \"A sculpture of Nandi, Shiva\'s bull, sits on the opposite side.\", \"It stands between Krishna Mandir and Bhimsen Temple, with a stone linga inside.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,250,0,15,'Partially damaged in the April 2015 earthquake and later repaired.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Bishwanath_Temple%2C_Patan.jpg/1280px-Bishwanath_Temple%2C_Patan.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bishwanath_Temple,_Patan.jpg','Safalphotos · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,lalitpur,unesco,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/328903213\", \"https://kathmandupost.com/miscellaneous/2015/06/11/patan-durbar-square-opens-to-public-from-today\"]','ढुङ्गाका हात्तीले रक्षा गरेको शिवको पगोडा; अर्कोतिर नन्दी गोरु पर्खेर बसेको छ।','कृष्ण मन्दिर र भीमसेन मन्दिरको बीचमा विश्वनाथ छ। यो भगवान् शिवको मन्दिर राजा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्लको पालामा सन् १६२७ मा बनेको हो। अगाडिको भर्‍याङबाट सुरु गर्नुहोस्, जहाँ ढोकामा दुईवटा ढुङ्गाका हात्ती पहरा दिइरहेका छन्। अनि अर्कोतिर घुम्नुहोस्: त्यहाँ शिवको भरोसिलो सवारी नन्दी गोरुको मूर्ति बसेको छ। भित्र, नदेखिने गरी, ढुङ्गाको लिङ्ग स्थापना गरिएको छ। शिवलाई पूजा गर्ने निराकार रूप यही हो। अब टाउको पछाडि फर्काएर कुँदिएका काठका छानाका टेकोहरू हेर्नुहोस्। धेरै आकृतिका बीचमा तपाईंले कामुक दृश्य पनि देख्न सक्नुहुन्छ। भारतका शिव मन्दिरमा यस्ता चित्र धेरै हुन्छन् र काठमाडौं उपत्यकामा पनि सामान्य छन्, र यिनलाई प्रायः सृष्टि र उर्वरताको प्रतीक मानिन्छ। अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पले मन्दिरमा आंशिक क्षति पुर्‍यायो, र त्यसपछि मर्मत गरियो। यो लाइनका सबैभन्दा पुराना मन्दिरमध्ये एक हो, कृष्ण मन्दिरभन्दा दश वर्ष अघि बनेको। त्यसैले तपाईं लगभग चार सय वर्षको भक्ति हेर्दै हुनुहुन्छ। यहाँ केही बेर रोकिनुहोस्, र स्थानीयहरू हिँड्दा भर्‍याङ छोएर जाने तरिका हेर्नुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्लको पालामा सन् १६२७ मा बनेको।\", \"अगाडिको ढोकाको रक्षा दुईवटा ढुङ्गाका हात्तीले गर्छन्।\", \"शिवको गोरु नन्दीको मूर्ति अर्कोतिर छ।\", \"यो कृष्ण मन्दिर र भीमसेन मन्दिरको बीचमा छ, र भित्र ढुङ्गाको लिङ्ग छ।\"]','अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पमा आंशिक क्षति भएको थियो, र पछि मर्मत गरियो।','[{\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Night of Shiva; devotees offer worship at Shiva shrines\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"शिवको रात; भक्तजन शिव मन्दिरमा पूजा गर्छन्\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Vishwanath_Temple_Elephants_and_Durbar_Square_%288094975626%29.jpg/1280px-Vishwanath_Temple_Elephants_and_Durbar_Square_%288094975626%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa\", \"caption\": \"Stone elephants guarding Vishwanath Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vishwanath_Temple_Elephants_and_Durbar_Square_(8094975626).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Patan-Vishwanath-10-Erdgeschoss-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Vishwanath-10-Erdgeschoss-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Ground floor of Vishwanath Temple, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Vishwanath-10-Erdgeschoss-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Patan-Vishwanath-11-Erdgeschoss-Relief-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Vishwanath-11-Erdgeschoss-Relief-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Carved relief on the ground floor\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Vishwanath-11-Erdgeschoss-Relief-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Patan-Vishwanath-22-Elefanten-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Vishwanath-22-Elefanten-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Stone elephants after the 2015 earthquake\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Vishwanath-22-Elefanten-Erdbebenschaden-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Vishwanath_Temple%2C_patan_durbar.jpg/1280px-Vishwanath_Temple%2C_patan_durbar.jpg\", \"author\": \"Deeplove thapa1\", \"caption\": \"Vishwanath Temple on Patan Durbar Square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vishwanath_Temple,_patan_durbar.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Two-roofed Shiva pagoda with a pillared ground-floor arcade; stone elephants flank the front stairs, a stone Nandi behind\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"elephant-statues\", \"nandi-bull\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [10, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 2, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(100,'taleju-bell','Taleju Bell','तलेजु घण्ट','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur','patan-durbar-square',27.673038,85.324907,'statue','Hindu','Taleju',1736,'18th century (1736, King Vishnu Malla)','Malla','Large cast bronze bell hung in a frame on a raised plinth',1,'The great bronze bell of the Malla kings, named for the royal goddess Taleju.','Near the palace front hangs a great bronze bell. This is the Taleju Bell, named for Taleju Bhawani, the royal goddess of the Malla kings. Travel guides record that King Vishnu Malla and his queen set it up in 1736, after an earlier bell installed in 1703 had been moved to the Rato Machhindranath Temple. Royal bells like this one sounded during worship of the goddess and served as a public signal, a way to call people to the palace. Look at the frame that holds it and the plinth beneath, and notice how the bell lines up beside the main temples of the square. Imagine its deep voice rolling across the rooftops of Yala in Malla times, when news and royal summons travelled by sound rather than screens. Few objects in the square connect you so directly to daily palace life. Admire it closely and take in the craftsmanship of the casting. From here, the entrances to Mul Chowk and the Taleju temples are only a few steps away.',NULL,'[\"Named after Taleju Bhawani, the personal deity of the Malla kings.\", \"Travel sources date it to 1736 and credit King Vishnu Malla.\", \"An earlier bell installed in 1703 was reportedly moved to the Rato Machhindranath Temple.\", \"It stands in alignment beside the main temples facing the palace.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,250,0,10,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Taleju_Bell_at_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Taleju_Bell_at_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taleju_Bell_at_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg','Harsh Mahaseth · CC BY-SA 4.0','statue,hindu,malla,lalitpur,unesco,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/199775523\", \"https://backpackandsnorkel.com/Nepal/Day3/5329k-TalejuBell/\", \"https://www.nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/friday-facts-patan-durbar-square\"]','मल्ल राजाहरूको विशाल काँसाको घण्ट, शाही देवी तलेजुको नामबाट नाम राखिएको।','दरबारको अगाडि नजिकै एउटा विशाल काँसाको घण्ट झुण्डिएको छ। यो तलेजु घण्ट हो, जसको नाम मल्ल राजाहरूकी शाही देवी तलेजु भवानीको नामबाट राखिएको हो। यात्रा गाइडहरूका अनुसार सन् १७३६ मा राजा विष्णु मल्ल र उनकी रानीले यो घण्ट राखेका थिए। त्यसअघि सन् १७०३ मा राखिएको घण्ट रातो मच्छिन्द्रनाथ मन्दिरमा सारिएको थियो। यस्ता शाही घण्ट देवीको पूजामा बजाइन्थे, र मानिसलाई दरबारमा बोलाउने सार्वजनिक सङ्केतको काम पनि गर्थे। घण्ट अडिएको फ्रेम र मुनिको चौतारी हेर्नुहोस्, र चोकका मुख्य मन्दिरहरूको छेउमा घण्ट कसरी मिलेर बसेको छ, त्यो पनि हेर्नुहोस्। मल्लकालमा समाचार र शाही बोलावट स्क्रिनबाट होइन, आवाजबाट पुग्थ्यो। त्यतिबेला यसको गहिरो आवाज यलका छानाहरूमाथि गुञ्जिएको कल्पना गर्नुहोस्। चोकका थोरै वस्तुले मात्र तपाईंलाई दरबारको दैनिक जीवनसँग यति सीधै जोड्छन्। नजिकबाट हेर्नुहोस् र ढलौटको कारिगरी मन पराउनुहोस्। यहाँबाट मूल चोक र तलेजु मन्दिरका ढोका केही पाइलामै छन्।',NULL,'[\"मल्ल राजाहरूकी आफ्नै देवी तलेजु भवानीको नामबाट नाम राखिएको।\", \"यात्रा स्रोतहरूले यसलाई सन् १७३६ को मान्छन् र राजा विष्णु मल्लको श्रेय दिन्छन्।\", \"सन् १७०३ मा राखिएको अघिल्लो घण्ट रातो मच्छिन्द्रनाथ मन्दिरमा सारिएको बताइन्छ।\", \"यो दरबारतिर फर्केका मुख्य मन्दिरहरूको छेउमा एउटै लाइनमा मिलेर बसेको छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Big_Bell_Nepal.JPG/1280px-Big_Bell_Nepal.JPG\", \"author\": \"Kuber Sodari\", \"caption\": \"The big Taleju Bell in its frame\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Big_Bell_Nepal.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Bell_of_Patan.jpg/1280px-Bell_of_Patan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rupson singh1\", \"caption\": \"Taleju Bell, Patan Durbar Square\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bell_of_Patan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Big_Bell%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Big_Bell%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Taleju Bell on its raised stone plinth\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Big_Bell,_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Patan_darbar_front_bell_on_sunset.jpg/1280px-Patan_darbar_front_bell_on_sunset.jpg\", \"author\": \"Pkatuwal\", \"caption\": \"Taleju Bell at sunset\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan_darbar_front_bell_on_sunset.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Patan-Palastplatz-24-Degutale-Talejuglocke-Cyasilim-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Palastplatz-24-Degutale-Talejuglocke-Cyasilim-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Taleju Bell between Degutale and Chyasin Dega\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Palastplatz-24-Degutale-Talejuglocke-Cyasilim-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"statue\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Big bronze bell under a small tiled roof with three gilded finials, held by two stone pillars on a tall carved stone plinth\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"stone\", \"colors\": [\"#5a4a32\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#9c8a6e\"], \"features\": [\"bell\", \"stone-pillar\", \"gilded-pinnacle\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [3, 2], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(101,'mul-chowk','Mul Chowk','मूल चोक','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur','patan-durbar-square',27.672997,85.325208,'courtyard','Hindu','Taleju Bhawani',NULL,'17th century; rebuilt by Srinivasa Malla after a fire in 1662 (c. 1665-1666)','Malla','Two-storey Newar palace courtyard with the gilded Bidya Mandir at its centre and Taleju temples around it',1,'The largest and most sacred courtyard of Patan palace, ringed by shrines of the royal goddess Taleju.','You are now in Mul Chowk, the central and largest of the three main courtyards of Patan\'s royal palace. This was the ritual heart of the Malla court. The original buildings burned in 1662 and were rebuilt within a few years by King Srinivasa Malla. In the centre stands a small gilded shrine, the Bidya Mandir, and around the courtyard rise temples of Taleju Bhawani, the kings\' personal goddess: the triple-roofed Taleju temple to the north and the Taleju Bhawani shrine on the south side. Look at the doorway to the Taleju shrine on the southern side. It is flanked by two river goddesses, Ganga standing on a tortoise and Jamuna on a makara, a mythical water creature. Their gilded forms are among the finest metalwork in the palace. The courtyard\'s temples were restored in 2014, and its walls and buildings needed repair again after the 2015 earthquake. Stand quietly for a moment and picture the royal rituals once performed on these flagstones.',NULL,'[\"Mul Chowk is the central and largest of the palace\'s three main courtyards.\", \"A small gilded temple, the Bidya Mandir, stands at its centre.\", \"The Taleju shrine doorway is flanked by Ganga on a tortoise and Jamuna on a makara.\", \"After a fire in 1662 the courtyard was rebuilt by Srinivasa Malla.\"]',NULL,NULL,1000,250,0,20,'Walls and buildings around the courtyard were damaged in the April 2015 earthquake and later repaired; the South Taleju temple was the subject of post-quake structural restoration.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Mul_Chowk%2C_Patan_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Mul_Chowk%2C_Patan_%281%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mul_Chowk,_Patan_(1).jpg','Radosław Botev · CC BY 3.0 pl','courtyard,hindu,malla,lalitpur,unesco,palace,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/pois/1432406\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/120443289\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/120443314\", \"https://cultureincrisis.org/projects/structural-assessment-and-restoration-of-the-south-tajelu-temple-and-other-structures-at-patan-royal-palace-affected-by-the-april-2015-nepal-earthquake\"]','पाटन दरबारको सबैभन्दा ठूलो र पवित्र आँगन, जसलाई शाही देवी तलेजुका मन्दिरले घेरेका छन्।','तपाईं अहिले मूल चोकमा हुनुहुन्छ। यो पाटनको राजदरबारका तीन मुख्य आँगनमध्ये बीचको र सबैभन्दा ठूलो हो। मल्ल दरबारको धार्मिक विधिको केन्द्र यही थियो। पुराना भवन सन् १६६२ मा जले, र राजा श्रीनिवास मल्लले केही वर्षभित्रै फेरि बनाए। बीचमा सानो सुनौलो मन्दिर, विद्या मन्दिर, छ। वरिपरि राजाहरूकी आफ्नै देवी तलेजु भवानीका मन्दिर उभिएका छन्: उत्तरमा तीन छाने तलेजु मन्दिर र दक्षिणतिर तलेजु भवानीको मन्दिर। दक्षिणतिरको तलेजु मन्दिरको ढोका हेर्नुहोस्। त्यसका दुवैतिर दुई नदी देवी छन्: कछुवामाथि उभिएकी गङ्गा र मकर नामको पौराणिक जलचरमाथि उभिएकी जमुना। तिनका सुनौला मूर्ति दरबारका सबैभन्दा राम्रा धातुकलामध्ये पर्छन्। चोकका मन्दिर सन् २०१४ मा मर्मत गरिएका थिए, र २०१५ को भूकम्पपछि यसका भित्ता र भवन फेरि मर्मत गर्नुपर्‍यो। केही बेर चुपचाप उभिनुहोस्, र यी ढुङ्गाका पाटामा कुनै बेला हुने शाही पूजाविधिको कल्पना गर्नुहोस्।',NULL,'[\"मूल चोक दरबारका तीन मुख्य आँगनमध्ये बीचको र सबैभन्दा ठूलो हो।\", \"यसको बीचमा सानो सुनौलो मन्दिर, विद्या मन्दिर, छ।\", \"तलेजु मन्दिरको ढोकाका दुवैतिर कछुवामाथि गङ्गा र मकरमाथि जमुना छन्।\", \"सन् १६६२ को आगलागीपछि श्रीनिवास मल्लले चोक फेरि बनाए।\"]','अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पमा चोकवरिपरिका भित्ता र भवनमा क्षति भयो र पछि मर्मत गरियो; दक्षिण तलेजु मन्दिर भूकम्पपछिको संरचनागत मर्मतको विषय थियो।','[{\"name\": \"Dashain\", \"note\": \"Main Durga festival; Taleju shrines and Durga temples draw worship and offerings\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ\", \"note_np\": \"दुर्गाको मुख्य चाड; तलेजुका मन्दिर र दुर्गा मन्दिरमा पूजा र चढावा चढाइन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Mool_Chowk_%28Main_courtyard_%29_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Mool_Chowk_%28Main_courtyard_%29_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Mul Chowk, the main palace courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mool_Chowk_(Main_courtyard_)_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Dashain_Ghar_Mool_Chowk_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%287%29.jpg/1280px-Dashain_Ghar_Mool_Chowk_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%287%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Dashain Ghar in Mul Chowk\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dashain_Ghar_Mool_Chowk_Patan_Durbar_Square_Patan_Lalitpur_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(7).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Golden_door%2C_Mul_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Golden_door%2C_Mul_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Golden door of the Taleju shrine in Mul Chowk\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Golden_door,_Mul_Chowk,_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Patan-Palast-Mul_Chowk-18-2015-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Palast-Mul_Chowk-18-2015-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Mul Chowk, Patan palace, 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Palast-Mul_Chowk-18-2015-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Mul_Chowk_%E2%80%93_Royal_Palace_Patan_%E2%80%93_01.jpg/1280px-Mul_Chowk_%E2%80%93_Royal_Palace_Patan_%E2%80%93_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Maesi64\", \"caption\": \"Mul Chowk, Royal Palace of Patan\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mul_Chowk_%E2%80%93_Royal_Palace_Patan_%E2%80%93_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Two-storey brick courtyard with a small gilded temple in the middle and a tall Taleju temple rising over one wing\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"golden-door\", \"carved-windows\", \"carved-struts\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"lion-statues\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [30, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(102,'sundari-chowk-tusha-hiti','Sundari Chowk and Tusha Hiti','सुन्दरी चोक र तुषा हिटी','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur','patan-durbar-square',27.672717,85.325137,'courtyard','Hindu',NULL,NULL,'17th century (King Siddhi Narasimha Malla; sources give 1626, 1627 or 1647 for Tusha Hiti)','Malla','Palace courtyard containing a sunken, octagonal stone royal bath with a gilt copper spout and 72 stone deity images',1,'A royal courtyard hiding Tusha Hiti, the sunken stone bath of King Siddhi Narasimha Malla.','Step into Sundari Chowk, the southern courtyard of the palace, and look down. Sunk about one and a half metres below your feet is Tusha Hiti, the royal bath credited to King Siddhi Narasimha Malla in the 17th century. The basin is octagonal, a nod to the king\'s devotion to the eight Nagas, and two stone serpents run around its rim. Its walls hold 72 stone images of gods and goddesses, among them the Ashtamatrikas, the Ashta Bhairavas and the ten avatars of Vishnu. Water once poured from a gilt copper spout showing Vishnu and Lakshmi riding Garuda. The spout you see is a replica; the original was stolen in 2010, later recovered, and its top part is now in the National Museum. A small replica of Krishna Mandir sits on the main axis of the bath. Legend says the king bathed here at dawn and meditated on a nearby stone slab. Today no water flows. Sundari Chowk became part of the Patan Museum in 2017.','According to legend, King Siddhi Narasimha Malla rose early each morning, bathed in Tusha Hiti and then meditated for hours on the stone slab beside it. Attendants brought towels and wraps while the queen watched from the carved windows above, and afterward the king lay on a stone bed to be massaged with oils. Some historians doubt the story, arguing the bath was meant for ritual offerings of water to the gods rather than royal bathing.','[\"Tusha Hiti is about 5.3 m long, 4 m wide and sits 150 cm below the courtyard.\", \"The bath holds 72 stone sculptures of deities, including the ten avatars of Vishnu.\", \"The original gilt spout was stolen in 2010 and recovered; its top portion is in the National Museum of Nepal.\", \"The bath appeared in the films Arabian Nights (1974) and Little Buddha (1993).\"]','10:30','17:30',1000,250,NULL,30,'After the April 2015 earthquake the bath\'s water became polluted, and by 2019 no water was flowing from the spout.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Sundari_chowk_and_Tusha_Hiti_in_the_middle.jpg/1280px-Sundari_chowk_and_Tusha_Hiti_in_the_middle.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sundari_chowk_and_Tusha_Hiti_in_the_middle.jpg','Suraj Belbase · CC BY-SA 4.0','courtyard,hindu,malla,lalitpur,unesco,legend,water,palace,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tusha_Hiti\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Museum\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/199772294\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/10034234966\"]','शाही आँगन, जसले राजा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्लको भुइँमुनिको ढुङ्गाको स्नानकुण्ड तुषा हिटी लुकाएको छ।','दरबारको दक्षिणी आँगन सुन्दरी चोकमा पस्नुहोस् र तल हेर्नुहोस्। तपाईंको खुट्टाभन्दा करिब डेढ मिटर तल तुषा हिटी छ। यो १७ औं शताब्दीका राजा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्लले बनाएको मानिने शाही स्नानकुण्ड हो। कुण्ड अष्टकोणीय छ, जसले राजाको आठ नागप्रतिको भक्ति देखाउँछ, र दुईवटा ढुङ्गाका सर्पले यसको किनार घेरेका छन्। यसका पर्खालमा देवीदेवताका ७२ वटा ढुङ्गाका मूर्ति छन्। तिनमा अष्टमातृका, अष्टभैरव र विष्णुका दश अवतार पर्छन्। पहिले गरुडमाथि सवार विष्णु र लक्ष्मी देखिने सुनको पानी चढाएको तामाको धाराबाट पानी खस्थ्यो। अहिले देखिने धारा नक्कल हो; सन् २०१० मा मूल धारा चोरी भयो, पछि फेला पर्‍यो, र अहिले त्यसको माथिल्लो भाग राष्ट्रिय संग्रहालयमा छ। स्नानकुण्डको मुख्य रेखामा कृष्ण मन्दिरको सानो नक्कल छ। भनिन्छ, राजा यहाँ बिहानै नुहाउँथे र नजिकैको ढुङ्गाको पाटामा ध्यान गर्थे। आज पानी बग्दैन। सुन्दरी चोक सन् २०१७ मा पाटन संग्रहालयको भाग बन्यो।','भनिन्छ, राजा सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्ल हरेक बिहान सबेरै उठ्थे, तुषा हिटीमा नुहाउँथे, अनि छेउको ढुङ्गाको पाटामा घण्टौँ ध्यान गर्थे। सेवकले तौलिया र लुगा ल्याइदिन्थे, र माथिका कुँदिएका झ्यालबाट रानी हेरिरहन्थिन्। त्यसपछि राजा तेलले मालिस गराउन ढुङ्गाको ओछ्यानमा पल्टन्थे। केही इतिहासकारले यो कथामा शङ्का गर्छन्। उनीहरूका अनुसार यो कुण्ड राजाको नुहाइका लागि होइन, देवतालाई विधिपूर्वक जल चढाउन बनाइएको थियो।','[\"तुषा हिटी करिब ५.३ मिटर लामो, ४ मिटर चौडा छ र आँगनभन्दा १५० सेन्टिमिटर तल छ।\", \"स्नानकुण्डमा विष्णुका दश अवतार लगायत देवताका ७२ वटा ढुङ्गाका मूर्ति छन्।\", \"सुनको पानी चढाएको मूल धारा सन् २०१० मा चोरी भयो र फेला पर्‍यो; त्यसको माथिल्लो भाग नेपालको राष्ट्रिय संग्रहालयमा छ।\", \"यो स्नानकुण्ड ‘अरेबियन नाइट्स’ (१९७४) र ‘लिटिल बुद्ध’ (१९९३) चलचित्रमा देखिएको थियो।\"]','अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पपछि स्नानकुण्डको पानी फोहोर भयो, र सन् २०१९ सम्म धाराबाट पानी बगेको थिएन।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Sundari_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Sundari_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Sundari Chowk courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sundari_Chowk,_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Sundari_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square2.jpg/1280px-Sundari_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square2.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Carved wooden facade of Sundari Chowk\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sundari_Chowk,_Patan_Durbar_Square2.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Ganesh_-_Wood_Caarving%2C_Sundari_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg/1280px-Ganesh_-_Wood_Caarving%2C_Sundari_Chowk%2C_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Ganesh woodcarving in Sundari Chowk\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ganesh_-_Wood_Caarving,_Sundari_Chowk,_Patan_Durbar_Square.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Patan-Palast-Sundhara_Chowk-02-Brunnen-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Palast-Sundhara_Chowk-02-Brunnen-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Tusha Hiti, the sunken royal bath\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Palast-Sundhara_Chowk-02-Brunnen-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Slightly_cusped_Tusha_Hiti_step-well_%2CGilt_Bronze_water_Spout_06.jpg/1280px-Slightly_cusped_Tusha_Hiti_step-well_%2CGilt_Bronze_water_Spout_06.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Gilt bronze water spout of Tusha Hiti\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slightly_cusped_Tusha_Hiti_step-well_,Gilt_Bronze_water_Spout_06.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Brick palace courtyard around a sunken stone bath lined with small deity carvings and a gilded spout\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#9c8a6e\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"water-spouts\", \"carved-windows\", \"carved-struts\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [30, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(103,'golden-temple','Golden Temple (Hiranya Varna Mahavihar)','हिरण्यवर्ण महाविहार','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur',NULL,27.675224,85.324711,'bahal','Buddhist','Shakyamuni Buddha',1409,'Traditionally founded in the 12th century; in its current form since 1409','Malla','Newar Buddhist bahal (monastery courtyard) with a three-roofed gilt pagoda shrine and a central Swayambhu chaitya',0,'Kwa Bahal, a gleaming Buddhist monastery where a boy priest under twelve tends the shrine of the Buddha.','Slip through the stone gate guarded by a pair of lions and you enter Hiranya Varna Mahavihar, the Gold-coloured Great Monastery, known locally as Kwa Bahal and to visitors as the Golden Temple. Tradition says it was founded in the 12th century; its current form dates from 1409. As you pass the gate, look up to find a Kalachakra mandala on the ceiling. In the courtyard, golden elephants stand on tortoises, and at the centre is a small chaitya identified with Swayambhu, believed older than the temple itself. Opposite rises the main shrine with three gilded roofs, its facade showing scenes from the Buddha\'s life. Inside sits a silver image of Shakyamuni Buddha, called Kwabaju. Now look for the priest: he is a boy, always under twelve, who serves for a month, walking the neighbourhood in silence each morning and evening while ringing a bell. The monastery also keeps an 800-year-old Prajnaparamita text. Remember to take off your shoes before entering.','According to legend, the Golden Temple was built at a spot where a rat was seen chasing a cat, an upside-down omen that marked the place as special and worthy of a monastery. The story is still remembered in the neighbourhood, and rats were still being fed at the site as recently as 1994. Visitors who notice small offerings of food in the courtyard may be seeing the last echoes of that tradition.','[\"Also called Kwa Bahal; the name means \\\"Gold-coloured Great Monastery\\\".\", \"The chief priest is a boy under twelve who serves for one month.\", \"It keeps an approximately 800-year-old Prajnaparamita manuscript, restored every three years.\", \"Its courtyard buildings were damaged in 2015 and restoration started in July 2021.\"]',NULL,NULL,100,NULL,NULL,30,'The courtyard buildings sustained structural damage in the 2015 earthquake; restoration began in July 2021.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Golden_Temple_%28Kwa_Bahal%29_01.jpg/1280px-Golden_Temple_%28Kwa_Bahal%29_01.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Golden_Temple_(Kwa_Bahal)_01.jpg','Nabin K. Sapkota · CC BY-SA 4.0','bahal,buddhist,malla,lalitpur,legend,courtyard,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hiranya_Varna_Mahavihar\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/4624856\", \"https://thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/golden-temple-patan.html\", \"https://eap.bl.uk/item/EAP838-1-1-5-28\"]','क्वा बहाल, चम्किलो बौद्ध विहार, जहाँ बाह्र वर्षभन्दा कम उमेरको बालकले बुद्धको मन्दिरको सेवा गर्छ।','दुईवटा सिंहले पहरा दिएको ढुङ्गाको ढोकाबाट भित्र पस्नुहोस्, तपाईं हिरण्यवर्ण महाविहारमा पुग्नुहुन्छ। यसको अर्थ सुनको रङको ठूलो विहार हो। स्थानीयले यसलाई क्वा बहाल भन्छन्, र पर्यटकले सुनको मन्दिर। परम्पराअनुसार यो १२ औं शताब्दीमा स्थापना भएको हो; यसको अहिलेको रूप सन् १४०९ को हो। ढोका नाघ्दा माथि छानामा कालचक्र मण्डल खोज्नुहोस्। आँगनमा सुनौला हात्ती कछुवामाथि उभिएका छन्, र बीचमा स्वयम्भूसँग जोडिएको सानो चैत्य छ, जसलाई मन्दिरभन्दा पनि पुरानो मानिन्छ। सामुन्ने तीन सुनौला छाना भएको मुख्य मन्दिर छ, जसको अगाडिको भागमा बुद्धको जीवनका दृश्य छन्। भित्र शाक्यमुनि बुद्धको चाँदीको मूर्ति छ, जसलाई क्वाबाजु भनिन्छ। अब पुजारी खोज्नुहोस्: उनी सधैँ बाह्र वर्षभन्दा कम उमेरको बालक हुन्छन्, एक महिना सेवा गर्छन्, र हरेक बिहान र साँझ घण्टी बजाउँदै चुपचाप टोल घुम्छन्। विहारमा ८०० वर्ष पुरानो प्रज्ञापारमिता ग्रन्थ पनि छ। भित्र पस्नुअघि जुत्ता खोल्न नबिर्सनुहोस्।','भनिन्छ, सुनको मन्दिर बिरालोलाई लखेटिरहेको मुसा देखिएको ठाउँमा बनेको हो। यो उल्टो शकुन थियो, जसले त्यो ठाउँलाई विशेष र विहार बनाउन योग्य देखायो। यो कथा अझै टोलमा सम्झिन्छ, र सन् १९९४ सम्म पनि त्यहाँ मुसालाई खान दिइन्थ्यो। आँगनमा खानेकुराका साना भेटी देख्नुभयो भने, तपाईंले त्यही परम्पराको बाँकी रहेको झल्को देख्दै हुनुहुन्छ।','[\"यसलाई क्वा बहाल पनि भनिन्छ; नामको अर्थ \\\"सुनको रङको ठूलो विहार\\\" हो।\", \"प्रमुख पुजारी बाह्र वर्षभन्दा कम उमेरको बालक हुन्छ, जसले एक महिना सेवा गर्छ।\", \"यहाँ करिब ८०० वर्ष पुरानो प्रज्ञापारमिता पाण्डुलिपि छ, जसलाई हरेक तीन वर्षमा मर्मत गरिन्छ।\", \"यसका आँगनका भवन सन् २०१५ मा क्षतिग्रस्त भए, र जुलाई २०२१ मा मर्मत सुरु भयो।\"]','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा आँगनका भवनमा संरचनागत क्षति भयो; मर्मत जुलाई २०२१ मा सुरु भयो।','[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Bells_%26_Coutryard_-_Kwa_Baha_%28Golden_Temple%29_%288094977504%29.jpg/1280px-Bells_%26_Coutryard_-_Kwa_Baha_%28Golden_Temple%29_%288094977504%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Greg Willis from Denver, CO, usa\", \"caption\": \"Bells and courtyard of Kwa Bahal\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bells_%26_Coutryard_-_Kwa_Baha_(Golden_Temple)_(8094977504).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Courtyard_of_golden_temple.jpg/1280px-Courtyard_of_golden_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Anim Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Courtyard of the Golden Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Courtyard_of_golden_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Entry_to_golden_temple.jpg/1280px-Entry_to_golden_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Anim Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Entrance to the Golden Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entry_to_golden_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Diyo_%28Oil_lamp%29_at_Golden_Temple.jpg/1280px-Diyo_%28Oil_lamp%29_at_Golden_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Dulal\", \"caption\": \"Butter lamps (diyo) at the Golden Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diyo_(Oil_lamp)_at_Golden_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Patan-Hiranyabarna_Mahavihar-30-Cella-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Patan-Hiranyabarna_Mahavihar-30-Cella-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Main shrine (cella) of Hiranya Varna Mahavihar\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan-Hiranyabarna_Mahavihar-30-Cella-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Enclosed monastery courtyard: a three-roofed gilded-copper pagoda shrine with a small gilded chaitya in the yard\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#c9a227\", \"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"golden-door\", \"bell\", \"chaityas\", \"lamps-diyo\", \"carved-windows\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [25, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(104,'kumbheshwar-temple','Kumbheshwar Temple','कुम्भेश्वर मन्दिर','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur',NULL,27.676581,85.326046,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva',1392,'14th century (c. 1392, King Jayasthiti Malla)','Malla','Free-standing five-tiered Newar pagoda with fine woodcarving, set in a complex with sacred ponds',0,'Patan\'s oldest temple: a five-roofed Shiva pagoda whose ponds are said to be fed from Gosainkunda.','About 200 metres north of Durbar Square you reach Kumbheshwar, built around 1392 by King Jayasthiti Malla and considered the oldest temple in Patan. Count the roofs: five. It is one of only two free-standing five-storey temples in the valley; the other is the famous Nyatapola in Bhaktapur. Kumbheshwar is dedicated to Shiva, and a large Nandi, his bull, kneels in front, facing the temple. Walk through the complex and you will find other shrines, including Bagalamukhi and Ulmanta Bhairava, along with two hiti ponds. Many believe the spring that feeds these ponds flows all the way from Gosainkunda, the sacred lake 43 kilometres north of Kathmandu. So on Janai Purnima, devotees take a dip here, which is said to equal bathing in Gosainkunda itself, and the courtyard fills with pilgrims. The upper part of the temple suffered in the 2015 earthquake. As you leave, look again at the tall tiers and notice the graceful proportions and fine woodcarving the temple is famous for.','It is popularly believed that the spring filling the ponds of Kumbheshwar originates in Gosainkunda, the holy lake in the mountains 43 km north of Kathmandu. Because of this hidden underground link, a ritual dip here during the festival of Janai Purnima is said to bring the same merit as bathing in Gosainkunda itself. For pilgrims who cannot make the long mountain trek, Kumbheshwar offers the blessing much closer to home.','[\"Built around 1392 by King Jayasthiti Malla, making it Patan\'s oldest temple.\", \"One of two free-standing five-storey temples in the valley, along with Nyatapola in Bhaktapur.\", \"A large Nandi bull faces the temple, marking it as a Shiva shrine.\", \"Its ponds are believed to be fed from Gosainkunda and draw crowds at Janai Purnima.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,'A structural study reports that the temple\'s top tier collapsed in the April 2015 earthquake.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Kumbheshwar_Temple_%2892152%29.jpg/1280px-Kumbheshwar_Temple_%2892152%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kumbheshwar_Temple_(92152).jpg','Janak Bhatta · CC BY 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,lalitpur,legend,water,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kumbheshwar_Temple\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1759661519\", \"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-319-99441-3_143.pdf\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/kumbeshwar-temple-complex-patan.html\"]','पाटनको सबैभन्दा पुरानो मन्दिर: शिवको पाँच छाने पगोडा, जसका पोखरीमा गोसाइँकुण्डबाट पानी आउँछ भनिन्छ।','दरबार क्षेत्रबाट करिब २०० मिटर उत्तर हिँड्दा तपाईं कुम्भेश्वर पुग्नुहुन्छ। यो करिब सन् १३९२ मा राजा जयस्थिति मल्लले बनाएका हुन्, र पाटनको सबैभन्दा पुरानो मन्दिर मानिन्छ। छाना गन्नुहोस्: पाँचवटा। उपत्यकामा एक्लै उभिएका पाँच तले मन्दिर दुईवटा मात्र छन्, र यो ती मध्ये एक हो। अर्को भक्तपुरको चर्चित न्यातपोल हो। कुम्भेश्वर शिवलाई समर्पित छ, र उनको सवारी ठूलो नन्दी गोरु अगाडि मन्दिरतिर फर्केर घुँडा टेकेर बसेको छ। परिसर घुम्दा अरू मन्दिर पनि भेट्नुहुन्छ, जसमा बगलामुखी र उल्मन्ता भैरव छन्, र दुईवटा हिटी पोखरी पनि छन्। धेरैले यी पोखरी भर्ने मूल काठमाडौँभन्दा ४३ किलोमिटर उत्तरको पवित्र ताल गोसाइँकुण्डबाटै आउँछ भन्ने विश्वास गर्छन्। त्यसैले जनै पूर्णिमामा भक्तजन यहाँ डुबुल्की मार्छन्, जसलाई गोसाइँकुण्डमै नुहाए जत्तिकै मानिन्छ, र आँगन तीर्थयात्रीले भरिन्छ। २०१५ को भूकम्पमा मन्दिरको माथिल्लो भागमा क्षति पुग्यो। फर्कने बेला अग्ला तहहरू फेरि हेर्नुहोस्, र यो मन्दिर जसका लागि प्रसिद्ध छ, त्यो सुन्दर अनुपात र बारीक काठको कुँदाइ ध्यान दिएर हेर्नुहोस्।','कुम्भेश्वरका पोखरी भर्ने मूल काठमाडौँभन्दा ४३ किलोमिटर उत्तरका हिमालको पवित्र ताल गोसाइँकुण्डबाट आउँछ भन्ने लोकविश्वास छ। यही भूमिगत जोडाइका कारण जनै पूर्णिमाको चाडमा यहाँ डुबुल्की मार्दा गोसाइँकुण्डमै नुहाए जत्तिकै पुण्य पाइन्छ भनिन्छ। लामो हिमाली यात्रा गर्न नसक्ने तीर्थयात्रीलाई कुम्भेश्वरले त्यही आशीर्वाद धेरै नजिकै दिन्छ।','[\"करिब सन् १३९२ मा राजा जयस्थिति मल्लले बनाएको, त्यसैले यो पाटनको सबैभन्दा पुरानो मन्दिर हो।\", \"उपत्यकाका दुईवटा एक्लै उभिएका पाँच तले मन्दिरमध्ये एक; अर्को भक्तपुरको न्यातपोल हो।\", \"ठूलो नन्दी गोरु मन्दिरतिर फर्केको छ, जसले यो शिवको मन्दिर हो भन्ने देखाउँछ।\", \"यसका पोखरीमा गोसाइँकुण्डबाट पानी आउँछ भन्ने विश्वास छ, र जनै पूर्णिमामा यहाँ भीड लाग्छ।\"]','एउटा संरचनागत अध्ययन अनुसार अप्रिल २०१५ को भूकम्पमा मन्दिरको माथिल्लो तह ढलेको थियो।','[{\"name\": \"Janai Purnima\", \"note\": \"Fair at the sacred ponds; a silver-gold linga is set in the pond for worship\", \"month\": \"Shrawan\", \"name_np\": \"जनै पूर्णिमा\", \"note_np\": \"पवित्र पोखरीमा मेला लाग्छ; पूजाका लागि पोखरीमा चाँदी र सुनको लिङ्ग राखिन्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Night of Shiva; devotees offer worship at Shiva shrines\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"शिवको रात; भक्तजन शिव मन्दिरमा पूजा गर्छन्\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/Kumbheshwar_Temple_%28Mahadev%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Five-tiered Kumbheshwar Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kumbheshwar_Temple_(Mahadev).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Kumbheshwar_Temple_%28Mahadev%29%2C_Patan.jpg/1280px-Kumbheshwar_Temple_%28Mahadev%29%2C_Patan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Kumbheshwar Temple under restoration scaffolding\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kumbheshwar_Temple_(Mahadev),_Patan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Crowd_queuing_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg/1280px-Crowd_queuing_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg\", \"author\": \"Perrine Aguiar\", \"caption\": \"Devotees queuing on Janai Purnima\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crowd_queuing_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Crowd_surronding_pond_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg/1280px-Crowd_surronding_pond_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg\", \"author\": \"Perrine Aguiar\", \"caption\": \"Crowd around the sacred pond on Janai Purnima\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crowd_surronding_pond_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Women_lighting_candles_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg/1280px-Women_lighting_candles_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg\", \"author\": \"Perrine Aguiar\", \"caption\": \"Women lighting candles on Janai Purnima\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Women_lighting_candles_Kumbheshwar_temple_Janai_Purnima.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Slender five-roofed brick pagoda in a courtyard with a walled sacred pond beside it; Nandi bull facing the door\", \"tiers\": 5, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"nandi-bull\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"water-spouts\", \"chaityas\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [10, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"pond\", \"brick-courtyard\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49');
INSERT INTO `monuments` VALUES (105,'mahabouddha-temple','Mahabouddha Temple (Temple of a Thousand Buddhas)','महाबौद्ध मन्दिर','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur',NULL,27.668998,85.327142,'shikhara','Buddhist','Buddha',NULL,'Late 16th century (Wikipedia dates it to 1585; other accounts give c. 1564 to 1610); rebuilt after the 1934 earthquake','Malla','Terracotta-clad shikhara modelled on the Mahabodhi Temple at Bodh Gaya, its tiles bearing Buddha images',0,'A terracotta shikhara inspired by Bodh Gaya, its tiles covered with countless small Buddhas.','Follow the narrow lanes south-east of Durbar Square and suddenly a tall terracotta tower appears, squeezed into a tiny courtyard. This is Mahabouddha, the Temple of a Thousand Buddhas. Its design is loosely based on the Mahabodhi Temple at Bodh Gaya in India, where the Buddha attained enlightenment. Step close and look at the surface: it is clad in terracotta tiles, and each tile carries a small image of the Buddha, which is how the temple earned its nickname. Wikipedia dates the temple to 1585, while other accounts place its beginning a little earlier and its completion around 1610. Local tradition credits a Patan priest, Abhaya Raj Shakya, who was inspired by a pilgrimage to Bodh Gaya. The great earthquake of 1934 destroyed the temple, and it was rebuilt afterward. Because the courtyard is so cramped, the best views come from the rooftops of the surrounding workshops, many of which sell Patan\'s famous metal statues. Ask politely, and you may be invited up.','Tradition says the priest Abhaya Raj Shakya began the temple after returning from a pilgrimage to Bodh Gaya, but he died soon after laying its foundation. His sons carried on the work for years, and the temple was finally completed by the family, a devotion that lasted across generations. Some accounts say one son nearly gave up before a goddess appeared and urged him to finish the work his father had begun.','[\"Its design is loosely based on the Mahabodhi Temple in Bodh Gaya, India.\", \"The nickname comes from the many terracotta tiles each bearing a Buddha image.\", \"Wikipedia dates the temple to 1585; other accounts give c. 1564 to 1610.\", \"It was rebuilt after the 1934 Nepal-India earthquake.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Mahabuddha%2C_Patan_2016-04-10b.jpg/1280px-Mahabuddha%2C_Patan_2016-04-10b.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahabuddha,_Patan_2016-04-10b.jpg','Christopher J. Fynn · CC BY-SA 4.0','shikhara,buddhist,malla,lalitpur,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahabouddha_Temple\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/564129617\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/mahaboudha-temple-patan.html\"]','बोधगयाबाट प्रेरित टेराकोटाको शिखर मन्दिर, जसका टायलमा अनगिन्ती साना बुद्ध छन्।','दरबार क्षेत्रको दक्षिणपूर्वका साँघुरा गल्ली हिँड्दै जानुहोस्। अचानक सानो आँगनमा निचोरिएर बसेको अग्लो टेराकोटाको टावर देखिन्छ। यो महाबौद्ध हो, हजार बुद्धको मन्दिर। यसको बनावट भारतको बोधगयामा रहेको महाबोधि मन्दिरबाट केही हदसम्म लिइएको हो, जहाँ बुद्धले ज्ञान पाएका थिए। नजिक गएर सतह हेर्नुहोस्: यो टेराकोटाका टायलले ढाकिएको छ, र हरेक टायलमा बुद्धको सानो आकृति छ। यसैले मन्दिरलाई यो उपनाम मिलेको हो। विकिपिडियाले मन्दिर १५८५ को हो भन्छ, तर अरू विवरणले सुरु अलि अघि र पूरा हुँदा करिब १६१० मा भएको भन्छन्। स्थानीय परम्परा अनुसार बोधगयाको तीर्थयात्राबाट प्रेरित भएका पाटनका पुजारी अभय राज शाक्यले यो सुरु गरेका थिए। सन् १९३४ को ठूलो भूकम्पले मन्दिर ढाल्यो, र त्यसपछि यसलाई फेरि बनाइयो। आँगन साँघुरो भएकाले सबैभन्दा राम्रो दृश्य वरपरका कार्यशालाका छतबाट देखिन्छ। ती धेरै कार्यशालामा पाटनका चर्चित धातुका मूर्ति बेचिन्छन्। नम्रतासाथ सोध्नुहोस्, तपाईंलाई माथि बोलाइन सक्छ।','परम्परा अनुसार पुजारी अभय राज शाक्यले बोधगयाको तीर्थयात्राबाट फर्केर मन्दिर सुरु गरे, तर जग हालेको केही समयमै उनको मृत्यु भयो। उनका छोराहरूले वर्षौँसम्म काम अघि बढाए, र अन्त्यमा परिवारले नै मन्दिर पूरा गर्‍यो। यो भक्ति कैयौँ पुस्तासम्म चल्यो। केही विवरण अनुसार एक छोराले काम छोडिदिन लाग्दा एकजना देवी देखा परिन् र बुबाले सुरु गरेको काम पूरा गर्न भनिन्।','[\"यसको बनावट भारतको बोधगयाको महाबोधि मन्दिरबाट केही हदसम्म लिइएको हो।\", \"यो उपनाम बुद्धको आकृति भएका धेरै टेराकोटा टायलबाट आएको हो।\", \"विकिपिडियाले मन्दिरलाई १५८५ को भन्छ; अरू विवरणले करिब १५६४ देखि १६१० सम्म भन्छन्।\", \"सन् १९३४ को नेपाल-भारत भूकम्पपछि यसलाई फेरि बनाइएको थियो।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Mahabuddha%2C_Patan_2016-04-10a.jpg/1280px-Mahabuddha%2C_Patan_2016-04-10a.jpg\", \"author\": \"Christopher J. Fynn\", \"caption\": \"Mahabouddha Temple in its narrow courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahabuddha,_Patan_2016-04-10a.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Mahabuddha%2C_Patan_2016-04-10c.jpg/1280px-Mahabuddha%2C_Patan_2016-04-10c.jpg\", \"author\": \"Christopher J. Fynn\", \"caption\": \"Terracotta shikhara of Mahabouddha\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahabuddha,_Patan_2016-04-10c.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Mahabouddha_Mandir%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur%2C_Nepal_04.jpg/1280px-Mahabouddha_Mandir%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur%2C_Nepal_04.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Mahabouddha Temple, Patan\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahabouddha_Mandir,_Patan,_Lalitpur,_Nepal_04.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Entrance_Gate_of_Mahabouddha_Mandir%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur%2C_Nepal_05.jpg/1280px-Entrance_Gate_of_Mahabouddha_Mandir%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur%2C_Nepal_05.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Entrance gate of Mahabouddha\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_Gate_of_Mahabouddha_Mandir,_Patan,_Lalitpur,_Nepal_05.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Mahaboudha_temple_also_known_as_temple_of_a_thousand.jpg/1280px-Mahaboudha_temple_also_known_as_temple_of_a_thousand.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prakat Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Tiles with Buddha images on the tower\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahaboudha_temple_also_known_as_temple_of_a_thousand.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"shikhara\", \"roof\": \"stone-spire\", \"notes\": \"Tall terracotta tower covered in small Buddha tiles, squeezed into a tiny courtyard hemmed in by houses\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#a0522d\", \"#c9a227\", \"#6b4a35\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"idol-visible\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [8, 8], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(106,'rato-machhindranath-temple','Rato Machhindranath Temple (Ta Bahal, Patan)','रातो मच्छिन्द्रनाथ मन्दिर','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur',NULL,27.670320,85.322889,'pagoda','Both','Rato Machhindranath (Bunga Dyah / Karunamaya)',1673,'Present temple from 1673; a temple has stood on the site since at least 1408','Malla','Three-tiered Newar pagoda in the centre of the Ta Bahal courtyard',0,'Patan home of Bunga Dyah, the red rain god honoured by Nepal\'s longest chariot festival.','South of Durbar Square, in the open courtyard of Ta Bahal, stands the three-tiered temple of Rato Machhindranath. The present building dates from 1673, though a temple has stood here since at least 1408. The deity has many names. Newars call him Bunga Dyah or Karunamaya, the compassionate one, a form of the Bodhisattva Avalokiteshvara; Hindus know him as Machhindranath. Rato means red, the colour of his image. He is believed to bring the monsoon rains. Each year, in the Rato Machhindranath Jatra, his image leaves this temple and rides a chariot about 60 feet tall, built at Pulchowk, on a month-long journey through the streets to Jawalakhel. It is the longest chariot festival in Nepal, and it ends with Bhoto Jatra, when a jewelled vest is held up for all to see. The god divides his year between Patan and his other home in Bungamati. Walk slowly around the courtyard, a place where Hindu and Buddhist devotion truly meet.','During a twelve-year drought, the sage Gorakhnath sat meditating on the serpents that bring rain. Only the arrival of his teacher Machhindranath could make him rise, so envoys brought Machhindranath to the valley. Gorakhnath stood to greet him, the serpents were freed and the rain returned. The clever king of Lalitpur then kept the god in his city, and every year since, the people of Patan have pulled his chariot through the streets to pray for good rains.','[\"The present temple dates from 1673; a temple has occupied the site since at least 1408.\", \"Rato means \\\"red\\\", the colour of the deity\'s image.\", \"His chariot festival is the longest in Nepal, ending with Bhoto Jatra at Jawalakhel.\", \"The deity spends about six months of the year in Bungamati and the rest in Patan.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur_01.jpg/1280px-Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur_01.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rato_Machhindranath_Temple,_Patan,_Lalitpur_01.jpg','Suraj Belbase · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,both,malla,lalitpur,hindu,buddhist,legend,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rato_Machindranath_Jatra\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bungamati\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/points-of-interest/rato-machhendranath-temple/1432440\", \"https://www.webpages.uidaho.edu/arch499/nonwest/nepal/Temples%20of%20Patan.htm\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/206482247\"]','रातो वर्षा देवता बुङ्ग द्यःको पाटनको घर, जहाँबाट नेपालको सबैभन्दा लामो रथजात्रा निस्कन्छ।','दरबार क्षेत्रको दक्षिणमा, ता बहालको खुला आँगनमा रातो मच्छिन्द्रनाथको तीन तले मन्दिर छ। अहिलेको भवन सन् १६७३ को हो, तर यहाँ कम्तीमा सन् १४०८ देखि मन्दिर छ। देवताका धेरै नाम छन्। नेवारहरू उनलाई बुङ्ग द्यः वा करुणामय भन्छन्, जो बोधिसत्त्व अवलोकितेश्वरको एउटा रूप हो। हिन्दूहरू उनलाई मच्छिन्द्रनाथ भन्छन्। रातो भनेको उनको मूर्तिको रङ। उनले मनसुनको वर्षा ल्याउँछन् भन्ने विश्वास छ। हरेक वर्ष रातो मच्छिन्द्रनाथ जात्रामा उनको मूर्ति यही मन्दिरबाट निस्कन्छ। पुल्चोकमा बनेको करिब ६० फिट अग्लो रथमा चढेर, गल्ली-गल्ली हुँदै जावलाखेलसम्मको एक महिना लामो यात्रा गर्छ। यो नेपालकै सबैभन्दा लामो रथजात्रा हो, र भोटो जात्राले यसको अन्त्य हुन्छ, जब रत्नजडित भोटो सबैले देख्ने गरी उचालिन्छ। देवताले आफ्नो वर्ष पाटन र बुङ्गमतीको अर्को घरमा बाँडेर बिताउँछन्। आँगनमा बिस्तारै घुम्नुहोस्, जहाँ हिन्दू र बौद्ध भक्ति साँच्चै भेट हुन्छन्।','बाह्र वर्षको खडेरीमा ऋषि गोरखनाथ वर्षा ल्याउने नागहरूमाथि ध्यान गरेर बसे। उनका गुरु मच्छिन्द्रनाथ आएपछि मात्र उनी उठ्न सक्थे, त्यसैले दूतहरूले मच्छिन्द्रनाथलाई उपत्यकामा ल्याए। गोरखनाथ उनलाई स्वागत गर्न उठे, नागहरू मुक्त भए, र वर्षा फर्कियो। ललितपुरका चलाख राजाले त्यसपछि देवतालाई आफ्नै सहरमा राखे। त्यसयता हरेक वर्ष पाटनका मानिस राम्रो वर्षाको प्रार्थना गर्दै उनको रथ गल्लीमा तान्छन्।','[\"अहिलेको मन्दिर सन् १६७३ को हो; यो ठाउँमा कम्तीमा सन् १४०८ देखि मन्दिर छ।\", \"रातो भनेको देवताको मूर्तिको रङ हो।\", \"उनको रथजात्रा नेपालकै सबैभन्दा लामो हो, र जावलाखेलमा भोटो जात्राले यसको अन्त्य हुन्छ।\", \"देवताले वर्षको करिब छ महिना बुङ्गमतीमा र बाँकी समय पाटनमा बिताउँछन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Rato Machhindranath Jatra\", \"note\": \"The god\'s tall chariot is pulled through Patan over several weeks\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"रातो मच्छिन्द्रनाथ जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"देवताको अग्लो रथ पाटनमा धेरै हप्तासम्म तानिन्छ\"}, {\"name\": \"Bhoto Jatra\", \"note\": \"Closing day of the chariot festival: the jewelled vest is shown at Jawalakhel\", \"month\": \"Jestha\", \"name_np\": \"भोटो जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"रथजात्राको अन्तिम दिन: जावलाखेलमा रत्नजडित भोटो देखाइन्छ\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur_02.jpg/1280px-Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur_02.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Rato Machhindranath Temple in Ta Bahal\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rato_Machhindranath_Temple,_Patan,_Lalitpur_02.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur_03.jpg/1280px-Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur_03.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Tiered roofs of Rato Machhindranath Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rato_Machhindranath_Temple,_Patan,_Lalitpur_03.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Tympanum_and_Lion_of_Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur_06.jpg/1280px-Tympanum_and_Lion_of_Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Patan%2C_Lalitpur_06.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Tympanum and stone lion at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tympanum_and_Lion_of_Rato_Machhindranath_Temple,_Patan,_Lalitpur_06.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Machhendre_bahal%2C_Patan.jpg/1280px-Rato_Machhindranath_Temple%2C_Machhendre_bahal%2C_Patan.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Rato Machhindranath Temple, Machhendra Bahal\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rato_Machhindranath_Temple,_Machhendre_bahal,_Patan.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Bungadyah_rath.jpg/1280px-Bungadyah_rath.jpg\", \"author\": \"Kamal Ratna Tuladhar\", \"caption\": \"Chariot (rath) of Bunga Dyah during the jatra\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bungadyah_rath.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"copper\", \"notes\": \"Three-roofed pagoda standing alone in a large open brick courtyard, guarded by stone lions, with pillars around it\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"lion-statues\", \"bell\", \"stone-pillar\", \"toran\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(107,'lagankhel-ashok-stupa','Lagankhel Ashok Stupa (Southern Stupa)','लगनखेल अशोक स्तूप','Lalitpur','Bagmati','Lalitpur',NULL,27.664924,85.323327,'stupa','Buddhist',NULL,NULL,'Traditionally attributed to Emperor Ashoka (c. 3rd century BCE); date unproven','unknown','Large grass-covered hemispherical brick-and-earth mound crowned by a small harmika and spire',0,'The largest of Patan\'s four Ashoka stupas, a grassy mound marking the old city\'s southern edge.','Climb the small rise just south of the Lagankhel bus park and you meet the largest of Patan\'s four Ashoka stupas. Local tradition says the Mauryan emperor Ashoka visited the valley around 249 BCE and raised four stupas at the cardinal points of the city: north, south, east and west. This is the southern one, known locally as Lagan Thura. Historians treat the Ashoka connection as tradition rather than proven fact, but the stupas are undeniably old. They were originally built from stacked bricks and over the centuries became grassy mounds, which is what you see here, crowned by a small spire. The historian Niels Gutschow suggests they marked the limits of the ancient town\'s sacred space. Because it sits on higher ground, this stupa has long dominated the local skyline. Walk clockwise around it, as Buddhists do, and look back toward the old city. Then imagine three more mounds like it standing guard at the other edges of ancient Yala.','Legend says Emperor Ashoka came to the Kathmandu Valley with his daughter Charumati and, to sanctify the city of Patan, raised four stupas at its cardinal points: north, south, east and west. The southern one at Lagankhel is the largest of the four, and together they are said to enclose the sacred city. Charumati is also linked by tradition to the Charumati Vihara at Chabahil in Kathmandu.','[\"It is the southern and largest of Patan\'s four stupas traditionally attributed to Emperor Ashoka.\", \"The Ashoka attribution (c. 249 BCE) is local tradition, not proven by archaeology.\", \"The stupas were originally brick and have become grassy mounds over time.\", \"The other three stand at Pulchowk (west), Ibahi (north) and Teta (east).\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,15,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Ashok_Stupa%2C_Lagankhel%2C_Patan3.jpg/1280px-Ashok_Stupa%2C_Lagankhel%2C_Patan3.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashok_Stupa,_Lagankhel,_Patan3.jpg','Shadow Ayush · CC BY-SA 4.0','stupa,buddhist,lalitpur,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/points-of-interest/lagan-southern-stupa/1508250\", \"https://archive.nepalitimes.com/news.php?id=1678\", \"https://english.onlinekhabar.com/biggest-stupas-in-kathmandu.html\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lalitpur,_Nepal\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/124177646\"]','पाटनका चार अशोक स्तूपमध्ये सबैभन्दा ठूलो, घाँसले ढाकिएको टिला, जसले पुरानो सहरको दक्षिणी सिमाना चिनाउँछ।','लगनखेल बस पार्कको ठीक दक्षिणको सानो उचाइमा चढ्नुहोस्, तपाईं पाटनका चारवटा अशोक स्तूपमध्ये सबैभन्दा ठूलो स्तूपमा पुग्नुहुन्छ। स्थानीय परम्परा अनुसार मौर्य सम्राट् अशोक करिब २४९ ईसा पूर्वमा उपत्यका आएका थिए, र सहरका चारै दिशामा, उत्तर, दक्षिण, पूर्व र पश्चिममा चारवटा स्तूप बनाएका थिए। यो दक्षिणको स्तूप हो, जसलाई स्थानीयले लगन थुरा भन्छन्। इतिहासकारहरू अशोकसँगको जोडाइलाई प्रमाणित तथ्य होइन, परम्परा मान्छन्। तर स्तूपहरू पक्कै पुराना छन्। यी सुरुमा थुपारिएका इँटाबाट बनेका थिए, र सयौँ वर्षमा घाँसले ढाकिएका टिला बने। तपाईंले यहाँ देख्ने यही हो, जसको टुप्पोमा सानो चुचुरो छ। इतिहासकार निल्स गुत्शोका अनुसार यिनले पुरानो सहरको पवित्र क्षेत्रको सिमाना चिनाउँथे। अग्लो ठाउँमा भएकाले यो स्तूप लामो समयदेखि वरपरको क्षितिजमा हावी छ। बौद्धहरूले जस्तै घडीको दिशामा यसको वरिपरि घुम्नुहोस्, र पुरानो सहरतिर फर्केर हेर्नुहोस्। अनि कल्पना गर्नुहोस्, यस्तै अरू तीनवटा टिला प्राचीन यलका अरू छेउमा पहरा दिइरहेका छन्।','भनिन्छ, सम्राट् अशोक आफ्नी छोरी चारुमतीसँग काठमाडौँ उपत्यका आए। पाटन सहरलाई पवित्र बनाउन उनले यसका चारै दिशामा, उत्तर, दक्षिण, पूर्व र पश्चिममा चारवटा स्तूप बनाए। लगनखेलको दक्षिणी स्तूप चारमध्ये सबैभन्दा ठूलो हो, र सबैले मिलेर पवित्र सहरलाई घेर्छन् भनिन्छ। परम्पराले चारुमतीलाई काठमाडौँको चाबहिलको चारुमती विहारसँग पनि जोड्छ।','[\"परम्परा अनुसार सम्राट् अशोकले बनाएको मानिने पाटनका चार स्तूपमध्ये यो दक्षिणको र सबैभन्दा ठूलो हो।\", \"अशोकसँगको जोडाइ (करिब २४९ ईसा पूर्व) स्थानीय परम्परा हो, पुरातत्त्वले प्रमाणित गरेको होइन।\", \"स्तूपहरू सुरुमा इँटाका थिए र समयसँगै घाँसले ढाकिएका टिला बनेका छन्।\", \"अरू तीनवटा पुल्चोक (पश्चिम), इबही (उत्तर) र तेता (पूर्व) मा छन्।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/LAGAN_THURA_-_SOUTHERN_STUPA.JPG/1280px-LAGAN_THURA_-_SOUTHERN_STUPA.JPG\", \"author\": \"Samir limbu\", \"caption\": \"Lagan Thur, the southern Ashok stupa\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LAGAN_THURA_-_SOUTHERN_STUPA.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Buddha_statue_of_ashok_stupa.JPG/1280px-Buddha_statue_of_ashok_stupa.JPG\", \"author\": \"Samir limbu\", \"caption\": \"Buddha statue at the Ashok stupa\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buddha_statue_of_ashok_stupa.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Ashok_Stupa.jpg/1280px-Ashok_Stupa.jpg\", \"author\": \"Dinesh 2016\", \"caption\": \"Grass-covered dome of the southern stupa\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashok_Stupa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Lagankhel_stupa%281%29.jpg/1280px-Lagankhel_stupa%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rai shreya\", \"caption\": \"Lagankhel stupa\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lagankhel_stupa(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Ashok_Stupa%2C_Lagankhel1.jpg/1280px-Ashok_Stupa%2C_Lagankhel1.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"Ashok Stupa, Lagankhel\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashok_Stupa,_Lagankhel1.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"stupa\", \"roof\": \"none\", \"notes\": \"Low wide grass-covered mound with a small white harmika and gilded spire, prayer flags, and a ring wall of prayer wheels\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#6b8e3a\", \"#c9a227\", \"#f5f2ea\"], \"features\": [\"harmika\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"prayer-flags\", \"prayer-wheels\", \"chaityas\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [30, 30], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"city-street\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(108,'guhyeshwari-temple','Guhyeshwari Temple','गुह्येश्वरी मन्दिर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.711111,85.353333,'pagoda','Both','Guhyeshwari (Guhyakali); Vajravarahi for Buddhists',NULL,'Ancient Shakti pitha; main renovation by King Pratap Malla in the 17th century CE','Malla','Newar pagoda-style shrine in the middle of a walled courtyard, crowned by gilded serpent (naga) finials; the goddess is worshipped in a kalash over a sacred spring',0,'A Shakti pitha by the Bagmati, about 1 km east of Pashupatinath, sacred to Hindu and Buddhist tantric worshippers.','Follow the Bagmati upstream from Pashupatinath for about a kilometre and you reach one of the most secret shrines in the valley. Guhyeshwari takes its name from the Sanskrit words guhya, hidden, and ishwari, goddess. Hindu texts say this is where a part of the goddess Sati\'s body fell when grieving Shiva carried her across the world, so it counts as a Shakti pitha, a seat of the mother goddess. Many people see Guhyeshwari as the consort of Pashupati, and pilgrims often visit both together. There is no ordinary statue at the centre. Instead, the goddess is worshipped in a sacred water jar, a kalash, covered in silver and gold, over a spring. Look up and you will see gilded serpents rising over the roof. Buddhists honour the same place as Vajravarahi. King Pratap Malla renovated the temple in the 17th century, and during Navaratri the courtyard is packed with worshippers.','When Sati gave up her life after her father Daksha insulted Shiva, the grieving god wandered the world carrying her body. Parts of it fell to earth in different places, and each became a Shakti pitha. Tradition holds that the secret part of Sati fell here on the bank of the Bagmati, which is why the goddess is called Guhyeshwari, the hidden goddess.','[\"The name comes from the Sanskrit guhya (secret or hidden) and ishwari (goddess).\", \"It lies about 1 km east of the Pashupati area, on the southern bank of the Bagmati.\", \"King Pratap Malla renovated the temple in the 17th century.\", \"Vajrayana Buddhists revere the site as sacred to Vajravarahi.\", \"Daily tantric rites are performed by Newar Karmacharya priests.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Pashupatinath-oberer_Zugang-10-Guhyeshvari-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Pashupatinath-oberer_Zugang-10-Guhyeshvari-2013-gje.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pashupatinath-oberer_Zugang-10-Guhyeshvari-2013-gje.jpg','Gerd Eichmann · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,both,malla,kathmandu,hindu,buddhist,legend,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guhyeshwari_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5615319\", \"https://www.nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/guhyeshwari-temple-a-sacred-shakti-peetha-in-kathmandu\", \"https://www.hopnepal.com/blog/guhyeshwari-temple-kathmandu-nepal\"]','बागमतीको किनारमा पशुपतिनाथभन्दा करिब १ किमी पूर्वमा रहेको शक्तिपीठ, जुन हिन्दू र बौद्ध दुवै तान्त्रिक साधकका लागि पवित्र छ।','पशुपतिनाथबाट बागमतीको किनारै किनार करिब एक किलोमिटर माथि जानुहोस्, तपाईं उपत्यकाको सबैभन्दा गोप्य मन्दिरमध्ये एउटामा पुग्नुहुन्छ। गुह्येश्वरी नाम संस्कृतका गुह्य अर्थात् गोप्य र ईश्वरी अर्थात् देवीबाट आएको हो। हिन्दू ग्रन्थअनुसार शोकमा डुबेका शिवले सतीको शरीर बोकेर संसार घुम्दा उनको एक अङ्ग यहीँ खसेको थियो, त्यसैले यो शक्तिपीठ, अर्थात् माता देवीको आसन मानिन्छ। धेरैले गुह्येश्वरीलाई पशुपतिकी सहचरी मान्छन्, र भक्तजन प्रायः दुवैको दर्शन सँगै गर्छन्। यहाँ बीचमा साधारण मूर्ति छैन। देवीलाई मूलमाथि राखिएको, चाँदी र सुनले मोडिएको पवित्र जलको कलशमा पूजा गरिन्छ। माथि हेर्नुहोस्, छानामाथि सुनौला सर्प उठेका देख्नुहुनेछ। बौद्धहरू यही ठाउँलाई वज्रवाराहीका रूपमा मान्छन्। राजा प्रताप मल्लले १७औँ शताब्दीमा मन्दिर जीर्णोद्धार गरे, र नवरात्रिमा आँगन भक्तजनले भरिन्छ।','पिता दक्षले शिवको अपमान गरेपछि सतीले प्राण त्यागिन्, अनि शोकमा डुबेका शिव उनको शरीर बोकेर संसारभर डुल्न थाले। शरीरका अङ्गहरू फरक फरक ठाउँमा खसे, र ती हरेक ठाउँ शक्तिपीठ बने। परम्पराअनुसार सतीको गोप्य अङ्ग बागमतीको किनारमा यहीँ खस्यो, त्यसैले देवीलाई गुह्येश्वरी, अर्थात् गोप्य देवी भनिन्छ।','[\"गुह्येश्वरी नाम संस्कृतका गुह्य (गोप्य वा लुकेको) र ईश्वरी (देवी) बाट बनेको हो।\", \"यो पशुपति क्षेत्रभन्दा करिब १ किमी पूर्वमा, बागमतीको दक्षिणी किनारमा छ।\", \"राजा प्रताप मल्लले १७औँ शताब्दीमा मन्दिर जीर्णोद्धार गरे।\", \"वज्रयान बौद्धहरू यो ठाउँलाई वज्रवाराहीको पवित्र स्थल मान्छन्।\", \"नेवार कर्माचार्य पुजारीहरूले यहाँ दैनिक तान्त्रिक पूजा गर्छन्।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Navaratri (Dashain)\", \"note\": \"The courtyard is crowded with worshippers during the nine nights of the goddess\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"नवरात्रि (दशैँ)\", \"note_np\": \"देवीका नौ रातमा आँगन भक्तजनले भरिन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Guhyeshwari Temple on the bank of the Bagmati\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The temple compound and its gateway\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(2).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%2810%29.jpg/1280px-Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%2810%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Guhyeshwari Temple, Pashupati area\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guhyeshwari_Temple_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(10).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Pashupatinath-oberer_Zugang-12-Votivstupas_bei_Guhyeshvari-2013-gje.jpg/1280px-Pashupatinath-oberer_Zugang-12-Votivstupas_bei_Guhyeshvari-2013-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Votive shrines near Guhyeshwari, 2013\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pashupatinath-oberer_Zugang-12-Votivstupas_bei_Guhyeshvari-2013-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Gaurighat_Guheshwori_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Gaurighat_Guheshwori_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Gauri Ghat on the Bagmati beside the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaurighat_Guheshwori_Pashupatinath_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Walled courtyard by the Bagmati; the central shrine has a gilded roof topped by four rising golden serpents\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"whitewashed-stone\", \"colors\": [\"#c9a227\", \"#f4f1ea\", \"#8b3a2b\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"bell\", \"lamps-diyo\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [20, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"river\", \"riverbank-ghats\", \"sacred-grove\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(109,'gokarneshwor-mahadev','Gokarneshwor Mahadev Temple','गोकर्णेश्वर महादेव मन्दिर','Gokarneshwor','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.739444,85.387778,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva (Gokarneshwor)',1582,'Present temple dates from 1582 CE; the site is believed to be older','Malla','Three-roofed Newar pagoda beside the Bagmati, with a Shiva linga in the sanctum and a large collection of stone statues around it',0,'A three-roofed Shiva temple on the Bagmati, famous for its statues and for Gokarna Aunsi, the Nepali Father\'s Day.','You are on the bank of the Bagmati, north-east of Boudhanath, where the river runs cleaner and greener than in the city. In front of you rises the three-roofed temple of Gokarneshwor Mahadev, the Lord of Gokarna. The present temple took its form in 1582, but people believe worship here is far older. Inside the sanctum is a Shiva linga, yet what makes Gokarna special is all around you. Walk slowly through the courtyard and look at the stone figures: Durga, Ganesh, Hanuman, Krishna, Indra riding his elephant, and a reclining Narayan. Behind the temple sits a patient Nandi bull. Every year, on the new moon of Bhadra, this quiet place fills with families. It is Gokarna Aunsi, the day Nepalis honour their fathers. Those whose fathers have died come to bathe in the river and make offerings for them. Down at the ghats, please be respectful: cremations still take place here.','One telling says the name Gokarna, cow\'s ear, comes from the shape of the land here. Another tradition links the place to a story in the Nepal Mahatmya, in which Brahma consecrated a great linga of Shiva at this spot. Gokarneshwor municipality itself notes there is no firm evidence for why the area is called Gokarna.','[\"The present three-roofed temple dates from 1582.\", \"The courtyard is known for its many stone sculptures, including Indra on an elephant and a reclining Narayan.\", \"Gokarna Aunsi, Nepal\'s Father\'s Day, brings crowds here on the new moon of Bhadra.\", \"The temple complex escaped damage in the 2015 earthquake.\"]',NULL,NULL,100,NULL,NULL,45,'A travel guide reports that the temple complex escaped damage in the 2015 earthquake.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_01.jpg/1280px-Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_01.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_01.jpg','Nabin K. Sapkota · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,gokarneshwor,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gokarneshwor_Mahadev_temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1534467\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/342842416\", \"https://www.thelongestwayhome.com/travel-guides/nepal/gokarna/guide-to-gokarna.html\", \"https://info.gokarneshwormun.gov.np/tourist-places/6\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/exploring-nepals-oldest-gem-gokarneshwar-mahadev-temple\"]','बागमतीको किनारमा रहेको तीन छाने शिव मन्दिर, आफ्ना मूर्तिहरू र नेपालको बुवाको मुख हेर्ने दिन गोकर्ण औँसीका लागि प्रसिद्ध।','तपाईं बौद्धनाथको उत्तरपूर्वमा बागमतीको किनारमा हुनुहुन्छ, जहाँ नदी सहरभन्दा सफा र हरियो देखिन्छ। तपाईंको अगाडि गोकर्णका स्वामी गोकर्णेश्वर महादेवको तीन छाने मन्दिर उभिएको छ। अहिलेको मन्दिरले १५८२ मा यो रूप लिएको हो, तर यहाँ पूजा त्योभन्दा धेरै पहिलेदेखि हुन्थ्यो भन्ने विश्वास छ। गर्भगृहभित्र शिवलिङ्ग छ, तर गोकर्णलाई खास बनाउने कुरा तपाईंको वरपर छ। आँगनमा बिस्तारै हिँड्दै ढुङ्गाका मूर्तिहरू हेर्नुहोस्: दुर्गा, गणेश, हनुमान, कृष्ण, हात्तीमा सवार इन्द्र र पल्टिरहेका नारायण। मन्दिरको पछाडि धैर्यले बसेको नन्दी साँढे छ। हरेक वर्ष भाद्रको औँसीमा यो शान्त ठाउँ परिवारले भरिन्छ। त्यो गोकर्ण औँसी हो, नेपालीले आफ्ना बुवालाई सम्मान गर्ने दिन। बुवा गुमाएकाहरू नदीमा नुहाउन र बुवाका नाममा भेटी चढाउन आउँछन्। तल घाटमा कृपया आदरपूर्वक व्यवहार गर्नुहोस्, किनकि यहाँ अहिले पनि दाहसंस्कार हुन्छ।','एउटा भनाइअनुसार यहाँको जमिनको आकार गाईको कानजस्तो भएकाले गोकर्ण नाम पर्‍यो। अर्को परम्पराले यो ठाउँलाई नेपाल महात्म्यको एउटा कथासँग जोड्छ, जसमा ब्रह्माले यहीँ शिवको ठूलो लिङ्ग स्थापना गरेका थिए। गोकर्णेश्वर नगरपालिकाले भने यो इलाकालाई किन गोकर्ण भनिन्छ भन्ने कुनै पक्का प्रमाण नभएको बताएको छ।','[\"अहिलेको तीन छाने मन्दिर १५८२ को हो।\", \"आँगन हात्तीमा सवार इन्द्र र पल्टिरहेका नारायणजस्ता धेरै ढुङ्गाका मूर्तिका लागि प्रसिद्ध छ।\", \"भाद्रको औँसीमा पर्ने नेपालको बुवाको मुख हेर्ने दिन गोकर्ण औँसीमा यहाँ भीड लाग्छ।\", \"सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा मन्दिर परिसरमा क्षति पुगेन।\"]','एउटा यात्रा गाइडका अनुसार सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा मन्दिर परिसर क्षतिबाट जोगिएको थियो।','[{\"name\": \"Gokarna Aunsi (Kushe Aunsi)\", \"note\": \"Father\'s Day: people bathe in the Bagmati and make offerings for their fathers\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"गोकर्ण औँसी (कुशे औँसी)\", \"note_np\": \"बुवाको मुख हेर्ने दिन: मानिसहरू बागमतीमा नुहाउँछन् र बुवाका नाममा भेटी चढाउँछन्।\"}, {\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Shiva\'s great night draws devotees to the linga\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"शिवको महान् रातमा भक्तजन शिवलिङ्गको दर्शन गर्न आउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/03_Gokarnashwar_Mahadev_Temple%2C_Gokarna%2C_Kathmandu.jpg/1280px-03_Gokarnashwar_Mahadev_Temple%2C_Gokarna%2C_Kathmandu.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Eastern side of the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:03_Gokarnashwar_Mahadev_Temple,_Gokarna,_Kathmandu.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_05.jpg/1280px-Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_05.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Gokarna Mahadev temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_05.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_09.jpg/1280px-Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_09.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Stone sculptures in the temple grounds\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_09.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_2017_01.jpg/1280px-Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_2017_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Gokarna Mahadev temple in 2017\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_2017_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_2017_05.jpg/1280px-Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_2017_05.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nabin K. Sapkota\", \"caption\": \"Temple grounds in 2017\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gokarna_Mahadev_Temple_2017_05.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Tall three-roofed pagoda by the Bagmati ghats, surrounded by many stone god statues, with a Nandi bull behind\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#4a3020\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"nandi-bull\", \"idol-visible\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [15, 15], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"river\", \"riverbank-ghats\", \"brick-courtyard\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(110,'charumati-stupa','Charumati Stupa','चारुमती विहार','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.715894,85.345872,'stupa','Buddhist','Buddha',NULL,'Tradition: built by Charumati, daughter of Emperor Ashoka, 3rd century BCE; Licchavi-era renovation c. 5th century CE','Licchavi','White hemispherical stupa with painted Buddha eyes on the harmika and a gilded spire, ringed by small votive chaityas and images',0,'An ancient Chabahil stupa traditionally credited to Charumati, daughter of the Indian emperor Ashoka.','Step off the busy Chabahil road and you find a white stupa that may be one of the oldest in the valley. Local tradition says it was built by Charumati, a daughter of the Indian emperor Ashoka, who married a Nepali prince named Devapala and settled here. Later she became a Buddhist nun, and the neighbourhood of Chabahil grew around her vihara. Look up at the painted eyes of the Buddha watching all four directions, and then down at the small chaityas, stupas and stone images clustered around the base. Some of them date from the Licchavi period. For a long time the link with Charumati was only a story. Then, during restoration work begun in 2002, a brick bearing her name was reportedly found, along with old coins, seals and small bronze images. Archaeologists say the connection still needs confirming. The stupa was repaired again after the 2015 earthquake.','Tradition says Emperor Ashoka came on pilgrimage to the Kathmandu Valley with his daughter Charumati. She married Devapala, a local prince, and stayed behind. In later life she became a nun and built this stupa and a vihara, around which the settlement of Chabahil grew.','[\"It is also known as Chabahil Stupa and Dhando Chaitya.\", \"Tradition credits Charumati, a daughter of Emperor Ashoka, with building it.\", \"Restoration began on 17 November 2002 after the stupa began to crack.\", \"A brick inscribed with Charumati\'s name was reportedly found during the restoration; archaeologists call the link unconfirmed.\", \"The stupa was restored again after the April 2015 earthquake.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,20,'The stupa was damaged and restored again after the April 2015 earthquake.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Charumati_Stupa.JPG/1280px-Charumati_Stupa.JPG','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charumati_Stupa.JPG','Nabin K. Sapkota · CC BY-SA 4.0','stupa,buddhist,licchavi,kathmandu,legend,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charumati_Stupa\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charumati\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q30174256\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/194280472\", \"https://nepalitimes.com/a-monument-to-an-indian-princess\", \"https://thingsasian.com/node/1203.html\", \"https://ecs.com.np/features/charumati-the-princess-and-the-stupa\"]','चाबहिलको प्राचीन स्तूप, परम्पराले जसलाई भारतीय सम्राट अशोककी छोरी चारुमतीले बनाएकी भन्छ।','व्यस्त चाबहिल सडकबाट अलि भित्र पस्नुहोस्, उपत्यकाकै सबैभन्दा पुरानो स्तूपमध्ये एक हुन सक्ने सेतो स्तूप भेट्नुहुन्छ। स्थानीय परम्पराअनुसार यो भारतीय सम्राट अशोककी छोरी चारुमतीले बनाएकी हुन्। उनले देवपाल नाम गरेका नेपाली राजकुमारसँग विवाह गरिन् र यहीँ बसिन्। पछि उनी बौद्ध भिक्षुणी भइन्, र उनको विहारको वरिपरि चाबहिल बस्ती बस्दै गयो। चारै दिशातिर हेर्ने बुद्धका रङ्गीन आँखा हेर्नुहोस्, अनि फेदमा जम्मा भएका साना चैत्य, स्तूप र ढुङ्गाका मूर्तितिर तल हेर्नुहोस्। तीमध्ये केही लिच्छविकालका हुन्। धेरै समयसम्म चारुमतीसँगको सम्बन्ध कथा मात्र थियो। त्यसपछि सन् २००२ मा सुरु भएको जीर्णोद्धारमा उनको नाम लेखिएको इँटा, साथै पुराना सिक्का, छाप र साना काँसाका मूर्ति भेटिएको भनिन्छ। पुरातत्त्वविद्हरू भने यो सम्बन्ध अझै पुष्टि हुनुपर्छ भन्छन्। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पपछि स्तूप फेरि मर्मत गरियो।','परम्पराअनुसार सम्राट अशोक आफ्नी छोरी चारुमतीसँग काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाको तीर्थयात्रामा आएका थिए। चारुमतीले यहाँका राजकुमार देवपालसँग विवाह गरिन् र यहीँ बसिन्। पछि उनी भिक्षुणी भइन् र यो स्तूप र एउटा विहार बनाइन्, जसको वरिपरि चाबहिल बस्ती बस्दै गयो।','[\"यसलाई चाबहिल स्तूप र ढन्दो चैत्य पनि भनिन्छ।\", \"परम्पराले यो स्तूप बनाउने श्रेय सम्राट अशोककी छोरी चारुमतीलाई दिन्छ।\", \"स्तूपमा चिरा पर्न थालेपछि सन् २००२ नोभेम्बर १७ मा जीर्णोद्धार सुरु भयो।\", \"जीर्णोद्धारका बेला चारुमतीको नाम लेखिएको इँटा भेटिएको भनिन्छ; पुरातत्त्वविद्हरू यो सम्बन्ध पुष्टि भएको छैन भन्छन्।\", \"सन् २०१५ को अप्रिलको भूकम्पपछि स्तूप फेरि जीर्णोद्धार गरियो।\"]','सन् २०१५ को अप्रिलको भूकम्पले स्तूपमा क्षति पुर्‍यायो, र त्यसपछि यसलाई फेरि जीर्णोद्धार गरियो।','[{\"name\": \"Buddha Jayanti\", \"note\": \"Buddha\'s birthday; devotees circle the stupa and light butter lamps\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"बुद्ध जयन्ती\", \"note_np\": \"बुद्धको जन्मदिन; भक्तजन स्तूप परिक्रमा गर्छन् र घिउका बत्ती बाल्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Chabahil_Stupa_eyes_%2801%29.jpg/1280px-Chabahil_Stupa_eyes_%2801%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Christopher J. Fynn\", \"caption\": \"Buddha\'s eyes on the harmika\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chabahil_Stupa_eyes_(01).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Chabahil_Stupa_top.jpg/1280px-Chabahil_Stupa_top.jpg\", \"author\": \"Christopher J. Fynn\", \"caption\": \"Top of the stupa and its spire\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chabahil_Stupa_top.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Charumati_Bihar%2C_Chabahil.jpg/1280px-Charumati_Bihar%2C_Chabahil.jpg\", \"author\": \"Anil Simkhada\", \"caption\": \"General view of Charumati Bihar, Chabahil\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charumati_Bihar,_Chabahil.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Charumati_Stupa_Image_01.jpg/1280px-Charumati_Stupa_Image_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"Charumati Stupa and the shrines around it\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charumati_Stupa_Image_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Chabahil.stupa.jpg/1280px-Chabahil.stupa.jpg\", \"author\": \"User:China_Crisis\", \"caption\": \"Chabahil stupa\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chabahil.stupa.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"stupa\", \"roof\": \"white-dome\", \"notes\": \"Mid-sized white dome with painted eyes and gilded spire, ringed by small stone chaityas, beside a busy city road\", \"tiers\": 1, \"walls\": \"white-plaster\", \"colors\": [\"#f4f1ea\", \"#c9a227\", \"#2b4c8c\"], \"features\": [\"dome-white\", \"harmika\", \"buddha-eyes\", \"gilded-pinnacle\", \"chaityas\", \"prayer-flags\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [20, 20], \"plinth_shape\": \"round\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"city-street\", \"newar-houses\", \"brick-courtyard\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(111,'bajrayogini-temple-sankhu','Bajrayogini Temple, Sankhu','बज्रयोगिनी मन्दिर','Sankhu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.743776,85.467231,'pagoda','Both','Vajrayogini (Ugratara)',NULL,'Main temple built under King Pratap Malla (17th century CE); site and inscriptions at Sankhu far older (538 CE)','Malla','Three-storey Newar pagoda in a hillside temple complex in pine forest, reached by a long stone stairway, rich in metalwork and carved wood',0,'A forest hilltop temple of the tantric goddess Vajrayogini above the old Newar town of Sankhu.','Climb the long stone stairway through the pine trees above Sankhu and you arrive at one of the holiest Newar Buddhist shrines in the valley. This is the temple of Vajrayogini, a tantric goddess also worshipped by Hindus. The main three-storey temple was built under King Pratap Malla, but this hillside was sacred long before. Legend says Vajrayogini once drained a lake from the Sankhu valley with her curved knife, then told King Sankhadev to build a town in the shape of a conch shell. The oldest inscription in Sankhu, from 538 CE, supports this story. Look around you: there is gilded metalwork, carved wood, an old stone water spout, and caves where famous Tibetan yogis are said to have meditated. Inside, the goddess has a red face and three eyes. The 2015 earthquake left the main temple unsafe, so it was propped up and restored. Each spring her chariot comes down to Sankhu.','Long ago the Sankhu valley was a lake. The goddess Vajrayogini cut through the hills with her curved knife and let the water drain away. She then appeared to the priest Jogdev and told King Sankhadev to build a town shaped like a conch shell, sankha, which is how Sankhu got its name.','[\"The main temple is a three-storey building attributed to King Pratap Malla.\", \"The oldest inscription in Sankhu dates to 538 CE.\", \"The site is on Nepal\'s UNESCO tentative list as \\\"Vajrayogini and early settlement of Sankhu\\\".\", \"Caves near the temple are linked to the Tibetan masters Marpa and Milarepa.\", \"The temple was declared unsafe after the 2015 earthquake and its statues were moved for safety during repairs.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,90,'The 2015 earthquake left the temple unsafe; statues were moved for safekeeping, the structure was propped with timber, and it was later restored.','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Bajrayogini_Temple_at_Bajrayogini.jpg/1280px-Bajrayogini_Temple_at_Bajrayogini.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bajrayogini_Temple_at_Bajrayogini.jpg','Mero Raja · CC BY-SA 3.0','pagoda,both,malla,sankhu,hindu,buddhist,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bajrayogini_Temple\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sankhu\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4848945\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/235411212\", \"https://whc.unesco.org/en/tentativelists/\"]','साँखुको पुरानो नेवार सहरमाथि, जङ्गलभित्रको डाँडामा रहेको तान्त्रिक देवी वज्रयोगिनीको मन्दिर।','साँखुमाथि चीडका रुखबीचको ढुङ्गाको लामो भर्‍याङ उक्लनुहोस्, तपाईं उपत्यकाका सबैभन्दा पवित्र नेवार बौद्ध मन्दिरमध्ये एउटामा पुग्नुहुन्छ। यो तान्त्रिक देवी वज्रयोगिनीको मन्दिर हो, जसलाई हिन्दूहरू पनि पूजा गर्छन्। मुख्य तीन तले मन्दिर राजा प्रताप मल्लको पालामा बनेको हो, तर यो डाँडा त्योभन्दा धेरै अघिदेखि पवित्र थियो। कथाअनुसार वज्रयोगिनीले आफ्नो बाङ्गो खुकुरीले साँखु उपत्यकाको ताल बगाइदिइन्, अनि राजा शङ्खदेवलाई शङ्खको आकारमा सहर बसाउन भनिन्। साँखुको सबैभन्दा पुरानो शिलालेख, सन् ५३८ को, यो कथालाई बलियो बनाउँछ। वरिपरि हेर्नुहोस्: सुनले मोडिएको धातुको काम, कुँदिएको काठ, पुरानो ढुङ्गाको धारा, र प्रसिद्ध तिब्बती योगीहरूले ध्यान गरेका भनिने गुफाहरू छन्। भित्र देवीको अनुहार रातो छ र तीन आँखा छन्। सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले मुख्य मन्दिर असुरक्षित बनायो, त्यसैले यसलाई टेको लगाइयो र पछि जीर्णोद्धार गरियो। हरेक वसन्तमा देवीको रथ साँखुमा झारिन्छ।','धेरै पहिले साँखु उपत्यका ताल थियो। देवी वज्रयोगिनीले आफ्नो बाङ्गो खुकुरीले पहाड काटेर पानी बगाइदिइन्। त्यसपछि उनी पुजारी जोगदेवको सामु देखा परिन् र राजा शङ्खदेवलाई शङ्ख (सङ्खा) को आकारमा सहर बसाउन भनिन्। यसरी साँखुले आफ्नो नाम पायो।','[\"मुख्य मन्दिर राजा प्रताप मल्लले बनाएको मानिने तीन तले भवन हो।\", \"साँखुको सबैभन्दा पुरानो शिलालेख सन् ५३८ को हो।\", \"नेपालको युनेस्को सम्भावित सूचीमा यो स्थल \\\"वज्रयोगिनी र साँखुको सुरुवाती बस्ती\\\" नामले राखिएको छ।\", \"मन्दिरनजिकका गुफाहरू तिब्बती गुरु मारपा र मिलारेपासँग जोडिएका छन्।\", \"सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पपछि मन्दिर असुरक्षित घोषणा गरियो र मर्मतका बेला मूर्तिहरू सुरक्षाका लागि अन्त सारिए।\"]','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पले मन्दिरलाई असुरक्षित बनायो; मूर्तिहरू सुरक्षाका लागि सारिए, संरचनालाई काठले टेको लगाइयो, र पछि जीर्णोद्धार गरियो।','[{\"name\": \"Bajrayogini Jatra\", \"note\": \"Nine-day festival; the goddess is carried down to Sankhu in a chariot\", \"month\": \"Chaitra\", \"name_np\": \"बज्रयोगिनी जात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"नौ दिने जात्रा; देवीलाई रथमा राखेर साँखु सहरमा ल्याइन्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Swasthani Brata (Madhav Narayan)\", \"note\": \"Month-long fast and worship of Madhav Narayan in Sankhu town, Poush to Magh full moon\", \"month\": \"Magh\", \"name_np\": \"स्वस्थानी व्रत (माधव नारायण)\", \"note_np\": \"साँखु सहरमा पौषदेखि माघ पूर्णिमासम्म एक महिनाभर उपवास बस्ने र माधव नारायणको पूजा गर्ने चलन छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/2015.07.16_Sankhu_94_Bajrayogini_Temple_View.jpg/1280px-2015.07.16_Sankhu_94_Bajrayogini_Temple_View.jpg\", \"author\": \"Drdonnayates\", \"caption\": \"The temple complex, July 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2015.07.16_Sankhu_94_Bajrayogini_Temple_View.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/2015.07.16_Sankhu_118_Bajrayogini_Temple_tops_and_pines.jpg/1280px-2015.07.16_Sankhu_118_Bajrayogini_Temple_tops_and_pines.jpg\", \"author\": \"Drdonnayates\", \"caption\": \"Temple roofs among the pine forest, 2015\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2015.07.16_Sankhu_118_Bajrayogini_Temple_tops_and_pines.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Sankhu_Vajarayogini_temple_under_restoration_13-04-2018.jpg/1280px-Sankhu_Vajarayogini_temple_under_restoration_13-04-2018.jpg\", \"author\": \"Christopher J. Fynn\", \"caption\": \"The main temple under restoration, April 2018\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sankhu_Vajarayogini_temple_under_restoration_13-04-2018.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Sankhu_Vajarayogini_and_Jogeshvara_temples13-04-2018.jpg/1280px-Sankhu_Vajarayogini_and_Jogeshvara_temples13-04-2018.jpg\", \"author\": \"Christopher J. Fynn\", \"caption\": \"Vajrayogini and Jogeshvara temples, 2018\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sankhu_Vajarayogini_and_Jogeshvara_temples13-04-2018.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/FlowerStoneMandala.jpg/1280px-FlowerStoneMandala.jpg\", \"author\": \"RobV\", \"caption\": \"Stone flower mandala at the temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FlowerStoneMandala.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"gilded-copper\", \"notes\": \"Three-roofed gilded pagoda in a small courtyard among pine trees, at the top of a long stone stairway\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#c9a227\", \"#3d5a3a\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"toran\", \"golden-door\", \"bell\", \"chaityas\", \"water-spouts\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [15, 15], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"forest\", \"brick-courtyard\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(112,'doleshwor-mahadev','Doleshwor Mahadev','डोलेश्वर महादेव','Suryabinayak','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.638889,85.438056,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva (as the head of Kedarnath)',NULL,'Said to be first built in the 12th century CE; renovated by King Bhupatindra Malla of Bhaktapur; tradition claims far greater age','Malla','Pagoda-style Shiva temple with a large linga, part of a cluster of five shrines in the village of Sipadol',0,'A Sipadol Shiva temple believed by many pilgrims to hold the head of the bull whose body is worshipped at Kedarnath.','You have come to the quiet village of Sipadol, south of Suryabinayak in Bhaktapur district. This modest pagoda is Doleshwor Mahadev, and many pilgrims believe it is linked to Kedarnath in India. Here is the story. After the Mahabharata war, the five Pandava brothers wanted Shiva\'s forgiveness, but Shiva hid from them in the form of a bull. When Bhima grabbed the animal, its head sank into the ground. The body is worshipped at Kedarnath, and the head, people say, appeared here. In 2009 the head priest of Kedarnath publicly declared Doleshwor to be the head of Kedarnath, and pilgrim numbers grew quickly. Historians are more cautious: the temple is said to have been built in the 12th century and renovated by King Bhupatindra Malla. Inside is a large Shiva linga. Come on Shivaratri or in Shrawan and you will find the village crowded with devotees.','After the Kurukshetra war, the Pandavas sought Shiva to atone for the killing. Shiva turned himself into a bull to avoid them. Bhima recognised him and caught hold of the bull, and its head sank into the earth. The hump stayed at Kedarnath, while the head is believed to have emerged at Doleshwor.','[\"It stands in Sipadol, Suryabinayak Municipality, Bhaktapur district.\", \"In 2009 the head priest of Kedarnath declared Doleshwor to be the head of Kedarnath.\", \"Sources say it was first built in the 12th century and renovated by King Bhupatindra Malla.\", \"A stone inscription on the premises is reported to be written in Kannada.\", \"Shivaratri and the month of Shrawan draw the biggest crowds.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Doleshwor_Mahadev_Temple_01.jpg/1280px-Doleshwor_Mahadev_Temple_01.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doleshwor_Mahadev_Temple_01.jpg','Prabina Karki · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,suryabinayak,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doleshwor_Mahadeva_Temple\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5288959\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/6397585285\", \"https://myrepublica.nagariknetwork.com/index.php/news/rediscovering-doleshwor-mahadev\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/doleshwor-mahadev-nepals-sacred-head-of-kedarnath\"]','सिपाडोलको शिव मन्दिर, जहाँ धेरै तीर्थयात्रीले केदारनाथमा पूजिने साँढेको टाउको रहेको विश्वास गर्छन्।','तपाईं भक्तपुर जिल्लाको सूर्यविनायकको दक्षिणमा रहेको शान्त गाउँ सिपाडोलमा आइपुग्नुभएको छ। यो साधारण पगोडा डोलेश्वर महादेव हो, र धेरै तीर्थयात्री यसलाई भारतको केदारनाथसँग जोडेर हेर्छन्। कथा यस्तो छ। महाभारत युद्धपछि पाँच पाण्डव दाजुभाइले शिवसँग क्षमा माग्न चाहे, तर शिव साँढे बनेर तिनीहरूबाट लुके। भीमले त्यो साँढेलाई समात्दा त्यसको टाउको जमिनमा गाडियो। धड केदारनाथमा पूजिन्छ, र टाउको चाहिँ यहाँ प्रकट भयो भन्ने मानिसहरूको विश्वास छ। सन् २००९ मा केदारनाथका मुख्य पुजारीले डोलेश्वर नै केदारनाथको टाउको हो भनी सार्वजनिक रूपमा घोषणा गरे, र त्यसपछि तीर्थयात्री छिटो बढे। इतिहासकारहरू भने अलि होसियार छन्: मन्दिर १२औँ शताब्दीमा बनेको र राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले जीर्णोद्धार गरेको भनिन्छ। भित्र ठूलो शिवलिङ्ग छ। शिवरात्रि वा श्रावणमा आउनुभयो भने गाउँ भक्तजनले भरिएको भेट्नुहुन्छ।','कुरुक्षेत्र युद्धपछि पाण्डवहरूले हत्याको प्रायश्चित्त गर्न शिवलाई खोजे। शिवले तिनीहरूबाट बच्न आफूलाई साँढे बनाए। भीमले उनलाई चिनेर साँढेलाई समाते, र साँढेको टाउको जमिनमा गाडियो। कुम केदारनाथमै रह्यो, र टाउको चाहिँ डोलेश्वरमा देखा परेको विश्वास गरिन्छ।','[\"यो भक्तपुर जिल्लाको सूर्यविनायक नगरपालिकाभित्र सिपाडोलमा पर्छ।\", \"सन् २००९ मा केदारनाथका मुख्य पुजारीले डोलेश्वरलाई केदारनाथको टाउको भनी घोषणा गरे।\", \"स्रोतहरूका अनुसार यो १२औँ शताब्दीमा पहिलो पटक बनेको थियो र राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले जीर्णोद्धार गरे।\", \"परिसरमा रहेको ढुङ्गाको शिलालेख कन्नड भाषामा लेखिएको भन्ने जानकारी छ।\", \"शिवरात्रि र श्रावण महिनामा सबैभन्दा बढी भीड हुन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Maha Shivaratri\", \"note\": \"Shiva\'s great night brings large crowds to Sipadol\", \"month\": \"Falgun\", \"name_np\": \"महाशिवरात्रि\", \"note_np\": \"शिवको महान् रातमा सिपाडोलमा ठूलो भीड लाग्छ।\"}, {\"name\": \"Shrawan month\", \"note\": \"Devotees offer milk and bel leaves to the linga, especially on Mondays\", \"month\": \"Shrawan\", \"name_np\": \"श्रावण महिना\", \"note_np\": \"भक्तजनले विशेषगरी सोमबार शिवलिङ्गमा दूध र बेलपत्र चढाउँछन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Doleshwor_Mahadeva.jpg/1280px-Doleshwor_Mahadeva.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Bhatta\", \"caption\": \"Doleshwor Mahadev temple, Sipadol\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doleshwor_Mahadeva.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Doleshwor_Mahadeva3.jpg/1280px-Doleshwor_Mahadeva3.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Bhatta\", \"caption\": \"The temple and its courtyard\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doleshwor_Mahadeva3.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Doleshwor_Mahadeva6.jpg/1280px-Doleshwor_Mahadeva6.jpg\", \"author\": \"Janak Bhatta\", \"caption\": \"Doleshwor Mahadev, Bhaktapur\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doleshwor_Mahadeva6.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Doleshwor_Mahadev_Temple_04.jpg/1280px-Doleshwor_Mahadev_Temple_04.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prabina Karki\", \"caption\": \"Temple surroundings\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doleshwor_Mahadev_Temple_04.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Doleshor_Mahadev.jpg\", \"author\": \"Prabina Karki\", \"caption\": \"Doleshwor Mahadev\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doleshor_Mahadev.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Modest brick pagoda with a Shiva linga, among smaller shrines on a rural hillside of fields\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"shiva-lingam\", \"bell\", \"trident\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"village\", \"terraced-fields\", \"forest\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(113,'balkumari-temple-thimi','Balkumari Temple, Thimi','बालकुमारी मन्दिर, ठिमी','Madhyapur Thimi','Bagmati','Bhaktapur',NULL,27.675948,85.385314,'pagoda','Hindu','Balkumari',NULL,'17th century CE','Malla','Three-roofed Newar pagoda on a square base, with a peacock on a pillar in front and peacock figures at the roof corners; a Bhairav shrine stands in the compound',0,'Thimi\'s three-roofed goddess temple, where the vermilion-throwing Sindoor Jatra begins at Nepali New Year.','You are in the old Newar town of Thimi, between Kathmandu and Bhaktapur, standing before the temple of the goddess Balkumari. It is one of four Kumari temples in the Kathmandu Valley and dates from the 17th century. Look at the pillar in front of the temple: a metal peacock sits on top. The peacock is the goddess\'s vehicle, and more peacocks once decorated the corners of the roofs. Now imagine this square at Nepali New Year. During Sindoor Jatra, part of the Bisket festival, dozens of palanquins called khats arrive from Thimi and nearby villages, each carrying a god or goddess. Men spin them around the temple while the crowd throws clouds of red vermilion powder into the air, until the whole square glows orange-red. A local legend says the goddess came here from Lubhu, brought by a princess who fell in love with a Thimi merchant. In 2015 an old Bhairav idol was stolen from the temple.','A merchant from Thimi fell in love with a princess of Lubhu. When she became pregnant she asked him to take her home with him. He agreed, on condition that she bring the goddess Balkumari too. So the princess carried the goddess with her, and Balkumari\'s home moved from Lubhu to Thimi.','[\"It is one of four Kumari temples in the Kathmandu Valley.\", \"The temple dates from the 17th century and has three roofs on a square base.\", \"A pillar topped by a peacock, the goddess\'s vehicle, stands in front.\", \"Sindoor Jatra starts here at Nepali New Year, with vermilion thrown into the air.\", \"In 2015 a 17th-century Digu Bhairav idol was stolen from the temple.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Balkumari_temple_of_Thimi.jpg/1280px-Balkumari_temple_of_Thimi.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balkumari_temple_of_Thimi.jpg','Bipinpraja · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,madhyapur thimi,legend,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balkumari_temple,_Bhaktapur\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q106597868\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/10068876012\", \"https://www.bhaktapur.com/discover/balkumari-temple-of-thimi/\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madhyapur_Thimi\"]','ठिमीको तीन छाने देवी मन्दिर, जहाँबाट नेपाली नयाँ वर्षमा सिन्दुर उडाउने सिन्दुरे जात्रा सुरु हुन्छ।','तपाईं काठमाडौँ र भक्तपुरबीचको पुरानो नेवार सहर ठिमीमा, देवी बालकुमारीको मन्दिरअगाडि उभिनुभएको छ। यो काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाका चार कुमारी मन्दिरमध्ये एउटा हो र १७औँ शताब्दीको हो। मन्दिरअगाडिको खम्बा हेर्नुहोस्: माथि धातुको मयूर बसेको छ। मयूर देवीको वाहन हो, र एक समय छानाका कुनामा अझ धेरै मयूर सजाइएका थिए। अब नेपाली नयाँ वर्षमा यो चोक कस्तो हुन्छ, कल्पना गर्नुहोस्। बिस्केट पर्वको भाग सिन्दुरे जात्रामा ठिमी र वरपरका गाउँबाट खट भनिने दर्जनौँ पालकी आउँछन्, हरेकमा एक देवता वा देवी बसेका हुन्छन्। मानिसहरूले तिनलाई मन्दिरवरिपरि घुमाउँछन्, भीडले हावामा रातो सिन्दुर उडाउँछ, र सारा चोक सुन्तला-रातो हुन्छ। स्थानीय किंवदन्तीअनुसार ठिमीका एक व्यापारीसँग माया बसेकी राजकुमारीले लुभूबाट देवीलाई यहाँ ल्याइन्। सन् २०१५ मा मन्दिरबाट एउटा पुरानो भैरवको मूर्ति चोरी भयो।','ठिमीका एक व्यापारी लुभूकी राजकुमारीसँग प्रेममा परे। राजकुमारी गर्भवती भएपछि उनले आफूलाई पनि घर लैजान भनिन्। व्यापारी राजी भए, तर देवी बालकुमारीलाई पनि साथमा ल्याउनुपर्छ भन्ने सर्त राखे। त्यसैले राजकुमारीले देवीलाई साथै बोकेर ल्याइन्, र बालकुमारीको बास लुभूबाट ठिमी सर्‍यो।','[\"यो काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाका चार कुमारी मन्दिरमध्ये एउटा हो।\", \"मन्दिर १७औँ शताब्दीको हो र वर्गाकार आधारमाथि तीन छाना छन्।\", \"अगाडि देवीको वाहन मयूर राखिएको खम्बा छ।\", \"नेपाली नयाँ वर्षमा यहीँबाट सिन्दुरे जात्रा सुरु हुन्छ, जहाँ सिन्दुर हावामा उडाइन्छ।\", \"सन् २०१५ मा १७औँ शताब्दीको दिगु भैरवको मूर्ति मन्दिरबाट चोरी भयो।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Sindoor Jatra (Bisket)\", \"note\": \"On 2 Baisakh palanquins circle the temple amid clouds of vermilion powder\", \"month\": \"Baisakh\", \"name_np\": \"सिन्दुरे जात्रा (बिस्केट)\", \"note_np\": \"बैशाख २ गते सिन्दुरको बादलबीच पालकीहरूले मन्दिर परिक्रमा गर्छन्।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Sindur_Jatra%2C_Madhyapur_Thimi%2C_Bhaktapur.jpg/1280px-Sindur_Jatra%2C_Madhyapur_Thimi%2C_Bhaktapur.jpg\", \"author\": \"Shadow Ayush\", \"caption\": \"A khat carried around the temple at Sindoor Jatra\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sindur_Jatra,_Madhyapur_Thimi,_Bhaktapur.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Balkumari_Jatra_01.jpg/1280px-Balkumari_Jatra_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Proxodimec\", \"caption\": \"Oil lamps offered to Balkumari at her jatra\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balkumari_Jatra_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Sindoor_Jatra_01.jpg/1280px-Sindoor_Jatra_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Proxodimec\", \"caption\": \"Palanquins and vermilion powder at Sindoor Jatra\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sindoor_Jatra_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Balkumari_temple.jpg/1280px-Balkumari_temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Newamiccha\", \"caption\": \"Balkumari temple, Madhyapur Thimi\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balkumari_temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Three-roofed brick pagoda in a town square; a metal peacock on a pillar in front and peacocks at the roof corners\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"toran\", \"stone-pillar\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 12], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"brick-courtyard\", \"newar-houses\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:49'),(114,'sheshnarayan-temple','Sheshnarayan Temple','शेषनारायण मन्दिर','Pharping','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.616774,85.264238,'pagoda','Both','Vishnu (Narayan on the serpent Shesha)',NULL,'Site traditionally dated to the Licchavi period; present main temple 17th century CE','Licchavi','Pagoda-style Vishnu temple tucked under a rocky cliff, with sacred ponds, Licchavi-era stone sculptures and a cave shrine beside it',0,'One of the four Narayan temples guarding the valley, beneath a cliff near Pharping with ponds and a sacred cave.','Just before the old town of Pharping, the road passes a cliff of grey rock. At its foot lie still green ponds and a small temple of Vishnu. This is Sheshnarayan, one of four Narayan temples said to guard the Kathmandu Valley from the four directions; the others are Changu, Ichangu and Bishankhu Narayan. Tradition links all four to the Licchavi king Vishnugupta. The main temple you see today is from the 17th century, but look closely at the courtyard: some of the carved stone images are much older, from the Licchavi era. In the ponds, carp swim around half-sunk carvings, including an image of the sun god Aditya. Above you, steps climb to the Yangleshö cave, where Buddhists believe Guru Padmasambhava meditated. So Hindus and Buddhists share this quiet place. Local belief even says the holy Bagmati river begins its journey near here.','Local tradition says the Bagmati, Nepal\'s most sacred river, has one of its sources here. Buddhists also believe Guru Padmasambhava and his consort meditated in the small cave above the temple, now called Yangleshö.','[\"It is one of the four Narayan temples of the valley, with Changu, Ichangu and Bishankhu Narayan.\", \"Tradition says the four were built in the reign of the Licchavi king Vishnugupta.\", \"Lonely Planet dates the present main temple to the 17th century.\", \"Ponds with carp and half-submerged carvings, including an image of Aditya, surround it.\", \"Steps lead up to the Yangleshö cave, linked to Guru Padmasambhava.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,45,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Shesh_Narayan.jpg/1280px-Shesh_Narayan.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shesh_Narayan.jpg','Ksssshl · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,both,licchavi,pharping,hindu,buddhist,legend,water,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheshnarayan_Temple\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharping\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7495631\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/3395315042\", \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/around-the-kathmandu-valley/pharping/attractions/shesh-narayan-temple/a/poi-sig/1432633/357132\", \"https://nepaltraveller.com/sidetrack/embracing-the-tranquility-of-shesh-narayan-temple\"]','उपत्यकाको रक्षा गर्ने चार नारायण मन्दिरमध्ये एउटा; फर्पिङनजिकै चट्टानको फेदमा पोखरी र पवित्र गुफासहित।','फर्पिङको पुरानो सहर पुग्नुअघि सडक खैरो चट्टानको भिरछेउबाट गुज्रन्छ। त्यसको फेदमा शान्त हरिया पोखरी र विष्णुको सानो मन्दिर छ। यो शेषनारायण हो, काठमाडौँ उपत्यकाको चारै दिशामा रक्षा गर्छन् भनिने चार नारायण मन्दिरमध्ये एउटा; बाँकी तीन चाँगु, इचङ्गु र विशङ्खु नारायण हुन्। परम्पराले चारैलाई लिच्छवि राजा विष्णुगुप्तसँग जोड्छ। अहिलेको मुख्य मन्दिर १७औँ शताब्दीको हो, तर आँगनलाई ध्यान दिएर हेर्नुहोस्: कुँदिएका केही ढुङ्गाका मूर्ति धेरै पुराना, लिच्छविकालका छन्। पोखरीमा कार्प माछा आधा डुबेका कुँदाइहरूवरिपरि पौडिन्छन्, ती मध्ये सूर्य देवता आदित्यको मूर्ति पनि छ। माथि भर्‍याङले यङ्लेशो गुफासम्म पुर्‍याउँछ, जहाँ बौद्धहरू गुरु पद्मसम्भवले ध्यान गरेका थिए भन्ने विश्वास गर्छन्। यसरी हिन्दू र बौद्ध दुवै यो शान्त ठाउँ साझा गर्छन्। स्थानीय विश्वासअनुसार पवित्र बागमती नदीले यहीँनजिकबाट यात्रा सुरु गर्छ।','स्थानीय परम्पराअनुसार नेपालको सबैभन्दा पवित्र नदी बागमतीको एउटा मुहान यहीँ छ। बौद्धहरू मन्दिरमाथिको सानो गुफामा, जसलाई अहिले यङ्लेशो भनिन्छ, गुरु पद्मसम्भव र उनकी सहचरीले ध्यान गरेको पनि विश्वास गर्छन्।','[\"चाँगु, इचङ्गु र विशङ्खु नारायणसँगै यो उपत्यकाका चार नारायण मन्दिरमध्ये एउटा हो।\", \"परम्पराअनुसार चारै मन्दिर लिच्छवि राजा विष्णुगुप्तको पालामा बनेका थिए।\", \"लोनली प्लानेटले अहिलेको मुख्य मन्दिर १७औँ शताब्दीको भनेको छ।\", \"कार्प माछा भएका पोखरीमा आदित्यको मूर्तिसहित आधा डुबेका कुँदाइहरू छन्।\", \"भर्‍याङ चढेर गुरु पद्मसम्भवसँग जोडिएको यङ्लेशो गुफासम्म पुगिन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Pharping0882.JPG/1280px-Pharping0882.JPG\", \"author\": \"Sundar1\", \"caption\": \"Temple grounds below the cliff\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pharping0882.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Kunda_Seshnarayan_Temple_Pharping_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%289%29.jpg/1280px-Kunda_Seshnarayan_Temple_Pharping_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%289%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"The holy ponds at Sheshnarayan\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kunda_Seshnarayan_Temple_Pharping_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(9).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Religious_Cave_Cave_Sesh_Narayan_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Religious_Cave_Cave_Sesh_Narayan_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%281%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Cave shrine in the rock face\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Religious_Cave_Cave_Sesh_Narayan_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(1).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Pharping-Sheshnarayan-12-Hindu-Fest-Tempel-2007-gje.jpg/1280px-Pharping-Sheshnarayan-12-Hindu-Fest-Tempel-2007-gje.jpg\", \"author\": \"Gerd Eichmann\", \"caption\": \"Festival day at the temple, 2007\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pharping-Sheshnarayan-12-Hindu-Fest-Tempel-2007-gje.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Seshnarayan_Temple_Sesh_Narayan_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Seshnarayan_Temple_Sesh_Narayan_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_%282%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Rajesh Dhungana\", \"caption\": \"Sheshnarayan Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seshnarayan_Temple_Sesh_Narayan_Dachhinkali_Kathmandu_Nepal_Rajesh_Dhungana_(2).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Small pagoda pressed against a grey cliff face, with square green ponds in front and stairs up to a cave\", \"tiers\": 2, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#6e6e66\", \"#4f7b6b\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"idol-visible\", \"rock-face\", \"water-spouts\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [10, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 1, \"surroundings\": [\"pond\", \"cave-mouth\", \"forest\", \"village\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:50'),(115,'akash-bhairab-temple','Akash Bhairab Temple','आकाशभैरव मन्दिर','Kathmandu','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.706003,85.309427,'courtyard','Both','Akash Bhairav (identified with the Kirati king Yalambar)',NULL,'Date of present building unknown; the deity\'s head is said to have been dug up several hundred years ago','unknown','Multi-storey town temple on the west side of Indra Chowk, partly covered in brass sheets, with shops on the ground floor, brass lions at the door and the deity\'s mask upstairs',0,'The Indra Chowk temple of Akash Bhairav, whose great mask is brought out into the square for Indra Jatra.','Stand in busy Indra Chowk, among cloth sellers and scooters, and look at the building on the west side. Shops fill its ground floor, but two metal lions guard a doorway, and stairs lead up to the shrine of Akash Bhairav, the Bhairav of the sky. People here also call him Aju, the first king, and identify him with Yalambar, a legendary Kirati king of Nepal. His big blue face, with huge eyes and a crown of skulls and serpents, is said to have been dug up from the ground several hundred years ago. Most of the year you climb upstairs to see him. But during Indra Jatra, the great mask is carried out and enthroned in the square below, and crowds come with sweets, flowers and coins. Notice the small image on his head: Buddhists see the Buddha there and Hindus see Brahma, so everyone can worship him.','Legend says Akash Bhairav is Yalambar, a Kirati king who gained great power through tantric worship. When he set out to join the Mahabharata war, Krishna is said to have cut off his head to keep him out of the battle, and it flew through the sky and landed in Kathmandu. The mask is understood to represent that head.','[\"The temple stands on the west side of Indra Chowk in old Kathmandu.\", \"Akash Bhairav is identified with Yalambar, a legendary Kirati king.\", \"His mask is displayed in the square during the Indra Jatra festival.\", \"Two metal lions guard the entrance, and the ground floor is used by shops.\", \"In 2007 Nepal\'s state airline sacrificed two goats to Akash Bhairav, whose symbol appears on its planes.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,15,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Akash_Bhairav_Temple_01.jpg/1280px-Akash_Bhairav_Temple_01.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akash_Bhairav_Temple_01.jpg','Suraj Belbase · CC BY-SA 4.0','courtyard,both,kathmandu,hindu,buddhist,legend,palace,art,festival,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akash_Bhairav\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indra_Chowk\", \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4700324\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/136526480\", \"https://nepalitimes.com/a-victim-of-the-mahabharatta\"]','इन्द्रचोकको आकाशभैरवको मन्दिर, जसको ठूलो मुखुन्डो इन्द्रजात्रामा चोकमा ल्याइन्छ।','कपडा पसल र स्कुटरको भीडले भरिएको इन्द्रचोकमा उभिनुहोस्, र पश्चिमपट्टिको भवनतिर हेर्नुहोस्। भुइँतलामा पसलहरू छन्, तर ढोकामा दुईवटा धातुका सिंहले पहरा दिएका छन्, र भर्‍याङले माथि आकाशका भैरव, आकाशभैरवको मन्दिरसम्म पुर्‍याउँछ। यहाँका मानिसले उनलाई आजु, अर्थात् पहिलो राजा पनि भन्छन्, र नेपालका पौराणिक किराँती राजा यलम्बरसँग जोड्छन्। ठूला आँखा र खप्पर तथा सर्पको मुकुट भएको उनको ठूलो निलो अनुहार धेरै सय वर्षअघि जमिनबाट खनेर निकालिएको भनिन्छ। वर्षको धेरैजसो समय उनको दर्शन गर्न माथि चढ्नुपर्छ। तर इन्द्रजात्रामा ठूलो मुखुन्डो बाहिर ल्याइन्छ र तलको चोकमा स्थापना गरिन्छ, अनि मिठाई, फूल र सिक्का लिएर भीड आउँछ। उनको शिरमा भएको सानो मूर्ति हेर्नुहोस्: बौद्धहरू त्यहाँ बुद्ध देख्छन् र हिन्दूहरू ब्रह्मा, त्यसैले सबैले उनको पूजा गर्न सक्छन्।','कथाअनुसार आकाशभैरव यलम्बर हुन्, तान्त्रिक पूजाबाट ठूलो शक्ति पाएका किराँती राजा। उनी महाभारत युद्धमा भाग लिन निस्कँदा कृष्णले उनलाई युद्धबाट टाढै राख्न उनको टाउको काटिदिए भनिन्छ, र त्यो आकाशमा उडेर काठमाडौँमा खस्यो। मुखुन्डोले त्यही टाउकोलाई जनाउँछ भन्ने बुझिन्छ।','[\"मन्दिर पुरानो काठमाडौँको इन्द्रचोकको पश्चिमपट्टि छ।\", \"आकाशभैरवलाई पौराणिक किराँती राजा यलम्बरसँग जोडेर हेरिन्छ।\", \"इन्द्रजात्राको बेला उनको मुखुन्डो चोकमा राखिन्छ।\", \"प्रवेशद्वारमा दुईवटा धातुका सिंहले पहरा दिन्छन्, र भुइँतला पसलले चलाएका छन्।\", \"सन् २००७ मा नेपालको सरकारी वायुसेवाले आकाशभैरवलाई दुईवटा बोका बलि दियो, जसको चिह्न उसका जहाजमा देखिन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Indra Jatra\", \"note\": \"The great mask is enthroned in Indra Chowk and decorated for eight days\", \"month\": \"Bhadra\", \"name_np\": \"इन्द्रजात्रा\", \"note_np\": \"ठूलो मुखुन्डोलाई इन्द्रचोकमा स्थापना गरेर आठ दिनसम्म सजाइन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Aakash_bhairav.jpg/1280px-Aakash_bhairav.jpg\", \"author\": \"Manjari Shrestha\", \"caption\": \"Akash Bhairav displayed during Indra Jatra\", \"license\": \"CC BY 2.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aakash_bhairav.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Akash_Bhairav_Temple_Toran.jpg/1280px-Akash_Bhairav_Temple_Toran.jpg\", \"author\": \"Suraj Belbase\", \"caption\": \"The carved torana over the shrine\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akash_Bhairav_Temple_Toran.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Akash_Bhairav_Temple_%E2%80%93_Kathmandu_%E2%80%93_01.jpg/1280px-Akash_Bhairav_Temple_%E2%80%93_Kathmandu_%E2%80%93_01.jpg\", \"author\": \"Maesi64\", \"caption\": \"Akash Bhairav Temple near Indra Chowk\", \"license\": \"CC0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akash_Bhairav_Temple_%E2%80%93_Kathmandu_%E2%80%93_01.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Akash_Bhairab.JPG/1280px-Akash_Bhairab.JPG\", \"author\": \"Rabs003\", \"caption\": \"Akash Bhairab, Indra Chowk\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akash_Bhairab.JPG\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Akash_Bhairab_Temple-IMG_2965.jpg/1280px-Akash_Bhairab_Temple-IMG_2965.jpg\", \"author\": \"Bijaya2043\", \"caption\": \"Akash Bhairab Temple\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akash_Bhairab_Temple-IMG_2965.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"courtyard\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Brass-fronted three-storey building over shops in a market square; metal lions at the door, blue Bhairav mask upstairs\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#b08d57\", \"#2b4c8c\"], \"features\": [\"lion-statues\", \"carved-windows\", \"toran\", \"idol-visible\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [12, 10], \"plinth_shape\": \"rectangular\", \"plinth_steps\": 0, \"surroundings\": [\"market-houses\", \"city-street\", \"stone-paved-plaza\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:50'),(116,'uma-maheshwar-kirtipur','Uma Maheshwar Temple, Kirtipur','उमा महेश्वर मन्दिर, कीर्तिपुर','Kirtipur','Bagmati','Kathmandu',NULL,27.679948,85.274703,'pagoda','Hindu','Shiva and Parvati (Uma Maheshwar)',1655,'17th century CE (1655, Nepal Sambat 775, per Kirtipur Municipality)','Malla','Three-roofed Newar pagoda with jhingati tile roofs on a four-stage brick plinth, guarded by two stone elephants, at the highest point of Kirtipur',0,'A three-roofed Shiva-Parvati temple guarded by stone elephants at the hilltop of Kirtipur.','You have reached the highest point of Kirtipur, about 1,414 metres above sea level. Turn around first: on a clear day the whole Kathmandu Valley spreads below you, with Himalayan peaks such as Langtang and Gaurishankar on the horizon. Now face the temple. Locals call it Kwacho Dega, the temple on the hill. Its proper name, Uma Maheshwar, honours Shiva and his consort Parvati together. Kirtipur Municipality dates it to 1655. Climb the four brick plinths and you will pass two stone elephants guarding the entrance. Look up at the three tiled roofs, the twenty carved pillars and the metal banner hanging from the pinnacle down to the first roof. Inside are images of Shiva and Parvati, with Saraswati and Ganesh. Sources disagree about earthquakes: one says the temple once had four roofs and lost one in 1934; another says an earlier quake left it in ruins until its restoration.',NULL,'[\"It stands at the highest point of Kirtipur, about 1,414 m.\", \"Kirtipur Municipality dates its construction to 1655 (NS 775).\", \"Two stone elephants guard the entrance on the first plinth.\", \"It has three roofs of jhingati tiles on a four-stage brick plinth.\", \"Locals call it Kwacho Dega, and it offers views to Langtang and Gaurishankar.\"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,30,NULL,'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Uma_Maheshwar_Temple_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Uma_Maheshwar_Temple_%281%29.jpg','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uma_Maheshwar_Temple_(1).jpg','Nirmal Dulal · CC BY-SA 4.0','pagoda,hindu,malla,kirtipur,art,bagmati','[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirtipur\", \"https://kirtipurmun.gov.np/heritage/uma-maheshwor\", \"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/323644532\", \"https://nepalitimes.com/the-city-of-good-deeds\", \"https://honeyguideapps.com/blog/?p=1682\"]','कीर्तिपुरको डाँडाको टुप्पोमा ढुङ्गाका हात्तीले पहरा दिएको तीन छाने शिव-पार्वती मन्दिर।','तपाईं कीर्तिपुरको सबैभन्दा अग्लो ठाउँमा, समुद्र सतहभन्दा करिब १,४१४ मिटरमा पुग्नुभएको छ। पहिले पछाडि फर्केर हेर्नुहोस्: मौसम सफा भए पूरै काठमाडौँ उपत्यका तपाईंको मुनि फैलिएको देखिन्छ, क्षितिजमा लाङटाङ र गौरीशङ्करजस्ता हिमाली चुचुरासहित। अब मन्दिरतिर फर्कनुहोस्। स्थानीयले यसलाई क्वाछो देगः, अर्थात् डाँडामाथिको मन्दिर भन्छन्। यसको औपचारिक नाम उमा महेश्वरले शिव र उनकी सहचरी पार्वतीलाई सँगै सम्मान गर्छ। कीर्तिपुर नगरपालिकाले यसलाई सन् १६५५ को मान्छ। इँटाका चार तहको चौकी उक्लिँदा प्रवेशद्वारमा पहरा दिइरहेका दुईवटा ढुङ्गाका हात्ती भेट्नुहुन्छ। माथि हेर्नुहोस्: झिँगटीका तीन छाना, बीसवटा कुँदिएका खम्बा, र चुचुरोबाट पहिलो छानासम्म झुन्डिएको धातुको पताका। भित्र शिव र पार्वतीका मूर्ति छन्, साथमा सरस्वती र गणेशका पनि। भूकम्पबारे स्रोतहरू एकमत छैनन्: एउटाले मन्दिरमा कुनै बेला चार छाना थिए र सन् १९३४ मा एउटा गुम्यो भन्छ; अर्कोले अघिल्लो भूकम्पले यसलाई भग्नावशेष बनाएको थियो र पछि जीर्णोद्धार गरियो भन्छ।',NULL,'[\"यो कीर्तिपुरको सबैभन्दा अग्लो ठाउँमा, करिब १,४१४ मिटरमा छ।\", \"कीर्तिपुर नगरपालिकाले यो मन्दिर सन् १६५५ (ने.सं. ७७५) मा बनेको भन्छ।\", \"पहिलो चौकीमा दुईवटा ढुङ्गाका हात्तीले प्रवेशद्वारमा पहरा दिएका छन्।\", \"चार तहको इँटाको चौकीमाथि झिँगटीका तीन छाना छन्।\", \"स्थानीयले यसलाई क्वाछो देगः भन्छन्, र यहाँबाट लाङटाङ र गौरीशङ्करसम्मको दृश्य देखिन्छ।\"]',NULL,'[{\"name\": \"Dashain (Mohani)\", \"note\": \"A special annual puja is held at the temple during Dashain\", \"month\": \"Ashwin\", \"name_np\": \"दशैँ (मोहनी)\", \"note_np\": \"दशैँमा मन्दिरमा वार्षिक विशेष पूजा गरिन्छ।\"}]','[{\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Uma_Maheshwar_Temple.jpg/1280px-Uma_Maheshwar_Temple.jpg\", \"author\": \"Tsephu\", \"caption\": \"Uma Maheshwar Temple, Kirtipur\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uma_Maheshwar_Temple.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Uma_Maheshwar_Temple_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Uma_Maheshwar_Temple_%282%29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Nirmal Dulal\", \"caption\": \"The temple on its stepped plinth\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uma_Maheshwar_Temple_(2).jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_13.jpg/1280px-Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_13.jpg\", \"author\": \"Harry Paudyal\", \"caption\": \"Kwacho Dega at the top of Kirtipur\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_13.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_16.jpg/1280px-Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_16.jpg\", \"author\": \"Harry Paudyal\", \"caption\": \"View over the valley from the temple hill\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_16.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_29.jpg/1280px-Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_29.jpg\", \"author\": \"Harry Paudyal\", \"caption\": \"Uma Maheshwar temple detail\", \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\", \"file_page\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uma_Maheshwar_Kritipur_IMG_7977_29.jpg\", \"license_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\"}]','{\"kind\": \"pagoda\", \"roof\": \"clay-tile\", \"notes\": \"Three-roofed brick pagoda on four stepped plinths with two stone elephants at the stair, on a hilltop with valley views\", \"tiers\": 3, \"walls\": \"red-brick\", \"colors\": [\"#8b3a2b\", \"#4a3020\", \"#c9a227\"], \"features\": [\"gilded-pinnacle\", \"carved-struts\", \"elephant-statues\", \"bell\"], \"height_m\": null, \"footprint_m\": [16, 16], \"plinth_shape\": \"square\", \"plinth_steps\": 4, \"surroundings\": [\"hilltop\", \"newar-houses\", \"himalaya-backdrop\"]}','2026-11-04 09:23:50');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `monuments` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `questions`;
/*!40101 SET @saved_cs_client     = @@character_set_client */;
/*!50503 SET character_set_client = utf8mb4 */;
CREATE TABLE `questions` (
  `id` int NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `monument_id` int NOT NULL,
  `question` varchar(400) COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL,
  `options` json NOT NULL,
  `answer_index` tinyint NOT NULL,
  `difficulty` tinyint NOT NULL DEFAULT '2',
  `rating` int NOT NULL DEFAULT '950',
  `explanation` varchar(400) COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
  `question_np` varchar(800) COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci DEFAULT NULL,
  `options_np` json DEFAULT NULL,
  `explanation_np` varchar(800) COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci DEFAULT NULL,
  `times_asked` int NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',
  `times_correct` int NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),
  KEY `monument_id` (`monument_id`),
  CONSTRAINT `questions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`monument_id`) REFERENCES `monuments` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=1161 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = @saved_cs_client */;

LOCK TABLES `questions` WRITE;
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `questions` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `questions` VALUES (1,1,'Which dynasty ruled from Bhaktapur Durbar Square until 1769?','[\"Licchavi\", \"Malla\", \"Shah\", \"Rana\"]',1,1,800,'The Malla kings of Bhaktapur ruled from this palace until the Gorkhali conquest of 1769.','सन् १७६९ सम्म भक्तपुर दरबार क्षेत्रबाट कुन वंशले शासन गर्‍यो?','[\"लिच्छवि\", \"मल्ल\", \"शाह\", \"राणा\"]','भक्तपुरका मल्ल राजाहरूले सन् १७६९ मा गोरखालीले जित्ने बेलासम्म यही दरबारबाट शासन गरे।',0,0),(2,1,'According to tradition, how many courtyards did the palace once have?','[\"55\", \"99\", \"108\", \"12\"]',1,2,950,'The palace is traditionally said to have had 99 courtyards; only about 15 remain.','परम्परा अनुसार दरबारमा पहिले कतिवटा चोक थिए?','[\"५५\", \"९९\", \"१०८\", \"१२\"]','परम्परा अनुसार दरबारमा ९९ वटा चोक थिए भनिन्छ। अहिले करिब १५ वटा मात्र बाँकी छन्।',0,0),(3,1,'In which year was the square inscribed as part of the Kathmandu Valley World Heritage Site?','[\"1969\", \"1979\", \"1989\", \"2006\"]',1,3,1100,'UNESCO inscribed the Kathmandu Valley, including this square, in 1979.','यो क्षेत्र कुन वर्ष काठमाडौँ उपत्यका विश्व सम्पदा स्थलमा सूचीकृत भयो?','[\"१९६९\", \"१९७९\", \"१९८९\", \"२००६\"]','युनेस्कोले सन् १९७९ मा यो क्षेत्रसहित काठमाडौँ उपत्यकालाई विश्व सम्पदामा राख्यो।',0,0),(4,1,'Which two earthquakes are blamed for reducing the square to its present open size?','[\"1505 and 1681\", \"1833 and 1934\", \"1934 and 1988\", \"1988 and 2015\"]',1,3,1100,'The 1833 and 1934 earthquakes destroyed many palaces and temples here.','यो क्षेत्र अहिले यति खुला देखिनुको कारण कुन दुई भूकम्पलाई मानिन्छ?','[\"१५०५ र १६८१\", \"१८३३ र १९३४\", \"१९३४ र १९८८\", \"१९८८ र २०१५\"]','सन् १८३३ र १९३४ का भूकम्पले यहाँका धेरै दरबार र मन्दिर ढाले।',0,0),(5,1,'What is the Newar name for Bhaktapur\'s palace square?','[\"Hanuman Dhoka\", \"Mangal Bazaar\", \"Khwopa Layaku\", \"Thamel\"]',2,4,1250,'Layaku means royal palace and Khwopa is the Newar name of Bhaktapur.','भक्तपुरको दरबार क्षेत्रलाई नेवारीमा के भनिन्छ?','[\"हनुमान ढोका\", \"मंगल बजार\", \"ख्वप लायकु\", \"ठमेल\"]','लायकु भनेको राजदरबार हो र ख्वप भक्तपुरको नेवारी नाम हो।',0,0),(6,1,'Whose gilded statue sits on a stone column facing the palace?','[\"Bhupatindra Malla\", \"Prithvi Narayan Shah\", \"Yaksha Malla\", \"Jang Bahadur Rana\"]',0,1,800,'The gilded statue shows King Bhupatindra Malla on a stone column, hands folded toward the palace.','ढुङ्गाको स्तम्भमाथि दरबारतिर फर्केको सुनले मोहोरिएको मूर्ति कसको हो?','[\"भूपतीन्द्र मल्ल\", \"पृथ्वीनारायण शाह\", \"यक्ष मल्ल\", \"जंगबहादुर राणा\"]','स्तम्भमाथि राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्ल दरबारतिर हात जोडेर बसेका छन्।',0,0),(7,1,'How much does a Nepali citizen pay to enter the square area?','[\"NPR 500\", \"NPR 200\", \"Nothing, it is free\", \"NPR 1,800\"]',2,1,800,'The ticket is NPR 1,800 for foreigners and NPR 500 for SAARC/China visitors; Nepali citizens enter free.','यो क्षेत्रमा नेपाली नागरिकले प्रवेश गर्न कति तिर्नुपर्छ?','[\"रु ५००\", \"रु २००\", \"केही पर्दैन, निःशुल्क छ\", \"रु १,८००\"]','विदेशीले रु १,८०० र सार्क/चिनियाँले रु ५०० तिर्छन्। नेपाली नागरिकलाई निःशुल्क छ।',0,0),(8,1,'Most of the surviving courtyards are linked to which goddess?','[\"Kumari\", \"Saraswati\", \"Annapurna\", \"Taleju\"]',3,2,950,'Of the roughly fifteen courtyards that survive, many are tied to the goddess Taleju.','बाँकी रहेका धेरैजसो चोक कुन देवीसँग जोडिएका छन्?','[\"कुमारी\", \"सरस्वती\", \"अन्नपूर्ण\", \"तलेजु\"]','बाँकी करिब १५ वटा चोकमध्ये धेरै तलेजु भवानीसँग जोडिएका छन्।',0,0),(9,1,'Which temple on the square was destroyed in 2015 and has since been rebuilt?','[\"Nyatapola Temple\", \"Vatsala Durga Temple\", \"Dattatreya Temple\", \"Bhairavnath Temple\"]',1,2,950,'The April 2015 earthquake destroyed the Vatsala Durga Temple, which has since been rebuilt.','सन् २०१५ को भूकम्पमा यो क्षेत्रको कुन मन्दिर ढल्यो र अहिले फेरि बनिसकेको छ?','[\"न्यातपोल मन्दिर\", \"वत्सला दुर्गा मन्दिर\", \"दत्तात्रेय मन्दिर\", \"भैरवनाथ मन्दिर\"]','सन् २०१५ अप्रिलको भूकम्पले वत्सला दुर्गा मन्दिर ढाल्यो। त्यो अहिले फेरि बनिसकेको छ।',0,0),(10,1,'The bullet mark said to be on the king statue\'s leg dates from the battle of which year?','[\"1934\", \"1833\", \"1769\", \"1505\"]',2,3,1100,'Tradition links the bullet mark on Bhupatindra Malla\'s statue to the battle of 1769, when the Gorkhalis conquered Bhaktapur.','राजाको मूर्तिको खुट्टामा देखिने गोलीको दाग कुन वर्षको युद्धको भनिन्छ?','[\"१९३४\", \"१८३३\", \"१७६९\", \"१५०५\"]','भनिन्छ, भूपतीन्द्र मल्लको मूर्तिको खुट्टाको दाग सन् १७६९ को युद्धको हो, जतिबेला गोरखालीले भक्तपुर जिते।',0,0),(11,2,'Which king completed the Palace of Fifty-five Windows?','[\"Yaksha Malla\", \"Bhupatindra Malla\", \"Ranajit Malla\", \"Prithvi Narayan Shah\"]',1,1,800,'Bhupatindra Malla completed it in 1708.','पचपन्न झ्याले दरबार कुन राजाले पूरा गरे?','[\"यक्ष मल्ल\", \"भूपतीन्द्र मल्ल\", \"रणजित मल्ल\", \"पृथ्वीनारायण शाह\"]','राजा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले सन् १७०८ मा यो दरबार पूरा गरे।',0,0),(12,2,'In which year was the palace completed?','[\"1427\", \"1680\", \"1708\", \"1934\"]',2,2,950,'Construction was completed in 1708.','दरबार कुन वर्षमा पूरा भएको थियो?','[\"१४२७\", \"१६८०\", \"१७०८\", \"१९३४\"]','सन् १६८१ को भूकम्पपछि सन् १७०८ मा यो दरबार पूरा भयो।',0,0),(13,2,'How many miniature raga carvings decorate the cornice?','[\"55\", \"99\", \"108\", \"147\"]',3,4,1250,'147 miniature carvings of musical ragas line the cornice above the ground floor.','कर्निसमा रागका कतिवटा साना कुँदाइ छन्?','[\"५५\", \"९९\", \"१०८\", \"१४७\"]','कर्निसमा सङ्गीतका रागहरूका १४७ वटा साना कुँदाइ छन्।',0,0),(14,2,'Which earthquake destroyed the top floor of the palace?','[\"1681\", \"1833\", \"1934\", \"2015\"]',2,3,1100,'The 1934 earthquake destroyed the top floor.','कुन भूकम्पले दरबारको माथिल्लो तला ढाल्यो?','[\"१६८१\", \"१८३३\", \"१९३४\", \"२०१५\"]','सन् १९३४ को भूकम्पले माथिल्लो तला ढालेको थियो।',0,0),(15,2,'Whom does the famous mural pair with Bhupatindra Malla as a cosmic couple?','[\"Queen Vishva Lakshmi\", \"Goddess Taleju\", \"Queen Ganga Rani\", \"Kumari\"]',0,5,1400,'The murals show Bhupatindra Malla and his queen, Vishva Lakshmi, as a cosmic Shiva and consort.','प्रसिद्ध भित्तेचित्रमा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लसँग शिव-पार्वतीको जोडीका रूपमा कसलाई देखाइएको छ?','[\"रानी विश्वलक्ष्मी\", \"तलेजु भवानी\", \"रानी गंगारानी\", \"कुमारी\"]','भित्तेचित्रमा राजा र रानी विश्वलक्ष्मीलाई ब्रह्माण्डका शिव र पार्वतीका रूपमा चित्रण गरिएको छ।',0,0),(16,2,'What is the Newar name of the Palace of Fifty-five Windows?','[\"Lun Dhwakha\", \"Nge Nyapa Jhya Layaku\", \"Khwopa Layaku\", \"Taleju Bhawani\"]',1,2,950,'In Newar the palace is called Nge Nyapa Jhya Layaku, meaning the royal palace of fifty-five windows.','पचपन्न झ्याले दरबारको नेवारी नाम के हो?','[\"लुन ध्वाखा\", \"ङे ङ्यापा झ्या लायकु\", \"ख्वप लायकु\", \"तलेजु भवानी\"]','नेवारीमा यो दरबारलाई ‘ङे ङ्यापा झ्या लायकु’ भनिन्छ, अर्थात् पचपन्न झ्याल भएको राजदरबार।',0,0),(17,2,'In what year did an earthquake ruin the older fifteenth-century palace on this site?','[\"1934\", \"1681\", \"1833\", \"1505\"]',1,2,950,'An earthquake in 1681 ruined the older palace, and Bhupatindra Malla completed this one in 1708.','यही ठाउँको पन्ध्रौँ शताब्दीको पुरानो दरबार कुन वर्षको भूकम्पले ध्वस्त पारेको थियो?','[\"१९३४\", \"१६८१\", \"१८३३\", \"१५०५\"]','सन् १६८१ को भूकम्पले पुरानो दरबार ध्वस्त पार्‍यो र सन् १७०८ मा भूपतीन्द्र मल्लले यो पूरा गरे।',0,0),(18,2,'What are the main building materials of the palace facade?','[\"Stone slabs\", \"Brick and timber\", \"Cast iron\", \"Marble\"]',1,1,800,'It is a brick-and-timber Newar palace with a long row of carved wooden windows.','दरबारको अगाडिको भाग मुख्य रूपमा केले बनेको छ?','[\"ढुङ्गाका पाता\", \"इँटा र काठ\", \"ढलौटे फलाम\", \"सङ्गमरमर\"]','यो इँटा र काठले बनेको नेवारी दरबार हो, जसमा कुँदिएका काठका झ्यालको लामो लहर छ।',0,0),(19,2,'What was used to patch the damaged top floor for decades after 1934?','[\"Thatch\", \"European roof tiles\", \"Tin sheets\", \"Slate\"]',1,3,1100,'For decades the top floor was patched with European roof tiles until a 2006 renovation restored traditional tiles.','सन् १९३४ पछि धेरै दशकसम्म बिग्रेको माथिल्लो तला केले टालिएको थियो?','[\"खर\", \"युरोपेली छानाका टाइल\", \"टिनका पाता\", \"स्लेट\"]','सन् २००६ को मर्मतले परम्परागत टाइल फर्काउनुअघि धेरै दशकसम्म युरोपेली टाइलले टालिएको थियो।',0,0),(20,2,'Can visitors usually go inside the palace?','[\"Yes, daily tours of every room\", \"No, it is viewed from the square\", \"Only during Bisket Jatra\", \"Only with a priest\"]',1,1,800,'The exterior is viewed from the square; the interior is not generally open to visitors.','पर्यटकले सामान्यतया दरबारभित्र जान पाउँछन्?','[\"पाउँछन्, हरेक कोठाको दैनिक भ्रमण हुन्छ\", \"पाउँदैनन्, चोकबाट बाहिरबाट हेरिन्छ\", \"बिस्केट जात्रामा मात्र पाउँछन्\", \"पुजारीसँग मात्र पाउँछन्\"]','बाहिरको भाग चोकबाट हेरिन्छ। भित्र सामान्यतया खुला छैन।',0,0),(21,3,'Which goddess is shown at the centre of the Golden Gate tympanum?','[\"Kali\", \"Taleju\", \"Saraswati\", \"Kumari\"]',1,2,950,'Taleju, tutelary goddess of the Mallas, is the main figure.','सुनढोकाको तोरणको बीचमा कुन देवी देखाइएको छ?','[\"काली\", \"तलेजु\", \"सरस्वती\", \"कुमारी\"]','तोरणको बीचको धेरै हात भएकी आकृति देवी तलेजुको हो।',0,0),(22,3,'In which year was the Golden Gate completed?','[\"1646\", \"1702\", \"1754\", \"1856\"]',2,2,950,'Work began in 1751 and finished in 1754.','सुनढोका कुन वर्षमा पूरा भएको थियो?','[\"१६४६\", \"१७०२\", \"१७५४\", \"१८५६\"]','सुनारका सन्तानले सन् १७५४ मा ढोका पूरा गरे।',0,0),(23,3,'Which king funded the completion of the gate?','[\"Ranajit Malla\", \"Yaksha Malla\", \"Bhupatindra Malla\", \"Jung Bahadur Rana\"]',0,3,1100,'Ranajit Malla provided the funds; his inscriptions flank the gate.','कुन राजाले ढोका पूरा गर्न खर्च जुटाए?','[\"रणजित मल्ल\", \"यक्ष मल्ल\", \"भूपतीन्द्र मल्ल\", \"जंगबहादुर राणा\"]','सय वर्षभन्दा बढीपछि राजा रणजित मल्लले परियोजनाको खर्च जुटाए।',0,0),(24,3,'Who first planned the gate in 1646?','[\"Pratap Malla\", \"Jagajjyoti Malla\", \"Jitamitra Malla\", \"Siddhi Narasingh Malla\"]',1,4,1250,'Jagajjyoti Malla brought goldsmiths from Lalitpur in 1646, but the work was postponed.','सन् १६४६ मा ढोकाको योजना पहिलो पटक कसले बनाए?','[\"प्रताप मल्ल\", \"जगज्योति मल्ल\", \"जितामित्र मल्ल\", \"सिद्धि नरसिंह मल्ल\"]','राजा जगज्योति मल्लले सन् १६४६ मा ललितपुरबाट सुनार ल्याएका थिए।',0,0),(25,3,'Which art historian called the gate the loveliest piece of art in the kingdom?','[\"Percy Brown\", \"Sylvain Lévi\", \"Henry Oldfield\", \"Götz Hagmüller\"]',0,5,1400,'Percy Brown, the English art historian, called it the loveliest piece of art in the kingdom.','कुन कला इतिहासकारले यो ढोकालाई राज्यकै सबैभन्दा सुन्दर कलाकृति भनेका थिए?','[\"पर्सी ब्राउन\", \"सिल्भाँ लेवी\", \"हेनरी ओल्डफिल्ड\", \"गोट्ज हागमुलर\"]','अङ्ग्रेज कला इतिहासकार पर्सी ब्राउनले यसलाई राज्यकै सबैभन्दा सुन्दर कलाकृति भनेका थिए।',0,0),(26,3,'What is the Newar name of the Golden Gate?','[\"Lun Dhwakha\", \"Taumadhi\", \"Layaku\", \"Khwopa\"]',0,1,800,'Lun Dhwakha is the Newar name of the Golden Gate.','सुनढोकाको नेवारी नाम के हो?','[\"लुन ध्वाखा\", \"तौमढी\", \"लायकु\", \"ख्वप\"]','सुनढोकालाई नेवारीमा लुन ध्वाखा भनिन्छ।',0,0),(27,3,'Which of these was one of the smiths who made the gate between 1751 and 1754?','[\"Bhaskara\", \"Divakara\", \"Subhakara\", \"Prabhakara\"]',2,5,1400,'The gate was made by the smiths Subhakara, Karunakara and Ratikara.','सन् १७५१ देखि १७५४ बीच ढोका बनाउने सुनारमध्ये एक को थिए?','[\"भास्कर\", \"दिवाकर\", \"सुभकर\", \"प्रभाकर\"]','ढोका सुभकर, करुणाकर र रतिकर नाम गरेका सुनारले बनाएका थिए।',0,0),(28,3,'How many years passed between the first plan in 1646 and the completion of the gate in 1754?','[\"54\", \"72\", \"108\", \"150\"]',2,3,1100,'1754 minus 1646 is 108 years, which is why the project is said to have stalled for over a century.','सन् १६४६ मा पहिलो योजना बनेदेखि सन् १७५४ मा ढोका पूरा हुँदासम्म कति वर्ष लाग्यो?','[\"५४\", \"७२\", \"१०८\", \"१५०\"]','१७५४ मा १६४६ घटाउँदा १०८ वर्ष हुन्छ। त्यसैले यो काम सय वर्षभन्दा बढी अडिएको भनिन्छ।',0,0),(29,3,'Who is allowed to enter the Taleju courtyard beyond the gate?','[\"Anyone with a ticket\", \"Only Hindus\", 